-- Entries: 126617.
return {
    ["\t显示"] = "Display",
    ["\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n备注：参考《封印物3-888现存90种机关谜题破解法》中机关破解方式，进入循环空间，<InvHighlight>连续破解3次机关谜题，可以打破记忆循环</>。"] = "\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n Note: Refer to the mechanism-breaking method in \"90 Existing Mechanism Puzzle Solutions for Sealed Artifact 3-888,\" enter the circular space, <InvHighlight> and solve the mechanism puzzles 3 times in a row to break the memory loop </>.",
    ["\n\n\n\n\n\n\n潜意识和梦境，都会受到音乐影响。\n其中的凶猛生物，也<InvHighlight>可能在音乐的影响下变得温和</>。"] = "\n \n \n \n \n \n \n Both the subconscious and dreams are influenced by music. \n The fierce creatures within <InvHighlight> may also become gentle under the influence of music. </>",
    ["\n\n\n\n\n\n　　<Mark id=\"#158\">如果那天，我能</>\n\n\n\n\n\n"] = "\n\n\n\n\n\n　　<Mark id=\"#158\">If only that day, I could have</>\n\n\n\n\n\n",
    ["\n\n\n\n\n\n　　<Mark id=\"#159\">郊外植物</>伤人事件究竟因什么而起？我没有找到任何线索。询问相关人员，他们也近乎失忆。没有人记得那天发生了什么！\n\n\n　　真可笑，难道以为我洛琳会因为这种困难就放弃调查吗？\n\n\n\n\n\n"] = "\n\n\n\n\n\n　　What exactly caused the <Mark id=\"#159\">suburban plant</> assault incident? I haven't found a single clue. When I asked the people involved, they were practically suffering from amnesia. No one remembers what happened that day!\n\n\n　　How ridiculous. Do they really think I, Lorin, would give up the investigation because of a little difficulty like this?\n\n\n\n\n\n",
    ["\n\n\n\n\n\n　　他嗦嗯，物植是有机会继续的，调差继续，太好了！\n\n　　祂来了，别想骗过我的眼睛。那团扭曲蠕动的东西，散发出红的蓝的光，像梦里的花朵，又像一轮圆月。\n\n　　我那天咀嚼着镜子，猫举着蘑菇将我推倒在森林，我从海里爬出来，吐出了一颗又一颗钻石，项链就戴在我的脖子上。\n小心身后！\n　　（意义不明的凌乱线条）\n\n\n\n\n\n"] = "\n \n \n \n \n \n He so-um, the plants have a chance to continue, the investigation continues, great! \n \n He has come, don't try to deceive my eyes. That twisted, wriggling thing emits red and blue light, like flowers in a dream, and also like a full moon. \n \n That day I was chewing on a mirror, a cat holding a mushroom pushed me down in the forest, I crawled out of the sea and spat out one diamond after another, and the necklace was worn around my neck. \n Watch out behind you! \n (Messy lines with no meaning) \n \n \n \n \n \n",
    ["\n\n\n\n\n\n　　嘿嘿，有线索了！奖励自己一块柠檬蛋糕！\n\n\n\n\n\n"] = "\n\n\n\n\n\n　　Hehe, I've got a lead! Time to reward myself with a lemon cake!\n\n\n\n\n\n",
    ["\n\n\n\n\n\n　　谢谢，我会还的。"] = "\n\n\n\n\n\n　　Thank you, I will pay it back.",
    ["\n\n\n\n\n<InvHighlight>“清晨纯露”</>，也被称为醒神剂——\n\n由<InvHighlight>梦境捕手的心脏</>、精灵花、秋水仙精华调配而成。\n能使服用者保持清醒，或有<Mark id=\"#159\">治疗嗜睡症</>的效果。"] = "\n\n\n\n\n<InvHighlight>\"Morning Dew\"</>, also known as a stimulant—\n\nis concocted from <InvHighlight>the heart of a Dream Catcher</>, spirit flower, and colchicine essence. \nIt can keep the user awake or have the effect of <Mark id=\"#159\">Healing narcolepsy</>.",
    ["\n\n\n\n\n梦境捕手，<InvHighlight>捕食梦境</>的凶猛生物。\n……\n它们痴迷<InvHighlight>牛奶</>和<InvHighlight>曼哈尔鱼</>的味道，这对它们有致命的吸引力。\n……\n如果睡前喝几口<Mark id=\"#159\">浸泡曼哈尔鱼眼珠的牛奶</>……"] = "\n \n \n \n \n Dream Catcher, <InvHighlight> a fierce creature that preys on dreams. </> \n ... \n They are obsessed with the taste of <InvHighlight> milk </> and <InvHighlight> Manhar fish, </> which has a fatal attraction for them. \n ... \n If you drink a few mouthfuls of <Mark id=\"#159\"> milk soaked with Manhar fish eyeballs </> before going to bed...",
    ["\n\n\n\n     《旅行周刊》编辑 安迪·凯恩斯\n\n\n\n"] = "\n\n\n\n \"Travel Weekly\" Editor Andy Cairns \n\n\n\n",
    ["\n\n\n\n<InvHighlight>5月18日 晴</>\n　　<Hide stylename=\"InvDefault_HW\" id=\"#157\">秘偶</>是什么……\n\n\n\n"] = "\n\n\n\n<InvHighlight>May 18th, Sunny</>\n　　<Hide stylename=\"InvDefault_HW\" id=\"#157\">What is a marionette</>...\n\n\n\n",
    ["\n\n\n\n　　<InvHighlight>捕梦网</>——接触非凡材料而染上灵性的渔网，是<Mark id=\"#159\">狩猎梦境捕手</>的有效方式。\n　　……\n　　最早发现者是位水手，他从噩梦中惊醒，发现渔网捕捉到一颗梦境捕手的<Hide stylename=\"Transparent\" id=\"#161\">心脏</>……"] = "\n \n \n \n <InvHighlight> </> Dream Catcher Net <Mark id=\"#159\">—a fishing net that has become spiritualized through contact with Beyonder material, is an effective way to </> hunt Dream Catchers. \n ... \n The first discoverer was a sailor who woke up from a nightmare to find that his fishing net had caught the <Hide stylename=\"Transparent\" id=\"#161\"> heart </> of a Dream Catcher...",
    ["\n\n\n　　我之所见是否为真实？金币的正面描摹着辉煌的光景，背面却沾满泥泞。飞速旋转的轴承，无情地将这个时代卷入蜕变的剧痛。\n\n　　罗塞尔·古斯塔夫的蒸汽机与改良火炮，图兰尼·冯·赫尔莫修因的第三代差分机，再精密的机械，其构成也不过是金属、热力与尘埃。然而这惊奇的人造物，不知疲倦地吞噬生命，在汗与泪中催化着一个不再需要星空照亮的时代。那只沾满油污的手，伤痕累累的手，不断向前伸出，而后缓慢地、坚定地，拨开了人类前路的迷雾……"] = "\n \n \n Is what I see real? The front of the gold coin depicts a glorious scene, but the back is covered in mud. The rapidly rotating bearings ruthlessly roll this era into the excruciating pain of transformation. \n \n Roselle Gustav's steam engine and improved artillery, Turani von Helmosin's third-generation difference engine—no matter how precise the machine, its composition is nothing more than metal, heat, and dust. However, this amazing man-made object tirelessly devours life, catalyzing an era that no longer needs the starry sky to illuminate it in sweat and tears. That oil-stained hand, that scarred hand, keeps reaching forward, and then slowly, firmly, pushes away the fog on the path ahead of humanity...",
    ["\n\n\n美酒、劲舞、无尽的欢愉！\n\n本酒馆开业只做三件事：激情、激情、还是<Hide id=\"#157_R\">***</>激情！\n\n每<Highlight>周四</>更有全场美酒<Highlight>激情半价</>！\n\n爱酒之人，勿失良机！"] = "\n\n\nFine wine, energetic dancing, and endless pleasure!\n\nThis tavern only does three things: passion, passion, and more <Hide id=\"#157_R\">***</> passion!\n\nEvery <Highlight>Thursday</>, all drinks are <Highlight>passionately half-price</>!\n\nWine lovers, don't miss out!",
    ["\n\n　　……\n\n　　那是1173年的特里尔，蒸汽机的白雾继笼罩因蒂斯后，席卷整个黑铁纪元。\n\n　　上万座轰鸣咆哮的工厂平地而起，数亿颗轧轧的齿轮摩擦咬合释出热量。油腻的沾灰的面孔，像迎风翕张的街头小报，源源不断流出厂房，吃力地飞进狭窄的公寓或棚屋，在瓦斯计费器的“叮当”脆响中，藉由煤气管道，于城市的暗夜里连成一片朦胧的光海。"] = "\n \n ... \n \n That was Trier in 1173, and the white mist of the steam engine, after shrouding Intis, swept across the entire Iron Age. \n \n Tens of thousands of roaring factories rose from the ground, and hundreds of millions of clanking gears rubbed and meshed, releasing heat. Greasy, dust-stained faces, like street tabloids flapping in the wind, flowed out of the factories continuously, struggling to fly into narrow apartments or shacks. Amidst the \"clinking\" of gas meters, through gas pipes, they connected into a hazy sea of light in the dark night of the city.",
    ["\n\n　　实践者的任务因此变得清晰：不是幻想打破极限，而是在极限之内逼近它。"] = " \n \n The practitioner's task therefore becomes clear: it is not to fantasize about breaking the limit, but to approach it within the limit.",
    ["\n\n　　文学经典回归！《大冒险家》作者佛尔思·沃尔女士佳作再版，带你领略别样的悬疑浪漫！\n\n"] = "\n \n A literary classic returns! A reprint of the masterpiece by \"The Great Adventurer\" author Ms. Fors Wall, taking you to appreciate a different kind of suspenseful romance! \n \n",
    ["\n\n　　黛丝死了，死在反锁的占卜室内。她平静地躺在<Mark id=\"#159\">法阵</>中央，手腕有一道精准的<Mark id=\"#159\">割伤</>。官方结论是<Tips stylename=\"Letter_Highlight\" id=\"#160\">自杀</>，但我知道，<Mark id=\"#159\">事情并非如此</>。 "] = "\n \n Daisy is dead, dead in the locked divination room. She lay peacefully in the center of the <Mark id=\"#159\"> magic circle, </> with a precise <Mark id=\"#159\"> cut </> on her wrist. The official conclusion is <Tips stylename=\"Letter_Highlight\" id=\"#160\"> suicide, </> but I know, <Mark id=\"#159\"> things are not so. </>",
    ["\n\n岁月如棋，落子无悔，一步踏错，便是百年。\n\n一副古老的棋盘静置于案，被放缓的时间里，隐约能看到一只大手和一只小手下棋的旧影。罗塞尔曾与贝尔纳黛对弈，谈起“烂柯棋局”的传说——那山中樵夫观棋片刻，人间已过百年。\n\n那时贝尔纳黛听不懂什么是烂柯，不懂为什么父亲总会把棋子下在交叉点上，也不懂什么是“观棋不语真君子，落子无悔大丈夫”，她只记得耍赖悔棋时父亲会轻拍她的头顶，手掌宽厚而温暖。"] = "\n\nTime is like a game of chess; once a piece is placed, there is no regret. One wrong step, and a hundred years have passed.\n\nAn ancient chessboard sat quietly on the desk. In the slowed time, one could faintly see the old shadows of a large hand and a small hand playing chess. Roselle once played against Bernadette and spoke of the legend of the \"Lanke Chess Game\"—the woodcutter in the mountains watched the game for a moment, and a hundred years had passed in the human world.\n\nAt that time, Bernadette didn't understand what Lanke was, why her father always placed his pieces on the intersections, or what \"a true gentleman watches the game in silence, and a real man never regrets his move\" meant. She only remembered that when she tried to cheat or take back a move, her father would gently pat her head, his palm broad and warm.",
    ["\n\n桃花林的尽头，是一旦离开便再也寻不到的归途。\n\n在因蒂斯郊外的桃花林中，罗塞尔常携小贝尔纳黛漫步。纷飞的桃花瓣下，他低声讲述着一个关于“桃花源”的古老传说——那是一片隐藏在桃林尽头的净土，生活在那里的人无忧无虑，可一旦离开，就再也找不到回去的路。\n\n贝尔纳黛那时懵懂，只觉得既然如此，那就不要离开。\n\n直到多年后，她才懂得人总会离开，才明白父亲口中的“桃花源”，是再也无法触及的旧日幻梦。"] = "\n\nAt the end of the peach blossom forest lies a path of no return once you leave.\n\nIn the peach blossom forest on the outskirts of Intis, Roselle often strolled with little Bernadette. Beneath the fluttering peach petals, he whispered an ancient legend about \"Peach Blossom Spring\"—a pure land hidden at the end of the peach forest where people lived without worry, but once they left, they could never find the way back.\n\nBernadette was naive then and thought that if that were the case, one should simply never leave.\n\nIt wasn't until many years later that she understood that people always have to leave, and realized that the \"Peach Blossom Spring\" her father spoke of was a Great Old One dream that could never be reached again.",
    ["\n\n由一根根豌豆藤蔓构筑起的青绿森林，摇晃的秋千不知勾起了谁的童年回忆。\n\n在众多童话故事中，“杰克与豌豆”被罗塞尔赋予了蒸汽与机械的奇想。他将平凡的豌豆藤描绘成由齿轮驱动的奇迹，让杰克用智慧改造巨人的城堡，将吃人的怪物变为烤蛋糕的伙伴。那也是贝尔纳黛好奇心最重的时候，“爸爸，巨人是弗萨克人吗？”“城堡怎么建在云上的呢，云不是水吗？”“要多高才能看到城堡呀，坐飞空艇能够看到吗？我想上去看看！”……\n\n多么古怪的问题都会获得回应，多么天真的想法都会得到满足。"] = "\n\nA green forest constructed from beanstalks; the swaying swing brings back someone's childhood memories.\n\nAmong the many fairy tales, \"Jack and the Beanstalk\" was imbued with steam and mechanical whimsy by Roselle. He depicted the ordinary beanstalk as a miracle driven by gears, letting Jack use his wisdom to renovate the giant's castle and turn the man-eating monster into a partner who bakes cakes. That was also when Bernadette was most curious. \"Papa, is the giant a Feynapotter?\" \"How is the castle built on the clouds? Aren't clouds water?\" \"How high do you have to be to see the castle? Can you see it if you take an airship? I want to go up and see!\"...\n\nNo matter how strange the questions, they would receive a response; no matter how naive the thoughts, they would be satisfied.",
    ["\n\n美酒、劲舞、无尽的欢愉！\n\n本酒馆开业只做三件事：激情、激情、还是<Hide id=\"#157_R\">***</>激情！\n\n每<Highlight>周四</>更有全场美酒<Highlight>激情半价</>！\n\n爱酒之人，勿失良机！"] = "\n \n Fine wine, hot dancing, endless pleasure! \n \n This tavern only does three things: passion, passion, and still <Hide id=\"#157_R\"> *** </> passion! \n \n Every <Highlight> Thursday </> there is fine wine <Highlight> passion half-price </>! \n \n Wine lovers, don't miss the opportunity!",
    ["\n \n                是谁造成了这一切？\n    <Letter_Highlight_HW>管家、医生、男爵夫人、仆人，</>            \n                凶手是他们中的哪个？"] = "\n \n                Who caused all of this?\n    <Letter_Highlight_HW>Butler, doctor, baroness, servant,</>            \n                Which one of them is the murderer?",
    ["\n  \n精准报时，人人可享！\n清洁上油，只要六便士！\n发条更换，质优价廉！\n怀表估价，现金收购旧表！\n\n机不可失，铁十字街平价钟表行即将调价！\n速来锁定今日低价！"] = "\n\nPrecise timekeeping, available to everyone!\nCleaning and oiling, only 6 pence!\nMainspring replacement, high quality and low price!\nPocket watch appraisal, cash for old watches!\n\nDon't miss this opportunity, the Iron Cross Street affordable clock shop is about to adjust prices!\nCome quickly to lock in today's low prices!",
    ["\n-----------------------------开始输出-----------------------------\n"] = "\n-----------------------------Start Output-----------------------------\n",
    ["\n1.每个人非肉体的部分分为四层，最核心叫精神体，也就是每个人最根本的灵性，万物有灵派认为，凡是生物都有灵性，都有精神体。\n2.精神体之外是星灵体，它是前者与灵界、与星空沟通的方式，属于前者的外在表现，和你当前的情绪直接相关，也是占卜的根源。\n3.再往外是心智体，与肉体结合。它牵涉头脑，属于你推理能力、思考能力、洞察能力和认识事物能力的综合呈现。\n4.最外层是以太体，它是你生命能量和肉体状态的表现，你看到的气场颜色就是以太体的外显象征。"] = "\n1. The non-physical part of everyone is divided into four layers. The core is called the spirit body, which is everyone's fundamental spirituality. The School of Thought of All Things Having Spirit believes that all living things have spirituality and a spirit body.\n2. Outside the spirit body is the astral body. It is the way the former communicates with the Spirit World and the starry sky. It belongs to the external manifestation of the former and is directly related to your current emotions. It is also the root of divination.\n3. Further out is the mental body, which is combined with the physical body. It involves the brain and belongs to the comprehensive presentation of your reasoning ability, thinking ability, insight, and ability to understand things.\n4. The outermost layer is the ether body, which is the manifestation of your life energy and physical state. The aura color you see is the external symbol of the ether body.",
    ["\n1345年4月12日 \n第一次摸到父亲的工具。锤子比想象中沉，手抖得厉害，把银片敲变形了。\n\n1345年8月3日 \n学会了辨认红宝石和石榴石的区别。\n\n1346年2月18日 \n母亲咳嗽又重了。周薪涨到12苏勒，买了些润喉的草药。\n\n1346年7月9日 \n独立完成了一枚银戒指的抛光。主顾是个码头工人，给未婚妻的。\n\n1347年3月15日 \n正式成为匠人学徒。父亲说我手稳，适合吃这碗饭。\n\n1347年11月2日 \n学会了镶嵌月光石。父亲点头了。\n\n1348年6月3日 \n周薪涨到1镑5苏勒。母亲炖了肉汤。\n\n1348年9月14日 \n第一次接定制单。顾客要一枚带苹果花纹的胸针，说送给妻子。画了三遍草图才满意。\n\n1349年1月20日 \n整理铺子旧物，发现一张泛黄的家谱图。有些名字被涂掉了。\n\n1349年3月8日 \n母亲的药粉快吃完了。这周多接些修活的单子。\n\n1349年6月28日 \n收到了一本奇怪的笔记。翻开第一页，那些符号……好像在哪里见过。"] = "\nApril 12, 1345 \nFirst time touching Father's tools. The hammer was heavier than I imagined, and my hands shook so much that I deformed the silver sheet.\n\nAugust 3, 1345 \nLearned to distinguish between rubies and garnets.\n\nFebruary 18, 1346 \nMother's cough worsened. Weekly wage rose to 12 sous; bought some throat-soothing herbs.\n\nJuly 9, 1346 \nIndependently finished polishing a silver ring. The client was a dock worker, for his fiancée.\n\nMarch 15, 1347 \nOfficially became a craftsman apprentice. Father said my hands are steady and I'm suited for this trade.\n\nNovember 2, 1347 \nLearned to set moonstones. Father nodded.\n\nJune 3, 1348 \nWeekly wage rose to 1 pound 5 sous. Mother stewed meat soup.\n\nSeptember 14, 1348 \nFirst custom order. Customer wanted a brooch with an apple pattern, said it was for his wife. Drew the sketch three times before he was satisfied.\n\nJanuary 20, 1349 \nOrganizing old items in the shop, found a yellowed family tree. Some names were crossed out.\n\nMarch 8, 1349 \nMother's herbal powder is almost gone. Need to take more repair jobs this week.\n\nJune 28, 1349 \nReceived a strange notebook. Opened the first page, those symbols... I feel like I've seen them somewhere.",
    ["\n3月4日：翻完了前三十六任的全部维护日志，没有发现任何异常。但那一夜它确实出了问题。答案不在日志里。那答案在哪里？\n\n3月11日：典籍里关于知识皇冠的记载只有只言片语——为什么这么少？是被删掉了吗？谁删的？必须找到更原始的文本。\n\n3月19日：十一本。还差一本。\n\n3月26日：不能停。停下来就会，就会？不能停。\n\n4月2日：它就在某个地方。找到它找到它找到它——\n\n4月3日：一定要找到它。\n\n（后面还有很多页，但字迹越来越潦草，到最后已经很难辨认。）"] = "\nMarch 4: Finished reading all the maintenance logs of the first 36 predecessors, found no abnormalities. But it really did have a problem that night. The answer is not in the logs. Where is the answer?\n\nMarch 11: The records in the classics about the Crown of Knowledge are only fragments—why so few? Was it deleted? Who deleted it? Must find more primitive texts.\n\nMarch 19: Eleven books. Still missing one.\n\nMarch 26: Cannot stop. If I stop, I will, I will? Cannot stop.\n\nApril 2: It is somewhere. Find it find it find it—\n\nApril 3: Must find it.\n\n(There are many pages behind, but the handwriting is getting more and more illegible, and it is hard to recognize by the end.)",
    ["\n5月24日\n晴天。漫山的雪反射的阳光非常刺眼，为了避免眼睛遭罪，我建议尼尔等太阳落山后再外出。他没把我的话放在心上，自顾自地收拾我们的东西，然后就先走了，他总是这样。\n我把东西收拾好追上他，远远望去，他在雪地里的影子有五个，朝着五个方向走。\n可能是我看错了，再望过去，只剩一个了。\n我们在山腰的位置扎营，距离登顶应该不远了。\n\n剩余物资：\n面包4份半\n肉干和肉肠3份\n糖1罐\n黄油3块\n酒2瓶\n水5瓶 路上找到水源，进行了补充"] = "\nMay 24\nSunny. The sunlight reflected by the mountains of snow is very dazzling. To avoid hurting our eyes, I suggested Neil go out after the sun sets. He didn't take my words to heart, packed our things on his own, and left first. He is always like this.\nI packed the things and caught up with him. Looking from afar, he had five shadows in the snow, walking in five directions.\nMaybe I saw it wrong. Looking again, there was only one left.\nWe camped at the waist of the mountain, it shouldn't be far from the summit.\n\nRemaining supplies:\nBread 4.5 portions\nBeef jerky and sausages 3 portions\nSugar 1 jar\nButter 3 blocks\nWine 2 bottles\nWater 5 bottles, found a water source on the way and replenished",
    ["\n8月11日晚上8点，铁十字街下街以糊制火柴盒为生的劳维斯太太突发疾病死亡。\n8月11日晚上10点，码头工人齐德跳入塔索克河，结束了贫穷的生命。\n8月11日晚上11点，西区济贫院内，破产的索尔斯企图纵火，制造惨案，但最终只烧死了自己。\n8月12号下午3点，码头工厂区海莉叶突然倒地死亡。\n……"] = "\nAugust 11, 8 PM, Mrs. Lawis, who lived by making matchboxes on Lower Street, died of a sudden illness.\nAugust 11, 10 PM, dock worker Zide jumped into the Tussock River, ending his poor life.\nAugust 11, 11 PM, inside the West District poorhouse, the bankrupt Sols attempted to commit arson and create a tragedy, but ended up burning only himself to death.\nAugust 12, 3 PM, Hayley in the dock factory area suddenly fell to the ground and died.\n……",
    ["\n<Delete id=\"#158\">1. 艾尔文·布朗 水仙花街 27 号</>  \n<Delete id=\"#158\">“格斗家”非凡特性（需要制作武器）</>  \n<Delete id=\"#158\">2. 玛丽娅·科尔 铁十字街</>  \n<Delete id=\"#158\">机械相关的神奇物品</>  \n<Delete id=\"#158\">3. 托马斯·霍夫曼 金梧桐大街 141号</>  \n<Delete id=\"#158\">护符和药水（为什么不找“药师”……）</>  \n<Delete id=\"#158\">4. 赛琳·维尔 豪尔斯街 6 号</>  \n<Delete id=\"#158\">“巫师”非凡特性（无特殊要求）</>  \n<Delete id=\"#158\">5. 罗克·范恩 佐特兰街 52号</>  \n<Delete id=\"#158\">“无面人”非凡特性（待交接）</>  \n<Delete id=\"#158\">6. 弗兰·斯戴尔 弗拉德街 3 号</>  \n<Delete id=\"#158\">机械相关的神奇物品</>  \n<Delete id=\"#158\">7. 海伦·萨契 斯蒂芬街 18号</>  "] = "\n<Delete id=\"#158\">1. Alwin Brown, 27 Daffodil Street</>  \n<Delete id=\"#158\">\"Brawler\" Beyonder characteristic (needs to make weapons)</>  \n<Delete id=\"#158\">2. Maria Cole, Iron Cross Street</>  \n<Delete id=\"#158\">Mechanics-related mystical item</>  \n<Delete id=\"#158\">3. Thomas Hoffman, 141 Golden Elm Street</>  \n<Delete id=\"#158\">Charms and potions (why not find a \"Pharmacist\"...)</>  \n<Delete id=\"#158\">4. Celine Ville, 6 Howls Street</>  \n<Delete id=\"#158\">\"Wizard\" Beyonder characteristic (no special requirements)</>  \n<Delete id=\"#158\">5. Rock Fane, 52 Zoutland Street</>  \n<Delete id=\"#158\">\"Faceless\" Beyonder characteristic (pending handover)</>  \n<Delete id=\"#158\">6. Fran Stale, 3 Vlad Street</>  \n<Delete id=\"#158\">Mechanics-related mystical item</>  \n<Delete id=\"#158\">7. Helen Sachi, 18 Stephen Street</>  ",
    ["\n<Letter_Highlight>怨灵残留的粉尘</>，165镑。\n木乃伊粉末，10克，5镑。\n鱼人黏液，30毫升，29镑。\n<Letter_Highlight>成年七彩蜥龙的龙翼160镑</>，心脏200镑。\n需要水鬼的脑组织，视完整程度，3镑至15镑不等。"] = "\n<Letter_Highlight>Dust left by a Wraith</>, 165 pounds.\nMummy powder, 10 grams, 5 pounds.\nMerfolk mucus, 30 milliliters, 29 pounds.\n<Letter_Highlight>Dragon wings of an adult Rainbow Lizard, 160 pounds</>, heart 200 pounds.\nNeed brain tissue of a Water Demon, depending on the degree of integrity, from 3 pounds to 15 pounds.",
    ["\n<Letter_Highlight>采摘草药</>：在第三个月升日采摘铁筷子草，6镑。\n<Letter_Highlight>短期雇佣</>：雇佣一位有航海经验的保镖，为期一月，600镑。\n<Letter_Highlight>金梧桐区案件</>：本周金梧桐区发生一起恶性入室抢劫杀人案，提供相关线索者，一经核实有效，即可获得10镑奖励。\n<Letter_Highlight>通缉悬赏</>：通缉犯海盗格斯出现于廷根，每条有效线索5镑。\n<Letter_Highlight>寻狗启事</>：三日前爱犬维纳于水仙花街走丢，通体黑色面部白色，若有线索，重金酬谢！"] = "\n<Letter_Highlight>Picking herbs</>: Pick iron clematis on the third day of the month, 6 pounds.\n<Letter_Highlight>Short-term employment</>: Hire a bodyguard with sailing experience, for one month, 600 pounds.\n<Letter_Highlight>Golden Elm District Case</>: A vicious home invasion and murder occurred in the Golden Elm District this week. Those who provide relevant clues, once verified as effective, can receive a 10-pound reward.\n<Letter_Highlight>Wanted Bounty</>: Wanted pirate Gus appeared in Tingen, 5 pounds per effective clue.\n<Letter_Highlight>Dog Search Notice</>: Three days ago, my beloved dog Vina was lost on Daffodil Street, all black with a white face. If there are clues, heavy reward!",
    ["\n<Mark id=\"#159\">私人</>垃圾桶，严禁乱丢垃圾！\n\n\n\n此垃圾桶仅供约翰一家使用，外人勿扰！违者后果自负！\n特别提醒：乱丢垃圾者，小心被<Hide id=\"#157\">“垃圾大王”</>盯上！——你不想惹麻烦吧？"] = "\n<Mark id=\"#159\">Private</> trash can, strictly forbidden to litter!\n\n\n\nThis trash can is for the use of the John family only, outsiders stay away! Violators will bear the consequences!\nSpecial reminder: Those who litter, be careful of being targeted by the <Hide id=\"#157\">\"Trash King\"</>!—You don't want to cause trouble, right?",
    ["\n<Tips stylename=\"Letter_Highlight\" id=\"#160\">接受拼租：</>\n白班与夜班工人可以共享一张床位。\n<Tips stylename=\"Letter_Highlight\" id=\"#160\">安全保障：</>\n管理员24小时巡逻，只保障您个人安全，不保障您财务安全。\n<Tips stylename=\"Letter_Highlight\" id=\"#160\">设施齐全：</>\n热水价格仅为冷水的一倍，灶台公用，按小时收费。\n<Tips stylename=\"Letter_Highlight\" id=\"#160\">价格实惠：</>\n“每周仅需8便士，押金10便士，欢迎年轻工人入住。\n咨询请找管理员老汤姆——他在一楼左手第一个房间，随时恭候！"] = "\n<Tips stylename=\"Letter_Highlight\" id=\"#160\">Accepting room sharing:</>\nDay shift and night shift workers can share a bed.\n<Tips stylename=\"Letter_Highlight\" id=\"#160\">Security guarantee:</>\nAdministrator patrols 24 hours a day, only guarantees your personal safety, does not guarantee your financial safety.\n<Tips stylename=\"Letter_Highlight\" id=\"#160\">Complete facilities:</>\nHot water price is only double that of cold water, stove is public, charged by the hour.\n<Tips stylename=\"Letter_Highlight\" id=\"#160\">Affordable price:</>\n\"Only 8 pence per week, 10 pence deposit, young workers are welcome to move in.\nFor inquiries, please find the administrator Old Tom—he is in the first room on the left on the first floor, waiting at any time!",
    ["\n<Tips stylename=\"Letter_Highlight\" u=\"1\" id=\"#160_R\">布满污迹的纸条上，只剩几行还能辨认的字：</>\n“我终于明白了……”\n“第一轮是<Letter_Highlight_HW>二号</>！二号是<Letter_Highlight_HW>真的</>！”\n“欲念使者说的都是<Letter_Highlight_HW>实话</>，可我们还是会死——”\n<Hide stylename=\"Transparent\" id=\"#161_R\">字迹断了</>，<Hide id=\"#157\">后面是一道擦过的暗色污痕。</>                                                                                         "] = "\n<Tips stylename=\"Letter_Highlight\" u=\"1\" id=\"#160_R\">On the stained note, only a few lines remain legible:</>\n\"I finally understand...\"\n\"The first round is <Letter_Highlight_HW>number two</>! Number two is <Letter_Highlight_HW>real</>!\"\n\"What the Desire Messenger said is all <Letter_Highlight_HW>truth</>, but we will still die—\"\n<Hide stylename=\"Transparent\" id=\"#161_R\">The handwriting broke</>, <Hide id=\"#157\">behind it is a dark stain that has been wiped.</>                                                                                         ",
    ["\n——上午——\n8：00-10：30   工作\n10：30-10：40  休息\n10：40-11：00 广播体操\n11：00-12：00  吃饭\n——午休——\n12：00-13：00\n——下午——\n13：00-15：30  工作\n15：30-15：40  休息\n15：40-16：00 跑操\n16：00-18：00  工作\n18：00后  晚餐（可外带）"] = "\n—Morning—\n8:00-10:30 Work\n10:30-10:40 Rest\n10:40-11:00 Radio gymnastics\n11:00-12:00 Eat\n—Lunch break—\n12:00-13:00\n—Afternoon—\n13:00-15:30 Work\n15:30-15:40 Rest\n15:40-16:00 Running exercises\n16:00-18:00 Work\nAfter 18:00 Dinner (can be taken away)",
    ["\n……\n\n从七月初起，廷根市儿童失踪事件多次发生，失踪者总人数为<Mark id=\"#159\"> 十三人 </>，其中男孩五人、女孩八人。\n目前已找到三人尸体，并已将凶手捉捕结案。\n但尸检检定致死原因均不同，归属于三例不同的现实普通事件。"] = "\n……\n\nSince the beginning of July, child disappearance incidents in Tingen have occurred many times. The total number of missing persons is <Mark id=\"#159\"> thirteen </>, including five boys and eight girls.\nCurrently, three bodies have been found, and the murderer has been caught and the case closed.\nBut the autopsy determined that the causes of death were all different, belonging to three different realistic ordinary events.",
    ["\n……\n\n暂未发现有非凡能力的残留，已抓获的作案者都是普通人、并无<Hide stylename=\"Transparent\" id=\"#161\">非凡能力</>或持有<Hide stylename=\"Transparent\" id=\"#161\">神奇物品</>，但无法完全排除此案件没有<Hide stylename=\"Transparent\" id=\"#161\">非凡者</>的参与。提议<Tips stylename=\"Letter_Normal\" u=\"4\" id=\"#160\">阿霍瓦郡警察厅特殊行动部第五、六、七小组</>提高警惕，加强巡逻。\n\n……"] = "\n……\n\nNo residue of Beyonder abilities has been found yet. The perpetrators who have been caught are all ordinary people, without <Hide stylename=\"Transparent\" id=\"#161\">Beyonder abilities</> or holding <Hide stylename=\"Transparent\" id=\"#161\">mystical items</>, but it cannot be completely ruled out that this case did not involve <Hide stylename=\"Transparent\" id=\"#161\">Beyonders</>. It is proposed that the <Tips stylename=\"Letter_Normal\" u=\"4\" id=\"#160\">Special Action Department Groups 5, 6, and 7 of the Ahowa County Police Department</> increase vigilance and strengthen patrols.\n\n……",
    ["\n……\n\n目前其余十人依旧下落不明。经过追踪调查，发现相关线索：\n1.失踪儿童年龄区间从八岁到十五岁不等\n2.失踪儿童最后目击出现地点主要在<Mark id=\"#159\"> 西区 </>和<Mark id=\"#159\"> 工厂区 </>。\n3.在案发地点附近，有人听到过疑似<Mark id=\"#159\">笛子 </>的声音。\n4.……"] = "\n……\n\nCurrently, the remaining ten people are still missing. After tracking and investigation, relevant clues were found:\n1. The age range of missing children is from eight to fifteen years old.\n2. The last sighting locations of missing children are mainly in the <Mark id=\"#159\"> West District </> and <Mark id=\"#159\"> Factory District </>.\n3. Near the crime scene, someone heard the sound of a suspected <Mark id=\"#159\">flute </mark>.\n4. ……",
    ["\n◆鲱鱼（新鲜）\n每桶50条 3桶 10苏勒/桶 <Delete id=\"#158\">103</> <Delete id=\"#158\">15 </>13苏勒\n\n◆鳕鱼（盐渍）\n每箱20磅 2箱 1金镑/箱 2金镑\n\n◆牡蛎 \n每篮100只 5篮 5苏勒/篮 55苏勒\n\n     合计  <Delete id=\"#158\">4金镑15苏勒 </>3金镑8苏勒"] = "\n◆Herring (fresh)\n50 per barrel, 3 barrels, 10 sous/barrel <Delete id=\"#158\">103</> <Delete id=\"#158\">15 </>13 sous\n\n◆Cod (salted)\n20 pounds per box, 2 boxes, 1 pound/box, 2 pounds\n\n◆Oysters \n100 per basket, 5 baskets, 5 sous/basket, 55 sous\n\n     Total  <Delete id=\"#158\">4 pounds 15 sous </>3 pounds 8 sous",
    ["\n　　<Letter_Highlight>《大冒险家·格尔曼海上历险》</>\n　　借阅人：丹尼 \n\n　　<Letter_Highlight>《机械制造工程基础》</>\n　　借阅人：菲利克斯\n　　……\n　　为了图书的正常流通，希望这些读者尽快归还所借图书，认真学习借阅相关的规章制度并遵照执行。"] = "\n　　<Letter_Highlight>\"Great Adventurer: Gehrman's Sea Adventures\"</>\n　　Borrower: Danny \n\n　　<Letter_Highlight>\"Fundamentals of Mechanical Engineering\"</>\n　　Borrower: Felix\n　　……\n　　For the normal circulation of books, I hope these readers will return the borrowed books as soon as possible, study the rules and regulations related to borrowing carefully, and comply with them.",
    ["\n　　<Letter_Highlight_HW>梅丽莎</>今天从贝克兰德回来，本来该我去接她的。\n　　但教会临时有点事，辛苦你帮我去黑荆棘接待一下。\n　　你在“愚者”先生的历史里见过她，虽然过了几年，她可能也长高了，但模样应该变化不大。\n　　给你个机会，好好表现！"] = "\n　　<Letter_Highlight_HW>Melissa</> is coming back from Backlund today, and I should have been the one to pick her up.\n　　But the church has something urgent, so please help me go to Blackthorn to receive her.\n　　You have seen her in Mr. Fool's history. Although a few years have passed and she may have grown taller, her appearance shouldn't have changed much.\n　　Giving you a chance, perform well!",
    ["\n　　……\n　　失踪者家属聚集警局门口抗议，警方表示“失踪案件均已登记处理”。据悉，近期此类事件已发生十余起，多为政府雇员。\n　　……\n\n<Note_Normal_HW>这些是我们的人，这家伙在干嘛！</>\n<Note_Normal_HW>他疯了，赶紧处理掉，不要留下把柄！</>\n<Note_Normal_HW>查理先生马上要参选了，这时候不能出任何丑闻！</>"] = "\n　　……\n　　Families of the missing gathered at the police station to protest, and the police stated that \"all disappearance cases have been registered and processed.\" It is reported that more than ten such incidents have occurred recently, mostly government employees.\n　　……\n\n<Note_Normal_HW>These are our people, what is this guy doing!</>\n<Note_Normal_HW>He's crazy, deal with it quickly, don't leave any evidence!</>\n<Note_Normal_HW>Mr. Charlie is about to run for office, there can't be any scandals at this time!</>",
    ["\n　　……什么烂戏，真没意思。\n　　男主角说话简直比我的房东康妮太太还啰嗦、还无聊！\n　　坐在这里的每一秒钟，我都在后悔没有选择去看马戏团的表演。\n　　幸好我带了纸笔，可以写写画画消磨一下时间。\n\n\n画点什么呢？一只小乌龟怎么样……"] = "\n　　……What a terrible play, really boring.\n　　The male lead speaks even more wordily and boringly than my landlady, Mrs. Connie!\n　　Every second I sit here, I regret not choosing to watch the circus performance.\n　　Fortunately, I brought paper and pen, so I can write and draw to pass the time.\n\n\nWhat should I draw? How about a little turtle...",
    ["\n　　一想到你要独自去那种地方，我就忍不住担忧你的安危。但我又与你一样好奇：他们真的和我们一样吗？无论是外表，还是内心？\n此次调查无疑是一项艰巨的任务，路途凶险，还请你务必保重。\n　　如果那里能收到来信，希望你能抽空报个平安。小玛莎和我一直期待着去廷根火车站接你回家的那天！\n　　愿女神庇佑你的归途平安无阻！"] = "\n　　Thinking that you are going to such a place alone, I can't help but worry about your safety. But I am as curious as you: Are they really the same as us? Whether it's appearance or heart?\nThis investigation is undoubtedly a daunting task, and the journey is dangerous, so please take care.\n　　If you can receive letters there, I hope you can find time to report that you are safe. Little Martha and I are looking forward to the day we go to Tingen Train Station to pick you up!\n　　May the Goddess bless your return journey to be safe and smooth!",
    ["\n　　不用意外！我预先知道你会到这里，留下了这封信，其他人看不到。\n　　我赶稿实在抽不开身，麻烦帮我把这本新书带给塔罗会的“月亮”先生。书钱我已经付过了！\n　　“月亮”目前以大地母神教会执事的身份，在金秋湖调查“丰饶污染”事件。你们正好可以借此认识一下。\n　　对了，“月亮”先生是血族，请一定不要叫他“吸血鬼”——那很不礼貌！\n　　附一张他自己很满意的画像，方便你辨认。\n（字迹越来越潦草……似乎没时间写更多了。） "] = "\n　　Don't be surprised! I knew in advance that you would come here and left this letter, others can't see it.\n　　I'm too busy with my manuscript to get away, so please help me bring this new book to Mr. Moon of the Tarot Club. I have already paid for the book!\n　　\"Moon\" is currently investigating the \"Abundance Corruption\" incident at Golden Autumn Lake as a deacon of the Earth Mother Church. You can just happen to get to know each other.\n　　By the way, Mr. Moon is a Sanguine, please don't call him a \"vampire\"—that's very rude!\n　　Attached is a portrait he is very satisfied with, for your identification.\n(The handwriting is getting more and more illegible... seems like there is no time to write more.) ",
    ["\n　　为给诸位更体面的购物环境，本店将\n　　于即日起暂停营业六周，全店翻修。\n\n　✦  新增进口原木打造专柜\n　✦  全店换装吊灯\n　✦  扩建二楼贵宾厅\n\n　　重新开业日期暂未确定，详情请关注 《贝克兰德邮报》\n　　凭报纸当日到店可享九折优惠"] = "\n　　To provide everyone with a more decent shopping environment, this shop will\n　　suspend business for six weeks starting today for a full renovation.\n\n　✦  Added counters made of imported logs\n　✦  Installed chandeliers throughout the shop\n　✦  Expanded the second-floor VIP lounge\n\n　　The reopening date has not yet been determined, for details please pay attention to the \"Backlund Post\"\n　　Present the newspaper on the day to enjoy a 90% Discount",
    ["\n　　今天画了一幅画，同学说很好看，我也觉得很好看。\n　　但是父亲说这很丑，他需要我种出好看的白菜，南瓜，去市场上卖个好价钱。\n　　我说好看的画，在画廊也能卖出好价钱。他说菜市场没有门，我们能走过去。画廊的门，我们可推不开。\n　　“永暗的蜡烛，不毁的身躯”，<Letter_RedBig>我觉得这个时代很坏，我不想在这个时代浪费时间了。</>"] = "\n　　Drew a picture today, my classmate said it was very beautiful, and I also think it is very beautiful.\n　　But Father said it was ugly, he needs me to grow good-looking cabbage and pumpkins to sell for a good price at the market.\n　　I said beautiful paintings can also sell for a good price in galleries. He said the vegetable market has no doors, and we can walk over. We can't push open the doors of the gallery.\n　　\"Candle of Eternal Darkness, Indestructible Body\", <Letter_RedBig>I think this era is very bad, I don't want to waste time in this era anymore.</>",
    ["\n　　今日，为女神带去了两束薄荷深眠花束。\n\n　　女神庇佑，只要能通过政府雇员考试，让考官爱上我我也愿意！\n\n　　……\n\n　　……\n\n　　失败了……\n\n　　努力出摊，售卖猪腿，争取为女神带去一整个深眠花园。"] = "\n　　Today, I brought two bouquets of mint and deep sleep flowers to the Goddess.\n\n　　May the Goddess bless, as long as I can pass the government employee exam, I am willing to let the examiner fall in love with me!\n\n　　……\n\n　　……\n\n　　Failed……\n\n　　Strive to set up a stall, sell pork legs, and strive to bring a whole deep sleep garden to the Goddess.",
    ["\n　　又落榜了……已经数不清是第几次落榜了……\n\n　　或许我生来就不适合成为一名政府雇员，仔细经营好那个小肉摊、和一个美丽的妻子一起过日子才是我应该过的生活。\n\n　　她会为我洗衣服，我会为她炖肉，让她成为全廷根吃过最多肉的女人。\n\n　　真是美好的生活……我该振作起来，努力去找一个妻子了。"] = "\n　　Failed the exam again... I have lost count of how many times I have failed...\n\n　　Perhaps I was not born to be a government employee. Carefully managing that small meat stall and living with a beautiful wife is the life I should be living.\n\n　　She will wash my clothes, I will stew meat for her, and let her become the woman who has eaten the most meat in all of Tingen.\n\n　　What a beautiful life... I should pull myself together and try hard to find a wife.",
    ["\n　　名称：看见我\n　　外观描述：一块<Letter_Highlight>透明水晶</>，约拇指大小，清澈无瑕。\n　　能力评估：持有者可“看见”他人的真实情绪与表层想法。持续注视目标可使其产生短暂的“认同感”，从而微妙引导对方行为。\n　　副作用警示：每次使用，持有者<Letter_Highlight>随机丢失</>一段属于自己的<Letter_Highlight>记忆</>。\n\n　　备注：三周前失窃，占卜显示仍处于<Letter_Highlight>激活</>状态。"] = "\n　　Name: See Me\n　　Appearance description: A piece of <Letter_Highlight>transparent crystal</>, about the size of a thumb, clear and flawless.\n　　Ability assessment: The holder can \"see\" others' true emotions and surface thoughts. Continuously staring at the target can make them have a brief \"sense of identification,\" thereby subtly guiding the other party's behavior.\n　　Side effect warning: Every time it is used, the holder <Letter_Highlight>randomly loses</> a piece of their own <Letter_Highlight>memory</>.\n\n　　Note: Stolen three weeks ago, divination shows it is still in an <Letter_Highlight>activated</> state.",
    ["\n　　嘿，我亲爱的玩家！\n　　既然你要和“国王”玩选择游戏，不了解规则可不行。所以我亲自为你编写了这份终极傻瓜……哦不，是《终极扑克速成指南》！\n\n　　<Letter_Highlight>五条</>：五张完全一样的扑克。\n\n　　<Letter_Highlight>顺子</>：数字连续的五张扑克。\n\n　　<Letter_Highlight>同花</>：花色相同的五张扑克。\n\n　　<Letter_Highlight>同花顺</>：花色相同，且数字连续的五张扑克。\n\n　　祝你好运……或者，祝你能看穿“好运”背后的把戏！"] = "\n　　Hey, my dear player!\n　　Since you are going to play a choice game with the \"King\", you can't do it without knowing the rules. So I personally wrote this ultimate dummy... oh no, it's the \"Ultimate Poker Quick Guide\" for you!\n\n　　<Letter_Highlight>Five of a Kind</>: Five identical poker cards.\n\n　　<Letter_Highlight>Straight</>: Five poker cards with consecutive numbers.\n\n　　<Letter_Highlight>Flush</>: Five poker cards of the same suit.\n\n　　<Letter_Highlight>Straight Flush</>: Five poker cards of the same suit and consecutive numbers.\n\n　　Good luck... or, I hope you can see through the tricks behind \"good luck\"!",
    ["\n　　在霍纳奇斯山脉下有一处终年被银色雾气包裹的森林，里面住着各自各样的珍稀动物。其中，有一头叫做邓恩的麋鹿住在森林的最深处，它有着云朵般柔软的灰色皮毛和比橡木还要坚实的巨大鹿角，走路时的蹄声沉稳地如同森林的呼吸。它是这座森林的守护者，拥有洞察森林每一个角落的力量，但这份力量也伴随着诅咒——每年第一场雪落下的时候，它就会开始遗忘。\n\n　　先是刚刚的对话，然后是昨天帮助过的动物，最后连自己的名字都如同飘落的雪花，落在地上了无痕迹。他只好把重要的事情都刻下来，做成木牌挂在鹿角上提醒自己。\n\n　　有一只叫戴莉的知更鸟住在森林的东边，雾气更加浓郁的地方。它有着绯红色的羽毛，它可以用歌声编织出金色的旋律，为迷路的生灵指引方向。但这里藏着它的秘密：每编织一段完整的旋律，它就会掉落一根羽毛，掉落的羽毛不会再生长。"] = "\n　　At the foot of the Hornacis Mountain Range, there is a forest covered in silver mist all year round, where all kinds of rare animals live. Among them, a moose named Dunn lives in the deepest part of the forest. It has gray fur as soft as clouds and huge antlers stronger than oak, and its hoofbeats when walking are as steady as the breathing of the forest. It is the guardian of this forest and has the power to gain insight into every corner of the forest, but this power is accompanied by a curse—when the first snow falls every year, it begins to forget.\n\n　　First, the conversation just now, then the animals it helped yesterday, and finally even its own name falls on the ground like falling snowflakes, leaving no trace. It has to carve down important things and make them into wooden signs to hang on its antlers to remind itself.\n\n　　A robin named Daly lives on the east side of the forest, where the mist is thicker. It has crimson feathers, and it can weave golden melodies with its singing to guide lost creatures. But there is a secret hidden here: every time it weaves a complete melody, it drops a feather, and the dropped feather will not grow again.",
    ["\n　　塔罗学派必读榜前五的优秀作品，贝尔纳黛会长倾心推荐！\n　　《观众的自我修养》据说是一位半神级观众领域的导师指导编纂的。\n　　《赞美太阳》“赞美太阳”不应流于表面，而该发自内心。\n　　《海上八万里》一本讲述海上生活的小说，书籍粉丝常因为作者是真水手还是假水手争论不休。\n　　《秘密的秘密》一本加入了神秘学元素的侦探小说，其开放式结局引发了巨大的争议。\n　　《学会看书》白塔途径学员的必修书目，同时是塔罗学派最热门的通识书籍。"] = "\n　　Top five excellent works on the Tarot Club's must-read list, highly recommended by President Bernadette!\n　　\"Self-Cultivation of a Spectator\" is said to have been compiled under the guidance of a demigod-level mentor in the Spectator pathway.\n　　\"Praise the Sun\": \"Praise the Sun\" should not be superficial, but should come from the heart.\n　　\"Eighty Thousand Miles at Sea\": A novel about life at sea, book fans often argue about whether the author is a real sailor or a fake sailor.\n　　\"Secret of Secrets\": A detective novel with occult elements, its open ending has sparked huge controversy.\n　　\"Learning to Read\": A required book for students of the White Tower pathway, and also the most popular general knowledge book of the Tarot Club.",
    ["\n　　好久不见。\n　　自廷根湖异变后，值夜者封锁了廷根湖边区域处理遗留的污染，目前已经处理完毕，重新解除了封锁。\n　　不过最近巡逻的同事告诉我，湖边近日忽然多了几张桌椅和帐篷，应该解除封锁后，有人来到这边进行了活动。\n　　保险起见，值夜者需要调查来到这边的人是否安全。如果你有时间的话，我希望你可以来廷根湖这边协助我们调查。\n　　新同事，期待着与你再一次见面。"] = "\n　　Long time no see.\n　　Since the mutation of Tingen Lake, the Nighthawks have blocked the area around Tingen Lake to deal with the remaining corruption, and it has now been processed and the blockade has been lifted.\n　　However, colleagues on patrol recently told me that a few tables, chairs, and tents have suddenly appeared by the lake recently. It should be that after the blockade was lifted, someone came here to carry out activities.\n　　To be safe, the Nighthawks need to investigate whether the people who came here are safe. If you have time, I hope you can come to Tingen Lake to assist us in the investigation.\n　　New colleague, looking forward to meeting you again.",
    ["\n　　如你所知，当下的廷根并不算风平浪静。就在几天前，我们又收到了一份郡警察厅的案件报告。经过一定的考虑和评估，我们一致认为，你是接手这个案件的合适人选。\n　　这个案件风险适中，是个不错的练手机会。在调查之余，也请你保护好自己——切记，安全第一。\n　　随信附上前期的调查档案，请仔细阅读。\n　　加油吧，新人值夜者。"] = "\n\tAs you know, Tingen is not exactly peaceful at the moment. Just a few days ago, we received another case report from the County Police Department. After some consideration and evaluation, we unanimously agreed that you are the right person to take on this case.\n\tThis case has moderate risk and is a good opportunity for practice. While investigating, please also protect yourself—remember, safety first.\n\tAttached to this letter is the preliminary investigation file; please read it carefully.\n\tGood luck, rookie Nighthawk.",
    ["\n　　如果你看到了这些文字，那是我在女神的神国求得了恩典，灵魂将它带到了你的面前。\n　　那些海盗不会放过任何一个人，我也不例外。我的时间不多了。\n　　最近总是在问候我们的小天使奥莉薇，但最后的时间我想呼唤你。\n　　我爱你戴娜，你永远是我心中最美丽的姑娘。"] = "\n\tIf you are reading these words, it means I have obtained grace in the Goddess's kingdom, and my soul has brought them to you.\n\tThose pirates will not spare anyone, and I am no exception. My time is running out.\n\tI have been asking about our little angel, Olivia, lately, but in my final moments, I want to call out to you.\n\tI love you, Dana. You will always be the most beautiful girl in my heart.",
    ["\n　　如果客人想在本店购买商品，请务必严格遵守以下规则，如有违者，后果自负。\n1.本店营业时间为每天3点至5点。\n2.店员工作时间为每天10点。\n3.请不要相信店员的话。\n4.购买三次商品后，请立即离开商店。"] = "\n\tIf a guest wishes to purchase items at this store, please strictly follow the rules below. Violators will bear the consequences.\n1. Our business hours are from 3:00 to 5:00 every day.\n2. Staff working hours are at 10:00 every day.\n3. Please do not trust the words of the staff.\n4. After purchasing three items, please leave the store immediately.",
    ["\n　　当你展开这封信笺时，芬芳的气息已将你包裹。这并非偶然，而是必然的命运——你被选中了。\n\n　　在贝克兰德雾气弥漫的街头，在廷根宁静的小巷深处，有这样一群人：他们追求极致的美丽，拥抱命运的无常，在灾厄中翩翩起舞。\n\n　　我们是春夜舞会。\n\n　　我们侍奉的是不幸与美丽的源头，是将灾难化作艺术的存在。在祂的庇护下，我们明晰了一个真理：\n\n　　真正的美，诞生于毁灭与重生之间。\n\n　　若你愿意加入我们，请前往\"珠宝店\"门口右侧。\n\n　　记住，我们不接受怯懦者，不欢迎虚伪者。唯有敢于凝视深渊，敢于拥抱真实的人，才配得上这场永不落幕的舞会。\n\n　　期待你的到来。"] = "\n\tWhen you unfold this letter, a fragrant scent has already enveloped you. This is not a coincidence, but an inevitable fate—you have been chosen.\n\n\tIn the fog-filled streets of Backlund, in the depths of the quiet alleys of Tingen, there is a group of people: they pursue ultimate beauty, embrace the impermanence of fate, and dance gracefully amidst disaster.\n\n\tWe are the Spring Night Ball.\n\n\tWe serve the source of misfortune and beauty, an existence that turns disaster into art. Under His shelter, we have realized a truth:\n\n\tTrue beauty is born between destruction and rebirth.\n\n\tIf you are willing to join us, please go to the right side of the entrance of the \"Jewelry Store\".\n\n\tRemember, we do not accept the cowardly, nor do we welcome the hypocritical. Only those who dare to gaze into the abyss and dare to embrace the truth are worthy of this never-ending Curtain Call.\n\n\tWe look forward to your arrival.",
    ["\n　　当午夜的钟声敲响，当星辰在天幕闪烁，当你在梦境与现实的边界徘徊——你听到了吗？那来自深处的低语，那安宁的呼唤。\n\n　　我们是安魂诗社。\n\n　　在女神的注视下，我们是夜晚的守护者，是亡者的歌者，是秘密的守卫。我们相信：\n\n　　黑夜不是恐惧的源头，而是安宁的居所。死亡不是终结的悲哀，而是解脱的开始。我们用诗歌抚慰失眠者，用仪式安抚亡灵，用沉默守护那些不能言说的秘密。\n\n　　若你愿意加入我们，请在新月之夜来到拉斐尔墓园深处，吟诵祷词：\n\n　　\"女神啊，请让安宁降临，\n　　让梦境包裹疲惫的灵魂，\n　　让黑夜庇护迷途的羔羊。\"\n\n　　我们会在黑暗中迎接你。\n　　我们会在静谧中认可你。\n　　我们会在诗歌中铭记你。\n\n　　但请记住，成为安魂诗社的一员，意味着你将承担起相应的责任——在他人入眠时保持清醒，在世界喧嚣时保持沉默，在光明炽烈时拥抱黑暗。\n\n　　你，准备好了吗？  愿黑夜庇护你，愿安宁与你同在。"] = "\n\tWhen the midnight bell tolls, when the stars blink in the sky, when you wander on the boundary between dreams and reality—do you hear it? That whisper from the depths, that peaceful call.\n\n\tWe are the Requiem Poetry Society.\n\n\tUnder the Goddess's Gaze, we are the Guardians of the night, the singers for the dead, and the keepers of secrets. We believe:\n\n\tThe night is not the source of horror, but a dwelling of peace. Death is not the sorrow of an end, but the beginning of liberation. We use poetry to comfort the insomniac, rituals to pacify the spirits, and silence to guard those unspeakable secrets.\n\n\tIf you are willing to join us, please come to the depths of Raphael Cemetery on the night of the new moon and recite the prayer:\n\n\t\"Oh Goddess, please let peace descend,\n\tLet dreams wrap around the weary soul,\n\tLet the night shelter the lost lamb.\"\n\n\tWe will welcome you in the darkness.\n\tWe will acknowledge you in the silence.\n\tWe will remember you in our poetry.\n\n\tBut please remember, becoming a member of the Requiem Poetry Society means you will shoulder corresponding responsibilities—staying awake while others sleep, remaining silent while the world is noisy, and embracing the darkness while the light is intense.\n\n\tAre you ready? May the night shelter you, and may peace be with you.",
    ["\n　　您的好意一如既往，您的行为让我困惑。\n　　您真的只是可怜我吗？这就是您的心意？\n　　您能至少与我面对面说一次话吗？\n　　……想必这封信也不会收到您的答复，但我会一直在这里，等待着您的出现。\n　　我从未见过春天，我的世界里，只有您来了。"] = "\n\tYour kindness is as consistent as ever, yet your behavior confuses me.\n\tAre you really just pitying me? Is this your true intention?\n\tCan you at least speak to me face-to-face once?\n\t...I suppose this letter will not receive a reply from you either, but I will always be here, waiting for your appearance.\n\tI have never seen spring; in my world, only you have arrived.",
    ["\n　　感谢您那日陪我完成这趟奇特的旅程。不瞒您说，我至今仍觉得周身萦绕着那罐头的味道，怕是好几天都散不掉。\n　　但您猜怎么着？女儿看了那些照片，笑得前仰后合。她终于愿意跟我聊聊天了——虽然多半是在笑话我，但至少，我们又说上话了。 \n　　她还给我布置了个新任务：把正版《大冒险家》从头到尾读一遍，再写篇读后感交给她。 \n　　另外，那天在码头遇见的后援会朋友邀我们参加下次的活动。女儿听说后，竟说“一起去看看”。我想，这或许是个不错的开始。\n\n又及：那些照片我还留着。每次看到，都觉得……来都来了，总得留点什么。"] = "\n\tThank you for accompanying me on this peculiar journey that day. To be honest, I still feel the smell of those canned goods lingering around me; I'm afraid it won't dissipate for several days.\n\tBut guess what? My daughter looked at those photos and laughed until she was doubled over. She is finally willing to chat with me—although mostly to make fun of me, at least we are talking again. \n\tShe even gave me a new Quest: read the original \"Great Adventurer\" from beginning to end and write a review for her. \n\tAlso, the friend from the fan club I met at the Dock that day invited us to participate in the next event. When my daughter heard about it, she actually said, \"Let's go take a look together.\" I think this might be a good start.\n\nP.S.: I still have those photos. Every time I see them, I feel... since I've already come, I must leave something behind.",
    ["\n　　我们要去贝克兰德和孩子一起过新年了，过完年就回来，提前祝大家新年快乐！\n\n\n歇业日期\n1349年12月20日~1350年1月5日"] = "\n\tWe are going to Backlund to spend the New Year with our children and will return after the holidays. Wishing everyone a Happy New Year in advance!\n\n\nClosure Dates\nDecember 20, 1349 ~ January 5, 1350",
    ["\n　　我很喜欢您上次寄来的礼物，谢谢您。这架木雕钢琴或许制作粗糙，却正好适合摆在我的书桌上。\n　　听闻您在葬礼后，不眠不休，成功逮捕了凶手，感谢您的付出！毋庸置疑，您是一名优秀的警察，请不要因为旁人的评价与压力改变初心。\n　　随信附上台历回礼，您可以记录重要的事。\n　　祝您工作顺利！永不迟到！"] = "\n\tI really like the gift you sent last time, thank you. This wooden carved piano might be crudely made, but it fits perfectly on my desk.\n\tI heard that after the funeral, you worked without sleep to successfully arrest the murderer. Thank you for your efforts! There is no doubt that you are an excellent police officer; please do not change your original intention because of others' evaluations and pressure.\n\tAttached to this letter is a calendar as a return gift; you can use it to Record important things.\n\tI wish you success in your work! May you never be late!",
    ["\n　　我用一瓶您给的牛奶换来了邻居家孩子的代笔。\n　　请原谅我如此冒昧，您的出现已经成了我每周里最期待的事——一位由香气构成的朋友。\n　　我不知道你的姓名，也永远不会知道你的模样，但我希望能有一个认识您的机会。\n\n　　若您愿意，下次来时，可否多停留片刻？让我给您一杯水，问问您的名字？"] = "\n\tI used a bottle of milk you gave me to get the neighbor's child to write this for me.\n\tPlease forgive my presumption; your appearance has become the thing I look forward to most every week—a friend made of fragrance.\n\tI don't know your name, and I will never know your appearance, but I hope to have a chance to get to know you.\n\n\tIf you are willing, could you stay a little longer next time you come? Let me give you a glass of water and ask for your name?",
    ["\n　　教会传来消息，封印物2-327“看见我”失窃。占卜显示线索指向黑伍德庄园。\n　　黑伍德男爵今晚举办舞会。我们需要一个善于观察的人混入舞会调查——你是序列9“观众”，没有比你更合适的人选。\n　　你的身份已安排妥当：贝克兰德来的新兴商人，听闻庄园有投资机会，受邀赴宴。\n　　记住，观众不登台。\n　　观察，不要打草惊蛇。"] = "\n\tThe Church has received news that the Sealed Artifact 2-327 \"See Me\" has been stolen. Divination shows that the clues point to Heywood Manor.\n\tBaron Heywood is hosting a Ball tonight. We need someone good at observation to sneak into the Ball to investigate—you are a Sequence 9 \"Spectator\", and there is no one more suitable than you.\n\tYour identity has been arranged: an emerging businessman from Backlund who heard about investment opportunities at the manor and was invited to the banquet.\n\tRemember, the Spectator does not take the stage.\n\tObserve, and do not alert the enemy.",
    ["\n　　日安！\n　　金秋湖最近越发热了，不知道您身体怎么样？如果您需要，可以托梦给我，我有最好的解暑茶。\n　　我最近很好。个头长高了一点，草药书看到了第六章，成功配出了咳嗽药剂，治好了汉娜婶婶的感冒。\n　　接下来我要开始练习更高级的药方。如果您不太忙的话，我想要几棵水刃草，用来做醒神药剂。因为没学会游泳，我一直没拿到它。\n　　如果您太忙也没关系！我会努力练习游泳的。"] = "\n\tGood day!\n\tGolden Autumn Lake has been getting hotter lately; I wonder how your health is? If you need to, you can send me a dream; I have the best tea for cooling off.\n\tI am doing very well recently. I have grown a little taller, read to the sixth chapter of the Herbs book, and successfully concocted a cough potion that cured Aunt Hannah's cold.\n\tNext, I am going to start practicing more advanced prescriptions. If you are not too busy, I would like a few stalks of Water Blade Grass to make a refreshing potion. Because I haven't learned to swim, I haven't been able to get it.\n\tIf you are too busy, that's okay too! I will work hard on practicing swimming.",
    ["\n　　最近还好吗？很高兴您能喜欢木雕钢琴。\n　　我能逮捕凶手，得益于同事的帮助和您的信任，我们会继续守护廷根。\n　　诚如您在葬礼上所言，冬天太过寒冷。所以，为了能在春天重逢，我们会努力生活，走出离别的阴霾。\n　　不知道您愿不愿意和我交个朋友，我认为，我们会有话可说。\n　　您寄来的礼物，我会好好使用，保证不忘记重要的日子，请放心。\n　　祝您工作顺利！"] = "\n\tHow are you doing lately? I'm glad you liked the wooden carved piano.\n\tMy ability to arrest the murderer was thanks to the help of my colleagues and your trust; we will continue to Guard Tingen.\n\tAs you said at the funeral, winter is too cold. Therefore, in order to reunite in the spring, we will strive to live and walk out of the haze of parting.\n\tI don't know if you are willing to be friends with me; I think we will have things to talk about.\n\tI will make good use of the gift you sent and promise not to forget important days, please rest assured.\n\tI wish you success in your work!",
    ["\n　　有点急事，待会回来。\n\n　　你可以在咖啡馆周围看看，旁边<Letter_Highlight_HW>中央广场</>上有一个叫做<Mark id=\"#159\">“旅行尖碑”</>的石碑，那是“魔术师”小姐和工匠制作的，开启后，就能在各地的旅行点之间穿梭。\n\n　　好东西，比走路快。\n\n　　注：不要走太远。\n"] = "\n　　I have some urgent business to attend to, I'll be back in a moment.\n\n　　You can look around the Cafe. There is a stone tablet called the <Mark id=\"#159\">\"Travel Obelisk\"</> in the <Letter_Highlight_HW>Central Plaza</> nearby. It was created by Miss \"Magician\" and the Artisan. Once activated, you can travel between various travel points across the land.\n\n　　It's a good item, much faster than walking.\n\n　　Note: Don't wander too far.\n",
    ["\n　　本人艾德蒙·唐泰斯，愿意向风暴郑重发誓：\n　　接受梅塞苔丝成为我的妻子，从今日起，无论贫穷与富有，不论祸福，贵贱，疾病还是健康，都爱你，珍视你，直至死亡。"] = "I, Edmond Dantès, solemnly swear to the Storm:\nI accept Mercedes as my wife. From this day forward, for better or for worse, for richer or for poorer, in sickness and in health, I will love you and cherish you until death.",
    ["\n　　沃尔女士说，真正的作家必须做一个记录者，深入最真实现场，切身感受故事的气息。\n　　雪怪算什么？我要写出最震撼人心的猎杀巨兽传奇！\n　　不对，那几拨探险家怎么打起来了？那是枪声吗？\n　　天啊，他们在争夺什么宝物？这比我原本的计划刺激多了！\n　　决定了，不写什么魔雪怪巨兽了。回去就写《雪山火拼记》！\n　　等等，他们怎么朝我来了？"] = "\n\tMs. Wall says that a true writer must be a recorder, delving into the most realistic scenes to personally feel the scent of the story.\n\tWhat's a snow monster? I am going to write the most shocking legend of hunting giant beasts!\n\n\tWait, why are those groups of explorers fighting? Was that a gunshot?\n\tOh my god, what treasure are they fighting over? This is much more exciting than my original plan!\n\tI've decided, I'm not writing about any snow monster giant beasts. I'll write \"Snowy Mountain Shootout\" when I get back!\n\tWait, why are they coming towards me?",
    ["\n　　没有任何一个窈窕淑女会愿意嫁给一个肉贩子！没有！\n\n　　我恨我身上的肉骚味！我恨透了这个世界！\n\n　　我<Delete id=\"#157\">一些难以展示的鲁恩脏话，粗俗不堪，表达了一个生活不意的人对世界和命运的痛恨。</>\n\n　　如果我成为一名政府雇员呢？\n\n　　如果我再努力一些，哪怕只是在那方正的建筑里端盘子，会不会有人愿意爱我？"] = "\n\tNo young lady would be willing to marry a meat butcher! None!\n\n\tI hate the smell of meat on me! I hate this world!\n\n\tI <Delete id=\"#157\">some Loen profanities that are hard to display, vulgar and crude, expressing the hatred of a person who is not doing well in life towards the world and fate.</>\n\n\tWhat if I become a government employee?\n\n\tIf I work harder, even if it's just serving plates in that square building, would someone be willing to love me?",
    ["\n　　灰色的麋鹿突然仰首长鸣，它角上的羽毛纷纷发出柔光，飘到空中接续起了戴莉未完成的歌。它的鹿角记住了每片羽毛中储存的音符，它笨拙的收集无意中保存了戴莉所有的歌声。\n\n　　直到鹿角触碰到最后一个音符的时刻，光亮也在出现在眼前，猫头鹰长老在洞口拼命甩着翅膀欢迎英雄的归来。\n\n　　戴莉再次醒来是在温暖而干燥的落叶堆里，它惊讶地发现身上覆盖着全新的羽毛——银白色的，如雾般轻盈蓬松。邓恩安静地守在落叶堆旁，角上依然挂着木牌，最新一块刻着：“戴莉拥有了一身新的羽毛，记得赞美它。”\n\n　　后来，森林里流传着这样的故事：这里有两位守护者，深沉的鹿蹄声和清亮的鸟叫声完美交融，它们在歌声和鹿角中记录每一朵花的绽放，每条溪流的改道和每个生命的成长。邓恩的遗忘还在循环，但它每天都赞美戴莉的羽毛；戴莉的羽毛不再随歌声掉落，每段旋律都让羽毛更有光泽。\n\n　　有些记忆会在冬雪中被埋藏，有些记忆会在回响中永恒。即使遗忘，善良也会为弱者驻足，即使失去，爱会赋予重构的勇气。"] = "\n\tThe gray elk suddenly raised its head and let out a long cry. The feathers on its antlers emitted a soft light, drifting into the Aerial to continue the song Daly had not finished. Its antlers remembered the notes stored in every feather, and its clumsy collection unintentionally preserved all of Daly's singing.\n\n\tUntil the moment the antlers touched the last note, the light also appeared before its eyes. The owl elder was flapping its wings desperately at the cave entrance to welcome the hero's return.\n\n\tDaly woke up again in a pile of warm and dry fallen leaves. It was surprised to find that it was covered with brand-new feathers—silver-white, as light and fluffy as mist. Dunn was quietly guarding the pile of leaves, with a wooden sign still hanging on his antlers, the latest one carved with: \"Daly has a new set of feathers, remember to praise it.\"\n\n\tLater, such a story circulated in the forest: there are two Guardians here, the deep sound of deer hooves and the clear chirping of birds blend perfectly. They record the blooming of every flower, the diversion of every stream, and the growth of every life in their songs and antlers. Dunn's Oblivion is still looping, but he praises Daly's feathers every day; Daly's feathers no longer fall with the singing, and every melody makes the feathers more lustrous.\n\n\tSome memories will be buried in the winter snow, and some memories will be eternal in the echoes. Even if forgotten, kindness will stop for the weak; even if lost, love will give the courage to reconstruct.",
    ["\n　　生意真差，守着摊子简直是浪费时间。\n\n　　要不去“莴苣与肉类”市场出摊试试呢？\n\n　　……\n\n　　算了，我受不了和那群人竞争，他们抢夺客人的样子就像看到猎物的红眼鬣狗。\n\n　　还是努力通过考试，成为政府雇员吧，明年，明年我一定会成功的！"] = "\n\tBusiness is so bad; guarding the stall is just a waste of time.\n\n\tShould I try setting up a stall at the \"Lettuce and Meat\" market?\n\n\t...\n\n\tForget it, I can't stand competing with that group of people; the way they snatch customers is like red-eyed hyenas seeing prey.\n\n\tI'd better work hard to pass the exam and become a government employee. Next year, next year I will definitely succeed!",
    ["\n　　生活太<Letter_RedBig>辛苦</>了，像我们这样穷苦的人，生来似乎就是为了劳作的。\n　　如果不劳作，今天吃完了饭，就要操心明天的饭在哪里。\n　　如果运气好，工厂给了我劳作的机会，今天工作结束，又要操心明天的工作。\n　　冷的时候，手上会长<Letter_RedBig>疮口</>，一点一点冻掉我的肉。\n　　热的时候，棉絮会钻进我的肺部，让我一点一点咳出我的<Letter_RedBig>灵魂</>。\n　　对我这样的人来说，明天是一种负担。\n　　“永暗的蜡烛，不毁的身躯”，我想要什么也不管，什么也不顾……直接睡过去。"] = "\n　　Life is too <Letter_RedBig>hard</>. It seems that poor people like us are born just to toil.\n　　If we don't toil, once we finish today's meal, we have to worry about where tomorrow's will come from.\n　　If we are lucky enough for the Factory to give us a chance to work, once today's work is done, we have to worry about tomorrow's work again.\n　　When it's cold, <Letter_RedBig>sores</> grow on my hands, freezing away my flesh bit by bit.\n　　When it's hot, cotton fibers drill into my lungs, making me cough out my <Letter_RedBig>soul</> bit by bit.\n　　For someone like me, tomorrow is a burden.\n　　\"Candle of eternal darkness, indestructible body,\" I want to ignore everything, disregard everything... and just fall asleep.",
    ["\n　　第十三个了，太爽了！太爽了！\n　　这金色子弹的效果太好了，有了它我还当什么雇佣杀手！\n　　不过那位先生的条件也够奇怪，不管目标是谁，只要在特定地点，特定时间杀……\n　　不管了，反正警察也不会真的抓我，他们说好了的！\n　　按照约定，明天晚上，一切就结束了。"] = "\n\tThe thirteenth one, so satisfying! So satisfying!\n\tThe effect of this golden Bullet is too good. With it, why would I still be a hired killer!\n\tBut that gentleman's conditions are strange enough; no matter who the target is, as long as it's at a specific location, at a specific time, kill...\n\tWhatever, the police won't really catch me anyway; they promised!\n\tAccording to the agreement, tomorrow night, everything will be finished.",
    ["\n　　紫丁香的味道很好闻，我把它插在窗前的花瓶里，也许您路过时能看见它们。\n\n　　您最近会多在门口停留一会儿，那我开门时，您又为什么总是一言不发呢？\n\n　　如果是秋天的风太凉，春天的时候，能和我见面吗？"] = "\n\tThe scent of lilacs is very pleasant. I put them in the vase by the window; perhaps you can see them when you pass by.\n\n\tYou have been lingering at the door a little longer lately, so why are you always silent when I Open Door?\n\n\tIf the autumn wind is too cold, can we meet in the spring?",
    ["\n　　老师死了，工坊也倒闭了。\n　　我做不好蜡烛，也救不回老师。\n　　糖厂的工作不适合我，糖是甜的，但糖厂是发苦的。\n　　我什么都做不好，谁也救不回。\n　　“永暗的蜡烛，不毁的身躯”，<Letter_RedBig>请带走我这个无用之人吧。</>"] = "\n\tThe teacher is dead, and the workshop has closed down.\n\tI can't make candles well, and I can't save the teacher.\n\tThe work at the sugar factory doesn't suit me; sugar is sweet, but the sugar factory is bitter.\n\tI can't do anything well, and I can't save anyone.\n\t\"Candle of Eternal Darkness, Indestructible Body\", <Letter_RedBig>please take away this useless person.</>",
    ["\n　　艾莉卡发现了。她质问我和贝丝的关系……争吵……我发誓我不是故意的……但磨坊烧起来了……她还在里面，她……\n　　……即使我出身贵族，发生这么大的事治安官也会找上门来。我必须去找贝丝。她在骨桥等我。她说会带我躲进山里……\n　　等等……贝丝身边的那个人是谁……那张脸……那不是艾莉卡吗？！她不是已经……\n　　她们在笑……向我走来……她们的脸在变化……变得和我……一样……"] = "\n\tErica found out. She questioned my relationship with Beth... an argument... I swear I didn't mean it... but the mill caught fire... she was still inside, she...\n\t...Even if I come from a noble family, the sheriff will come knocking after such a big incident. I must go find Beth. She is waiting for me at Bone Bridge. She said she would take me to hide in the mountains...\n\tWait... who is that person beside Beth... that face... isn't that Erica?! Didn't she already...\n\tThey are laughing... walking towards me... their faces are changing... becoming... just like... mine...",
    ["\n　　药量还是老样子，每日一次，禁止加量。上周你私自加量的事，不要再有第二次。\n　　心悸的频率没有下降，这是我目前最担心的，再这样下去，你的心脏撑不了多久了。\n       如果下次又半夜发作，别硬扛，不管几点，都要让约翰先生来找我。\n       霍克斯先生，我是你的医生，观察你是我的本分，这不是监视！如果你连我都开始怀疑，那恰恰说明，那东西对你的影响比我想的还要深，这让我很不安。\n　　下周四下午三点，我会准时到。希望那个时候，你还是我认识的那个霍克斯先生。"] = "\n\tThe dosage is the same as before, once a day, increasing the dose is prohibited. Do not let the incident where you privately increased the dose last week happen a second time.\n\tThe frequency of palpitations has not decreased, which is my biggest concern at the moment. If this continues, your heart won't last long.\n\tIf you have another episode in the middle of the night next time, don't try to tough it out. No matter what time it is, have Mr. John come find me.\n\tMr. Hawkes, I am your doctor; observing you is my duty, this is not surveillance! If you even start to doubt me, that just shows that the influence of that thing on you is even deeper than I thought, which makes me very uneasy.\n\tNext Thursday at 3:00 PM, I will arrive on time. I hope that by then, you are still the Mr. Hawkes I know.",
    ["\n　　让我猜猜……你肯定在想'这些牌到底怎么走'对不对？    \n　　放心，就算你不懂扑克，我也不会嘲笑你~\n 　　作为一个负责的主持人，我还是准备了这本宝典——《傻瓜都能懂的牌经》！\n\n 　　所谓<Letter_Highlight>顺子</>，就是连续的5个数字，比如：4-5-6-7-8。\n 　　明白了吗？必须一个跟一个，不能跳着来！也<Letter_Highlight>不能反悔！</>\n\n 　　花色？在这里，爱情不分种族~红心、黑桃、方块、梅花，混着来都行！\n 　　重要的只有<Letter_Highlight>数字顺序</>，记住了吗？\n\n 　　如果你踩错了……嘻嘻，你会摔下去，摔下去，再摔下去！\n\n 　　——爱你的解说员，小丑 敬上"] = "\n\tLet me guess... you must be thinking 'how do these cards even work', right?    \n\tDon't worry, even if you don't understand poker, I won't laugh at you~\n \tAs a responsible host, I have prepared this treasure book—\"The Card Sutra Even a Fool Can Understand\"!\n\n \tA so-called <Letter_Highlight>Straight</> is 5 consecutive numbers, for example: 4-5-6-7-8.\n \tUnderstand? They must be one after another, you can't skip! And you <Letter_Highlight>cannot take it back!</>\n\n \tSuits? Here, love knows no race~ Hearts, Spades, Diamonds, Clubs, mixing them is fine!\n \tThe only thing that matters is the <Letter_Highlight>numerical order</>, got it?\n\n \tIf you step wrong... hehe, you will fall down, fall down, and fall down again!\n\n \t—Yours truly, the commentator, Clown",
    ["\n　　该死的皮诺亚欺骗了我！\n\n　　他拿走了我整整3金镑，却没有替我通过考试！\n\n　　该死的老鼠！小偷！我绝对不会放过他！"] = "\n\tThat damn Pinoia deceived me!\n\n\tHe took 3 pounds from me, but didn't help me pass the exam!\n\n\tDamn rat! Thief! I will never let him go!",
    ["\n　　购买人：艾德温·霍克斯男爵\n　　出售方：<Hide id=\"#157\">夜鸦收藏会</>\n　　交易物品：<Hide id=\"#157\">疑思之镜</>\n　　年代：距今约八百年\n　　已知效果：\n　　佩戴后，可短暂提升观察力与记忆能力。持有者能够注意到常人难以察觉的细节，发现环境中的异常信息、矛盾与隐藏线索。\n\n　          <Letter_Highlight> ————警告————</>                        \n　　长期使用后，可能出现以下症状：\n　　持续性的被窥视感。对自身记忆产生怀疑。认知混乱。偶尔察觉视野边缘出现并不存在的人影。\n　　本组织不对使用者产生的任何精神异常负责。若出现严重症状，请立即停止使用并销毁该物品。\n\n<Note_Normal_HW>它让我看到了一些本不该知道的事。</>\n<Note_Normal_HW>好像，有什么东西跟随它进入了宅邸。</>"] = "\n\tPurchaser: Baron Edwin Hawkes\n\tSeller: <Hide id=\"#157\">Night Raven Collection Society</>\n\tTraded Item: <Hide id=\"#157\">Mirror of Suspicion</>\n\tAge: Approximately eight hundred years old\n\tKnown Effects:\n\tAfter wearing it, it can briefly enhance observation and memory. The holder can notice details that are difficult for ordinary people to perceive, discovering abnormal information, contradictions, and hidden clues in the environment.\n\n\t          <Letter_Highlight> ————Warning————</>                        \n\tAfter long-term use, the following symptoms may appear:\n\tA persistent feeling of being watched. Doubts about one's own memory. Cognitive confusion. Occasionally perceiving figures that do not exist in the periphery of vision.\n\tThis organization is not responsible for any mental abnormalities caused by the user. If severe symptoms appear, please stop using it immediately and destroy the item.\n\n<Note_Normal_HW>It made me see some things I shouldn't have known.</>\n<Note_Normal_HW>It seems like something followed it into the mansion.</>",
    ["\n　　这一年的最后一天，森林遭遇了百年未遇的暴雪，猫头鹰长老召集起了一场紧急会议。\n\n　　 “北边山洞上方的积雪发生了崩塌，那里面还住着冬眠的蝙蝠一家，我们不能放着它们不管。”\n\n　　所有的动物都沉默了，它们基本不和蝙蝠来往，只有邓恩在去年春天去过那个洞穴，但它早就忘记里面什么样了。\n\n　　“我们去吧！”戴莉跳到了鹿角顶端，“就算你在里面迷失了方向，我的歌声也能把我们带到正确的道路上。”\n\n　　它们就这样进入了洞穴，里面结构错综复杂，邓恩和戴莉费了不少力气才找到受伤的蝙蝠一家。就在它们准备离开洞穴的时候，外面狂风大作，无数雪花被风裹挟而来，挡住了所有的光。邓恩又尝试了几个方向，比找不到出口更令人绝望的是蝙蝠一家越来越微弱的呼吸。\n\n　　戴莉飞到了它耳边开始歌唱，金色的旋律指引抚平了邓恩有些焦躁的心情，他沿着音符亮起的方向走去。十米，五十米，一百米……眼前仍然没有出现洞口的光亮，戴莉意识到前往出口的代价可能比想象中更多。\n\n　　没有犹豫。\n\n　　它飞得更高了，飞到邓恩根本看不清的地方，歌唱到背上的羽毛所剩无几，她开始下坠。\n\n　　眼前还是没有出现光亮。"] = "\n\tOn the last day of this year, the forest encountered a blizzard unseen in a hundred years, and the owl elder convened an emergency meeting.\n\n\t \"The snow above the cave in the north has collapsed, and a family of hibernating bats still lives inside. We cannot just leave them alone.\"\n\n\tAll the animals were silent; they basically didn't associate with bats. Only Dunn had been to that cave last spring, but he had long forgotten what it looked like inside.\n\n\t\"Let's go!\" Daly jumped to the top of the antlers, \"Even if you lose your way inside, my singing can lead us to the right path.\"\n\n\tThey entered the cave just like that. The structure inside was intricate, and it took Dunn and Daly quite a bit of effort to find the injured bat family. Just as they were preparing to leave the cave, a violent storm raged outside, and countless snowflakes were carried by the wind, blocking all light. Dunn tried a few more directions, and what was more desperate than not finding the exit was the increasingly weak breathing of the bat family.\n\n\tDaly flew to his ear and began to sing. The golden melody guided and smoothed out Dunn's somewhat restless mood, and he walked along the direction where the notes lit up. Ten meters, fifty meters, one hundred meters... there was still no light from the cave entrance in sight. Daly realized that the cost of reaching the exit might be more than imagined.\n\n\tWithout hesitation.\n\n\tIt flew higher, flying to a place where Dunn couldn't see clearly at all, singing until there were few feathers left on its back, and she began to fall.\n\n\tThere was still no light in sight.",
    ["\n　　这地方太邪门了。已经失踪三个人了，寻宝队的其他人居然还要继续？他们有病吧？\n　　想不通，真的想不通。为什么这么多人发现怪事还不跑？考古的、勘探的、寻宝的……他们不要命了吗？\n　　算了，罗塞尔大帝曾说过，人各有命——我先逃了。顺着这条河划出去，然后找个教堂住下，天天祷告直到这邪门的事过去。\n　　再见了！这见鬼的霍纳奇斯山！"] = "\n\tThis place is too evil. Three people have already gone missing, and the rest of the treasure hunting team still wants to continue? Are they sick?\n\tI can't figure it out, I really can't figure it out. Why do so many people see strange things and still not run? Archaeologists, surveyors, treasure hunters... don't they want to live?\n\tForget it, Emperor Roselle once said, everyone has their own fate—I'm escaping first. I'll row out along this river, then find a church to stay in, and pray every day until this evil thing passes.\n\tGoodbye! This godforsaken Hornacis Mountain!",
    ["\n　　邓恩和戴莉认识之后，戴莉就以“自己的羽毛掉光了，好冷”为理由在邓恩头上筑了巢，并为他重复每个被遗忘的信息；邓恩则载着它巡视森林，用厚厚的灰色皮毛为它挡风，用鹿角为它摘下最高处的浆果。\n\n　　戴莉喜欢趴在它脑袋靠后一些的位置，并时常抱怨它额前的毛发不够厚实。\n\n　　一天，戴莉发现邓恩从地上捡起来什么东西，固定在角上后它发现是自己掉落的羽毛。\n\n 　　“这些羽毛太美了，我舍不得它们就这样被遗忘。”邓恩甩了甩头，“即使我明天就会忘记为什么要这么做，但我的角会记得这种发痒的感觉。”\n\n　　戴莉的心轻轻颤动，她激动地盘旋在邓恩的两角之间，准备一展歌喉抖落几根崭新的羽毛。邓恩阻止了它这种会让自己更冷的行为，请它帮忙整理那些收集好的羽毛。戴莉将它们和一个个木牌挂在一起，让它们在风雪中碰撞，与鹿蹄声和鸟鸣声组成森林的曲调。"] = "\n\tAfter Dunn and Daly met, Daly built a nest on Dunn's head on the grounds that \"my feathers have fallen out, it's so cold,\" and repeated every forgotten piece of information for him; Dunn carried it to patrol the forest, using his thick gray fur to block the wind for it, and using his antlers to pick berries from the highest places.\n\n\tDaly liked to lie on the back of its head and often complained that the hair on its forehead wasn't thick enough.\n\n\tOne day, Daly saw Dunn pick something up from the ground, and after fixing it on its antlers, it discovered it was the feathers it had dropped.\n\n \t\"These feathers are too beautiful, I can't bear for them to be forgotten like this.\" Dunn shook his head, \"Even if I forget why I'm doing this tomorrow, my antlers will remember this itchy feeling.\"\n\n\tDaly's heart trembled gently. It circled excitedly between Dunn's two antlers, preparing to show off its voice and shake off a few brand-new feathers. Dunn stopped this behavior that would make it even colder and asked it to help organize the collected feathers. Daly hung them together with wooden signs, letting them collide in the wind and snow, forming the forest's tune with the sound of deer hooves and bird chirps.",
    ["\n　　银雾森林迎来了今年的第一场雪，东边的雾气也越发浓厚，掉落了不少羽毛的戴莉在窝里冻得直发抖。枝头小小的巢穴无法抵御寒冷，顶上抖落的一坨雪将巢穴砸落下去，戴莉还没来得及发出叫声，就发现自己被温暖的灰色皮毛包裹——它落在了一只灰麋鹿的头顶。\n\n 　　“我察觉到这里有动物需要帮助，是你吗？”那只灰麋鹿这么说道。\n\n 　　“如果你是来给我带来温暖的，那确实是我。”恢复了体温的戴莉在麋鹿的头顶蹦跶了几下，继续说道：“我叫戴莉， 你的名字是什么？”\n\n　　 “我是……抱歉，我忘记了我的名字。”\n\n　　戴莉这才注意到，麋鹿的角上挂着许多小木牌，上面写着“我叫邓恩”、我是森林的守护者”、“每天巡逻看谁需要帮助”……\n\n　　 “你叫邓恩，”戴莉轻声说，她听树洞里的松鼠一家提起过这头每到冬天就会失忆的麋鹿，曾一天给他们送了三次松子，“你是银雾森林的守护者。”"] = "\n\tThe Silver Mist Forest welcomed the first snow of the year, and the fog in the east became thicker. Daly, who had lost many feathers, was shivering in the nest from the cold. The small nest on the branch couldn't resist the cold, and a clump of snow shaken from the top knocked the nest down. Before Daly could even make a sound, it found itself wrapped in warm gray fur—it had landed on the top of a gray elk's head.\n\n \t\"I sensed that an animal here needed help, is it you?\" The gray elk said so.\n\n \t\"If you are here to bring me warmth, then it is indeed me.\" Daly, having recovered its body temperature, hopped a few times on the elk's head and continued: \"My name is Daly, what is your name?\"\n\n\t \"I am... sorry, I forgot my name.\"\n\n\tOnly then did Daly notice that many small wooden signs were hanging on the elk's antlers, with things written on them like \"My name is Dunn\", \"I am the Guardian of the forest\", \"Patrol every day to see who needs help\"...\n\n\t \"Your name is Dunn,\" Daly said softly. It had heard the squirrel family in the tree hole mention this elk that would lose its memory every winter and had once sent them pine nuts three times in one day, \"You are the Guardian of the Silver Mist Forest.\"",
    ["\n《女士审美》（第六号至十一号刊 合集）　　订购人：克莉丝汀\n\n《漆黑的管家》精装典藏版 　　订购人：塞巴斯蒂安\n\n《调教的艺术》入门至精进三卷 　　订购<Hide stylename=\"Transparent\" id=\"#161\">口口口口口</>"] = "\n\"Ladies' Aesthetics\" (Issues 6 to 11 Collection) Purchaser: Christine\n\n\"The Pitch-Black Butler\" Hardcover Collector's Edition Purchaser: Sebastian\n\n\"The Art of Discipline\" Introductory to Advanced Three Volumes Purchaser: <Hide stylename=\"Transparent\" id=\"#161\">XXXXX</>",
    ["\n《廷根酒徒威廉与血腥奇遇记：身为醉酒无赖的他发现廷根的吸血鬼巢穴，他的房东还有城中的工厂大王与银行家实际上是吸血鬼；讲述他如何独力以木桩刺穿吸血鬼的贪利之心，由此成为鲁恩最负盛名的吸血鬼猎人的故事》\n\n作者：克利夫·威廉\n\n<Letter_Highlight_HW>能火！！！</>\n\n该死的巴兹尔，到处说我坏话，你只能活两个章节！\n<Hide stylename=\"Transparent\" id=\"#161\">这一段内容是编的这一段内容是编的这一段</>\n<Delete id=\"#158\">猫不会说话。</>\n<Delete id=\"#158\">鸽子也是。</>"] = "\n\"Tingen Drunkard William and the Bloody Adventure: As a drunken rogue, he discovers a vampire nest in Tingen; his landlord and the city's factory tycoon and banker are actually vampires; telling the story of how he single-handedly pierces the vampires' greed with a wooden stake, thus becoming Loen's most renowned vampire hunter\"\n\nAuthor: Cliff William\n\n<Letter_Highlight_HW>It will be a hit!!!</>\n\nDamn Basil, talking bad about me everywhere, you can only live for two chapters!\n<Hide stylename=\"Transparent\" id=\"#161\">This part of the content is made up this part of the content is made up this</>\n<Delete id=\"#158\">Cats cannot talk.</>\n<Delete id=\"#158\">Neither can pigeons.</>",
    ["\n《我最喜欢的事情》\n我最喜欢在上课的时候闭上眼睛，因为很舒服。眼睛前面<Hide id=\"#157\">甲</>黑乎乎的，耳朵里面也黑乎乎的。\n拉夫老师说，起来！上课不许睡觉。\n原来我最喜欢的事情是上课<Hide id=\"#157\">睡</>垂觉。"] = "\n\"My Favorite Thing\"\nI like to close my eyes during class the most because it's very comfortable. In front of my eyes it's <Hide id=\"#157\">A</> pitch black, and inside my ears it's also pitch black.\nTeacher Ruff says, get up! No sleeping in class.\nSo my favorite thing is <Hide id=\"#157\">sleep</>ing in class.",
    ["\n《我最喜欢的事情》\n我最喜欢的事，呃，这不能说啊！\n走在成长的道路上，注定要背负很多秘密……\n拉夫老师，别怪我。\n等你收卷，我就要做最喜欢的事情了。"] = "\n\"My Favorite Thing\"\nMy favorite thing, uh, I can't say that!\nWalking on the road of growth, I am destined to carry many secrets...\nTeacher Ruff, don't blame me.\nWhen you collect the papers, I will do my favorite thing.",
    ["\n一\n次\n机\n会"] = "\nA\n\nChance",
    ["\n一段时间不见，有想我吗？\n我是上个冬天来到这里的灰色花猫，最爱睡在集市的丝瓜筐里。\n我想对帮过我的人说，谢谢你们。\n如果没有那些碎肉和剩鱼，我早就长不大啦。\n最近，我住进了村口的稻草房子里，也有了新的名字。\n我叫<Letter_Highlight_HW>毛毛草</>，再见面的时候，请叫我的名字吧。\n谢谢你们！"] = "\nIt's been a while, have you missed me?\nI am the gray cat that came here last winter, and I love sleeping in the loofah basket at the market the most.\nI want to say to those who have helped me, thank you.\nIf it weren't for those scraps of meat and leftover fish, I wouldn't have grown up.\nRecently, I moved into the straw house at the entrance of the village and have a new name.\nMy name is <Letter_Highlight_HW>Fuzzy Grass</>, when we meet again, please call my name.\nThank you all!",
    ["\n专治疑难杂症，诊金低廉，医术高超！\n\n现<Highlight>主治病症</>包括但不限于：\n\n<Highlight>止小儿夜啼</>、<Highlight>治挑食多动</>、<Highlight>助力智力发育</>、\n<Highlight>祛痘除癣</>、<Highlight>清除腋下足底异味</>、<Highlight>防治瘟疫</>、\n<Highlight>老鼠害虫扑杀</>、<Highlight>野猫野狗驱逐</>、<Highlight>住家环境布置</>、\n<Highlight>菜园杂草清除</>、<Highlight>廷根市再就业培训</>等。\n\n行医四十年，业务纯熟，值得信赖！"] = "\nSpecializing in difficult and miscellaneous diseases, low consultation fees, superb medical skills!\n\nCurrently <Highlight>treating conditions</> include but are not limited to:\n\n<Highlight>Stopping children's night crying</>, <Highlight>curing picky eating and hyperactivity</>, <Highlight>aiding intellectual development</>,\n<Highlight>removing acne and ringworm</>, <Highlight>clearing underarm and foot odors</>, <Highlight>preventing and treating plagues</>,\n<Highlight>rat and pest extermination</>, <Highlight>stray cat and dog expulsion</>, <Highlight>home environment layout</>,\n<Highlight>vegetable garden weed removal</>, <Highlight>Tingen City re-employment training</>, etc.\n\nPracticing medicine for forty years, business is skilled, trustworthy!",
    ["\n为\n什\n么\n？"] = "\nWhy\n\n?",
    ["\n为庆祝战争胜利，\n\n本俱乐部为每位新加入的会员免费提供100枚子弹！\n\n老会员每介绍一位新人加入，可获得30枚子弹！\n\n每月将举行一场射击比赛，\n\n获胜者可免除当月会费！\n\n愿女神庇佑您与您爱的人。"] = "\nTo celebrate the victory of the war,\n\nThis club provides 100 Bullets for free to every new member!\n\nOld members can receive 30 Bullets for every new member they introduce!\n\nA shooting competition will be held every month,\n\nWinners can be exempted from that month's membership fee!\n\nMay the Goddess Protection be with you and your loved ones.",
    ["\n为确保游客的人身安全，采摘期间，请务必遵守以下规则。\n1.苹果是一种圆形的红色水果，表皮光滑，口感甜脆。请不要采摘苹果之外的东西。\n2.如果你看见苹果上长出稻谷，请立即远离，并寻找看守人员。\n<Delete id=\"#158\">3.长出小麦是正常的，请放心品尝。</>\n4.请注意，苹果不会长出任何人体组织。\n5.如果你服用了长出稻谷或器官的苹果，不要尝试呕吐，请立即寻找看守人员。\n6.本告示共有五条。\n0.欢迎大家前来湖心岛果园品尝苹果！"] = "\nTo ensure the personal safety of tourists, please strictly follow the rules below during picking.\n1. An apple is a round red fruit with smooth skin and a sweet and crisp taste. Please do not pick anything other than apples.\n2. If you see rice growing on an apple, please stay away immediately and find the security personnel.\n<Delete id=\"#158\">3. It is normal for wheat to grow, please feel free to taste it.</>\n4. Please note that apples will not grow any human tissue.\n5. If you have consumed an apple with rice or organs growing on it, do not try to vomit, please find the security personnel immediately.\n6. This notice has five items.\n0. Welcome everyone to come to the Lake Island Orchard to taste apples!",
    ["\n为鲜花停留的人，\n赞美你的好奇心！\n请随意取用车上的花朵，\n我会派人定期来补货。\n希望花朵的色彩，\n能让你繁忙的生活开心一点。"] = "\nTo those who stop for flowers,\nI praise your curiosity!\nFeel free to take the flowers from the cart,\nI will send someone to restock regularly.\nI hope the colors of the flowers,\ncan make your busy life a little happier.",
    ["\n主讲医师：康拉德医生\n地点：廷根大学大礼堂\n守护健康 保障安全 珍惜生命\n让医疗之光普惠廷根\n参与讲座可以在现场领取家用医疗包一份！\n无需入场费 | 欢迎全市朋友听讲 | 不提供餐饮"] = "\nKeynote Speaker: Dr. Conrad\nLocation: Tingen University Auditorium\nGuard Health, Ensure Safety, Cherish Life\nLet the light of medicine benefit all of Tingen\nParticipate in the lecture and receive a complimentary home medical kit on-site!\nNo admission fee | Friends from all over the city are welcome to attend | No food or drinks provided",
    ["\n五月庄园也出现异常   \n部分工人失踪\n庄园的“夫人”和“管家”\n也都是月亮仆从成员"] = "\nAn anomaly has also appeared at May Manor.\nSome workers have gone missing.\nThe manor's \"Mistress\" and \"Butler\"\nare both members of the Moon Servant.",
    ["\n亲爱的朋友们：\n　　你们读到这行字时，我大概正趴在甲板上抢救被狂暴海的巨浪打翻的芒果青柠酱。\n　　很高兴地告诉大家，我战时的灵感“黑麦朗姆弹壳泡芙”已经找到了绝佳的制作材料——因蒂斯南部的褐色李子，它们的甜度正好能中和朗姆的苦涩。\n　　我不久后就会回到鲁恩，真想快点将这一路上的冒险故事分享给你们！\n　　备注：如果邮差送来草垛扎着的木箱，请不要打开——那八成是我从某个岛上找到的变异蘑菇，能挤出牛奶，真是太神奇了。"] = "\nDear friends:\n　　By the time you read this, I am likely sprawled on the deck, desperately trying to save the mango-lime sauce that was overturned by the giant waves of the Berserk Sea.\n　　I am happy to tell you all that I have finally found the perfect ingredient for my wartime inspiration, the 'Rye Rum Shell Puff'—brown plums from southern Intis. Their sweetness is just enough to neutralize the bitterness of the rum.\n　　I will be returning to Loen soon, and I can't wait to share the adventure stories from this journey with you!\n　　Note: If the postman delivers a wooden crate tied with straw, please do not open it—it is most likely a mutated mushroom I found on some island. It can be squeezed to produce milk; it's truly magical.",
    ["\n今天苹果花开了，我摘了几朵放在你床边。 你说你喜欢这个味道， 所以我每年都会摘。\n\n不管发生什么，这里的花还会开， 妈妈也还会在。\n\n你只管好好睡， 等你醒来，一切都会好的。"] = "\nToday the apple blossoms bloomed, and I picked a few to place by your bedside. You said you liked this scent, so I pick them every year.\n\nNo matter what happens, the flowers here will bloom again, and Mother will still be here.\n\nYou just need to sleep well. When you wake up, everything will be fine.",
    ["\n今晚就把安迪埋了吧。\n他是好警察，也是个好卧底，替我给他带束花。\n上面的指示是，什么都别问，什么都别说。\n另外……要小心！"] = "\nLet's bury Andy tonight.\nHe was a good policeman and a good undercover agent. Bring a bouquet of flowers for him on my behalf.\nThe orders from above are: don't ask anything, don't say anything.\nAlso... be careful!",
    ["\n从前有一个小女孩，只有一只眼睛，没有妈妈。\n\n有一天，月亮送给她一只兔子。 兔子说：我帮你找妈妈。 小女孩说：好呀好呀。\n\n兔子找来了第一个妈妈， 把她变成了一只蝴蝶。 小女孩说：太好啦，蝴蝶妈妈不会跑走了。\n\n兔子又找来第二个，第三个，第四个…… 蝴蝶越来越多， 小女孩的口袋里装满了翅膀的声音。\n\n有人问她：你不难过吗？ 小女孩想了想，说： 难过的时候，我就数一数蝴蝶， 一只，两只，三只…… 数着数着就好了。\n\n【全文完】"] = "\nOnce upon a time, there was a little girl who had only one eye and no mother.\n\nOne day, the moon gave her a rabbit. The rabbit said: I will help you find your mother. The little girl said: Yay, yay.\n\nThe rabbit found the first mother and turned her into a butterfly. The little girl said: That's great, Butterfly Mother won't run away.\n\nThe rabbit found a second, a third, a fourth... There were more and more butterflies, and the little girl's pockets were filled with the sound of wings.\n\nSomeone asked her: Aren't you sad? The little girl thought for a moment and said: When I feel sad, I count the butterflies, one, two, three... and as I count, I feel better.\n\n[End of Story]",
    ["\n以女神之名，播撒慈爱之光\n\n<Letter_Highlight>食物供应</>\n黑面包和豌豆汤\n\n<Letter_Highlight>夜间庇护</>\n提供吊床或地铺\n\n<Letter_Highlight>工作机会</>\n简单易上手的劳动\n\n床位有限，需排队，最多入住五天"] = "\nIn the name of the Goddess, spreading the light of compassion\n\n<Letter_Highlight>Food Supply</>\nBlack bread and pea soup\n\n<Letter_Highlight>Night Shelter</>\nHammocks or floor mats provided\n\n<Letter_Highlight>Job Opportunities</>\nSimple and easy manual labor\n\nBeds are limited, queuing is required, maximum stay of five days",
    ["\n你\n接\n下\n来\n的\n表\n现"] = "\nYour\n\nPerformance\n\nNext",
    ["\n你看那床前洒落的\n莫非是秋霜的痕迹？\n不，我亲爱的朋友\n那是月亮投下的温柔低语\n\n我不禁抬起双眼\n凝视那轮皎洁\n________________\n________________"] = "\nLook at what is scattered by the bedside\nCould it be the traces of autumn frost?\nNo, my dear friend\nThat is the gentle whisper cast by the moon\n\nI cannot help but raise my eyes\nTo gaze at that bright orb\n________________\n________________",
    ["\n像这种窗子，\n关得不严实，\n趴在窗沿底下，\n就很容易听见……"] = "\nWindows like this,\nif not closed tightly,\nif you crouch under the windowsill,\nit's very easy to hear...",
    ["\n像这种门，\n锁芯从来不换，\n撬开一次，\n就能打开第二次。"] = "\nDoors like this,\nthe lock core is never changed.\nOnce picked,\nit can be opened a second time.",
    ["\n关于本品：\n本品为针对灵体的专项封印器具，对怨灵、执念型恶灵及强负面灵性体均有显著效力。\n价格不菲。效果对得起价格。\n\n\n负面反应说明：\n购入者注视镜面时，可能出现以下感受：\n持续的\"吸引感\"，难以移开视线\n无由来的落泪冲动\n想要打破镜子的念头\n以上均属正常。\n\n\n使用方法\n封印步骤：\n对准目标\n确保对方身影被镜面完整照到\n保持照射，持续时间越长，封印效果越稳定\n目标被完全封入镜中空间后，其灵性将被持续消耗、削弱，无法自行逃逸\n\n\n终结步骤：\n以魔镐敲击镜面，恶灵将被削弱力量后勾出，使用者可自行选择割喉亦或砍下其头部，使之被永久消灭。\n\n\n静置与保管\n不使用时，建议镜面朝内、背面朝外放置，或以厚布完全遮盖。\n\n\n附：\n请勿将其在无遮蔽状态下过夜放置。\n若已如此放置，次日请检查镜框内侧银片。\n若发现划痕——请确认划痕的方向。\n若为由外向内，属正常磨损。\n若为由里向外，请将镜面立即翻转，背面朝外，随后自行做仪式驱魔、净化处理。"] = "\nAbout this product:\nThis is a specialized sealing apparatus for spirits, highly effective against wraiths, obsession-type evil spirits, and entities with strong negative spirituality.\nIt is not cheap. The effect is worth the price.\n\n\nNegative Reaction Description:\nWhen the purchaser gazes into the mirror surface, they may experience the following:\nA continuous 'sense of attraction,' making it difficult to look away\nA sudden, inexplicable urge to weep\nThe thought of wanting to break the mirror\nAll of the above are normal.\n\n\nUsage Instructions\nSealing Steps:\nAim at the target\nEnsure the target's figure is fully reflected in the mirror\nMaintain the reflection; the longer the duration, the more stable the sealing effect\nOnce the target is completely sealed into the mirror space, its spirituality will be continuously consumed and weakened, making it unable to escape on its own\n\n\nFinish Steps:\nStrike the mirror surface with a magic pickaxe; the evil spirit will be weakened and drawn out. The user can then choose to slit its throat or decapitate it, causing it to be permanently destroyed.\n\n\nStorage and Maintenance\nWhen not in use, it is recommended to place the mirror face-in and back-out, or cover it completely with a thick cloth.\n\n\nAppendix:\nDo not leave it in an uncovered state overnight.\nIf it has been left this way, please check the silver foil on the inside of the mirror frame the next day.\nIf you find scratches—please check the direction of the scratches.\nIf they are from the outside in, it is normal wear and tear.\nIf they are from the inside out, please turn the mirror over immediately, back-out, and then perform your own ritual of exorcism and purification.",
    ["\n午夜俱乐部，排解你的午夜忧愁\n\n提供：歌舞、棋牌、台球、香醇美酒\n\n下午两时起接受当晚预订，会员包间需提前预约。"] = "\nMidnight Club, relieving your midnight sorrows\n\nOffers: Song and dance, chess and cards, billiards, mellow wine\n\nReservations for the evening are accepted starting at 2:00 PM; member private rooms require advance booking.",
    ["\n半高礼帽（黑）   一顶 …… 五苏勒六便士\n\n小　计  ……………… 五苏勒六便士\n新顾客折让  ………… 减  三 便士\n应　收  ………………五苏勒三便士\n\n收　到  ………………  六苏勒\n找　零  ………………  九便士\n\n· 礼帽如有褶皱、污渍，凭此单回店免费修整一次。\n· 非人为损坏，三日内可换。\n\n维尔克尔衣帽店"] = "\nHalf-top hat (black)   One …… 5 Sol 6 Pence\n\nSubtotal  ……………… 5 Sol 6 Pence\nNew Customer Discount  ………… Minus 3 Pence\nTotal Due  ……………… 5 Sol 3 Pence\n\nReceived  ………………  6 Sol\nChange  ………………  9 Pence\n\n· If the hat has creases or stains, bring this receipt back to the store for one free repair.\n· Non-human damage can be exchanged within three days.\n\nWilker Hat & Clothing Store",
    ["\n原谅我的不辞而别。\n今晚的吻已经让我失去了所有理智，\n如果继续待下去，我怕自己会做出更疯狂的事。\n但这样的相会太过草率，您值得更好的。\n三天后，午夜时分，郊外睡莲盛开的池塘边。\n届时，我会准备好一切……等您来品尝完整的我。"] = "\nForgive me for leaving without saying goodbye.\nThe kiss tonight has already made me lose all my reason,\nIf I stayed any longer, I fear I would do something even crazier.\nBut such a meeting was too hasty; you deserve better.\nThree days from now, at midnight, by the pond where the water lilies bloom in the suburbs.\nBy then, I will have everything ready... waiting for you to come and taste the complete me.",
    ["\n各位市民请注意，近日廷根市内邪教分子日益猖狂，请不要轻信异教言论！发现任何可疑的人和事，务必及时向警局或教会检举。\n\n\n<Delete id=\"#158\">只有那位主才能真正体恤凡人</>\n<Delete id=\"#158\">予汝福地，护汝安眠</>"] = "\nCitizens, please be aware that recently, cultists in Tingen have become increasingly rampant. Please do not easily trust heretical rhetoric! If you discover any suspicious people or matters, be sure to report them to the police or the church in a timely manner.\n\n\n<Delete id=\"#158\">Only that Lord can truly empathize with mortals</>\n<Delete id=\"#158\">Grant you a blessed land, protect your slumber</>",
    ["\n喜报！\n\n本季度已成功为廷根清除<Highlight>23,480</>只啮齿类公民！\n\n凡引荐五位邻居签约者，\n可额外获赠<Mark id=\"#159_R\">镀银捕鼠夹</>与《家庭防疫指南》烫金手册一册。\n\n切勿让这些长胡须的夜行盗贼继续玷污鲁恩王国的卫生荣光！"] = "\nGood News!\n\nThis quarter, we have successfully cleared <Highlight>23,480</> rodent citizens for Tingen!\n\nAnyone who refers five neighbors to sign up\nwill receive an additional <Mark id=\"#159_R\">Silver-Plated Mousetrap</> and a gold-stamped copy of the 'Family Epidemic Prevention Guide'.\n\nDo not let these long-whiskered nocturnal thieves continue to tarnish the sanitary glory of the Loen Kingdom!",
    ["\n嗨，小猫。\n　　一月不见，我猜你是陷入了那不知要花多久的“沉睡”。\n　　我马上会毕业离开霍伊大学，但作为一个信守诺言的男人，我亲手为你的苏醒准备了盛大的晚宴！我的父亲终于默许了我做饭的爱好，不管他认为这有多不体面。\n　　而这都要归功于你，我亲爱的朋友，在你挑剔舌头的点评后，我才终于敢把食物端给其他人。和你在一起的时光是那么纯粹，即使是纯粹的难吃，也让我无比想念。我父亲给我准备了精美厨具，但我还是更喜欢咱们破烂的简易灶台。\n　　等你苏醒！就直接来我家吧！\n　　我刚学会做新的因蒂斯酱烤小牛扒！迫不及待想让你尝尝味道了！\n　　期待你赶快醒来，我信赖的美食品鉴官。"] = "\nHi, kitten.\n　　It's been a month, and I guess you've fallen into that 'slumber' that I don't know how long will take.\n　　I will be graduating and leaving Hoy University soon, but as a man who keeps his promises, I have personally prepared a grand banquet for your awakening! My father has finally tacitly approved of my hobby of cooking, regardless of how unseemly he thinks it is.\n　　And all of this is thanks to you, my dear friend. It was only after your critical tongue's reviews that I finally dared to serve food to others. The time spent with you was so pure; even the pure bad taste makes me miss it immensely. My father prepared exquisite kitchenware for me, but I still prefer our broken, simple stove.\n　　When you wake up! Just come straight to my house!\n　　I just learned how to make a new Intis sauce-roasted veal steak! I can't wait for you to taste it!\n　　Looking forward to you waking up soon, my trusted food critic.",
    ["\n嘻哈哈\n哈哈哈哈哈...\n哈哈哈哈哈哈哈...\n哈哈哈哈哈哈哈哈...！"] = "\nHehehe\nHahahahaha...\nHahahahahahaha...\nHahahahahahahaha...!",
    ["\n因演员曼妮身体原因，话剧《背叛者指环》以下场次的演出将进行演员变更\n\n演出时间 1354年 6月19日 下午2点\n\n原：曼妮 海尔顿\n现：莉莉娅 海尔顿"] = "\nDue to actress Manny's health reasons, the following performances of the play 'The Traitor's Ring' will have a cast change\n\nPerformance Time: June 19, 1354, 2:00 PM\n\nOriginal: Manny Helton\nNew: Lilia Helton",
    ["\n基酒：\n● 冰原黑麦酒（弗萨克北境特产） —— 3份\n● 高纯度雪岭蒸馏烈酒 —— 2份\n香料与药草：\n● 冻原杜松子 —— 一小把（约12颗）\n● 极北苔藓浸液 —— 数滴\n● 冰霜薄荷叶 —— 3片\n● 熏烤橡木炭片 —— 少许\n秘制添加：\n● 蜂蜜糖浆（用于中和烈性） —— 半匙\n● 雪水融化液 —— 适量\n\n金秋湖，我的家乡。\n那里有老查克的酒馆， 有小柯莱的菜园， 有我熟悉的每一条路。\n以此旅行途中所得配方，献给老查克，实现我们的约定。\n——记于1284年秋天 帕利诺"] = "\nBase Liquor:\n● Icefield Rye Whiskey (Specialty of the Northern Feynapotter) —— 3 parts\n● High-purity Snow Ridge Distilled Spirit —— 2 parts\nSpices and Herbs:\n● Tundra Juniper Berries —— A small handful (about 12)\n● Far North Moss Infusion —— A few drops\n● Frost Mint Leaves —— 3 leaves\n● Smoked Oak Charcoal Chips —— A pinch\nSecret Additions:\n● Honey Syrup (used to neutralize the strength) —— Half a spoon\n● Melted Snow Water —— Appropriate amount\n\nGolden Autumn Lake, my hometown.\nThere is Old Chuck's tavern, Little Cole's vegetable garden, and every road I am familiar with.\nWith the recipe obtained during this trip, I dedicate it to Old Chuck to fulfill our promise.\n——Recorded in the autumn of 1284, Palino",
    ["\n夜总会里，邦尼为女孩戴上项链。\n她笑得很温柔，说这项链名为“自由”。\n女孩浑然不知，“自由”的另一头。\n一直攥在邦尼手里。"] = "\nAt the Nightclub, Bonnie puts a necklace on the girl.\nShe smiles very gently and says this necklace is called \"Freedom.\"\nThe girl is completely unaware that the other end of \"Freedom\"\nhas always been held in Bonnie's hand.",
    ["\n大家在问：\n%s"] = "\n Everyone is asking: \n%s",
    ["\n女神没有回应我的祈祷，天一刻也不暗下来，我无法入眠。\n\n镇上的大家好像都不用睡觉，也许是我出了问题。\n\n其他地方也许就不一样了吧？"] = "\nThe Goddess did not respond to my prayer. The sky never gets dark, and I cannot fall into slumber.\n\nEveryone in town seems not to need sleep; perhaps something is wrong with me.\n\nMaybe it's different in other places?",
    ["\n她和他、他和她、<Hide stylename=\"Transparent\" id=\"#161\">她和她、他和他、</>\n缠绵悱恻的爱情故事，尽在廷根大剧院！\n\n\n<Note_Normal_HW>**的，谁把后面的字涂掉了，我就爱看这个！</>\n\n<Note_Normal_HW>算了吧，老兄，这附近还有小屁孩呢，而且你真有钱去买廷根大剧院的票？</>\n\n<Note_Normal_HW>说得好像附近的小屁孩有几个认识字一样！</>"] = "\nShe and he, he and she, <Hide stylename=\"Transparent\" id=\"#161\">she and she, he and he,</>\npassionate love stories, all at the Tingen Grand Theater!\n\n\n<Note_Normal_HW>** of it, whoever scribbled out the words at the back, I love watching this!</>\n\n<Note_Normal_HW>Forget it, buddy, there are kids nearby, and do you really have the money to buy a ticket to the Tingen Grand Theater?</>\n\n<Note_Normal_HW>As if any of the kids nearby know how to read!</>",
    ["\n寻找通体褐色，遍布花纹，背部有花瓣形斑纹的狸花猫“毛球”\n\n如有线索，请送至<Mark id=\"#159\">豪尔斯街35号</>\n\n线索酬金：<Letter_Highlight_HW>1金镑</>\n寻回酬金：<Letter_Highlight_HW>10金镑</>"] = "\nLooking for a brown, patterned tabby cat named 'Furball' with petal-shaped markings on its back\n\nIf you have any clues, please send them to <Mark id=\"#159\">35 Howls Street</>\n\nClue Reward: <Letter_Highlight_HW>1 Pound</>\nRecovery Reward: <Letter_Highlight_HW>10 Pounds</>",
    ["\n寻猫：米莎\n灰色条纹，四脚雪白，左耳有一小缺口。性格胆小。于佐特兰街附近走失。若有线索，请联络磨坊街17号布兰登家，有重金酬谢。\n\n<Letter_Highlight_HW>您可以去佐特兰街36号2楼的黑荆棘安保公司，上次我的小狗泡芙走丢了两个月，他们半天就找回来了！</>"] = "\nLost Cat: Misha\nGray stripes, four white paws, small notch in the left ear. Timid personality. Lost near Zoutland Street. If you have any clues, please contact the Brandon family at 17 Mill Street. A generous reward is offered.\n\n<Letter_Highlight_HW>You can go to the Blackthorn Security Company on the 2nd floor of 36 Zoutland Street. Last time my puppy Puff went missing for two months, they found him in half a day!</>",
    ["\n寻猫：米莎\n灰色条纹，四脚雪白，左耳有一小缺口。性格胆小。于佐特兰街附近走失。若有线索，请联络磨坊街17号布兰登家，有重金酬谢。\n\n<Letter_Highlight_HW>米莎！好可爱的名字！我前天在花廊最靠外面的长椅下看到过一只灰色的小猫影子，但没看清。它会不会喜欢这里的花香？祝你早点找到它！0w0</>\n<Letter_Highlight_HW>—— 一个爱猫的路人</>"] = "\nLost Cat: Misha\nGray stripes, four white paws, small notch in the left ear. Timid personality. Lost near Zoutland Street. If you have any clues, please contact the Brandon family at 17 Mill Street. A generous reward is offered.\n\n<Letter_Highlight_HW>Misha! What a cute name! I saw a shadow of a small gray cat under the outermost bench at the flower gallery the day before yesterday, but I didn't see it clearly. Would it like the scent of the flowers here? Hope you find it soon! 0w0</>\n<Letter_Highlight_HW>—— A cat-loving passerby</>",
    ["\n寻猫：米莎\n灰色条纹，四脚雪白，左耳有一小缺口。性格胆小。于佐特兰街附近走失。若有线索，请联络磨坊街17号布兰登家，有重金酬谢。\n\n<Letter_Highlight_HW>重金？有多重？（我开玩笑的！）</>\n<Letter_Highlight_HW>说真的，去问问这附近有个什么能找东西的公司。他们上次帮我找回了钥匙，快得邪门。就说是奥利安娜太太的朋友介绍的，没准儿给你折扣。</>"] = "\nLost Cat: Misha\nGray stripes, four white paws, small notch in the left ear. Timid personality. Lost near Zoutland Street. If you have any clues, please contact the Brandon family at 17 Mill Street. A generous reward is offered.\n\n<Letter_Highlight_HW>Generous reward? How generous? (I'm joking!)</>\n<Letter_Highlight_HW>Seriously, go ask around for some company nearby that can find things. They helped me find my keys last time, it was freakishly fast. Just say you were referred by Mrs. Orianna's friend, maybe they'll give you a discount.</>",
    ["\n尊敬的客人：\n　　您好。\n　　本包厢现已开启私人仪式。 内有贵宾正在与玫瑰进行深度交流。\n　　非受邀者请勿敲门、请勿窥探、请勿倾听。 惊扰沉醉中的灵魂，将被视为对花园的亵渎。"] = "\nRespected Guest:\n　　Greetings.\n　　This private room has now initiated a private ritual. A distinguished guest is currently having a deep exchange with the roses inside.\n　　Non-invitees, please do not knock, do not peek, and do not listen. Disturbing a soul in intoxication will be considered a desecration of the garden.",
    ["\n尊敬的市民，为了您的安全，请勿擅自进入施工地带。\n\n\n新增：\n如果您有需要，请在不慎掉入坑内后高呼救命。\n如果一刻钟内没人赶到，请保持情绪镇定与体力充足。\n不必焦急，我们将在上班时间将您救出。\n\n<Note_Normal_HW>这玩意儿根本没用，这个月已经掉进去十几个人了。</>\n<Note_Normal_HW>天知道把这些家伙捞出来多麻烦！还是派个人守着吧。</>"] = "\nRespected citizens, for your safety, please do not enter the construction zone without authorization.\n\n\nNew Addition:\nIf you have a need, please shout for help after accidentally falling into the pit.\nIf no one arrives within a quarter of an hour, please remain calm and conserve your energy.\nDo not be anxious; we will rescue you during working hours.\n\n<Note_Normal_HW>This thing is completely useless; over a dozen people have already fallen in this month.</>\n<Note_Normal_HW>Heaven knows how much trouble it is to fish these guys out! Better just send someone to guard it.</>",
    ["\n尊贵的市民请注意:  \n敝司以科学精神与公共卫生之名义，\n郑重收购各类啮齿类恶徒\n——无论灰须流寇或黑尾叛党！\n\n<Highlight>*蒸汽动力啮齿类无害化处理箱*</>\n誓将每只阴沟暴君转化为鲁恩王国文明进步的养料！\n\n酬金如下：\n- 完整鼠尾二分之一便士\n- 鲜活样本三便士（附赠镀锡铁皮尊严终结舱） \n\n瘟疫与烦恼，一网打尽！"] = "\nRespected citizens, please note: \nOur company, in the name of scientific spirit and public health,\nsolemnly acquires all kinds of rodent villains\n—whether gray-whiskered bandits or black-tailed rebels!\n\n<Highlight>*Steam-Powered Rodent Neutralization Box*</>\nSwearing to transform every sewer tyrant into nourishment for the civilized progress of the Loen Kingdom!\n\nRewards are as follows:\n- Complete rat tail: 1/2 penny\n- Live specimen: 3 pence (includes a tin-plated Dignity Termination Chamber)\n\nPlagues and troubles, caught in one net!",
    ["\n尊贵的市民阁下，\n若您正为家中猖獗的啮齿类入侵者所困扰，\n请允许敝公司向您呈献本纪元最富人道主义的解决方案！\n\n敝司独创的<Highlight>*蒸汽动力啮齿类无害化处理箱*</>，\n采用专利消毒工艺与黄铜捕笼装置，\n每日<Highlight>中午</>由戴徽章制服的绅士专员上门服务。\n\n凡向本司移交老鼠者，\n不仅可获市政厅表彰的<Highlight>“廷根卫生大使”</>勋章，\n每只完整个体更可兑换三便士酬金！\n\n注：尾巴缺损者折半，幼崽按葡萄干布丁原料价收购"] = "\nRespected citizen,\nIf you are troubled by rampant rodent invaders in your home,\nplease allow our company to present you with the most humanitarian solution of this era!\n\nOur company's original <Highlight>*Steam-Powered Rodent Neutralization Box*</>,\nutilizes patented disinfection technology and a brass cage device,\nwith door-to-door service provided daily at <Highlight>noon</> by gentleman agents in uniform with badges.\n\nAnyone who hands over rats to our company\nwill not only receive the <Highlight>'Tingen Hygiene Ambassador'</> medal awarded by City Hall,\nbut each complete specimen can also be exchanged for a 3-penny reward!\n\nNote: Those with missing tails are half-price; pups are purchased at the price of raisin pudding ingredients",
    ["\n少年人啊！\n莫让智慧之火熄灭于指间！\n\n凡获得学校通知书却无力支付学费者，\n鲁恩慈善助学基金会将助您求学。\n\n申请资格：\n须持教区推荐信或学校录取通知书、家庭工薪证明\n\n申请方式：\n将自荐信投递于<Highlight>当地黑夜教堂</>处"] = "\nYoung people!\nDo not let the fire of wisdom be extinguished between your fingers!\n\nAnyone who has received a school admission notice but cannot afford the tuition,\nthe Loen Charity Scholarship Foundation will help you with your studies.\n\nApplication Qualifications:\nMust hold a parish recommendation letter or school admission notice, and family income proof\n\nApplication Method:\nSubmit your self-recommendation letter to the <Highlight>local Evernight Church</>",
    ["\n尼尔说这条路他走过七次。\n一路上，他说了三遍。我不信——如果他真的走过七次，为什么连帐篷都不会搭？我蹲在他身后，看他第三次把帐篷布穿反，雪水渗进手套，冷得像在舔我的骨头。\n万幸，我们在天黑前支起了帐篷。\n\n剩余物资：\n面包6份      佩姬给我们准备了18磅，分成了8份\n肉干和肉肠5份\n糖1罐\n黄油4块\n酒3瓶        晚上庆祝，消耗1瓶\n水5瓶        暂时充足，不过路上可以留意水源\n\n\n我想起来，在上山的路上我和尼尔还碰到一个奇怪的人——一个什么装备都没有带，穿着整齐西装的男子，看样子四十来岁，很有气质，眼睛是深蓝色的，很好看。\n我很少会注意一个人的眼睛，但从见到他开始，我就一直盯着他眼睛看，我从他的瞳孔中看到了我的影子。\n他友好地向我们询问下山的路，我指给他我们来时的路。"] = "\nNeil said he has walked this road seven times.\nAlong the way, he said it three times. I don't believe it—if he really had walked it seven times, why couldn't he even set up a tent? I crouched behind him, watching him put the tent fabric on backward for the third time. Snow water seeped into my gloves, cold enough to feel like it was licking my bones.\nFortunately, we set up the tent before dark.\n\nRemaining supplies:\nBread 6 portions      Peggy prepared 18 pounds for us, divided into 8 portions\nBeef jerky and sausages 5 portions\nSugar 1 jar\nButter 4 blocks\nWine 3 bottles        Celebrating tonight, consumed 1 bottle\nWater 5 bottles        Currently sufficient, but we can keep an eye out for water sources on the road\n\n\nI remember, on the way up the mountain, Neil and I met a strange person—a man in a neat suit who didn't carry any equipment. He looked to be in his forties, very charismatic, with deep blue eyes, very beautiful.\nI rarely pay attention to a person's eyes, but from the moment I saw him, I kept staring at his eyes. I saw my own reflection in his pupils.\nHe asked us for the way down the mountain in a friendly manner, and I pointed him to the path we had come from.",
    ["\n岁月如棋，落子无悔，一步踏错，便是百年。\n\n一副古老的棋盘静置于案，被放缓的时间里，隐约能看到一只大手和一只小手下棋的旧影。罗塞尔曾与贝尔纳黛对弈，谈起“烂柯棋局”的传说——那山中樵夫观棋片刻，人间已过百年。\n\n那时贝尔纳黛听不懂什么是烂柯，不懂为什么父亲总会把棋子下在交叉点上，也不懂什么是“观棋不语真君子，落子无悔大丈夫”，她只记得耍赖悔棋时父亲会轻拍她的头顶，手掌宽厚而温暖。"] = "\nYears are like a game of chess; once a piece is placed, there is no turning back. One wrong step, and a century passes.\n\nAn ancient chessboard sat quietly on the desk. In the slowed time, one could vaguely see the old shadows of a large hand and a small hand playing chess. Roselle once played against Bernadette and spoke of the legend of the \"Rotten Axe Chess Game\"—the woodcutter watched the game for a moment, and a century had passed in the human world.\n\nBack then, Bernadette didn't understand what a \"rotten axe\" was, didn't understand why her father always placed his pieces on the intersections, and didn't understand what it meant to be \"a true gentleman who watches in silence and a real man who never regrets his move.\" She only remembered that when she tried to cheat or take back a move, her father would gently pat her head, his palm broad and warm.",
    ["\n帕里克：\n\n　　你还好吗？前几天我和菲丽丝一起，回了趟科诺桑小镇。\n布兰登先生还是老样子，在镍币书店教孩子们读书，和当时教我们识字一样。\n　　你最近怎么样？什么时候回来看看？我们很想你。"] = "\nPalik:\n\n　　Are you okay? A few days ago, Phyllis and I went back to Konoson Small Town.\nMr. Brandon is still the same, teaching children to read at the Nickel Bookstore, just like when he taught us to read back then.\n　　How have you been lately? When will you come back to visit? We miss you very much.",
    ["\n年轻的非凡者，\n　　我已到达间海郡，决定暂时在韦尔奇老宅安顿下来。\n　　韦尔奇的离世还萦绕在他父亲身上，与这老家伙一起看着壁炉的火光发呆时，我才终于又有了些时间开始流动的实感。\n　　我路上总是在想，如果当时我没有沉睡，就能帮一把他......但说到底，成为半神的我和其他流浪猫好像也没什么不同，只是活得更久一点。对一只猫来说，这或许有点太久了，我记不清这是第多少次发现朋友离我而去。\n　　无论如何，睡吧，韦尔奇。这次我会记得。谢谢你，年轻的非凡者，这对我意义非凡。"] = "\nYoung Beyonder,\n　　I have arrived in Midseashire County and decided to settle down in the Welch old mansion for the time being.\n　　Welch's passing still lingers on his father. Only when I was staring blankly at the fireplace fire with this old guy did I finally have the real feeling of time starting to flow again.\n　　On the way, I kept thinking, if I hadn't been in a slumber at that time, I could have helped him... but in the end, being a Demigod doesn't seem any different from other stray cats, just living a bit longer. For a cat, this might be a bit too long; I can't remember how many times I've discovered friends leaving me.\n　　Regardless, sleep, Welch. This time I will remember. Thank you, young Beyonder, this means a lot to me.",
    ["\n廷根旅游，就选特好玩旅店！\n\n店内特供廷根旅行指南\n免费看中央广场精彩马戏表演\n凭旅店消费享受美味餐馆八折优惠！\n\n另：特好玩旅店同样欢迎口袋拮据的旅行家们，\n只要您愿意付出一些时间或能力。\n\n有意者请前往：\n学院大道西侧，廷根图书馆对面“特好玩旅店”！"] = "\nTingen tourism, choose the 'Very Fun' Hotel!\n\nSpecial Tingen Travel Guide provided in the hotel\nFree admission to the wonderful circus performance at Central Plaza\nEnjoy an 80% discount at delicious restaurants with your hotel receipt!\n\nAlso: The 'Very Fun' Hotel also welcomes travelers with tight pockets,\nas long as you are willing to contribute some time or skills.\n\nInterested parties, please head to:\nWest side of College Avenue, 'Very Fun' Hotel opposite the Tingen Library!",
    ["\n当大家准备散场的时候，有人大喊——戈登失踪了。\n是戴维的声音，据他所说，他们本来在一起喝酒的，戈登突然就不见了。\n曼斯教授让所有人都帮忙找，我们从营地找到营地外，都没有找到。\n正当所有人都回到营地后，戴维也不见了。\n戈登和戴维是最先发现山顶遗迹的人，也是最早失踪的。营地里去过山顶遗迹的人，都担心下一个失踪的是自己。\n尽管接下来的几天里没有人失踪，但曼斯教授和几位研究员先生都提议先暂时撤离，我们只好收拾东西，准备离开。"] = "\nWhen everyone was preparing to leave, someone shouted—Gordon is missing.\nIt was Davy's voice. According to him, they were drinking together, and Gordon suddenly disappeared.\nProfessor Mans asked everyone to help look for him. We searched from the camp to outside the camp, but couldn't find him.\nJust as everyone returned to the camp, Davy disappeared too.\nGordon and Davy were the first to discover the ruins on the mountain and were also the first to go missing. Everyone in the camp who had been to the ruins on the mountain was worried that they would be the next to go missing.\nAlthough no one went missing in the following days, Professor Mans and several researchers suggested evacuating first, so we had to pack our things and prepare to leave.",
    ["\n当季新品“未来梦”，梦中窥见后日谈\n\n招牌特调“火烧玫瑰”，坠入花海温柔乡\n\n更多精品美酒，尊贵人士的首选\n\n邀请您前来品尝！"] = "\nSeasonal new arrival 'Future Dream', glimpse the epilogue in a dream\n\nSignature cocktail 'Burning Rose', fall into the gentle land of a flower sea\n\nMore premium fine wines, the first choice for distinguished people\n\nInviting you to come and taste!",
    ["\n很久很久以前，丰饶之树还只是一粒小小的种子。\n\n它沉眠于大地母神教会中，由圣者精心保管。圣者知晓它身负生机与荒芜两种强大的力量，不能被轻易种下。\n\n直到那场背弃誓言的战争降临。大地化为焦土，生机纷纷湮灭，圣者站在同伴和敌人的尸体间，落下了一滴泪。 \n\n至少，要让这片大地重生。 \n\n种子进入泥土后迅速生长，生机怦然降临之时，荒芜也伸出爪牙——于是圣者挺身而出，将无尽的荒芜统统纳入身躯。\n\n变动终于平息，丰饶之树睁开了眼睛。\n\n她化为人形的灵体，懵懂如婴孩，裹着一袭金色的披风。 \n\n一个遥远的声音在她心头回荡： \n\n这是大地的礼物。\n\n这是丰饶的呼唤。"] = "\nOnce upon a time, the Tree of Abundance was just a tiny seed.\n\nIt slumbered in the Church of the Earth Mother, carefully guarded by a Saint. The Saint knew that it carried two powerful forces, vitality and desolation, and could not be planted easily.\n\nUntil the war that betrayed the oath arrived. The earth turned into scorched earth, vitality was annihilated one after another, and the Saint stood among the corpses of companions and enemies, shedding a tear.\n\nAt the very least, let this land be reborn.\n\nAfter the seed entered the soil, it grew rapidly. When vitality arrived with a bang, desolation also stretched out its claws—so the Saint stepped forward, taking all the endless desolation into their own body.\n\nThe change finally subsided, and the Tree of Abundance opened its eyes.\n\nShe turned into a human-shaped spirit, ignorant as an infant, wrapped in a golden cloak.\n\nA distant voice echoed in her heart:\n\nThis is the gift of the earth.\n\nThis is the call of abundance.",
    ["\n很高兴告诉大家，著名的“大胃王”洛罗被廷根和谐安宁的氛围吸引，决定暂时定居在此！\n\n他曾在1小时内吃掉100个迪西馅饼！126块小羊排！\n\n他将随时于西大道表演自己超乎常人的胃口！欢迎各位前来欣赏！"] = "\nWe are happy to tell everyone that the famous 'Big Eater' Loro has been attracted by the harmonious and peaceful atmosphere of Tingen and has decided to settle here for the time being!\n\nHe once ate 100 Dicy pies in 1 hour! 126 lamb chops!\n\nHe will perform his extraordinary appetite on West Avenue at any time! Everyone is welcome to come and enjoy!",
    ["\n循环音效 [%s], [打断模式] 不允许配置为 [NOT_INTERRUPT] "] = "\nLooping sound effect [%s], [Interrupt Mode] cannot be configured as [NOT_INTERRUPT] ",
    ["\n恭逢黑夜女神诞辰圣祭，圣赛缪尔教堂谨定于冬礼日举行守夜弥撒。现将当日活动安排敬告如下：\n\n时间：晚间10:00 准时开始\n地点：圣赛缪尔教堂前广场（若遇雨雪，移至教堂正厅）\n主持：安东尼·史蒂文森主教\n\n注意事项（请务必遵守）：\n守夜弥撒是我主诞辰最为神圣的仪式，请诸位信众严肃对待：\n1. 请勿迟到。弥撒准点开启，迟到者须在广场外围静立等候，待特定环节结束后方可入场。\n2. 保持肃静。仪式期间禁止交谈、喧哗、随意走动。\n3. 着装得体。建议穿着深色或素色正装，避免鲜艳色彩。\n4. 遵从引导。现场侍从将引导站位与跪拜次序，请予配合。"] = "\nIn celebration of the Evernight Goddess's birthday festival, St. Samuel Cathedral has scheduled a vigil mass on the Winter Festival. The arrangements for the day's activities are hereby notified as follows:\n\nTime: Starts promptly at 10:00 PM\nLocation: Square in front of St. Samuel Cathedral (in case of rain or snow, move to the main hall of the cathedral)\nPresider: Bishop Anthony Stevenson\n\nNotes (Please be sure to comply):\nThe vigil mass is the most sacred ceremony of our Lord's birthday; please treat it seriously:\n1. Do not be late. The mass starts on time. Latecomers must stand quietly outside the square and can only enter after specific segments are completed.\n2. Maintain silence. Talking, making noise, or walking around at will is prohibited during the ceremony.\n3. Dress appropriately. It is recommended to wear dark or plain formal attire, avoiding bright colors.\n4. Follow guidance. On-site attendants will guide the standing positions and kneeling order; please cooperate.",
    ["\n戈登和戴维发现了山上一个被积雪覆盖的遗迹入口，他们回到营地将消息报告给曼斯教授，教授当即就带着一些学者和几个护卫往山上赶。\n而我和另外几个学员则留在了营地，准备必要的物资。边搬东西的时候我边想，不久后我也要称呼戈登和戴维他们“研究员先生”了吧。\n对于新遗迹的考古研究是相当累人的工作，研究员们还在遗迹入口确认遗迹的建筑风格，而我们这些不受重视的学员就只能干剩下的粗重杂活，像是搬运物资或是清理现场之类的。\n回到营地，曼斯教授很兴奋，有几个研究员提议在营地开个庆功宴，曼斯教授也同意了，终于能放松一下了。\n庆功宴将持续一整晚……"] = "\nGordon and Davy discovered a ruins entrance covered by snow on the mountain. They returned to the camp to report the news to Professor Mans, and the professor immediately took some scholars and a few guards to rush up the mountain.\nAnd I and a few other students stayed in the camp, preparing the necessary supplies. While moving things, I thought, soon I will also be calling Gordon and Davy 'Mr. Researcher', right?\nArchaeological research on new ruins is quite tiring work. The researchers were still confirming the architectural style of the ruins at the entrance, and we, the ignored students, could only do the remaining rough work, like moving supplies or cleaning up the site.\nBack at the camp, Professor Mans was very excited. Several researchers suggested having a celebration banquet in the camp, and Professor Mans agreed. Finally, we could relax a bit.\nThe celebration banquet will last all night...",
    ["\n我\n很\n期\n待"] = "\nI\n\nLook\n\nForward\n\nTo It",
    ["\n我们在一起耳语\n寂静而毫无意义\n如风掠过干草\n或老鼠的脚踩过碎玻璃\n在我们的干地窖\n\n有态而无形，有影而无色\n瘫痪的力，没有动作的手势；\n那些直视的眼睛\n跨过死亡的另一王国的人\n记得我们——如果记得——不是迷失的\n\n狂暴的灵魂，而只是\n填塞起来的人\n我们围着沼泽转圈\n睡莲，睡莲\n我们围着沼泽转圈\n在清晨五点\n\n在观念与现实之间\n在动作与行为之间\n落下阴影\n所属之地\n\n世界就这样告终\n世界就这样告终\n世界就这样告终\n不是一声巨响，而是一声呜咽"] = "\nWe whisper together\nQuiet and meaningless\nAs wind over dry grass\nOr rat's feet over broken glass\nIn our dry cellar\n\nShape without form, shade without color\nParalyzed force, gesture without motion;\nThose who have crossed\nWith direct eyes, to death's other Kingdom\nRemember us—if at all—not as lost\n\nViolent souls, but only\nAs the hollow men\nWe go round the prickly pear\nPrickly pear, prickly pear\nWe go round the prickly pear\nAt five o'clock in the morning\n\nBetween the idea\nAnd the reality\nBetween the motion\nAnd the act\nFalls the Shadow\n\nThis is the way the world ends\nThis is the way the world ends\nThis is the way the world ends\nNot with a bang but a whimper",
    ["\n我叫康修娜，我想我叫康修娜，大家叫我康修娜。\n嗨，我是书店的店员，有什么我能帮你的吗？\n不对，我要离开！离开！我要喝有温度的汤！看能翻开的书！\n……康修娜。\n我叫康修娜，是书店的店员。\n康修娜。\n……你是谁？"] = "\nMy name is Kangxiuna, I think my name is Kangxiuna, everyone calls me Kangxiuna.\nHi, I'm a clerk at the bookstore, is there anything I can help you with?\nNo, I want to leave! Leave! I want to drink soup with temperature! Read books that can be opened!\n...Kangxiuna.\nMy name is Kangxiuna, I'm a clerk at the bookstore.\nKangxiuna.\n...Who are you?",
    ["\n我叫康修娜，是书店的店员，我的工作是站在门口朝大家微笑。\n\n我的脸有点笑僵了，所以我决定写点东西。\n\n今天英森特还是那副懒样子，只会抱怨书店生意不好。\n\n唉，快点到吃午饭的时间吧……午饭？我吃过……午饭吗？"] = "\nMy name is Kangxiuna, I'm a clerk at the bookstore, and my job is to stand at the door and smile at everyone.\n\nMy face is a bit stiff from smiling, so I decided to write something.\n\nToday, Inset is still that lazy self, only complaining that the bookstore business is bad.\n\nSigh, hurry up to lunchtime... lunch? Have I eaten... lunch?",
    ["\n我和几个学员从昨晚开始就在收拾东西，很快就能离开这诡异的地方了。\n昨晚，有两位研究员先生消失了，还有几个人因为害怕而跑出了营地，我认为这并不是理智的选择，因为野外的环境更加恶劣。\n我能看得出来曼斯教授也十分不安，但他是我们一行人的主心骨。他今天看起来是强撑着下达的指示，毕竟对于人类而言——未知是最古老最强烈的恐惧，就连曼斯教授也不例外。\n稍后，我们将消耗一部分带来的食物（这将减少我们行李的重量），然后我们就会启程。\n\n我决定一路记录下目前所见的一切，因为就在刚才，我看见一个活生生的人，从我眼前消失。我已经做好最坏的打算，或许这本日记将是我留在这个世界上的最后一抹痕迹。\n\n一旁的学员转过头对我说，曼斯教授也不见了，下一个会（日记戛然而止）"] = "\nMy fellow students and I have been packing since last night, and we will soon be able to leave this eerie place.\nLast night, two researchers disappeared, and several others ran out of the camp out of fear. I do not consider this a rational choice, as the environment in the wild is even harsher.\nI can tell that Professor Mans is also very uneasy, but he is the backbone of our group. He seemed to be forcing himself to issue instructions today. After all, for humans—the unknown is the oldest and most intense horror, and Professor Mans is no exception.\nShortly, we will consume a portion of the food we brought (which will reduce the weight of our luggage), and then we will set off.\n\nI have decided to record everything I see along the way, because just a moment ago, I saw a living person disappear right before my eyes. I have prepared for the worst; perhaps this diary will be the last trace I leave in this world.\n\nA student beside me turned and said to me that Professor Mans is also gone, and the next one will be (the diary ends abruptly)",
    ["\n我的天啊大家都怎么回事！\n\n永远只说那几句话，斐琳一刻不停地站在桥上钓了一辈子鱼！\n\n没人觉得奇怪吗？\n\n……不，为什么我之前不觉得奇怪？"] = "\nMy god, what is wrong with everyone!\n\nThey only ever say those few sentences. Philine has been standing on the bridge fishing for a lifetime without stopping for a second!\n\nDoesn't anyone find it strange?\n\n...No, why didn't I find it strange before?",
    ["\n推荐套餐\n前菜：因蒂斯青酱焗蜗牛\n主菜：特级油封鸭腿\n甜品：罗塞尔酥皮挞"] = "\nRecommended Set Menu\nAppetizer: Intis Green Sauce Baked Snails\nMain Course: Premium Duck Confit\nDessert: Roselle Puff Tart",
    ["\n提供最贴心的房屋租赁服务！\n\n<Letter_Highlight>信誉保障</>\n廷根市公证所公证的租赁合同\n\n<Letter_Highlight>房型多样</>\n适宜小家庭和大家庭的多种户型供您选择\n\n<Letter_Highlight>配置齐全</>\n房屋配备基础家具、独立盥洗室和瓦斯管道\n\n欢迎您前往<Mark id=\"#159\">水仙花街2至6号</>参观我们的房屋！"] = "\nProviding the most thoughtful housing rental services!\n\n<Letter_Highlight>Reputation Guaranteed</>\nRental contracts notarized by the Tingen Notarization Office\n\n<Letter_Highlight>Diverse Housing Types</>\nVarious layouts suitable for small and large families for you to choose from\n\n<Letter_Highlight>Fully Equipped</>\nHouses are equipped with basic furniture, independent washrooms, and gas pipelines\n\nWe welcome you to visit our houses at <Mark id=\"#159\">2-6 Daffodil Street</>!",
    ["\n摘要：\n今晨九时接获报案，一位名叫黛西·埃尔顿的青年女性陷入了异常<Mark id=\"#159\">昏迷</>状态。该名女性现居于<Letter_Highlight>廷根市北郊的别墅</>，由家中的管家和仆役看顾……\n\n标注：\n疑似<Mark id=\"#159\">非凡事件</>。"] = "\nSummary:\nReceived a report at nine this morning. A young woman named Daisy Elton has fallen into an abnormal <Mark id=\"#159\">Stun</> state. The woman currently resides in a <Letter_Highlight>villa in the northern suburbs of Tingen</>, and is being looked after by the butler and servants at home...\n\nNote:\nSuspected <Mark id=\"#159\">Beyonder incident</>.",
    ["\n无论是拯救世界的勇者还是打猎的好手\n一把趁手的武器都必不可少\n劳格拉斯武器店静候您的光临\n\n热卖推荐\n<Letter_Highlight>绅士左轮</>\n<Letter_Highlight>黄铜雕花燧发枪</>\n<Letter_Highlight>双筒猎枪</>\n\n\n<Delete id=\"#158\">办全类武器使用证请联系</><Hide stylename=\"Transparent\" id=\"#161\">老杰克</>\n\n廷根市警察局<Mark id=\"#159\">特别提醒</>：\n请合法取得武器使用证，违法办证人员已被缉拿"] = "\nWhether you are a hero saving the world or an expert hunter,\na handy weapon is essential.\nLogras Weapon Shop awaits your visit.\n\nHot Recommendations\n<Letter_Highlight>Gentleman's Revolver</>\n<Letter_Highlight>Brass Engraved Flintlock</>\n<Letter_Highlight>Double-barreled Shotgun</>\n\n\n<Delete id=\"#158\">For weapon usage permits, please contact</><Hide stylename=\"Transparent\" id=\"#161\">Old Jack</>\n\n<Mark id=\"#159\">Special Reminder</> from the Tingen Police Department:\nPlease obtain weapon usage permits legally. Those who obtain them illegally have already been apprehended.",
    ["\n替人占卜真的很好赚—— 大部分人只是想要个人帮他们壮胆。 \n\n---------------------------------------------\n\n今天给人占卜，明明显示的结果是这样的，但竟然错了。 怎么可能，占卜不会有错， 也许是看错了。\n\n---------------------------------------------\n\n（中间几页被血迹沾染了，读不太清）\n\n---------------------------------------------\n\n 我见过太多人把启示当成天命， 然后死亡。"] = "\nDivination for others is really profitable—most people just want someone to help them build up their courage. \n\n---------------------------------------------\n\nDivined for someone today. Even though the result was clearly this, it turned out to be wrong. How is that possible? Divination cannot be wrong. Perhaps I misread it.\n\n---------------------------------------------\n\n(The middle pages are stained with blood and are difficult to read)\n\n---------------------------------------------\n\n I have seen too many people treat revelations as destiny, and then die.",
    ["\n本月阅读活动主题为“艺术熏陶”。\n\n推荐阅读书目：《鲁恩早期古典诗歌集》《罗塞尔诗选》\n推荐戏剧欣赏：《伯爵归来》《傲慢者》《背叛者指环》"] = "\nThis month's reading activity theme is \"Artistic Cultivation\".\n\nRecommended reading list: \"Collection of Early Loen Classical Poetry\", \"Selected Poems of Roselle\"\nRecommended drama appreciation: \"The Count's Return\", \"The Arrogant\", \"The Traitor's Ring\"",
    ["\n桃花林的尽头，是一旦离开便再也寻不到的归途。\n\n在因蒂斯郊外的桃花林中，罗塞尔常携小贝尔纳黛漫步。纷飞的桃花瓣下，他低声讲述着一个关于“桃花源”的古老传说——那是一片隐藏在桃林尽头的净土，生活在那里的人无忧无虑，可一旦离开，就再也找不到回去的路。\n\n贝尔纳黛那时懵懂，只觉得既然如此，那就不要离开。\n\n直到多年后，她才懂得人总会离开，才明白父亲口中的“桃花源”，是再也无法触及的旧日幻梦。"] = "\n The end of the peach blossom forest is a path of no return once you leave. \n\n In the peach blossom forest on the outskirts of Intis, Roselle often strolled with little Bernadette. Under the fluttering peach petals, he whispered an ancient legend about a \"Peach Blossom Spring\"—a pure land hidden at the end of the peach forest where people lived without a care, but once they left, they could never find their way back. \n\n Bernadette was naive then and felt that if that were the case, she simply wouldn't leave. \n\n It wasn't until many years later that she understood people always leave, and realized the \"Peach Blossom Spring\" in her father's words was a dream of the Great Old Ones that could never be reached again.",
    ["\n此处茶点由卡斯伯特女士免费提供，请随意取用。\n\n若柠檬蛋糕的清新能勾起您的兴趣，\n\n巧克力奶贝的甜蜜能为您带来幸福。\n\n欢迎前往佐兰特街的卡斯伯特甜品俱乐部，我们期待像您这样有品味的人加入。"] = "\nRefreshments here are provided free of charge by Ms. Cuthbert, please help yourself.\n\nIf the freshness of the lemon cake piques your interest,\n\nmay the sweetness of the chocolate milk shell bring you happiness.\n\nWelcome to the Cuthbert Dessert Club on Zorant Street; we look forward to having someone with your taste join us.",
    ["\n每日安排：7点起床，8点到达愚者教堂做祈祷，8点15到8点45早餐，12点到3点午餐及锻炼。\n周一上午代数学，下午高等几何；周二上午物理学，下午机械科学；周三导师会谈，周四周五实践课程。周六周日休息。\n\n\n啊啊啊上学真的好累，但我要好好努力，以后争取到贝克兰德生活！"] = "\nDaily schedule: Wake up at 7, arrive at the Fool Church for prayer at 8, breakfast from 8:15 to 8:45, lunch and exercise from 12 to 3.\nMonday morning Algebra, afternoon Advanced Geometry; Tuesday morning Physics, afternoon Mechanical Science; Wednesday mentor meeting, Thursday and Friday practical courses. Saturday and Sunday off.\n\n\nAhhh, school is really tiring, but I must work hard and strive to live in Backlund in the future!",
    ["\n波拿巴餐厅\n招牌特色\n因蒂斯红酒炖牛肉\n因蒂斯香槟\n黑松露与牛肝菌"] = "\nBonaparte Restaurant\nSignature Specialties\nIntis Red Wine Beef Stew\nIntis Champagne\nBlack Truffle and Porcini Mushrooms",
    ["\n洛克金氏资本集团 · 财务部 \n债务人：工厂区第7批安置人员\n\n住房租赁费：3镑12苏勒\n饮食供应费：2镑8苏勒\n通勤运输费 ：1镑4苏勒\n\n附加费用：\n滞纳金(累计89天)：2镑3苏勒\n行政管理费：15苏勒\n强制保险税：8苏勒\n\n应付总额：9镑10苏勒\n注：根据《底层劳动者债务清偿条例》，逾期未付者，将启动\"强制清退程序\"。"] = "\nRockkin Capital Group · Finance Department \nDebtor: 7th Batch of Resettled Personnel in the Factory District\n\nHousing Rental Fee: 3 pounds 12 soli\nFood Supply Fee: 2 pounds 8 soli\nCommuter Transport Fee: 1 pound 4 soli\n\nAdditional Fees:\nLate Fee (accumulated 89 days): 2 pounds 3 soli\nAdministrative Fee: 15 soli\nCompulsory Insurance Tax: 8 soli\n\nTotal Payable: 9 pounds 10 soli\nNote: According to the \"Regulations on Debt Settlement for Low-income Laborers\", those who fail to pay on time will be subject to the \"Forced Eviction Procedure\".",
    ["\n活动规则：\n1. 支付<Letter_Highlight>1苏勒</>即可获得挑战资格。\n2. 主办方将展示一枚<Letter_Highlight>“幸运蛋” </>，请仔细观察它的纹路、色泽与形态。\n3. 在规定时间内，从100枚鸡蛋中找出它——你就是赢家！\n\n最终胜者奖励：<Letter_Highlight>10000苏勒</>！\n比赛可以重复参与！下一个“万镑户”就是你！\n\n（每位参与者离场时均可获赠<Letter_Highlight>新鲜鸡蛋</>一枚，愿大地母神赐福于你。） "] = "\nEvent Rules:\n1. Pay <Letter_Highlight>1 soli</> to enter the challenge.\n2. The organizer will display a <Letter_Highlight>\"Lucky Egg\" </>. Carefully observe its markings, color, and shape.\n3. Find it among 100 eggs within the time limit—and you win!\n\nGrand Prize: <Letter_Highlight>10000 soli</>!\nYou may enter as many times as you like! You could be the next person worth ten thousand pounds!\n\n(Every participant will receive <Letter_Highlight>a fresh egg</> upon leaving. May the Earth Mother bless you.) ",
    ["\n漫山的雪，也许今天是第二天，也许是第三天？\n我找不到尼尔了，营地也不见了。\n东西都没了，还好我在身上放了些食物……\n\n物资\n面包大约三分之一份\n糖3颗\n水半瓶"] = "\nSnow-covered mountains, perhaps today is the second day, or maybe the third?\nI can't find Neil, and the camp is gone too.\nEverything is gone, it's a good thing I kept some food on me...\n\nSupplies\nBread about one-third portion\nSugar 3 pieces\nWater half a bottle",
    ["\n激动？幸福？紧张？我无法用任何语言和文字描述我现在的心情。\n我和尼尔登顶了！\n幸运的尼尔找到了一颗琥珀，这将作为他的登顶纪念物。\n我也学着他在山上找，不过没什么特别的东西，我将山顶的雪混杂了一些土装到了瓶子里。\n\n下山物资：\n面包2份\n肉干和肉肠1份\n糖1罐\n黄油1块\n水2瓶"] = "\nExcited? Happy? Nervous? I cannot describe my feelings in any language or words.\nNeil and I reached the summit!\nLucky Neil found a piece of amber, which will serve as his summit souvenir.\nI also tried to look for one on the mountain like him, but there was nothing special. I mixed some soil from the mountain peak with snow and put it in a bottle.\n\nDescent supplies:\nBread 2 portions\nBeef jerky and meat sausage 1 portion\nSugar 1 jar\nButter 1 block\nWater 2 bottles",
    ["\n由一根根豌豆藤蔓构筑起的青绿森林，摇晃的秋千不知勾起了谁的童年回忆。\n\n在众多童话故事中，“杰克与豌豆”被罗塞尔赋予了蒸汽与机械的奇想。他将平凡的豌豆藤描绘成由齿轮驱动的奇迹，让杰克用智慧改造巨人的城堡，将吃人的怪物变为烤蛋糕的伙伴。那也是贝尔纳黛好奇心最重的时候，“爸爸，巨人是弗萨克人吗？”“城堡怎么建在云上的呢，云不是水吗？”“要多高才能看到城堡呀，坐飞空艇能够看到吗？我想上去看看！”……\n\n多么古怪的问题都会获得回应，多么天真的想法都会得到满足。"] = "\n A green forest constructed from pea vines; the swaying swing evokes childhood memories for someone.\n\n Among many fairy tales, \"Jack and the Beanstalk\" was imbued with Roselle's whimsy for steam and machinery. He depicted the ordinary beanstalk as a miracle driven by gears, letting Jack use his wisdom to remodel the giant's castle and turn the man-eating monster into a partner for baking cakes. That was also when Bernadette was most curious: \"Papa, is the giant a Feynapotter?\" \"How is the castle built on the clouds? Aren't clouds water?\" \"How high do you have to be to see the castle? Can you see it from an airship? I want to go up and see!\"...\n\n Every strange question would receive a response, and every naive thought would be satisfied.",
    ["\n省时省力，畅行廷根——脚踏车，您的出行新选择！\n\n快速便捷：告别拥挤的马车和漫长的步行，脚踏车让您轻松穿梭于大街小巷\n锻炼身体：骑行有助于锻炼身体，让您更健康\n经济实惠：一次购买，长久使用\n特别优惠：现在购买，立享8折优惠！数量有限，先到先得！"] = "\nSave Time and Effort—Ride Through Tingen with Ease! Choose a bicycle for the way you travel.\n\nFast and Convenient: Leave crowded carriages and long walks behind. A bicycle lets you move through streets and alleys with ease.\nStay Fit: Cycling is excellent exercise and helps keep you healthy.\nGreat Value: Buy it once and use it for years.\nSpecial Offer: Buy now for only 8 tenths of the regular price! Limited stock—first come, first served!",
    ["\n睡莲仙女三部曲！经典再版！\n《睡莲仙女的诞生》\n她在夜色中诞生，湖水织就她的衣袍，小镇的传说，就此开始。\n《睡莲仙女的奉献》\n为了的欢乐与幸福，她用一切换取永恒的白昼。\n《睡莲仙女的沉睡》\n她沉入湖心，在深眠中等待下一段故事的开启……"] = "\nWater Lily Fairy Trilogy! Classic Reprint!\n\"The Birth of the Water Lily Fairy\"\nShe was born in the night, the lake water wove her robes, and the legend of the small town began here.\n\"The Dedication of the Water Lily Fairy\"\nFor the sake of joy and happiness, she traded everything for eternal daylight.\n\"The Slumber of the Water Lily Fairy\"\nShe sank into the heart of the lake, waiting in deep sleep for the next story to begin...",
    ["\n租金<Mark id=\"#159_R\">4-8苏勒</>每周\n\n享有充足自然光！空气流通良好！\n临近优质公用取水点。\n楼下有便利公共舆洗室，每两周打扫一次。\n<Mark id=\"#159_R\">预付</>一月租金，可签约三个月！\n\n谢绝：携带大量孩童者、无固定收入者、传染病患。\n\n请联系<Letter_Highlight>霍金斯太太</>。"] = "\nRent <Mark id=\"#159_R\">4-8 soli</> per week\n\nEnjoy plenty of natural light! Good air circulation!\nNear a high-quality public water source.\nThere is a convenient public washroom downstairs, cleaned every two weeks.\n<Mark id=\"#159_R\">Prepay</> one month's rent to sign a three-month contract!\n\nRefused: Those with many children, those without fixed income, those with infectious diseases.\n\nPlease contact <Letter_Highlight>Mrs. Hawkins</>.",
    ["\n空的。那个大风车里面是空的。\n\n教堂的门也推不开。\n\n女神啊。如果我在做梦，请让我醒过来吧。"] = "\nEmpty. The inside of that big windmill is empty.\n\nI can't push open the church door either.\n\nEvernight Goddess. If I am dreaming, please let me wake up.",
    ["\n第7次记录：同样的咒文，在葡萄藤旁低声念和在空地上直接念，结果完全不同。前者更柔和，后者更急躁。\n\n第11次记录：为受伤的卷毛狒狒处理伤口时，先安抚，再引导生命力流动，效果比直接催生血肉更好。\n\n第16次记录：蘑菇精喜欢亮晶晶的光点。若将绿焰拆成更细小的流萤状，它们会自己围过来，施术消耗反而降低。\n\n第22次记录：今天尤德拉之树的回响比昨天更清晰了一点。\n\n第31次记录：实验外溢的问题越来越明显，苹果长得太快，湖里的龟似乎也受了影响……不管了，等这一轮数据整理完再处理。\n\n（后面夹着几页零散的补记，字迹明显变快了。）"] = "\n7th record: The same incantation, whispered beside the grapevines versus chanted directly in the open space, the results are completely different. The former is gentler, the latter is more impatient.\n\n11th record: When treating the wounds of the Curly-Haired Baboon, pacifying it first and then guiding the flow of life force works better than directly stimulating flesh growth.\n\n16th record: Mushroom sprites like shiny light spots. If the green flames are broken down into finer firefly-like shapes, they will gather around on their own, and the consumption of the spell is reduced.\n\n22nd record: The echo of the Yodra Tree was clearer today than yesterday.\n\n31st record: The problem of experimental overflow is becoming more and more obvious. The apples are growing too fast, and the turtles in the lake seem to have been affected... Never mind, I'll deal with it after this round of data is organized.\n\n(A few scattered supplementary notes are tucked in the back, the handwriting is noticeably faster.)",
    ["\n第一个月：向父亲证明我擅长规划自己的人生。\n第一年：蜜月旅行（目的地见附录），海蒂感到幸福。\n第三年：换大房子，海蒂在我宣布拥有新房产时喜极而泣。\n……\n第十年：孩子入学，甜蜜亲吻我和海蒂的脸颊。"] = "\nFirst month: Prove to my father that I am good at planning my own life.\nFirst year: Honeymoon trip (destination see appendix), Heidi feels happy.\nThird year: Move to a bigger house, Heidi wept with joy when I announced that we had a new property.\n...\nTenth year: The child starts school and gives me and Heidi a sweet kiss on the cheek.",
    ["\n第二十周，我要回去！我要回去！！我的头发缠绕我，我的指甲缠绕我！！！把我扎进南瓜田扎进丰饶树扎进大地里深深地深深地……深深地……\n\n\n\n\n这里的果子\n非常美味"] = "\nWeek 20, I want to go back! I want to go back!! My hair is wrapping around me, my fingernails are wrapping around me!!! Stabbing me into the pumpkin field, into the Tree of Abundance, into the earth, deeply, deeply... deeply...\n\n\n\n\nThe fruits here\nare very delicious",
    ["\n纯水6000毫升\n30片金薄荷叶子\n5朵深眠花\n800克夜香草\n5束洋甘菊"] = "\nPure water 6000 milliliters\n30 golden mint leaves\n5 deep sleep flowers\n800 grams of night grass\n5 bundles of chamomile",
    ["\n罗珊和几位市民 \n在中央广场瓦解消散\n失踪地点共三个\n近期失踪者可能还活着"] = "\nRoselle and several citizens\ndissipated at the Central Plaza.\nThere are three locations where they went missing.\nThe recent missing persons may still be alive.",
    ["\n美酒、劲舞、无尽的欢愉！\n\n本酒馆开业只做三件事：激情、激情、还是<Hide id=\"#157_R\">***</>激情！\n\n每<Highlight>周四</>更有全场美酒<Highlight>激情半价</>！\n\n爱酒之人，勿失良机！\n\n◆酒馆内禁止赌博、斗殴、诈骗客人与侍者，\n凡有以上冲动者请自行移步至店门外解决。"] = "\nFine wine, energetic dancing, endless pleasure!\n\nThis tavern only does three things upon opening: passion, passion, and <Hide id=\"#157_R\">***</> passion!\n\nEvery <Highlight>Thursday</> there is <Highlight>passionate half-price</> on all fine wines!\n\nWine lovers, don't miss this opportunity!\n\n◆Gambling, fighting, and defrauding guests and waiters are prohibited in the tavern.\nAnyone with such impulses, please step outside the shop to resolve it.",
    ["\n致迷途的羔羊与渴求庇护的灵魂：\n\n我主自称愚者，在过去，在现在，也在未来，他是支配灵界的伟大主宰，也是执掌好运的黄黑之王，更是每个生灵追求永恒的道标。\n\n他是怜悯的，他是仁慈的，他是这个世界的救主……他的仁爱播撒在人间，为家家户户带去温暖。我们将这关怀化作触手可及的回馈，将愚者的福音传遍大地……\n\n如有聆听福音的需要，请根据背面的地图指引，于夜深人静之时拜访<Letter_Highlight>奇迹邮筒</>。\n\n<Letter_Normal_HW>注：请不要在公开场合宣传愚者教会。</>"] = "\nTo the lost lambs and souls seeking shelter:\n\nMy Lord calls himself the Fool. In the past, in the present, and in the future, he is the great master who dominates the Spirit World, the King of Yellow and Black who holds good luck, and the beacon for every living being pursuing eternity.\n\nHe is compassionate, he is merciful, he is the savior of this world... His benevolence is spread among the people, bringing warmth to every household. We turn this care into tangible feedback, spreading the gospel of the Fool across the land...\n\nIf you have a need to listen to the gospel, please visit the <Letter_Highlight>Miracle Mailbox</> in the dead of night according to the map on the back.\n\n<Letter_Normal_HW>Note: Please do not promote the Church of the Fool in public.</>",
    ["\n若您渴望成为政府雇员，请选择我们的夜间学堂！\n识字就能来，结业保送市政厅考试！\n\n<Highlight>开课详情</>\n◆每逢二四六夜间授课\n◆学费1磅12苏勒\n\n月月准点发金镑，刮风下雨不下岗。\n高薪体面又轻松，码头扛包百倍强！\n\n<Highlight>水仙花街6号\"金笔杆\"商行</>报名，名额只收<Mark id=\"#159_R\"> 30人 </>，手慢明年挤破头！"] = "\nIf you aspire to become a government employee, please choose our night school!\nIf you can read, you can come; graduation guarantees a recommendation for the City Hall exam!\n\n<Highlight>Course Details</>\n◆Classes held at night on Tuesdays, Thursdays, and Saturdays\n◆Tuition 1 pound 12 soli\n\nGet paid in gold pounds on time every month, no layoffs regardless of wind or rain.\nHigh salary, decent and easy, a hundred times better than carrying bags at the dock!\n\nSign up at <Highlight>\"Golden Pen\" Firm, 6 Daffodil Street</>, only <Mark id=\"#159_R\"> 30 spots </> available, if you're slow, you'll be fighting for a spot next year!",
    ["\n蒙黑夜女神庇佑，本教堂自成立以来，仰赖诸位信众慷慨捐赠，得以维系圣工、扶助贫弱。\n　　为便于统一计数、提升管理效率，自即日起，本教堂所设之慈善奉献箱，统一只接受现金捐赠，不再收取任何形式的支票。\n　　凡此前已开具支票者，仍可于本公告发布之日起七日内，于教堂办公处办理退还或更换手续。由此给您带来的不便，我们深表歉意，恳请诸位信众予以理解与配合。\n　　愿信徒永沐星月柔辉，得女神指引安然前行。\n\n　　赞美女神。"] = "\nUnder the protection of the Evernight Goddess, since the establishment of this church, we have relied on the generous donations of all believers to maintain holy work and help the poor and weak.\n　　To facilitate unified counting and improve management efficiency, effective immediately, the charity donation boxes set up by this church will only accept cash donations and will no longer accept checks in any form.\n　　Those who have previously issued checks can still go to the church office within seven days from the date of this announcement to handle refund or replacement procedures. We deeply apologize for the inconvenience this may cause you and sincerely ask for the understanding and cooperation of all believers.\n　　May believers forever bathe in the soft glow of the stars and moon, and be guided by the Goddess to move forward safely.\n\n　　Praise the Goddess.",
    ["\n该如何描摹你，\n用目光，用声音。\n像忽明忽灭的焰火，\n湖中雪絮。\n我听见你。"] = "\nHow should I describe you,\nwith eyes, with voice.\nLike flickering Flame Fire,\nSnowflakes in the lake.\nI hear you.",
    ["\n请各位认真看看这篇公告！\n我们的老约翰死了，别管你认不认识，有什么奇怪的东西还在老约翰身上！\n我不知道怎么去描述，但是老约翰还会在半夜走动，在没有心跳和呼吸的情况下。\n我们不知道应该找谁，医生还是牧师。\n任何知道或有相关消息的人请来铁十字街东南角，位于中街和金梧桐大道之间。\n如果能让老约翰安睡，将会得到一笔丰厚报酬。"] = "\nEveryone, please take a serious look at this announcement!\nOur Old John is dead. Regardless of whether you know him or not, something strange is still on Old John!\nI don't know how to describe it, but Old John still walks in the middle of the night, without a heartbeat or breathing.\nWe don't know who to look for, a doctor or a priest.\nAnyone who knows or has relevant information, please come to the southeast corner of Iron Cross Street, between Middle Street and Golden Indus Avenue.\nIf you can let Old John sleep in peace, you will receive a generous reward.",
    ["\n诸君！请勿让求学的孩子蒙尘！\n诚邀尊贵的绅士淑女以金镑铺就求学阶梯。\n\n凡捐赠者，皆可登入《黑夜烛光》名录，\n您的善心会获得女神赐福。\n\n捐赠处：<Highlight>当地黑夜教堂</>\n\n附注：本会会计师系贝克兰德大学认证，\n收支账目每月刊登于《廷根日报》第三版"] = "\nGentlemen! Please do not let the children seeking knowledge be covered in dust!\nWe cordially invite noble gentlemen and ladies to pave the way for education with gold pounds.\n\nAll donors can be entered into the \"Evernight Candlelight\" directory,\nand your kindness will be blessed by the Goddess.\n\nDonation location: <Highlight>Local Evernight Church</>\n\nNote: Our association's accountant is certified by Backlund University,\nand the income and expenditure accounts are published in the third edition of the \"Tingen Daily\" every month.",
    ["\n车次           时间         站台       目的地\n\nTG056     10:00-19:00       1      贝克兰德\nTG187     12:33-21:06       2         金秋湖\nTG304     14:14-17:50       2      贝克兰德\nTG775     15:00-15:30       1      睡莲小镇\nTG214     16:03-22:10       1         金秋湖\n\n……………"] = "\nTrain No.           Time         Platform       Destination\n\nTG056     10:00-19:00       1      Backlund\nTG187     12:33-21:06       2         Golden Autumn Lake\nTG304     14:14-17:50       2      Backlund\nTG775     15:00-15:30       1      Water Lily Town\nTG214     16:03-22:10       1         Golden Autumn Lake\n\n……………",
    ["\n近期某些爱情小说，引发了对吸血鬼不必要的狂热。\n现做以下概念澄清，帮助大家进行严谨的小说创作：\n吸血鬼多指因为黑暗力量而产生吸血冲动的堕落个体，在小说中应充当反派角色。\n若有必要创作相关小说，应采用“血族”一词。血族指古老智慧的血液贵族，他们恪守传统，注重礼仪，更应被当做主角书写。\n笔者倡议多创作以血族为主角的荣耀小说，避免过分沉溺虚幻的恋爱情节。"] = "\nRecent romance novels have sparked unnecessary fanaticism about vampires.\nI am making the following conceptual clarifications to help everyone with rigorous novel writing:\n\"Vampire\" mostly refers to fallen individuals who have developed an urge to suck blood due to dark powers, and should act as villains in novels.\nIf it is necessary to write related novels, the term \"Blood Clan\" should be used. Blood Clan refers to ancient and wise blood aristocrats who adhere to traditions, pay attention to etiquette, and should be written as protagonists.\nI advocate writing more glorious novels with Blood Clan as protagonists, avoiding excessive indulgence in illusory romantic plots.",
    ["\n这个动画我没有!!! 播不出!!! \n模型ID:%s\n动画ID:%s\n缺失动画:%s %s\nNPCID:%s"] = "\nI don't have this animation!!! Cannot play it!!! \nModel ID:%s\nAnimation ID:%s\nMissing animation:%s %s\nNPC ID:%s",
    ["\n金狼一挥手，台下数千人同时起立。\n提线早已勒进喉咙。\n这些站起来的，已经不是人了。\n\"你们想要安全，就把意识交给我，\n这是双赢的买卖。\""] = "\nWith a wave of Golden Wolf's hand, thousands of people in the audience stood up simultaneously.\nThe strings had already tightened around their throats.\nThose who stood up were no longer human.\n\"If you want safety, hand your consciousness over to me.\nThis is a win-win deal.\"",
    ["\n金秋湖 12\n拉姆德古堡 10\n兜里 15\n\n——到底怎么选！"] = "\nGolden Autumn Lake 12\nLamud Castle 10\nIn the pocket 15\n\n——How on earth should I choose!",
    ["\n铁十字街平价钟表行\n\n“时间属于每个人“\n全廷根<Mark id=\"#159_R\">最低价</>！现金交易，赊账利息另计。\n修理概不退换，开盖即认可报价！"] = "\nIron Cross Street Affordable Clock and Watch Shop\n\n\"Time belongs to everyone\"\n<Mark id=\"#159_R\">Lowest price</> in all of Tingen! Cash transactions, interest on credit will be calculated separately.\nNo returns or exchanges after repair, opening the cover means accepting the quote!",
    ["\n雪下了一整晚。早上起来帐篷都被埋了半截，尼尔提议我们提早启程加快行程，如果考虑到意外情况补给可能不太够。\n我们把东西都收拾好，准备启程。\n\n剩余物资：\n面包3份\n肉干和肉肠2份\n糖1罐 尼尔昨晚外出了一趟，回来的时候吃了几颗\n黄油2块 山上太冷，我们昨晚把黄油涂抹在面包上，并且放在火上烤着吃\n酒1瓶 水太重了，只留一瓶等登顶后庆祝\n水3瓶"] = "\nIt snowed all night. When we woke up in the morning, the tent was half buried. Neil suggested we set off early to speed up the journey, as supplies might not be enough if we consider accidents.\nWe packed everything up and prepared to set off.\n\nRemaining supplies:\nBread 3 portions\nBeef jerky and meat sausage 2 portions\nSugar 1 jar Neil went out last night and ate a few pieces when he came back\nButter 2 blocks It was too cold on the mountain, we spread the butter on the bread last night and roasted it over the fire to eat\nWine 1 bottle Water is too heavy, only kept one bottle to celebrate after reaching the summit\nWater 3 bottles",
    ["\n音效 [%s] 还没有生成对应的lua配置信息, 本地请先执行脚本生成\n //C7/Development/Mainline/Tools/WwiseTools/ProcessAudioResource/ProcessAudioResource.bat"] = "\nSound effect [%s] does not have corresponding lua configuration information generated yet. Please run the script locally to generate it\n //C7/Development/Mainline/Tools/WwiseTools/ProcessAudioResource/ProcessAudioResource.bat",
    ["\n龙啸将至。\n我将不<Hide id=\"#157\">畏高、不惧火、不后退。我将不恋温床，不贪安逸，</>不向恐惧低头。\n我这平庸的人生，注定<Hide id=\"#157\">光辉万丈</>。\n我要将旗帜，<Hide id=\"#157\">插在最高</>的地方。\n我是刺向龙<Hide id=\"#157\">心的长矛，龙焰中的坚盾，风暴里的号角，黑暗之中的光芒。</>\n为猎龙献上生命与心脏！\n\n猎龙人：凯文·斯托克   <Hide id=\"#157\">瑞尔·比</>伯"] = "\nDragon's roar is coming.\nI will not <Hide id=\"#157\">fear heights, fear fire, or retreat. I will not cling to a warm bed, or covet comfort,</> or bow to horror.\nThis mediocre life of mine is destined to be <Hide id=\"#157\">glorious</>.\nI will plant the flag <Hide id=\"#157\">at the highest</> place.\nI am the spear piercing the dragon's <Hide id=\"#157\">heart, the shield in the dragon's fire, the horn in the storm, the light in the darkness.</>\nOffer my life and heart for dragon hunting!\n\nDragon Hunter: Kevin Stock   <Hide id=\"#157\">Ray Bieber</>",
    ["\n龙啸将至。\n我将不畏高、不惧火、不后退。我将不恋温床，不贪安逸，不向恐惧低头。\n我这平庸的人生，注定光辉万丈。\n我要将旗帜，插在最高的地方。\n我是刺向龙心的长矛，龙焰中的坚盾，风暴里的号角，黑暗之中的光芒。\n为猎龙献上生命与心脏！\n\n猎龙人：凯文·斯托克   瑞尔·比伯"] = "\nDragon's roar is coming.\nI will not fear heights, fear fire, or retreat. I will not cling to a warm bed, or covet comfort, or bow to horror.\nThis mediocre life of mine is destined to be glorious.\nI will plant the flag at the highest place.\nI am the spear piercing the dragon's heart, the shield in the dragon's fire, the horn in the storm, the light in the darkness.\nOffer my life and heart for dragon hunting!\n\nDragon Hunter: Kevin Stock   Ray Bieber",
    ["\n（一）\n我们是5月23日上午上山的，上山的时候碰到了一个穿着整齐西装的男人，四十来岁的样子，他向我们询问下山的路，给我感觉像城堡里的伯爵先生一样，佐治将下山的路告诉给他。没走两步，我回头，他消失不见了。\n佐治说要学习搭帐篷，我给他示范了三次，最后反倒是我被帐篷难倒了，这新买的帐篷不太顶用。\n\n物资：\n面包——8余6\n肉类制品——6余5\n糖——1罐约1磅\n黄油——4余4\n酒——4余3\n水——5余5 明天留意水源\n\n（二）\n今天是晴天，雪很刺眼。\n佐治每隔一段时间就要看他的那本登山日志，像个老道的登山者一样，物资的记录就交给他了。\n其实他这是第二次跟我登山，上一次我跟他走的是古堡附近的野山。\n\n（三）\n今天是赶路的一天，我们必须赶在明天前抵达山顶，否则物资会不够。\n晚上，我发现扎营的地方附近有水源，很幸运，我们暂时不缺水了。\n但我隐约感觉有“野兽”在注视我们的帐篷，今晚只好我来守夜了。\n\n（四）\n在山上找到了一颗琥珀，把佐治羡慕坏了。这是我在霍纳奇斯登山以来最特殊的一个登顶纪念品。\n奇怪的是，这颗琥珀是从什么时候到我手里的？我为什么会不记得？\n琥珀里还有一只小虫子，听说琥珀里面的虫子可是跨越了千万年时间的“时间旅客”？千万年前的虫子长这样？\n\n（五）\n珀琥是不本根那"] = "\n(I)\nWe went up the mountain on the morning of May 23rd. When we were going up, we met a man in a neat suit, about forty years old. He asked us for the way down the mountain. He gave me the feeling of a Count in a castle. George told him the way down. After walking a few steps, I looked back, and he had disappeared.\nGeorge said he wanted to learn how to set up a tent. I demonstrated it to him three times, but in the end, I was the one stumped by the tent. This newly bought tent is not very useful.\n\nSupplies:\nBread——8 left 6\nMeat products——6 left 5\nSugar——1 jar about 1 pound\nButter——4 left 4\nWine——4 left 3\nWater——5 left 5 Keep an eye on water sources tomorrow\n\n(II)\nToday is a sunny day, the snow is blinding.\nGeorge checks his mountaineering log every once in a while, like an experienced mountaineer. The recording of supplies is left to him.\nActually, this is his second time mountaineering with me. Last time I walked with him on the wild mountains near the ancient castle.\n\n(III)\nToday is a day of rushing. We must reach the summit before tomorrow, otherwise, the supplies will not be enough.\nIn the evening, I found a water source near the campsite. Fortunately, we are not short of water for the time being.\nBut I vaguely felt that \"beasts\" were watching our tent, so I have to keep watch tonight.\n\n(IV)\nFound a piece of amber on the mountain, which made George very envious. This is the most special summit souvenir I have had since mountaineering in Hornacis.\nStrangely, when did this amber get into my hands? Why don't I remember?\nThere is a small bug in the amber. I heard that the bugs in amber are \"time travelers\" that have spanned millions of years? Do bugs from millions of years ago look like this?\n\n(V)\nAmber is not root",
    [" \n                是谁造成了这一切？\n    <Letter_Highlight_HW>管家、医生、男爵夫人、仆人，</>            \n                凶手是他们中的哪个？"] = " \n                Who caused all of this? \n    <Letter_Highlight_HW>Butler, doctor, viscountess, servant, </>            \n                Which one of them is the murderer?",
    ["  \n精准报时，人人可享！\n清洁上油，只要六便士！\n发条更换，质优价廉！\n怀表估价，现金收购旧表！\n\n机不可失，铁十字街平价钟表行即将调价！\n速来锁定今日低价！"] = "\n Precise timekeeping, for everyone to enjoy! \n Cleaning and oiling, only six pence! \n Mainspring replacement, high quality and low price! \n Pocket watch appraisal, cash purchase of old watches! \n\n Don't miss out, Iron Cross Street affordable clock shop is about to adjust prices! \n Hurry to lock in today's low price!",
    ["                   晚上好，侦探。\n               这里刚好死了一个人。\n               要来玩一场游戏吗？"] = "Good evening, detective.\nSomeone just died here.\nWould you like to play a game?",
    ["         亨利·怀恩 与 艾米莉亚·布鲁尔\n               明日正午，湖边花亭。\n               邀请您见证爱与幸福！"] = "Henry Wayne and Amelia Brewer\nTomorrow at noon, at the lakeside flower pavilion.\nWe invite you to witness our love and happiness!",
    ["         只是我遗留的一片扭曲的残念罢了，却自以为是斯蒂姆宫的主人？呵呵，但我的力量，又哪是那么好利用的。那只是我意志的一部分，被扭曲和污染的一部分，并不是真正的我……"] = "        It is just a piece of distorted remnant thought I left behind, yet it thinks it is the master of the Steam Palace? Heh, but my power is not so easily used. That is only a part of my will, a part that has been distorted and corrupted, not the real me...",
    ["         是否确认永久删除角色\n（删除后昵称将在开服30天后释放）"] = "         Are you sure you want to permanently delete this character?\n(After deletion, the nickname will be released 30 days after the server launch.)",
    ["        “上午好，不，中午好，班森。”\n        这位男子正是他和梅丽莎的兄长，班森·莫雷蒂，今年才25岁，因发际线后退，面容老相，看起来都快30了。\n        他黑发褐瞳，与克莱恩有几分相像，但没那种淡淡的书卷气。\n        “中午好，克莱恩，面试怎么样？”班森站了起来，嘴角流露出微笑。\n        他的黑色外套和半高礼帽都挂在高低床的凸出处。\n        “非常差。”克莱恩没有表情地回答道。\n        眼见班森愣住，克莱恩轻笑补充：\n        “事实上，我根本没参加面试，我提前找到了工作，周薪3镑……”\n        他将之前对梅丽莎说过的话语又重复了一遍。\n        班森神情缓和下来，摇头笑道：\n        “有种看见孩子长大的感觉……嗯，这份工作还不错。”\n\n        ——第一卷《小丑》第二十六章 练习"] = "“Good morning, no, good afternoon, Benson.” \n This man was his and Melissa’s older brother, Benson Moretti, only 25 years old this year. Because of his receding hairline and old-looking face, he looked almost 30. \n He had black hair and brown eyes, somewhat similar to Klein, but without that faint scholarly air. \n “Good afternoon, Klein, how was the interview?” Benson stood up, a smile appearing on the corners of his mouth. \n His black coat and top hat were hanging on the protrusion of the bunk bed. \n “Very bad.” Klein replied expressionlessly. \n Seeing Benson stunned, Klein chuckled and added: \n “In fact, I didn’t attend the interview at all. I found a job in advance, with a weekly salary of 3 pounds…” \n He repeated what he had said to Melissa before. \n Benson’s expression softened, and he shook his head and smiled: \n “I have a feeling of watching a child grow up… well, this job is not bad.” \n \n —— Volume 1: Clown, Chapter 26: Practice",
    ["        ……原来是这样。斯蒂姆宫，你应该与我一样沉眠于历史，但为何又突然重现世间，是谁……想要利用我的力量、我的气息……"] = "        ...So that's how it is. Steam Palace, you should be sleeping in history just like me, but why have you suddenly reappeared in the world? Who... wants to use my power, my aura...",
    ["        一开始，这个孩子的出生并没有给这个没落的贵族——因蒂斯王国的古斯塔夫家族，带来太多惊喜。\n        但当他长大之后，却忽然在机械、文学、音乐、美术等许多领域展现出无与伦比的才能，并带领古斯塔夫家族再次走向繁盛，连神明都亲自为他降下祝福，称他为“蒸汽之子”。\n        他发明了蒸汽机，让所有人踩着蒸汽的热意快步走进蒸汽与机械时代，亲手开启了席卷整个世界的工业革命。他改良了帆船和火炮，让因蒂斯的强大威震整片大陆。他撰写小说与戏剧，谱写乐曲与诗歌，发明塔罗与纸牌，创造游戏与传说。他还发明抽水马桶，发起爱国卫生运动……这一切彻底改变世界。\n        他是前所未有的天才、是时代的主角和开拓者，他就是——\n        罗塞尔·古斯塔夫！"] = "        At first, the birth of this child did not bring too many surprises to this declining noble family—the Gustav family of the Intis Republic. \n But when he grew up, he suddenly displayed unparalleled talent in many fields such as mechanics, literature, music, and art, and led the Gustav family to prosperity once again, with even the gods personally bestowing blessings upon him, calling him the \"Son of Steam.\" \n He invented the steam engine, allowing everyone to step quickly into the Steam and Machinery Era with the heat of steam, personally initiating the Industrial Revolution that swept the entire world. He improved sailing ships and artillery, making Intis's power shake the entire continent. He wrote novels and plays, composed music and poetry, invented tarot and cards, and created games and legends. He also invented the flush toilet and initiated the patriotic health movement... All of this completely changed the world. \n He is an unprecedented genius, the protagonist and pioneer of the era, and he is— \n Roselle Gustav!",
    ["        丰饶的气息……或许也是一种扭曲和污染，一种背叛和诅咒……"] = "        The scent of abundance... perhaps it is also a kind of distortion and corruption, a kind of betrayal and curse...",
    ["        也许在那之前，我——罗塞尔·古斯塔夫，因蒂斯的皇帝，终将归来。"] = "        Perhaps before that, I—Roselle Gustav, the Emperor of Intis, will eventually return.",
    ["        也许是陌生的敌人？我这一生见过无数的敌人，经历过无数的危险，面对过无数的疯狂……"] = "        Perhaps an unfamiliar enemy? I have seen countless enemies in my life, experienced countless dangers, and faced countless madnesses...",
    ["        但在此之前，请记得我，一个与你们一样来自异乡的灵魂，一个曾经想要回到故乡的人。"] = "        But before that, please remember me, a soul from a foreign land like you, a person who once wanted to return to his hometown.",
    ["        但并非所有危险都以危险的模样出现，它会伪装，伪装成祝福，伪装成信仰，甚至伪装成一种恩赐。"] = "        But not all dangers appear in the form of danger; it will disguise itself, disguise itself as a blessing, disguise itself as faith, and even disguise itself as a kind of gift.",
    ["        但当这一切真正发生时，我感受到的却只是……平静。"] = "        But when all this really happened, what I felt was only... peace.",
    ["        但我几乎忘记了，我原本来自于一个和平的年代，不曾沾染战争的气息。或许因为我始终是用一种游戏的心态对待这个世界，到最后，连对待生命的态度都变得轻薄……"] = "        But I had almost forgotten that I originally came from a peaceful era, never having been stained by the scent of war. Perhaps because I have always treated this world with a gaming mentality, in the end, even my attitude toward life has become frivolous...",
    ["        但这里本就弱肉强食，疯狂又诡异。战争是永恒的主题，例如那场第四纪的四皇之战……"] = "        But this place is inherently a place where the strong prey on the weak, mad and bizarre. War is an eternal theme, such as that War of the Four Emperors in the Fourth Epoch...",
    ["        你们……终于来了，并且已经迈出了一大步。"] = "        You... have finally arrived, and you have already taken a big step.",
    ["        出发吧，大航海家罗塞尔·哥伦布·麦哲伦·古斯塔夫，去验证你的猜想吧！"] = "        Set sail, great navigator Roselle Columbus Magellan Gustav, and go verify your hypothesis!",
    ["        到,<Tips id=\"#160\">弗兰奇</>公寓，找到房东弗兰奇先生问询卡尔合租人信息，以便后续调查"] = "        Arrive at <Tips id=\"#160\">Frankie</> Apartment, find the landlord Mr. Frankie to inquire about Karl's roommate information for subsequent investigation",
    ["        到弗兰奇公寓，找房东弗兰奇先生，问询卡尔合租人信息，以便后续调查。"] = "        Go to Frankie Apartment, find the landlord Mr. Frankie, and inquire about information on Karl's roommate to facilitate subsequent investigations.",
    ["        到恶龙酒吧地下市场找保罗，问询查理是否接触神秘学物品；向老板斯维因表明身份，可进入地下市场调查。"] = "        Go to the Evil Dragon Bar underground market to find Paul and inquire if Charlie had come into contact with any mystical items; reveal your identity to the boss, Swain, to gain access to the underground market for investigation.",
    ["        前往斯林面包房，找到斯林太太，询问她是否想到新的线索。"] = "        Head to Slin's Bakery, find Mrs. Slin, and ask if she has thought of any new clues.",
    ["        又是什么惊扰了我的沉眠？这次的客人好像并非故人，也不是什么熟悉的朋友。"] = "        What has disturbed my slumber again? This guest does not seem to be an old friend, nor is it any familiar friend.",
    ["        后来，不论是晋升通识者途径序列2的知识导师时，还是跨途径晋升窥秘人途径序列1知识皇帝时，甚至强行转到不相邻途径，晋升序列0黑皇帝时，我都曾回想过当初的选择——选择非凡途径，就是选择敌人和盟友。"] = "        Later, whether it was when I advanced to Sequence 2 Knowledge Mentor of the Savant pathway, or crossed pathways to advance to Sequence 1 Knowledge Emperor of the Mystery Pryer pathway, or even forcibly switched to a non-adjacent pathway to advance to Sequence 0 Black Emperor, I have always recalled my initial choice—choosing a Beyonder pathway is choosing your enemies and allies.",
    ["        听，这是因蒂斯民众的呼声！执政官罗塞尔·古斯塔夫，我喜欢这个称呼。\n        在这场与索伦家族的博弈中，我险胜一筹。但他们不愧是从第四纪存续至今的古老家族，底蕴和积累深厚得可怕。要不是因蒂斯深陷纷乱已久，民众的不满日益滋长，我根本无法点燃暴乱的火星，站到现在的位置上。\n        接下来，就是逐步推行那些我构思已久的政策。当然，首先是——\n        旧城区真是太脏了！爱国卫生行动必须尽快推广，首都下水道和公共厕所也要尽快改善。所有居民都要烧水喝、勤洗手，不许乱扔垃圾和随地大小便！\n        顺便，每个人都要接受义务教育，"] = "Listen, this is the voice of the Intis people! Consul Roselle Gustav, I like this title. \n In this game of chess with the Sauron Family, I won by a narrow margin. But they are indeed an ancient family that has survived since the Fourth Epoch; their foundation and accumulation are terrifyingly deep. If it weren't for the fact that Intis had been mired in chaos for a long time and the dissatisfaction of the people was growing, I would never have been able to ignite the sparks of riot and stand in my current position. \n Next, it's time to gradually implement the policies I've been conceiving for a long time. Of course, first is— \n The Old City is just too dirty! Patriotic health campaigns must be promoted as soon as possible, and the capital's sewers and public toilets must also be improved as soon as possible. All residents must boil water to drink, wash their hands frequently, and are not allowed to litter or urinate and defecate everywhere! \n By the way, everyone must receive compulsory education,",
    ["        听，这是因蒂斯民众的呼声！执政官罗塞尔·古斯塔夫，我喜欢这个称呼。\n        在这场与索伦家族的博弈中，我险胜一筹。但他们不愧是从第四纪存续至今的古老家族，底蕴和积累深厚得可怕。要不是因蒂斯深陷纷乱已久，民众的不满日益滋长，我根本无法点燃暴乱的火星，站到现在的位置上。\n        接下来，就是逐步推行那些我构思已久的政策。当然，首先是——\n        旧城区真是太脏了！爱国卫生行动必须尽快推广，首都下水道和公共厕所也要尽快改善。所有居民都要烧水喝、勤洗手，不许乱扔垃圾和随地大小便！\n        顺便，每个人都要接受义务教育，都要接受招生考试的毒打！每一个！\n        我要打造一个干净温馨、整洁明亮，处处是诗歌，家家有花草的首都特里尔。\n        但永恒烈阳教会那群家伙是傻子吗？\n        我保护贸易与推行新法的目的之一，就是为了与他们和解啊！和气生财的道理懂不懂？要追究谋权篡位的事到什么时候，他们果然是被太阳烤坏了脑袋——该死，有点想念故乡的烤脑花了。"] = "Listen, this is the voice of the Intis people! Consul Roselle Gustav, I like this title. \n In this game of chess against the Sauron family, I won by a narrow margin. But they truly deserve to be an ancient family that has survived since the Fourth Epoch; their foundation and accumulation are terrifyingly deep. If it weren't for the fact that Intis had been mired in chaos for so long and the people's dissatisfaction was growing daily, I would never have been able to ignite the sparks of rebellion and stand where I am today. \n Next, it is time to gradually implement the policies I have been conceiving for a long time. Of course, first is— \n The old city district is just too dirty! The patriotic health campaign must be promoted as soon as possible, and the capital's sewers and public toilets must be improved quickly. All residents must boil water to drink, wash their hands frequently, and are forbidden from littering or urinating and defecating in public! \n By the way, everyone must receive compulsory education and suffer the torture of entrance exams! Everyone! \n I want to build a clean, cozy, tidy, and bright capital of Trier, where poetry is everywhere and every home has flowers and plants. \n But are those guys in the Church of the Eternal Blazing Sun idiots? \n One of my purposes for protecting trade and promoting new laws was to reconcile with them! Don't they understand the principle that harmony brings wealth? How long are they going to pursue the matter of usurping power? They must have had their brains baked by the sun—damn it, I kind of miss the grilled brains from my hometown.",
    ["        在因蒂斯共和国越发强盛时，罗塞尔·古斯塔夫不再将野心局限在国家内部，而是将目光投向了整片大陆。\n        他南征北战，利用自己的各种发明，带领军队让鲁恩王国、费内波特王国、弗萨克帝国等北大陆强国相继低头，将伦堡等小国纳入保护范围。他还在狂暴海之中开辟了新航道，找到了南大陆，殖民时代从此开始。\n        他不再满足执政官的位置。1192年，罗塞尔·古斯塔夫将因蒂斯共和国重新改为帝国，自称“凯撒大帝”。\n        他成为一位真正的帝王，一位逐渐威严冷酷的帝王。"] = "        As the Intis Republic became more and more powerful, Roselle Gustav no longer limited his ambition to the interior of the country, but set his sights on the entire continent. \n He fought north and south, using his various inventions to lead his army to make powerful nations of the Northern Continent such as the Loen Kingdom, Feynapotter Kingdom, and Feysac Empire bow their heads one after another, and brought small countries like Lenburg under his protection. He also opened up new shipping lanes in the Berserk Sea and found the Southern Continent, and the colonial era began from then on. \n He was no longer satisfied with the position of Consul. In 1192, Roselle Gustav changed the Intis Republic back into an Empire and proclaimed himself \"Emperor Caesar.\" \n He became a true monarch, a monarch who gradually became majestic and cold.",
    ["        在罗塞尔大帝的末年，反对他的力量逐渐集结强大，他似乎被神明和时代厌倦。\n        英雄也会陨落，正如每天的太阳都会落下。1198年，他被刺杀，陨落于白枫宫。\n        这是一个传奇皇帝的一生，一个时代主角的一生。属于他的时代结束了，但人们还在传唱着他所著的诗歌，使用着他的发明，航行在他开辟的航道中……生活在被他颁布的律法与制度影响的城市中。\n        罗塞尔·古斯塔夫，永远的罗塞尔大帝。"] = "        In the later years of Emperor Roselle, the forces opposing him gradually gathered and became strong, and he seemed to be tired of by the gods and the era. \n Heroes will also fall, just as the sun sets every day. In 1198, he was assassinated and fell in the White Maple Palace. \n This is the life of a legendary emperor, the life of a protagonist of an era. The era that belonged to him has ended, but people are still singing the poems he wrote, using his inventions, sailing the shipping lanes he opened... living in cities influenced by the laws and systems he promulgated. \n Roselle Gustav, the eternal Emperor Roselle.",
    ["        在黎明降临之前，因蒂斯被历史的阴影和现实的纷争笼罩。\n        直到1173年，罗塞尔·古斯塔夫高举革新的火光，带领这个国家走入了新的时代。他为这片混乱的土地带来新的秩序、律法与文明，将旧时代的腐朽肮脏全部涤清。\n        新的法律开始保障工人权益，义务教育让孩子们走入学堂，高等学校统一考试为国家培养人才，国家债券与基金的设立让因蒂斯的经济又一次复苏运转。《民法典》的光辉照耀在每个人的身上，就像破开迷雾的太阳。\n        因蒂斯首都特里尔又一次被欢笑与鲜花环绕，让我们赞美——\n        伟大的因蒂斯共和国！伟大的共和国执政官罗塞尔！"] = "        Before the dawn arrived, Intis was shrouded in the shadows of history and the disputes of reality. \n Until 1173, Roselle Gustav held high the torch of innovation and led this country into a new era. He brought new order, laws, and civilization to this chaotic land, cleansing all the decay and filth of the old era. \n New laws began to protect the rights of workers, compulsory education allowed children to enter schools, unified entrance examinations for higher education cultivated talents for the country, and the establishment of national bonds and funds allowed the Intis economy to recover and operate once again. The brilliance of the Civil Code shone upon everyone, like the sun breaking through the fog. \n The Intis capital, Trier, was once again surrounded by laughter and flowers. Let us praise— \n The great Intis Republic! The great Republic Consul Roselle!",
    ["        夏尔，算算时间他应该已经去世了。死亡是一份礼物，希望他能作为普通人去度过幸福的一生。这是我们其他所有人都无法获得的平静……\n        博诺瓦……该死的蒸汽与机械之神，别让我逮到你！还有查拉图和“门”，等我复活了，我绝对一个个上门好好拜访！我的孩子应当肆意自由地活着，而不是成为神明的傀儡！不知道他那纯粹的神性中，有没有那么一点对我这个父亲的爱……一点点就够了。\n        心爱的贝尔纳黛，应验了查拉图的预言，她终究憎恨、厌弃和离开了我。不知道我被刺杀后她怎么样了……\n        头开始疼了，那家伙的呓语声真是难听。我又得睡了，我不会将这份污染带到这个世界上，这里还有我想守护的东西。哈哈，就跟我一起被封印在这里吧！\n        但我终会归来，只要我的子民还在信仰我，只要我留下的文明与规则没有消逝，只要这个世界还有人记得我的名字……连归来的口号我都想好了——因蒂斯的子民们，你们的皇帝回来了！\n        但在又一次的沉眠前，我似乎看到了一些被我遗忘了许久的东西……炸鸡、可乐、游戏机、家，和好像老去了一些的爸妈……\n        那是或许平凡乏味但再也回不去的人生。\n        故乡啊……"] = "        Charles, calculating the time, he should have passed away by now. Death is a gift; I hope he can spend a happy life as an ordinary person. This is a peace that none of the rest of us can ever obtain...\n        Bernadette... damn you, God of Steam and Machinery, don't let me catch you! And Zarathul and the \"Door,\" once I am resurrected, I will definitely visit you one by one! My child should live freely and wantonly, not become a puppet of the gods! I wonder if there is even a tiny bit of love for me, her father, in that pure divinity of hers... just a little bit would be enough.\n        My beloved Bernadette, Zarathul's prophecy has come true; she eventually hated, abandoned, and left me. I wonder how she is doing after I was assassinated...\n        My head is starting to ache; that guy's babbling is truly unpleasant. I have to sleep again. I will not bring this corruption into this world; there are still things here I want to protect. Haha, just be sealed here with me!\n        But I will eventually return, as long as my people still believe in me, as long as the civilization and rules I left behind have not faded, as long as there is still someone in this world who remembers my name... I have even thought of the slogan for my return—People of Intis, your Emperor has returned!\n        But before falling into another slumber, I seem to have seen some things I had forgotten for a long time... fried chicken, cola, game consoles, home, and my parents who seem to have aged a bit...\n        That is a life that might have been ordinary and dull, but one I can never return to.\n        My homeland...",
    ["        将近两百年过去了，我还是会反复回想起那个难忘的起点，非凡之路的起点——"] = "        Nearly two hundred years have passed, and I still repeatedly recall that unforgettable starting point, the starting point of the Beyonder path—",
    ["        很久没有再写日记了，在这个黑暗的陵寝中，在疯狂与污染交织的缝隙里，清醒是困难的。\n        回首这一生，我从一个普通的穿越者，变成了改变世界的大帝。我发明了蒸汽机，建立了共和国，征服了海洋，书写了法律……但我也失去了太多——我的故乡，我的平凡，我的孩子们的爱，还有……我自己。\n        黄涛，你还记得吗？那个在地球上熬夜看小说、打游戏、抱怨工作的普通青年？那个想念妈妈做的红烧肉、想念和朋友撸串吹牛的普通人？有时候我觉得自己好像做了一个很长的梦，梦里我成为了无所不能的大帝，但醒来时，我只"] = "        It has been a long time since I last wrote in my diary. In this dark mausoleum, in the gaps where madness and corruption intertwine, staying clear-headed is difficult.\n        Looking back on this life, I went from an ordinary transmigrator to an Emperor who changed the world. I invented the steam engine, established the republic, conquered the oceans, and wrote the laws... but I also lost too much—my homeland, my ordinariness, the love of my children, and... myself.\n        Huang Tao, do you still remember? That ordinary young man on Earth who stayed up late reading novels, playing games, and complaining about work? That ordinary person who missed his mother's braised pork, missed hanging out with friends, eating skewers, and bragging? Sometimes I feel like I had a very long dream, in which I became an omnipotent Emperor, but when I wake up, I only",
    ["        很久没有再写日记了，在这个黑暗的陵寝中，在疯狂与污染交织的缝隙里，清醒是困难的。\n        回首这一生，我从一个普通的穿越者，变成了改变世界的大帝。我发明了蒸汽机，建立了共和国，征服了海洋，书写了法律……但我也失去了太多——我的故乡，我的平凡，我的孩子们的爱，还有……我自己。\n        黄涛，你还记得吗？那个在地球上熬夜看小说、打游戏、抱怨工作的普通青年？那个想念妈妈做的红烧肉、想念和朋友撸串吹牛的普通人？有时候我觉得自己好像做了一个很长的梦，梦里我成为了无所不能的大帝，但醒来时，我只想要一张回家的车票。\n        但我知道，我回不去了。即使成为真神，即使拥有改变一切的力量，我也回不去那个有网络、有外卖、有平凡幸福的家了。\n        所以，我只能把这里当成我的家，把这个世界当成我另一个的家乡。\n        我留下了蒸汽机，留下了法律，留下了航道，留下了故事和诗歌……我希望这个世界能变得更好，希望后来的人能少受一些苦，希望他们能记住——曾经有一个人，从很远的地方来，把这里当成了自己的家。\n        贝尔纳黛，如果你能看到这份日记，我想告诉你：爸爸不是一个好皇帝，也不是一个好父亲。我做出了太多错误的选择，伤害了太多我爱的人。但如果重来一次，我还是会选择保护你，哪怕你看不到，哪怕你恨我。\n        还有夏尔、博诺瓦……我的孩子们。愿你们能在这个我亲手改变过的世界里，找到属于自己的幸福。\n        我也许又要沉眠了。我不知道，哪一次道别，会成为真正的告别。但不要悲伤。我，罗塞尔·古斯塔夫，黄涛——即使死亡，也要死得轰轰烈烈！况且……谁说我真的死了呢？\n        只要还有人记得我的名字，只要我的故事还在流传，只要这个世界还在使用我留下的发明和律法……我就从未真正离开。等着吧，总有一天，你们会听到那句话——\n        因蒂斯的子民们，你们的皇帝，回来了！"] = "It has been a long time since I wrote in my diary. In this dark mausoleum, in the gaps where madness and corruption intertwine, clarity is difficult. \n Looking back on this life, I went from an ordinary transmigrator to an Emperor who changed the world. I invented the steam engine, established the Republic, conquered the oceans, wrote the laws... but I also lost too much—my hometown, my ordinariness, the love of my children, and... myself. \n Huang Tao, do you remember? That ordinary young man on Earth who stayed up late reading novels, playing games, and complaining about work? That ordinary person who missed the braised pork made by his mom and missed hanging out with friends to eat skewers and brag? Sometimes I feel like I had a very long dream, in which I became an omnipotent Emperor, but when I wake up, I only want a ticket home. \n But I know, I can't go back. Even if I become a True God, even if I possess the power to change everything, I can't go back to that home with the internet, takeout, and ordinary happiness. \n So, I can only treat this place as my home and this world as my other hometown. \n I left behind the steam engine, the laws, the shipping routes, the stories, and the poems... I hope this world can become better, I hope later generations can suffer less, and I hope they can remember—there was once a person who came from very far away and treated this place as his own home. \n Bernadette, if you can see this diary, I want to tell you: Dad is not a good Emperor, nor is he a good father. I made too many wrong choices and hurt too many people I loved. But if I could do it all over again, I would still choose to protect you, even if you can't see it, even if you hate me. \n And Charles, Bernadette... my children. May you find your own happiness in this world that I changed with my own hands. \n I might have to sleep again. I don't know which farewell will be the real one. But don't be sad. I, Roselle Gustav, Huang Tao—even if I die, I will die with a bang! Besides... who said I really died? \n As long as there is still someone who remembers my name, as long as my story is still being told, as long as this world is still using the inventions and laws I left behind... I have never truly left. Just wait, one day, you will hear that sentence— \n Citizens of Intis, your Emperor has returned!",
    ["        我又一次感受到了祂的气息，这股堕落的、令人厌恶的力量。是祂引诱了我，将我逼上绝路，成为现在这副模样。这么多年过去了，祂依旧在窥视这个世界。"] = "        I have felt His aura once again, this corrupt, disgusting power. It was He who seduced me, forced me into a dead end, and turned me into this state. So many years have passed, and He is still peeking at this world.",
    ["        我始终不喜欢鲁恩那群家伙装模作样的架子，但在共同的敌人面前，无论是鲁恩、因蒂斯、费内波特还是任何别的国家，都需要站在同一战线上——为了守护我们的家园。"] = "        I have never liked the pretentious airs of those Loen fellows, but in the face of a common enemy, whether it is Loen, Intis, Feynapotter, or any other country, we must stand on the same front—to protect our home.",
    ["        我感受过太多不同的气息了，异样的、疯狂的、邪恶的、诡异的……"] = "        I have felt too many different auras—strange, mad, evil, bizarre...",
    ["        我是罗塞尔·古斯塔夫，但我要记得我真正的姓名——黄涛。\n        这封日记写于我自己的陵墓中，现在的我既没有活着、也没有死去，只是偶尔会获得短暂的清醒。我似乎迷失了很久，只能一遍又一遍回想我挂念的那些东西，让我不要真的被疯狂与污染控制。\n        可笑的是，我曾经拼命搏来的那些荣誉，什么蒸汽机、狗屎蒸汽之子，这些原本就不属于我的东西对稳定认知一点用都没有，只会反噬我。\n        我这辈子真正挂念的，是我的孩子们……"] = "I am Roselle Gustav, but I must remember my real name—Huang Tao. \n This diary was written in my own mausoleum. The current me is neither alive nor dead; I only occasionally gain brief moments of clarity. I seem to have been lost for a long time, and I can only recall the things I care about over and over again so that I am not truly controlled by madness and corruption. \n It is ridiculous that those honors I fought for with my life, like the steam engine, that bullshit Son of Steam—these things that didn't belong to me in the first place are of no use in stabilizing my cognition and will only backfire on me. \n The things I truly care about in this life are my children…",
    ["        我是罗塞尔·古斯塔夫，但我要记得我真正的姓名——黄涛。\n        这封日记写于我自己的陵墓中，现在的我既没有活着、也没有死去，只是偶尔会获得短暂的清醒。我似乎迷失了很久，只能一遍又一遍回想我挂念的那些东西，让我不要真的被疯狂与污染控制。\n        可笑的是，我曾经拼命搏来的那些荣誉，什么蒸汽机、狗屎蒸汽之子，这些原本就不属于我的东西对稳定认知一点用都没有，只会反噬我。\n        我这辈子真正挂念的，是我的孩子们……\n        夏尔，算算时间他应该已经去世了。死亡是一份礼物，希望他能作为普通人去度过幸福的一生。这是我们其他所有人都无法获得的平静……\n        博诺瓦……该死的蒸汽与机械之神，别让我逮到你！还有查拉图和“门”，等我复活了，我绝对一个个上门好好拜访！我的孩子应当肆意自由地活着，而不是成为神明的傀儡！不知道他那纯粹的神性中，有没有那么一点对我这个父亲的爱……一点点就够了。\n        心爱的贝尔纳黛，应验了查拉图的预言，她终究憎恨、厌弃和离开了我。不知道我被刺杀后她怎么样了……\n        头开始疼了，那家伙的呓语声真是难听。我又得睡了，我不会将这份污染带到这个世界上，这里还有我想守护的东西。哈哈，就跟我一起被封印在这里吧！\n        但我终会归来，只要我的子民还在信仰我，只要我留下的文明与规则没有消逝，只要这个世界还有人记得我的名字……连归来的口号我都想好了——因蒂斯的子民们，你们的皇帝回来了！\n        但在又一次的沉眠前，我似乎看到了一些被我遗忘了许久的东西……炸鸡、可乐、游戏机、家，和好像老去了一些的爸妈……\n        那是或许平凡乏味但再也回不去的人生。\n        故乡啊……"] = "I am Roselle Gustav, but I must remember my real name—Huang Tao. \n This diary was written in my own mausoleum. Right now, I am neither alive nor dead; I only occasionally gain brief moments of clarity. I seem to have been lost for a long time, and I can only recall the things I care about over and over again so that I am not truly controlled by madness and corruption. \n It is ridiculous that the honors I once fought for, all that steam engine stuff, that bullshit Son of Steam, these things that never belonged to me are of no use in stabilizing my cognition and will only backfire on me. \n What I truly care about in this life are my children... \n Charles, calculating the time, he should have passed away by now. Death is a gift; I hope he can spend a happy life as an ordinary person. This is the peace that none of the rest of us can obtain... \n Bernadette... damn God of Steam and Machinery, don't let me catch you! And Zaratul and the \"Door,\" once I am resurrected, I will definitely visit each of you! My children should live freely and wantonly, not become puppets of the gods! I don't know if there is even a little bit of love for me, their father, in that pure divinity of his... a little bit is enough. \n Beloved Bernadette, the prophecy of Zaratul has come true; she eventually hated, abandoned, and left me. I don't know how she is after I was assassinated... \n My head is starting to hurt; that guy's gibberish is really unpleasant. I have to sleep again. I will not bring this corruption into this world; there are still things I want to protect here. Haha, just be sealed here with me! \n But I will eventually return, as long as my people still believe in me, as long as the civilization and rules I left behind have not faded, as long as there is still someone in this world who remembers my name... I have even thought of the slogan for my return—Citizens of Intis, your Emperor has returned! \n But before falling into another slumber, I seem to have seen some things I had forgotten for a long time... fried chicken, cola, game consoles, home, and my parents who seem to have aged a bit... \n That is a life that might have been ordinary and dull but can never be returned to. \n Hometown...",
    ["        我曾以为我会愤怒，会不甘，会咆哮着控诉命运的不公和众神的狡诈。"] = "        I once thought I would be angry, unwilling, and roar in accusation of the unfairness of fate and the cunning of the gods.",
    ["        我曾经是这片大地的主人，手持火炮、纵横五海。在属于我的年代里，踩在所有国家的头上，何等畅快！"] = "        I was once the master of this land, holding cannons and traversing the five seas. In the era that belonged to me, stepping on the heads of all countries, how refreshing it was!",
    ["        我看不清楚祂真正的模样，只觉得这丰饶的气息似曾相识……"] = "        I cannot see His true appearance clearly, I only feel that this scent of abundance is familiar...",
    ["        我站在“黑王座号”的船头，张开双臂，对格林和爱德华兹他们说：“想要我的财宝吗？那就到迷雾海的尽头来寻找吧，我将所有的财宝都藏在了这里！”\n        但他们完全不懂我的幽默，竟然问我是不是真的有额外的财宝。真是无趣啊，你们这样是做不了我的天启四骑士的！但他们依旧愿意追随我在那片充满迷雾的海洋里冒险。\n        我一直在想，北大陆西边是迷雾海，东面是苏尼亚海，我怀疑这两大海洋的尽头还有别的大陆，就像狂暴海的尽头是南大陆一样，说不定我能发现一个全新的大陆，西大陆！"] = "I stood at the bow of the \"Black Throne,\" spread my arms, and said to Green, Edwards, and the others, \"Do you want my treasure? Then go find it at the end of the Fog Sea; I have hidden all my treasure there!\" \n But they completely failed to understand my humor and actually asked if I really had extra treasure. How boring; you guys can't be my Four Horsemen of the Apocalypse like this! But they are still willing to follow me on adventures in that ocean full of fog. \n I have been thinking, to the west of the Northern Continent is the Fog Sea, and to the east is the Sonia Sea. I suspect that there are other continents at the ends of these two great oceans, just like the end of the Berserk Sea is the Southern Continent. Maybe I can discover a brand new continent, the Western Continent!",
    ["        我站在“黑王座号”的船头，张开双臂，对格林和爱德华兹他们说：“想要我的财宝吗？那就到迷雾海的尽头来寻找吧，我将所有的财宝都藏在了这里！”\n        但他们完全不懂我的幽默，竟然问我是不是真的有额外的财宝。真是无趣啊，你们这样是做不了我的天启四骑士的！但他们依旧愿意追随我在那片充满迷雾的海洋里冒险。\n        我一直在想，北大陆西边是迷雾海，东面是苏尼亚海，我怀疑这两大海洋的尽头还有别的大陆，就像狂暴海的尽头是南大陆一样，说不定我能发现一个全新的大陆，西大陆！\n        出发吧，大航海家罗塞尔·哥伦布·麦哲伦·古斯塔夫，去验证你的猜想吧！"] = "I stood at the bow of the \"Black Throne,\" spread my arms, and said to Green and Edwards and the others: \"Do you want my treasure? Then go to the end of the Fog Sea to find it; I have hidden all my treasures there!\" \n But they didn't understand my humor at all and actually asked me if there was really any extra treasure. How boring; you guys can't be my Four Knights of the Apocalypse like this! But they were still willing to follow me on adventures in that sea full of fog. \n I have been thinking, to the west of the Northern Continent is the Fog Sea, and to the east is the Sonia Sea. I suspect that there are other continents at the ends of these two great oceans, just like the Southern Continent is at the end of the Berserk Sea. Maybe I can discover a brand new continent, the Western Continent! \n Set sail, great navigator Roselle Columbus Magellan Gustav, go and verify your conjecture!",
    ["        所以，再次睡去吧，直到那个应该醒来的时刻。"] = "        So, go to sleep again, until the moment that I should wake up.",
    ["        最近日记写得越来越少了，我察觉到体内仿佛有另一个自己在苏醒，这不仅仅来源于高序列的疯狂，也来源于……星空的某种污染。这污染伴随我似乎很久了……\n        我是怎么走到这种地步的呢？我也忘记了。\n        陵寝已经建好，我要自己走进那座坟墓了。\n        永恒烈阳教会的那群家伙和索伦家族惦记我这条命已经很久了，这次，就送他们一份大礼吧。"] = "        I've been writing less and less in my diary lately. I sense another self awakening within my body. This doesn't just come from the madness of high Sequences, but also from... some kind of corruption from the starry sky. This corruption seems to have been with me for a long time... \n        How did I end up like this? I've forgotten too. \n        The mausoleum has been built, and I must walk into that grave myself. \n        The Eternal Blazing Sun Church and the Solomon family have been eyeing my life for a long time. This time, I'll give them a big gift.",
    ["        有趣，有趣，原来是这样……"] = "        Interesting, interesting, so that's how it is...",
    ["        末日……还有多久？"] = "        The apocalypse... how much time is left?",
    ["        现在，还不是真正的我该醒来的时候。"] = "        Now, it is not the time for the real me to wake up.",
    ["        班森踱了几步，一脸严肃地反驳道：\n         “不，没有之一。”\n        没有之一……克莱恩愣了愣，很快反应过来，与哥哥相视而笑。\n        果然是班森擅长的嘲讽式幽默。\n        班森嘴角上翘，一本正经地补充道：\n         “你应该明白，要制定一个合理又简单的币制需要一个前提，那就是懂得数数，掌握了十进制，可惜，在那些大人物里面，这样的人才太稀少了。”\n\n        ——第一卷《小丑》第二十六章 练习"] = "Benson paced a few steps and retorted with a serious face: \n “No, there is no one else.” \n No one else… Klein was stunned for a moment, then quickly reacted and smiled at his brother. \n It was indeed the taunting humor that Benson was good at. \n Benson raised the corners of his mouth and added solemnly: \n “You should understand that to formulate a reasonable and simple currency system, there is a prerequisite, which is knowing how to count and mastering the decimal system. Unfortunately, among those big shots, such talents are too rare.” \n \n —— Volume 1: Clown, Chapter 26: Practice",
    ["        硝烟，争夺，死亡，战争……又要开始了。"] = "        Gunsmoke, strife, death, war... it is about to begin again.",
    ["        祂还没有放弃污染我、利用我，哪怕只是一抹被遗留在非凡特性里的残存意识……"] = "        He has not yet given up on corrupting me, using me, even if it is only a remnant consciousness left in a Beyonder characteristic...",
    ["        纵观罗塞尔大帝的传奇一生，除了陆地上的革新与统治，他也是海洋上的传奇与霸主。 \n        他充满探索欲和开拓精神，带领舰队在五海的风暴中探索。他发现了狂暴海中的安全航道，开启了对南大陆的殖民时代。无论是为了黄金还是资源，无论是为了探索还是掠夺……不可否认的是，罗塞尔对于海上航道的探索，为这个世界开启了一个新的时代。\n         伴随着争议、奴役、罪恶和咒骂，五海之上的将军与王者们，曾歌颂他的名；借助安全航道，登上南大陆的殖民者们，曾歌颂他的名；从事南北大陆贸易，促进南北大陆通商的商人们，曾歌颂他的名。\n        他在冒险和开拓中，拓宽了这个世界的边界。"] = "        Looking back at the legendary life of Emperor Roselle, besides his innovation and rule on land, he was also a legend and hegemon on the ocean. \n He was full of desire for exploration and a pioneering spirit, leading his fleet to explore the storms of the Five Seas. He discovered the safe shipping lanes in the Berserk Sea and opened the colonial era of the Southern Continent. Whether for gold or resources, whether for exploration or plunder... it is undeniable that Roselle's exploration of sea routes opened a new era for this world. \n Accompanied by controversy, slavery, sin, and curses, the generals and kings of the Five Seas once sang his name; with the help of safe shipping lanes, the colonists who landed on the Southern Continent once sang his name; the merchants who engaged in trade between the Northern and Southern Continents and promoted commerce between them once sang his name. \n In adventure and pioneering, he broadened the boundaries of this world.",
    ["        罗塞尔·古斯塔夫已经死去一百五十多年了，但他的名字从未被遗忘。\n        在因蒂斯的首都特里尔，他的雕像依然矗立在广场中央。每年他的诞辰，人们都会举行盛大的活动来纪念他。鲁恩王国的工厂里，工人们使用着他发明的机器，孩子们在学校里学习着他推行的知识。迷雾海的商船沿着他开辟的航道航行，南大陆的殖民地里，冒险者们讲述着他的传说。\n        他是一个穿越者，一个异乡人，一个永远回不去故乡的游子。但他也是蒸汽之子，因蒂斯共和国的执政官，凯撒大帝，罗塞尔大帝，一个强大的非凡者，一个父亲——一个改变了整个世界的人。\n        他犯过错，走过弯路，被污染，被背叛，最终陨落于白枫宫。但他也创造过，保护过，爱过，留下过一个时代的辉煌与文明。\n        也许正如他在日记中写的那样：如果能够重来，他或许会选择做一个普通人，回到那个有炸鸡和可乐的世界，陪在父母身边，过着平凡而温暖的一生。但历史没有如果。罗塞尔·古斯塔夫无可选择地成为时代的主角。\n        我们对罗塞尔大帝的一生了解得还不够多，但我们知道他是——一个时代的开端，一个闪耀的传奇，一个永不褪色的名字。"] = "Roselle Gustav has been dead for over one hundred and fifty years, but his name has never been forgotten. \n In Trier, the capital of Intis, his statue still stands in the center of the square. Every year on his birthday, people hold grand events to commemorate him. In the factories of the Loen Kingdom, workers use the machines he invented, and children learn the knowledge he promoted in schools. Merchant ships in the Fog Sea sail along the routes he pioneered, and in the colonies of the Southern Continent, adventurers recount his legends. \n He was a transmigrator, a foreigner, a wanderer who could never return to his homeland. But he was also the Son of Steam, the Consul of the Intis Republic, Caesar the Great, Emperor Roselle, a powerful Beyonder, a father—a man who changed the entire world. \n He made mistakes, took detours, was corrupted, and was betrayed, eventually falling in the White Maple Palace. But he also created, protected, loved, and left behind the brilliance and civilization of an era. \n Perhaps as he wrote in his diary: if he could do it all over again, he might have chosen to be an ordinary person, returning to that world with fried chicken and cola, staying by his parents' side, and living an ordinary and warm life. But history has no 'ifs.' Roselle Gustav had no choice but to become the protagonist of the era. \n We do not know enough about Emperor Roselle's life, but we know what he was—the beginning of an era, a shining legend, a name that never fades.",
    ["        罗塞尔戏剧节又是……呵呵，我明白了。难为她想出了这种主意，不愧是我的女儿。可惜，我的本体无法离开这座陵墓，不然一定要去凑凑热闹。"] = "        The Roselle Theater Festival is... Heh, I understand. It's hard for her to come up with such an idea; she is worthy of being my daughter. It's a pity that my true body cannot leave this mausoleum, otherwise I would definitely go and join in the fun.",
    ["        自从成为天使后，我能感受到自己人性的逐渐流失。\n        子民们就是我的锚，是他们的赞美让我不至于失控。整片大陆都在呼喊我的名字，特里尔远比以前宏伟热闹，但当我戴着王冠坐在王座上时，却只觉得厌倦……\n        从月亮上回来后，我终于看清了这个世界的疯狂与扭曲。哈哈哈哈，原来的我简直像个小丑，捧着一点机遇与成就就洋洋得意，自以为是时代的主角。但这一切都终将毁灭，我所创造的一切，所热爱的东西，这座城市，这个国家，这片大陆，甚至这个星球，终究……"] = "Ever since I became an Angel, I have been able to feel the gradual loss of my humanity. \n My subjects are my anchors; it is their praise that keeps me from losing control. The entire continent is calling my name, and Trier is far more magnificent and lively than before, but when I sit on the throne wearing the crown, I only feel weary… \n After returning from the moon, I finally saw the madness and distortion of this world. Hahahaha, the original me was like a clown, holding onto a little bit of opportunity and achievement, feeling smug and thinking I was the protagonist of the era. But all of this will eventually be destroyed; everything I created, everything I loved, this city, this country, this continent, and even this planet, will eventually…",
    ["        自从成为天使后，我能感受到自己人性的逐渐流失。\n        子民们就是我的锚，是他们的赞美让我不至于失控。整片大陆都在呼喊我的名字，特里尔远比以前宏伟热闹，但当我戴着王冠坐在王座上时，却只觉得厌倦……\n        从月亮上回来后，我终于看清了这个世界的疯狂与扭曲。哈哈哈哈，原来的我简直像个小丑，捧着一点机遇与成就就洋洋得意，自以为是时代的主角。但这一切都终将毁灭，我所创造的一切，所热爱的东西，这座城市，这个国家，这片大陆，甚至这个星球，终究……\n        只有成为真神，才能守护我想保护的东西。但无论是“窥秘人”还是“通识者”途径的成神之路都已经被堵死了。隔着遥远的时光，我突然理解那位“血皇帝”为什么会做出那样疯狂的选择，有机会可真想跟他喝上一杯。\n        我也是真的疯了，不是吗？"] = "Ever since I became an Angel, I have been able to feel the gradual loss of my humanity. \n The citizens are my anchors; it is their praise that keeps me from losing control. The entire continent is shouting my name, and Trier is far more magnificent and lively than before, but when I sit on the throne wearing the crown, I only feel weary... \n After returning from the moon, I finally saw the madness and distortion of this world. Hahahaha, the original me was just like a clown, holding onto a little opportunity and achievement, feeling smug and thinking I was the protagonist of the era. But all of this will eventually be destroyed; everything I created, everything I loved, this city, this country, this continent, even this planet, will eventually... \n Only by becoming a True God can I protect what I want to protect. But the paths to godhood for both the Mystery Pryer and Savant pathways have already been blocked. Across the distant time, I suddenly understand why that \"Blood Emperor\" would make such a crazy choice. If there were a chance, I would really like to have a drink with him. \n I am truly crazy too, aren't I?",
    ["        虽然它的能力已不足巅峰的十分之一，但毕竟曾是我最骄傲的设计，必须尽早将它压制封印……小家伙们，交给你们了，不要再让绯红降临在大地上。"] = "        Although its power is less than a tenth of its peak, it was, after all, my proudest design. It must be suppressed and sealed as soon as possible... Little ones, I leave it to you. Do not let the crimson descend upon the earth again.",
    ["        贝尔纳黛·古斯塔夫，罗塞尔·古斯塔夫的长女，前因蒂斯皇女，最受罗塞尔宠爱的孩子。\n        她诞生于罗塞尔执政前，在罗塞尔执政时站在父亲的身侧共沐荣光，却在罗塞尔成为大帝后离开因蒂斯。\n        没有人知道这位皇女去了哪里，宫廷里的人说在“那段时间”，他们经常听到大帝与皇女争吵的声音。也有人说罗塞尔预言了自己的死亡，早早地让自己最心爱的女儿离开，不要被纷争波及。\n        喧嚣并未随着大帝的陨落而沉默，反而随着时间的流逝而成为历史、传奇或传记中的一部分。在这些真真假假的传说中，有人说曾在大海上见过神似贝尔纳黛·古斯塔夫的人，而她要去往的方向似乎指向了狂暴海。\n        那人说得笃定，自称祖先曾是罗塞尔大帝的宫廷侍从，家中珍藏皇女油画像一幅，绝不会认错，下一秒却因为醉酒又欠钱跟人打成一团。\n        而此时，距罗塞尔大帝的陨落已经过去了一百五十四年。"] = "Bernadette Gustav, the eldest daughter of Roselle Gustav, former Intis Princess, and the child most favored by Roselle. \n She was born before Roselle took power and stood by her father's side to share in the glory during his reign, yet she left Intis after Roselle became Emperor. \n No one knows where this princess went. People in the palace said that during \"that period,\" they often heard the sounds of arguments between the Emperor and the Princess. Others said that Roselle had foreseen his own death and had his most beloved daughter leave early so she would not be caught up in the conflict. \n The clamor did not fall silent with the Emperor's fall; instead, as time passed, it became a part of history, legends, or biographies. Among these true and false tales, some say they have seen someone resembling Bernadette Gustav on the high seas, and the direction she was heading seemed to point toward the Berserk Sea. \n That person spoke with certainty, claiming their ancestor was a court attendant to Emperor Roselle and that a portrait of the Princess was treasured in their home, insisting they could never be mistaken, only to get into a brawl with others the next second due to being drunk and in debt. \n At this time, one hundred and fifty-four years had passed since the fall of Emperor Roselle.",
    ["        这个世界实在是太无聊了！连像样的小说也没有，更别提网文、游戏和电影了，只能靠我自己来写了。\n        穿越到这个世界已经很久了，自从成为“通识者”途径的非凡者后，我靠着魔药的力量完整地回想起以前学过的所有知识，赞美义务教育与我的二本学历！然后我大抄特抄……哦，是将先进的文化与知识传播到这个世界。\n        凭借着才华与魅力，贵族们拉拢我，教会也喜欢我，没落的古斯塔夫家族又一次站在这个王国的顶端，我那便宜老爹老妈真应该谢谢我。但也有些想念我真正的家，成为这个途径的非凡者也是为了找到回家的方法。黄涛啊黄"] = "This world is just too boring! There are no decent novels, let alone web novels, games, or movies; I have to write them myself. \n It has been a long time since I crossed into this world. Ever since I became a Beyonder of the \"Savant\" pathway, I have relied on the power of the potion to fully recall all the knowledge I learned before. Praise compulsory education and my undergraduate degree! Then I copied and copied… oh, I mean, I spread advanced culture and knowledge to this world. \n Relying on talent and charm, the nobles court me, the Church likes me, and the fallen Gustav Family stands at the top of this kingdom once again. My cheap old man and old lady should really thank me. But I also miss my real home. Becoming a Beyonder of this pathway is also to find a way home. Huang Tao, ah Huang",
    ["        这个世界实在是太无聊了！连像样的小说也没有，更别提网文、游戏和电影了，只能靠我自己来写了。\n        穿越到这个世界已经很久了，自从成为“通识者”途径的非凡者后，我靠着魔药的力量完整地回想起以前学过的所有知识，赞美义务教育与我的二本学历！然后我大抄特抄……哦，是将先进的文化与知识传播到这个世界。\n        凭借着才华与魅力，贵族们拉拢我，教会也喜欢我，没落的古斯塔夫家族又一次站在这个王国的顶端，我那便宜老爹老妈真应该谢谢我。但也有些想念我真正的家，成为这个途径的非凡者也是为了找到回家的方法。黄涛啊黄涛，可不能忘了初衷，还是要勤奋提升序列。\n        那个“占卜家”途径的老骗子查拉图虽然教了我不少非凡知识，但一旦涉及到真正的隐秘，他就开始笑而不语，说来说去还是要我帮他去偷教会里那本安提哥努斯笔记。\n        再说一遍，等我成为高序列强者，看到一个占卜家就揍一个！"] = "This world is just too boring! There aren't even any decent novels, let alone web novels, games, or movies; I have to write them myself. \n It has been a long time since I transmigrated to this world. Ever since I became a Beyonder of the Savant pathway, I have been able to recall all the knowledge I learned before thanks to the power of the potion. Praise compulsory education and my undergraduate degree! Then I copied everything... oh, I mean, I spread advanced culture and knowledge to this world. \n Relying on my talent and charm, the nobles courted me, the churches liked me, and the declining Gustav family stood at the pinnacle of this kingdom once again. My cheap old man and mom really should thank me. But I also miss my real home; becoming a Beyonder of this pathway is also to find a way back home. Huang Tao, oh Huang Tao, you must not forget your original intention; you still need to diligently increase your Sequence. \n That old liar Zaratul of the Seer pathway taught me quite a bit of Beyonder knowledge, but whenever it involves true secrets, he starts smiling without a word, saying over and over that I need to help him steal that Antigonus Notebook from the church. \n Let me say it again: once I become a high-Sequence powerhouse, I will beat up every Seer I see!",
    ["        这依旧是一个我所熟悉的世界。你们使用的器物，行走的道路，演出的戏剧……都很好，都是我曾经构想过的模样——蒸汽在街巷中流淌，律法维护公平，铁甲舰和飞艇姿态昂扬……我就说我才是真正的时代主角，在我之前，众生蒙昧而活；在我之后，浪潮滚滚向前。而你们，已经卷入时代的洪流。"] = "        This is still a world I am familiar with. The artifacts you use, the paths you walk, the plays you perform... they are all very good, all the way I once envisioned—steam flowing in the alleys, laws maintaining fairness, ironclad ships and airships standing tall... I told you I was the true protagonist of the era. Before me, all living things lived in ignorance; after me, the waves roll forward. And you, you have already been swept into the torrent of the era.",
    ["        这次又是哪个倒霉鬼被祂盯上了，北大陆……鲁恩王国……廷根……五月庄园吗？"] = "        Which unlucky fellow has He set His eyes on this time? The Northern Continent... Loen Kingdom... Tingen... May Manor?",
    ["        这次，我又睡了多久？这股熟悉的气息……外面的世界发生了什么，吵闹到足以将我唤醒。"] = "        This time, how long have I slept again? This familiar scent... What has happened in the outside world, noisy enough to wake me up.",
    ["        那个引诱我的存在还在盘旋，那个污染我的力量还在窥视，但我知道，有人会替我守护这一切。因为我已经看到了——在未来的某一刻，当危机从星空而来，你们也是这个世界的希望之一……"] = "        That existence who seduced me is still circling, that power that corrupted me is still peeking, but I know that someone will protect all of this for me. Because I have already seen it—at some point in the future, when the crisis comes from the starry sky, you are also one of the hopes of this world...",
    ["        那时我有两个选择，成为通识者途径的非凡者，或者窥秘人途径的非凡者，我的选择很简单——通识者，拥有完整序列的通识者！让自身变得强大，依靠自己的力量回到故乡，而不是寄希望于危险的外力。但当初的选择还是太草率了，不管是学徒，还是占卜家，或者偷盗者，都更好。可惜，没办法回头了……"] = "        Back then, I had two choices: become a Beyonder of the Savant pathway, or a Beyonder of the Mystery Pryer pathway. My choice was simple—Savant, a Savant with a complete sequence! To make myself strong and rely on my own power to return to my hometown, rather than pinning my hopes on dangerous external forces. But my choice back then was still too rash. Whether it was Apprentice, Seer, or Marauder, all would have been better. Unfortunately, there is no turning back...",
    ["        非凡之路如同在狂暴的海洋上冒险和开拓，但非凡远比海洋疯狂和凶险……这两条道路，我都是亲历者。"] = "        The path of the Beyonder is like adventuring and pioneering on a Berserk Sea, but the extraordinary is far more mad and dangerous than the ocean... I have personally experienced both of these paths.",
    ["       梅丽莎微皱眉头道：\n       “为什么要坐公共马车？到学校得4个便士，来回就是8便士，算上你和班森，我们一天就要在公共马车上花费24便士，整整2苏勒，一周，嗯，不算周日，就是12苏勒，略等于我们的房租了！”\n       停停停，不要炫耀你的数学水平……克莱恩好笑地压了下手。\n       梅丽莎先是停顿，接着又补充了一句：\n       “我走路去学校挺好的，老师说每个人都要经常锻炼，而且我还能在路上捡到一些破损的零件。”\n\n       ——第一卷《小丑》第三十九章 有趣的技巧"] = "Melissa frowned slightly and said: \n “Why take a public carriage? It costs 4 pence to get to school, 8 pence for a round trip. Counting you and Benson, we would spend 24 pence on public carriages a day, a full 2 Soles. A week, well, not counting Sunday, is 12 Soles, which is slightly equal to our rent!” \n Stop, stop, stop, don’t show off your math skills… Klein pressed his hand down amusedly. \n Melissa paused first, then added: \n “I think it’s fine to walk to school. The teacher said everyone should exercise frequently, and I can pick up some damaged parts on the way.” \n \n —— Volume 1: Clown, Chapter 39: Interesting Technique",
    ["       梅丽莎深深看了他一眼，忽地转身，小跑步进了里间，拿出一个由齿轮、锈铁、弹簧和发条等拼凑成的乌龟状物品。\n快速扭紧发条，梅丽莎将这物品放在了书桌上。\n       咔咔咔，哒哒哒，那“乌龟”一跳一走，很有节律，让人不由自主就将注意力转移到了它身上。\n       “感觉烦恼的时候，看着它这么动一动，会舒服很多，我最近经常这样，很有效的！克莱恩，你试一试。”梅丽莎眸光明亮地邀请道。\n       克莱恩没拒绝妹妹的好意，凑近看着那“乌龟”，等到它停止才笑道：\n       “简单和规律确实能带来放松。”\n       不等梅丽莎再说，他指着“乌龟”，随口问道：\n       “自己做的？什么时候做的？我怎么不知道？”\n       “我用学校不要的材料和路上捡到的东西做的，前两天才弄好。”梅丽莎表情如常，嘴角翘了几分。\n       “很厉害啊。”克莱恩由衷赞道。\n       作为一名在机械方面动手能力差的男孩子，他小时候拼个四驱车都要死要活。\n       梅丽莎下巴微抬，眼睛略弯，语气平淡地回答：\n       “还好，还好。”\n       “过分的谦虚是坏品格。”克莱恩轻笑道，“这是只乌龟吧？”\n       房间内的气氛突然沉凝了一下，梅丽莎的嗓音幽幽如同绯红轻纱般响起：\n       “它是人偶。”\n\n       ——第一卷《小丑》第十六章 狗拿耗子"] = "Melissa looked at him deeply, suddenly turned around, trotted into the inner room, and took out a turtle-shaped object pieced together from gears, rusty iron, springs, and clockwork. \n Quickly tightening the clockwork, Melissa placed the object on the desk. \n Click, click, click, da, da, da, the “turtle” jumped and walked, very rhythmic, making people involuntarily shift their attention to it. \n “When you feel troubled, watching it move like this will make you feel much better. I’ve been doing this a lot lately, it’s very effective! Klein, you try it.” Melissa invited with bright eyes. \n Klein didn’t refuse his sister’s kindness, leaned close to watch the “turtle,” and didn’t smile until it stopped: \n “Simplicity and regularity can indeed bring relaxation.” \n Without waiting for Melissa to say more, he pointed to the “turtle” and asked casually: \n “Did you make it yourself? When did you make it? Why didn’t I know?” \n “I made it with materials the school didn’t want and things I picked up on the road. I just finished it two days ago.” Melissa’s expression was as usual, the corners of her mouth raised a little. \n “That’s amazing.” Klein praised sincerely. \n As a boy with poor hands-on ability in mechanics, he struggled to assemble a four-wheel drive car when he was a child. \n Melissa raised her chin slightly, her eyes curved slightly, and she replied in a flat tone: \n “It’s okay, it’s okay.” \n “Excessive modesty is a bad character.” Klein chuckled, “This is a turtle, right?” \n The atmosphere in the room suddenly condensed, and Melissa’s voice sounded like crimson gauze: \n “It’s a doll.” \n \n —— Volume 1: Clown, Chapter 16: A Dog Catching a Mouse",
    ["      “这份尸检报告相当完美，尤其是示意图的绘制……弗莱，听说你曾经想成为一位画家?”层层叠叠的卷宗后，戴莉微笑着抬头，看向面前青年沉默而苍白的面容。\n\n      “是的，戴莉女士。”弗莱略带意外地回答：“这的确对现在的工作有一定帮助。”\n      “在听说你会被调去贝克兰德后，弗莱就一直在学习，直到能顺利接手这部分事务。”房门被推开，邓恩握着一份文件走了进来。\n      他看向二人的目光深邃而温和：“你可以放心了，戴莉——以及，你的正式调令到了。”\n\n      文件在苦涩的咖啡香气中展开，戴莉将它接过，目光却在邓恩和弗莱身上来回流转，直到露出一个不带任何轻佻的微笑。\n      “我一直都很放心，毕竟在我之前和在我之后，都有那么可靠的守护者。”"] = "      \"This autopsy report is quite perfect, especially the drawing of the schematic... Frye, I heard you once wanted to be a painter?\" Behind layers of files, Daly looked up with a smile at the silent, pale face of the young man before her.\n\n      \"Yes, Ms. Daly.\" Frye answered with slight surprise: \"It does indeed help with my current work to some extent.\"\n      \"Ever since he heard he would be transferred to Backlund, Frye has been studying until he could smoothly take over this part of the affairs.\" The door was pushed open, and Dunn walked in holding a document.\n      His gaze toward the two was deep and gentle: \"You can rest easy, Daly—and, your official transfer order has arrived.\"\n\n      The document was unfolded amidst the bitter aroma of coffee. Daly took it, but her gaze wandered between Dunn and Frye until she revealed a smile without any hint of frivolity.\n      \"I have always been at ease, after all, both before me and after me, there have been such reliable Guardians.\"",
    ["      他们看到一个涂着红黄白等各色油彩的小丑跑了过来，不知从哪里变出了一束花，一束塞维亚菊。\n      这束花凑到了梅丽莎和班森眼前，颜色金黄，象征着快乐。\n      梅丽莎和班森略显茫然地望向对面的小丑，只见他满是红黄白等各色油彩的脸上，嘴角高高翘起，固定着一个快乐的笑容，浮夸的笑容，滑稽的笑容。"] = "      They saw a clown painted in various colors like red, yellow, and white run over, producing a bouquet of flowers from nowhere—a bouquet of Sevia chrysanthemums.\n      This bouquet was thrust in front of Melissa and Benson, its color golden, symbolizing happiness.\n      Melissa and Benson looked at the clown opposite them with slight bewilderment, only to see the corners of his mouth, on a face full of red, yellow, and white paint, curled high, fixed in a happy smile, an exaggerated smile, a comical smile.",
    ["      反隐"] = "      Anti-Invisibility",
    ["      善于观察筹谋、在一切之前做好预期，一直是阿尔杰的操守。然而现在，他的心理预期正在崩塌——\n      家具喷涌着牛奶，天花板降下蘑菇，散落的泥土像血肉一样鼓动，随后大副先生从土堆中探出头来。\n      “您好，我听船长说了，您想要之前对付原始月亮信徒的那种蘑菇。”弗兰克·李露出了热情的笑容。“得请您等一等。嗯，想来一些果汁吗？”\n      “果汁……”阿尔杰目光凝重地看向房间角落，有根长在牛肉上的藤条正流出清香的汁液。\n      “不了，我暂时不渴。”阿尔杰谨慎地摇了摇头。\n      弗兰克略显遗憾，不过很快再次露出笑容：“船长说我可以索取一些合理报酬……阿尔杰先生，您是水手途径的高序列非凡者……”\n      阿尔杰警惕了起来。\n      “能提供一些您海洋生物化后的血肉吗？我想知道这种‘鱼肉’能否和蘑菇发生反应……”"] = "      Being observant and calculating, and preparing for everything in advance, had always been Alger's code of conduct. However, his psychological expectations were now collapsing—\n      Furniture was spewing milk, mushrooms were descending from the ceiling, and the scattered soil was pulsating like flesh, after which Mr. First Mate poked his head out from the pile of dirt.\n      \"Hello, I heard from the Captain that you wanted the kind of mushrooms used against the Primordial Moon believers previously.\" Frank Lee revealed an enthusiastic smile. \"You'll have to wait a moment. Hmm, would you like some fruit juice?\"\n      \"Fruit juice...\" Alger looked solemnly toward the corner of the room, where a vine growing on beef was dripping with fragrant juice.\n      \"No, I'm not thirsty for now.\" Alger shook his head cautiously.\n      Frank looked slightly regretful, but soon smiled again: \"The Captain said I could request some reasonable compensation... Mr. Alger, you are a high-Sequence Beyonder of the Sailor pathway...\"\n      Alger became vigilant.\n      \"Could you provide some of your flesh after your marine creature transformation? I want to know if this 'fish meat' can react with the mushrooms...\"",
    ["      在不被目标发现的情况下跟踪对方，是值夜者的必修技巧。这堂课的考核内容由老尼尔布置：监视一名外来逃犯，掌握其行动规律。\n      伦纳德，气质潇洒的不眠者，向着午夜诗人的方向高歌猛进；弗莱，气质阴郁的收尸人，成为非凡者后更向着冰冷阴暗一去不回。这样的两个人，想要隐匿在人群中，是一件挑战。\n      伦纳德换上粗布工装，出没在目标居住的街角。第二天，有人来问他是不是在等人，第三天，逃犯更换了居住地，第四天，他发现自己被人跟上。甩开跟踪者后，郁闷的伦纳德回到黑荆棘，弗莱已经坐在桌边等他。\n      “你是怎么做到的，弗莱？我监视了他好几天，还差点被他的手下发现……”\n      对方将报告推了过来，平静地回答：“我雇佣了黑帮。”"] = "      Tracking a target without being discovered is a required skill for Nighthawks. The assessment for this lesson was set by Old Neil: monitor an outside fugitive and master their behavioral patterns.\n      Leonard, the dashing Sleeper, was charging toward the path of the Midnight Poet; Frye, the gloomy Corpse Collector, went further toward the cold and dark after becoming a Beyonder. For such two people, wanting to hide in a crowd was a challenge.\n      Leonard changed into coarse work clothes and haunted the street corner where the target lived. The next day, someone came to ask if he was waiting for someone; the third day, the fugitive changed their residence; the fourth day, he discovered he was being followed. After shaking off the pursuer, the depressed Leonard returned to Blackthorn, and Frye was already sitting at the table waiting for him.\n      \"How did you do it, Frye? I monitored him for several days and almost got discovered by his subordinates...\"\n      The other party pushed the report over and replied calmly: \"I hired a gang.\"",
    ["      守夜人：赛勒斯·莫宁\n安魂诗社"] = "      Nighthawk: Cyrus Morning \n Requiem Poetry Society.",
    ["      感谢你对托马斯一事的调查，我们也查明了他的来历。\n      他曾是鲁恩皇家军团成员，在南大陆作战时获得非凡特性，成为非凡者。回到鲁恩后，成为了黑夜教会的牧师，凭借教会的资源，一步步晋升为序列6“死灵导师”。\n      我们从他旧日同僚处得知，他在战场上负责伤亡登记，经手过大量死亡通知。退役后，长期被噩梦困扰。灵教团正是抓住了这一点，以“永暗蜡烛”为饵，许诺他从恐惧中解脱，最终将他变成了棋子。\n\n      此事背后，灵教团的影子已清晰可见。如果今后遇到与此相关的线索，请务必告知我。"] = "      Thank you for your investigation into the Thomas matter; we have also ascertained his origins. \n      He was once a member of the Loen Royal Army and obtained a Beyonder characteristic while fighting in the Southern Continent, becoming a Beyonder. After returning to Loen, he became a priest of the Church of the Night. Relying on the Church's resources, he advanced step by step to Sequence 6 \"Necromancer.\" \n      We learned from his former colleagues that he was responsible for casualty registration on the battlefield and handled a large number of death notifications. After retiring, he was long plagued by nightmares. The Rose School of Thought seized upon this, using the \"Candle of Eternal Darkness\" as bait, promising him relief from his horror, and ultimately turned him into a pawn. \n\n      Behind this matter, the shadow of the Rose School of Thought is already clearly visible. If you encounter any clues related to this in the future, please be sure to inform me.",
    ["      戴莉笑了，旋即在朦胧的视线里看见了那个身穿黑色风衣，发际线较高，有幽邃灰眸的男人，看见他以手按胸，弯腰伸掌，邀请自己跳舞。\n      她探出了自己的手，她的思绪随之变得滞涩。\n      穿黑风衣的灰眸男人拉起了异变逐渐退去的戴莉，在伦纳德的目光中，在喷泉乱流的破败广场里，跳起了轻快的舞蹈。"] = "      Daly smiled, and in her hazy vision, she saw the man in the black trench coat with the high hairline and deep gray eyes. She saw him press a hand to his chest, bow, and extend his palm, inviting her to dance.\n      She reached out her hand, and her thoughts became filled with Stagnation.\n      The gray-eyed man in the black trench coat pulled up Daly, whose mutations were gradually receding. Under Leonard's gaze, in the dilapidated square amidst the turbulent fountain, they began to Dance a lighthearted dance.",
    ["      接引人：莉丝·埃文斯\n春夜舞会"] = "      Guide: Lis Evans \n Spring Night Ball.",
    ["      金毛大狗吓得跳了起来，转身面对了主人。\n      它慌乱而快速地摇起尾巴，嘴部张合几次后才震荡了周围的空气道：\n      “我……”\n      “我不知道该怎么解释，毕竟我只是一条狗。”\n      听到这句话，奥黛丽一时竟无言以对。"] = "      The golden retriever was so startled it jumped up and turned to face its master.\n      It wagged its tail in a flustered and rapid manner, and only after its mouth opened and closed several times did it vibrate the surrounding air to say:\n      \"I...\"\n      \"I don't know how to explain it, after all, I am just a dog.\"\n      Hearing this, Audrey was momentarily speechless.",
    ["      阳光斜照进客厅，佛尔思瘫在沙发里，发出意义不明的哀叹，手边的笔记本上只胡乱画了只卷毛狒狒。\n\n      “我本以为《大冒险家》第二卷的进度很理想。”奥黛丽端着茶杯，眼眸含笑，“看来还是遇到了一些困难，比如……如何处理真实与虚构的占比？”\n      佛尔思沮丧地合上笔记本：“那位编辑先生一定不知道，他在要求我杜撰谁的虚假罗曼史。”\n      奥黛丽露出了更加愉快的笑容：“而他更不知道，沃尔女士为之痛苦的，并非不想写，而是——她也很想写。”\n\n      甜香交织的会客室中，女孩们的笑声像饼干上的砂糖一般突然滚落。桌边安静趴着的金毛大狗扫了扫尾巴，眼睛微微睁开，很快又舒服地眯了起来。\n      ——这片刻闲暇，便是她们赖以穿梭于末日阴影之下，最温柔也最坚实的“锚点”。 "] = "      Sunlight slanted into the living room. Fors lay sprawled on the sofa, letting out an inexplicable sigh, with only a crudely drawn curly-haired baboon on the notebook beside her hand.\n\n      \"I thought the progress of the second volume of 'The Great Adventurer' was quite ideal.\" Audrey held her teacup, her eyes smiling, \"It seems you've encountered some difficulties, such as... how to handle the ratio of reality to fiction?\"\n      Fors closed her notebook in frustration: \"That editor gentleman must not know whose fake romance he is asking me to fabricate.\"\n      Audrey revealed an even more pleasant smile: \"And he knows even less that what Ms. Wall is agonizing over is not that she doesn't want to write, but—she also very much wants to write.\"\n\n      In the parlor intertwined with sweet fragrance, the girls' laughter rolled out suddenly like the sugar on a biscuit. The golden retriever lying quietly by the table flicked its tail, its eyes opening slightly, before quickly squinting comfortably again.\n      —This brief leisure was the gentlest and most solid \"anchor\" they relied on to traverse beneath the shadows of the apocalypse.",
    ["      驱散"] = "      Dispel",
    ["     8月11日晚上8点,<Tips id=\"#160\">铁十字街下街</>以糊制火柴盒为生的劳维斯太太突发疾病死亡。突发疾病死亡.\n     由于近期<Mark id=\"#159\">异常死亡案件</>数量超过正常值,已移交给鲁恩王。"] = "     August 11th, 8 PM, Mrs. Lawis, who made a living making matchboxes on <Tips id=\"#160\">Iron Cross Street Lower Street</>, died of a sudden illness. Died of a sudden illness. \n     Due to the recent number of <Mark id=\"#159\">abnormal death cases</> exceeding the normal value, it has been handed over to the Loen Kingdom.",
    ["    叹息之种·狩怪"] = "    Seed of Sighs · Monster Hunt",
    ["    愚蠢，竟敢污蔑我的收藏！"] = "    Stupid, how dare you slander my collection!",
    ["    感觉有什么不对……"] = "    Something feels wrong...",
    ["    顺序\r\n必将失控"] = "    Sequence\r\nWill inevitably lead to loss of control",
    ["   <Hide stylename=\"Transparent\" id=\"#161_R\">……</>我有一种预感，今晚会有大事发生。不过多亏了我买的那些宝贝，还有我可爱的灵蛇灵鼠们，现在我与其说是害怕，不如说特别兴奋，就好像，有人会帮我解决这些事一样……命运不都是这样的吗？越过一个生死难关，然后晋升到下一个序列……\n\n  而且，门窗、香料，仪式用品，我都已经做好了准备，还有“那个东西”也放在了床边。写完这篇后，我将去等待那个时刻。等“它”真的来了的时候，我也不会害怕……嗯，我不应该害怕，我的封印物，我的宠物，我自己……可以做到的！"] = " <Hide stylename=\"Transparent\" id=\"#161_R\">...</>I have a premonition that something big will happen tonight. However, thanks to the treasures I bought, and my lovely spirit snakes and spirit rats, now, rather than being afraid, I am particularly excited, as if someone will help me solve these things... Isn't fate always like this? Overcoming a life-and-death crisis, and then advancing to the next Sequence... \n\n And, the doors and windows, incense, and ritual supplies, I have already prepared everything, and \"that thing\" is also placed by the bed. After finishing this entry, I will go and wait for that moment. When \"it\" really comes, I won't be afraid... Hmm, I shouldn't be afraid, my Sealed Artifact, my pets, myself... I can do it!",
    ["   古典舞"] = "   Classical Dance",
    ["   民族舞"] = "   Folk Dance",
    ["   鼓掌舞"] = "   Clapping Dance",
    ["  %s太美了！好看！"] = "  %s is so beautiful! Amazing!",
    ["  %s次内必出<Quality_6>危险等级1</>封印物"] = "Guaranteed <Quality_6> Danger Level 1 </> Sealed Artifact within %s pulls",
    ["  一只松鼠，一个可爱的、特别的孩子，它的身体有点特殊。刚刚好，我现在也“有点特殊”。我该为它取个什么名字好呢？"] = "  A squirrel, a cute, special child, its body is a bit special. Just right, I am also \"a bit special\" now. What name should I give it?",
    ["  吉米尼很聪明，而且，这么说或许有点早，我想它很忠诚。今天的饲料增加了香草，看着它进食的快乐模样，我敢说，吉米尼简直要爱惨我了。哈哈，或许我们能在历史上共同留下姓名……"] = " Gemini is very smart, and, perhaps it's a bit early to say this, I think it is very loyal. Today's feed was supplemented with vanilla, and looking at its happy appearance while eating, I dare say, Gemini is about to love me to death. Haha, perhaps we can leave our names in history together...",
    ["  很久很久以前，丰饶之树还只是一粒种子，由大地母神教会的圣者悉心保管。直到那场背弃誓言的战争将大地化为焦土，圣者落下了泪。为了让焦土重生，她将种子埋入泥土，又以己身吸纳荒芜。丰饶之树破土而出，化为稚嫩的人形灵体，裹着金色披风。她的名字叫西尔维娅。\n\n  “大地，在呼唤我。”"] = "A long, long time ago, the Tree of Abundance was just a seed, carefully kept by the Saints of the Church of the Earth Mother. Until that war of broken oaths turned the earth into scorched soil, the Saint shed tears. In order to let the scorched soil be reborn, she buried the seed into the soil and absorbed the desolation with her own body. The Tree of Abundance broke through the soil, turning into a delicate humanoid spirit wrapped in a golden cloak. Her name is Sylvia. \n \n \"The earth is calling me.\"",
    ["  我给它制作了一些饲料，混合了莓果、柑橘。它很满意，看来我的方向是正确的。吃完这些之后，我宣布了它的名字，吉米尼没有表示反对。这是我们羁绊加深的开始。"] = "  I made some feed for it, mixed with berries and citrus. It is very satisfied; it seems my direction is correct. After it finished eating, I announced its name, and Gemini did not object. This is the beginning of our deepening bond.",
    ["  控制/伤害"] = "  Control/Damage",
    ["  猎犬安德鲁，管家驯养的忠实伙伴，生性机警，身形威猛，独爱苹果。曾随管家前往廷根招工，后来五月庄园发生异变，污染侵蚀了它的生命与意志，外表也变得扭曲可怖。在某种存在的驱使下，它依旧遵从管家的指令，徘徊在庄园各处，驱逐着不速之客。\n  “嗷呜——嗷呜——”\n  ——人，你看起来好小。不要害怕，安德鲁还和之前一样。呜……是苹果，喜欢……"] = "Hound Andrew, the loyal companion raised by the butler, is alert by nature, powerful in build, and has a unique love for apples. He once accompanied the butler to Tingen to recruit workers. Later, when the May Manor suffered a catastrophe, corruption eroded his life and will, and his appearance became twisted and terrifying. Driven by some existence, he still follows the butler's orders, wandering throughout the manor and driving away uninvited guests. \n \"Awoo—awoo—\" \n ——Human, you look so small. Do not be afraid, Andrew is still the same as before. Woo... it's an apple, I like it...",
    ["  舞王狒哥原本只是湖边的普通狒狒。它唯一关心的，是今天能不能捡到面包。直到丰饶之树的力量浸染了它的血肉，它忽然开窍了——那些人类对着大树晃胳膊踢腿的奇怪动作，原来叫跳舞！它足尖打着拍子，很快沉迷其中，吃饭哪有跳舞重要，面包屑哪有节奏重要。它成了金秋湖的舞王，带着群狒从早跳到晚，试图邀请每个路过的旅人加入。\n  ——不如跳舞。"] = "Dancing King Baboon Brother was originally just an ordinary baboon by the lake. The only thing it cared about was whether it could find bread today. Until the power of the Tree of Abundance permeated its flesh and blood, it suddenly had an epiphany—those strange movements humans made, shaking their arms and kicking their legs at the big tree, were actually called dancing! It tapped its toes to the beat and soon became addicted to it; what was eating compared to dancing, what were breadcrumbs compared to rhythm? It became the dancing king of Golden Autumn Lake, leading the troop of baboons to dance from morning till night, trying to invite every passing traveler to join in. \n ——Might as well dance.",
    ["  该角色等级超过15级，删除后将有7天的追回期。"] = "  This character is above level 15; there will be a 7-day recovery period after deletion.",
    [" %s记忆碎片：%s"] = " %s Memory Fragment: %s",
    [" <DPS>来输出</>"] = " <DPS> for DPS </>",
    [" <DecH>工艺：</>刺绣锦缎・花簇繁饰\n没人能断言绽放需要多长的等待，但绽放至半的美好已足以让人珍惜。"] = " <DecH>Craftsmanship: </>Embroidered Brocade · Flower Cluster Embellishments\nNo one can assert how long the wait for blooming takes, but the beauty of half-blooming is enough to be cherished.",
    [" <DecH>工艺：</>古旧织锦・密约纹路\n历经岁月洗礼的披风，似乎记录着一段被遗忘的盟约。"] = " <DecH>Craft: </>Antique Brocade & Secret Covenant Patterns\nA cloak weathered by the passage of time, seemingly recording a forgotten covenant.",
    [" <DecH>工艺：</>流光真丝・鳞粉点染\n蝴蝶虽已在黄昏离去，蝶翼的幻影却仍停驻于披风之上。"] = " <DecH>Craftsmanship: </>Flowing Light Silk · Scale Powder Staining\nAlthough the butterfly has left at dusk, the phantom of the butterfly wings still lingers on the cape.",
    [" <Default>已签到</> <Red>%s</><Default> 天（</><Red>%s</><Default> 后重置）</>"] = " <Default> has checked in for </> <Red>%s</><Default> days (resets in </><Red>%s</><Default>)</>",
    [" <Healer>来治疗</>"] = " <Healer> to heal </>",
    [" <Highlight>工艺：</>刺绣锦缎・花簇繁饰\n没人能断言绽放需要多长的等待，但绽放至半的美好已足以让人珍惜。"] = " <Highlight>Craft: </>Embroidered Brocade/Flower Cluster Ornament\nNo one can assert how long the wait for blooming will take, but the beauty of a half-bloom is enough to be cherished.",
    [" <Highlight>工艺：</>古旧织锦・密约纹路\n历经岁月洗礼的披风，似乎记录着一段被遗忘的盟约。"] = "<Highlight>Craft: </>Antique Brocade · Secret Covenant Pattern\nA cape weathered by time, seemingly recording a forgotten covenant.",
    [" <Highlight>工艺：</>流光真丝・鳞粉点染\n蝴蝶虽已在黄昏离去，蝶翼的幻影却仍停驻于披风之上。"] = " <Highlight>Craft: </>Flowing Light Silk/Scale Powder Pointing\nAlthough the butterfly has already left at dusk, the phantom of its wings still lingers on the cloak.",
    [" <MT>来防御</>"] = " <MT> to defend </>",
    [" Chapter名: "] = " Chapter Name: ",
