    ["5排队trigger"] = "5 Queuing Trigger",
    ["5月23日\n　　尼尔说这条路他走过七次。\n　　一路上他说了三遍，我不信——如果他真的走过七次，为什么连帐篷都不会搭？我蹲在他身后，看他第三次把帐篷布穿反，雪水渗进手套，冷得像在舔我的骨头。\n　　万幸，我们在天黑前支起了帐篷。\n\n剩余物资：\n面包6份    佩姬为我们准备了18磅分成了8份\n肉干和肉肠5份\n糖1罐\n黄油4块\n酒3瓶      酒3瓶 → 2瓶（晚上庆祝消耗1瓶）\n水5瓶      暂时充足，路上可以留意水源"] = "May 23rd\n　　Neil said he has walked this path seven times.\n　　He said it three times along the way, but I don't believe it—if he really had walked it seven times, why wouldn't he even know how to set up a tent? I crouched behind him, watching him put the tent fabric on backward for the third time. Snow water seeped into my gloves, cold as if it were licking my bones.\n　　Fortunately, we set up the tent before dark.\n\nRemaining supplies:\nBread: 6 portions (Peggy prepared 18 lbs for us, divided into 8 portions)\nDried meat and sausages: 5 portions\nSugar: 1 jar\nButter: 4 blocks\nWine: 3 bottles (Wine: 3 bottles → 2 bottles (1 consumed for the evening celebration))\nWater: 5 bottles (Temporarily sufficient; can keep an eye out for water sources on the way)",
    ["5月24日\n晴天。\n　　雪面反射的阳光非常刺眼，为了避免眼睛遭罪，我建议尼尔太阳落山后再出发。他没把我的话放在心上，自顾自地收拾东西，然后先走了——他总是这样。\n　　我把东西收拾好追上他，远远望去，他在雪地里的影子竟有五个，朝五个方向散开。\n　　可能是我看错了，再望过去，只剩一个。我们在山腰的位置扎营，距离登顶应该不远了。"] = "May 24th \n Sunny. \n　　The sunlight reflected off the snow is very blinding. To avoid hurting our eyes, I suggested to Neil that we set off after sunset. He didn't take my words to heart, packed his things on his own, and left first—he is always like this. \n　　I packed my things and caught up with him. Looking from afar, he actually had five shadows in the snow, spreading out in five directions. \n　　Maybe I saw wrong. Looking again, there was only one. We camped at the mountainside; we shouldn't be far from the summit.",
    ["5月24日\n晴天。漫山的雪反射的阳光非常刺眼，为了避免眼睛遭罪，我建议尼尔等太阳落山后再外出。他没把我的话放在心上，自顾自地收拾我们的东西，然后就先走了，他总是这样。\n我把东西收拾好追上他，远远望去，他在雪地里的影子有五个，朝着五个方向走。\n可能是我看错了，再望过去，只剩一个了。\n我们在山腰的位置扎营，距离登顶应该不远了。\n\n剩余物资：\n面包4份半\n肉干和肉肠3份\n糖1罐\n黄油3块\n酒2瓶\n水5瓶 路上找到水源，进行了补充"] = "May 24th \n Sunny. The sunlight reflected by the snow-covered mountains is very dazzling. To avoid eye strain, I suggested Neil go out after sunset. He didn't take my words to heart, packed our things on his own, and left first. He's always like this. \n I packed up and caught up with him. Looking from afar, he had five shadows in the snow, walking in five directions. \n Maybe I saw wrong, looking again, there was only one left. \n We camped halfway up the mountain, it shouldn't be far from the summit. \n \n Remaining supplies: \n 4.5 loaves of bread \n 3 portions of jerky and sausage \n 1 jar of sugar \n 3 blocks of butter \n 2 bottles of liquor \n 5 bottles of water. Found a water source on the way and replenished.",
    ["5月25日\n　　雪下了一整晚。早上起来帐篷都被埋了半截，尼尔提议我们提早启程加快行程，考虑到意外情况，补给可能不太够。\n我们把东西都收拾好，准备启程。\n\n剩余物资：\n面包3份\n肉干和肉肠2份\n糖1罐 尼尔昨晚外出了一趟，回来的时候吃了几颗\n黄油2块 山上太冷，我们昨晚把黄油涂抹在面包上，并且放在火上烤着吃\n酒1瓶 水太重了，只留一瓶等登顶后庆祝\n水3瓶"] = "May 25th\n　　It snowed all night. When we woke up in the morning, the tent was half-buried. Neil suggested we set off early to speed up the journey; considering unexpected situations, the supplies might not be enough.\nWe packed everything up and prepared to set off.\n\nRemaining supplies:\nBread: 3 portions\nDried meat and sausages: 2 portions\nSugar: 1 jar (Neil went out last night and ate a few pieces when he returned)\nButter: 2 blocks (It was too cold on the mountain, so we spread the butter on the bread last night and roasted it over the fire to eat)\nWine: 1 bottle (Water is too heavy, so we only kept one bottle to celebrate after reaching the summit)\nWater: 3 bottles",
    ["5月26日\n　　激动？幸福？紧张？我无法用任何语言和文字描述现在的心情。\n我和尼尔登顶了！\n　　尼尔很幸运，找到一颗琥珀，这将作为他的登顶纪念。我也学着他在山上找，不过没什么特别的。最后我将山顶的雪混了些土，装到瓶子里。\n\n下山物资：\n面包2份\n肉干和肉肠1份\n糖1罐\n黄油1块\n水2瓶"] = "May 26th\n　　Excited? Happy? Nervous? I cannot describe my current mood with any language or words.\nNeil and I reached the summit!\n　　Neil was lucky and found an amber, which will serve as his summit souvenir. I also tried to look for one on the mountain like him, but there was nothing special. In the end, I mixed some soil with the snow from the summit and put it in a bottle.\n\nSupplies for the descent:\nBread: 2 portions\nDried meat and sausages: 1 portion\nSugar: 1 jar\nButter: 1 block\nWater: 2 bottles",
