    ["<Assistant_Title1>【Broadcast】</>\n<Assistant_Title2>Required Level: </>Cognition Level <Assistant_Red>Level 2</>\n<Assistant_Title2>System Access: </><Assistant_System>Chat - Broadcast (Bottom Right)</>{JumpToUI:[【前往查看】]|1250041}\n<Assistant_Title2>How to Purchase: </>You can purchase quickly via the broadcast panel, or in the <Assistant_System>Mall - Secret Collection</>.\n<Assistant_Title2>Item Introduction - Global Broadcast: </>After using this item, you can send a marquee broadcast to the entire server.\n<Assistant_Title2>Item Introduction - Heart Feather · Oracle Broadcast: </>After using this item, you can send a marquee broadcast to the entire server, and receive a gift of bound Pounds for the World Channel worth half the item's value.\n<Assistant_Title2>Item Introduction - Swift Lightning · Oracle Broadcast: </>After using this item, you can send a marquee broadcast to the entire server, and receive a gift of bound Pounds for the World Channel worth half the item's value."] = "<Assistant_Title1>【Broadcast】</>\n<Assistant_Title2>Required Level: </>Cognition Level <Assistant_Red>Level 2</>\n<Assistant_Title2>System Access: </><Assistant_System>Chat - Broadcast (Bottom Right)</>{JumpToUI:[【View】]|1250041}\n<Assistant_Title2>How to Purchase: </>You can purchase quickly via the broadcast panel, or in the <Assistant_System>Mall - Secret Collection</>.\n<Assistant_Title2>Item Introduction - Global Broadcast: </>After using this item, you can send a marquee broadcast to the entire server.\n<Assistant_Title2>Item Introduction - Heart Feather · Oracle Broadcast: </>After using this item, you can send a marquee broadcast to the entire server, and receive a gift of bound Pounds for the World Channel worth half the item's value.\n<Assistant_Title2>Item Introduction - Swift Lightning · Oracle Broadcast: </>After using this item, you can send a marquee broadcast to the entire server, and receive a gift of bound Pounds for the World Channel worth half the item's value.",
    ["<Assistant_Title1>【Call of the Snowfield】</>\n<Assistant_Title2>Quest Type: </><Assistant_Property2>Life in the Era</>\n<Assistant_Title2>Quest Description: </>Under the snow that never melts, there are unknown stories hidden.\n<Assistant_Title2>How to Accept: </>After your Acting level reaches <Assistant_Red>Level 63</>, head to {Location:[霍纳奇斯山脉(406,364)]|30610;26480;-920;2;5200086;0} to trigger the quest.\n<Assistant_Title2>Quest Rewards</>: Cognitive Experience, Bound Sol, invoices, Adventure Medals, World Adventure Treasure progress"] = "<Assistant_Title1>【Call of the Snowfield】</>\n<Assistant_Title2>Quest Type: </><Assistant_Property2>Life in the Era</>\n<Assistant_Title2>Quest Description: </>Under the snow that never melts, there are unknown stories hidden.\n<Assistant_Title2>How to Accept: </>After your Acting level reaches <Assistant_Red>Level 63</>, head to {Location:[Hornacis Mountains(406,364)]|30610;26480;-920;2;5200086;0} to trigger the quest.\n<Assistant_Title2>Quest Rewards</>: Cognitive Experience, Bound Sol, invoices, Adventure Medals, World Adventure Treasure progress",
    ["<Assistant_Title1>【Castle Template】</>\n<Assistant_Title2>Usage Instructions: </>\nOpen <Assistant_System>Menu - Castle - Template - Recommended</> tab, or {JumpToUI:[点击这里]|1250327}, to browse and download recommended templates.\nOpen <Assistant_System>Menu - Castle - Template - My</> tab, select a saved template, and click <Assistant_System>Apply Template</> to apply it to your current castle.\nIn <Assistant_System>Castle - Decoration Interface - Save/Apply</>, you can also apply saved templates or save your current castle decoration as a template.\n<Assistant_Title2>Tip: </>\nYou can also go to the <Assistant_System>Decoration Plaza</> to view templates uploaded by other players; you can save and use templates you like.\n<Assistant_Title2>Delete Template: </>\nTo delete a saved template, go to <Assistant_System>Menu - Castle - Template - My</>, select the target template, and click the delete button in the <Assistant_System>top right corner</>."] = "<Assistant_Title1>【Castle Template】</>\n<Assistant_Title2>Usage Instructions: </>\nOpen <Assistant_System>Menu - Castle - Template - Recommended</> tab, or {JumpToUI:[Click Here]|1250327}, to browse and download recommended templates.\nOpen <Assistant_System>Menu - Castle - Template - My</> tab, select a saved template, and click <Assistant_System>Apply Template</> to apply it to your current castle.\nIn <Assistant_System>Castle - Decoration Interface - Save/Apply</>, you can also apply saved templates or save your current castle decoration as a template.\n<Assistant_Title2>Tip: </>\nYou can also go to the <Assistant_System>Decoration Plaza</> to view templates uploaded by other players; you can save and use templates you like.\n<Assistant_Title2>Delete Template: </>\nTo delete a saved template, go to <Assistant_System>Menu - Castle - Template - My</>, select the target template, and click the delete button in the <Assistant_System>top right corner</>.",
    ["<Assistant_Title1>【Chat - Emoticons】</>\n<Assistant_Title2>System Access: </><Assistant_System>Chat - Emoticon button next to input box</>\n<Assistant_Title2>Emoticons: </>Includes emojis, system emoticons, and custom emoticons. \n<Assistant_Title2>Upload Custom Emoticons: </>In the Custom Emoticons tab, click the + button to upload your own; they can be used after approval. \n<Assistant_Title2>Custom Emoticon Limit: </>Limit is 50 custom emoticons. \n<Assistant_Title2>Emoticon Sync: </>All characters under the same account sync all emoticons by default. \n<Assistant_Title3>Recommended Searches: </>{SendAnswer:[聊天]|1413}"] = "<Assistant_Title1>【Chat - Emoticons】</>\n<Assistant_Title2>System Access: </><Assistant_System>Chat - Emoticon button next to input box</>\n<Assistant_Title2>Emoticons: </>Includes emojis, system emoticons, and custom emoticons. \n<Assistant_Title2>Upload Custom Emoticons: </>In the Custom Emoticons tab, click the + button to upload your own; they can be used after approval. \n<Assistant_Title2>Custom Emoticon Limit: </>Limit is 50 custom emoticons. \n<Assistant_Title2>Emoticon Sync: </>All characters under the same account sync all emoticons by default. \n<Assistant_Title3>Recommended Searches: </>{SendAnswer:[Chat]|1413}",
    ["<Assistant_Title1>【Child in the Chimney】</>\n<Assistant_Title2>Quest Type: </><Assistant_Property2>Life in the Era</>\n<Assistant_Title2>Quest Description: </>Near the factory, there are scolding sounds from a drunkard and a child's crying. What happened?\n<Assistant_Title2>How to Accept: </>After your Acting level reaches <Assistant_Red>Level 64</>, head to {Location:[廷根(974,1173)]|-2552;17366;-1828;2;5200002;0} to trigger the quest.\n<Assistant_Title2>Quest Rewards</>: Cognitive Experience, Bound Sol, invoices, Adventure Medals, World Adventure Treasure progress"] = "<Assistant_Title1>【Child in the Chimney】</>\n<Assistant_Title2>Quest Type: </><Assistant_Property2>Life in the Era</>\n<Assistant_Title2>Quest Description: </>Near the factory, there are scolding sounds from a drunkard and a child's crying. What happened?\n<Assistant_Title2>How to Accept: </>After your Acting level reaches <Assistant_Red>Level 64</>, head to {Location:[Tingen(974,1173)]|-2552;17366;-1828;2;5200002;0} to trigger the quest.\n<Assistant_Title2>Quest Rewards</>: Cognitive Experience, Bound Sol, invoices, Adventure Medals, World Adventure Treasure progress",
    ["<Assistant_Title1>【City of Shadows】</>\n<Assistant_Title2>Introduction: </>Under the guidance of Miss Justice, you enter a world formed by the collective subconscious of Tingen. Everything that happens here will not have a direct impact on reality. However, clearing the malice in the subconscious will disturb the source of reality. Delve into the event scenes, complete plot, challenge, and competition events to save this city.\n<Assistant_Title2>Gameplay Guide: </>\n1. Complete the <Assistant_System>\"Sinful Tingen\"</> plot to unlock the system; open the map, switch to the Exploration tab, switch to the \"City of Shadows\" tab, select an unlocked event icon on the map, and click to automatically navigate to the target.\n2. Arrive at the designated area and use methods such as talking to relevant NPCs to start the event.\n3. Complete to {SendAnswer:事件|877}obtain relevant rewards.\n<Assistant_Title2>Scene Features: </>\nEntering Sinful Tingen, vehicle control is in realistic driving mode.\n<Assistant_Title2>Beginner Tips: </>\n1. It is recommended to prioritize completing the main plot events in Sinful Tingen upon first entry to unlock more gameplay.\n2. The <Assistant_Red>Fierce Battle · Bonnie</> event requires reaching the recommended Beyonder rating and level.\n3. Limited-time multiplayer competition events are open daily; compete with other players to win ranking rewards."] = "<Assistant_Title1>【City of Shadows】</>\n<Assistant_Title2>Introduction: </>Under the guidance of Miss Justice, you enter a world formed by the collective subconscious of Tingen. Everything that happens here will not have a direct impact on reality. However, clearing the malice in the subconscious will disturb the source of reality. Delve into the event scenes, complete plot, challenge, and competition events to save this city.\n<Assistant_Title2>Gameplay Guide: </>\n1. Complete the <Assistant_System>\"Sinful Tingen\"</> plot to unlock the system; open the map, switch to the Exploration tab, switch to the \"City of Shadows\" tab, select an unlocked event icon on the map, and click to automatically navigate to the target.\n2. Arrive at the designated area and use methods such as talking to relevant NPCs to start the event.\n3. Complete to {SendAnswer:Event|877}obtain relevant rewards.\n<Assistant_Title2>Scene Features: </>\nEntering Sinful Tingen, vehicle control is in realistic driving mode.\n<Assistant_Title2>Beginner Tips: </>\n1. It is recommended to prioritize completing the main plot events in Sinful Tingen upon first entry to unlock more gameplay.\n2. The <Assistant_Red>Fierce Battle · Bonnie</> event requires reaching the recommended Beyonder rating and level.\n3. Limited-time multiplayer competition events are open daily; compete with other players to win ranking rewards.",
    ["<Assistant_Title1>【Club - Buildings and Funds】</>\n<Assistant_Title2>System Access: </><Assistant_System>Menu - Club - Building Upgrade</>{JumpToUI:[【前往查看】]|1250318}\n<Assistant_Title2>Source of Funds: </>Club Activity Allowance and Club activities.\n<Assistant_Title2>Fund Description: </>Can be used for Club building upgrades to improve Club strength, benefits, and scale.\n<Assistant_Title2>Club Fund Consumption: </>Building upgrades consume Club funds and require a certain amount of time. Each building has corresponding level-up effects, and other buildings cannot exceed the level of the Council Hall.\n<Assistant_Title2>Building upgrade caps are gradually opened based on server time:</>Level 3: After 8:00 AM on the 7th day of server launch\nLevel 4: After 8:00 AM on the 14th day of server launch\nLevel 5: After 8:00 AM on the 21st day of server launch\nLevel 6: After 8:00 AM on the 30th day of server launch\nLevel 7: After 8:00 AM on the 45th day of server launch\nLevel 8: After 8:00 AM on the 60th day of server launch \n<Assistant_Title3>Recommended Searches: </>{SendAnswer:[俱乐部]|1400}, {SendAnswer:[俱乐部-俱乐部职位]|1402}, {SendAnswer:[俱乐部-俱乐部活跃]|1403}, {SendAnswer:[俱乐部-俱乐部活跃津贴]|1404}"] = "<Assistant_Title1>【Club - Buildings and Funds】</>\n<Assistant_Title2>System Access: </><Assistant_System>Menu - Club - Building Upgrade</>{JumpToUI:[【View】]|1250318}\n<Assistant_Title2>Source of Funds: </>Club Activity Allowance and Club activities.\n<Assistant_Title2>Fund Description: </>Can be used for Club building upgrades to improve Club strength, benefits, and scale.\n<Assistant_Title2>Club Fund Consumption: </>Building upgrades consume Club funds and require a certain amount of time. Each building has corresponding level-up effects, and other buildings cannot exceed the level of the Council Hall.\n<Assistant_Title2>Building upgrade caps are gradually opened based on server time:</>Level 3: After 8:00 AM on the 7th day of server launch\nLevel 4: After 8:00 AM on the 14th day of server launch\nLevel 5: After 8:00 AM on the 21st day of server launch\nLevel 6: After 8:00 AM on the 30th day of server launch\nLevel 7: After 8:00 AM on the 45th day of server launch\nLevel 8: After 8:00 AM on the 60th day of server launch \n<Assistant_Title3>Recommended Searches: </>{SendAnswer:[Club]|1400}, {SendAnswer:[Club-Club Position]|1402}, {SendAnswer:[Club-Club Activity]|1403}, {SendAnswer:[Club-Club Activity Allowance]|1404}",
    ["<Assistant_Title1>【Club - Club Activity Allowance】</>\n<Assistant_Title2>System Access: </><Assistant_System>Menu - Club - Benefits - Activity Allowance</>{JumpToUI:[【前往查看】]|1250320}\n<Assistant_Title2>Gameplay Description: </>Complete activity allowance quests to earn Peer Emblems, Club activity, and Club fund rewards.\nClub activity is the sum of individual activity values of current Club members; reaching corresponding values allows you to claim extra rewards.\nActivity allowance rewards will refresh every Monday at 8:00; please claim your rewards in time.\n<Assistant_Title3>Recommended Searches: </>{SendAnswer:[俱乐部]|1400}, {SendAnswer:[俱乐部-俱乐部分红]|1405}, {SendAnswer:[俱乐部-俱乐部活跃]|1403}"] = "<Assistant_Title1>【Club - Club Activity Allowance】</>\n<Assistant_Title2>System Access: </><Assistant_System>Menu - Club - Benefits - Activity Allowance</>{JumpToUI:[【View】]|1250320}\n<Assistant_Title2>Gameplay Description: </>Complete activity allowance quests to earn Peer Emblems, Club activity, and Club fund rewards.\nClub activity is the sum of individual activity values of current Club members; reaching corresponding values allows you to claim extra rewards.\nActivity allowance rewards will refresh every Monday at 8:00; please claim your rewards in time.\n<Assistant_Title3>Recommended Searches: </>{SendAnswer:[Club]|1400}, {SendAnswer:[Club-Club Dividends]|1405}, {SendAnswer:[Club-Club Activity]|1403}",
    ["<Assistant_Title1>【Club - Club Activity】</>\n<Assistant_Title2>Activity Level: </>Club activity levels are divided from high to low into \nQuiet Affairs (<720)\nRoutine Operations (720~2400)\nProsperous Affairs (>2400)\n<Assistant_Title2>Source of Activity: </>Activity Allowance\n<Assistant_Title2>Activity Description: </>The higher the Club activity, the higher the weekly Club dividend reward.\n<Assistant_Title2>Activity Consumption: </>Daily Club maintenance will deduct 5% of the current activity. If the activity remains at 'Quiet Affairs' for 7 consecutive days, the Council Hall level will be reduced by 1.<Assistant_Red>If the Council Hall level is lower than level 1, the Club will be automatically disbanded.</>\n<Assistant_Title3>Recommended Searches: </>{SendAnswer:[俱乐部]|1400}, {SendAnswer:[俱乐部-俱乐部活跃津贴]|1404}, {SendAnswer:[俱乐部-俱乐部分红]|1405}"] = "<Assistant_Title1>【Club - Club Activity】</>\n<Assistant_Title2>Activity Level: </>Club activity levels are divided from high to low into \nQuiet Affairs (<720)\nRoutine Operations (720~2400)\nProsperous Affairs (>2400)\n<Assistant_Title2>Source of Activity: </>Activity Allowance\n<Assistant_Title2>Activity Description: </>The higher the Club activity, the higher the weekly Club dividend reward.\n<Assistant_Title2>Activity Consumption: </>Daily Club maintenance will deduct 5% of the current activity. If the activity remains at 'Quiet Affairs' for 7 consecutive days, the Council Hall level will be reduced by 1.<Assistant_Red>If the Council Hall level is lower than level 1, the Club will be automatically disbanded.</>\n<Assistant_Title3>Recommended Searches: </>{SendAnswer:[Club]|1400}, {SendAnswer:[Club-Club Activity Allowance]|1404}, {SendAnswer:[Club-Club Dividends]|1405}",
    ["<Assistant_Title1>【Club - Club Dividends】</>\n<Assistant_Title2>System Access: </><Assistant_System>Menu - Club - Benefits - Dividends</>{JumpToUI:[【前往查看】]|1250319}\n<Assistant_Title2>Gameplay Description: </>You can claim Club dividend rewards once a week.\nClub dividend rewards are affected by the Club's activity level and your personal activity in the current Club last week.\nClub dividend rewards will refresh every Monday at 8:00; please claim your rewards in time.\n<Assistant_Title3>Recommended Searches: </>{SendAnswer:[俱乐部]|1400}, {SendAnswer:[俱乐部-俱乐部活跃津贴]|1404}, {SendAnswer:[俱乐部-俱乐部活跃]|1403}"] = "<Assistant_Title1>【Club - Club Dividends】</>\n<Assistant_Title2>System Access: </><Assistant_System>Menu - Club - Benefits - Dividends</>{JumpToUI:[【View】]|1250319}\n<Assistant_Title2>Gameplay Description: </>You can claim Club dividend rewards once a week.\nClub dividend rewards are affected by the Club's activity level and your personal activity in the current Club last week.\nClub dividend rewards will refresh every Monday at 8:00; please claim your rewards in time.\n<Assistant_Title3>Recommended Searches: </>{SendAnswer:[Club]|1400}, {SendAnswer:[Club-Club Activity Allowance]|1404}, {SendAnswer:[Club-Club Activity]|1403}",
    ["<Assistant_Title1>【Club - Club Positions】</>\n<Assistant_Title2>President: </>The President is the leader of the Club, holding the highest authority and representing the Club in handling internal management and diplomatic rights.\n<Assistant_Title2>Vice President: </>The Vice President is an important position assisting the President, holding high authority second only to the President, and can exercise some internal management and diplomatic rights on behalf of the President, appointed by the President.\n<Assistant_Title2>Director: </>Directors are management positions in the Club with a certain degree of management authority, appointed by the President, up to 3 people.\n<Assistant_Title2>Group Leader: </>Group Leaders are the core management for Club activities, responsible for the appointment and dismissal of members within the group, and organizing activities like league team formation. Each Club has 4 groups, each with a maximum of 30 people; members within a group automatically gain qualification for league participation.\n<Assistant_Title2>Club Star: </>Club Stars are the face of the Club, responsible for recruiting and entertaining new members, appointed by the President, up to 2 people.\n<Assistant_Title2>Official Member: </>Official Members are the backbone of the Club and can participate in Club activities.<Assistant_Red>Some activities only support Official Members participating</>.\n<Assistant_Title2>Reserve Member: </>Reserve Members are the reserve force of the Club and cannot participate in some Club activities. Keep working hard, stay active, and contact management to join as an Official Member.\n<Assistant_Title2>Position Adjustment: </>Club members can hold management positions, group positions, and Club Star positions simultaneously; management positions include President, Vice President, and Director.\n<Assistant_Title2>Permission Adjustment: </>The Club President can adjust the permission allocation for different positions in the permission adjustment interface.\n<Assistant_Title3>Recommended Searches: </>{SendAnswer:[俱乐部]|1400}, {SendAnswer:[俱乐部-俱乐部建筑和资金]|1401}, {SendAnswer:[俱乐部-俱乐部活跃]|1403}"] = "<Assistant_Title1>【Club - Club Positions】</>\n<Assistant_Title2>President: </>The President is the leader of the Club, holding the highest authority and representing the Club in handling internal management and diplomatic rights.\n<Assistant_Title2>Vice President: </>The Vice President is an important position assisting the President, holding high authority second only to the President, and can exercise some internal management and diplomatic rights on behalf of the President, appointed by the President.\n<Assistant_Title2>Director: </>Directors are management positions in the Club with a certain degree of management authority, appointed by the President, up to 3 people.\n<Assistant_Title2>Group Leader: </>Group Leaders are the core management for Club activities, responsible for the appointment and dismissal of members within the group, and organizing activities like league team formation. Each Club has 4 groups, each with a maximum of 30 people; members within a group automatically gain qualification for league participation.\n<Assistant_Title2>Club Star: </>Club Stars are the face of the Club, responsible for recruiting and entertaining new members, appointed by the President, up to 2 people.\n<Assistant_Title2>Official Member: </>Official Members are the backbone of the Club and can participate in Club activities.<Assistant_Red>Some activities only support Official Members participating</>.\n<Assistant_Title2>Reserve Member: </>Reserve Members are the reserve force of the Club and cannot participate in some Club activities. Keep working hard, stay active, and contact management to join as an Official Member.\n<Assistant_Title2>Position Adjustment: </>Club members can hold management positions, group positions, and Club Star positions simultaneously; management positions include President, Vice President, and Director.\n<Assistant_Title2>Permission Adjustment: </>The Club President can adjust the permission allocation for different positions in the permission adjustment interface.\n<Assistant_Title3>Recommended Searches: </>{SendAnswer:[Club]|1400}, {SendAnswer:[Club - Club Buildings and Funds]|1401}, {SendAnswer:[Club - Club Activity]|1403}",
    ["<Assistant_Title1>【Club Brawl - Gameplay Rules】</>\n When registration opens, the mode will randomly select <Assistant_Red>16</> players from the club members to serve as <Assistant_Property1>Illusion Projections</> for participants to use. All participants use the same types of projections. \n The competition is divided into multiple rounds. Players can choose projections to enter into <Assistant_Property1>any round</> to participate in the competition. Projections that have already been entered cannot be <Assistant_Property1>reused</>. \n When the designated round begins, the projections for that round will be summoned and <Assistant_Property1>fight automatically</>. Participants can go to the club headquarters to <Assistant_Property1>watch the battle</>.\n<Assistant_Title3> Recommended Search: </>{SendAnswer:[俱乐部乱斗]|8}, {SendAnswer:[俱乐部乱斗-得分规则]|10}"] = "<Assistant_Title1>【Club Brawl - Gameplay Rules】</>\n When registration opens, the mode will randomly select <Assistant_Red>16</> players from the club members to serve as <Assistant_Property1>Illusion Projections</> for participants to use. All participants use the same types of projections. \n The competition is divided into multiple rounds. Players can choose projections to enter into <Assistant_Property1>any round</> to participate in the competition. Projections that have already been entered cannot be <Assistant_Property1>reused</>. \n When the designated round begins, the projections for that round will be summoned and <Assistant_Property1>fight automatically</>. Participants can go to the club headquarters to <Assistant_Property1>watch the battle</>.\n<Assistant_Title3> Recommended Search: </>{SendAnswer:[Club Brawl]|8}, {SendAnswer:[Club Brawl - Scoring Rules]|10}",
    ["<Assistant_Title1>【Club Brawl - Scoring Rules】</>\n Players will accumulate scores based on the performance of their projections on the battlefield: \n According to the survival ranking, the top three projections will receive <Assistant_Red>60, 40, 30</> points respectively, \n for every other projection that dies, your own projection gains <Assistant_Red>3</> points, \n and killing other projections grants <Assistant_Red>5</> points. \n Players must enter at least <Assistant_Red>8</> projections to receive rewards. After the competition ends, those with excellent total scores and those with outstanding projection data will receive additional <Assistant_Property1>title</> rewards.\n<Assistant_Title3> Recommended Search: </>{SendAnswer:[俱乐部乱斗]|8}, {SendAnswer:[俱乐部乱斗-玩法规则]|9}"] = "<Assistant_Title1>【Club Brawl - Scoring Rules】</>\n Players will accumulate scores based on the performance of their projections on the battlefield: \n According to the survival ranking, the top three projections will receive <Assistant_Red>60, 40, 30</> points respectively, \n for every other projection that dies, your own projection gains <Assistant_Red>3</> points, \n and killing other projections grants <Assistant_Red>5</> points. \n Players must enter at least <Assistant_Red>8</> projections to receive rewards. After the competition ends, those with excellent total scores and those with outstanding projection data will receive additional <Assistant_Property1>title</> rewards.\n<Assistant_Title3> Recommended Search: </>{SendAnswer:[Club Brawl]|8}, {SendAnswer:[Club Brawl - Gameplay Rules]|9}",
    ["<Assistant_Title1>【Club Brawl】</>\n<Assistant_Title2> Gameplay Background: </><Assistant_System>Club Brawl</> originates from a mirror-disk-style Sealed Artifact that possesses the abilities of an Ancient Scholar. Players can temporarily act as a <Assistant_Property1>Summoner</> using the abilities of an Ancient Scholar to summon <Assistant_Property1>Historical Projections</> from within to duel. The Historical Projections are selected from the player's state at a certain point in the past and take on the corresponding appearance.\n<Assistant_Title2> Opening Rules: </> The mode opens for registration every Tuesday and Thursday at <Assistant_Red>12:00</>, and battles take place in the evening from <Assistant_Red>19:00 to 20:30</> (the server's first competition will open for registration on Saturday at <Assistant_Red>12:00 noon</>). \n The number of rounds opened will be determined by the <Assistant_Property2>number of participants</> in the previous session (the first competition within the club will be determined by the <Assistant_Property2>number of club members</>).\n<Assistant_Title2> Participation Requirements: </> Club members must have at least <Assistant_Red>20</> people and an activity level of <Assistant_Red>100</> or more.\n<Assistant_Title3> Recommended Search: </>{SendAnswer:[俱乐部乱斗-玩法规则]|9}, {SendAnswer:[俱乐部乱斗-得分规则]|10}"] = "<Assistant_Title1>【Club Brawl】</>\n<Assistant_Title2> Gameplay Background: </><Assistant_System>Club Brawl</> originates from a mirror-disk-style Sealed Artifact that possesses the abilities of an Ancient Scholar. Players can temporarily act as a <Assistant_Property1>Summoner</> using the abilities of an Ancient Scholar to summon <Assistant_Property1>Historical Projections</> from within to duel. The Historical Projections are selected from the player's state at a certain point in the past and take on the corresponding appearance.\n<Assistant_Title2> Opening Rules: </> The mode opens for registration every Tuesday and Thursday at <Assistant_Red>12:00</>, and battles take place in the evening from <Assistant_Red>19:00 to 20:30</> (the server's first competition will open for registration on Saturday at <Assistant_Red>12:00 noon</>). \n The number of rounds opened will be determined by the <Assistant_Property2>number of participants</> in the previous session (the first competition within the club will be determined by the <Assistant_Property2>number of club members</>).\n<Assistant_Title2> Participation Requirements: </> Club members must have at least <Assistant_Red>20</> people and an activity level of <Assistant_Red>100</> or more.\n<Assistant_Title3> Recommended Search: </>{SendAnswer:[Club Brawl - Gameplay Rules]|9}, {SendAnswer:[Club Brawl - Scoring Rules]|10}",
    ["<Assistant_Title1>【Club】</>\n<Assistant_Title2>Required Level: </>Cognition Level <Assistant_Red>Level 20</>\n<Assistant_Title2>System Access: </><Assistant_System>Menu - Club</>{JumpToUI:[【前往查看】]|1250052}\n<Assistant_Title2>System Introduction: </>Once your character reaches level 20, you can choose to join a Club or create your own. Participate in various Club activities to earn generous rewards and Peer Emblems, which can be exchanged for reward items in the Club Shop.\n<Assistant_Title2>Creating a Club: </>Creating a Club requires a creation fee. After creation, if the number of responses reaches 4 within 24 hours, the creation is successful; otherwise, it fails.<Assistant_Red>Neither failed creation nor voluntary cancellation will result in a refund of the creation fee.</>\n<Assistant_Title2>Club Types: </>Clubs are divided into Leisure Clubs and Combat Clubs. You can adjust this in the Club Information modification section. Leisure Clubs will not display Extraordinary Ratings in the member list.\n<Assistant_Title2>Rename Item: </>You can purchase a Renaming Notice in the <Assistant_System>Mall - Secret Collection</> to change the Club's name and emblem text.\n<Assistant_Title2>Activity Restrictions: </>1. Club Member Lock Rule: During Club-based activities (such as <Assistant_System>Four-Way League, Phantom of the Opera, Hunting City War, Highland War</>), Clubs <Assistant_Red>do not allow members to join or leave.</>\n2. Club Activity Pathway Limit: Some Club activities have restrictions on the number of <Assistant_Red>Pathways</> participating; see the Club activity instructions for details.\n3. Before participating in activities, please confirm the position allocation. <Assistant_Red>Some activities only support Official Members participating</>. Official Members are the backbone of the Club and can participate in Club activities; Reserve Members are the reserve force of the Club and cannot participate in some activities. You can maintain an active status and contact management to be promoted to an Official Member.\n<Assistant_Title3>Basic Function Details: </>{SendAnswer:[俱乐部-俱乐部建筑和资金]|1401}, {SendAnswer:[俱乐部-俱乐部职位]|1402}, {SendAnswer:[俱乐部-俱乐部活跃]|1403}, {SendAnswer:[场景-俱乐部]|567}"] = "<Assistant_Title1>【Club】</>\n<Assistant_Title2>Required Level: </>Cognition Level <Assistant_Red>Level 20</>\n<Assistant_Title2>System Access: </><Assistant_System>Menu - Club</>{JumpToUI:[【Go to View】]|1250052}\n<Assistant_Title2>System Introduction: </>Once your character reaches level 20, you can choose to join a Club or create your own. Participate in various Club activities to earn generous rewards and Peer Emblems, which can be exchanged for reward items in the Club Shop.\n<Assistant_Title2>Creating a Club: </>Creating a Club requires a creation fee. After creation, if the number of responses reaches 4 within 24 hours, the creation is successful; otherwise, it fails.<Assistant_Red>Neither failed creation nor voluntary cancellation will result in a refund of the creation fee.</>\n<Assistant_Title2>Club Types: </>Clubs are divided into Leisure Clubs and Combat Clubs. You can adjust this in the Club Information modification section. Leisure Clubs will not display Extraordinary Ratings in the member list.\n<Assistant_Title2>Rename Item: </>You can purchase a Renaming Notice in the <Assistant_System>Mall - Secret Collection</> to change the Club's name and emblem text.\n<Assistant_Title2>Activity Restrictions: </>1. Club Member Lock Rule: During Club-based activities (such as <Assistant_System>Four-Way League, Phantom of the Opera, Hunting City War, Highland War</>), Clubs <Assistant_Red>do not allow members to join or leave.</>\n2. Club Activity Pathway Limit: Some Club activities have restrictions on the number of <Assistant_Red>Pathways</> participating; see the Club activity instructions for details.\n3. Before participating in activities, please confirm the position allocation. <Assistant_Red>Some activities only support Official Members participating</>. Official Members are the backbone of the Club and can participate in Club activities; Reserve Members are the reserve force of the Club and cannot participate in some activities. You can maintain an active status and contact management to be promoted to an Official Member.\n<Assistant_Title3>Basic Function Details: </>{SendAnswer:[Club - Club Buildings and Funds]|1401}, {SendAnswer:[Club - Club Positions]|1402}, {SendAnswer:[Club - Club Activity]|1403}, {SendAnswer:[Scene - Club]|567}",
    ["<Assistant_Title1>【Courage to Confess】</>\n<Assistant_Title2>Quest Type: </><Assistant_Property2>Acting Story</>\n<Assistant_Title2>Quest Description: </>On a bench at the street corner, a young man's shoulders are trembling slightly. He has a bouquet of flowers and a letter in front of him, but he can't bring himself to reach out.\n<Assistant_Title2>How to Accept: </>Complete the main story Chapter 2 \"Tides of the Era\", advance to Sequence 9, head to {Location:[廷根(982,778)]|-1990;-22115;-1300;2;5200002;0}, and talk to <Assistant_Red> Fraser </> to accept the quest.\n<Assistant_Title2>Quest Rewards</>: Cognitive Experience, invoices, Adventure Medals, World Adventure Treasure progress"] = "<Assistant_Title1>【Courage to Confess】</>\n<Assistant_Title2>Quest Type: </><Assistant_Property2>Acting Story</>\n<Assistant_Title2>Quest Description: </>On a bench at the street corner, a young man's shoulders are trembling slightly. He has a bouquet of flowers and a letter in front of him, but he can't bring himself to reach out.\n<Assistant_Title2>How to Accept: </>Complete the main story Chapter 2 \"Tides of the Era\", advance to Sequence 9, head to {Location:[Tingen(982,778)]|-1990;-22115;-1300;2;5200002;0}, and talk to <Assistant_Red> Fraser </> to accept the quest.\n<Assistant_Title2>Quest Rewards</>: Cognitive Experience, invoices, Adventure Medals, World Adventure Treasure progress",
    ["<Assistant_Title1>【Covenant Action Points and Weekly Cap】</>\nCovenant Action Points are mainly obtained through corresponding Covenant gameplay and are used to increase the current Covenant level.\n\n<Assistant_Title2>Weekly Cap Rules:</>\nCovenant Action Points have a weekly acquisition cap and can be accumulated for a maximum of two weeks.\n\n<Assistant_Title2>General Experience:</>\nWhen the Action Points for a single Covenant overflow, they are converted into General Action Points. General Action Points can be used for upgrading other Covenants.\n\n<Assistant_Title3>Recommended Searches:</>{SendAnswer:[教团等级、突破与奖励]|1277}"] = "<Assistant_Title1>【Covenant Action Points and Weekly Cap】</>\nCovenant Action Points are mainly obtained through corresponding Covenant gameplay and are used to increase the current Covenant level.\n\n<Assistant_Title2>Weekly Cap Rules:</>\nCovenant Action Points have a weekly acquisition cap and can be accumulated for a maximum of two weeks.\n\n<Assistant_Title2>General Experience:</>\nWhen the Action Points for a single Covenant overflow, they are converted into General Action Points. General Action Points can be used for upgrading other Covenants.\n\n<Assistant_Title3>Recommended Searches:</>{SendAnswer:[Covenant Level, Breakthrough, and Rewards]|1277}",
    ["<Assistant_Title1>【Covenant Level, Breakthrough, and Rewards】</>\nAfter joining a Covenant, you start at Level 1 by default. Obtain Action Points through Covenant gameplay; once the requirements are met, you can increase your level.\n\n<Assistant_Title2>Breakthrough Quests:</>\nFor some levels, you must complete a Breakthrough Quest after reaching the required Action Points. Action Points will continue to accumulate while the Breakthrough Quest is incomplete. Once completed, your level can continue to increase.\n\n<Assistant_Title2>Claiming Rewards:</>\nYou can claim rewards directly in the level rewards interface.\n\n<Assistant_Title3>Recommended Searches:</>{SendAnswer:[教团行动值与周上限]|1276}"] = "<Assistant_Title1>【Covenant Level, Breakthrough, and Rewards】</>\nAfter joining a Covenant, you start at Level 1 by default. Obtain Action Points through Covenant gameplay; once the requirements are met, you can increase your level.\n\n<Assistant_Title2>Breakthrough Quests:</>\nFor some levels, you must complete a Breakthrough Quest after reaching the required Action Points. Action Points will continue to accumulate while the Breakthrough Quest is incomplete. Once completed, your level can continue to increase.\n\n<Assistant_Title2>Claiming Rewards:</>\nYou can claim rewards directly in the level rewards interface.\n\n<Assistant_Title3>Recommended Searches:</>{SendAnswer:[Covenant Action Points and Weekly Cap]|1276}",
    ["<Assistant_Title1>【Covenant Tenets and Exclusive Gameplay】</>\nEach Covenant has its own rules; please follow them and complete weekly quests, otherwise, you will be penalized.\n\n<Assistant_Title2>Exclusive Gameplay:</>\nDifferent Covenants have different exclusive gameplay and abilities. Beyonders can try different Covenant gameplay by switching Covenants.\n\n<Assistant_Title3>Recommended Searches:</>{SendAnswer:[教团行动值与周上限]|1276}"] = "<Assistant_Title1>【Covenant Tenets and Exclusive Gameplay】</>\nEach Covenant has its own rules; please follow them and complete weekly quests, otherwise, you will be penalized.\n\n<Assistant_Title2>Exclusive Gameplay:</>\nDifferent Covenants have different exclusive gameplay and abilities. Beyonders can try different Covenant gameplay by switching Covenants.\n\n<Assistant_Title3>Recommended Searches:</>{SendAnswer:[Covenant Action Points and Weekly Cap]|1276}",
    ["<Assistant_Title1>【Covenant/TRPG】</>\n<Assistant_System>Covenants</> are the core growth and faction system within the TRPG framework. After joining a Covenant, you can obtain an independent <Assistant_Property1>Covenant Level</>, <Assistant_Property1>Covenant Attributes</>, and exclusive gameplay corresponding to that Covenant.\n\n<Assistant_Title2>Main Content:</>\n1. Select a Covenant and complete attribute configuration.\n2. Obtain Covenant Action Points and various rewards through Covenant gameplay.\n3. Increase your Covenant Level to unlock rewards such as actions, appearances, and titles.\n4. Use attributes like Charm, Intuition, Knowledge, and Force for checks during exploration and Covenant gameplay.\n\n<Assistant_Title3>Recommended Searches:</>{SendAnswer:[如何加入教团]|1273}, {SendAnswer:[教团属性说明]|1275}, {SendAnswer:[教团行动值与周上限]|1276}"] = "<Assistant_Title1>【Covenant/TRPG】</>\n<Assistant_System>Covenants</> are the core growth and faction system within the TRPG framework. After joining a Covenant, you can obtain an independent <Assistant_Property1>Covenant Level</>, <Assistant_Property1>Covenant Attributes</>, and exclusive gameplay corresponding to that Covenant.\n\n<Assistant_Title2>Main Content:</>\n1. Select a Covenant and complete attribute configuration.\n2. Obtain Covenant Action Points and various rewards through Covenant gameplay.\n3. Increase your Covenant Level to unlock rewards such as actions, appearances, and titles.\n4. Use attributes like Charm, Intuition, Knowledge, and Force for checks during exploration and Covenant gameplay.\n\n<Assistant_Title3>Recommended Searches:</>{SendAnswer:[How to Join a Covenant]|1273}, {SendAnswer:[Covenant Attribute Explanation]|1275}, {SendAnswer:[Covenant Action Points and Weekly Cap]|1276}",
    ["<Assistant_Title1>【Delivering Feelings】</>\n<Assistant_Title2>Quest Type: </><Assistant_Property2>City Roaming</>\n<Assistant_Title2>Quest Description: </>Beside a bench, several young men and women are gathered, whispering to each other, their eyes occasionally drifting toward the closed door of Blackthorn Security Company.\n<Assistant_Title2>How to Accept: </>Once your Acting Level reaches <Assistant_Red>19</>, head to {Location:[廷根(792,908)]|-20980;-9030;-1499;2;5200002;0} to trigger the quest.\n<Assistant_Title2>Quest Rewards</>: Cognition EXP, Invoice Receipt, Adventure Medal, World Adventure Treasure Progress"] = "<Assistant_Title1>【Delivering Feelings】</>\n<Assistant_Title2>Quest Type: </><Assistant_Property2>City Roaming</>\n<Assistant_Title2>Quest Description: </>Beside a bench, several young men and women are gathered, whispering to each other, their eyes occasionally drifting toward the closed door of Blackthorn Security Company.\n<Assistant_Title2>How to Accept: </>Once your Acting Level reaches <Assistant_Red>19</>, head to {Location:[Tingen(792,908)]|-20980;-9030;-1499;2;5200002;0} to trigger the quest.\n<Assistant_Title2>Quest Rewards</>: Cognition EXP, Invoice Receipt, Adventure Medal, World Adventure Treasure Progress",
    ["<Assistant_Title1>【Dominator's Clash】</>\n<Assistant_Title2>Gameplay Description:</><Assistant_System>Dominator's Clash</> is a <Assistant_Red>3v3 fair competition</> mode, where you can form a team of up to <Assistant_Red>3 people</> to participate in matchmaking. After entering the gameplay, all players will have their attributes adjusted for fairness, and Sealed Artifacts will be unified to <Assistant_Red>Level 3</>.\n<Assistant_Title2>Victory Conditions:</>In the match, dead players cannot be resurrected by Spectator professions. Defeat all players in the enemy team, or deal more damage when the time limit ends to achieve victory.\n<Assistant_Title2>Opening and Rewards:</>The gameplay entry shows the opening time as <Assistant_Red>10:00-1:00</>. You can get a first-win reward once per day in Dominator's Clash, and unused first-win counts can be accumulated up to <Assistant_Red>3 times</>; winning will consume one first-win count and grant double Rank Point rewards.\n<Assistant_Title2>Participation Method:</>{JumpToUI:[前往主宰争锋]|1250094}"] = "<Assistant_Title1>【Dominator's Clash】</>\n<Assistant_Title2>Gameplay Description:</><Assistant_System>Dominator's Clash</> is a <Assistant_Red>3v3 fair competition</> mode, where you can form a team of up to <Assistant_Red>3 people</> to participate in matchmaking. After entering the gameplay, all players will have their attributes adjusted for fairness, and Sealed Artifacts will be unified to <Assistant_Red>Level 3</>.\n<Assistant_Title2>Victory Conditions:</>In the match, dead players cannot be resurrected by Spectator professions. Defeat all players in the enemy team, or deal more damage when the time limit ends to achieve victory.\n<Assistant_Title2>Opening and Rewards:</>The gameplay entry shows the opening time as <Assistant_Red>10:00-1:00</>. You can get a first-win reward once per day in Dominator's Clash, and unused first-win counts can be accumulated up to <Assistant_Red>3 times</>; winning will consume one first-win count and grant double Rank Point rewards.\n<Assistant_Title2>Participation Method:</>{JumpToUI:[Go to Dominator's Clash]|1250094}",
    ["<Assistant_Title1>【End-Time Hunt】</>\n<Assistant_Title2>Gameplay Description:</><Assistant_System>End-Time Hunt</> is a <Assistant_Property1>500-player free-for-all</> field gameplay taking place in the <Assistant_Red>City of Dragon Hunting</>. You can defeat supernatural creatures or hostile players to obtain <Assistant_Property1>Scarlet Relic Materials</> and Rank Points.\n<Assistant_Title2>Core Objective:</>Submit <Assistant_Property1>Scarlet Relic Materials</> to the <Assistant_System>Hunting Butler</> to advance the hunting progress and unlock stage rewards. Scarlet Relics are only effective within the City of Dragon Hunting and will be automatically invalidated and cleared upon leaving.\n<Assistant_Title2>Hunting Time:</>The gameplay is open all day; daily <Assistant_Red>19:00—20:00</> is Hunting Time, with additional sessions on Saturday and Sunday from <Assistant_Red>14:00—15:00</>. During Hunting Time, the amount of Rank Points involved in killing or being killed is doubled.\n<Assistant_Title2>Royal City Event:</>10 minutes after the start of the Friday night Hunting Time, i.e., <Assistant_Red>19:10</>, the Dragon - Projection will refresh in the center of the Royal City; outside of Friday night sessions, the Royal City Guardian will refresh 10 minutes after the start of other Hunting Times.\n<Assistant_Title2>Team Settlement:</>The killer and up to 29 team members who meet the assist conditions participate in the reward settlement. Scarlet Relics are distributed equally among the participants, with remainders prioritized to the killer, and the rest randomly distributed among other participants.\n<Assistant_Title2>Plunder Rules:</>The more fragments displayed above a player's head, the higher the proportion of Scarlet Relics that can be plundered; for every 500 fragments increased, the plunder proportion increases accordingly.\n<Assistant_Title2>Rank Rules:</>When your rank is below <Assistant_Red>Count Tier 1</>, you will not lose Rank Points when killed. Rank Points obtained by killing players will be reduced according to rules during 01:00—08:00 daily and when repeatedly killing the same target within a short period.\n<Assistant_Title2>Participation Method:</>{JumpToUI:[前往终末猎杀]|1250342}"] = "<Assistant_Title1>【End-Time Hunt】</>\n<Assistant_Title2>Gameplay Description:</><Assistant_System>End-Time Hunt</> is a <Assistant_Property1>500-player free-for-all</> field gameplay taking place in the <Assistant_Red>City of Dragon Hunting</>. You can defeat supernatural creatures or hostile players to obtain <Assistant_Property1>Scarlet Relic Materials</> and Rank Points.\n<Assistant_Title2>Core Objective:</>Submit <Assistant_Property1>Scarlet Relic Materials</> to the <Assistant_System>Hunting Butler</> to advance the hunting progress and unlock stage rewards. Scarlet Relics are only effective within the City of Dragon Hunting and will be automatically invalidated and cleared upon leaving.\n<Assistant_Title2>Hunting Time:</>The gameplay is open all day; daily <Assistant_Red>19:00—20:00</> is Hunting Time, with additional sessions on Saturday and Sunday from <Assistant_Red>14:00—15:00</>. During Hunting Time, the amount of Rank Points involved in killing or being killed is doubled.\n<Assistant_Title2>Royal City Event:</>10 minutes after the start of the Friday night Hunting Time, i.e., <Assistant_Red>19:10</>, the Dragon - Projection will refresh in the center of the Royal City; outside of Friday night sessions, the Royal City Guardian will refresh 10 minutes after the start of other Hunting Times.\n<Assistant_Title2>Team Settlement:</>The killer and up to 29 team members who meet the assist conditions participate in the reward settlement. Scarlet Relics are distributed equally among the participants, with remainders prioritized to the killer, and the rest randomly distributed among other participants.\n<Assistant_Title2>Plunder Rules:</>The more fragments displayed above a player's head, the higher the proportion of Scarlet Relics that can be plundered; for every 500 fragments increased, the plunder proportion increases accordingly.\n<Assistant_Title2>Rank Rules:</>When your rank is below <Assistant_Red>Count Tier 1</>, you will not lose Rank Points when killed. Rank Points obtained by killing players will be reduced according to rules during 01:00—08:00 daily and when repeatedly killing the same target within a short period.\n<Assistant_Title2>Participation Method:</>{JumpToUI:[Go to End-Time Hunt]|1250342}",
    ["<Assistant_Title1>【Enthusiastic Actor】</>\n<Assistant_Title2>Quest Type: </><Assistant_Property2>Era Anecdotes</>\n<Assistant_Title2>Quest Description: </>Someone is hawking goods at the Lamud Town station; could you find something good there?\n<Assistant_Title2>How to Accept: </>After reaching Acting Level <Assistant_Red>66</>, go to {Location:[拉姆德古堡(17,363)]|-8170;26423;1601;2;5200130;0}to trigger the quest.\n<Assistant_Title2>Quest Rewards</>: Cognition EXP, Invoices, Adventure Medals, World Adventure Treasure Progress"] = "<Assistant_Title1>【Enthusiastic Actor】</>\n<Assistant_Title2>Quest Type: </><Assistant_Property2>Era Anecdotes</>\n<Assistant_Title2>Quest Description: </>Someone is hawking goods at the Lamud Town station; could you find something good there?\n<Assistant_Title2>How to Accept: </>After reaching Acting Level <Assistant_Red>66</>, go to {Location:[Lamud Castle(17,363)]|-8170;26423;1601;2;5200130;0}to trigger the quest.\n<Assistant_Title2>Quest Rewards</>: Cognition EXP, Invoices, Adventure Medals, World Adventure Treasure Progress",
    ["<Assistant_Title1>【Eternal Night Remnant Veil】</>\n<Assistant_Title2>Description: </>Dungeon Drop Accessory\n<Assistant_Title2>Usage: </>After use, you will obtain the Eternal Night Remnant Veil. You can click <Assistant_System>Appearance - Change Outfit</> to view and use it. \n<Assistant_Title2>Acquisition: </>Obtained via <Assistant_Link>{SendAnswer:[五月庄园·城堡]|21}</>"] = "<Assistant_Title1>【Eternal Night Remnant Veil】</>\n<Assistant_Title2>Description: </>Dungeon Drop Accessory\n<Assistant_Title2>Usage: </>After use, you will obtain the Eternal Night Remnant Veil. You can click <Assistant_System>Appearance - Change Outfit</> to view and use it. \n<Assistant_Title2>Acquisition: </>Obtained via <Assistant_Link>{SendAnswer:[May Manor · Castle]|21}</>",
    ["<Assistant_Title1>【Event】</>\n<Assistant_Title2>Event Goal: </>Various unexpected events will constantly occur in the City of Shadows. Participate in and complete events to obtain bounty rewards and advance gameplay progress.\n<Assistant_Title2>Tips: </>Prioritize completing {SendAnswer:剧情事件|879} to gradually unlock more {SendAnswer:挑战事件|880} and {SendAnswer:竞技事件|881} and experience the complete City of Shadows content.\n<Assistant_Title2>1. Event Types (includes three types): </>\n<Assistant_Title3>① Plot Events: </>Advance the plot and unlock more gameplay content.\n<Assistant_Title3>② Challenge Events: </>Complete boss challenges, racing, and other gameplay to obtain rich rewards. Note: Fierce Battle · Bonnie will convert attributes based on the player's combat power, affecting the challenge.\n<Assistant_Title3>③ Competition Events: </>Participate in resource contention, chases, and compete with other players in the same arena.\n<Assistant_Title2>2. Event Refresh Rules: </>Only events that are currently unlocked and meet the activation conditions will be displayed. As the plot progresses, more events will be gradually unlocked.\n<Assistant_Title3>Plot Events: </>Unlocked after completing prerequisites; they will not refresh randomly.\n<Assistant_Title3>Challenge Events: </>Continuously refresh after meeting activation conditions; they reappear approximately 10 seconds after completion.\n<Assistant_Title3>Competition Events: </>Open for matchmaking at specified times daily; starts after successful matchmaking.\n<Assistant_Title2>3. Reward Rules: </>\n<Assistant_Title3>① Plot Events: </>Complete to claim rewards.\n<Assistant_Title3>② Challenge Events: </>Racing challenges distribute rewards based on ranking; Fierce Battle · Bonnie has tiered rewards based on performance; difficult boss events do not have tiered rewards.\n<Assistant_Title3>③ Competition Events: </>Rewards are distributed based on final ranking.\n<Assistant_Title2>4. Reward Cap: </>There is no limit to the number of times event rewards can be claimed, but there is a weekly cap on the Bounty Value that can be obtained. You can continue to participate in events after reaching the cap, but you will not continue to receive Bounty Value.\n<Assistant_Title2>5. Failure Conditions: </>\nFailure to complete event objectives within the specified time.\nLeaving the event area too far during the event is considered a voluntary abandonment."] = "<Assistant_Title1>【Event】</>\n<Assistant_Title2>Event Goal: </>Various unexpected events will constantly occur in the City of Shadows. Participate in and complete events to obtain bounty rewards and advance gameplay progress.\n<Assistant_Title2>Tips: </>Prioritize completing {SendAnswer:Plot Events|879} to gradually unlock more {SendAnswer:Challenge Events|880} and {SendAnswer:Competition Events|881} and experience the complete City of Shadows content.\n<Assistant_Title2>1. Event Types (includes three types): </>\n<Assistant_Title3>① Plot Events: </>Advance the plot and unlock more gameplay content.\n<Assistant_Title3>② Challenge Events: </>Complete boss challenges, racing, and other gameplay to obtain rich rewards. Note: Fierce Battle · Bonnie will convert attributes based on the player's combat power, affecting the challenge.\n<Assistant_Title3>③ Competition Events: </>Participate in resource contention, chases, and compete with other players in the same arena.\n<Assistant_Title2>2. Event Refresh Rules: </>Only events that are currently unlocked and meet the activation conditions will be displayed. As the plot progresses, more events will be gradually unlocked.\n<Assistant_Title3>Plot Events: </>Unlocked after completing prerequisites; they will not refresh randomly.\n<Assistant_Title3>Challenge Events: </>Continuously refresh after meeting activation conditions; they reappear approximately 10 seconds after completion.\n<Assistant_Title3>Competition Events: </>Open for matchmaking at specified times daily; starts after successful matchmaking.\n<Assistant_Title2>3. Reward Rules: </>\n<Assistant_Title3>① Plot Events: </>Complete to claim rewards.\n<Assistant_Title3>② Challenge Events: </>Racing challenges distribute rewards based on ranking; Fierce Battle · Bonnie has tiered rewards based on performance; difficult boss events do not have tiered rewards.\n<Assistant_Title3>③ Competition Events: </>Rewards are distributed based on final ranking.\n<Assistant_Title2>4. Reward Cap: </>There is no limit to the number of times event rewards can be claimed, but there is a weekly cap on the Bounty Value that can be obtained. You can continue to participate in events after reaching the cap, but you will not continue to receive Bounty Value.\n<Assistant_Title2>5. Failure Conditions: </>\nFailure to complete event objectives within the specified time.\nLeaving the event area too far during the event is considered a voluntary abandonment.",
    ["<Assistant_Title1>【Exploration】</>\n<Assistant_Title2>Instructions:</>In the world of Lord of Mysteries, you can explore the 【Order World】 in various maps, as well as the 【City Dark Side】 gameplay in Tingen. Participating in the gameplay increases the completion of the Order World and the bounty value of the City Dark Side, allowing you to claim generous progress rewards.\n<Assistant_Title2>Entrance Guide:</>\n1. TRPG Entrance\nOpen the menu to enter 【TRPG】, join any sect, and then enter the 【Order World】 or 【City Dark Side】. Select the corresponding gameplay or event and click 【Go】 to automatically pathfind.\n2. Map Entrance\nOpen the map in the top right corner, switch to the 【Exploration】 tab, and select to enter the 【Order World】 or 【City Dark Side】. Then select the gameplay or event you want to experience and click 【Go】 to automatically pathfind.\n<Assistant_Title3>Recommended:</>{JumpToUI:廷根探索合集|1301900}, {JumpToUI:金秋湖探索合集|1301901}, {JumpToUI:拉姆德古堡探索合集|1301902}, {JumpToUI:睡莲小镇探索合集|1301903}, {JumpToUI:霍纳奇斯山脉探索合集|1301904}, {JumpToUI:霍纳奇斯花海探索合集|1301905}\n<Assistant_Title2>Exploration Tips:</>\n{SendAnswer:1.灵性之跃|882}: During exploration, you can long-press the jump button to enter the spirituality leap state; click the jump button again to leap higher!\n{SendAnswer:2.灵视|883}: Click the spirit vision button to enter the spirit vision state, where you can discover nearby treasure chests, quest clues, and interactive puzzle points."] = "<Assistant_Title1>【Exploration】</>\n<Assistant_Title2>Instructions:</>In the world of Lord of Mysteries, you can explore the 【Order World】 in various maps, as well as the 【City Dark Side】 gameplay in Tingen. Participating in the gameplay increases the completion of the Order World and the bounty value of the City Dark Side, allowing you to claim generous progress rewards.\n<Assistant_Title2>Entrance Guide:</>\n1. TRPG Entrance\nOpen the menu to enter 【TRPG】, join any sect, and then enter the 【Order World】 or 【City Dark Side】. Select the corresponding gameplay or event and click 【Go】 to automatically pathfind.\n2. Map Entrance\nOpen the map in the top right corner, switch to the 【Exploration】 tab, and select to enter the 【Order World】 or 【City Dark Side】. Then select the gameplay or event you want to experience and click 【Go】 to automatically pathfind.\n<Assistant_Title3>Recommended:</>{JumpToUI:Tingen Exploration Collection|1301900}, {JumpToUI:Golden Autumn Lake Exploration Collection|1301901}, {JumpToUI:Lamud Castle Exploration Collection|1301902}, {JumpToUI:Water Lily Town Exploration Collection|1301903}, {JumpToUI:Hornacis Mountains Exploration Collection|1301904}, {JumpToUI:Hornacis Flower Sea Exploration Collection|1301905}\n<Assistant_Title2>Exploration Tips:</>\n{SendAnswer:1. Spirituality Leap|882}: During exploration, you can long-press the jump button to enter the spirituality leap state; click the jump button again to leap higher!\n{SendAnswer:2. Spirit Vision|883}: Click the spirit vision button to enter the spirit vision state, where you can discover nearby treasure chests, quest clues, and interactive puzzle points.",
    ["<Assistant_Title1>【Family - Level Rules】</>\n<Assistant_Title2>Rapport and Level: </>Complete weekly family Quests to earn Rapport and increase the family level. The weekly Rapport acquisition cap is <Assistant_Red>2000 points</>. \n<Assistant_Title2>Weekly Quests: </>Family members can earn Rapport by teaming up to participate in corresponding gameplay. \n    <Assistant_Property1>High-Multiplier Rapport: </>Earned during the first few completions of each quest per week; after exceeding this limit, only the normal multiplier is granted. \n    <Assistant_Property1>Refresh Time: </>Quests refresh weekly. \n<Assistant_Title3>Recommended Searches: </>{SendAnswer:[家族]|665}, {SendAnswer:[家族-契约方式]|666}, {SendAnswer:[家族-奖励说明]|667}, {SendAnswer:[家族-展台规则]|669}"] = "<Assistant_Title1>【Family - Level Rules】</>\n<Assistant_Title2>Rapport and Level: </>Complete weekly family Quests to earn Rapport and increase the family level. The weekly Rapport acquisition cap is <Assistant_Red>2000 points</>. \n<Assistant_Title2>Weekly Quests: </>Family members can earn Rapport by teaming up to participate in corresponding gameplay. \n    <Assistant_Property1>High-Multiplier Rapport: </>Earned during the first few completions of each quest per week; after exceeding this limit, only the normal multiplier is granted. \n    <Assistant_Property1>Refresh Time: </>Quests refresh weekly. \n<Assistant_Title3>Recommended Searches: </>{SendAnswer:[Family]|665}, {SendAnswer:[Family - Covenant Method]|666}, {SendAnswer:[Family - Reward Description]|667}, {SendAnswer:[Family - Showcase Rules]|669}",
    ["<Assistant_Title1>【Family - Recruitment Method】</>\n<Assistant_Title2>Responding to Recruitment: </>Beyonders who have not joined a family can choose to initiate or join a recruitment response from other Beyonders. The Beyonder who initiates the response becomes the <Assistant_Property1>Family Chief</> by default. \n<Assistant_Title2>Creating a Family: </>During the recruitment response phase, once the family's response count reaches <Assistant_Red>3 or more members</>, the family can be created. During the creation process, the Chief can adjust the family name and member positions. \n<Assistant_Title2>Joining a Family: </>When a family has fewer than <Assistant_Red>14 members</>, the Chief can initiate family recruitment. Other Beyonders can submit an application, and upon approval by the Chief, they can join the family directly. \n<Assistant_Title3>Recommended Searches: </>{SendAnswer:[家族]|665}, {SendAnswer:[家族-奖励说明]|667}, {SendAnswer:[家族-等级规则]|668}, {SendAnswer:[家族-展台规则]|669}"] = "<Assistant_Title1>【Family - Recruitment Method】</>\n<Assistant_Title2>Responding to Recruitment: </>Beyonders who have not joined a family can choose to initiate or join a recruitment response from other Beyonders. The Beyonder who initiates the response becomes the <Assistant_Property1>Family Chief</> by default. \n<Assistant_Title2>Creating a Family: </>During the recruitment response phase, once the family's response count reaches <Assistant_Red>3 or more members</>, the family can be created. During the creation process, the Chief can adjust the family name and member positions. \n<Assistant_Title2>Joining a Family: </>When a family has fewer than <Assistant_Red>14 members</>, the Chief can initiate family recruitment. Other Beyonders can submit an application, and upon approval by the Chief, they can join the family directly. \n<Assistant_Title3>Recommended Searches: </>{SendAnswer:[Family]|665}, {SendAnswer:[Family - Reward Description]|667}, {SendAnswer:[Family - Level Rules]|668}, {SendAnswer:[Family - Showcase Rules]|669}",
    ["<Assistant_Title1>【Family - Reward Description】</>\n<Assistant_Title2>Family Attribute Bonus: </>Teaming up with a certain number of members from the same family within a Dungeon grants additional <Assistant_Property1>Resurrection count bonuses</> and <Assistant_Property1>attribute replenishment bonuses</>. There is a <Assistant_Red>24-hour</> cooldown period after leaving a family. \n<Assistant_Title2>Dungeon Reward Bonus: </>In specific Dungeons, clearing the level while teamed up with a certain number of members from the same family grants <Assistant_Property1>extra rewards</>. There is a <Assistant_Red>24-hour</> cooldown period after leaving a family. \n<Assistant_Title2>Family Shop Rewards: </>Completing family Quests grants <Assistant_Property1>Rapport</> and <Assistant_Property1>Companion Emblem</> rewards. Upon meeting certain family level and membership duration requirements, you can exchange them for <Assistant_System>Companion Shop</> <Assistant_Property1>precious rewards</>. \n<Assistant_Title2>Family Title: </>Joining a family automatically grants a <Assistant_Property1>Family Title</>. The Chief can modify the family name in the family details. Name changes have a <Assistant_Red>30-day</> cooldown. Once modified, the family title will be updated accordingly. \n<Assistant_Title2>Family Showcase: </>As the family level increases, exclusive scenes for the family showcase will be unlocked. For specific rules, please refer to <Assistant_Property1>Family - Showcase Rules</>. \n<Assistant_Title3>Recommended Searches: </>{SendAnswer:[家族]|665}, {SendAnswer:[家族-契约方式]|666}, {SendAnswer:[家族-等级规则]|668}, {SendAnswer:[家族-展台规则]|669}"] = "<Assistant_Title1>【Family - Reward Description】</>\n<Assistant_Title2>Family Attribute Bonus: </>Teaming up with a certain number of members from the same family within a Dungeon grants additional <Assistant_Property1>Resurrection count bonuses</> and <Assistant_Property1>attribute replenishment bonuses</>. There is a <Assistant_Red>24-hour</> cooldown period after leaving a family. \n<Assistant_Title2>Dungeon Reward Bonus: </>In specific Dungeons, clearing the level while teamed up with a certain number of members from the same family grants <Assistant_Property1>extra rewards</>. There is a <Assistant_Red>24-hour</> cooldown period after leaving a family. \n<Assistant_Title2>Family Shop Rewards: </>Completing family Quests grants <Assistant_Property1>Rapport</> and <Assistant_Property1>Companion Emblem</> rewards. Upon meeting certain family level and membership duration requirements, you can exchange them for <Assistant_System>Companion Shop</> <Assistant_Property1>precious rewards</>. \n<Assistant_Title2>Family Title: </>Joining a family automatically grants a <Assistant_Property1>Family Title</>. The Chief can modify the family name in the family details. Name changes have a <Assistant_Red>30-day</> cooldown. Once modified, the family title will be updated accordingly. \n<Assistant_Title2>Family Showcase: </>As the family level increases, exclusive scenes for the family showcase will be unlocked. For specific rules, please refer to <Assistant_Property1>Family - Showcase Rules</>. \n<Assistant_Title3>Recommended Searches: </>{SendAnswer:[Family]|665}, {SendAnswer:[Family - Covenant Method]|666}, {SendAnswer:[Family - Level Rules]|668}, {SendAnswer:[Family - Showcase Rules]|669}",
    ["<Assistant_Title1>【Family - Showcase Rules】</>\n<Assistant_Title2>System Entry: </><Assistant_System>Menu - Family - Edit Showcase</>\n<Assistant_Title2>Editing Permissions: </>Different family members have different permissions to change showcase content. \n    <Assistant_Property1>Ordinary Members: </>Only their own character. \n    <Assistant_Property1>Chief: </>All member characters (the configurable action range is limited to what the corresponding player has unlocked), <Assistant_Property1>Camera</>, <Assistant_Property1>Scene</> (configurable range is limited to what the Chief has unlocked), <Assistant_Property1>Set Pieces</> (configurable range is limited to what the Chief has unlocked), <Assistant_Property1>Wind Direction</>, <Assistant_Property1>Color Grading</>. \n<Assistant_Title2>Showcase Removal: </>When a family member leaves the family, the following content for that player will be automatically removed from the showcase: \n    <Assistant_Property1>Showcase Character</>\n    <Assistant_Property1>Scene</> (if used) \n    <Assistant_Property1>Set Pieces</> (if used) \n<Assistant_Title2>Showcase Unlocks: </>As the family level increases, exclusive family showcase scenes are unlocked at level 2 and level 6. These scenes can only be used in the family showcase. \n<Assistant_Title3>Recommended Searches: </>{SendAnswer:[家族]|665}, {SendAnswer:[家族-契约方式]|666}, {SendAnswer:[家族-奖励说明]|667}, {SendAnswer:[家族-等级规则]|668}"] = "<Assistant_Title1>【Family - Showcase Rules】</>\n<Assistant_Title2>System Entry: </><Assistant_System>Menu - Family - Edit Showcase</>\n<Assistant_Title2>Editing Permissions: </>Different family members have different permissions to change showcase content. \n    <Assistant_Property1>Ordinary Members: </>Only their own character. \n    <Assistant_Property1>Chief: </>All member characters (the configurable action range is limited to what the corresponding player has unlocked), <Assistant_Property1>Camera</>, <Assistant_Property1>Scene</> (configurable range is limited to what the Chief has unlocked), <Assistant_Property1>Set Pieces</> (configurable range is limited to what the Chief has unlocked), <Assistant_Property1>Wind Direction</>, <Assistant_Property1>Color Grading</>. \n<Assistant_Title2>Showcase Removal: </>When a family member leaves the family, the following content for that player will be automatically removed from the showcase: \n    <Assistant_Property1>Showcase Character</>\n    <Assistant_Property1>Scene</> (if used) \n    <Assistant_Property1>Set Pieces</> (if used) \n<Assistant_Title2>Showcase Unlocks: </>As the family level increases, exclusive family showcase scenes are unlocked at level 2 and level 6. These scenes can only be used in the family showcase. \n<Assistant_Title3>Recommended Searches: </>{SendAnswer:[Family]|665}, {SendAnswer:[Family - Contract Methods]|666}, {SendAnswer:[Family - Reward Explanation]|667}, {SendAnswer:[Family - Level Rules]|668}",
    ["<Assistant_Title1>【Family】</>\n<Assistant_Title2>Unlock Level: </>Cognitive Level <Assistant_Red>37</>\n<Assistant_Title2>System Entry: </><Assistant_System>Menu-Family</>{JumpToUI:[【前往查看】]|1250091}\n<Assistant_Title2>System Introduction: </>In the name of the family, with oaths as locks, be each other's anchors on the edge of the abyss of fate. Find friends with common goals to establish a family contract, complete family quests to increase family level, and obtain <Assistant_Property1>Companion Emblems</> to exchange for <Assistant_Property1>precious rewards</>.\n<Assistant_Title3>Detailed Rules: </>{SendAnswer:[家族-契约方式]|666}, {SendAnswer:[家族-奖励说明]|667}, {SendAnswer:[家族-等级规则]|668}, {SendAnswer:[家族-展台规则]|669}"] = "<Assistant_Title1>【Family】</>\n<Assistant_Title2>Unlock Level: </>Cognitive Level <Assistant_Red>37</>\n<Assistant_Title2>System Entry: </><Assistant_System>Menu-Family</>{JumpToUI:[【Go to View】]|1250091}\n<Assistant_Title2>System Introduction: </>In the name of the family, with oaths as locks, be each other's anchors on the edge of the abyss of fate. Find friends with common goals to establish a family contract, complete family quests to increase family level, and obtain <Assistant_Property1>Companion Emblems</> to exchange for <Assistant_Property1>precious rewards</>.\n<Assistant_Title3>Detailed Rules: </>{SendAnswer:[Family - Contract Methods]|666}, {SendAnswer:[Family - Reward Explanation]|667}, {SendAnswer:[Family - Level Rules]|668}, {SendAnswer:[Family - Showcase Rules]|669}",
    ["<Assistant_Title1>【Firearm Shooting Gameplay】</>\n<Assistant_Title2>Activation Rules: </>In <Assistant_System>Story Quests</> and <Assistant_System>Sinful Tingen</>'s <Assistant_Property1>certain specific levels</>, the firearm function will be activated as the level progresses. \n<Assistant_Title2>Ability Introduction: </>After activating firearms, use the Basic Attack button to shoot directly, and use skills to switch between different firearms, aim down sights, and perform auxiliary knockback effects. \nIn different levels, the types of activated firearms will vary; please use them reasonably to defeat enemies. \n<Assistant_Title3>Recommended Search: </>{SendAnswer:[瞄准射击]|903}, {SendAnswer:[手枪]|899}, {SendAnswer:[霰弹枪]|900}, {SendAnswer:[狙击枪]|901}"] = "<Assistant_Title1>【Firearm Shooting Gameplay】</>\n<Assistant_Title2>Activation Rules: </>In <Assistant_System>Story Quests</> and <Assistant_System>Sinful Tingen</>'s <Assistant_Property1>certain specific levels</>, the firearm function will be activated as the level progresses. \n<Assistant_Title2>Ability Introduction: </>After activating firearms, use the Basic Attack button to shoot directly, and use skills to switch between different firearms, aim down sights, and perform auxiliary knockback effects. \nIn different levels, the types of activated firearms will vary; please use them reasonably to defeat enemies. \n<Assistant_Title3>Recommended Search: </>{SendAnswer:[Aiming and Shooting]|903}, {SendAnswer:[Pistol]|899}, {SendAnswer:[Shotgun]|900}, {SendAnswer:[Sniper Rifle]|901}",
    ["<Assistant_Title1>【Flicker of a Match】</>\n<Assistant_Title2>Quest Type: </><Assistant_Property2>Life in the Era</>\n<Assistant_Title2>Quest Description: </>A weak cry comes from Lower Street on Iron Cross Street in Tingen; it sounds like a girl's voice.\n<Assistant_Title2>How to Accept: </>After your Acting level reaches <Assistant_Red>Level 60</>, head to {Location:[廷根(763,1244)]|-23665;24457;-2004;2;5200002;0} to trigger the quest.\n<Assistant_Title2>Quest Rewards</>: Cognitive Experience, Bound Sol, invoices, Adventure Medals, World Adventure Treasure progress"] = "<Assistant_Title1>【Flicker of a Match】</>\n<Assistant_Title2>Quest Type: </><Assistant_Property2>Life in the Era</>\n<Assistant_Title2>Quest Description: </>A weak cry comes from Lower Street on Iron Cross Street in Tingen; it sounds like a girl's voice.\n<Assistant_Title2>How to Accept: </>After your Acting level reaches <Assistant_Red>Level 60</>, head to {Location:[Tingen(763,1244)]|-23665;24457;-2004;2;5200002;0} to trigger the quest.\n<Assistant_Title2>Quest Rewards</>: Cognitive Experience, Bound Sol, invoices, Adventure Medals, World Adventure Treasure progress",
    ["<Assistant_Title1>【Four-Way League】</>\n<Assistant_Title2>Gameplay Description:</><Assistant_System>Four-Way League</> is a large-scale battlefield gameplay between Clubs. Each match features <Assistant_Red>4 Clubs</> competing in the same arena, with each Club fielding up to <Assistant_Red>60 official members</>, for a total of <Assistant_Red>240 players</> per match; a single Club can have at most <Assistant_Red>16 people</> of the same Pathway on the field. Each match lasts <Assistant_Red>23 minutes</>.\n<Assistant_Title2>Tournament Rules:</>Each round consists of two matches. Before the first match of each round, the 1st/2nd, 3rd/4th, 5th/6th, and 7th/8th place teams of the group enter different match groups and are randomly assigned while satisfying this rule. The top 2 of each group in the first match enter the Winner's Bracket, and the bottom 2 enter the Loser's Bracket; the second match consists of Winner's Bracket and Loser's Bracket duels to determine the 1st to 8th place for the round.\n<Assistant_Title2>Victory Rules:</>The Club that reaches <Assistant_Red>3000 points</> first immediately secures victory; if no one reaches 3000 points when the match ends, the ranking is based on current points. If points are equal, compare <Assistant_Property1>Total Kills</>, then <Assistant_Property1>Total Club Beyonder Rating</>.\n<Assistant_Title2>In-Match Points:</>The only source of in-match points is Guardian ownership settlement. The first to occupy a Guardian gains <Assistant_Red>50 points</>; every <Assistant_Red>5 seconds</> during small settlements, each occupied Guardian provides <Assistant_Red>1 point</>; every <Assistant_Red>30 seconds</> during large settlements, each occupied Guardian provides <Assistant_Red>18 points</>. At the <Assistant_Red>4th, 8th, 12th, 16th, and 20th minutes</> of the match, high-multiplier Guardian ownership settlements will randomly refresh, providing <Assistant_Red>72 or 108 points</> per occupied Guardian.\n<Assistant_Title2>Strategic Server Screening Points:</>During the first two rounds of the league in the <Assistant_Property1>Strategic Server Screening Phase</>, the Strategic Server Screening Point rules will be enabled. 1st to 4th place in a single match receive <Assistant_Red>30, 15, 10, 5 points</> respectively; 1st to 4th place in the final of the first round receive <Assistant_Red>60, 50, 45, 40 points</>, and 5th to 8th place receive <Assistant_Red>10 points</> each; 1st to 4th place in the final of the second round receive <Assistant_Red>200, 100, 70, 50 points</>, and 5th to 8th place receive <Assistant_Red>15 points</> each. After the first two rounds of the league in the Strategic Server Screening Phase, the top 4 Clubs in total Strategic Server Screening points in this division will advance to the <Assistant_Property1>Four-Way League Apocalypse Group</> and gain the qualification to <Assistant_Property1>participate in the Strategic Server</>.\n<Assistant_Title2>Tie-breaking:</>Strategic Server Screening rankings are primarily ordered by <Assistant_Property1>Total Strategic Server Screening Points</> from high to low. If total points are equal: after the first or second round of the league, sort by the Club's <Assistant_Property1>Final Ranking</> in this round, with the higher rank taking priority; after the first match of each round of the Four-Way League, the final ranking for this round has not yet been determined, so tied Clubs are not distinguished by rank, and the current display order does not represent the final ranking of this round.\n<Assistant_Title2>Guardian Contention:</>There are <Assistant_Red>5 Guardians</> on the battlefield. The Club that lands the final blow on a Guardian gains control of it; after ownership, the Guardian will immediately respawn and belong to that side. Guardians cannot be healed, but will slowly recover health automatically when there are no enemies nearby.\n<Assistant_Title2>Resources and Command:</>Defeating enemy players or occupying Guardians grants resource points and automatically accumulates Morale Level. The President, Vice-President, and Councilors can consume resource points to release Command Skills.\n<Assistant_Title2>Command Skills:</><Assistant_Property1>Declaration of Defeating the Enemy</> consumes 1000 resource points, increasing all members' Pathway Suppression by 15% for 20 seconds, cooldown 180 seconds; <Assistant_Property1>Forced March</> consumes 600 resource points, increasing all members' movement speed by 60% for 10 seconds, cooldown 120 seconds; <Assistant_Property1>Zeroing Edict</> consumes 1500 resource points, clearing the current resurrection wait for all members and covering members who fall in battle within the following 5 seconds, cooldown 240 seconds; <Assistant_Property1>Summon Teleport</> consumes 2400 resource points, summoning all members to the designated assembly point, cooldown 240 seconds; <Assistant_Property1>Sanctuary Protection</> consumes 1000 resource points, restoring 50% of the maximum health of all your side's Guardians, cooldown 180 seconds.\n<Assistant_Title2>Participation Method:</>{JumpToUI:[前往四方联赛]|1250063}"] = "<Assistant_Title1>【Four-Way League】</>\n<Assistant_Title2>Gameplay Description:</><Assistant_System>Four-Way League</> is a large-scale battlefield gameplay between Clubs. Each match features <Assistant_Red>4 Clubs</> competing in the same arena, with each Club fielding up to <Assistant_Red>60 official members</>, for a total of <Assistant_Red>240 players</> per match; a single Club can have at most <Assistant_Red>16 people</> of the same Pathway on the field. Each match lasts <Assistant_Red>23 minutes</>.\n<Assistant_Title2>Tournament Rules:</>Each round consists of two matches. Before the first match of each round, the 1st/2nd, 3rd/4th, 5th/6th, and 7th/8th place teams of the group enter different match groups and are randomly assigned while satisfying this rule. The top 2 of each group in the first match enter the Winner's Bracket, and the bottom 2 enter the Loser's Bracket; the second match consists of Winner's Bracket and Loser's Bracket duels to determine the 1st to 8th place for the round.\n<Assistant_Title2>Victory Rules:</>The Club that reaches <Assistant_Red>3000 points</> first immediately secures victory; if no one reaches 3000 points when the match ends, the ranking is based on current points. If points are equal, compare <Assistant_Property1>Total Kills</>, then <Assistant_Property1>Total Club Beyonder Rating</>.\n<Assistant_Title2>In-Match Points:</>The only source of in-match points is Guardian ownership settlement. The first to occupy a Guardian gains <Assistant_Red>50 points</>; every <Assistant_Red>5 seconds</> during small settlements, each occupied Guardian provides <Assistant_Red>1 point</>; every <Assistant_Red>30 seconds</> during large settlements, each occupied Guardian provides <Assistant_Red>18 points</>. At the <Assistant_Red>4th, 8th, 12th, 16th, and 20th minutes</> of the match, high-multiplier Guardian ownership settlements will randomly refresh, providing <Assistant_Red>72 or 108 points</> per occupied Guardian.\n<Assistant_Title2>Strategic Server Screening Points:</>During the first two rounds of the league in the <Assistant_Property1>Strategic Server Screening Phase</>, the Strategic Server Screening Point rules will be enabled. 1st to 4th place in a single match receive <Assistant_Red>30, 15, 10, 5 points</> respectively; 1st to 4th place in the final of the first round receive <Assistant_Red>60, 50, 45, 40 points</>, and 5th to 8th place receive <Assistant_Red>10 points</> each; 1st to 4th place in the final of the second round receive <Assistant_Red>200, 100, 70, 50 points</>, and 5th to 8th place receive <Assistant_Red>15 points</> each. After the first two rounds of the league in the Strategic Server Screening Phase, the top 4 Clubs in total Strategic Server Screening points in this division will advance to the <Assistant_Property1>Four-Way League Apocalypse Group</> and gain the qualification to <Assistant_Property1>participate in the Strategic Server</>.\n<Assistant_Title2>Tie-breaking:</>Strategic Server Screening rankings are primarily ordered by <Assistant_Property1>Total Strategic Server Screening Points</> from high to low. If total points are equal: after the first or second round of the league, sort by the Club's <Assistant_Property1>Final Ranking</> in this round, with the higher rank taking priority; after the first match of each round of the Four-Way League, the final ranking for this round has not yet been determined, so tied Clubs are not distinguished by rank, and the current display order does not represent the final ranking of this round.\n<Assistant_Title2>Guardian Contention:</>There are <Assistant_Red>5 Guardians</> on the battlefield. The Club that lands the final blow on a Guardian gains control of it; after ownership, the Guardian will immediately respawn and belong to that side. Guardians cannot be healed, but will slowly recover health automatically when there are no enemies nearby.\n<Assistant_Title2>Resources and Command:</>Defeating enemy players or occupying Guardians grants resource points and automatically accumulates Morale Level. The President, Vice-President, and Councilors can consume resource points to release Command Skills.\n<Assistant_Title2>Command Skills:</><Assistant_Property1>Declaration of Defeating the Enemy</> consumes 1000 resource points, increasing all members' Pathway Suppression by 15% for 20 seconds, cooldown 180 seconds; <Assistant_Property1>Forced March</> consumes 600 resource points, increasing all members' movement speed by 60% for 10 seconds, cooldown 120 seconds; <Assistant_Property1>Zeroing Edict</> consumes 1500 resource points, clearing the current resurrection wait for all members and covering members who fall in battle within the following 5 seconds, cooldown 240 seconds; <Assistant_Property1>Summon Teleport</> consumes 2400 resource points, summoning all members to the designated assembly point, cooldown 240 seconds; <Assistant_Property1>Sanctuary Protection</> consumes 1000 resource points, restoring 50% of the maximum health of all your side's Guardians, cooldown 180 seconds.\n<Assistant_Title2>Participation Method:</>{JumpToUI:[Go to Four-Way League]|1250063}",
    ["<Assistant_Title1>【Friends - Friend List】</>\n<Assistant_Title2>System Access: </><Assistant_System>Menu - Friends</>{JumpToUI:[【前往查看】]|1250030}\n<Assistant_Title2>Friend Limit: </>The limit for friends on the current server is 200, and cross-server friends have an independent group with a limit of 50.\n<Assistant_Title2>Visibility Settings: </><Assistant_System>In Friends - Settings (Top Right)</>, you can set the visibility range of your online status. You can choose from four states: Visible to All, Invisible to All, Invisible to Specific People, or Partially Visible. You can also adjust visibility and invisibility ranges in the settings. If there are players in a group chat who are not your friends, this visibility setting will not take effect.\n<Assistant_Title2>Friend Groups: </><Assistant_System>Below Menu - Friends</>, click <Assistant_System>Create Group</> to create custom friend groups; you can create up to 6 groups. After creating a group, you can sort and quickly delete them via <Assistant_System>Manage Groups</>.\n<Assistant_Title2>Club Members: </>This group list displays current Club members who are not your friends by default.\n<Assistant_Title3>Recommended Searches: </>{SendAnswer:[好友]|1406}, {SendAnswer:[好友-私聊]|1408}, {SendAnswer:[好友-群聊]|1409}, {SendAnswer:[好友-好友度]|1410}, {SendAnswer:[好友-跨服好友]|1411}, {SendAnswer:[好友-删除拉黑]|1412}"] = "<Assistant_Title1>【Friends - Friend List】</>\n<Assistant_Title2>System Access: </><Assistant_System>Menu - Friends</>{JumpToUI:[【Go to View】]|1250030}\n<Assistant_Title2>Friend Limit: </>The limit for friends on the current server is 200, and cross-server friends have an independent group with a limit of 50.\n<Assistant_Title2>Visibility Settings: </><Assistant_System>In Friends - Settings (Top Right)</>, you can set the visibility range of your online status. You can choose from four states: Visible to All, Invisible to All, Invisible to Specific People, or Partially Visible. You can also adjust visibility and invisibility ranges in the settings. If there are players in a group chat who are not your friends, this visibility setting will not take effect.\n<Assistant_Title2>Friend Groups: </><Assistant_System>Below Menu - Friends</>, click <Assistant_System>Create Group</> to create custom friend groups; you can create up to 6 groups. After creating a group, you can sort and quickly delete them via <Assistant_System>Manage Groups</>.\n<Assistant_Title2>Club Members: </>This group list displays current Club members who are not your friends by default.\n<Assistant_Title3>Recommended Searches: </>{SendAnswer:[Friends]|1406}, {SendAnswer:[Friends - Private Chat]|1408}, {SendAnswer:[Friends - Group Chat]|1409}, {SendAnswer:[Friends - Friendliness]|1410}, {SendAnswer:[Friends - Cross-Server Friends]|1411}, {SendAnswer:[Friends - Delete and Block]|1412}",
    ["<Assistant_Title1>【Friends - Group Chat】</>\n<Assistant_Title2>System Access: </><Assistant_System>Menu - Friends - Group Chat</>\n<Assistant_Title2>Create and Join Group Chat: </><Assistant_System>In Menu - Friends - Group Chat</>, click the Create Group Chat button to create a group and invite friends to join. You can also join existing group chats through invitations from group members.\n<Assistant_Title2>Group Chat Members: </>The limit for a single group chat is 50 people; group chats support cross-server friends joining.\n<Assistant_Title2>Group Chat Voice: </>Click <Assistant_System>Create Voice</> to initiate a group voice call; group chat voice is not mutually exclusive with voice rooms or team voice.\n<Assistant_Title3>Recommended Searches: </>{SendAnswer:[好友]|1406}, {SendAnswer:[好友-好友列表]|1407}, {SendAnswer:[好友-私聊]|1408}, {SendAnswer:[好友-好友度]|1410}, {SendAnswer:[好友-跨服好友]|1411}, {SendAnswer:[好友-删除拉黑]|1412}"] = "<Assistant_Title1>【Friends - Group Chat】</>\n<Assistant_Title2>System Access: </><Assistant_System>Menu - Friends - Group Chat</>\n<Assistant_Title2>Create and Join Group Chat: </><Assistant_System>In Menu - Friends - Group Chat</>, click the Create Group Chat button to create a group and invite friends to join. You can also join existing group chats through invitations from group members.\n<Assistant_Title2>Group Chat Members: </>The limit for a single group chat is 50 people; group chats support cross-server friends joining.\n<Assistant_Title2>Group Chat Voice: </>Click <Assistant_System>Create Voice</> to initiate a group voice call; group chat voice is not mutually exclusive with voice rooms or team voice.\n<Assistant_Title3>Recommended Searches: </>{SendAnswer:[Friends]|1406}, {SendAnswer:[Friends - Friend List]|1407}, {SendAnswer:[Friends - Private Chat]|1408}, {SendAnswer:[Friends - Friendliness]|1410}, {SendAnswer:[Friends - Cross-Server Friends]|1411}, {SendAnswer:[Friends - Delete and Block]|1412}",
    ["<Assistant_Title1>【Friends - Private Chat】</>\n<Assistant_Title2>System Access: </><Assistant_System>Menu - Friends</>{JumpToUI:[【前往查看】]|1250030}\n<Assistant_Title2>Pin Friend: </><Assistant_System>In Friends - Private Chat - Settings (Bottom Right)</> chat settings, you can pin a friend. Regardless of whether they are online, they will be displayed at the top of your friend list.\n<Assistant_Title2>Friend Remarks: </><Assistant_System>In Friends - Private Chat - Settings (Bottom Right)</> chat settings, you can set your own remarks for friends.\n<Assistant_Title2>Do Not Disturb: </><Assistant_System>In Friends - Private Chat - Settings (Bottom Right)</> chat settings, you can toggle Do Not Disturb. Once enabled, messages from that player will no longer trigger pop-ups or red dot notifications.\n<Assistant_Title3>Recommended Searches: </>{SendAnswer:[好友]|1406}, {SendAnswer:[好友-好友列表]|1407}, {SendAnswer:[好友-群聊]|1409}, {SendAnswer:[好友-好友度]|1410}, {SendAnswer:[好友-跨服好友]|1411}, {SendAnswer:[好友-删除拉黑]|1412}"] = "<Assistant_Title1>【Friends - Private Chat】</>\n<Assistant_Title2>System Access: </><Assistant_System>Menu - Friends</>{JumpToUI:[【Go to View】]|1250030}\n<Assistant_Title2>Pin Friend: </><Assistant_System>In Friends - Private Chat - Settings (Bottom Right)</> chat settings, you can pin a friend. Regardless of whether they are online, they will be displayed at the top of your friend list.\n<Assistant_Title2>Friend Remarks: </><Assistant_System>In Friends - Private Chat - Settings (Bottom Right)</> chat settings, you can set your own remarks for friends.\n<Assistant_Title2>Do Not Disturb: </><Assistant_System>In Friends - Private Chat - Settings (Bottom Right)</> chat settings, you can toggle Do Not Disturb. Once enabled, messages from that player will no longer trigger pop-ups or red dot notifications.\n<Assistant_Title3>Recommended Searches: </>{SendAnswer:[Friends]|1406}, {SendAnswer:[Friends - Friend List]|1407}, {SendAnswer:[Friends - Group Chat]|1409}, {SendAnswer:[Friends - Friendliness]|1410}, {SendAnswer:[Friends - Cross-Server Friends]|1411}, {SendAnswer:[Friends - Delete and Block]|1412}",
    ["<Assistant_Title1>【Friends】</>\n<Assistant_Title2>Required Level: </>Cognition Level <Assistant_Red>Level 2</>\n<Assistant_Title2>System Access: </><Assistant_System>Menu - Friends</>{JumpToUI:[【前往查看】]|1250030}\n<Assistant_Title2>System Introduction: </>In the Friends interface, you can search for, add, and manage friends, view friend personal information and online status, and perform operations such as private chatting and gifting.\n<Assistant_Title2>Adding Friends: </><Assistant_System>Under the Friends - Add</> tab, enter a character nickname or numeric ID to search for friends on the current server or cross-server.\n<Assistant_Title2>Friend Requests: </><Assistant_System>Under the Friends - Requests</> tab, you can manage friend request information. \n<Assistant_Title2>Friend Recommendations: </><Assistant_System>Under the Friends - Add</> tab, the system automatically recommends friends from the current server.\n<Assistant_Title2>Friend Pop-up Settings: </><Assistant_System>In Settings - Social - Information Settings</>, you can manage whether to display friend request pop-ups.\n<Assistant_Title3>Basic Function Details: </>{SendAnswer:[好友-好友列表]|1407}, {SendAnswer:[好友-私聊]|1408}, {SendAnswer:[好友-群聊]|1409}, {SendAnswer:[好友-好友度]|1410}, {SendAnswer:[好友-跨服好友]|1411}, {SendAnswer:[好友-删除拉黑]|1412}"] = "<Assistant_Title1>【Friends】</>\n<Assistant_Title2>Required Level: </>Cognition Level <Assistant_Red>Level 2</>\n<Assistant_Title2>System Access: </><Assistant_System>Menu - Friends</>{JumpToUI:[【Go to View】]|1250030}\n<Assistant_Title2>System Introduction: </>In the Friends interface, you can search for, add, and manage friends, view friend personal information and online status, and perform operations such as private chatting and gifting.\n<Assistant_Title2>Adding Friends: </><Assistant_System>Under the Friends - Add</> tab, enter a character nickname or numeric ID to search for friends on the current server or cross-server.\n<Assistant_Title2>Friend Requests: </><Assistant_System>Under the Friends - Requests</> tab, you can manage friend request information. \n<Assistant_Title2>Friend Recommendations: </><Assistant_System>Under the Friends - Add</> tab, the system automatically recommends friends from the current server.\n<Assistant_Title2>Friend Pop-up Settings: </><Assistant_System>In Settings - Social - Information Settings</>, you can manage whether to display friend request pop-ups.\n<Assistant_Title3>Basic Function Details: </>{SendAnswer:[Friends - Friend List]|1407}, {SendAnswer:[Friends - Private Chat]|1408}, {SendAnswer:[Friends - Group Chat]|1409}, {SendAnswer:[Friends - Friendliness]|1410}, {SendAnswer:[Friends - Cross-Server Friends]|1411}, {SendAnswer:[Friends - Delete and Block]|1412}",
