    ["<Assistant_Title1>【Utopia Theater】</>\n<Assistant_Title2>Dungeon Type: </><Assistant_Property1>Solo/Duo Dungeon</>\n<Assistant_Title2>Features: </>\n  <Assistant_Property1>Memory Fragments: </>Players have a chance to obtain residual memories dropped by defeated marionettes that have suffered a loss of control. You can choose various memory fragments to strengthen your abilities, constantly growing and changing to face stronger challenges on each floor.\n  <Assistant_Property1>Memory Fragment Gifting: </>In duo mode, players can use the Memory Retrace function in the memory fragment interface to convert their own memory fragments into a retraceable form that teammates can pick up, allowing you to share fragments and grow together.\n<Assistant_Title2>Participation Requirements: </>\n    <Assistant_Property1>Normal Difficulty: </>Level 30\n    <Assistant_Property1>Hard Difficulty: </>Level 30, unlocked after clearing Normal Difficulty\n    <Assistant_Property1>Nightmare Difficulty: </>Level 61, unlocked after clearing Normal Difficulty\n<Assistant_Title2>How to Participate: </>Click <Assistant_System>Menu - World Adventure - Dungeon - </>{JumpToUI:[乌托邦剧院]|1302351}to participate.\n<Assistant_Title2>Party Size: </>Enter solo or as a duo.\n<Assistant_Title2>Rewards: </>World Adventure Chest, Gold Thread, Random Marionette Fragment Box, etc.\n    <Assistant_Property1>First-Clear Rewards for Each Difficulty: </>Bound Pounds, Purple/Gold Random Marionette Fragment Box\n    <Assistant_Property1>Weekly Progress Rewards: </>World Adventure Chest, Gold Thread, Purple/Gold Random Marionette Fragment Box\n<Assistant_Red>Each difficulty provides 1 first-clear reward; you can earn progress rewards up to a limit of 1200 Stage Echoes per week.</>\n<Assistant_Title2>Covenant Bonus: </>\n    <Assistant_Property1>Players who form a Covenant relationship</>and enter duo mode will receive extra resurrection counts and extra Marionette Essence (used for purchasing important items within the dungeon)."] = "<Assistant_Title1>【Utopia Theater】</>\n<Assistant_Title2>Dungeon Type: </><Assistant_Property1>Solo/Duo Dungeon</>\n<Assistant_Title2>Features: </>\n  <Assistant_Property1>Memory Fragments: </>Players have a chance to obtain residual memories dropped by defeated marionettes that have suffered a loss of control. You can choose various memory fragments to strengthen your abilities, constantly growing and changing to face stronger challenges on each floor.\n  <Assistant_Property1>Memory Fragment Gifting: </>In duo mode, players can use the Memory Retrace function in the memory fragment interface to convert their own memory fragments into a retraceable form that teammates can pick up, allowing you to share fragments and grow together.\n<Assistant_Title2>Participation Requirements: </>\n    <Assistant_Property1>Normal Difficulty: </>Level 30\n    <Assistant_Property1>Hard Difficulty: </>Level 30, unlocked after clearing Normal Difficulty\n    <Assistant_Property1>Nightmare Difficulty: </>Level 61, unlocked after clearing Normal Difficulty\n<Assistant_Title2>How to Participate: </>Click <Assistant_System>Menu - World Adventure - Dungeon - </>{JumpToUI:[Utopia Theater]|1302351}to participate.\n<Assistant_Title2>Party Size: </>Enter solo or as a duo.\n<Assistant_Title2>Rewards: </>World Adventure Chest, Gold Thread, Random Marionette Fragment Box, etc.\n    <Assistant_Property1>First-Clear Rewards for Each Difficulty: </>Bound Pounds, Purple/Gold Random Marionette Fragment Box\n    <Assistant_Property1>Weekly Progress Rewards: </>World Adventure Chest, Gold Thread, Purple/Gold Random Marionette Fragment Box\n<Assistant_Red>Each difficulty provides 1 first-clear reward; you can earn progress rewards up to a limit of 1200 Stage Echoes per week.</>\n<Assistant_Title2>Covenant Bonus: </>\n    <Assistant_Property1>Players who form a Covenant relationship</>and enter duo mode will receive extra resurrection counts and extra Marionette Essence (used for purchasing important items within the dungeon).",
    ["<Assistant_Title1>【Vampire's Love】</>\n<Assistant_Title2>Quest Type: </><Assistant_Property2>Life in the Era</>\n<Assistant_Title2>Quest Description: </>Miss Magician asks you to deliver a newly released novel to Mr. Moon.\n<Assistant_Title2>How to Accept: </>After your Acting level reaches <Assistant_Red>Level 61</>, head to {Location:[廷根(1239,1062)]|24189;6189;-2205;2;5200002;0} to trigger the quest.\n<Assistant_Title2>Quest Rewards: </> Cognitive Experience, Bound Sol, invoices, Adventure Medals, World Adventure Treasure progress"] = "<Assistant_Title1>【Vampire's Love】</>\n<Assistant_Title2>Quest Type: </><Assistant_Property2>Life in the Era</>\n<Assistant_Title2>Quest Description: </>Miss Magician asks you to deliver a newly released novel to Mr. Moon.\n<Assistant_Title2>How to Accept: </>After your Acting level reaches <Assistant_Red>Level 61</>, head to {Location:[Tingen(1239,1062)]|24189;6189;-2205;2;5200002;0} to trigger the quest.\n<Assistant_Title2>Quest Rewards: </> Cognitive Experience, Bound Sol, invoices, Adventure Medals, World Adventure Treasure progress",
    ["<Assistant_Title1>【Voice Room - Host Permissions】</>\n<Assistant_Title2>System Access: </><Assistant_System>Voice Room - Permission Settings (Bottom Left)</>{JumpToUI:[【前往查看】]|1250316}\n<Assistant_Title2>Free Speech Mode: </>All players can unmute and speak.\n<Assistant_Title2>Host-Set Speech Permissions: </>In this mode, players can click the unmute button to request to speak; once the host approves, they gain speaking rights. The host can also manually adjust speaking permissions in the player list.\n<Assistant_Title2>Host-Set Speech Order: </>In this mode, up to 8 microphone slots can be set. It defaults to sequential speaking; only the host and the player on Mic 1 can unmute. Once the player on Mic 1 finishes, they must manually click to step down from the mic to pass the turn to the player on Mic 2.\n<Assistant_Title2>Mute: </>Muted players cannot use real-time voice, send voice messages, or send text messages in this voice room. The host can manage this in the Mute Management tab.\n<Assistant_Title2>Blacklist: </>Blacklisted players will be kicked from the voice room and cannot re-enter. The host can manage this in the Blacklist tab.\n<Assistant_Title3>Recommended Searches: </>{SendAnswer:[语音房-普通语音房]|1396}, {SendAnswer:[语音房-玩法语音房]|1397}, {SendAnswer:[语音房-常驻房间]|1398}"] = "<Assistant_Title1>【Voice Room - Host Permissions】</>\n<Assistant_Title2>System Access: </><Assistant_System>Voice Room - Permission Settings (Bottom Left)</>{JumpToUI:[【Go to View】]|1250316}\n<Assistant_Title2>Free Speech Mode: </>All players can unmute and speak.\n<Assistant_Title2>Host-Set Speech Permissions: </>In this mode, players can click the unmute button to request to speak; once the host approves, they gain speaking rights. The host can also manually adjust speaking permissions in the player list.\n<Assistant_Title2>Host-Set Speech Order: </>In this mode, up to 8 microphone slots can be set. It defaults to sequential speaking; only the host and the player on Mic 1 can unmute. Once the player on Mic 1 finishes, they must manually click to step down from the mic to pass the turn to the player on Mic 2.\n<Assistant_Title2>Mute: </>Muted players cannot use real-time voice, send voice messages, or send text messages in this voice room. The host can manage this in the Mute Management tab.\n<Assistant_Title2>Blacklist: </>Blacklisted players will be kicked from the voice room and cannot re-enter. The host can manage this in the Blacklist tab.\n<Assistant_Title3>Recommended Searches: </>{SendAnswer:[Voice Room-Standard Voice Room]|1396}, {SendAnswer:[Voice Room-Play Voice Room]|1397}, {SendAnswer:[Voice Room-Permanent Room]|1398}",
    ["<Assistant_Title1>【Voice Room - Permanent Room】</>\n<Assistant_Title2>System Access: </><Assistant_System>Play Voice Room - Settings (Bottom Right) - Permanent Button (Top Right)</>{JumpToUI:[【前往查看】]|1250316}\n<Assistant_Title2>Permanent Item: </>You can purchase a Permanent Contract in the <Assistant_System>Mall - Secret Collection</>. Using it converts a Play Voice Room into a permanent room and adds 30 days of permanent duration. A single item can extend the duration by 30 days, with a maximum cumulative extension of 90 days.\n<Assistant_Title2>Function Introduction: </>After converting to a permanent room, the voice room will be retained even after you <Assistant_Red>exit the permanent voice room or go offline</>, and the host will retain their host status.<Assistant_Red>Permanent voice rooms cannot have their host status transferred.</>\n<Assistant_Title2>Quantity Limit: </>Each character can own a maximum of <Assistant_Red>1 permanent voice room</>.\n<Assistant_Title2>Disbanding the Room: </>A permanent voice room can be disbanded by the host; once disbanded, it <Assistant_Red>cannot be recovered</>;\n<Assistant_Title3>Recommended Searches: </>{SendAnswer:[语音房-房主权限]|1395}, {SendAnswer:[语音房-普通语音房]|1396}, {SendAnswer:[语音房-玩法语音房]|1397}"] = "<Assistant_Title1>【Voice Room - Permanent Room】</>\n<Assistant_Title2>System Access: </><Assistant_System>Play Voice Room - Settings (Bottom Right) - Permanent Button (Top Right)</>{JumpToUI:[【Go to View】]|1250316}\n<Assistant_Title2>Permanent Item: </>You can purchase a Permanent Contract in the <Assistant_System>Mall - Secret Collection</>. Using it converts a Play Voice Room into a permanent room and adds 30 days of permanent duration. A single item can extend the duration by 30 days, with a maximum cumulative extension of 90 days.\n<Assistant_Title2>Function Introduction: </>After converting to a permanent room, the voice room will be retained even after you <Assistant_Red>exit the permanent voice room or go offline</>, and the host will retain their host status.<Assistant_Red>Permanent voice rooms cannot have their host status transferred.</>\n<Assistant_Title2>Quantity Limit: </>Each character can own a maximum of <Assistant_Red>1 permanent voice room</>.\n<Assistant_Title2>Disbanding the Room: </>A permanent voice room can be disbanded by the host; once disbanded, it <Assistant_Red>cannot be recovered</>;\n<Assistant_Title3>Recommended Searches: </>{SendAnswer:[Voice Room-Host Permissions]|1395}, {SendAnswer:[Voice Room-Standard Voice Room]|1396}, {SendAnswer:[Voice Room-Play Voice Room]|1397}",
    ["<Assistant_Title1>【Voice Room - Play Voice Room】</>\n<Assistant_Title2>Required Level: </>Cognition Level <Assistant_Red>Level 10</>\n<Assistant_Title2>System Access: </><Assistant_System>Chat Panel - Voice Room</>{JumpToUI:[【前往查看】]|1250316}\n<Assistant_Title2>Capacity Limit: </>Voice rooms can hold up to 1000 people.\n<Assistant_Title2>Default Speech Mode: </>Play voice rooms default to Host-Set Speech Order mode; you must click the unmute button to request to speak, and the host must approve it.\n<Assistant_Title2>Heartbeat Signal: </>Players on the mic sequence automatically gain guest status; the player on Mic 1 is the Guest of Honor. All guests in the voice room can express emotions by switching their 'Light Up' status. You can view the current speaking and 'Light Up' status of all guests more intuitively via the live interface in the top right corner of the room.\n<Assistant_Title2>Host Operations: </>The host can adjust the speech order in member permission settings, set mutes and room blacklists, and adjust room information, extend the duration of a permanent room, or transfer host status in the right sidebar settings.\n<Assistant_Title2>Other Operations: </>You can share the voice room link or distribute voice room gifts via the right sidebar.\n<Assistant_Title3>Recommended Searches: </>{SendAnswer:[语音房-房主权限]|1395}, {SendAnswer:[语音房-普通语音房]|1396}, {SendAnswer:[语音房-常驻房间]|1398}"] = "<Assistant_Title1>【Voice Room - Play Voice Room】</>\n<Assistant_Title2>Required Level: </>Cognition Level <Assistant_Red>Level 10</>\n<Assistant_Title2>System Access: </><Assistant_System>Chat Panel - Voice Room</>{JumpToUI:[【Go to View】]|1250316}\n<Assistant_Title2>Capacity Limit: </>Voice rooms can hold up to 1000 people.\n<Assistant_Title2>Default Speech Mode: </>Play voice rooms default to Host-Set Speech Order mode; you must click the unmute button to request to speak, and the host must approve it.\n<Assistant_Title2>Heartbeat Signal: </>Players on the mic sequence automatically gain guest status; the player on Mic 1 is the Guest of Honor. All guests in the voice room can express emotions by switching their 'Light Up' status. You can view the current speaking and 'Light Up' status of all guests more intuitively via the live interface in the top right corner of the room.\n<Assistant_Title2>Host Operations: </>The host can adjust the speech order in member permission settings, set mutes and room blacklists, and adjust room information, extend the duration of a permanent room, or transfer host status in the right sidebar settings.\n<Assistant_Title2>Other Operations: </>You can share the voice room link or distribute voice room gifts via the right sidebar.\n<Assistant_Title3>Recommended Searches: </>{SendAnswer:[Voice Room-Host Permissions]|1395}, {SendAnswer:[Voice Room-Standard Voice Room]|1396}, {SendAnswer:[Voice Room-Permanent Room]|1398}",
    ["<Assistant_Title1>【Voice Room - Standard Voice Room】</>\n<Assistant_Title2>Required Level: </>Cognition Level <Assistant_Red>Level 10</>\n<Assistant_Title2>System Access: </><Assistant_System>Chat Panel - Voice Room</>{JumpToUI:[【前往查看】]|1250316}\n<Assistant_Title2>Capacity Limit: </>Voice rooms can hold up to 1000 people.\n<Assistant_Title2>Default Speech Mode: </>Standard voice rooms default to Free Speech Mode; click the unmute button next to the input box to unmute automatically. If the current room is set to Host-Set Speech Permissions or Host-Set Speech Order, you must click the unmute button to request to speak, and the host must approve it.\n<Assistant_Title2>Host Operations: </>The host can adjust the speech mode in member permission settings, set mutes and room blacklists, and adjust room information and type or transfer host status in the right sidebar settings.\n<Assistant_Title2>Other Operations: </>You can share the voice room link or distribute voice room gifts via the right sidebar.\n<Assistant_Title3>Recommended Searches: </>{SendAnswer:[语音房-房主权限]|1395}, {SendAnswer:[语音房-玩法语音房]|1397}, {SendAnswer:[语音房-常驻房间]|1398}"] = "<Assistant_Title1>【Voice Room - Standard Voice Room】</>\n<Assistant_Title2>Required Level: </>Cognition Level <Assistant_Red>Level 10</>\n<Assistant_Title2>System Access: </><Assistant_System>Chat Panel - Voice Room</>{JumpToUI:[【Go to View】]|1250316}\n<Assistant_Title2>Capacity Limit: </>Voice rooms can hold up to 1000 people.\n<Assistant_Title2>Default Speech Mode: </>Standard voice rooms default to Free Speech Mode; click the unmute button next to the input box to unmute automatically. If the current room is set to Host-Set Speech Permissions or Host-Set Speech Order, you must click the unmute button to request to speak, and the host must approve it.\n<Assistant_Title2>Host Operations: </>The host can adjust the speech mode in member permission settings, set mutes and room blacklists, and adjust room information and type or transfer host status in the right sidebar settings.\n<Assistant_Title2>Other Operations: </>You can share the voice room link or distribute voice room gifts via the right sidebar.\n<Assistant_Title3>Recommended Searches: </>{SendAnswer:[Voice Room-Host Permissions]|1395}, {SendAnswer:[Voice Room-Play Voice Room]|1397}, {SendAnswer:[Voice Room-Permanent Room]|1398}",
    ["<Assistant_Title1>【Wailing Black Market】</>\n<Assistant_Title2> Gameplay Type: </><Assistant_Property1>Blackthorn Incident Log</>\n<Assistant_Title2> How to Participate: </> After reaching <Assistant_Property1>Level 40</>, Beyonders can click <Assistant_System>Menu - World Adventure - Dungeon - Blackthorn Incident Log - Wailing Black Market</> to participate.\n<Assistant_Title2> Number of Participants: </> Team up with 5-6 people, or choose AI mode to go.\n<Assistant_Title2> Gameplay Rewards: </> Level 45 Golden Equipment, Beyonder Materials, etc. 1 reward attempt per day <Assistant_Red>(shared reward attempts with Blackthorn Incident Log)</>.\n<Assistant_Title2> Boss Strategy: </>{JumpToUI:[朗伯·绞索]|1302136}"] = "<Assistant_Title1>【Wailing Black Market】</>\n<Assistant_Title2> Gameplay Type: </><Assistant_Property1>Blackthorn Incident Log</>\n<Assistant_Title2> How to Participate: </> After reaching <Assistant_Property1>Level 40</>, Beyonders can click <Assistant_System>Menu - World Adventure - Dungeon - Blackthorn Incident Log - Wailing Black Market</> to participate.\n<Assistant_Title2> Number of Participants: </> Team up with 5-6 people, or choose AI mode to go.\n<Assistant_Title2> Gameplay Rewards: </> Level 45 Golden Equipment, Beyonder Materials, etc. 1 reward attempt per day <Assistant_Red>(shared reward attempts with Blackthorn Incident Log)</>.\n<Assistant_Title2> Boss Strategy: </>{JumpToUI:[Lambert Noose]|1302136}",
