    ["——{{PlayerName}}——请请请请注意您的身份，您无权干预演出的正常进行。"] = "—{{PlayerName}}—Please, please, please, please mind your status; you have no right to interfere with the normal progress of the performance.",
    ["——上午——\n8：00-10：30   工作\n10：30-10：40  休息\n10：40-11：00 广播体操\n11：00-12：00  吃饭\n——午休——\n12：00-13：00\n——下午——\n13：00-15：30  工作\n15：30-15：40  休息\n15：40-16：00 跑操\n16：00-18：00  工作\n18：00后  晚餐（可外带）"] = "——Morning—— \n 8:00-10:30 Work \n 10:30-10:40 Rest \n 10:40-11:00 Radio Calisthenics \n 11:00-12:00 Meal \n ——Lunch Break—— \n 12:00-13:00 \n ——Afternoon—— \n 13:00-15:30 Work \n 15:30-15:40 Rest \n 15:40-16:00 Running Exercise \n 16:00-18:00 Work \n After 18:00 Dinner (Takeout allowed)",
    ["——哎呀！怎么有只青蛙？！唔，看起来倒没摔坏……"] = "—Oh my! Why is there a frog?! Hmm, it doesn't look broken...",
    ["——在那个世界里，梅高欧丝一战无人牺牲。圣堂随后给予守护了全廷根的值夜者小队任职贝克兰德的机会，但邓恩和弗莱都拒绝了。\n\n      戴莉从贝克兰德赶回来时已是深夜，她照例拎了一瓶邓恩和弗莱都爱喝的酒。\n      “所以，你真拒绝了圣堂的邀请？”她靠在桌边，目光落在邓恩脸上。\n      邓恩抬起头，看向她。火光在他灰色的眼睛里轻轻晃了晃。\n      “你比我更适合那里。”他说，声音平静而厚重，“在廷根，这里的人认得我，我也认得每一条街、每一扇窗。我想留在这里，继续守护着它。”\n      弗莱默默给自己倒了一杯，举起来：“我也是。”\n      戴莉沉默片刻，轻声笑了一下：“就知道你会这么说。”\n      她拎过酒瓶也满上。三只杯子在壁炉前碰到一起，清脆的一声响。\n      窗外的廷根，在不眠的守护者注视中，安安静静地睡着。"] = "—In that world, no one sacrificed their life in the battle against Megose. The Cathedral subsequently gave the Nighthawks squad that guarded all of Tingen the opportunity to take up posts in Backlund, but Dunn and Frye both refused. \n\n      Daly returned from Backlund late at night; she brought a bottle of the wine that both Dunn and Frye loved, as was her custom. \n      \"So, you really refused the Cathedral's invitation?\" She leaned against the table, her gaze resting on Dunn's face. \n      Dunn looked up at her. The firelight flickered gently in his gray eyes. \n      \"You are more suited for that place than I am,\" he said, his voice calm and heavy. \"In Tingen, the people here know me, and I know every street, every window. I want to stay here and continue guarding it.\" \n      Frye silently poured himself a glass and raised it: \"Me too.\" \n      Daly was silent for a moment, then laughed softly: \"I knew you would say that.\" \n      She grabbed the bottle and filled her own glass. Three glasses clinked together in front of the fireplace with a crisp sound. \n      Outside the window, Tingen slept quietly under the watchful eyes of the sleepless Guardians.",
    ["——在那个平行世界里，奥黛丽和苏茜合作解决了佛尔思同伴的案件。\n\n      贝克兰德，霍尔家的花园。奥黛丽坐在吊椅上，阳光透过藤蔓洒下斑驳的光影。\n      几天前，佛尔思·沃尔来访时的神情又浮现在她眼前。那位气质慵懒的作家露出郑重的神色：“我有位同伴被关入了监狱，正等待着最后的审判，我希望你们能够救她出来，无论用什么办法。”\n      而同行的格莱林特子爵派人咨询了熟悉的大律师，对方说有把握只是轻判，但无罪辩护的难度很高，除非当事人能拿到精神有问题或者心智发育不健全的医疗证明……\n      奥黛丽记得自己当时答应了佛尔思会认真考虑。作家小姐离开时还回头看了一眼，淡蓝色的眼睛里藏着期待。\n      “医疗证明……”奥黛丽轻声自语，眉头微蹙。她不是没想过用霍尔家的影响力去疏通，但那会暴露她和佛尔思、休之间的关系。况且，那位黑帮头目虽然出具了原谅声明，严重伤害的案件却依然可能被起诉。\n      身旁趴着的苏茜竖起耳朵，用只有奥黛丽能听见的声音小声说：“那个黑帮头目，还在医院里？”\n      奥黛丽低头看她，目光微动。\n      “我去试一试。”苏茜摇了摇尾巴提议道。\n      当天夜里，苏茜悄悄潜入病房。她用“观众”的能力温和地引导那位“体面的绅士”回忆——对方终于记起，是自己先动了手，休只是自卫。醒来后，他主动向检察官更正了证词。\n      几天后，休被无罪释放。佛尔思来霍尔家道谢时，感慨“检察官突然发现了新证据，运气真好”。\n      奥黛丽微笑着点头：“是啊，运气真好。”\n      苏茜趴在她脚边，尾巴拍打着地毯，心满意足。"] = "—In that parallel world, Audrey and Susie worked together to solve the case involving Fors's companion. \n\n      Backlund, the Hall family garden. Audrey sat on a hanging chair, sunlight casting dappled light and shadows through the vines. \n      A few days ago, the expression on Fors Wall's face when she visited appeared in her mind again. That lazy-tempered writer had shown a solemn look: \"I have a companion who has been thrown into prison and is waiting for the final verdict. I hope you can save her, no matter what method you use.\" \n      And the accompanying Viscount Glaint had sent someone to consult a well-known lawyer, who said there was a chance for a light sentence, but an acquittal was very difficult unless the defendant could obtain a medical certificate stating they had mental issues or were mentally underdeveloped... \n      Audrey remembered that she had promised Fors she would consider it carefully. When the writer left, she had looked back, anticipation hidden in her light blue eyes. \n      \"Medical certificate...\" Audrey whispered to herself, her brows slightly furrowed. It wasn't that she hadn't thought about using the Hall family's influence to pull strings, but that would expose her relationship with Fors and Xio. Moreover, although the gang leader had issued a statement of forgiveness, the case of grievous injury could still be prosecuted. \n      Susie, lying beside her, pricked up her ears and whispered in a voice only Audrey could hear: \"That gang leader, is he still in the hospital?\" \n      Audrey looked down at her, her gaze flickering. \n      \"I'll go give it a try,\" Susie suggested, wagging her tail. \n      That night, Susie quietly snuck into the hospital room. She used her Spectator ability to gently guide the \"decent gentleman\" to recall—the other party finally remembered that he had struck first and that Xio was only acting in self-defense. After waking up, he took the initiative to correct his testimony to the prosecutor. \n      A few days later, Xio was acquitted. When Fors came to the Hall residence to thank her, she sighed, \"The prosecutor suddenly found new evidence; what good luck.\" \n      Audrey smiled and nodded: \"Yes, what good luck.\" \n      Susie lay at her feet, her tail thumping against the carpet, feeling satisfied.",
    ["——对了，她不久前才上过药！可以顺着草药的气味找！"] = "—Right, she applied medicine not long ago! I can track her by the scent of the herbs!",
    ["——我明白，你要看住我，我绝不买！"] = "—I understand, you have to keep an eye on me, I will definitely not buy it!",
    ["——我知道了！她那么想见丈夫，肯定会去丈夫所在的地方……那就是拉斐尔墓园！"] = "—I've got it! She wants to see her husband so badly, she must have gone to where he is... that would be Raphael Cemetery!",
    ["——摘录于宫廷诗会集，1859页。\n经典的罗塞尔式韵律，形象地表达了知识的沉重，让在场的所有人沉默。"] = "—Excerpted from the Court Poetry Collection, page 1859.\nThe classic Roselle-style rhythm vividly expresses the weight of knowledge, leaving everyone present in silence.",
    ["——本店主打—"] = "—Our shop's specialties—",
    ["——祝福你们，愿你们的爱情如花朵般纯净无暇。女神一定会赐福你们的结合。"] = "—Blessings to you both, may your love be as pure and flawless as a flower. The Goddess will surely bless your union.",
    ["——终于！五年了！有人能听见我了！"] = "—Finally! Five years! Someone can hear me!",
    ["——贝克兰德脚踏车股份有限公司"] = "—Backlund Bicycle Co., Ltd.",
    ["“%d”级封印物最多生效%d词条效果"] = "'%d' Grade Sealed Artifact can have at most %d entry effects active",
    ["“%s”不足，无法聚合"] = "Insufficient \"%s\", cannot aggregate",
    ["“0”级封印物……需要注意什么？"] = "Grade 0 Sealed Artifact... what do I need to pay attention to?",
    ["“0”级封印物？"] = "Grade 0 Sealed Artifact?",
    ["“0”级封印物？！那伦纳德先生昨夜离开……"] = "Grade 0 Sealed Artifact?! Then Mr. Leonard left last night...",
    ["“0”级表示非常危险，不可打听，不可外传，不可描述，不可窥探……"] = "Grade 0 means it is extremely dangerous, must not be inquired about, must not be spread, must not be described, must not be peeked at...",
    ["“0”级表示非常危险，最高重视度和保密等级，不可打听、不可外传、不可描述、不可窥探，只能封印于总部圣堂的地底。"] = "\"Grade 0\" means extremely dangerous, highest priority and security level. Do not inquire, do not spread, do not describe, do not spy. It can only be sealed in the underground of the headquarters cathedral.",
    ["“0级” 非常危险"] = "'Grade 0' Very dangerous",
    ["“1173年，他推翻国王的统治，成为因蒂斯共和国的首任执政官。”\n“1192年，他将因蒂斯共和国改为帝国，登上王座，自称凯撒大帝。”"] = "\"In 1173, he overthrew the king's rule and became the first consul of the Intis Republic.\"\n\"In 1192, he changed the Intis Republic into an empire, ascended the throne, and proclaimed himself Emperor Caesar.\"",
    ["“1184年1月1日，盛大的新年晚会，弗洛纳尔夫人真是一个尤物啊。”"] = "\"January 1st, 1184. A grand New Year's party. Mrs. Flonal is truly a stunner.\"",
    ["“11月18日。真是件神奇的事情，一个异想天开的实验，我发现了一位困于风暴之中、迷失于黑暗深处的可怜家伙。”"] = "\"November 18th. What a magical thing. Through a whimsical experiment, I discovered a poor fellow trapped in a storm and lost in the depths of darkness.\"",
    ["“1”级是高度危险，可有限利用，保密等级是教区主教和值夜者执事及以上。"] = "\"Grade 1\" is highly dangerous, can be used with limitations. Security level is for diocesan bishops and Nighthawk deacons and above.",
    ["“1级” 高度危险"] = "'Grade 1' Highly dangerous",
    ["“2”级危险物……危险、谨慎且节制使用，所以做这个动作是因为封印物的特殊性？"] = "\"Grade 2\" dangerous object... Dangerous, use with caution and restraint. So, is this action performed because of the special nature of the Sealed Artifact?",
    ["“2”级封印物提升到“1”级封印物的必要素材。"] = "Necessary material to upgrade a Grade 2 Sealed Artifact to a Grade 1 Sealed Artifact.",
    ["“2”级封印物，危险，须谨慎且节制地利用……"] = "\"Grade 2\" Sealed Artifact, dangerous, must be used with caution and restraint...",
    ["“2”级是危险，谨慎且节制使用，保密等级是主教和值夜者小队队长及以上。"] = "\"Grade 2\" is dangerous, use with caution and restraint. Security level is for bishops and Nighthawk team captains and above.",
    ["“2级” 危险"] = "'Grade 2' Dangerous",
    ["“3”级封印物提升到“2”级封印物的必要素材。"] = "Necessary material to upgrade a Grade 3 Sealed Artifact to a Grade 2 Sealed Artifact.",
    ["“3”级是有一定危险，需小心使用，必须三人以上行动才能申请，保密等级是值夜者正式成员。"] = "\"Grade 3\" is somewhat dangerous, must be used carefully. Must have at least three people to apply. Security level is for official Nighthawks.",
    ["“3级” 有一定危险"] = "'Grade 3' Somewhat dangerous",
    ["“<P_Yellow>永暗的蜡烛</>”，请见证我的死亡，请收留我的灵魂。"] = "“<P_Yellow>Candle of Eternal Darkness</>”, please witness my death, please take in my soul.",
    ["“<P_Yellow>风暴比烈酒更烈</>。”"] = "<P_Yellow>The storm is fiercer than strong liquor.</>",
    ["“……<P_Yellow>‘它’</>绝不可能被卖掉……也不会遗失……”"] = "“……<P_Yellow>‘It’</> can never be sold…… nor will it be lost……”",
    ["“……<P_Yellow>它</>……所有的心血……都是为了……”"] = "“……<P_Yellow>It</>…… all the heart's blood…… is for……”",
    ["“……呜呜……妈妈……不要留下我……”"] = "“……Wuu wuu…… Mom…… don't leave me behind……”",
    ["“……带我离开这里……”"] = "“……Take me away from here……”",
    ["“……所有神奇物品加起来，都比不上<P_Yellow>‘它’</>的壮丽……”"] = "“……All mystical items combined are not as magnificent as <P_Yellow>‘it’</>……”",
    ["“……知识的化身——伟大的隐匿贤者……”"] = "\"...Avatar of Knowledge—the great Hidden Sage...\"",
    ["“《西维拉斯郡私人史料研读》，作者：阿兹克·艾格斯”……好厉害！"] = "“A Study of Private Historical Materials of Sivellas County, Author: Azik Eggers”…… Amazing!",
    ["“一个变数，诞生了。”"] = "'A variable has been born.'",
    ["“一个来自神秘的大海，一个沉眠黑暗的棺木。如阳光般温暖的公主殿下，是否能融化他冰封多年的心？”"] = "'One from the mysterious sea, one a coffin sleeping in darkness. Can the princess, as warm as the sun, melt his heart that has been frozen for years?'",
    ["“一物藏匿，羔羊归家之音……”，小羊玩偶？"] = "\"One thing hidden, the sound of the lamb returning home...\", a lamb doll?",
    ["“一阵悠扬的琴声响起……”"] = "\"A melodious sound of a zither rings out...\"",
    ["“万都之都”号\n即将启程！"] = "The \"City of Cities\" \n is about to set sail!",
    ["“万都之都”号的每一个角落都经过精心设计。"] = "Every corner of the 'Capital of Capitals' has been meticulously designed.",
    ["“万都之都”号船票开售，所有人注意有序排队，不要拥挤！"] = "\"City of Cities\" tickets are on sale, everyone please queue in an orderly fashion, do not crowd!",
    ["“不宜进食”，他就一口饭不吃！“不宜近水”，他连脸都不洗！"] = "“Not suitable for eating,” and he won't eat a single bite! “Not suitable for being near water,” and he won't even wash his face!",
    ["“不属于这个时代的愚者”"] = "The Fool that doesn't belong to this era",
    ["“不属于这个时代的愚者”……感觉不错，足够安全。"] = "\"The Fool that doesn't belong to this era\"... Feels good, safe enough.",
    ["“不属于这个时代的愚者”……还不够精确，需要补一句。"] = "\"The Fool that doesn't belong to this era\"... Not precise enough, need to add a sentence.",
    ["“不灭之心”、“圣者之石”和“永生之水”之类的，各种各样的名字"] = "\"Heart of Immortality,\" \"Saint's Stone,\" and \"Water of Eternal Life,\" and various other names.",
    ["“不眠者”是这样的……"] = "\"Nighthawks\" are like this...",
    ["“不眠者”途径的非凡者需要通过吟唱诗篇来影响周围生灵。"] = "Beyonders of the \"Sleepless\" pathway need to influence surrounding living beings by chanting poems.",
    ["“世界”先生醒了？"] = "Mr. World is awake?",
    ["“世界”先生，你给予的那件非凡武器超乎我预料得好，我已经攒够功勋，兑换到材料，晋升序列8了。"] = "\"The World\", the Beyonder weapon you provided was better than I expected. I have saved enough merit to exchange for materials and advance to Sequence 8.",
    ["“东侧”"] = "East Side",
    ["“丝绒夫人”"] = "\"Lady Velvet\"",
    ["“丝绒女王”"] = "\"Queen Velvet\"",
    ["“丢掉她！”"] = "“Throw her away!”",
    ["“两把大剑双双镇守在此庭，混乱与秩序的世界逐渐交融合一，趋于稳定。”"] = "\"Two greatswords stand guard in this courtyard, the worlds of chaos and order gradually merging into one, tending toward stability.\"",
    ["“丹德莉丝（的衣服）安眠于此。\n你是女神赐予我的礼物。”"] = "“Dendris (her clothes) rests here in Slumber. \n You are the gift the Goddess bestowed upon me.”",
    ["“为‘命运’劳作”，双关很有意思不是吗？自从成为这家咖啡馆的侍者我就在准备这个笑话了。"] = "\"Working for 'fate'\"—the pun is quite interesting, isn't it? I've been preparing this joke ever since I became a waiter at this cafe.",
    ["“为什么没有关系？奥莉薇可是我和泰利最爱的女儿啊！”戴娜再次举枪。"] = "\"Why wouldn't it matter? Olivia is the daughter that Terry and I love the most!\" Dena raised her gun again.",
    ["“为我们的友谊，干杯！”"] = "\"To our friendship, cheers!\"",
    ["“主人”？“陛下”？不，还是算了，总觉得既羞耻又心虚……"] = "\"Master\"? \"Your Majesty\"? No, forget it. I always feel both ashamed and guilty...",
    ["“主宰者”伯德温·威瑟尔"] = "Baldwin Wetherell, the \"Dominator\"",
    ["“丽莎晚年在梦境和现实中徘徊，\n感谢女神，她终于结束了那场噩梦。”"] = "“In her later years, Lisa wandered between dreams and reality, \n thank the Goddess, she finally ended that Nightmare.”",
    ["“书籍是人类进步的阶梯”……我考考你，这句话是谁说的？"] = "\"Books are the ladder of human progress\"... Let me test you, who said this?",
    ["“于是以扳手为笔，油污为墨”"] = "\"So using a wrench as a pen, and oil stains as ink\"",
    ["“于此处长眠的是荒原诗人莉莲，\n喜欢探索自然的她回到了自然的怀抱。”"] = "“Lying here is the wilderness poet Lillian, \n who loved exploring nature and has returned to the embrace of nature.”",
    ["“五月二十六日，我很享受‘通识者’身份。奇怪的是，当我以‘通识者’自居、做的事都与它相符时，让我发疯的耳语安静了不少。这就是查拉图先生提过的<P_Yellow>‘扮演’</>？这或许是解决魔药隐患的关键。​”"] = "\"May 26th, I quite enjoy the status of a 'Savant'. Strangely, when I identify as a 'Savant' and do things consistent with it, the whispers that drive me mad have quieted down quite a bit. Is this the <P_Yellow>'Acting'</> that Mr. Zarathul mentioned? This might be the key to solving the hidden dangers of potions.\"",
    ["“亲爱的女儿，爸爸的抽屉里有一块怀表，是给你留的。”"] = "\"Dear daughter, there is a pocket watch in Daddy's drawer, it's left for you.\"",
    ["“亲爱的妈妈，我已到达贝克兰德，在帕特叔叔的帮助下获得了工作，父亲的项链鼓励着我，庇护着我，我获得了不少小费。我想，祖父所需要的医药费，我们很快就能攒齐。”\n“亲爱的妈妈，我认识了一个医师朋友，又见证了一些……特别的事情。我找到了更好的工作。另外，钱款已汇回家。包裹里有给祖父的药品，还有给您和妹妹买的新裙子。妹妹还有额外的礼物，请告诉她，那是考上大学的祝贺。康斯顿是个好地方，等到假期，我们可以在那里重聚。”\n“亲爱的妈妈，战争开始了！我想，首都应该会是最安全的地方，我已经寄钱，无论如何都要买到来这里的车票；如果不行，尽快发电报告诉我，我立刻动身，我们在康斯顿见！”"] = "\"Dear Mom, I have arrived in Backlund and obtained a job with the help of Uncle Pat. Father's necklace encourages me and shelters me; I have earned quite a bit in tips. I think we will soon be able to save up for Grandfather's medical expenses.\" \n\"Dear Mom, I have met a doctor friend and witnessed some... special things. I have found a better job. Also, the money has been sent home. In the package, there is medicine for Grandfather, as well as new dresses for you and my sister. There is an extra gift for my sister; please tell her it is a congratulation for getting into university. Conston is a good place; when the holidays come, we can reunite there.\" \n\"Dear Mom, the war has started! I think the capital should be the safest place. I have already sent money; no matter what, you must buy a train ticket here. If that's not possible, send me a telegram as soon as possible, and I will set off immediately. We will meet in Conston!\"",
    ["“人更是”是什么意思？ "] = "What does \"people are even more so\" mean?",
    ["“仁慈的母亲啊，他们根本没有真正理解您的意志！”"] = "\"Merciful Mother, they have not truly understood your will at all!\"",
    ["“今天和温斯特采购蔬菜，试吃结束后回归！”"] = "'Purchasing vegetables with Winster today, returning after the tasting!'",
    ["“今天陪金采购蔬菜，试吃结束后回归！”"] = "'Purchasing vegetables with Jin today, returning after the tasting!'",
    ["“从廷根火车站乘坐火车，很快就能抵达……”嗯，就是这里了。"] = "“Take a train from Tingen Train Station, and you will arrive soon……” Hmm, this is the place.",
    ["“从爱上世界的那天，就开始踏上了旅途……”"] = "\"From the day it fell in love with the world, it began its journey...\"",
    ["“他”——还是“她”？"] = "\"He\"—or \"She\"?",
    ["“他”的帮助？"] = "\"His\" help?",
    ["“他”？"] = "\"He\"?",
    ["“他们”指的是？"] = "Who do you mean by \"they\"?",
    ["“他们称我为管道诗人”"] = "\"They call me the pipe poet\"",
    ["“以心为誓，守护吾爱”，看来是杰温先生送给芙拉女士的。她让这件信物陪自己入睡吗……"] = "\"Sworn by the heart, to protect my love.\" It seems this was a gift from Mr. Jevon to Ms. Fula. Does she let this keepsake accompany her to sleep...",
    ["“仰望绯月派”？听起来还挺浪漫的。"] = "\"Looking Up at the Crimson Moon School\"? Sounds quite romantic.",
    ["“优雅”风尚度鉴定"] = "'Elegance' Fashion Rating",
    ["“优雅大公”"] = "\"Elegant Duke\"",
    ["“优雅夫人”"] = "\"Elegant Lady\"",
    ["“伟大母亲”眷顾你了 “伟大母亲”眷顾你了！"] = "The \"Great Mother\" has blessed you. The \"Great Mother\" has blessed you!",
    ["“伟大母亲”，现已确认为▇▇▇▇的化身，繁衍与生育的象征，掌握生命孕育与血肉繁衍，占据▇▇▇▇权柄。信仰祂的组织包括▇▇母亲、玫瑰学派、原始月亮。\n向祂祈求会获得旺盛的繁衍能力，但会逐渐丧失理智，性情狂热，探求生命与灵性本质的禁忌，陷入对生育与繁衍的欲望……\n献祭的密契仪式需要大量的血肉与生命，过程伴随着极致的疯狂和混乱……\n廷根危机中，月亮仆从以献祭整座城市为代价，制造邪神子嗣降临的容器，带来毁灭性的灾难……"] = "\"Great Mother\", now confirmed to be an avatar of ▇▇▇▇, the symbol of reproduction and fertility, mastering the conception of life and the proliferation of flesh and blood, occupying the ▇▇▇▇ authority. Organizations that believe in Her include the ▇▇ Mother, the Rose School of Thought, and the Primordial Moon.\nPraying to Her will grant vigorous reproductive ability, but one will gradually lose their sanity, become fanatical, seek the taboos of life and the essence of spirituality, and fall into the desire for birth and reproduction...\nThe secret ritual of sacrifice requires a large amount of flesh, blood, and life, and the process is accompanied by extreme madness and chaos...\nDuring the Tingen crisis, the Moon Servant sacrificed the entire city as the price to create a vessel for the descent of the evil god's offspring, bringing about a devastating catastrophe...",
    ["“但待到白昼睁开了眼睛”"] = "\"But when the daylight opened its eyes\"",
    ["“佛尔思亲笔签名典藏版小说”……这些是采买清单里该出现的东西吗？"] = "\"Fors's autographed collector's edition novel\"… Are these things that should appear on a shopping list?",
    ["“你以为奥莉薇是泰利的妻子吗？”面对挣扎着的亚伦，戴娜嘲讽着。"] = "\"Do you think Olivia is Terry's wife?\" Dena sneered at the struggling Aaron.",
    ["“你好，克莱恩。”"] = "\"Hello, Klein.\"",
    ["“你小时候说想要会响的钟，爸爸没舍得买。现在后悔了。”"] = "\"When you were little, you said you wanted a clock that chimes, but I couldn't bear to buy it. I regret it now.\"",
    ["“你想要金子、宝石，亦或者土地？”"] = "\"Do you want gold, gems, or land?\"",
    ["“你是个没有家的怪物！”"] = "“You're a monster without a home!”",
    ["“你最近有做桃色之梦吗？你桃色之梦的主角都有谁？”"] = "\"Have you had any erotic dreams lately? Who are the protagonists of your erotic dreams?\"",
    ["“你永远是廷根市值夜者小队的一员”……这是你说的，我也更喜欢这个身份。"] = "\"You will always be a member of the Tingen Nighthawks\"... This is what you said, and I also prefer this identity.",
    ["“你这个没用的废物，跟你病死的妈一样废物！”"] = "“You useless piece of trash, just as useless as your mother who died of sickness!”",
    ["“你醒啦？”\n不远处的小女孩向你问候。你这才发现，自己正在一个野营地里。"] = "\"Are you awake?\" \n A little girl nearby greets you. Only then do you realize that you are in a campsite.",
    ["“信仰之跃”？"] = "'Leap of Faith'?",
    ["“倒吊人”"] = "\"The Hanged Man\"",
    ["“倒吊人”。"] = "\"The Hanged Man\".",
    ["“倒吊人”先生，听说……您会唱歌？"] = "Mr. “The Hanged Man”, I heard…… you can sing?",
    ["“倒吊人”先生，您当初是怎么加入塔罗会的？"] = "Mr. “The Hanged Man”, how did you join the Tarot Club back then?",
    ["“倒吊人”：不是失败，“堕落母神”污染了新生者的记忆，记忆关联的梦境太多，我们必须与“祂”的意志反复交手，才能收集足够信息，为这最后一次做充分的准备。"] = "\"The Hanged Man\": It's not a failure. The \"Mother Goddess of Depravity\" has corrupted the reborn one's memories, and there are too many dreams associated with the memories. We must repeatedly clash with \"Her\" will to collect enough information and make full preparations for this final time.",
    ["“倒吊人”：这次的笔记有问题，新生者因它的诅咒而自杀。"] = "\"The Hanged Man\": There is a problem with the notebook this time; the reborn one committed suicide due to its curse.",
    ["“倦坐在路边，取下这本书来……”"] = "\"Nodding by the fire, take down this book...\"",
    ["“值夜者小队藉此查到海纳斯 邓恩巧合地在他梦里”"] = "\"The Nighthawks squad used this to track down Haines, and Dunn coincidentally entered his dream\"",
    ["“做得不错，{{小伙子|小姑娘}}很有前途嘛！“一只海精灵随着夸奖一同出现了，面对被抓的结局表现得很平静，“这是给爱知识人的奖励。"] = "\"Well done, { { young man | young lady } }, you have a bright future!\" A Sea Spirit appeared along with the praise, remaining calm in the face of being caught. \"This is a reward for those who love knowledge.\"",
    ["“克莱恩？”\n老尼尔疑惑的呼唤，把克莱恩拉回了现实。"] = "\"Klein?\" \n Old Neil's puzzled call pulled Klein back to reality.",
    ["“具体可以去咨询……大学的历史教授……”"] = "\"You can consult... the history professor at the university...\"",
    ["“典籍中有关‘愚者’先生座下天使的部分也需要修改……”"] = "\"The part in the classics about the Angels under Mr. Fool also needs to be revised...\"",
    ["“典籍中有关愚者先生座下天使的部分也需要修改……”"] = "\"The parts of the scriptures concerning the angels under Mr. Fool also need to be revised...\"",
    ["“出入无法携带武器的禁地时，可将大剑存放于此处石棺中。”\n\n“混乱大剑只能使用秩序之力取回，秩序大剑只能使用混乱之力取回。”"] = "\"When entering forbidden grounds where weapons are prohibited, you may store your greatsword in this stone coffin.\"\n\n\"The Greatsword of Chaos can only be retrieved using the power of Order; the Greatsword of Order can only be retrieved using the power of Chaos.\"",
    ["“击败”,“资源点数”,“占领祭坛”"] = "\"Defeat\", \"Resource Points\", \"Occupy Altar\"",
    ["“别打了，爸爸……疼……好痛……”"] = "“Stop hitting me, Dad…… it hurts…… so painful……”",
    ["“剥面人”强尼"] = "\"Face-Peeler\" Johnny",
    ["“剥面人”强尼的恶念并未从潜意识世界中完全消散。扮演等级达到45级后，你可以再次向其发起挑战，那时的战斗将更加凶险。"] = "The malice of Johnny, the Face-Ripper, has not completely dissipated from the subconscious world. Once your Acting level reaches 45, you can challenge him again, and the battle will be even more perilous.",
    ["“剥面人”挑战"] = "Face-Ripper Challenge",
    ["“剥面人”挑战%s第%s%s"] = "Face-Ripper Challenge %s No. %s %s",
    ["“剥面人”挑战竞速"] = "'Faceless' Speed Challenge",
    ["“剥面人”的阴影从未散去，是时候做个了断了。"] = "The shadow of the Face-Ripper has never faded; it is time to put an end to it.",
    ["“勤奋”的工人"] = "\"Diligent\" Worker",
    ["“南威尔海滩的贝壳吟唱”"] = "\"The singing of seashells on the South Will beach\"",
    ["“占位”"] = "\"Placeholder\"",
    ["“占卜家”只是序列9，世界上应该有不少“占卜家”。"] = "\"Seer\" is only Sequence 9; there should be quite a few \"Seers\" in the world.",
    ["“占卜家”途径学姐"] = "\"Seer\" Pathway senior",
    ["“占卜家”魔药材料"] = "\"Seer\" potion materials",
    ["“却把我的诗稿垫在漏水的轴承底——”"] = "\"Yet they use my poetry drafts to pad the leaking bearing base—\"",
    ["“历史”权柄深化，对历史迷雾的利用更进一步。拥有“愿望”的能力，是部分“奇迹”权柄的体现，在不可能中创造可能。"] = "The authority of 'History' is deepened, and the use of the Fog of History is furthered. Possessing the ability of 'Wish' is a manifestation of part of the 'Miracle' authority, creating possibilities in the impossible.",
    ["“历史的开拓者——罗塞尔大帝与蒸汽革命浪潮”。"] = "\"Pioneer of History—Emperor Roselle and the Steam Revolution Wave\".",
    ["“厨王之王”？这么夸张的称号？"] = "\"King of Chefs\"? Such an exaggerated title?",
    ["“可怕的家伙，离我远一点！”"] = "“Terrible guy, stay away from me!”",
    ["“名画大盗”"] = "'Masterpiece Thief'",
    ["“向天空伸长脖子，唱出优雅的歌谣。”"] = "\"Stretching their necks toward the sky, singing elegant songs.\"",
    ["“吟游诗人”"] = "\"Bard\"",
    ["“启明小队”最近调查过的一个案件，会在其中重现和演绎。"] = "A case recently investigated by the \"Dawn Squad\" will be recreated and reenacted within it.",
    ["“启示”"] = "“Revelation”",
    ["“吵死了！怎么有人大半夜不睡觉啊！”一只海精灵骂骂咧咧地出现，哼哼唧唧地被抓住了。"] = "\"So noisy! Why is someone not sleeping in the middle of the night!\" A Sea Spirit appeared, cursing and grumbling, and was caught while whining.",
    ["“呜————”银制的哨子被吹响，像夜莺温柔的呢喃、像夏夜温煦的风。\n失控者停下攻击的动作，疯狂的眼眸中竟又凝起些许理智。\n他看到了所有的遗憾被弥补、所有的不堪被抹去、所有的悲伤还未涌起。他看到了另一种幸福的结局。\n做一场美梦吧，梦中的一切都还未堕落。\n永眠于美梦吧，把今生的痛苦就此掩埋。\n值夜者的猎魔子弹穿过了风，带走失控者的生命。异化后恐怖的身躯摇晃倒下，但是笑着的。\n“愿女神庇佑你。”队友收起枪祈祷，又摸了摸肩上亲昵落下的小鸟，“这件封印物真是无害，毕竟，谁会把这些鸟儿当做负面作用呢？”\n阿诺德拿出存放封印物的箱子，将夜莺银哨轻放了回去，妥帖地收在了身边。\n他身形挺拔、眼神坚定、笑声爽朗，像极了一个故人。\n“或许是因为，曾有一个温柔的灵魂栖息其中。”"] = "\"Woo—\" The silver whistle was blown, like the gentle murmur of a nightingale, like the warm breeze of a summer night. \nThe Out-of-Control Person stopped their attack, and a glimmer of reason actually condensed in their mad eyes. \nThey saw all regrets being mended, all ugliness being wiped away, and all sadness yet to arise. They saw another happy ending. \nHave a beautiful dream; in the dream, nothing has fallen yet. \nSleep forever in the beautiful dream, and bury the pain of this life here. \nThe Nighthawk's Demon Hunter Bullet passed through the wind, taking away the life of the Out-of-Control Person. The terrifying, mutated body swayed and fell, but it was smiling. \n\"May the Goddess protect you.\" The teammate put away the gun and prayed, then stroked the little bird that had affectionately landed on their shoulder. \"This Sealed Artifact is truly harmless; after all, who would consider these birds as a negative effect?\" \nArnold took out the box for storing Sealed Artifacts and gently placed the Nightingale Silver Whistle back, tucking it away securely. \nHis figure was upright, his eyes firm, and his laughter hearty, looking very much like an old friend. \n\"Perhaps it is because a gentle soul once resided within it.\"",
    ["“命运天使”乌洛琉斯，命运途径的天使之王，远古太阳神的追随者。"] = "\"Angel of Fate\" Ouroboros, King of Angels of the Fate pathway, follower of the Ancient Sun God.",
    ["“唯有混乱与秩序相交之时。”"] = "\"Only when Chaos and Order intersect.\"",
    ["“啊，三只洁白柔软的精灵——”"] = "\"Ah, three pure white and soft elves—\"",
    ["“善良天使行走街头，清新之风温柔协助……”天使？廷根出动这种级别的大人物了？"] = "“Kind Angel walks the streets, a fresh breeze gently assists……” Angel? Tingen has dispatched a big shot of that level?",
    ["“善良的艾德温”，嗤，行吧，只要你喜欢这名号……"] = "\"Kind Edwin\", pfft, fine, whatever, as long as you like that title...",
    ["“喵……”<P_Heart>（一声微弱而带着祈求的叫声，它湿漉漉的小脑袋蹭过你的指尖）。</>"] = "\"Meow...\" <P_Heart>(A weak and pleading meow, its wet little head rubbed against your fingertips). </>",
    ["“嘘。”\n“正义”女士轻轻打断了你的话。"] = "\"Shh.\" \n \"Justice\" gently interrupted your words.",
    ["“四方联赛”"] = "\"Four-Way League\"",
    ["“四月八号，我在黑王座号船头，对格林和爱德华兹说：‘想要我的财宝？去迷雾海尽头寻找吧！’”"] = "\"April 8th, I stood at the bow of the Black Throne and said to Green and Edwards: 'Want my treasure? Go find it at the end of the Fog Sea!'\"",
    ["“圆脸蛋的爱人是……”，你好呀，{{先生|女士}}。我们新学了一首歌！您感兴趣吗？"] = "\"The round-faced lover is...\", hello, {{Mr.|Ms.}}. We learned a new song! Are you interested?",
    ["“圆脸蛋的爱人是我全部的快乐。”"] = "\"The lover with round cheeks is all of my happiness.\"",
    ["“圆脸蛋的爱人是我快乐的全部。”"] = "\"The lover with round cheeks is all my happiness.\"",
    ["“在壁炉的火焰熄灭之前,让我们找寻它们跟星星之间的关联吧……”"] = "\"Before the fireplace flame goes out, let us search for the connection between them and the stars...\"",
    ["“在壁炉的火焰熄灭之前……”"] = "\"Before the fireplace's flames go out...\"",
    ["“在海盗将军的层层围袭中，格尔曼如一闪迅捷的弧光，他瞬间隐没在滚滚烟尘中。周遭突然静得出奇——”"] = "“Amidst the layers of encirclement by the Pirate Admiral, Gehrman was like a swift arc of light, instantly vanishing into the rolling smoke and dust. The surroundings suddenly became eerily quiet—”",
    ["“在那些书籍面前，我感觉自己像只卷毛狒狒。”"] = "\"In front of those books, I feel like a Curly-Haired Baboon.\"",
    ["“在铁皮上刻下无人读懂的诗句”"] = "\"Carving poems that no one understands on iron sheets\"",
    ["“在音乐的影响下变得温和”？它怎么反而更暴躁了？"] = "“Becomes gentle under the influence of music”? Why has it become even more irritable instead?",
    ["“堕落母神”又影响了我的梦境，我感觉……差点就醒不过来了。"] = "The \"Mother Tree of Desire\" has influenced my dreams again. I feel like... I almost couldn't wake up.",
    ["“堕落的终极，悖逆的君王，统御一切失序的最终敕令。 ”欢迎加入【黑皇帝】势力！诸君，该开启战争了！"] = "\"The ultimate of depravity, the rebellious monarch, the final decree that governs all disorder.\" Welcome to the [Black Emperor] faction! Gentlemen, it is time to start the war!",
    ["“壁炉在夏日是否会熄灭呢？然而它们是明亮的……\""] = "“Will the fireplace go out in summer? Yet they are bright……”",
    ["“夜之国”由古神的后裔建立，现已毁灭。"] = "\"Land of Night\" was established by the descendants of ancient gods and has now been destroyed.",
    ["“夜访魔女”"] = "Night-visiting Witch",
    ["“夜鸢伯爵”"] = "“Count Night-Kite”",
    ["“大作家”？上周我投给《廷根日报》的短篇又被退稿了，编辑先生的评语是“缺乏必要的戏剧冲突与商业前景”。简单来说，不够爽……真让人头疼……"] = "\"Great Writer\"? The short story I submitted to the \"Tingen Daily\" last week was rejected again, the editor's comment was \"lacks necessary dramatic conflict and commercial prospects\". Simply put, not exciting enough... It's really a headache...",
    ["“大棕熊”"] = "Big Brown Bear",
    ["“大胃王”"] = "Big Eater",
    ["“大胆的尝试恰好遇上了克莱恩 后者成功解决了这起超凡案件……”"] = "\"The bold attempt happened to encounter Klein, and the latter successfully resolved this Extraordinary case……\"",
    ["“太阳”"] = "\"The Sun\"",
    ["“太阳”先生"] = "Mr. Sun",
    ["“太阳”先生是个很单纯的人，温暖，善良……很难想象经历过这个世界黑暗面的人还能保持这份真诚。"] = "Mr. Sun is a very simple person, warm, kind… It's hard to imagine that someone who has experienced the dark side of this world can still maintain such sincerity.",
    ["“太阳”先生说，把学派当成家，那是什么？那群人嘴里念叨的故乡吗？"] = "Mr. Sun says to treat the Tarot Club as home, what is that? Is that the hometown that group of people keeps muttering about?",
    ["“太阳”精油"] = "'Sun' Essential Oil",
    ["“太阳”，我选择“太阳”。在白银之城，阳光还照射着大地的时候，还有光，还有希望。"] = "\"The Sun\", I choose \"The Sun\". In the City of Silver, when the sunlight still shines on the earth, there is still light, and there is still hope.",
    ["“失控”"] = "\"Loss of control\"",
    ["“头狼”挑战"] = "Alpha Wolf Challenge",
    ["“头狼”挑战%s第%s%s"] = "Alpha Wolf Challenge %s No. %s %s",
    ["“头狼”挑战竞速"] = "'Alpha Wolf' Speed Challenge",
    ["“头狼”鲁珀"] = "Luper, the Alpha Wolf",
    ["“头狼”鲁珀彻底疯狂，向你亮出了獠牙。"] = "Luper, the Alpha Wolf, has gone completely mad and bared his fangs at you.",
    ["“头狼”鲁珀的恶念并未从潜意识世界中完全消散。扮演等级达到38级后，你可以再次向其发起挑战，那时的战斗将更加凶险。"] = "The malice of Luper, the Alpha Wolf, has not completely dissipated from the subconscious world. Once your Acting level reaches 38, you can challenge him again, and the battle will be even more perilous.",
    ["“奇迹师”梅林"] = "Merlin, the Miracle Invoker",
    ["“女神之叹”项链"] = "'Goddess's Sigh' Necklace",
    ["“女神的凝望”"] = "\"Goddess's Gaze\"",
    ["“女神！”如果祂听见，一定会答应。"] = "\"Goddess!\" If She hears, She will definitely agree.",
    ["“她亲生爸妈也是疯子。”"] = "“Her biological parents were also Madmen.”",
    ["“她便在晕眩中蔫萎凋落”"] = "\"She withered and fell in a dizzying haze\"",
    ["“她像天使一般飞去了……”"] = "\"She flew away like an Angel...\"",
    ["“她和他、他和她、她和她、他和他、缠绵悱恻的爱情故事”？"] = "“She and he, he and she, she and she, he and he, lingering and sentimental love stories”?",
    ["“她是个怪胎！”"] = "“She's a freak!”",
    ["“她是个疯子！”"] = "“She's a Madman!”",
    ["“她是魔鬼！”"] = "“She's a devil!”",
    ["“她的爸妈把她丢在了救济院门口。”"] = "“Her parents left her at the gate of the orphanage.”",
    ["“她的花一夜开到天明”"] = "\"Her flowers bloomed until dawn in a single night\"",
    ["“她经常说些诡异的话，太可怕了。”"] = "“She often says weird things, it's too scary.”",
    ["“好运 顺利”"] = "\"Good luck, smooth sailing\"",
    ["“好运”带来的冰淇淋，也是能带来好运的冰淇淋！"] = "Ice cream brought by \"Good Luck\" is also ice cream that can bring good luck!",
    ["“如果不能拯救她，那就去陪伴她。”"] = "\"If I cannot save her, then I will accompany her.\"",
    ["“如若你想要我的一切……”"] = "\"If you want everything I have...\"",
    ["“妈妈，妈妈救救我……”"] = "“Mom, Mom, save me……”",
    ["“妈妈，怎样你才会更爱我呢？“\n强尼8岁时，和隔壁小威廉一起回来，但妈妈抱小威廉抱得更久。\n妈妈说：“等你变成个好孩子。”\n他不知道怎么变成好孩子，但知道怎么变成小威廉。强尼剥下了小威廉的脸皮，戴着他的脸，等妈妈冲他笑，等妈妈抱抱他。\n如果所有的乖孩子都是他就好了，这样所有的爱就都是给他的。\n回过神来时，他已经剥下了太多张脸，得费些力气，才能把他们的表情调整成微笑。\n终于有一天，他和父亲一样高了。\n\"你会一直抱着我吗，妈妈？\"\n母亲盯着他的脸，没有回答，只是一味地尖叫，表示拒绝的尖叫。\n如果妈妈不能爱自己，那就让妈妈永远离不开自己。\n“抱抱强尼？”他吻了这双新做好的靴子，就像小时每夜睡前，妈妈亲吻他的额头。"] = "\"Mom, what do I have to do for you to love me more?\" \nWhen Johnny was 8, he came back with little William from next door, but Mom hugged little William for longer. \nMom said: \"When you become a good boy.\" \nHe didn't know how to become a good boy, but he knew how to become little William. Johnny peeled off little William's face, wore it, and waited for Mom to smile at him, waited for Mom to hug him. \nIf all the good boys were him, then all the love would be for him. \nWhen he came to his senses, he had already peeled off too many faces; it took some effort to adjust their expressions into a smile. \nFinally, one day, he was as tall as his father. \n\"Will you always hug me, Mom?\" \nHis mother stared at his face without answering, only screaming—a scream that signaled refusal. \nIf Mom couldn't love him, then he would make sure Mom could never leave him. \n\"Hug Johnny?\" He kissed these newly made boots, just like Mom kissed his forehead every night before he went to sleep when he was little.",
    ["“孤儿帮”？"] = "“Orphan Gang”?",
    ["“学徒”途径学长"] = "\"Apprentice\" Pathway senior",
    ["“学徒真好用”，是这么说的吧？"] = "\"Apprentices are so useful,\" is that what you said?",
    ["“它”……看起来，这是前屋主心中最重要的东西。"] = "“It”…… It looks like this is the most important thing in the former owner's heart.",
    ["“它”的真身"] = "The true form of \"It\"",
    ["“它走过的路越来越长，长到离开了整个房子，整个小镇，整个国家……”"] = "\"The path it traveled grew longer and longer, so long that it left the entire house, the entire small town, the entire country...\"",
    ["“安提科勋爵的负债花销和不经营产业是为了维持贵族的体面，这很常见。不允许售卖酒庄里的酒只是因为喜欢美酒，不允许妻子卖酒也可以说成是对妻子的珍视，没有出轨行为，这怎么能算背叛了婚姻呢？”几位律师都是这样的答复。"] = "\"Lord Antigonus's debts and lack of business management were merely to maintain the dignity of a nobleman; this is quite common. Not allowing the sale of wine from the winery was simply because he loved fine wine, and forbidding his wife from selling wine can also be described as cherishing her. There was no infidelity, so how can this be considered a betrayal of marriage?\" These were the replies from several lawyers.",
    ["“安曼达”纯露是什么"] = "What is 'Amanda' Hydrosol",
    ["“安格尔威德之梦”"] = "Dream of Angellwade",
    ["“审判”女士"] = "Miss Judgment",
    ["“审判官”布莱克"] = "Blake, the Judge",
    ["“审判官”布莱克挑战竞速"] = "'Inquisitor' Blake Speed Challenge",
    ["“审判官”布莱克的恶念并未从潜意识世界中完全消散。扮演等级达到55级后，你可以再次向其发起挑战，那时的战斗将更加凶险。"] = "The malice of Blake, the Judge, has not completely dissipated from the subconscious world. Once your Acting level reaches 55, you can challenge him again, and the battle will be even more perilous.",
    ["“审判官”挑战"] = "Judge Challenge",
    ["“审判官”挑战%s第%s%s"] = "Judge Challenge %s No. %s %s",
    ["“审判官”挑战竞速"] = "'Inquisitor' Speed Challenge",
    ["“密契仪式”能够影响目标的精神体、星灵体、心智体、以太体，密契非凡觉醒对应的则是个体对于不同领域的掌握能力。选择发展不同的密契非凡觉醒，对相应领域的能力掌握程度也会不同。"] = "The \"Mystic Pact Ritual\" can affect a target's spirit body, astral projection, mental body, and ether body. Mystic Beyonder awakenings correspond to an individual's mastery over different domains. Choosing to develop different Mystic Beyonder awakenings will result in different levels of mastery over the corresponding domains.",
    ["“富商”阿玛拉"] = "Amara, the Merchant",
    ["“封印物的历史投影消散时，会留下一段独属于它的历史气息。”\n“这些有什么用处吗？”\n“当然，历史气息可以提升封印物的等级和能力，最高提升到到1级，也就是高度危险状态。”\n“能提升到0级吗？”\n“0级？你们这些天真的小脑瓜真敢想啊，至少升到中序列再考虑这些吧！”"] = "\"When a Sealed Artifact's historical projection dissipates, it leaves behind a trace of its unique historical aura.\" \n \"What is the use of these?\" \n \"Of course, historical aura can increase a Sealed Artifact's grade and ability, up to Grade 1, which is a highly dangerous state.\" \n \"Can it be upgraded to Grade 0?\" \n \"Grade 0? You naive little heads really dare to think; at least wait until you reach mid-sequence before considering such things!\"",
    ["“尊敬的阿兹克先生……太久没有给您写信，不知道您最近过得怎么样……”"] = "\"Respected Mr. Azik…… It has been too long since I last wrote to you. I wonder how you have been lately……\"",
    ["“尊敬的阿兹克先生……我这段时间了解了不少古代历史……”"] = "\"Respected Mr. Azik…… I have learned quite a bit about ancient history during this time……\"",
    ["“尊敬的阿兹克先生……由于一些复杂的原因，我可能将沉睡很长一段时间，很抱歉，也许很久没法给您写信了……”"] = "\"Respected Mr. Azik…… Due to some complex reasons, I may fall into a deep sleep for a long time. I am very sorry; I might not be able to write to you for a long while……\"",
    ["“尊敬的阿兹克先生……自从进入九月，贝克兰德的气温一天比一天低……”"] = "\"Respected Mr. Azik…… Since entering September, the temperature in Backlund has been dropping day by day……\"",
    ["“就偷了这么一点钱回来，是想饿死我吗！”"] = "“You only stole this little bit of money back, are you trying to starve me to death!”",
    ["“就算是狂风和激流，也会突然改变方向。”"] = "'Even a violent storm and torrent can suddenly change direction.'",
    ["“尽管你狭长的眼里透出的并非高兴。”"] = "\"Even though what shows in your narrow eyes is not joy.\"",
    ["“工人游记的残页泛黄”"] = "\"The yellowed pages of a worker's travelogue\"",
    ["“工匠”……这是“通识者”途径的序列6，能够制作机械奇物和非凡物品。"] = "“Artisan”…… This is Sequence 6 of the “Savant” Pathway, capable of crafting mechanical marvels and mystical items.",
    ["“工匠”奥斯瓦尔德"] = "\"Artisan\" Oswald",
    ["“巨人号”真宏伟啊……"] = "\"The 'Giant' is truly magnificent...\"",
    ["“巫王”卡拉曼从玫瑰学派接过这个人偶时，它的眼眶还是空的。\n“记住，”交付者警告，“用你的血肉喂它。别让它长出眼睛。”\n卡拉曼不以为意。一个巴掌大的玩具能有多危险？\n人偶确实很好用——它能让死物复活，让神奇物品听命，甚至瞬移逃生。卡拉曼赢得了无数场战斗，名声鹊起。\n但有一天，他忘记喂养了。\n第二天，人偶的左眼眶长出了一颗玻璃珠般的眼球。\n卡拉曼慌忙切下手指，用鲜血涂抹，眼球消退了。但从那以后，他每晚都梦见那个人偶——它坐在床边，空洞的眼眶直视着他，十指连按，像在弹奏丧歌。\n后来克莱恩击杀了卡拉曼，人偶作为战利品落入他手。\n当克莱恩用“母神之血”进行“友好协商”时，人偶的十指剧烈颤抖，比起像是终于遇见了可以谈判的对手，更像是看见了不可名状的恐惧。\n从那以后，它安分了。但那两个黑洞，仍在等待主人失误的那一天。"] = "When 'Witch King' Karaman accepted this doll from the Rose School of Thought, its eye sockets were still empty. \n 'Remember,' the deliverer warned, 'feed it with your flesh and blood. Don't let it grow eyes.' \n Karaman didn't care. How dangerous could a palm-sized toy be? \n The doll was indeed very useful—it could resurrect dead objects, make mystical items obey, and even teleport to escape. Karaman won countless battles and became famous. \n But one day, he forgot to feed it. \n The next day, a glass-bead-like eyeball grew in the doll's left eye socket. \n Karaman hurriedly cut his finger and smeared it with blood, and the eyeball receded. But from then on, he dreamed of that doll every night—it sat by the bed, its hollow eye sockets staring straight at him, its ten fingers pressing, as if playing a funeral song. \n Later, Klein killed Karaman, and the doll fell into his hands as a trophy. \n When Klein used the 'Blood of the Mother' for 'friendly negotiation', the doll's ten fingers trembled violently; it looked more like it had seen an indescribable horror than finally meeting an opponent it could negotiate with. \n Since then, it has behaved itself. But those two black holes are still waiting for the day its master makes a mistake.",
    ["“布置”？等等 ，该不会今天所有东西又都是你们组织的吧？"] = "“Arrangement”? Wait, could it be that everything today was organized by you guys again?",
    ["“帕斯河谷的彩虹酿酒”"] = "\"Brewing rainbow wine in the Pass Valley\"",
    ["“干不了”？ 哈，小子，我花钱……花钱买你来，不是为了听这个的。"] = "\"Can't do it\"? Ha, kid, I paid... I paid for you to come here, not to hear that.",
    ["“幸运蛋”"] = "\"Lucky Egg\"",
    ["“幸运蛋”在……"] = "\"Lucky Egg\" is at...",
    ["“幽蓝复仇者”号船长。“塔罗会”创始成员之一，代号“倒吊人”。"] = "Captain of the \"Blue Avenger.\" One of the founding members of the Tarot Club, codenamed \"The Hanged Man.\"",
    ["“廷根出现了新的危机”"] = "\"A new crisis has emerged in Tingen\"",
    ["“廷根市著名慈善家德维尔爵士重磅推荐！你，也来试试看吧！”"] = "'Highly recommended by the famous Tingen philanthropist, Sir Dervill! You, come and try it too!'",
    ["“廷根的烟囱冒出的黑烟，有些人开始工作，有些人开始交易”……不太合适。"] = "\"Black smoke rises from the chimneys of Tingen; some people start working, some people start trading\"... Not quite appropriate.",
    ["“廷根非正常死亡案件超过6起” “市议员梅纳德先生在家中死亡”……"] = "\"There have been over 6 unnatural deaths in Tingen\" \"City Councilor Mr. Maynard died at home\"……",
    ["“开出铁锈色的花”"] = "\"Blooming with rust-colored flowers\"",
    ["“开膛手杰斯”在你的一顿发力下，终于倒在了地上，不省人事。\n这时，一道较为耳熟的女声和男声从你背后响起……"] = "\"Ripper Jess\" finally collapsed to the ground after your exertion, unconscious. \nAt this moment, a familiar female voice and a male voice sounded from behind you...",
    ["“弗兰奇先生的智商还不如卷毛狒狒”——用幽默包裹责任感的莫雷蒂家长兄 。"] = "\"Mr. Frank's IQ is not even as good as a Curly-Haired Baboon\"—the eldest brother of the Moretti family who wraps his sense of responsibility in humor.",
    ["“当你老了，头发花白，睡意沉沉。”"] = "\"When you are old, your hair is gray, and you are full of sleep.\"",
    ["“当初的选择还是太草率了，现在看来不管是学徒还是占卜家，或者偷盗者，都更加好。”"] = "\"The initial choice was still too rash. Now it seems that whether it's an Apprentice, a Seer, or a Marauder, they would all be better.\"",
    ["“当最后一根轴承断裂”"] = "\"When the last bearing breaks\"",
    ["“当最后一颗铆钉锈蚀”"] = "\"When the last rivet rusts\"",
    ["“当红女歌手竟在街边做出此事”！"] = "'Popular female singer actually does this on the street'!",
    ["“律令师”休"] = "Hugh, the Imperative Mage",
    ["“徘徊于虚妄之中的灵，被人驱使的上界生物，独属于戴莉·西蒙妮的信使”……呵呵，你不觉得很酷吗？"] = "“A spirit wandering in falsehood, a creature of the upper realm driven by others, the messenger belonging exclusively to Daly Simone”…… Hehe, don't you think it's cool?",
    ["“心理医生”"] = "“Psychiatrist”",
    ["“心脏”是下一场比赛的入场券，明天早上十点，在<P_Yellow>休息室</>公布题目。"] = "The \"Heart\" is the ticket for the next competition. At ten o'clock tomorrow morning, the topic will be announced in the <P_Yellow>Lounge</>.",
    ["“忽地一声惊呼：‘在那！’只见格尔曼·斯帕罗已凌空跃起，一枪、两枪、三枪……伴随着血花炸响的，还有疯狂冒险家的名号！”"] = "“Suddenly, a cry of surprise: ‘There!’ Gehrman Sparrow had already leaped into the air, one shot, two shots, three shots…… along with the blooming of blood, the name of the Madman adventurer echoed!”",
    ["“总得去大剧场看一次戏剧。”"] = "\"Must go to the Grand Theater to watch a play at least once.\"",
    ["“恶作剧之神”阿蒙藏有时之虫的宝箱散落在各处，触碰时之裂隙能唤出阿蒙的谜题。"] = "The treasure chests containing the Worms of Time hidden by the \"God of Mischief\" Amon are scattered everywhere; touching the rifts in time can summon Amon's puzzles.",
    ["“惩戒天使”，祂是主的雷霆，主的怒火，主的手掌，主赐祂权柄，为主审判所有的堕落者和不洁者。"] = "The “Angel of Punishment”, He is the Lord's thunder, the Lord's wrath, the Lord's palm, and the Lord grants Him the authority to judge all the fallen and the unclean on His behalf.",
    ["“惩戒天使”，祂是主的雷霆，主的怒火，主的手掌，是所有堕落者和不洁者的审判官及处刑人。"] = "The \"Angel of Punishment,\" He is the Lord's thunder, the Lord's wrath, the Lord's palm, the judge and executioner of all the fallen and the unclean.",
    ["“愚者”"] = "“The Fool”",
    ["“愚者”先生"] = "Mr. Fool",
    ["“愚者”先生……就是，就是高大威武的那位！报纸上说您爱听笑话——<P_Heart>（突然抽噎）</>我、我要是摔成肉饼……可就没人讲隔壁瘸腿汤姆被鹅追着跑的糗事了！"] = "\"Mr. Fool\"... that is, that tall and mighty one! The newspaper says you love jokes—<P_Heart> (suddenly sobbing) </> If I... if I get squashed into a meat patty... there will be no one left to tell the embarrassing story of Lame Tom next door being chased by a goose!",
    ["“愚者”先生为你嫁接了来自未来的命运，你可以使用更高序列的力量。随着你的实力越来越强大，你学会的技能种类和威力也将不断增长。技能分为普通技能、特殊技能、扮演技能三类，最多同时装配四个普通技能或者扮演技能。特殊技能无需装配，包括普通攻击、解控技能和终结技能。"] = "Mr. Fool has grafted a destiny from the future for you, allowing you to use powers of higher Sequences. As you grow stronger, the variety and power of the skills you learn will also increase. Skills are divided into three categories: Normal Skills, Special Skills, and Roleplay Skills. You can equip up to four Normal Skills or Roleplay Skills at once. Special Skills do not need to be equipped and include Basic Attacks, Control Break Skills, and Finisher Skills.",
    ["“愚者”先生为你嫁接的力量中，还包含常用的非凡能力。"] = "The power grafted for you by Mr. Fool also includes some commonly used Beyonder abilities.",
    ["“愚者”先生仁慈而怜悯，是这个世界的救主，却让我们以“他”而非“祂”来称呼。"] = "Mr. Fool is kind and merciful, the savior of this world, yet he lets us refer to him as \"him\" rather than \"Him\".",
    ["“愚者”先生从历史中定位到了无数神话生物，利用“嫁接”将力量转移到源堡，得到了神话织茧。"] = "Mr. Fool located countless Mythical Creatures from history and used 'Grafting' to transfer their power to Sefirah Castle, obtaining Mythical Fabric.",
    ["“愚者”先生以屏障碎片为基石，于灵界中开辟了一片安全空间，在此建立塔罗学派。"] = "Mr. “Fool” used fragments of the Barrier as a cornerstone to open up a safe space in the Spirit World, establishing the Tarot Club here.",
    ["“愚者”先生以屏障碎片为基石，于灵界中开辟了一片安全空间，在此建立塔罗学院。"] = "Mr. Fool used fragments of the barrier as a cornerstone to carve out a safe space in the Spirit World, where he established the Tarot Academy.",
    ["“愚者”先生利用自己的权柄，在命运之河中开辟出一条世界命运的支流。"] = "Mr. Fool used his authority to carve out a tributary of the world's fate within the River of Fate.",
    ["“愚者”先生向你投来注视。"] = "Mr. Fool is casting his gaze upon you.",
    ["“愚者”先生指引我们，让你先加入黑荆棘安保公司。"] = "Mr. \"Fool\" guides us to let you join the Blackthorn Security Company first.",
    ["“愚者”先生是一位仁慈的神明。没有他的帮助，我也无法逃脱被邪神污染的命运……"] = "Mr. “Fool” is a merciful God. Without his help, I would not have been able to escape the fate of being corrupted by an evil god……",
    ["“愚者”先生是一位宽和的神明，不会苛责你的。是教会发生了什么事吗？"] = "Mr. “Fool” is a gentle God and will not blame you. Did something happen at the Church?",
    ["“愚者”先生是位仁慈的神明，廷根是他的起点。"] = "Mr. \"Fool\" is a benevolent god, and Tingen is his starting point.",
    ["“愚者”先生是得到所有教会认可的正神，塔罗学派的成功修建也是得益于他的帮助。"] = "Mr. Fool is a true God recognized by all churches, and the successful construction of the Tarot Club is also thanks to his help.",
    ["“愚者”先生是得到所有教会认可的正神，塔罗学院的成功修建也是得益于他的帮助。"] = "Mr. Fool is a true god recognized by all churches, and the successful construction of the Tarot Academy was also thanks to his help.",
    ["“愚者”先生沉睡前，发现一颗特殊的光茧。为争取对抗末日的更多希望……"] = "Before Mr. Fool fell into a deep sleep, he discovered a special cocoon of light. To strive for more Hope to fight against the apocalypse……",
    ["“愚者”先生沉睡前，将许多和你一样的旧日灵魂释放。"] = "Before Mr. Fool fell into a deep slumber, he released many souls from the ancient days like you.",
    ["“愚者”先生的力量果然深不可测……您一定很感激他。"] = "Mr. “Fool”'s power is indeed unfathomable…… You must be very grateful to him.",
    ["“愚者”先生赐予的封印物【乌托邦剧院】，可以帮助非凡者掌握并操控秘偶。\n获得秘偶后，可以使用秘偶的技能（仅限1个），并获得秘偶带来的角色属性提升效果。\n重复获得的秘偶，可以用来进行秘偶培养，提升秘偶的能力。\n星之虫类型的秘偶，可以幻形为其他非凡者的外貌，幻形后可以自由进行装扮。"] = "The Sealed Artifact [Utopia Theater] bestowed by Mr. Fool can help Beyonders master and control marionettes. \n After obtaining a marionette, you can use one of its skills (limited to 1) and gain the character attribute bonuses provided by the marionette. \n Duplicate marionettes can be used for marionette cultivation to improve their abilities. \n Star Worm-type marionettes can shapeshift into the appearance of other Beyonders and can be freely dressed up after shapeshifting.",
    ["“愚者”先生赐予的铁质卷烟盒，可以清除知识的污染……"] = "The iron cigarette case bestowed by Mr. Fool can clear the corruption of knowledge...",
    ["“愚者”先生！你怎么会在这里？"] = "Mr. \"Fool\"! How are you here?",
    ["“愚者”先生，“倒吊人”先生，我有个问题想要请教。<P_Yellow>扮演</>究竟是什么意思？"] = "Mr. \"Fool\", Mr. \"Hanged Man\", I have a question I would like to ask. <P_Yellow>Acting</>, what does it actually mean?",
    ["“愚者”先生，您不觉得这种“聚会”很有意思吗？"] = "Mr. \"Fool\", don't you think this kind of \"gathering\" is very interesting?",
    ["“愚者”先生，您介意多几次现在这样的“尝试”吗？"] = "Mr. \"Fool\", do you mind having a few more \"attempts\" like this?",
    ["“愚者”先生，我觉得这是一个很好的提议，只要“聚会”变成定期，有的事情如果您不方便出面，完全可以转交给我们。"] = "Mr. \"Fool\", I think this is a very good proposal. As long as the \"gathering\" becomes regular, if there are things you find inconvenient to handle, you can completely hand them over to us.",
    ["“愚者”先生？"] = "Mr. Fool?",
    ["“愚者”派其眷者格尔曼·斯帕罗，行于神弃之地，传播主的光辉，带来光明与温暖。"] = "“Fool” sends his Blessed, Gehrman Sparrow, to walk in the Forsaken Land of the Gods, spreading the Lord's radiance and bringing light and warmth.",
    ["“愚者”的馈赠"] = "Gift of The Fool",
    ["“感谢你的速度，也谢谢你的善良。”"] = "'Thank you for your speed, and thank you for your kindness.'",
    ["“慷慨号”是？"] = "What is the 'Generosity'?",
    ["“戏法大师”魔药配方"] = "\"Magician\" potion formula",
    ["“我”"] = "\"I\"",
    ["“我”的情况"] = "My situation",
    ["“我不知道该怎么解释，毕竟我只是一条狗。”"] = "\"I don't know how to explain it; after all, I am just a dog.\"",
    ["“我们做的事情看似简单，却实实在在影响着一个又一个孩子的人生，所以，我们得尽快开始，不能浪费时间。”"] = "“What we do seems simple, but it truly affects the lives of one child after another, so we must start as soon as possible and cannot waste time.”",
    ["“我们是一群时刻对抗着危险和疯狂的可怜虫，也是廷根的守护者。”"] = "\"We are a group of poor souls constantly fighting against danger and madness, and we are also the Guardians of Tingen.\"",
    ["“我们是守护者，也是一群时刻对抗着危险和疯狂的可怜虫。”"] = "\"We are Guardians, and also a group of poor wretches constantly fighting against danger and madness.\"",
    ["“我们有一颗足以照亮整座贝克兰德的宝石，她的智慧，她的美貌，她的品格，她的礼仪，都无可挑剔。”"] = "\"We have a gem bright enough to illuminate all of Backlund; her wisdom, her beauty, her character, and her etiquette are all impeccable.\"",
    ["“我会回忆起那些我们携手探寻过的梦境，回忆起曾困扰我们的每一个非凡案件或封印物，回忆起风吹的方向，还有月亮的形状和颜色。”"] = "\"I will recall those dreams we explored together, recall every Beyonder case or Sealed Artifact that once troubled us, recall the direction of the wind, and the shape and color of the moon.\"",
    ["“我听见生锈的星星在叹息”"] = "\"I hear the rusty stars sighing\"",
    ["“我想留在黑荆棘，一直保护这里。”"] = "\"I want to stay in Blackthorn and protect this place forever.\"",
    ["“我没有背叛白银城……”曾经的话语消散在黄昏中。"] = "\"I did not betray the City of Silver...\" The words once spoken dissipated in the twilight.",
    ["“我没有背叛白银城。”"] = "\"I did not betray the City of Silver.\"",
    ["“我的工具箱里藏着远方”"] = "\"My toolbox hides the distance\"",
    ["“我的手指在阀门上跳圆舞曲”"] = "\"My fingers dance a waltz on the valve\"",
    ["“我的爱情——”"] = "\"My love—\"",
    ["“我的脑袋快要爆炸了……仪式魔法、神秘学知识……”"] = "\"My head is about to explode... Ritual Magic, occult knowledge...\"",
    ["“我的诗会在废墟中发芽”"] = "\"My poems will sprout in the ruins\"",
    ["“我看见你有金子一般的心。”"] = "\"I see you have a heart of gold.\"",
    ["“我要建立一座由蒸汽驱动的浮空国度，它应当拥有思考能力和情绪，贯彻机械与蒸汽的至高美学。”罗塞尔说道。那时，他刚刚成为通识者途径序列2知识导师，站在世界的顶点，眼中充满无限可能。\n但这个愿望没来得及实现，纵使站在时代浪尖的罗塞尔本人也没有想到，畅想这一未来的时刻竟是他人生最高峰。权力的血雨腥风紧随而来，时代浪潮能裹挟着他冲上天空，也能将他沉入海底。\n蒸汽之国，最终成了一座只存在于构想中的神国，只有他死去时佩戴的王冠记得这一切——这究竟是幸运还是不幸？苏醒的王冠依靠污染的力量将其化作实体，新生的机械之城一刻不停地成长着，轰鸣声、齿轮声和发条转动声代替了脉搏与心跳的声音。罗塞尔的野心，在他死后以一种意想不到的方式不断蔓延……"] = "\"I want to build a floating kingdom driven by steam; it should possess the ability to think and have emotions, embodying the supreme aesthetics of machinery and steam,\" Roselle said. At that time, he had just become a Sequence 2 Knowledge Mentor of the Savant pathway, standing at the pinnacle of the world, his eyes filled with infinite possibilities. \nBut this wish never had the chance to be realized. Even Roselle himself, standing at the crest of the era, never imagined that the moment he envisioned this future would be the peak of his life. The bloody storms of power followed closely behind; the tides of the era could carry him to the sky, but they could also sink him into the abyss. \nThe Kingdom of Steam eventually became a divine kingdom that existed only in concept; only the crown he wore when he died remembers all of this—is this fortune or misfortune? The awakened crown relied on the power of corruption to manifest it into reality, and the newborn City of Machinery grew without a moment's pause. The sounds of roaring, gears, and clockwork replaced the sound of pulses and heartbeats. Roselle's ambition continued to spread after his death in an unexpected way...",
    ["“我见工匠，如见理性的辉光。”\n罗塞尔·古斯塔夫"] = "\"To see an artisan is to see the radiance of reason.\"\nRoselle Gustav",
    ["“我言爱之将死，她殷切地希望我把这话收回……”"] = "\"I spoke of love's impending death, and she earnestly hoped I would take those words back...\"",
    ["“我说过一万遍了，魔药的关键不是掌握和挖掘，而是消化和扮演。”"] = "\"I have said it ten thousand times, the key to a potion is not mastery and excavation, but digestion and Acting.\"",
    ["“战争的具现，征服的化身，纷争与战火的绝对主宰。 ”欢迎加入【血皇帝】势力！诸君，该开启战争了！"] = "\"The manifestation of war, the avatar of Conquest, the absolute master of strife and flames.\" Welcome to the [Blood Emperor] faction! Gentlemen, it is time to start the war!",
    ["“战士”途径学姐"] = "\"Warrior\" Pathway senior",
    ["“战士”途径的非凡者拥有高序列以下几乎无人能打破的防御，哪怕步枪子弹也很难伤害到我们。"] = "Beyonders of the Warrior Pathway possess a Defense that almost no one below high Sequence can break; even rifle Bullets can hardly harm us.",
    ["“战士”途径进入中高序列后非常擅长发现不同怪物的弱点，某种程度上，这些经验也可以应用到人类身上。"] = "After entering the middle and high Sequence, Beyonders of the Warrior Pathway are very adept at discovering the weaknesses of different monsters; to some extent, these experiences can also be applied to humans.",
    ["“所有人都会……包括我”。\n看到这句话的瞬间，你猛然从梦中惊醒。"] = "\"Everyone will... including me.\" \n The moment you saw this sentence, you woke up from your dream with a start.",
    ["“所有人都会死，包括我”……什么意思？"] = "\"Everyone will die, including me\"... What does that mean?",
    ["“执掌好运的黄黑之王”"] = "\"The King of Yellow and Black who wields good luck\"",
    ["“执掌好运的黄黑之王”，就它了！"] = "\"The King of Yellow and Black who wields good luck\", that's the one!",
    ["“执掌好运的黄黑之王！”"] = "\"The Yellow and Black King who controls good luck!\"",
    ["“扫描右侧图形以获得墓主人全部信息……”右侧的正方形图案由一个个黑色的小方块组成，看不出任何形状。"] = "'Scan the graphic on the right to obtain all information about the tomb owner...' The square pattern on the right is composed of small black squares, and no shape can be discerned.",
    ["“指证”。当你构建出完整的逻辑链条，就必须以坚定的意志和灵性，将你的推论“呈现”出来。"] = "\"Testimony.\" When you construct a complete logical chain, you must use firm will and spirituality to \"present\" your deduction.",
    ["“排兵布阵，纵横捭阖。”——这是某位学员教给我的“罗塞尔文”，你听着或许不会陌生。"] = "“Deploying troops and formations, maneuvering across the board.” — this is the \"Roselle language\" a certain student taught me; it might not sound unfamiliar to you.",
    ["“接过它，你再也没有怯懦的资格了。”  \n许多年前，科林·伊利亚特从前任首席手中接过这顶冠冕开始，这句话就时常回荡在他耳边。\n为了守护白银城，他总会毫不迟疑地拔剑，无论对手，无论代价。\n即使现在面对的是掩埋历史的天使之王，即使那代价会倾覆自己的所有。\n他依然拔出剑来，剑锋直指幽暗的最深处，绝无退缩，绝无迟疑。\n阳光炽烈，鲜血滚烫，他从未感觉如此自豪。"] = "'Accept it, and you no longer have the qualification to be cowardly.' \n Many years ago, when Colin Iliad accepted this crown from the previous Chief, this sentence often echoed in his ears. \n To protect the City of Silver, he would always draw his sword without hesitation, regardless of the opponent, regardless of the cost. \n Even if he is now facing a King of Angels who buries history, even if the cost would overturn everything he has. \n He still drew his sword, the blade pointing directly into the deepest darkness, never retreating, never hesitating. \n The sun was scorching, the blood was boiling, he had never felt so proud.",
    ["“摇篮”"] = "Cradle",
    ["“收尸人”了解很多不死生物的特点和弱点，能被无智慧的亡灵误认为同类而免遭袭击，并能直接看到部分恶灵。"] = "\"Corpse Collector\" understands many characteristics and weaknesses of undead creatures, can be mistaken for their own kind by mindless undead to avoid being attacked, and can directly see some evil spirits.",
    ["“收尸人”的战斗能力应该是其中最强的，另外两个序列都缺乏直接的对敌手段。"] = "The combat ability of a 'Corpse Collector' should be the strongest among them; the other two sequences lack direct means of confronting enemies.",
    ["“收尸人”途径能够驱使亡灵，看起来又神秘又酷炫，但我有些害怕尸体……"] = "The \"Corpse Collector\" pathway can drive the undead, which sounds mysterious and cool, but I'm a bit afraid of corpses...",
    ["“救赎天使”是我主的号角，是神谕的传达者。"] = "The “Angel of Redemption” is the horn of my Lord and the messenger of the divine oracle.",
    ["“救赎天使”，祂向世人传递主的声音，主赐给祂死而复生的奇迹，替主救赎被众神遗弃的失落城邦。"] = "The “Angel of Redemption”, He conveys the Lord's voice to the world, the Lord grants Him the miracle of resurrection, and He redeems the lost city-state abandoned by the gods on behalf of the Lord.",
    ["“教授”：伟大的母亲 我要向您 献上整个廷根 求您赐予新生！"] = "\"Professor\": Great Mother, I wish to offer the entire Tingen to you. Please grant me rebirth!",
    ["“斗邪恶”"] = "'Fight Evil'",
    ["“新生之种”……这倒像是颗“种子”，放到祭坛上试试。"] = "\"Seed of Rebirth\"... this actually looks like a \"seed\"; let's try placing it on the altar.",
    ["“新生活要开始了。”"] = "\"A new life is about to begin.\"",
    ["“施佩尔陷入沉睡中……”"] = "\"Spear has fallen into a deep slumber...\"",
    ["“无暗者”戴里克"] = "Derrick, the Unshadowed",
    ["“无暗者”戴里克人如其名，像是太阳一样热情火热，他迫不及待地想要和学员进行亲切交流，帮助学员提升乱世中的自保能力。"] = "Derrick, the Unshadowed, is as his name suggests, as enthusiastic and fiery as the sun. He cannot wait to have friendly exchanges with the students to help them improve their self-preservation ability in troubled times.",
    ["“时之天使”，祂是古老年代里的天使，最终臣服于我主，为他敲击天国之钟。"] = "The “Angel of Time”, He is an Angel from ancient times who eventually submitted to my Lord and strikes the bell of the Kingdom of Heaven for Him.",
    ["“时之天使”，祂是古老年代里的天使，最终臣服于我主，为祂敲击天国之钟。"] = "The \"Angel of Time,\" He is an angel from ancient times who eventually submitted to my Lord, striking the bell of the Kingdom of Heaven for Him.",
    ["“时之天使”，祂用血肉侍奉主，是主虔诚的信徒，曾用血肉侍奉主，主赐给祂时间的权柄，让祂得以侍奉主到永恒。"] = "The “Angel of Time”, He serves the Lord with His flesh and blood, is a devout believer of the Lord, once served the Lord with His flesh and blood, and the Lord grants Him the authority of time, allowing Him to serve the Lord for eternity.",
    ["“时尚公爵”？"] = "'Fashion Duke'?",
    ["“星之女王”嘉德丽雅的部下，“未来号“大副，称号”毒素专家“。尤其擅长培育具有特殊功能的蘑菇，他的发明既能解决食物短缺问题，也存在失控风险。"] = "Subordinate of the \"Queen of Stars\" Cattleya, First mate of the Future, title \"Toxin Expert\". Especially skilled in cultivating mushrooms with special functions; his inventions can solve food shortages but also carry the risk of loss of control.",
    ["“星星”"] = "\"Star\"",
    ["“星星”先生"] = "Mr. Star",
    ["“星星”先生已经告诉我了，那些没能从镜中世界回来的市民……"] = "Mr. \"Star\" has already told me, those citizens who couldn't return from the mirror world...",
    ["“星星”先生？"] = "Mr. \"Star\"?",
    ["“星星”有什么特别的含义吗？"] = "Does the “Star” have any special meaning?",
    ["“星星”（捏脸用）"] = "\"Star\" (for character customization)",
    ["“星星”：别担心了诸位，“愚者”先生会让奇迹，站在我们这一边的。"] = "\"The Star\": Don't worry, everyone. Mr. Fool will make miracles stand on our side.",
    ["“暗天使”萨斯利尔的躯壳沉睡于巨人王庭， 遭到了混沌海的侵蚀。"] = "The shell of the \"Dark Angel\" Sasrir sleeps in the Giant King's Court, having been eroded by the Sea of Chaos.",
    ["“暗黑”风尚度鉴定"] = "'Dark' Fashion Rating",
    ["“暗黑伯爵”"] = "“Count Dark”",
    ["“最佳劳模”奖章"] = "\"Best Model Worker\" Medal",
    ["“最后一页”……那句话的意思是——此处是知识的终点。准备好了吗？"] = "\"The last page\"... that phrase means—this is the end of knowledge. Are you ready?",
    ["“最后一页”的知识在呼唤求知者……"] = "The knowledge on the 'Last Page' is calling to the seeker...",
    ["“最好的哥哥，最好的弟弟，最好的同事。”"] = "\"The best brother, the best younger brother, the best colleague.\"",
    ["“月亮”先生"] = "Mr. “Moon”",
    ["“月亮”先生的画像"] = "Portrait of Mr. \"Moon\"",
    ["“月亮”先生，您认识我？"] = "Mr. “Moon”, do you know me?",
    ["“月光夫人”"] = "“Lady Moonlight”",
    ["“有10个黑影在9点飘到5个人的家里，\n6点3分2秒才四散开来。”"] = "'10 dark shadows drifted to 5 people's homes at 9 o'clock, \n and only scattered at 6:03:02.'",
    ["“未来号”大副，称号“毒素专家”，对生物研究有着极大的兴趣和高超的技术，培养出的神奇蘑菇为神弃之地的人们提供了更好的生存环境。"] = "First mate of the \"Future,\" titled \"Toxin Expert.\" He has a great interest in biological research and possesses superb techniques. The Magic Mushrooms he cultivated have provided a better living environment for the people in the Forsaken Land of the Gods.",
    ["“未来号”的大副，弗兰克·李。"] = "First mate of the Future, Frank Lee.",
    ["“末日还有十几年就将来临，每个人都可能毁灭，包括神灵。”"] = "\"The apocalypse will arrive in a dozen years or so, and everyone may be destroyed, including the Gods.\"",
    ["“杀了她！”"] = "“Kill her!”",
    ["“来自异世界的愚者”？倒是够精确。不行，这会暴露我最大的秘密。"] = "\"The Fool from another world\"? It's accurate enough. No, this will expose my biggest secret.",
    ["“枯干的蒲草没有歌,但它们还在唱,它们是在我胸中唱……”"] = "\"The withered reeds have no song, but they are still singing; they are singing in my chest...\"",
    ["“枯干的蒲草没有歌，但它们还在唱，它们在我胸中唱!”"] = "\"The withered reeds have no song, but they are still singing; they are singing in my chest!\"",
    ["“柔和”，“合理”，最重要的两个单词。"] = "\"Gentle,\" \"reasonable,\" the two most important words.",
    ["“格尔曼”"] = "“Gehrman”",
    ["“格尔曼同款狼鱼罐头”！"] = "\"Gehrman-style Wolf-Fish Canned Food\"!",
    ["“棕熊”埃尔就是爸爸！很厉害吧！爸爸为了给妹妹治病一直特别努力赚钱……"] = "\"Brown Bear\" Er is my dad! Isn't he amazing? Dad has been working extra hard to earn money to treat my little sister's illness...",
    ["“橙红的脚掌，悄然划破粼粼的波光。”"] = "\"Orange-red feet, quietly cutting through the shimmering waves.\"",
    ["“欢 迎 来 到 真 实 的 世 界 ！”\n陷入黑暗前，你听到疯癫的男士这样说。"] = "\"W E L C O M E  T O  T H E  R E A L  W O R L D !\" \n Before falling into darkness, you hear the crazed man say this.",
    ["“欢迎您的到来！过去的战争夺走了我的声音，但这儿很安全，有醇香的红茶和很软的鹅毛枕头。”"] = "'Welcome! The past war took away my voice, but it is safe here, with mellow black tea and very soft goose-down pillows.'",
    ["“歌剧魅影”是贝克兰德最负盛名的时装盛典。"] = "\"The Phantom of the Opera\" is Backlund's most prestigious fashion gala.",
    ["“歌剧魅影”曾是一位神秘魔女的私人舞台，她在此处举行过无数场精彩动人的表演。如今舞台向各大俱乐部敞开大门，是展示俱乐部风华的最佳场所。胜者不仅能赢得万众瞩目的荣耀，更会得到神秘「魅影」的馈赠。"] = "\"The Phantom of the Opera\" was once the private stage of a mysterious Witch, where she held countless brilliant and moving performances. Today, the stage is open to all major clubs and is the best place to showcase a club's elegance. The winner will not only win the glory of being in the spotlight but will also receive a gift from the mysterious \"Phantom.\"",
    ["“正义”"] = "\"Justice\"",
    ["“正义”。"] = "\"Justice\".",
    ["“正义”女士"] = "Ms. “Justice”",
    ["“正义”女士勇敢坚定，美丽优雅，她关心着学派的每个人，无论遇到任何困难，和她聊聊好像都能轻松解决。"] = "Ms. Justice is brave, firm, beautiful, and elegant. She cares about everyone in the club, and no matter what difficulties arise, talking to her seems to make them easily resolved.",
    ["“正义”女士委托我，安排你在这里见习一段时间，学习处理一些事件。"] = "Lady Justice entrusted me to arrange for you to intern here for a period of time to learn how to handle some incidents.",
    ["“正义”女士是真正的贵族，优雅、高贵、美丽、十分强大又十分慷慨……"] = "Lady Justice is a true aristocrat—elegant, noble, beautiful, extremely powerful, and very generous...",
    ["“正义”女士的馈赠，给人一种莫名的安心感。降低你受到的伤害，并把承受过的苦难化作财富，按累积伤害提升防御。财富压身太久，你会不堪重负。"] = "A gift from Ms. Justice, giving one an inexplicable sense of peace. It reduces the damage you take and turns the suffering you have endured into wealth, increasing defense based on accumulated damage. If the wealth weighs on you for too long, you will be overwhelmed.",
    ["“正义”女士，您的宠物狗会、会说话？"] = "Ms. Justice, your pet dog can, can it talk?",
    ["“正义”女士，要不要尝试一下我们培育出来的高歌蘑菇？"] = "Ms. Justice, would you like to try the Singing Mushrooms we cultivated?",
    ["“正义”女士：也许你以后会习惯这样的意外。"] = "Lady Justice: Perhaps you will get used to such accidents in the future.",
    ["“正义”女士：但今天是你的第一天……"] = "Lady Justice: But today is your first day...",
    ["“正义”女士：我们还有另一条路可以选择。"] = "Lady Justice: We have another path we can choose.",
    ["“正义”小姐"] = "Miss Justice",
    ["“正义”小姐不好意思打扰一下，关于仪式魔法……我翻阅了许多资料，但总觉得纸上谈兵，难以真正把握其精髓。"] = "Ms. “Justice”, sorry to bother you, regarding Ritual Magic…… I have read many materials, but I always feel like it's just empty talk, and it's hard to truly grasp its essence.",
    ["“正义”小姐写信给我，说我或许需要一处地方落脚……<P_Heart>（四处张望）</>但这是哪儿呢？"] = "Ms. “Justice” wrote to me, saying I might need a place to stay……<P_Heart>（Looking around）</>But where is this?",
    ["“正义”小姐的助手"] = "Miss \"Justice\"'s assistant",
    ["“正义”小姐见证了你的倒下，也见证了你重新站起来；被看见的意志，不会轻易熄灭。受到伤害降低30%，造成伤害增加40%。"] = "Miss Justice witnessed your fall, and she also witnessed you standing back up; the will that has been seen will not be easily extinguished. Damage taken reduced by 30%, damage dealt increased by 40%.",
    ["“正义”小姐说 你可能需要帮助 代价是一杯咖啡"] = "Miss \"Justice\" says you might need help. The price is a cup of coffee.",
    ["“正义”小姐说，你可能需要帮助，代价是一杯咖啡。"] = "Miss \"Justice\" said you might need help, the price is a cup of coffee.",
    ["“正义”小姐赠予的钱包，沉甸甸的，里面装着价值不菲的金钱。"] = "A wallet gifted by Miss Justice, heavy and filled with valuable money.",
    ["“正义”小姐馈赠的精致钱包，能够带来潜意识和心灵的守护，抵御部分非凡伤害。但负面效果是……产生强烈的花钱冲动！"] = "An exquisite wallet gifted by Miss Justice, capable of bringing subconscious and spiritual protection, resisting some Beyonder damage. But the negative effect is... generating a strong urge to spend money!",
    ["“正义”小姐，您怎么在这儿？"] = "Miss Justice, why are you here?",
    ["“正义”小姐，新客人！"] = "Miss Justice, a new guest!",
    ["“正义”小姐，新客人，咖啡好了！"] = "Miss Justice, new guest, the coffee is ready!",
    ["“正义”：别担心，神明不止一位，伟大的存在将帮助你……"] = "\"Justice\": Don't worry, there is more than one God, and a great existence will help you...",
    ["“正义”：没关系，还有希望。第二十一次尝试，重新开始。"] = "\"Justice\": It's okay, there is still hope. Twenty-first attempt, start over.",
    ["“正义”：（深吸一口气）好，一次新的梦境，开始了。"] = "\"Justice\": (Takes a deep breath) Good, a new dream has begun.",
    ["“死亡天使”是跟随我主最久的存在，是冥界的执政官。"] = "The “Angel of Death” is the existence that has followed my Lord the longest and is the administrator of the Underworld.",
    ["“死亡天使”，祂曾陷入失忆的诅咒，在主的帮助下逐渐找回自我，成为主的护翼，自亘古到永久。"] = "The “Angel of Death”, He once fell into the curse of amnesia, gradually found himself with the Lord's help, and became the Lord's wings, from ancient times to eternity.",
    ["“死亡执政官”向你投来注视。"] = "The Death Archon is casting his gaze upon you.",
    ["“死亡的本质，亡者的君主，所有生灵最后的归宿。”欢迎加入【冥皇】势力！诸君，该开启战争了！"] = "\"The essence of death, the monarch of the dead, the final destination for all living beings.\" Welcome to the [Underworld Emperor] faction! Gentlemen, it is time to start the war!",
    ["“母亲”也会祝福你，给你最好的礼物。"] = "The \"Mother\" will also bless you and give you the best gift.",
    ["“母亲”！“母亲”！"] = "\"Mother\"! \"Mother\"!",
    ["“毛毛草”…… 什么时候我也能有自己的新名字呢？"] = "\"Fuzzy Grass\"… When will I be able to have my own new name?",
    ["“水手”和“观众”。"] = "\"Sailor\" and \"Spectator\".",
    ["“水银天使”是命运的化身，是我主最宠爱的天使。"] = "The “Angel of Mercury” is the avatar of fate and is the angel my Lord favors the most.",
    ["“水银天使”是命运的化身，是我主最宠爱的天使；“死亡天使”是跟随我主最久的存在，是冥界的执政官；“救赎天使”是我主的号角，是祂神谕的传达者；“生命天使”是智慧的结晶，是每个人体内永不磨灭的灵性。"] = "The \"Angel of Mercury\" is the avatar of fate, the angel most favored by my Lord; the \"Angel of Death\" is the existence that has followed my Lord the longest, the administrator of the Underworld; the \"Angel of Redemption\" is the horn of my Lord, the messenger of His oracle; the \"Angel of Life\" is the crystallization of wisdom, the inextinguishable spirituality within every person.",
    ["“水银天使”，祂被吞尾的恶蛇追逐，遇主而重生，因信仰而得救，依此成全命运的奇迹。"] = "The “Angel of Mercury”, He is chased by the Ouroboros, reborn upon meeting the Lord, saved by faith, and thus fulfills the miracle of fate.",
    ["“永暗蜡烛”是我制作的。"] = "The “Candle of Eternal Darkness” was made by me.",
    ["“汪汪！”"] = "\"Woof!\"",
    ["“汪，汪汪！”"] = "“Woof, woof woof!”",
    ["“没有人见过风，但他会在你需要时出现”。你一挥手，就制服了这些埋伏于此的劫匪。我们的相遇，果然是命运的指引。"] = "\"No one has seen the wind, but he will appear when you need him.\" With a wave of your hand, you subdued these bandits lying in ambush here. Our meeting is truly the guidance of fate.",
    ["“泥沼深处的黑斑青蛙……生吞之后，那名村妇全身鼓胀……醒来，却看到亡父的灵魂……”嗯？这里还有批注……“我不能再忍受哪怕一天……亲爱的，等着我！”"] = "\"Black-spotted frog from the depths of the mire... after swallowing it raw, the village woman's whole body swelled up... upon waking, she saw the soul of her late father...\" Hmm? There are annotations here... \"I cannot endure even one more day... My dear, wait for me!\"",
    ["“注意你左侧的人”。后来才知道，她是在提醒邻座男士，他的绶带扣松开了。"] = "\"Watch the person on your left.\" I only found out later that she was reminding the gentleman next to her that his sash buckle had come undone.",
    ["“注视从星空投来，大地将四分五裂，世间的一切都会不复存在。”"] = "\"A gaze is cast from the starry sky, the earth will be torn apart, and everything in the world will cease to exist.\"",
    ["“泰利当然没有说过，因为他已经被你杀死了！”"] = "\"Of course Terry didn't say that, because he has already been killed by you!\"",
    ["“浴火的吞尾蛇”"] = "Ouroboros in Flames",
    ["“海盗女王将贵族小姐按在墙上，邪笑道：‘就算你喊破喉咙也没人来救你的！’话音未落，格尔曼从天而降，逼退女王：‘放开她。’”"] = "\"The Pirate Queen pinned the noble lady against the wall and smirked, 'Even if you scream until your throat breaks, no one will come to save you!' Before the words faded, Gehrman descended from the sky, forcing the Queen back: 'Let her go.'\"",
    ["“混乱”大剑"] = "'Chaos' Greatsword",
    ["“混乱”大剑-不可采集"] = "'Chaos' Greatsword - Uncollectible",
    ["“清新空气，从你我做起。特供无烟煤，欲购从速。”"] = "“Fresh air, starting with you and me. Special supply of smokeless coal, buy while stocks last.”",
    ["“清除墨水”的副作用，有概率尝到它涂抹过的文字的气味。"] = "The side effect of “Eraser Ink” is that there is a chance to taste the scent of the words it has wiped away.",
    ["“火光遍及处，燃烧的生命从灰烬中新生”……"] = "\"Where the firelight reaches, the burning life is reborn from the ashes\"…",
    ["“火种”无法再正常使用，算是光荣牺牲了。"] = "“Fire Seed” can no longer be used normally; it can be considered to have sacrificed itself gloriously.",
    ["“火种”曾属于我的一位朋友……"] = "“Fire Seed” once belonged to a friend of mine……",
    ["“火种二号”，能窃取对方的非凡能力。"] = "“Fire Seed No. 2”, capable of stealing the target's Beyonder powers.",
    ["“灰雾之上的神秘主宰”"] = "\"The mysterious ruler above the gray fog\"",
    ["“灰雾之上的神秘主宰”。"] = "\"The mysterious ruler above the gray fog\".",
    ["“点燃深眠花梗驱邪”……一些神秘学偏方？"] = "\"Light the Deep Sleep Flower stalk to exorcise evil\"… Some occult folk remedies?",
    ["“烈焰”"] = "“Flame”",
    ["“焦糖炸弹”"] = "\"Caramel Bomb\"",
    ["“焦糖炸弹”是什么……过去看看。"] = "What is a \"Caramel Bomb\"... I'll go take a look.",
    ["“焦糖炸弹”的名字里出现了焦糖，这代表着它使用了焦糖上色……"] = "The name \"Caramel Bomb\" contains caramel, which means it uses caramel for coloring...",
    ["“焦糖炸弹”能清洁马桶，这符合你的设想吗？"] = "\"Caramel Bomb\" can clean the toilet, does this meet your expectations?",
    ["“然后她像天使一般飞去了……”是的，还有什么比天使更值得形容动人的爱情？"] = "\"And then she flew away like an angel...\" Yes, what is more worthy of describing moving love than an angel?",
    ["“煤渣模糊了月亮的光晕”"] = "\"Cinders blur the halo of the moon\"",
    ["“煤渣模糊了月亮的光晕”……"] = "\"Cinders blur the moon's halo\"...",
    ["“爱妻奥莉薇，我寄回家的那笔货款，你存进贝克兰德银行了对吗？”"] = "“My dear wife Olivia, the payment for the goods I sent home, you deposited it into the Backlund Bank, right?”",
    ["“爱情总是伴随着谎言”，不过谁又知道，这句话本身是不是一种欺诈？"] = "\"Love is always accompanied by lies,\" but who knows if this statement itself is a form of deception?",
    ["“爸爸这辈子没给你什么好东西，就这块表是新买的。”"] = "\"Daddy hasn't given you anything good in this life, this watch is the only thing I bought new.\"",
    ["“特拉斯：\n我准备好迎接黑夜了，那么黑夜准备好迎接我了吗？”"] = "“Triss: \n I am ready to welcome the night, so is the night ready to welcome me?”",
    ["“特殊服务”指的是什么？"] = "What does \"special service\" refer to?",
    ["“猎人”们总攻前最后的休整地，充斥着战意的气息。占领后可攻击战争石碑，固定每分钟获得30点资源。"] = "The final resting place for \"Hunters\" before their all-out attack, filled with the aura of Battle Intent. After occupying it, you can Attack the War Stele to gain 30 resources every minute.",
    ["“献给我忠实的朋友华特森，她的主人敬上。”"] = "“Dedicated to my loyal friend Watson, from her master.”",
    ["“现在魔改一版更爽更刺激的《基督山伯爵》还不是轻轻松松，因蒂斯人民一定会欲罢不能的。”"] = "\"Now, modifying a version of 'The Count of Monte Cristo' to be even more exciting and thrilling is a piece of cake, the people of Intis will definitely be addicted.\"",
    ["“生命天使”是智慧的结晶，是每个人体内永不磨灭的灵性。"] = "The “Angel of Life” is the crystallization of wisdom and the undying spirituality within everyone.",
    ["“生命天使”，祂是主智慧的光辉，是每个人体内永不磨灭的灵性，是主给予大地的恩赐。"] = "The “Angel of Life”, He is the radiance of the Lord's wisdom, the undying spirituality within everyone, and the gift the Lord gives to the earth.",
    ["“生日快乐！欢迎来到我的生日会！哥哥说，他会给我准备一个大大的惊喜！”"] = "\"Happy birthday! Welcome to my birthday party! Brother said he would prepare a big surprise for me!\"",
    ["“白色羽毛，在翡翠般的水面漂浮荡漾。”"] = "\"White feathers, floating and rippling on the emerald water surface.\"",
    ["“白蔷薇夫人”"] = "“Lady White Rose”",
    ["“白霜夫人”"] = "“Lady White Frost”",
    ["“百里挑蛋”挑战赛"] = "\"One in a Hundred\" Challenge",
    ["“百里挑蛋”挑战赛开启，一万苏勒花落谁家？"] = "'One in a Hundred Eggs' challenge begins, who will win the ten thousand Sol?",
    ["“看见了真实造物主的清晰形象 受到了巨大的伤害……”"] = "\"Saw the clear image of the True Creator and suffered immense damage……\"",
    ["“看见我”最大的作用，其实是——操控！"] = "The greatest use of “See Me” is actually—control!",
    ["“看见我”源于观众途径序列6催眠师的能力。"] = "“See Me” originates from the Hypnotist ability of the Spectator Pathway Sequence 6.",
    ["“眠于红茧的纯白之人，主宰新生与堕落的神子，末日最后的可能性。”"] = "\"The pure white one sleeping in the red cocoon, the divine child who rules over rebirth and corruption, the final possibility of the apocalypse.\"",
    ["“知识与智慧之神”向你投来注视。"] = "The God of Knowledge and Wisdom is casting his gaze upon you.",
    ["“知识就是力量”——这并不是象征性质的语句。"] = "“Knowledge is Power” — this is not a symbolic statement.",
    ["“知识皇冠”中残存着我父亲的意志，如果能短暂唤醒他的残影，或许能摧毁屏障。"] = "The will of my father remains in the \"Knowledge Crown\". If I can briefly awaken his afterimage, perhaps I can destroy the barrier.",
    ["“知识皇冠”的来源"] = "Origin of the Crown of Knowledge",
    ["“砰。”"] = "\"Bang.\"",
    ["“破晓”并非消灭黑暗，而是在黑暗中发光。"] = "\"Dawn\" is not about eliminating darkness, but about shining in the darkness.",
    ["“破晓之时”挑战赛"] = "\"Dawn's Arrival\" Challenge Tournament",
    ["“破晓之时”第二轮比赛，又将迎来什么挑战？"] = "What challenges will the second round of the \"Dawn's Arrival\" competition bring?",
    ["“破晓号”的原型是一艘曾航行在海上的船。"] = "The prototype of the \"Dawn\" was a ship that once sailed on the sea.",
    ["“碎嘴子”"] = "“Chatterbox”",
    ["“祂”在哪里注视我？"] = "Where is \"He\" watching me from?",
    ["“祂将在此处诞生新的子嗣。”"] = "\"He shall give birth to new offspring here.\"",
    ["“祂的声音，一直在我的耳边回响……”"] = "\"His voice has been echoing in my ears...\"",
    ["“祝你也能回到廷根拥有这样的一天。”"] = "\"I hope you can also return to Tingen and have a day like this.\"",
    ["“神话织茧”承载着某些古老存在的形态残影。用灰雾尘埃将它编织完整，你便能短暂借来神明的力量。"] = "\"Mythical Creature Form\" carries the residual shadows of certain ancient existences. By weaving it complete with the dust of the gray fog, you can briefly borrow the power of a God.",
    ["“神说，无效。”"] = "\"The God said, 'Invalid.'\"",
    ["“神降”仪式"] = "\"Divine Descent\" ritual",
    ["“神降”仪式的材料都准备好后，我将陪同你一起开启仪式，见证奇迹般神降之时。"] = "After the materials for the “divine descent” ritual are all prepared, I will accompany you to start the ritual and witness the miraculous moment of divine descent.",
    ["“神降”仪式进度"] = "\"Divine Descent\" ritual progress",
    ["“神降”仪式进度 %s%%"] = "\"Divine Descent\" ritual progress %s %%",
    ["“神降”仪式进度 %s%%\n%s"] = "\"Divine Descent\" ritual progress %s %% \n %s",
    ["“秩序”大剑"] = "'Order' Greatsword",
    ["“秩序”大剑-不可采集"] = "'Order' Greatsword - Uncollectible",
    ["“秩序的基石，法则的起源，裁决万理的唯一审判者。 ”欢迎加入【夜皇】势力！诸君，该开启战争了！"] = "\"The cornerstone of order, the origin of laws, the sole judge who rules over all principles.\" Welcome to the [Night Emperor] faction! Gentlemen, it is time to start the war!",
    ["“窥秘人”……途径……序列6…………卷轴教授……"] = "\"Mystery Pryer\"... Pathway... Sequence 6... Scroll Professor...",
    ["“窥秘人”和“占卜家”都可以更好地掌握神秘学领域的知识，里面可能就有我回家的线索。"] = "Both 'Mystery Pryer' and 'Seer' can better master knowledge in the field of mysticism; there might be clues to my home inside.",
    ["“第二份礼物是什么？”\n\n“是一艘叫做‘幽蓝复仇者’的幽灵船，已经停在了港口。”"] = "\"What is the second gift?\" \n\n \"It's a ghost ship called the 'Blue Avenger,' and it's already docked at the port.\"",
    ["“第二十次了，希望新生者能走得更远一点。”"] = "\"It's the twentieth time, I hope the reborn one can go a little further.\"",
    ["“精油工厂如果是我的大草原，那每天早上一杯咖啡，就是用鞭子鞭策自己。”"] = "\"If the essential oil factory is my prairie, then a cup of coffee every morning is whipping myself with a lash.\"",
    ["“糟了！糟了！有人发现我了！”"] = "\"Oh no! Oh no! Someone has discovered me!\"",
    ["“累了？那是你躺得还不够。”不愿透露姓名的工人如是说道。\n持续参与，将获得某些神秘存在的馈赠。"] = "'Tired? That's because you haven't laid down enough.' So said an anonymous worker. \n Continued participation will earn you gifts from certain mysterious existences.",
    ["“红月之跃”？"] = "'Leap of the Red Moon'?",
    ["“红月种子”孕育"] = "Crimson Moon Seed Gestation",
    ["“纪念伟大的罗塞尔大帝，他不愧是那个时代的主角——”\n“在狂暴海中开拓安全航道，开启对南大陆的通航贸易时代。”\n“改良火炮、帆船、造纸术和印刷术……还发明了报纸。”"] = "\"Commemorating the great Emperor Roselle, he is truly the protagonist of that era—\"\n\"Pioneering safe shipping lanes in the Berserk Sea, opening the era of maritime trade with the Southern Continent.\"\n\"Improving artillery, sailing ships, papermaking, and printing... and even inventing the newspaper.\"",
    ["“纯真”风尚度鉴定"] = "'Innocence' Fashion Rating",
    ["“纯真子爵”"] = "“Viscount Innocence”",
    ["“纵火家”"] = "“Pyromaniac”",
    ["“织梦人”奥黛丽"] = "Audrey, the Dream Weaver",
    ["“织梦黑匣”将在集体潜意识中，编织一个<P_Yellow>三天前的场景</>。"] = "The \"Dream-Weaving Black Box\" will weave a <P_Yellow>scene from three days ago</> in the collective subconscious.",
    ["“绑定苏勒”不足，无法一键聚合"] = "Insufficient \"Bound Soule\", cannot aggregate with one tap",
    ["“给人一种回家的感觉。”"] = "\"Gives one a feeling of home.\"",
    ["“绝望魔镜”卷宗"] = "\"Magic Mirror of Despair\" dossier",
    ["“绝望魔镜”对应序列4的绝望魔女非凡特性，要比序列1的“知识皇冠”容易解决。"] = "\"Magic Mirror of Despair\" corresponds to the Sequence 4 Despair Witch Beyonder characteristic, which is easier to solve than the Sequence 1 \"Knowledge Crown\".",
    ["“绝望魔镜”是进入镜中廷根的唯一入口。"] = "\"Magic Mirror of Despair\" is the only entrance to Tingen in the Mirror.",
    ["“绯红侯爵”"] = "“Marquis Crimson”",
    ["“罗塞尔发明实用蒸汽机，推动工业革命的浪潮。”"] = "\"Roselle invented the practical steam engine, driving the wave of the Industrial Revolution.\"",
    ["“罗森的民俗草药店”……就是这里。"] = "\"Rosen's Folk Herbal Shop\"... this is the place.",
    ["“美丽的女士，你刻意留下的破绽实在拙劣。不过，这种小聪明倒让我更感兴趣了，卢娜女士。”\n“可当她垂下眼眸，那一举一动纯洁无辜，风情万种却又不曾察觉，真是……真是天生的尤物啊。陷阱又如何？我当然有分寸。让这场考验来得更猛烈些吧……”\n“清晨的阳光洒在她的脸上，多么美好，我望向床边的镜子，一切如同油画一般……等等，镜子里是个……男人？！难道这是……传说中的魔女？！”\n“但看着这张脸，谁能说她不比真正的女人更动人？我的心里慢慢生出了别样的滋味……”\n“魔女的滋味……确实不错。”"] = "\"Beautiful lady, the flaw you deliberately left is truly clumsy. However, this kind of cleverness makes me even more interested, Ms. Luna.\" \n\"But when she lowered her eyes, every movement was pure and innocent, charming and yet unaware—truly... truly a natural femme fatale. So what if it's a trap? I naturally have my own sense of proportion. Let this test come even more fiercely...\" \n\"The morning sunlight spilled onto her face, how wonderful. I looked at the mirror by the bed, everything was like an oil painting... Wait, is that a... man in the mirror?! Could this be... the legendary Witch?!\" \n\"But looking at this face, who could say she isn't more moving than a real woman? A different kind of taste slowly grew in my heart...\" \n\"The taste of the Witch... is indeed not bad.\"",
    ["“翡翠歌谣”耳环"] = "'Emerald Ballad' Earrings",
    ["“老尼尔会弹钢琴？”"] = "\"Old Neil can play the piano?\"",
    ["“聚合因子”不足，无法一键聚合"] = "Insufficient \"Aggregation Factor\", cannot aggregate with one tap",
    ["“至高的绯红之主啊，伟大的厄难与恐惧女皇……”\n“我祈求您降下眷顾，眷顾您迷失的羔羊——赛琳娜！”"] = "\"Oh, Supreme Lord of Crimson, Great Empress of Calamity and Horror...\" \n \"I pray for your favor, favor your lost lamb—Selina!\"",
    ["“致我苏醒的友人”？"] = "“To my awakened friend”?",
    ["“色彩派”引发讨论！"] = "\"Color School\" sparks discussion!",
    ["“艾拉” "] = "Ayla",
    ["“莫比乌斯环”的未知谜题增加到11个，我决定将它的危险等级提升为2级。"] = "The unknown puzzles of the \"Mobius Ring\" have increased to 11, I have decided to raise its danger level to Level 2.",
    ["“莫比乌斯环”的未知谜题增加到8个，我决定将它的危险等级提升为2级。"] = "The unknown puzzles of the \"Mobius Ring\" have increased to 8, I have decided to raise its danger level to Level 2.",
    ["“葬于石像之旁”……难道在石像旁边？过去看看。"] = "\"Buried beside the stone statue\"... could it be next to the stone statue? Let's go take a look.",
    ["“蒲公英”"] = "“Dandelion”",
    ["“蒲公英”……梦里那个小女孩的哥哥！"] = "\"Dandelion\"... the older brother of the little girl in the dream!",
    ["“蒲公英”先生可是最受器重、最有潜力的神仆之一。"] = "Mr. \"Dandelion\" is one of the most valued and potential servants of God.",
    ["“蒲公英”先生命令我拦住你，我必须遵守。"] = "Mr. \"Dandelion\" ordered me to stop you, and I must obey.",
    ["“蒲公英”先生应该安全了 撤退！"] = "Mr. \"Dandelion\" should be safe now. Retreat!",
    ["“血迹”已经干了，颜色却还很鲜红。如果是血，颜色应该更黯淡。"] = "The \"bloodstain\" has dried, but the color is still very bright red. If it were blood, the color should be duller.",
    ["“行测”是行政能力测试的简称，唉，我都不知道这门要考什么……"] = "\"Administrative Ability Test\" is the abbreviation for the civil service exam. Sigh, I don't even know what this subject tests...",
    ["“被凝视羞得无处可躲”"] = "\"Shamed by the Gaze, with nowhere to hide\"",
    ["“观众”的序列名，会让人误以为这是一个只擅长观察与辅助的途径。但实际上，这也是一种伪装，让人更轻敌的伪装。"] = "The Sequence name \"Spectator\" might lead people to mistakenly think this is a Pathway only good at observation and support. But in reality, it is also a form of disguise, a disguise that makes people underestimate the user.",
    ["“警局侦破一起入室骚扰案，疑似神秘接头组织再现身……”"] = "“Police department solves a case of residential harassment, suspected mysterious underground organization reappears……”",
    ["“让我们找寻它们跟星星之间的关联吧……”"] = "\"Let us find the connection between them and the stars...\"",
    ["“让我们欢迎新加入的正式成员，\n 克莱恩·莫雷蒂！干杯！”"] = "\"Let us welcome our newly joined official member, \n Klein Moretti! Cheers!\"",
    ["“议院治安队”藏在暗处的利刃，为议员先生扫平政途上的一切障碍。"] = "The hidden blade of the Council's Security Force, clearing all obstacles on the political path for the Councilman.",
    ["“请注视我，注视这卑微的知识追逐者！”"] = "\"Please gaze upon me, gaze upon this humble pursuer of knowledge!\"",
    ["“读心”霍普医生"] = "'Mind Reader' Dr. Hope",
    ["“贝克兰德夜总会香花女士的印有她唇印的丝巾，顺便问问她，还记得当时那个美妙的午夜吗？”"] = "\"A silk scarf with the lipstick print of Ms. Fragrant from the Backlund Nightclub, and by the way, ask her if she still remembers that wonderful midnight?\"",
    ["“赛琳娜·伍德偶然间、巧合地从她的神秘学老师海纳斯处看到了魔镜占卜的真正咒文……\n大胆的尝试恰好遇上了克莱恩，后者成功解决了这起超凡案件……"] = "\"Selina Wood accidentally and coincidentally saw the true incantation for mirror divination from her occult teacher, Haines... \n Her bold attempt happened to encounter Klein, and the latter successfully solved this Beyonder case...",
    ["“赛琳娜伍德偶然间 巧合地从她的神秘学老师海纳斯处看到了魔镜占卜的真正咒文……”"] = "\"Selina Wood accidentally and coincidentally saw the true incantation for mirror divination from her occult teacher, Haines……\"",
    ["“赛琳娜，生日快乐，这是给你的礼物。”伊丽莎白将护符递给生日宴会的主角，赛琳娜立刻将它戴在了脖颈上。\n“谢谢你，伊丽莎白！我太喜欢这个护身符了。”赛琳娜握住了好朋友的手，高兴地摇晃着，“我现在感觉很放松，身体好像更健康了！”\n“你喜欢就好。”伊丽莎白微笑起来，然后陪好友一起去门口迎接客人。\n她想着，有机会一定要谢谢地下市场那位神秘的绅士，是他帮助自己挑选了这个最好的礼物。"] = "'Selina, happy birthday, this is a gift for you.' Elizabeth handed the amulet to the protagonist of the birthday party, and Selina immediately put it around her neck. \n 'Thank you, Elizabeth! I love this amulet so much.' Selina held her best friend's hand and shook it happily, 'I feel very relaxed now, my body seems to be healthier!' \n 'As long as you like it.' Elizabeth smiled, then accompanied her friend to the door to greet guests. \n She thought that if she had the chance, she must thank the mysterious gentleman in the underground market; it was he who helped her choose this best gift.",
    ["“赞美……愚者……”"] = "\"Praise... the Fool...\"",
    ["“走过最长的路的小虫子却伤心地哭了，因为……”\n“它被困在了世界的尽头。”"] = "\"The little bug that had traveled the longest path cried sadly, because...\" \n \"It was trapped at the end of the world.\"",
    ["“这一局，黑棋先行。”"] = "'In this game, the black pieces move first.'",
    ["“这个世界，是有缝隙的。”"] = "\"This world has cracks.\"",
    ["“这块晶石是一口金色泉水的心脏。”\n从村中的老者手中得到这枚护符时，他还不是一位士兵。但随着战况的逐步胶着，他也同无数原本生活在弗萨克小村的年轻人一样，被征召进了队伍，前往了不知何处的战场。\n他不知道这场战争从何而起，也不知这场战斗为何结束。在生命最后的时光，他只看到了夜色铺满了天际，而衰朽的辉光自高空落下。\n直到胜利者拨开了他已经冰冷的衣襟，护符上的结晶映照着那坠落的黄昏，仍旧金黄。"] = "\"This crystal is the heart of a golden spring.\" \nWhen he received this amulet from the village elder, he was not yet a soldier. But as the war situation gradually reached a stalemate, he, like countless young people who originally lived in the small Feynapotter village, was conscripted into the ranks and headed to a battlefield somewhere unknown. \nHe did not know where this war started, nor did he know why this battle ended. In the final moments of his life, he only saw the night covering the horizon, and the decaying radiance falling from the high sky. \nUntil the victor pushed aside his already cold collar, the crystal on the amulet reflected the falling dusk, still golden.",
    ["“这就是魔法的力量。”"] = "\"This is the power of magic.\"",
    ["“这样的币制简直违背直觉，它一定是世界上最愚蠢的币制之一。”克莱恩困惑地调侃鲁恩的货币体质。\n“不，没有之一。”班森严肃纠正，“你应该明白，要制定合理又简单的币制需要一个前提，那就是懂得数数！可惜，在那些大人物里面，这样的人才太稀少了。”"] = "'Such a currency system is simply counter-intuitive; it must be one of the stupidest currency systems in the world.' Klein teased the Loen currency system in confusion. \n 'No, not one of.' Benson corrected seriously, 'You should understand that to formulate a reasonable and simple currency system, there is a prerequisite, which is knowing how to count! Unfortunately, among those big shots, such talents are too rare.'",
    ["“这里发生什么都不奇怪”——他在暗示什么？"] = "“Nothing is strange here” — what is he implying?",
    ["“这里是我的国度”"] = "\"This is my kingdom\"",
    ["“远离她！”"] = "“Stay away from her!”",
    ["“迷人”到我都看不清自己有多少只手指了……"] = "\"Charming\" enough that I can't even see how many fingers I have...",
    ["“送礼就送木乃伊粉，贵族们都爱用！”"] = "'Give mummy powder as a gift, nobles love it!'",
    ["“通灵者”"] = "Spirit Medium",
    ["“那么，今天的睡前故事，讲的是一只好奇的小虫子……”"] = "\"So, tonight's bedtime story is about a curious little bug...\"",
    ["“那会使我更欣喜。”"] = "\"That would make me even happier.\"",
    ["“那位”"] = "\"That One\"",
    ["“那天，他走进了一家咖啡厅……”"] = "'That day, he walked into a cafe...'",
    ["“那种”是哪种？"] = "What do you mean by 'that kind'?",
    ["“金手指”"] = "“Golden Finger”",
    ["“钻头”"] = "Drill",
    ["“钻头”出场动画"] = "\"Drill\" entrance animation",
    ["“钻头”挑战"] = "Drill Challenge",
    ["“钻头”挑战%s第%s%s"] = "Drill Challenge %s No. %s %s",
    ["“钻头”挑战竞速"] = "'Drill' Speed Challenge",
    ["“钻头”狂暴 —— 电刑降临！"] = "\"Drill\" Berserk — Electrocution Descent!",
    ["“钻头”的恶念并未从潜意识世界中完全消散。扮演等级达到51级后，你可以再次向其发起挑战，那时的战斗将更加凶险。"] = "The malice of Drill has not completely dissipated from the subconscious world. Once your Acting level reaches 51, you can challenge him again, and the battle will be even more perilous.",
    ["“钻头”过载！已昏厥！"] = "\"Drill\" overloaded! Fainted!",
    ["“银骑士”科林"] = "'Silver Knight' Colin",
    ["“门”已经打开，“正义”女士，你准备好对他心理治疗了吗？"] = "The \"Door\" has been opened. Ms. Justice, are you ready to provide him with psychological therapy?",
    ["“门”领域对致命伤害的封印锁链缠绕你的心脏。单次受伤造成的生命值损失不得超过最大生命值的25%。"] = "\"Door\" domain seals of fatal damage wrap around your heart. Single-instance damage cannot exceed 25% of your maximum HP.",
    ["“闪现”的极致是“无处不在”。"] = "The ultimate form of Flash is \"omnipresence.\"",
    ["“闪电速递”的口号是——廷根市内，半小时达！"] = "The slogan for \"Lightning Delivery\" is—within Tingen, delivered in half an hour!",
    ["“阁下，我们该怎么称呼您？”\n　　阿尔杰微微点头，跟着庄重问道：\n　　“阁下，我们该怎么称呼您？”\n　　周明瑞听得愣了一下，放在青铜长桌上的手指轻轻敲动起来，脑海内霍然闪过了之前占卜的内容。\n　　他往后一靠，收回右手，十指交叉着抵于下巴，微笑看着两人道：\n　　“你们可以称呼我……”\n　　说到这里，他顿了顿，语气轻和而平淡地开口：\n　　“愚者。”\n\n　　——第一卷《小丑》第六章 非凡者"] = "\"Your Excellency, how should we address you?\" \n Alger nodded slightly and followed up solemnly: \n \"Your Excellency, how should we address you?\" \n Zhou Mingrui was stunned for a moment, his fingers tapping gently on the bronze long table, and the content of his previous divination flashed through his mind. \n He leaned back, withdrew his right hand, clasped his fingers together against his chin, and looked at the two of them with a smile: \n \"You may address me as...\" \n Having said this, he paused, and spoke in a gentle and calm tone: \n \"The Fool.\" \n \n —Volume 1 \"Clown\", Chapter 6: Beyonder",
    ["“隐者”"] = "\"The Hermit\"",
    ["“隐者”女士，不用担心，我们无法窥见命运，但我们依然有撼动命运的可能。"] = "Ms. Hermit, do not worry. We cannot glimpse fate, but we still have the possibility of shaking it.",
    ["“隐者”：这次又失败了。这是第十九次死亡，新生者无法承受更多了。"] = "\"The Hermit\": Failed again this time. This is the nineteenth death; the reborn one cannot bear any more.",
    ["“雪幕裁缝”"] = "“Snow-Curtain Tailor”",
    ["“霍纳奇斯……弗雷格拉……”"] = "\"Hornacis... Flegrea...\"",
    ["“霜序小姐”"] = "“Miss Frost-Order”",
    ["“非凡物质”数量过少，无法一键聚合"] = "Insufficient \"Beyonder Material\" quantity, cannot aggregate with one tap",
    ["“鞋子破了要换双新的，必须是廷根水仙花街13号……”呃，这个也算他正常吧。"] = "\"If your shoes are broken, you need to change to a new pair, it must be 13 Daffodil Street, Tingen…\" Uh, I guess this is normal for him.",
    ["“韦尔奇、娜娅、克莱恩，1348年于霍伊大学”。"] = "\"Welch, Naya, Klein, 1348, at Hoy University\".",
    ["“项圈”……"] = "\"Collar\"…",
    ["“顾问”……我知道了，是老崔让你来的。"] = "\"Consultant\"… I see, Old Cui sent you.",
    ["“风信子”"] = "\"Hyacinth\"",
    ["“风信子”女士 有人跟踪我"] = "Ms. \"Hyacinth\", someone is following me.",
    ["“风信子”？她称呼女孩的哥哥为“蒲公英”？"] = "\"Hyacinth\"? She calls the girl's brother \"Dandelion\"?",
    ["“高贵的夫人，这苹果就像您的脸颊一样红润！请您收下它吧，只要两便士！”"] = "\"Noble lady, this apple is as rosy as your cheeks! Please accept it, only two pennies!\"",
    ["“魔女的滋味真不错啊！”——罗塞尔.古斯塔夫"] = "\"The taste of the Witch is truly not bad!\" — Roselle Gustav",
    ["“魔术师”"] = "Magician",
    ["“魔术师”女士"] = "Miss Magician",
    ["“魔术师”女士佛尔思利用空间隐匿能力将部分失控区域隐藏，留下的特殊图腾。"] = "A special totem left behind by Miss Magician Fors after using her space concealment ability to hide parts of the loss of control area.",
    ["“魔术师”女士，对您来说，“愚者”先生是个什么样的存在？"] = "Ms. “Magician”, to you, what kind of existence is Mr. “Fool”?",
    ["“魔术师”女士，对您来说，愚者先生是个什么样的存在？"] = "Ms. Magician, what kind of existence is Mr. Fool to you?",
    ["“魔术师”女士，您小时候……是什么样的？"] = "Ms. “Magician”, what were you like…… when you were a child?",
    ["“魔术师”女士，您的能力是怎么来的？"] = "Ms. “Magician”, how did you obtain your powers?",
    ["“魔术师”女士，我读过您的《暴风山庄》，非常精彩！"] = "Ms. “Magician”, I have read your “Storm Villa”, it is very wonderful!",
    ["“魔术师”小姐"] = "Miss Magician",
    ["“魔术师”小姐托我把这本书带给您。 "] = "Ms. “Magician” asked me to bring this book to you.",
    ["“魔术师”小姐拜托你将一本新上市的小说转交给“月亮”先生。"] = "Miss Magician has asked you to pass a newly released novel to Mr. Moon.",
    ["“魔术师”小姐的信件"] = "Letter from Miss Magician",
    ["“魔术师”小姐的信和托付的书籍，要尽快交给“月亮”先生。"] = "A letter and a book entrusted by Miss Magician, to be delivered to Mr. Moon as soon as possible.",
    ["“魔术师”小姐的委托完成了，我也离开这里吧。"] = "Ms. “Magician”'s commission is complete, I should leave here too.",
    ["“魔术师”小姐的新书"] = "Miss \"Magician\"'s new book",
    ["“魔术师”小姐？您……还好吗？需要帮忙吗？"] = "Miss Magician? Are you... alright? Do you need any help?",
    ["“魔术师”：“正义”女士，按照计划，门已打开。"] = "\"Magician\": Miss Justice, according to the plan, the door has been opened.",
    ["“魔术师”：第二十次，又失败了？意外状况实在太多了。"] = "\"Magician\": The twentieth time, failed again? There are simply too many unexpected situations.",
    ["“黄金梦想号”……"] = "\"Golden Dream\"...",
    ["“黑夜四兄弟姐妹”乐队持续招募新成员中！"] = "The \"Four Siblings of the Night\" band is still recruiting new members!",
    ["“黑夜女神！“……如果祂听见，一定会答应，"] = "\"Evernight Goddess!\"... If She hears, She will surely agree,",
    ["“黑皇帝”向你投来注视。"] = "The Black Emperor is casting his gaze upon you.",
    ["“齿轮咬碎了黄昏的余晖”"] = "\"Gears crush the afterglow of dusk\"",
    ["”正义“女士"] = "Ms. “Justice”",
    ["”知识皇冠”的来源"] = "The origin of the \"Crown of Knowledge\"",
    ["……\n\n46. 伦堡、马锡和费内波特王国的法定金币分别是（     ）、（     ）和（     ）。\n\n47. 罗塞尔大帝陨落于（     ）后，因蒂斯回归（     ）政体。\n \n48. 违背常理、凌乱不对称、喜爱黑色是（     ）的建筑风格特点。\n \n49. 因蒂斯和鲁恩两国以（     ）和（     ）为国界标志物。\n \n50. 二十年战争是指621年爆发的（     ）和（     ）之间的战争，战败国失去了领土（     ）。\n \n\n……"] = "...\n\n 46. The legal gold coins of the Lenburg, Masin, and Feynapotter Kingdoms are (     ), (     ), and (     ) respectively.\n\n 47. After the fall of Emperor Roselle, Intis returned to a (     ) political system.\n \n 48. Violating common sense, messy and asymmetrical, and a preference for black are the architectural characteristics of (     ).\n \n 49. The border markers between Intis and Loen are (     ) and (     ).\n \n 50. The Twenty Years' War refers to the war between (     ) and (     ) that broke out in 621, and the defeated country lost the territory of (     ).\n \n\n...",
    ["……\n\n从七月初起，廷根市儿童失踪事件多次发生，失踪者总人数为<Mark id=\"#159\"> 十三人 </>，其中男孩五人、女孩八人。\n目前已找到三人尸体，并已将凶手捉捕结案。\n但尸检检定致死原因均不同，归属于三例不同的现实普通事件。"] = "...\n \n Since the beginning of July, child disappearance cases have occurred multiple times in Tingen. The total number of missing persons is <Mark id=\"#159\"> thirteen </>, including five boys and eight girls. \n Three bodies have been found so far, and the culprit has been caught and the case closed. \n However, the autopsy results for the cause of death were all different, belonging to three separate ordinary real-world incidents.",
    ["……\n\n暂未发现有非凡能力的残留，已抓获的作案者都是普通人、并无<Hide stylename=\"Transparent\" id=\"#161\">非凡能力</>或持有<Hide stylename=\"Transparent\" id=\"#161\">神奇物品</>，但无法完全排除此案件没有<Hide stylename=\"Transparent\" id=\"#161\">非凡者</>的参与。提议<Tips stylename=\"Letter_Normal\" u=\"4\" id=\"#160\">阿霍瓦郡警察厅特殊行动部第五、六、七小组</>提高警惕，加强巡逻。\n\n……"] = "...\n\n No residual Beyonder abilities have been found yet. The perpetrators who have been captured are all ordinary people, without <Hide stylename=\"Transparent\" id=\"#161\"> Beyonder abilities </> or in possession of <Hide stylename=\"Transparent\" id=\"#161\"> mystical items </>, but it cannot be completely ruled out that this case did not involve <Hide stylename=\"Transparent\" id=\"#161\"> Beyonders </>. It is proposed that the <Tips stylename=\"Letter_Normal\" u=\"4\" id=\"#160\"> 5th, 6th, and 7th squads of the Special Operations Department of the Awwa County Police Department </> increase vigilance and strengthen patrols. \n\n...",
    ["……\n\n目前其余十人依旧下落不明。经过追踪调查，发现相关线索：\n1.失踪儿童年龄区间从八岁到十五岁不等\n2.失踪儿童最后目击出现地点主要在<Mark id=\"#159\"> 西区 </>和<Mark id=\"#159\"> 工厂区 </>。\n3.在案发地点附近，有人听到过疑似<Mark id=\"#159\">笛子 </>的声音。\n4.……"] = "……\n\n Currently, the other ten people remain missing. Following investigation, the following clues have been discovered: \n1. The age range of the missing children is between eight and fifteen years old.\n2. The last sightings of the missing children were mainly in <Mark id=\"#159\"> the West District </> and <Mark id=\"#159\"> the Factory District </>.\n3. Near the crime scenes, someone heard the sound of what is suspected to be a <Mark id=\"#159\"> flute </>.\n4.……",
    ["……1349年6月28日，是今天的新闻。"] = "...June 28, 1349, is today's news.",
    ["……<P_Heart>（他说的话半句也不能信，但我可以借助这个机会把他引诱出来。）</>"] = "...<P_Heart> (I can't believe a word he says, but I can use this opportunity to lure him out.)</>",
    ["……<P_Heart>（刚才我们去过右街？）</>"] = "...<P_Heart> (Did we go to Right Street just now?)</>",
    ["……<P_Heart>（刚才我还在房间里，转眼就出现在这个神秘的地方，难不成……是非凡事件！）</>"] = "...<P_Heart> (I was just in my room a moment ago, and in the blink of an eye, I appeared in this mysterious place. Could it be... a Beyonder incident!) </>",
    ["……<P_Heart>（刚才这里响应了我的想法？我似乎可以利用这片空间。好厉害！）</>"] = "...<P_Heart> (Did this place respond to my thoughts just now? I seem to be able to use this space. How amazing!)</>",
    ["……<P_Heart>（呼噜……）</>"] = "……<P_Heart> (Purr……) </>",
    ["……<P_Heart>（小声嘟囔）</>……究竟是从哪里搞到的材料，我也好想要一双这样的翅膀。"] = "……<P_Heart>(Muttering softly)</>…… Where on earth did you get the materials? I also really want a pair of wings like this.",
    ["……<P_Heart>（松一口气）</>以前我认为呼吸和心跳是生命的象征，但我最近产生很多疑惑。"] = "...<P_Heart> (Sighs in relief) </> I used to think that breathing and heartbeat were symbols of life, but I have had many doubts recently.",
    ["……<P_Heart>（沉默了许久）</>因为我要为我的朋友复仇，所以选择了离开这里，去成长，去变强。"] = "……<P_Heart>(Silent for a long time)</>Because I want to take revenge for my friend, so I chose to leave here, to grow, to become stronger.",
    ["……<P_Heart>（能强制将我拉入这种空间，而我没有察觉到任何异常。从没听过这种可怕的能力……）</>"] = "...<P_Heart> (To be able to forcibly pull me into this kind of space without me noticing any abnormality. I've never heard of such a terrifying ability...) </>",
    ["……<P_Heart>（诡异的笔记，成为值夜者和非凡者……哪件事都没办法跟班森商量。）</>"] = "...<P_Heart> (The eerie notebook, becoming a Nighthawk and a Beyonder... I can't discuss either of these things with Benson.)</>",
    ["……<P_Heart>（这里是哪里？我想做什么？你们又是谁？我也想知道……）</>"] = "...<P_Heart> (Where is this? What do I want to do? Who are you all? I want to know too...)</>",
    ["……<P_Heart>（这里是哪里？我想做什么？我也想知道……）</>"] = "...<P_Heart> (Where is this? What do I want to do? I want to know too...) </>",
    ["……<P_Heart>（邓恩先生那样的非凡者？不，我并不是，我也想知道。）</>"] = "...<P_Heart> (A Beyonder like Mr. Dunn? No, I am not, and I want to know too.)</>",
    ["……<P_Yellow>瑞尔·比伯</>的位置。"] = "...the location of <P_Yellow>Ray Bieber</>.",
    ["……{{PlayerName}}！醒醒！"] = "……{{PlayerName}}! Wake up!",
    ["……{{先生|女士}}，您瞧，我还能说什么呢？"] = "...{{ Mr. | Miss }}, you see, what else can I say?",
    ["……“心脏”对我已经没用了，你拿去完成比赛吧。"] = "…The \"Heart\" is useless to me now, you take it to finish the competition.",
    ["…………我好像明白了。"] = "…………I think I understand.",
    ["……一个彻头彻尾的怪物。请你……帮帮他吧。"] = "...a complete monster. Please... help him.",
    ["……一杯。"] = "……One glass.",
    ["……一袋，两袋……还剩很多啊……"] = "...One bag, two bags... There's still plenty left...",
    ["……三十年后河水在西，不要小瞧贫穷的少年！"] = "...Thirty years of the river flowing west, don't look down on a poor youth!",
    ["……不、不好笑吗？"] = "...W-Wasn't it funny?",
    ["……不。"] = "...No.",
    ["……不会。"] = "……Won't.",
    ["……不像我们想的那样，这里的助学基金足以覆盖我的所有支出。"] = "...It's not what we thought; the scholarship fund here is enough to cover all my expenses.",
    ["……不好意思啊客人，今天刚好卖完了，下次一定。"] = "...Sorry, customer, we just sold out. Definitely next time.",
    ["……不如先向他打听一下。"] = "...Why not ask him about it first?",
    ["……不如我来帮你找找看吧，猫咪阁下？"] = "……Why don't I help you look for it, Your Excellency Cat?",
    ["……不对劲。"] = "...Something's wrong.",
    ["……不打扰了，下次见。"] = "...I won't disturb you, see you next time.",
    ["……不擦，谢谢。"] = "...No shine, thanks.",
    ["……不是眼力不行，我是胃不行，呕……"] = "...It's not my eyesight that's failing, it's my stomach, ugh...",
    ["……不用了，谢谢。"] = "……No need, thank you.",
    ["……不知道她收到请柬了吗？"] = "...I wonder if she received the invitation?",
    ["……不知道，我听旁边那个戴金丝眼镜的叔叔说的，他还说糖里有心理暗示什么的，听不懂。"] = "...I don't know, I heard it from that uncle with the gold-rimmed glasses next to me. He also said something about Psychological Suggestion in the candy, I don't understand.",
    ["……不知道，我是听一个戴眼镜的叔叔说的，他还说什么糖里藏着情绪……他们大人的话就是这样让人听不懂。"] = "...I don't know, I heard it from an uncle with glasses. He also said something about emotions hidden in the candy... Adults' words are always so hard to understand.",
    ["……不知道，这里很安静，不用思考。"] = "……I don't know, it's very quiet here, no need to think.",
    ["……不管怎么说，我不能放任一个超凡生物在外游荡。"] = "……In any case, I cannot leave a Beyonder creature wandering outside.",
    ["……不请自来的客人？"] = "...An uninvited guest?",
    ["……不过也糟糕不到哪里去。"] = "…But it couldn't be any worse.",
    ["……不过，你瞧这只小白猫，我是说，她还挺漂亮，对吧？我把她收养了怎么样？"] = "...However, look at this little white cat, I mean, she's quite pretty, right? How about I adopt her?",
    ["……不！！我的完美反派——我的鲜血盛宴！！"] = "……No!! My perfect villain—my blood feast!!",
    ["……不，不，如果真让他听到有人在议论，我们两个明天就得坐火车逃命去！"] = "...No, no, if he really hears someone talking about it, we'll both have to take a train and run for our lives tomorrow!",
    ["……为什么？"] = "...Why?",
    ["……为你高兴"] = "…Happy for you",
    ["……也可能是哪位绅士，我们没法假设只有女士对这本杂志感兴趣。"] = "...It could also be some gentleman; we cannot assume that only ladies are interested in this magazine.",
    ["……也好，我很少遇到能说话的人，陪我走走吧。"] = "...That's fine, I rarely meet people I can talk to, walk with me.",
    ["……也没什么特别的。我住在贝克兰德桥区的一间小公寓，我和母亲相依为命。"] = "……Nothing special. I lived in a small apartment in the Backlund Bridge district, and my mother and I depended on each other.",
    ["……也许吧。但据我所知，高序列的材料会更加昂贵。"] = "……Perhaps. But as far as I know, materials for higher Sequences are even more expensive.",
    ["……也？"] = "...Huh?",
    ["……亡灵？！"] = "……Undead?!",
    ["……人有时候应该保守点，不能对所有新事物都太好奇。"] = "…Sometimes people should be more conservative and not be too curious about all new things.",
    ["……什么事都叫我分心，让我无法专注于诗歌艺术……"] = "...Everything distracts me, making me unable to focus on the art of poetry...",
    ["……什么情况？"] = "...What's going on?",
    ["……什么时候跑进来的，完全没发现！"] = "……When did you sneak in? I didn't notice you at all!",
    ["……什么时候进来的，完全没发现！"] = "...When did you get in? I didn't notice at all!",
    ["……什么都不需要。"] = "……Don't need anything.",
    ["……什么？"] = "...What?",
    ["……从见到你的第一眼，我就再也挪不开我的视线了。"] = "...From the first moment I saw you, I couldn't take my eyes off you.",
    ["……仔细一看只是前主人吃番茄酱时留下的痕迹。"] = "…Looking closely, it's just a stain left by the previous owner when they were eating ketchup.",
    ["……仔细一看，确实是人偶！"] = "...Looking closely, it really is a doll!",
    ["……他从地上起来了，“诅咒”也算是解除了吧。"] = "……He got up from the ground, the “Curse” can be considered lifted, right?",
    ["……他几年前去世了。"] = "……He passed away a few years ago.",
    ["……他刚才的表情，也有点不对劲？"] = "…His expression just now, was it also a bit off?",
    ["……他又迟到了。<P_Heart>  (苦笑)</> 不对，是我又忘了，他已经不会来了。 "] = "…He's late again. <P_Heart> (bitter smile) </> No, I forgot again, he won't be coming anymore.",
    ["……他真的不想见我。"] = "...He really doesn't want to see me.",
    ["……他睡着了。"] = "…He fell asleep.",
    ["……他离开了。"] = "...He left.",
    ["……他说……孤儿需要救赎……只要追随真实造物主……我们都可以回到……自己的家……"] = "...He said... orphans need salvation... as long as you follow the True Creator... we can all return... to our own home...",
    ["……他还是死了好。"] = "……It's better that he's dead.",
    ["……以后不看了。"] = "...I won't watch it anymore.",
    ["……伟大的圣者来到这片充满纷争的土地，用怜悯炼成金黄的树叶，以慈爱抚慰疮痍的大地。"] = "…The great Saint came to this land full of strife, refining golden leaves with compassion and soothing the scarred earth with kindness.",
    ["……伦纳德先生？伦纳德先生？"] = "...Mr. Leonard? Mr. Leonard?",
    ["……似乎是个住所？"] = "...Seems to be a residence?",
    ["……但你看起来好像有些难过。"] = "...But you look a bit sad.",
    ["……但弄湿裙子妈妈要生气的。"] = "...But Mom will be angry if I get my dress wet.",
    ["……但您的<P_Yellow>脱发</>太严重了，我实在无能为力。"] = "...But your <P_Yellow>hair loss</> is too severe, I really can't do anything about it.",
    ["……但愿吧。可我不希望她跟着我受苦，更不希望她被困在这里，像我们一样，永远看不到外面的世界。"] = "...I hope so. But I don't want her to suffer with me, and I don't want her to be trapped here, like us, never seeing the world outside.",
    ["……但我不敢高声说话，唯恐惊扰了天上诸神的安眠。"] = "...But I dare not speak loudly, for fear of disturbing the Slumber of the Gods in the heavens.",
    ["……但抱歉，我真的想要回家。"] = "...But sorry, I really want to go home.",
    ["……你一个人全都说完了啊！"] = "...You said it all by yourself!",
    ["……你一个人，没问题吗？"] = "...Are you alright on your own?",
    ["……你为什么觉得我会抓你？"] = "...Why do you think I would catch you?",
    ["……你也买了票？"] = "...You bought a ticket too?",
    ["……你令我很失望……"] = "...You disappoint me...",
    ["……你们不懂，你们从来不想懂。"] = "……You don't understand, you never want to understand.",
    ["……你们在干什么？"] = "……What are you doing?",
    ["……你刚刚讲了个笑话？"] = "...Did you just tell a joke?",
    ["……你占卜的结果是对的吗？"] = "……Is the result of your divination correct?",
    ["……你在胡说，师父是正经的钟表匠人，他怎么可能——"] = "...You are talking nonsense, Master is a proper clockmaker, how could he possibly—",
    ["……你对查尔斯少爷就这么好吗？"] = "...Are you really that good to Master Charles?",
    ["……你就失踪在这片水里，三十年了，我每天给你送东西，你也不愿意回来见见我……"] = "…You went missing in this water thirty years ago, I bring you things every day, but you don't want to come back to see me…",
    ["……你就是新来的家伙，弗莱警官的手下？"] = "...You're the new guy, Frye's subordinate?",
    ["……你开始挣扎了"] = "…You have started to struggle",
    ["……你快参加面试了，我给你做豌豆炖羔羊肉。"] = "...You are about to have an interview, I will make you pea stewed lamb.",
    ["……你想见我的父亲？但工厂已经委托给我管理了，我也不知道盒饭怎么会变成这样。"] = "...You want to see my father? But the factory has already been entrusted to me to manage, and I don't know how the boxed lunches ended up like this either.",
    ["……你投到过吗？"] = "...Have you ever cast it?",
    ["……你昨天不是问过吗？"] = "……Didn't you ask yesterday?",
    ["……你替八个人祈祷？"] = "…You are praying for eight people?",
    ["……你的解读别具一格。"] = "...Your interpretation is quite unique.",
    ["……你真好，亲爱的，能再帮我做一件事吗？"] = "……You are so kind, my dear. Could you do one more thing for me?",
    ["……你真爱赌"] = "...You really love to gamble",
    ["……你继续计划，我自己找。"] = "...You continue with your plan, I'll look for it myself.",
    ["……你能陪我喝到第几杯？"] = "…How many drinks can you keep up with me for?",
    ["……你被骂不冤。"] = "...You deserve to be scolded.",
    ["……你说什么？"] = "……What did you say?",
    ["……你说呢？"] = "…What do you think?",
    ["……你说想和我组队参赛，还算数吗？"] = "…You said you wanted to team up with me for the competition, does that still count?",
    ["……你说，这滑梯结实吗？"] = "...Tell me, is this slide sturdy?",
    ["……你还真会起名字。"] = "……You really know how to name things.",
    ["……你这是扫地还是打架？发力轻一点，核心要稳……"] = "...Are you sweeping the floor or starting a fight? Use less force, keep your core steady...",
    ["……先别说这些，快下来吧，呃，我原谅你。"] = "...Let's not talk about that for now, come down quickly, uh, I forgive you.",
    ["……先找个地方坐坐，我有点撑不住了。 "] = "...Let's find a place to sit first; I can't hold on much longer.",
    ["……先离开吧"] = "...Let's leave first",
    ["……入职结束了，我们这两位老朋友，也要叙叙旧了。"] = "...The onboarding is over, and we two old friends should also catch up.",
    ["……再见……海伦娜……"] = "……Goodbye……Helena……",
    ["……再见。"] = "……Goodbye.",
    ["……准确地说，在等它回来。"] = "...To be precise, I'm waiting for it to return.",
    ["……几点了？"] = "…What time is it?",
    ["……刚才的状态很奇怪，也许它的精神影响还没散去。我必须再次向你的提醒表示感谢。"] = "…The state just now was very strange; perhaps its mental influence hasn't dissipated yet. I must thank you again for your reminder.",
    ["……别逼我骂人。"] = "...Don't force me to curse.",
    ["……别那样看着我，我可没有斯普林那种特殊癖好。我喜欢待在这里，是因为我的朋友们都在。"] = "……Don't look at me like that, I don't have that special hobby of Spring's. I like staying here because my friends are all here.",
    ["……别那样看着我，我可没有斯普林那种特殊癖好。我申请看守这里，是因为我的朋友们都在。"] = "…Don't look at me like that, I don't have that special hobby like Spring. I applied to guard this place because my friends are all here.",
    ["……别，别让它们跑出去！"] = "...Don't, don't let them run out!",
    ["……到底谁在买？"] = "...Who exactly is buying?",
    ["……加油"] = "...Good luck",
    ["……勉强的解释。我对美食的态度没有变，我会如实报道今天发现的疑问……但是，你不想证明自己对厨艺的态度没有改变吗……厨王之王？"] = "...A forced explanation. My attitude toward gourmet food hasn't changed, I will report the questions I discovered today truthfully... but, don't you want to prove that your attitude toward culinary arts hasn't changed... King of Chefs?",
    ["……十五个便士，十六个便士，十七个便士……"] = "...Fifteen pennies, sixteen pennies, seventeen pennies...",
    ["……原本它已经被封印了，妥善保管的情况下不会造成新的损害，但，我和同伴受到了它们的蛊惑……"] = "…Originally it had already been sealed, and it wouldn't have caused any new damage if kept properly, but my companions and I were bewitched by them…",
    ["……原来海蒂扔戒指时我心口一痛，是戒指掉进了口袋…… "] = "...So when Heidi threw the ring, my heart ached because the ring had fallen into my pocket...",
    ["……原来真正的笔友是——大叔？！"] = "...So the real pen pal is—the uncle?!",
    ["……原谅我的失态。十几年过去了，我终于走到了这里。"] = "...Forgive my lack of composure. After more than ten years, I have finally arrived here.",
    ["……去年这个时候，您还夸我的花是东区最好的花。"] = "...At this time last year, you even praised my flowers as the best in the East District.",
    ["……发生了什么？我怎么会在这里？"] = "...What happened? Why am I here?",
    ["……只会让你再次跪在地上，看着血流成河。"] = "……It will only make you kneel on the ground again, watching the blood flow like a river.",
    ["……可以是可以。"] = "...It can work.",
    ["……可恶！"] = "...Damn it!",
    ["……可惜神不会创造同样的灵魂两次。"] = "……It's a pity that God will not create the same soul twice.",
    ["……可惜，哦不，我是说，那太美好，可惜我不能，不对，是他没有……不对……"] = "……What a pity, oh no, I mean, that was so beautiful, it's a pity I can't, no, it's that he didn't… no…",
    ["……可是上次带头罢工的，年终奖金被扣完了。"] = "...But the last person who led a strike had their year-end bonus deducted entirely.",
    ["……可是我爸爸就是不懂。"] = "...But my dad just doesn't understand.",
    ["……可能您坐过我的马车，女士。"] = "……Perhaps you have ridden in my carriage, Madam.",
    ["……听起来，你这份工作干得很辛苦。"] = "…Sounds like you're working very hard at this job.",
    ["……呃……好痛，这么快就发作了吗……"] = "...Uh... it hurts, has it started so soon...",
    ["……呃。"] = "……Uh.",
    ["……呃，手持……<P_Heart> （翻找）</>……奇怪……放哪去了……"] = "…Uh, holding… <P_Heart> (rummaging) </>… Strange… where did I put it…",
    ["……呃，阁、阁下，或许您……"] = "...Uh, Your, Your Excellency, perhaps you...",
    ["……告诉贝尔纳黛殿下……"] = "……Tell Her Highness Bernadette……",
    ["……呵，你身上没有老鼠的味道。"] = "...Heh, you don't smell like a rat.",
    ["……呼……呼……"] = "...Hoo... hoo...",
    ["……呼，梦中并没有更多的信息。"] = "...Phew, there was no more information in the dream.",
    ["……和客人的数量差不多吧，我、我会成为全廷根最幽默的咖啡师的。"] = "...It's about the same as the number of customers. I, I will become the most humorous barista in all of Tingen.",
    ["……和您交谈真是愉悦的体验。"] = "...It is truly a pleasant experience to converse with you.",
    ["……和我吗？呃……我，抱歉，我有些紧张。"] = "...With me? Uh... I, sorry, I'm a bit nervous.",
    ["……咖啡是老尼尔推荐的口味，尝尝看。"] = "…Coffee is the flavor recommended by Old Neil, try it.",
    ["……咳咳，总之，这一切绝不会是我的技术问题。"] = "...Ahem, anyway, this is definitely not a technical issue on my part.",
    ["……咳，好重的血腥味。"] = "……Cough, such a heavy smell of blood.",
    ["……哈哈"] = "...Haha",
    ["……哈哈。"] = "……Haha.",
    ["……哈哈哈……"] = "...Hahaha...",
    ["……哎呀，忘记你还在这里了。"] = "...Oh my, forgot you were still here.",
    ["……哎，那位男士叫艾德蒙，是黛西小姐的心上人，但埃尔顿子爵和夫人始终反对。"] = "...Hey, that gentleman is named Edmund, he is Miss Daisy's sweetheart, but Viscount Elton and his wife have always opposed it.",
    ["……哥、哥哥！木偶怎么……动了？！"] = "...Brother, big brother! How did the puppet... move?!",
    ["……哦，怎么会发生这样的事，简直是灾难！"] = "……Oh, how could such a thing happen? It's simply a disaster!",
    ["……哦，想要加入罗塞尔大帝的探索队，当然要好好准备。"] = "……Oh, if you want to join Emperor Roselle's Exploration team, you must prepare well.",
    ["……哦，是昨天买我玫瑰花的客人。您今天也需要玫瑰吗？最新鲜的玫瑰，刚从树上采摘下来的。"] = "...Oh, it's the customer who bought my roses yesterday. Do you need roses today too? The freshest roses, just picked from the tree.",
    ["……哦，请原谅，没有留意到您的到来，我再占用这里一小会就好。"] = "...Oh, please forgive me, I didn't notice your arrival. I'll just occupy this space for a little while longer.",
    ["……哪里……来不及……"] = "……Where…… it's too late……",
    ["……哭声？"] = "...Crying?",
    ["……唉。"] = "...Sigh.",
    ["……唤醒他，让他从痛苦中解脱吧。"] = "...Awaken him and let him be released from his pain.",
    ["……唯有亲眼所见的恶徒鲜血，才能换得泰利和奥莉薇的安息。"] = "……Only the blood of the evildoers seen with my own eyes can earn Terry and Olivia their rest.",
    ["……啊。"] = "...Ah.",
    ["……啊啊啊啊啊啊，我不想坐牢啊！"] = "...Ahhhhh, I don't want to go to jail!",
    ["……啊？"] = "...Huh?",
    ["……啊？这个……我似乎没什么印象了。"] = "…Huh? This… I don't seem to have any impression of it.",
    ["……啾唧……"] = "...Chirp...",
    ["……喂，你借封印物的时候，尽量对他们好点……不要淋到雨。"] = "…Hey, when you borrow a Sealed Artifact, try to be nice to them… don't let them get rained on.",
    ["……喵。"] = "...Meow.",
    ["……嗝……呃。"] = "...*Hic*... Ugh.",
    ["……嗬……报幕……员……"] = "...Hah... Announcer...",
    ["……嗯……好……"] = "……Hmm…… okay……",
    ["……嗯。买香水的顾客，过几天多半会来退货。"] = "…Hmm. Customers who buy perfume will mostly come to return it in a few days.",
    ["……嗯，嗯？！"] = "…Hmm, huh?!",
    ["……嗯，没有我爱吃的。"] = "...Hmm, nothing I like to eat.",
    ["……嘿嘿。"] = "……Hehe.",
    ["……嘿嘿，现在我每天都会处理一下衣物，盖住了味道，大家就会和我说话了吧？"] = "…Hehe, now I deal with my clothes every day, covering up the smell, will everyone talk to me then?",
    ["……噢，一点也不好，我的小猫在捉老鼠时摔进湖里淹死了。"] = "…Oh, it's not good at all, my kitten fell into the lake and drowned while catching a mouse.",
    ["……因为在等待戈多？"] = "……Because of waiting for Godot?",
    ["……因为我不想结业。结业考试之后，我就要去城里生活了。老师说，这是为了让我得到更好的教育。"] = "...Because I don't want to graduate. After the final exam, I have to go live in the city. The teacher said this is so I can get a better education.",
    ["……在这一点上，我后悔与蒸汽教会走得太近。"] = "……On this point, I regret getting too close to the Church of Steam.",
    ["……在这种情况下，借和贷必定共存，二者也必定等价……"] = "...In this situation, borrowing and lending must coexist, and both must be equivalent...",
    ["……城市？"] = "……City?",
    ["……多余的事就少打听。"] = "...Don't ask about things that don't concern you.",
    ["……大白天的，这是可以直接说的吗！"] = "...In broad daylight, is this something that can be said directly!",
    ["……太独特了，我还是喜欢吃普通口味。"] = "…It's too unique, I still prefer the regular flavor.",
    ["……夫人，您认错人了。我只是个过路的旅人。"] = "...Ma'am, you have mistaken me for someone else. I am just a passing traveler.",
    ["……头好疼……"] = "...My head hurts so much...",
    ["……女士，我完全理解您，别担心，我会制定完美计划！"] = "...Ms., I completely understand you, don't worry, I will formulate the perfect plan!",
    ["……女神啊，我觉得他们不会聘用你的。"] = "...Oh Goddess, I don't think they will hire you.",
    ["……她、他……他们都……呕……"] = "...She, he... they all... ugh...",
    ["……好。不要逞强，我去找西迦他们支援。"] = "...Alright. Don't push yourself; I'll go find Xiga and the others for support.",
    ["……好了！"] = "……Alright!",
    ["……好吧。我有个朋友患上<P_Yellow>沉睡症</>，我要用“心脏”调配药剂治疗她。"] = "……Alright. I have a friend suffering from <P_Yellow>Somnolence Disorder</>, and I need to use a “Heart” to concoct a potion to treat her.",
    ["……好吧。我来这里只是不想回去擦瓷器，以及——"] = "...Fine. I came here just because I didn't want to go back to polish the porcelain, and—",
    ["……好吧，你想去哪？过会儿陪你去。"] = "……Alright, where do you want to go? I'll accompany you in a while.",
    ["……好吧，你有成为政客的潜力。"] = "...Well, you have the potential to be a politician.",
    ["……好吧，我帮你找。"] = "...Alright, I'll help you look for it.",
    ["……好吧，至少收获了一块肉。"] = "...Alright, at least I got a piece of meat.",
    ["……好吧，那你在这里干什么？"] = "……Alright, then what are you doing here?",
    ["……好吧，那我去劝劝伊琳。"] = "...Alright, then I will go and persuade Irene.",
    ["……好吧，那我试试。"] = "……Alright, I'll give it a try.",
    ["……好孩子，安息吧。"] = "...Good child, rest in peace.",
    ["……好想喝“焦糖炸弹”！"] = "...I really want to drink a 'Caramel Bomb'!",
    ["……好的。"] = "...Okay.",
    ["……好酸的情诗，不知道跟着小狗能不能找到主人？"] = "…What a cheesy love poem, I wonder if I can find the owner by following the puppy?",
    ["……好陌生，我为什么会在这里？"] = "...How strange, why am I here?",
    ["……好，下路，快！安妮，跟紧本杰明，我来把路打开。"] = "…Alright, bottom lane, quick! Annie, stick close to Benjamin, I'll open the path.",
    ["……好，我愿意相信您。我们开始吧，让我想想……"] = "...Fine, I'm willing to trust you. Let's begin, let me think...",
    ["……如果您不相信，可以到处打听，您会知道这片街区到底有多安全。"] = "……If you don't believe me, you can ask around; you will know just how safe this neighborhood is.",
    ["……如果是真爱，也未必不行。"] = "…If it's true love, it might not be impossible.",
    ["……如果是这样，那事情就不好办了。"] = "……If that's the case, then things will be difficult to handle.",
    ["……如果有人愿意干的话，也不是不行。"] = "…If someone is willing to do it, it's not impossible.",
    ["……如果病床上的亲人拖垮了你的耐心、你的生活、甚至你的爱，你会怎么对待他呢？"] = "...If a loved one on their deathbed drains your patience, your life, and even your love, how would you treat them?",
    ["……学会系鞋带了吗？这次没人帮你了……别被绊倒了……"] = "……Have you learned to tie your shoelaces? No one is here to help you this time…… don't get tripped up……",
    ["……它叫“咕噜噜”，是我的信使，不，朋友。"] = "…It's called \"Gulu,\" it's my messenger, no, my friend.",
    ["……安全屋有危险！"] = "……The Safe House is in danger!",
    ["……安全起见，不能叫醒他，必须先送他回去。"] = "……For safety's sake, we cannot wake him; we must send him back first.",
    ["……对。每一个来买瓜的，都是。"] = "……Yes. Everyone who comes to buy melons is.",
    ["……对不起，我太冲动了。今天我所有的计划都被打破了，这一点都不符合我的计……"] = "...I'm sorry, I was too impulsive. All my plans for today have been ruined, this doesn't fit my pla...",
    ["……对了，她会回来吗？"] = "...By the way, will she come back?",
    ["……对了，我有个办法。"] = "...Right, I have an idea.",
    ["……对了，试试书里那首歌！"] = "……Right, let's try that song from the book!",
    ["……小戴莉，是戴莉吗？"] = "...Little Daly, is that Daly?",
    ["……小阿诺德这几年，过得怎么样？"] = "...How has little Arnold been these past few years?",
    ["……尖尖的，有点像一根手指？等等，它开始扇我了！"] = "...Pointy, kind of like a finger? Wait, it's starting to slap me!",
    ["……尤朵拉……在等……阿诺德……回家……"] = "...Yodora... is waiting for... Arnold... to come home...",
    ["……就在这里？"] = "……Right here?",
    ["……就这一晚上，别叫我太太。行吗？"] = "...Just for tonight, don't call me 'Ma'am'. Can you do that?",
    ["……尼尔？"] = "…Neil?",
    ["……居然如此华丽精美，完全是我的那些珍藏衣饰比不过的……不，只是差一点点……好吧，差挺多的。"] = "……To be so gorgeous and exquisite, it's completely incomparable to my treasured clothing and accessories…… No, it's just a little bit worse…… Alright, it's quite a bit worse.",
    ["……左……好的！"] = "...Left... Alright!",
    ["……已经等了很久吗？"] = "...Have you been waiting for a long time?",
    ["……布雷登，你说的那场战争——"] = "……Braden, that war you mentioned——",
    ["……希望莱纳老爷原谅我对这把可怜门锁的所作所为，毕竟这都是为了调查。"] = "…I hope Mr. Rayner will forgive me for what I did to this poor door lock; after all, it was all for the sake of the investigation.",
    ["……带我去找伊妮德"] = "...Take me to Enid",
    ["……很久很久以前，在……在……"] = "...A long, long time ago, in... in...",
    ["……很抱歉，这道菜并不在菜单上，我也很久没做过章鱼了。"] = "...I'm very sorry, this dish is not on the menu, and I haven't cooked octopus in a long time either.",
    ["……很特殊的人。"] = "...A very special person.",
    ["……很遗憾"] = "...What a pity",
    ["……很高兴看到你出现在这里。"] = "……I'm very happy to see you here.",
    ["……必须……挣脱……不然……会死……"] = "……Must……break free……otherwise……I will die……",
    ["……快跑。"] = "...Run.",
    ["……怎么会如此华丽精美？之前我以为私人高端定制的翅膀就足够完美了，如今看来在这双翅膀面前简直不堪一击。"] = "……How could it be so gorgeous and exquisite? I previously thought that private high-end custom wings were perfect enough, but now they seem vulnerable in front of this pair of wings.",
    ["……怎么哭得更厉害了？不是说格尔曼能止住小孩的哭嚎吗，唉，我可不擅长哄孩子啊……"] = "……Why is it crying even harder? Didn't they say Gehrman could stop a child's wailing? Sigh, I'm not good at coaxing children……",
    ["……怎么回事？"] = "...What's going on?",
    ["……总之，一切都弄清楚了。那就离开这里吧。"] = "……Anyway, everything is clear now. Let's leave this place.",
    ["……总之，下楼梯后沿主路走，迷路了就回到主路。"] = "...In short, walk along the main road after going downstairs, and if you get lost, return to the main road.",
    ["……总之，后来家里就没了收入，但好在我找到了这份工作，替那边的富家公子卖票。"] = "...Anyway, later the family lost its income, but fortunately I found this job, selling tickets for the rich young master over there.",
    ["……您最好不要知道。"] = "...You'd better not know.",
    ["……您有这样的心态做什么都会成功的。"] = "...You will succeed in whatever you do with such a mindset.",
    ["……您看出来了？这是我自己做着玩的小东西。"] = "……You noticed? This is a little something I made for fun.",
    ["……您确定她会喜欢这个“回报”吗？"] = "……Are you sure she will like this “reward”?",
    ["……您觉得怎么样？"] = "...What do you think?",
    ["……情趣……海盗女王和贵族小姐……"] = "...Romantic interest... Pirate Queen and noble lady...",
    ["……情？"] = "…Feeling?",
    ["……感觉像是有一层新的感官在慢慢展开。"] = "…It feels like a new layer of senses is slowly unfolding.",
    ["……感谢你的聆听，休息时间结束，我要继续演奏了。"] = "...Thank you for listening, break time is over, I have to continue playing.",
    ["……愿她安眠。"] = "…May she rest in peace.",
    ["……我不可以想。"] = "...I cannot think.",
    ["……我不流鼻涕"] = "...I don't have a runny nose",
    ["……我不能多说，但是，超过一万镑，关于铁。"] = "...I cannot say much, but, over ten thousand pounds, regarding iron.",
    ["……我不能选择跟着殿下吗？"] = "……Can I not choose to follow Her Highness?",
    ["……我为我之前的无礼向您致歉。您是对的……我很佩服。"] = "...I apologize for my previous rudeness. You are right... I admire you.",
    ["……我乞求女神的力量……我期待黑夜的眷顾……"] = "...I pray for the power of the Evernight Goddess... I look forward to the favor of the night...",
    ["……我也想知道。你看我的发型，这像没事吗？我本来有一头飘逸的秀发……"] = "...I want to know too. Look at my hairstyle, does this look like nothing is wrong? I originally had a head of flowing, beautiful hair...",
    ["……我也是。"] = "...Me too.",
    ["……我们一定要这么不务正业吗？"] = "…Must we be so unprofessional?",
    ["……我们可以探索并建立针对空间传送的数学模型。"] = "…We can explore and build a mathematical model for spatial teleportation.",
    ["……我们都看到了。"] = "……We all saw it.",
    ["……我会尽力的。"] = "……I will do my best.",
    ["……我再考虑考虑吧。"] = "...Let me think about it some more.",
    ["……我准备在你身上尝试一个新的仪式魔法了，你这个恶心的小家伙！"] = "...I am preparing to try a new Ritual Magic on you, you disgusting little thing!",
    ["……我刚刚是不是听到猫说话了？"] = "……Did I just hear a cat talk?",
    ["……我刚刚看见，我的助手在路口缠着一个穿风衣的人， 不会就是……"] = "…I just saw my assistant pestering someone in a trench coat at the intersection, it couldn't be…",
    ["……我刚才在想，是不是因为我们想自己开店，想要摆脱原来的生活，才遭受了这些不幸。"] = "...I was just thinking, is it because we wanted to open our own shop and escape our previous lives that we suffered these misfortunes?",
    ["……我只押一点点钱，就一点点，绝对不会影响生活，嘿嘿。"] = "...I'll only bet a little bit of money, just a little, it definitely won't affect my life, hehe.",
    ["……我只是一个路过的充满正义感的普通市民。难道说这一切只是一场戏吗？！"] = "...I'm just a passing ordinary citizen with a sense of Justice. Could it be that all of this is just a play?!",
    ["……我向你奉上我的血肉、我的发肤，请赐予这里……"] = "……I offer you my flesh and blood, my hair and skin, please grant this place……",
    ["……我在这里盯着你。如果我的同事来了，你一定要走。"] = "...I am watching you here. If my colleague comes, you must leave.",
    ["……我好像明白了，黑荆棘安保公司是一个伪装？"] = "...I seem to understand, is the Blackthorn Security Company a disguise?",
    ["……我学会了阿诺德的歌，阿诺德也喜欢我……家人、跟我走……"] = "...I learned Arnold's song, and Arnold likes me too... Family, come with me...",
    ["……我家里已经没人了。"] = "……There's no one left in my family.",
    ["……我居然真的帮别人抓过老鼠？我？！怎么可能！"] = "……Did I actually help someone catch a mouse? Me?! How is that possible!",
    ["……我已经醒来，收到了你所有的信……"] = "……I have already awakened and received all your letters……",
    ["……我带着浑浑噩噩的记忆苏醒了很多次，至少这次我记得他。"] = "……I have awakened many times with muddled memories, but at least this time, I remember him.",
    ["……我很喜欢少爷，毕竟在这个世上没有什么事比做仆人更让我快活了。"] = "...I like the young master very much; after all, there is nothing in this world that makes me happier than being a servant.",
    ["……我必须确认，湖灵会造成什么危害？它是否损伤过你们的身体或精神？"] = "...I must confirm, what harm does the Lake Spirit cause? Has it damaged your body or mind?",
    ["……我怎么知道你们合约是真是假！反正……反正扣得太狠了……算我倒霉！"] = "...How would I know if your contract is real or fake! Anyway... anyway, the deduction was too harsh... consider me unlucky!",
    ["……我想做一名蒸汽机械师。"] = "……I want to be a Steam Mechanic.",
    ["……我想做得更好。"] = "……I want to do better.",
    ["……我想活，想一直一直活，但我们有活路吗？只要活着，就要过这种日子吗？"] = "……I want to live, I want to live on and on, but do we have a way out? As long as we're alive, must we live like this?",
    ["……我手上有两份序列9的魔药配方，“水手”和“观众”。"] = "...I have two Sequence 9 potion formulas on hand, \"Sailor\" and \"Spectator\".",
    ["……我才是这里的管家。"] = "...I am the butler here.",
    ["……我把我所有的钱都拿去……投资……"] = "……I took all my money to…… invest……",
    ["……我拒绝。"] = "……I refuse.",
    ["……我教你一个买水果的技巧吧。"] = "……Let me teach you a trick for buying fruit.",
    ["……我明白了。情况确实不乐观。"] = "…I understand. The situation is indeed not optimistic.",
    ["……我明白了！"] = "…I understand!",
    ["……我明白了，这十几年，你隐瞒了真实身份，和最重要的事——"] = "…I understand. For these past ten-plus years, you have hidden your true identity and the most important thing—",
    ["……我明白的，值夜者的死亡率一直都很高。"] = "...I understand, the mortality rate of Nighthawks has always been very high.",
    ["……我是正式送货员，不是学徒送货员。"] = "...I am an official courier, not an Apprentice courier.",
    ["……我是韦尔奇的朋友。"] = "……I am a friend of Welch.",
    ["……我有一条钻石项链，想找你交易。"] = "...I have a diamond necklace, I'd like to trade it with you.",
    ["……我没有察觉到，我确实处理得不太妥当。"] = "...I didn't notice, I really didn't handle it properly.",
    ["……我猜，还是拒绝？"] = "...I guess, refuse it after all?",
    ["……我的一生都在被知识追逐，可我又哪里不是一生都在追逐知识呢？"] = "……My whole life has been spent being chased by knowledge, but haven't I also spent my whole life chasing knowledge?",
    ["……我的好伙伴，我会向协会申请的。"] = "...My good Partner, I will apply to the Association.",
    ["……我的梦和灵感告诉我，就是这里。"] = "...My dream and Inspiration tell me that this is the place.",
    ["……我的琴声能让人分手？"] = "……My piano playing can make people break up?",
    ["……我看见了……真的是一个很好很好的——"] = "……I saw it…… it really was a very, very good—",
    ["……我真的想好了吗？或许审查的消息是假的呢？女神啊，请告诉我命运的指示吧……"] = "...Have I really thought it through? What if the news about the audit is fake? Goddess, please show me the guidance of fate...",
    ["……我知道了。谢谢你，弗莱先生！"] = "…I see. Thank you, Mr. Frye!",
    ["……我知道要怎么越狱了，原来这么简单！"] = "...I know how to break out of prison now, it's actually so simple!",
    ["……我知道，让我一个人呆着吧，{{先生|女士}}。"] = "...I know, let me be alone, {Mr.{Ms.|}}.",
    ["……我终于明白了让<Letter_Highlight_HW>“它”</>活过来的办法……是的，它会永远陪着我！……"] = "……I finally understand the way to make <Letter_Highlight_HW>\"It\"</> come alive…… Yes, It will stay with me forever!……",
    ["……我能够理解您现在的感受，或许没人能比我更理解。"] = "...I can understand how you feel right now; perhaps no one understands it better than I do.",
    ["……我被辞退了。"] = "...I was fired.",
    ["……我被驯兽师占卜了命运？"] = "...Was my fate divined by a Beast Tamer?",
    ["……我要去买更多能让自己时尚的珠宝！"] = "...I'm going to buy more jewelry to make myself fashionable!",
    ["……我这样？"] = "……Like this?",
    ["……我送您过去吧，再熟悉的路也可能遇到意外。"] = "...I'll escort you over, even familiar roads can have accidents.",
    ["……我，我会控制好它们的……我尽快！"] = "...I, I will keep them under control... I will as soon as possible!",
    ["……我？"] = "...Me?",
    ["……或许我们不该与那样低劣的境况相比——哦该死！我发誓刚才有只大蜘蛛爬过你的帽檐！"] = "...Perhaps we shouldn't compare ourselves to such inferior circumstances—oh, damn it! I swear a big spider just crawled over the brim of your hat!",
    ["……或许贝尔纳黛殿下会喜欢。"] = "……Perhaps Her Highness Bernadette would like it.",
    ["……战争带来的伤害仍未平息。"] = "……The damage caused by the war has yet to subside.",
    ["……所以你怀疑与阿诺德在一起的“朋友”——尤朵拉就是儿童失踪案的犯人？"] = "...So you suspect that the \"friend\" with Arnold—Yodora—is the culprit behind the child abduction case?",
    ["……所以你这个月又攒不下钱了。"] = "...So you couldn't save any money this month either.",
    ["……所以，你用愚者福音，交换别人为你完成论文？"] = "...So, you used the Gospel of the Fool to exchange for others to complete your thesis?",
    ["……所以？"] = "...So?",
    ["……报幕员在最后一幕里问过：故事的走向，是否如你所愿？你的命运，又是谁在支配？"] = "…The narrator asked in the final act: Did the story unfold as you wished? And who is it that controls your destiny?",
    ["……抱歉。"] = "……Sorry.",
    ["……抱歉，我失态了。"] = "...Sorry, I lost my composure.",
    ["……抱歉，我失态了，我刚把学生们的结业试卷收上来，那个小混蛋——<P_Yellow>罗丁</>突然跳起来，叫着要去厕所。"] = "...Sorry, I lost my composure. I just collected the students' final exam papers, and that little brat—<P_Yellow>Rodin</>—suddenly jumped up, shouting that he had to go to the bathroom.",
    ["……抱，抱歉，我……我不……那个，擅长接、接待……别在意。"] = "...So, sorry, I... I don't... well, I'm not good at, at receiving... don't mind me.",
    ["……拆散"] = "…Tear apart",
    ["……拜托，该尖叫的人是我吧。"] = "...Please, I should be the one screaming.",
    ["……拿着它，你会回家的……孩子。"] = "……Take it, you will go home…… child.",
    ["……搞错了？什么意思……罗珊有危险？！"] = "……A mistake? What do you mean…… Is Rozanne in danger?!",
    ["……无上的女神啊，请您庇佑菲尔德家族。"] = "...Supreme Goddess, please protect the Feild Family.",
    ["……无妨。我已经达成了我的目的。"] = "…No matter. I have already achieved my goal.",
    ["……既然被你发现了，我就对你坦白吧。"] = "...Since you've discovered it, I'll be honest with you.",
    ["……时间过得真快啊。"] = "……Time flies so fast.",
    ["……是。"] = "……Yes.",
    ["……是你呀。"] = "……It's you.",
    ["……是啊，我发誓要守护罗塞尔大帝发明的下水道系统。"] = "...Yeah, I swore to guard the sewer system invented by Emperor Roselle.",
    ["……是我冒失了。"] = "...It was my rashness.",
    ["……是我出现幻觉了吗……居然能在这种地方，听到这么好听的旋律……"] = "…Am I hallucinating… to actually hear such a beautiful melody in a place like this…",
    ["……是我误会了。"] = "…I misunderstood.",
    ["……是的，我很能够理解你，克莱恩先生。那是我们共同的故乡，我也常常会怀念起那时候的日子。"] = "……Yes, I can very much understand you, Mr. Klein. That is our shared hometown, and I often miss the days back then.",
    ["……是酒？你跟你的酒过日子去吧！"] = "……Is it alcohol? Go live your life with your alcohol!",
    ["……晚安，会长。"] = "……Good night, President.",
    ["……晚安，院长。"] = "…Good night, Dean.",
    ["……普通人调查失控非凡者，你应该庆幸自己还活着。但你的状态……"] = "…For an ordinary person to investigate a Beyonder who has lost control, you should be thankful you are still alive. But your condition…",
    ["……普通人调查失控非凡者，你应该庆幸自己还活着。让我看看你的状态。"] = "…For an ordinary person to investigate a Beyonder who has lost control, you should be thankful you are still alive. Let me check your condition.",
    ["……最近有人举报莱纳工厂传出了奇怪的声音，难道就是这个？"] = "...Someone recently reported strange noises coming from the Leiner Factory. Could this be it?",
    ["……朋友，你可能是误会了，我真的没有危害"] = "...Friend, you might have misunderstood; I really pose no threat.",
    ["……杀害韦尔奇先生和娜娅女士的罪犯已全部落网，相信蔓延在廷根的恐慌气氛将得到缓解……"] = "...The criminals who murdered Mr. Welch and Ms. Naya have all been apprehended. I believe the atmosphere of Horror spreading through Tingen will be alleviated...",
    ["……杰瑞米去哪了？怎么不来帮我们发牌。"] = "…Where did Jeremy go? Why isn't he here to help us deal the cards?",
    ["……枪声？"] = "…Gunshots?",
    ["……柠檬、香草、巧克力，美味清新沁心脾！"] = "...Lemon, vanilla, chocolate, delicious, refreshing, and heart-warming!",
    ["……欠得好。"] = "...Well deserved.",
    ["……歌声……好听的歌声……妈妈……"] = "...Singing... beautiful singing... Mother...",
    ["……正是隔壁的花店老板娘斯嘉丽！"] = "...It's Scarlett, the owner of the flower shop next door!",
    ["……死定了。"] = "…Dead for sure.",
    ["……殿下……"] = "...Your Highness...",
    ["……殿下，这是一种血肉魔法，通过被吞食的方式让灵体寄生于他人体内，并逐渐控制吞食者的身体，达到灵体永生的目的……"] = "...Your Highness, this is a type of Flesh Magic. By being consumed, a spirit parasite enters another's body and gradually takes control of the host, achieving the goal of eternal life for the spirit...",
    ["……每当梨花开遍了天涯，河上飘着柔曼的轻纱。"] = "……Whenever pear blossoms bloom across the horizon, soft gauze floats upon the river.",
    ["……比南大陆更南，比北大陆更北，比苏尼亚海更东，比迷雾海更西……"] = "……Further south than the Southern Continent, further north than the Northern Continent, further east than the Sonia Sea, further west than the Fog Sea……",
    ["……比地心更深，比星空更高……"] = "……Deeper than the Earth's core, higher than the starry sky……",
    ["……毕竟我们三个一向做什么都在一起。"] = "...After all, the three of us have always done everything together.",
    ["……毕竟有些人，什么都没有留下。"] = "……After all, some people leave nothing behind.",
    ["……水平还挺特别的。"] = "……The level is quite unique.",
    ["……污染已经清除，你可以走了。"] = "…The corruption has been cleared; you may leave.",
    ["……汪呜？"] = "……Woof?",
    ["……没……问题……"] = "...No... problem...",
    ["……没事，可能最近休息太少了。"] = "...It's fine, maybe I've been resting too little lately.",
    ["……没什么。有些晚了，回家吧。 "] = "…It's nothing. It's getting late, let's go home.",
    ["……没什么。这里比之前的菜品更丰富了。"] = "...Nothing. The dishes here are richer than before.",
    ["……没关系。"] = "...It's okay.",
    ["……没有。"] = "...No.",
    ["……没有办法继续询问了。"] = "...There's no way to continue questioning.",
    ["……没有太多有用的线索，需要注意的只有一点。"] = "...Not many useful clues, only one thing to note.",
    ["……没有？看来，今天我们都该休息了。嗯，这是不需要灵性直觉也能得到的启示。"] = "……None? It seems we should both rest today. Hmm, this is an revelation one can get without spirituality intuition.",
    ["……没用的，我试过几十次了。"] = "…It's useless, I've tried dozens of times.",
    ["……没礼貌的小家伙！"] = "...You rude little thing!",
    ["……没错。"] = "…That's right.",
    ["……没错，我独自经历了这一切。"] = "...That's right, I experienced all of this alone.",
    ["……烟草、消毒水和薄荷叶？有点呛人，但能令人精神起来的味道。"] = "...Tobacco, disinfectant, and mint leaves? A bit pungent, but a scent that can wake one up.",
    ["……烟草、薄荷和消毒水的味道……"] = "...The smell of tobacco, mint, and disinfectant...",
    ["……然后我们全体冲上去，和龙大战了三百回合！"] = "...And then we all charge up and fight the dragon for three hundred rounds!",
    ["……熟悉的声音，刚刚和雪莉发生争执的人似乎也在里面。"] = "…A familiar voice; the person who was just arguing with Shirley seems to be in there too.",
    ["……爱管闲事？"] = "...Meddlesome?",
    ["……牙齿尖尖？打架的茶？"] = "……Sharp teeth? Fighting tea?",
    ["……猎龙城？"] = "...Dragon Hunting City?",
    ["……猎龙计划？真要猎龙？"] = "...Dragon Hunting Plan? Are we really going to hunt a dragon?",
    ["……猫？是猫在说……？"] = "……A cat? Is the cat talking……?",
    ["……献上生命与心脏！大功告成！"] = "...Offer your life and heart! Mission accomplished!",
    ["……玛格丽特小姐对您完全没有那种想法，她在想诊费和蛋糕。"] = "……Ms. Margaret has absolutely no such thoughts about you; she is thinking about the consultation fee and cake.",
    ["……现在，我们是一体了。没有软弱，只有绝对的控制。"] = "……Now, we are one. No weakness, only absolute control.",
    ["……瑞尔·比伯的位置。"] = "...The location of Ray Bieber.",
    ["……画得一般。"] = "...The drawing is mediocre.",
    ["……疯狂地追逐着我……"] = "…Madly chasing after me…",
    ["……直到追到西边太阳落下的谷地，他们与太阳一同进入长眠。"] = "……Until they reached the valley where the sun sets in the west, they entered a long Slumber along with the sun.",
    ["……相信我们……疏通穴位……"] = "...Trust us... clearing the acupoints...",
    ["……看得出来。"] = "...I can tell.",
    ["……看您并没有想要用餐的意思，请离开吧。"] = "…Since you don't seem to want to dine, please leave.",
    ["……看来面对苦痛而无可奈何的命运，她也微笑着走了下去。"] = "...It seems that she walked on with a smile even in the face of painful and helpless fate.",
    ["……看起来命运的指点已经降下，今天您还是适合进入俱乐部，找一名真正的占卜师占卜一下。"] = "...It seems the guidance of fate has already descended. Today, it is still suitable for you to enter the club and find a real divination master to perform a divination.",
    ["……真好。"] = "...How nice.",
    ["……真是奇怪，我从来不留人过夜，她叫什么？"] = "……How strange, I never let people stay overnight, what is her name?",
    ["……真是热闹啊。"] = "...It's really lively here.",
    ["……真是精彩，就连我也开始期待后面的情节了，罗塞尔大帝真是讲故事的天才。"] = "...Truly wonderful, even I am starting to look forward to the subsequent plot, Emperor Roselle is truly a genius at storytelling.",
    ["……真有这么神奇？"] = "...Is it really that magical?",
    ["……真的？你救了我，我……相信你。"] = "...Really? You saved me, I... trust you.",
    ["……码头那天晚上到底发生了什么？"] = "…What exactly happened at the dock that night?",
    ["……确实能理解他们的反应。"] = "……I can certainly understand their reaction.",
    ["……祂的精神化为永恒烈阳、风暴之主、知识与智慧之神，祂的智慧中诞生了人类。"] = "...His spirit turned into the Eternal Blazing Sun, the Lord of Storms, and the God of Knowledge and Wisdom; humanity was born from His wisdom.",
    ["……福生……玄黄……仙尊……"] = "……Blessings……of the mysterious……Immortal Lord……",
    ["……笛子？是叔叔给尤朵拉的……笛子可以让家人们听话……跟我回家……"] = "...Flute? It was given to Yodora by Uncle... The flute can make the family members listen... Come home with me...",
    ["……等你正式入学后，考虑一下我们。"] = "…Once you have officially enrolled, consider joining us.",
    ["……等我喝完这瓶酒。"] = "...Wait until I finish this bottle of wine.",
    ["……等等。剧情居然已经进行到这里了……可真让我意外……"] = "……Wait. The plot has actually progressed to this point…… It really surprises me……",
    ["……等等。贵客您竟然能来到这儿…...可真让我意外......"] = "…Wait. To think that a distinguished guest like you could come here… it really surprises me…",
    ["……等等，是拉夫老师派你来拿东西的吗？"] = "...Wait, did Teacher Lav send you to get something?",
    ["……等等，那个整天没有正经事，到处疯玩的臭小子在哪？"] = "...Wait, where is that brat who has no serious business all day and runs around playing wildly?",
    ["……算了算了，威尔森，这里是俱乐部门口。"] = "…Forget it, forget it, Wilson, we are at the entrance of the club.",
    ["……算了算了，我给你就是了。真是长见识……"] = "...Forget it, forget it, I'll give it to you. I've really learned something today...",
    ["……算了，利用就利用，回速递站。"] = "...Forget it, let them use me, back to the delivery station.",
    ["……算了，来都来了。"] = "...Forget it, I'm already here.",
    ["……细节不重要！重点是战略！"] = "…Details aren't important! The point is strategy!",
    ["……终于，可以不用再等了。"] = "...Finally, I don't have to wait anymore.",
    ["……绝望吗？"] = "…Are you in despair?",
    ["……罗珊这是急着去哪？"] = "……Where is Rozanne in such a hurry to go?",
    ["……罗珊，怎么了。"] = "...Rozanne, what's wrong?",
    ["……美丽的姑娘站在峻峭的岸上，歌声好像明媚的春光。"] = "……A beautiful girl stands on the steep bank, her singing like bright spring light.",
    ["……老头子走的时候，我说我还有孩子。"] = "……When the old man left, I said I still had children.",
    ["……老子抗议！老子不写了！不！写！了！"] = "...I protest! I'm not writing anymore! Not! Writing! Anymore!",
    ["……耳朵受到了冲击，好像见到了去世多年的爷爷。"] = "…My ears were impacted, I think I saw my grandfather who passed away years ago.",
    ["……背叛者，渎神的……叛徒！"] = "...Traitor, you blasphemous... turncoat!",
    ["……胡说什么，我下班了！"] = "…What nonsense, I'm off work!",
    ["……能不能让我安静睡个觉。"] = "...Can you just let me get some quiet sleep.",
    ["……至少，你没有让她伤害其他人，防止了她的堕落，也保护了更多的廷根市民——作为守护者，你没有失职。"] = "…At the very least, you did not let her harm others, prevented her fall, and protected more Tingen citizens—as a guardian, you have not failed your duty.",
    ["……艾登……"] = "……Aiden……",
    ["……芙拉女士一定是想模仿传说，自己也吃下黑斑青蛙！因为这样就能看见亡灵了！这就是她口中的“去见杰温”！"] = "…Ms. Fula must have wanted to imitate the legend and eat a black-spotted frog herself! Because that way, she could see spirits! This is what she meant by 'going to see Jewen'!",
    ["……茜安，你想不想要一间自己的餐厅，光明正大地做菜？"] = "...Xian, do you want your own restaurant to cook openly?",
    ["……莎莉丝特。"] = "…Celeste.",
    ["……萨洛米，我好怀念我们一起照顾花圃的日子。"] = "...Salome, I miss the days we spent tending the flower garden together.",
    ["……蒙巴顿先生，我还什么都没说呢。"] = "...Mr. Mountbatten, I haven't said anything yet.",
    ["……薪水可是一千费尔金……"] = "…The salary is one thousand gold pounds…",
    ["……蘑菇不需要光合作用。"] = "……Mushrooms don't need photosynthesis.",
    ["……蘑菇不需要朋友。"] = "...Mushrooms don't need friends.",
    ["……虽然不能帮你实现，但我有个游戏，能让你成为大帝，体验万人敬仰的感觉！"] = "...Although I can't make it happen for you, I have a game that can let you become the Emperor and experience the feeling of being admired by thousands!",
    ["……行，不计划。"] = "...Fine, no plan.",
    ["……要是人心也像这玩意儿该多好。"] = "...If only human hearts were like this thing.",
    ["……让我们彻底忘掉那场战争，安娜。"] = "...Let's completely forget about that war, Anna.",
    ["……记得吗？我的琴声曾帮你解决了咖啡厅的麻烦。"] = "...Remember? My music once helped you resolve that trouble at the café.",
    ["……记得！就是连杀了五位少女，拿走她们不同器官的“血腥屠夫”？小时候，我母亲经常拿这件事吓唬我妹妹。"] = "…I remember! Is it the 'Bloody Butcher' who killed five young girls in a row and took different organs from them? When I was a child, my mother often used this story to scare my sister.",
    ["……证件也是可以伪造的，在我的家乡，这种劣质的证件两苏勒一个。"] = "...Documents can also be forged. In my hometown, these low-quality documents are two Sol each.",
    ["……话说，你好像一直带着婚戒？你现在结婚了吗？"] = "...By the way, you seem to have been wearing a wedding ring? Are you married now?",
    ["……说得太好了！从“征服”到“敬畏”，这个解读让诗的境界豁然开朗！"] = "...Well said! From \"Conquest\" to \"Awe\", this interpretation makes the realm of the poem suddenly clear!",
    ["……说来有些离奇，我的能力是从一个老太太那里得到的。是安丽萨太太，她是我的病人，那时我还是一个诊所的医生。"] = "……It's a bit bizarre, but I got my powers from an old lady. It was Mrs. Anlisa; she was my patient when I was still a doctor at a clinic.",
    ["……说起来，大家凑钱买的旧黑板，前段时间被镇上的恶霸破坏了。"] = "…Speaking of which, the old blackboard that everyone chipped in to buy was destroyed by a town bully a while ago.",
    ["……诶？"] = "...Eh?",
    ["……请给我点时间，让我再考虑一下吧。"] = "……Please give me some time, let me think about it again.",
    ["……请问你有没有看见一枚戒指掉在这附近？"] = "...Excuse me, have you seen a ring dropped around here?",
    ["……谢谢……谢谢你，我没事……"] = "...Thank you... thank you, I'm fine...",
    ["……谢谢。"] = "...Thank you.",
    ["……谢谢您接受我的采访，桌上的食物，这些都是采访的报酬"] = "...Thank you for accepting my interview. The food on the table is the payment for the interview.",
    ["……贝尔纳黛殿下会喜欢么？"] = "……Would Her Highness Bernadette like it?",
    ["……贝尔纳黛殿下可是个诚实的人！"] = "……Her Highness Bernadette is an honest person!",
    ["……资料并不多，他们已经尽力了。"] = "...There isn't much information, they have already done their best.",
    ["……走吧。不过道歉之前，我得先计划好怎么说——"] = "...Let's go. But before I apologize, I have to plan how to say it—",
    ["……走开，让我自己一个人在这里。"] = "...Go away, let me be here by myself.",
    ["……跟我走。别惊讶，这不是条寻常路。"] = "……Follow me. Don't be surprised, this isn't an ordinary path.",
    ["……还以为是真有哪个女明星在码头打起来了呢。"] = "...I thought some female celebrity was actually fighting at the dock.",
    ["……还是想不起来。"] = "...Still can't remember.",
    ["……还是看看别的地方吧。"] = "...Let's look somewhere else.",
    ["……还是算了，谢谢你。"] = "……Never mind, thank you.",
    ["……还没到站，该死的，难道又要晚点了？"] = "...Not at the station yet, damn it, is it going to be late again?",
    ["……还真是，手感也不差。"] = "...It really is, the texture isn't bad either.",
    ["……这不是什么需要否认的事情。"] = "...This is not something that needs to be denied.",
    ["……这世上存在一些超乎寻常的事情。教授是个讲究人，但我上次见他时，他的体毛和指甲已经垂到地上了。"] = "...There are some extraordinary things in this world. The professor is a fastidious person, but when I last saw him, his body hair and nails were already dragging on the ground.",
    ["……这两个人什么时候跑进来的，完全没发现！"] = "…When did these two sneak in? I didn't notice at all!",
    ["……这个世界讨厌我……尤朵拉不是怪物……"] = "...This world hates me... Yodora is not a monster...",
    ["……这个小家伙，我记得它、我依旧记得它，记得他们……"] = "...This little one, I remember it, I still remember it, remember them...",
    ["……这么一想过去也不太美好，美好的只是他们。"] = "...Thinking about it this way, the past wasn't that beautiful either; what was beautiful were just them.",
    ["……这么快就出事了？你确实应该成为非凡者，这样才能更从容地应对那些古怪诡异的事件。"] = "...Something happened so soon? You should indeed become a Beyonder so that you can deal with those strange and eerie events more calmly.",
    ["……这也是我的荣幸，感谢您的邀请。"] = "...This is also my honor, thank you for your invitation.",
    ["……这二者之间有什么必然联系？"] = "…Is there any necessary connection between the two?",
    ["……这应该就是尤朵拉了。"] = "...This must be Yodora.",
    ["……这张悲喜剧面具名为“戏剧大师”，对应学徒途径序列8 戏法大师。戴上面具后，使用者会获得相应的序列能力。"] = "…This comedy-tragedy mask is called 'Drama Master,' corresponding to the Apprentice pathway, Sequence 8, Trickmaster. After wearing the mask, the user will gain the corresponding Sequence abilities.",
    ["……这张悲喜剧面具名为“戏剧大师”，对应序列8 戏法大师。上面融合了戏剧大师蒙特利死前残留的力量，比较危险。戴上面具后，使用者即可掌握一系列不算强力的戏法，包括刮风、制造雾气、爆发闪光等。但只要把它戴在身上，就会有一定几率迷路。除此之外，使用者在佩戴期间，会越来越觉得自己是一个真正的戏剧大师，身边的人会控制不住地按照自己的意愿去表演一出喜剧或悲剧，所以佩戴时间不得超过两个小时。"] = "...This tragicomedy mask is called 'Drama Master', corresponding to Sequence 8, Trickmaster. It contains the residual power of the late Drama Master Monterey, making it quite dangerous. Upon wearing the mask, the user gains a series of not-so-powerful tricks, including summoning wind, creating fog, and bursting flashes. However, as long as it is carried on one's person, there is a certain chance of getting lost. Furthermore, while wearing it, the user will increasingly feel like a true drama master, and those around them will uncontrollably perform a comedy or tragedy according to the user's will, so it must not be worn for more than two hours.",
    ["……这是一场秘密的约会。"] = "……This is a secret date.",
    ["……这是什么情况。不过刚好带了些零钱，拿去吧。"] = "...What's going on. But I happened to bring some change, take it.",
    ["……这是什么？"] = "...What is this?",
    ["……这是瑞尔·比伯学徒时期的经历？"] = "...Is this the experience of Ray Bieber during his apprenticeship?",
    ["……这是！"] = "...This is...!",
    ["……这样能行吗？"] = "...Will this work?",
    ["……这没你的事，你最好小心自己因为翘课太多而被开除！"] = "...This has nothing to do with you. You'd better be careful about getting expelled for skipping too many classes!",
    ["……这种事，也不少见。 但是，您的曲子……至少在我这儿，永远是最好的。"] = "...Things like this aren't rare. But your music... at least to me, it will always be the best.",
    ["……这种未解的数学难题或者经典悖论，祂是不会回答的。"] = "…He will not answer such unsolved mathematical problems or classic paradoxes.",
    ["……这要是登不出来，我就完蛋了。"] = "...If this doesn't get published, I'm finished.",
    ["……这让我想到罗塞尔日记里，大帝说过的那句话：“占卜家”总是说一半藏一半，从来不把事情讲明白吗？"] = "……This reminds me of that line from Roselle's diary, where the Emperor said: “Seers” always say half and hide half, never explaining things clearly?",
    ["……这话听起来怎么像骂人呢？"] = "……Why does that sound like an insult?",
    ["……这里似乎是一处据点？"] = "...This seems to be a stronghold?",
    ["……这里有一行中文批注，是罗塞尔写的：“我看过那么多<P_Yellow>爽文</>，早摸清套路了……”"] = "...There is a line of Chinese annotations here, written by Roselle: \"I've read so many <P_Yellow>web novels</>, I figured out the tropes long ago...\"",
    ["……这里有好多孩子哭声，令人绝望。"] = "...There are so many children crying here, it's despairing.",
    ["……这，这难道是被人吃光了……"] = "…This, could this have been eaten up by someone…",
    ["……追求知识的道路，需要谨慎。"] = "...The path of pursuing knowledge requires caution.",
    ["……遥远的故乡。或许正暗合了大帝晚年，对某个辉煌却无法回去的过去的深沉怀念。"] = "...A distant hometown. Perhaps it coincides with the Emperor's deep nostalgia in his later years for a certain glorious past that he could never return to.",
    ["……邓恩叔叔、戴莉姐姐，我终于考上了霍伊大学，说真的，这很不容易。"] = "...Uncle Dunn, Sister Daly, I finally got into Hoy University, honestly, it wasn't easy.",
    ["……那不是你的错。人们在战场上相遇，只有一个选择。那不是任何士兵的错。"] = "…That was not your fault. When people meet on the battlefield, there is only one choice. That is not the fault of any soldier.",
    ["……那么比赛正式开始！让我们喊出罗塞尔大帝的名言——"] = "...Then the competition officially begins! Let's shout the famous quote of Emperor Roselle—",
    ["……那也没什么用啊。"] = "...That's useless anyway.",
    ["……那你是难过！"] = "...Then you are sad!",
    ["……那你站在这里想做什么？"] = "...Then what are you standing here for?",
    ["……那可是酒馆！我不能再给自己花钱的机会了！"] = "...That's a tavern! I can't give myself another chance to spend money!",
    ["……那场官司，纺织厂的老板都要来亲自找我。"] = "...For that lawsuit, the owner of the textile mill had to come find me personally.",
    ["……那好吧。"] = "……Alright then.",
    ["……那它值多少钱？"] = "...Then how much is it worth?",
    ["……那我9便士！"] = "...Then I'll pay 9 pence!",
    ["……那时你闻到雏菊的清香了吗？"] = "...Did you smell the fragrance of daisies back then?",
    ["……那时候，我跟邓恩都非常悲伤。"] = "...At that time, Dunn and I were both very sad.",
    ["……那是他吵得太烦人，我忘不掉，不行吗？ "] = "…That's because he was being too annoying, I couldn't forget, is that not allowed?",
    ["……那群知识走狗觊觎教会的封印物·尤德拉之树，一路追讨到这里。为了阻止他们，我不得不违反规定，让树触碰到了大地……"] = "...That group of knowledge-seeking lackeys coveted the Church's Sealed Artifact, the Tree of Yodra, and chased it all the way here. To stop them, I had to break the rules and let the tree touch the earth...",
    ["……那走吧，跟我去基地。你救了我，我理应帮你。还有，我叫兰格。"] = "...Then let's go, come with me to the base. You saved me, I should help you. Also, my name is Lange.",
    ["……都免费，全部免费，一便士都不会收的，请放心。"] = "...It's all free, completely free, not a single penny will be charged, please rest assured.",
    ["……都好商量，都好商量。"] = "…Everything is negotiable, everything is negotiable.",
    ["……钢琴也有弦吗？"] = "…Do pianos have strings too?",
    ["……队长、戴莉女士？"] = "...Captain, Ms. Daly?",
    ["……队长，我刚24岁，还远不到被说老的年纪。"] = "...Captain, I'm only 24, far from being called old.",
    ["……阿瑟，继续坐着吧，你别说话了。"] = "…Arthur, keep sitting, stop talking.",
    ["……陈年旧事，不值一提。"] = "...Old news, not worth mentioning.",
    ["……除了玛丽安之外，其他人都离开。"] = "...Everyone except Marianne, leave.",
    ["……难道是“街角相遇，美味相随”不好听？"] = "...Is it that 'Meet at the street corner, deliciousness follows' doesn't sound good?",
    ["……雪崩也会埋葬你们自己人。"] = "…An avalanche will also bury your own people.",
    ["……零花钱正好够。"] = "...My pocket money is just enough.",
    ["……非凡物品提前崩溃，这种情况很少见。"] = "…It is rare for a Beyonder item to break down prematurely.",
    ["……韦尔奇？"] = "……Welch?",
    ["……项链我不卖了，你还给我吧。"] = "...I'm not selling the necklace anymore, give it back to me.",
    ["……饿了。"] = "...Hungry.",
    ["……马桶变得好干净！"] = "...The toilet has become so clean!",
    ["……骨笛对他没有作用……鸟儿们在追随阿诺德……"] = "...The bone flute has no effect on him... The birds are following Arnold...",
    ["……高塔……您似乎即将面对一场巨大的危机，请一定要小心。"] = "...Tower... You seem to be about to face a huge crisis, please be careful.",
    ["……黄油两磅，鸡蛋一打"] = "...Two pounds of butter, a dozen eggs",
    ["……黄黑之王。"] = "...The King of Yellow and Black.",
    ["……黑色的怨念沿着玫瑰的枝干，一路延伸到了地底！"] = "...Black resentment followed the rose stems all the way underground!",
    ["……龙？"] = "...Dragon?",
    ["……（阿罗德斯劈下了一道闪电，等该功能接入后加入表现）"] = "… (Arrodes strikes down a bolt of lightning, to be added once the feature is integrated)",
    ["……？不是大哥你……？"] = "...? It's not you, big brother...?",
    ["…做得很好，我们的廷根大侦探。"] = "…Well done, our great detective of Tingen.",
    ["…好…谢谢你，小妹妹…我相信我的妈妈，我也很爱她。"] = "...Okay... thank you, little sister... I believe in my mother, and I love her very much.",
    ["…脚印？它果然在这附近！得想想办法捉住它"] = "...Footprints? It really is nearby! I must think of a way to catch it.",
    ["←  想"] = "←  Think",
    ["←  红色"] = "←  Red",
    ["←  绿色"] = "←  Green",
    ["←  自己"] = "←  Self",
    ["←  视觉"] = "←  Vision",
    ["←  需要"] = "←  Need",
    ["◆侯爵茶鎏金焦糖布蕾"] = "◆ Marquis Tea Gilded Crème Brûlée",
    ["◆命运特调"] = "◆ Fate Special Blend",
    ["◆月夜风味浓缩"] = "◆ Moonlit Night Flavored Concentrate",
    ["◆深眠药箱拿铁"] = "◆ Deep Sleep Latte",
    ["◆甜冰茶"] = "◆ Sweet Iced Tea",
    ["◆费尔默咖啡"] = "◆ Filmer Coffee",
    ["◆金手柑甜品拼盘"] = "◆ Golden Bergamot Dessert Platter",
    ["◆间海奶油蛤蜊浓汤"] = "◆ Midseashire Creamy Clam Chowder",
    ["◆高地苔原蛋糕"] = "◆ Highland Tundra Cake",
    ["◆鲱鱼（新鲜）\n每桶50条 3桶 10苏勒/桶 <Delete id=\"#158\">103</> <Delete id=\"#158\">15 </>13苏勒\n\n◆鳕鱼（盐渍）\n每箱20磅 2箱 1金镑/箱 2金镑\n\n◆牡蛎 \n每篮100只 5篮 5苏勒/篮 55苏勒\n\n     合计  <Delete id=\"#158\">4金镑15苏勒 </>3金镑8苏勒"] = "◆Herring (Fresh) \n 50 per barrel, 3 barrels, 10 soli/barrel <Delete id=\"#158\"> 103 </> <Delete id=\"#158\"> 15 </> 13 soli \n\n ◆Cod (Salted) \n 20 lbs per box, 2 boxes, 1 gold pound/box, 2 gold pounds \n\n ◆Oysters \n 100 per basket, 5 baskets, 5 soli/basket, 55 soli \n\n Total <Delete id=\"#158\"> 4 gold pounds 15 soli </> 3 gold pounds 8 soli",
    ["　　\n\n　　……\n\n　　罗塞尔相貌俊美，落魄贵族的出身更为之增添了深沉气质与勇往无前的生命力。\n\n　　出色的相貌与更为出色的学识与行动力，使之从青年起就成为了因蒂斯适婚男女的梦中爱侣。\n\n　　……\n\n　　（大片被啃食的痕迹）\n\n　　……与之相伴一生的眷侣玛蒂尔达女士，来自阿贝多家族……\n\n　　（大片被啃食的痕迹）"] = "\n \n ... \n \n Roselle was handsome, and his background as a fallen noble added a deep temperament and an indomitable vitality to him. \n \n His outstanding appearance and even more outstanding knowledge and drive made him the dream lover of marriageable men and women in Intis from his youth. \n \n ... \n \n (Large areas of gnawed marks) \n \n ... Lady Matilda, his companion for life, came from the Abedo family... \n \n (Large areas of gnawed marks)",
    ["　　\n\n　　库默尔首先意识到，问题不在于整数本身，而在于我们对“素数”的理解过于狭隘。\n　　他引入理想数，并非作为一种技巧，而是作为一种必然：当原有的数不够用时，我们必须构想出新的数，使唯一分解律在更广阔的范围内重新成立。\n　　\n\n　　本书沿着这条路径展开，从同余的基本性质出发，逐步深入到二次型、分圆域与理想类群，试图为算术建立一套完整的、内在一致的理论框架。"] = "　　\n\n　　Kummer was the first to realize that the problem did not lie in the integers themselves, but in our overly narrow understanding of \"prime numbers.\" \n　　He introduced ideal numbers not as a mere technique, but as a necessity: when the existing numbers are insufficient, we must conceive of new ones to ensure that the law of unique factorization holds once again within a broader scope. \n　　\n\n　　This book unfolds along this path, starting from the basic properties of congruence and gradually delving into quadratic forms, cyclotomic fields, and ideal class groups, attempting to establish a complete and internally consistent theoretical framework for arithmetic.",
    ["　　\n\n　　知识是被扛在肩上的，它有重量，会消耗体力，背负者必须为它付出代价。\n　　这个古老民族或许比后世许多哲学体系更早地触及了一个真相——知道得越多，承受得越重。\n　　遗憾的是，现存文献大多残损。本书所能依赖的，仅有零星出土的陶片刻铭、后世抄本中的引述，以及邻近语族中若干可疑的同源词。这些材料足以暗示方向，却不足以支撑定论。\n　　笔者如实呈现证据的匮乏，而非用推测填补空白——在语源学这门学科里，承认无知本身就是一种诚实。"] = " \n \n Knowledge is carried on the shoulders; it has weight and consumes physical strength, and the bearer must pay a price for it. \n This ancient nation perhaps touched a truth earlier than many later philosophical systems—the more you know, the heavier you bear. \n Regrettably, most existing documents are damaged. What this book can rely on are only sporadic inscriptions on unearthed pottery shards, citations in later manuscripts, and several suspicious cognate words in neighboring language families. These materials are enough to suggest a direction, but not enough to support a conclusion. \n The author presents the lack of evidence truthfully, rather than filling the gaps with speculation—in the discipline of etymology, admitting ignorance itself is a kind of honesty.",
    ["　　\n　　……人类理性在其知识的某个门类里有一种特殊的命运，就是为一些它无法摆脱的问题所困扰。因为这些问题是由理性自身的本性向自己提出来的，但它又不能回答它们。因为它超越了人类理性的一切能力。\n　　这种困境并非源于无知，而是源于理性自身的冲动——它渴望超越经验的界限，去追问那些无法被感官验证的终极。于是理性陷入了永久的自我撕裂：它既不能停止追问，又无法给出确证的答案。"] = " \n ...Human reason has a special fate in a certain category of its knowledge, which is that it is troubled by some problems it cannot escape. Because these problems are proposed to it by the nature of reason itself, yet it cannot answer them. Because they transcend all the capabilities of human reason. \n This predicament does not stem from ignorance, but from the impulse of reason itself—it longs to transcend the boundaries of experience and question those ultimates that cannot be verified by the senses. Thus, reason falls into a permanent self-tearing: it can neither stop questioning nor provide a confirmed answer.",
    ["　　\n　　柠檬味清洁药剂现已全城热销！\n　　由罗森的民俗草药店研发，清新柠檬香，洁净更安心！该药剂上市以来迅速成为廷根居民的清洁首选。即日起到店选购，还可享“买二赠一”限时优惠，欢迎前来体验！ "] = "\n Lemon-scented cleaning agent is now a bestseller across the city! \n Developed by Rosen's Folk Herb Shop, it features a fresh lemon scent for a cleaner, more reassuring home! Since its launch, this agent has quickly become the cleaning choice for Tingen residents. Purchase in-store starting today and enjoy a \"buy two, get one free\" limited-time offer. We welcome you to come and experience it!",
    ["　　\n　　（大片被啃食的痕迹）\n\n　　<Mark id=\"#157\">1155年5月19日</>，因蒂斯共和国<InvHighlight>皇长女</>诞生……罗塞尔为爱女起名<Mark id=\"#157\">贝尔纳黛·古斯塔夫……</>\n\n　　……\n\n　　（大片被啃食的痕迹）"] = "\n (Large areas of gnawed marks) \n \n <Mark id=\"#157\"> May 19, 1155 </>, the eldest daughter of the <InvHighlight> Intis Republic </> was born... Roselle named his beloved daughter <Mark id=\"#157\"> Bernadette Gustav </> ... \n \n ... \n \n (Large areas of gnawed marks)",
    ["　　25日晚7点15分，查理参加廷根大剧院罗塞尔戏剧节晚宴，9点宴毕与蒙特利会谈，约10点独自离开后失踪。查理经营南北大陆贸易20年，是罗塞尔忠实崇拜者。经查曾贩卖违禁材料，由地下摊主保罗代售。"] = "　　June 25th, 7:15 PM, Charlie attended the Tingen Grand Theater Roselle Drama Festival banquet, had a meeting with Monterey after the banquet at 9:00 PM, and went missing after leaving alone around 10:00 PM. Charlie had been operating trade between the North and South continents for 20 years and was a loyal admirer of Roselle. Investigation shows he had sold contraband materials, which were sold on his behalf by underground stall owner Paul.",
    ["　　6月24日，卡尔同事兼合租人托尼报案：卡尔22日下班后失联，至今未上班。警方推测其22日夜间失踪，无目击证人，失踪地点不明。据了解，卡尔性格友善，但酗酒严重，喜欢赞美罗塞尔，诉说过往经历。"] = "　　June 24th, Karl's colleague and roommate Tony reported: Karl lost contact after getting off work on the 22nd and has not been to work since. Police speculate he went missing on the night of the 22nd; there are no eyewitnesses, and the location of the disappearance is unknown. It is understood that Karl had a friendly personality but was a heavy drinker who liked to praise Roselle and talk about his past experiences.",
    ["　　6月27日上午8点，金梧桐区下水道入口传出阵阵恶臭。根据警方调查，恶臭的源头指向休伯特议员居住的切斯庄园。据悉，休伯特议员家中马桶于6月26日晚发生故障。"] = "　　June 27th, 8:00 AM, a foul stench emanated from the sewer entrance in the Golden Phoenix District. According to police investigations, the source of the stench pointed to Chase Manor, where Councilman Hubert resides. It is reported that the toilet in Councilman Hubert's home malfunctioned on the night of June 26th.",
    ["　　6月27日晚上9点，被人发现死于春夜沙龙的卧室内。根据案发现场的情况和尸检报告，初步断定为饮酒过度和连续纵欲导致的猝死。"] = "　　June 27th, 9:00 PM, found dead in the bedroom of the Spring Night Salon. Based on the crime scene and autopsy report, it was preliminarily determined to be sudden death caused by excessive drinking and continuous debauchery.",
    ["　　6月28日，正在改编《伯爵归来》的剧作家施佩尔忽然罹患严重的精神疾病。根据心理诊所的初步检查，诊断为精神压力和工作习惯导致的妄想性障碍。 "] = "　　June 28th, playwright Speer, who was adapting \"The Count Returns,\" suddenly suffered from a severe mental illness. According to a preliminary examination at the psychological clinic, it was diagnosed as a delusional disorder caused by mental stress and work habits.",
    ["　　6月29日，梅森工厂女工娜塔报案，妹妹温妮突然失踪，因失踪时间未超过48小时，暂未开始调查。"] = "　　June 29th, Mason Factory worker Nata reported that her younger sister Winnie had suddenly gone missing. As the disappearance time has not exceeded 48 hours, an investigation has not yet begun.",
    ["　　<Hide stylename=\"InvDefault_HW\" id=\"#157\">我不想死在这里我想回到贝克兰德当街头画家我很想家我很想家我很想家谁能救救我</>\n　　<InvDefault_HW>冷，饿</>\n　　<Hide stylename=\"InvDefault_HW\" id=\"#161\">我害了所有人，我不配当队长，对不起所有人我让你们白白去死了我犯了杀人的罪我太懦弱了我搞砸了所有</>\n　　<InvDefault_HW>对不起，兄弟们</>\n　　<InvHighlight>（日记到此为止。不过每隔几页都有士兵们的速写，有的在睡觉，有的在举枪瞄准，姿态生动，看得出绘画功底深厚。）</>"] = "<Hide stylename=\"InvDefault_HW\" id=\"#157\"> I don't want to die here I want to go back to Backlund to be a street painter I miss home so much I miss home so much I miss home so much who can save me </> \n <InvDefault_HW> Cold, hungry </> \n <Hide stylename=\"InvDefault_HW\" id=\"#161\"> I harmed everyone, I am not fit to be a captain, I'm sorry to everyone I let you die in vain I committed the crime of murder I was too cowardly I messed everything up </> \n <InvDefault_HW> I'm sorry, brothers </> \n <InvHighlight> (The diary ends here. However, every few pages there are sketches of soldiers, some sleeping, some aiming their guns, the poses are vivid, showing a deep foundation in drawing.) </>",
    ["　　<InvDefault_HW> 1351年2月20日 </>\n　　<InvDefault_HW>今天是与大部队走散的第十天。时间越久，返回的希望就越渺茫。</>\n　　……\n　　<InvDefault_HW>1351年3月4日</>\n　　<InvDefault_HW>走散的第二十二天，情况在逐渐变坏，食物要耗尽了，更重要的是，环绕的弗萨克人彻底困住了我们。</>\n　　……"] = "<InvDefault_HW> February 20, 1351 </> \n <InvDefault_HW> Today is the tenth day since I got separated from the main force. The longer time passes, the slimmer the hope of returning becomes. </> \n ... \n <InvDefault_HW> March 4, 1351 </> \n <InvDefault_HW> The twenty-second day of being separated, the situation is gradually worsening. Food is about to run out, and more importantly, the surrounding Feysacians have completely trapped us. </> \n ...",
    ["　　<InvDefault_HW>“如果你是来给我带来温暖的，那确实是我。”恢复了体温的戴莉在麋鹿的头顶蹦跶了几下，继续说道：“我叫戴莉， 你的名字是什么？”</>\n\n　　<InvDefault_HW> “我是……抱歉，我忘记了我的名字。”</>\n\n　　<InvDefault_HW>戴莉这才注意到，麋鹿的角上挂着许多小木牌，上面写着“我叫邓恩”、我是森林的守护者”、“每天巡逻看谁需要帮助”……</>\n\n　　<InvDefault_HW>“你叫邓恩，”戴莉轻声说，她听树洞里的松鼠一家提起过这头每到冬天就会失忆的麋鹿，曾一天给他们送了三次松子，“你是银雾森林的守护者。”</>"] = "　　<InvDefault_HW>\"If you've come to bring me warmth, then that is indeed me.\" Daly, having regained her body temperature, hopped a few times on the moose's head and continued, \"My name is Daly. What is your name?\"</>\n\n　　<InvDefault_HW> \"I am... I'm sorry, I have forgotten my name.\"</>\n\n　　<InvDefault_HW>Only then did Daly notice that many small wooden plaques were hanging on the moose's antlers, with words written on them like \"My name is Dunn,\" \"I am the Guardian of the forest,\" \"Patrol every day to see who needs help\"...</>\n\n　　<InvDefault_HW>\"Your name is Dunn,\" Daly said softly. She had heard the squirrel family in the tree hole mention this moose that would lose its memory every winter, having once delivered pine nuts to them three times in a single day, \"You are the Guardian of the Silver Mist Forest.\"</>",
    ["　　<InvDefault_HW>“我们去吧！”戴莉跳到了鹿角顶端，“就算你在里面迷失了方向，我的歌声也能把我们带到正确的道路上。”</>\n\n　　<InvDefault_HW>它们就这样进入了洞穴，里面结构错综复杂，邓恩和戴莉费了不少力气才找到受伤的蝙蝠一家。就在它们准备离开洞穴的时候，外面狂风大作，无数雪花被风裹挟而来，挡住了所有的光。邓恩又尝试了几个方向，比找不到出口更令人绝望的是蝙蝠一家越来越微弱的呼吸。</>"] = "　　<InvDefault_HW>\"Let's go!\" Daly jumped to the top of the antlers, \"Even if you get lost inside, my singing can lead us on the right path.\"</>\n\n　　<InvDefault_HW>They entered the cave just like that. The structure inside was intricate and complex, and it took Dunn and Daly quite a bit of effort to find the injured bat family. Just as they were preparing to leave the cave, a gale blew outside, and countless snowflakes were carried by the wind, blocking all light. Dunn tried several more directions. More desperate than not finding the exit was the increasingly weak breathing of the bat family.</>",
    ["　　<InvDefault_HW>一天，戴莉发现邓恩从地上捡起来什么东西，固定在角上后它发现是自己掉落的羽毛。</>\n\n　　<InvDefault_HW>“这些羽毛太美了，我舍不得它们就这样被遗忘。”邓恩甩了甩头，“即使我明天就会忘记为什么要这么做，但我的角会记得这种发痒的感觉。”</>\n\n　　<InvDefault_HW>戴莉的心轻轻颤动，她激动地盘旋在邓恩的两角之间，准备一展歌喉抖落几根崭新的羽毛。邓恩阻止了它这种会让自己更冷的行为，请它帮忙整理那些收集好的羽毛。戴莉将它们和一个个木牌挂在一起，让它们在风雪中碰撞，与鹿蹄声和鸟鸣声组成森林的曲调。</>"] = "　　<InvDefault_HW>One day, Daly discovered that Dunn had picked something up from the ground and fixed it to its antlers; it realized it was one of its own fallen feathers.</>\n\n　　<InvDefault_HW>\"These feathers are too beautiful; I can't bear for them to be forgotten just like that.\" Dunn shook its head, \"Even if I forget why I did this tomorrow, my antlers will remember this itching sensation.\"</>\n\n　　<InvDefault_HW>Daly's heart trembled gently. She fluttered excitedly between Dunn's two antlers, preparing to show off her voice and shake off a few brand-new feathers. Dunn stopped her from doing something that would make her even colder and asked her to help organize the collected feathers. Daly hung them together with the wooden plaques, letting them collide in the wind and snow, composing the forest's melody along with the sound of deer hooves and birdsong.</>",
    ["　　<InvDefault_HW>先是刚刚的对话，然后是昨天帮助过的动物，最后连自己的名字都如同飘落的雪花，落在地上了无痕迹。他只好把重要的事情都刻下来，做成木牌挂在鹿角上提醒自己。</>\n\n　　<InvDefault_HW>有一只叫戴莉的知更鸟住在森林的东边，雾气更加浓郁的地方。它有着绯红色的羽毛，它可以用歌声编织出金色的旋律，为迷路的生灵指引方向。但这里藏着它的秘密：每编织一段完整的旋律，它就会掉落一根羽毛，掉落的羽毛不会再生长。</>"] = "　　<InvDefault_HW> First, the recent conversations, then the animals it helped yesterday, and finally, even its own name falls to the ground like drifting snowflakes, leaving no trace. It has no choice but to carve important matters onto wooden plaques and hang them on its antlers to remind itself. </>\n\n　　<InvDefault_HW> A robin named Daly lives in the eastern part of the forest, where the mist is even thicker. It has crimson feathers and can weave golden melodies with its song to guide lost creatures. But here lies its secret: for every complete melody it weaves, it loses a feather, and the lost feathers never grow back. </>",
    ["　　<InvDefault_HW>在霍纳奇斯山脉下有一处终年被银色雾气包裹的森林，里面住着各自各样的珍稀动物。</>\n\n　　<InvDefault_HW>其中，有一头叫做邓恩的麋鹿住在森林的最深处，它有着云朵般柔软的灰色皮毛和比橡木还要坚实的巨大鹿角，走路时的蹄声沉稳地如同森林的呼吸。它是这座森林的守护者，拥有洞察森林每一个角落的力量，但这份力量也伴随着诅咒——每年第一场雪落下的时候，它就会开始遗忘。</>"] = "　　<InvDefault_HW>At the foot of the Hornacis Mountain Range lies a forest shrouded in silver mist all year round, home to all kinds of rare animals.</>\n\n　　<InvDefault_HW>Among them, a moose named Dunn lives in the deepest part of the forest. It has gray fur as soft as clouds and massive antlers sturdier than oak. Its hoofbeats as it walks are as steady as the forest's breathing. It is the Guardian of this forest, possessing the power to gain insight into every corner of the forest, but this power comes with a curse—when the first snow of the year falls, it begins to forget.</>",
    ["　　<InvDefault_HW>它惊讶地发现身上覆盖着全新的羽毛——银白色的，如雾般轻盈蓬松。邓恩安静地守在落叶堆旁，角上依然挂着木牌，最新一块刻着：“戴莉拥有了一身新的羽毛，记得赞美它。”</>\n\n　　<InvDefault_HW>后来，森林里流传着这样的故事：这里有两位守护者，深沉的鹿蹄声和清亮的鸟叫声完美交融，它们在歌声和鹿角中记录每一朵花的绽放，每条溪流的改道和每个生命的成长。</>\n\n　　<InvDefault_HW>邓恩的遗忘还在循环，但它每天都赞美戴莉的羽毛；戴莉的羽毛不再随歌声掉落，每段旋律都让羽毛更有光泽。</>"] = "　　<InvDefault_HW>It was surprised to find its body covered in brand-new feathers—silver-white, as light and fluffy as mist. Dunn stood guard quietly beside the pile of leaves, with the wooden plaques still hanging on its antlers. The newest one was engraved with: \"Daly has a new set of feathers; remember to praise her.\"</>\n\n　　<InvDefault_HW>Later, such a story circulated in the forest: there are two Guardians here, the deep sound of deer hooves and the clear birdsong blending perfectly. They record every blooming flower, the diversion of every stream, and the growth of every life in their songs and on their antlers.</>\n\n　　<InvDefault_HW>Dunn's forgetting still cycles, but it praises Daly's feathers every day; Daly's feathers no longer fall out with her singing, and every melody makes the feathers more lustrous.</>",
    ["　　<InvDefault_HW>戴莉飞到了它耳边开始歌唱，金色的旋律指引抚平了邓恩有些焦躁的心情，他沿着音符亮起的方向走去。十米，五十米，一百米……眼前仍然没有出现洞口的光亮，戴莉意识到前往出口的代价可能比想象中更多。</>\n\n　　<InvDefault_HW>没有犹豫。</>\n\n　　<InvDefault_HW>它飞得更高了，飞到邓恩根本看不清的地方，歌唱到背上的羽毛所剩无几，她开始下坠。</>\n\n　　<InvDefault_HW>眼前还是没有出现光亮。</>"] = "　　<InvDefault_HW> Daly flew to its ear and began to sing. The golden melody guided and soothed Dunn's somewhat agitated mood, and he walked in the direction where the notes shone. Ten meters, fifty meters, one hundred meters... Still, no light from the cave entrance appeared before them. Daly realized that the cost of reaching the exit might be greater than imagined. </>\n\n　　<InvDefault_HW> Without hesitation. </>\n\n　　<InvDefault_HW> It flew higher, to a place where Dunn couldn't see clearly at all, singing until there were almost no feathers left on its back, and it began to fall. </>\n\n　　<InvDefault_HW> Still, no light appeared before them. </>",
    ["　　<InvDefault_HW>有些记忆会在冬雪中被埋藏，有些记忆会在回响中永恒。</>\n\n　　<InvDefault_HW>即使遗忘，善良也会为弱者驻足，即使失去，爱会赋予重构的勇气。</>"] = "　　<InvDefault_HW>Some memories will be buried in the winter snow, and some memories will be eternal in the echoes.</>\n\n　　<InvDefault_HW>Even if forgotten, kindness will pause for the weak; even if lost, love will grant the courage to reconstruct.</>",
    ["　　<InvDefault_HW>灰色的麋鹿突然仰首长鸣，它角上的羽毛纷纷发出柔光，飘到空中接续起了戴莉未完成的歌。它的鹿角记住了每片羽毛中储存的音符，它笨拙的收集无意中保存了戴莉所有的歌声。</>\n\n　　<InvDefault_HW>直到鹿角触碰到最后一个音符的时刻，光亮也在出现在眼前，猫头鹰长老在洞口拼命甩着翅膀欢迎英雄的归来。</>\n\n　　<InvDefault_HW>戴莉再次醒来是在温暖而干燥的落叶堆里。</>"] = "　　<InvDefault_HW>The gray moose suddenly raised its head and let out a long cry. The feathers on its antlers emitted a soft light one after another, floating into the air to continue the song Daly hadn't finished. Its antlers had memorized the notes stored in every feather; its clumsy collection had inadvertently preserved all of Daly's singing.</>\n\n　　<InvDefault_HW>The moment the antlers touched the final note, light also appeared before them. The Owl Elder was frantically flapping its wings at the cave entrance, welcoming the heroes' return.</>\n\n　　<InvDefault_HW>Daly woke up again in a pile of warm and dry fallen leaves.</>",
    ["　　<InvDefault_HW>这一年的最后一天，森林遭遇了百年未遇的暴雪，猫头鹰长老召集起了一场紧急会议。</>\n\n　　<InvDefault_HW>“北边山洞上方的积雪发生了崩塌，那里面还住着冬眠的蝙蝠一家，我们不能放着它们不管。”</>\n\n　　<InvDefault_HW>所有的动物都沉默了，它们基本不和蝙蝠来往，只有邓恩在去年春天去过那个洞穴，但它早就忘记里面什么样了。</>"] = "　　<InvDefault_HW>On the last day of that year, the forest encountered a blizzard unseen in a century. The Owl Elder convened an emergency meeting.</>\n\n　　<InvDefault_HW>\"The snow above the cave in the north has collapsed. The bat family that hibernates there is still inside; we cannot leave them to their fate.\"</>\n\n　　<InvDefault_HW>All the animals fell into silence. They basically didn't interact with the bats. Only Dunn had been to that cave last spring, but it had long since forgotten what it looked like inside.</>",
    ["　　<InvDefault_HW>邓恩和戴莉认识之后，戴莉就以“自己的羽毛掉光了，好冷”为理由在邓恩头上筑了巢，并为他重复每个被遗忘的信息；邓恩则载着它巡视森林，用厚厚的灰色皮毛为它挡风，用鹿角为它摘下最高处的浆果。</>\n\n　　<InvDefault_HW>戴莉喜欢趴在它脑袋靠后一些的位置，时常抱怨它额前的毛发不够厚实。</>"] = "　　<InvDefault_HW>After Dunn and Daly got to know each other, Daly built a nest on Dunn's head under the pretext that \"my feathers have all fallen out, I'm so cold,\" and repeated every forgotten piece of information to him; Dunn would carry her to patrol the forest, using its thick gray fur to shield her from the wind and its antlers to pick berries from the highest branches.</>\n\n　　<InvDefault_HW>Daly liked to lie on the back of its head, often complaining that the fur on its forehead wasn't thick enough.</>",
    ["　　<InvDefault_HW>银雾森林迎来了今年的第一场雪，东边的雾气也越发浓厚，掉落了不少羽毛的戴莉在窝里冻得直发抖。枝头小小的巢穴无法抵御寒冷，顶上抖落的一坨雪将巢穴砸落下去，戴莉还没来得及发出叫声，就发现自己被温暖的灰色皮毛包裹——它落在了一只灰麋鹿的头顶。</>\n\n　　<InvDefault_HW>“我察觉到这里有动物需要帮助，是你吗？”那只灰麋鹿这么说道。</>"] = "　　<InvDefault_HW> The Silver Mist Forest welcomed the first snow of the year, and the mist in the east grew even thicker. Daly, having lost many feathers, shivered in its nest from the cold. The tiny nest on the branch could not withstand the chill, and a clump of snow shaken from above knocked the nest down. Before Daly could even let out a cry, it found itself wrapped in warm, grey fur—it had landed on the head of a grey moose. </>\n\n　　<InvDefault_HW> \"I sensed that an animal here needed help. Is it you?\" the grey moose said. </>",
    ["　　<InvHighlight>罗塞尔·古斯塔夫</>，与其简单称之为“大帝”，更应称之为一个时代，一个传奇。\n\n　　历史孕育了不计其数名留青史的统治者，却只出现了一个罗塞尔·古斯塔夫，他的学识、品味、创造心、行动力堪称神赐——他的出现所造福的并不只是因蒂斯，更是这个世界、这个时代！"] = "<InvHighlight> Roselle Gustav </>, rather than simply calling him \"Emperor,\" he should be called an era, a legend. \n \n History has nurtured countless rulers who have left their names in history, but there has only been one Roselle Gustav. His knowledge, taste, creativity, and drive can be called god-given—the benefits brought by his appearance are not just for Intis, but for this world, this era!",
    ["　　<Letter_Highlight>《大冒险家·格尔曼海上历险》</>\n　　借阅人：丹尼 \n\n　　<Letter_Highlight>《机械制造工程基础》</>\n　　借阅人：菲利克斯\n　　……\n　　为了图书的正常流通，希望这些读者尽快归还所借图书，认真学习借阅相关的规章制度并遵照执行。"] = "<Letter_Highlight> \"The Great Adventurer: Gehrman's Sea Adventures\" </>\n Borrower: Danny \n\n <Letter_Highlight> \"Fundamentals of Mechanical Engineering\" </>\n Borrower: Felix \n ... \n For the normal circulation of books, we hope these readers will return the borrowed books as soon as possible, study the relevant borrowing rules and regulations carefully, and comply with them.",
    ["　　<Letter_Highlight_HW>梅丽莎</>今天从贝克兰德回来，本来该我去接她的。\n　　但教会临时有点事，辛苦你帮我去黑荆棘接待一下。\n　　你在“愚者”先生的历史里见过她，虽然过了几年，她可能也长高了，但模样应该变化不大。\n　　给你个机会，好好表现！"] = "<Letter_Highlight_HW> Melissa </> is coming back from Backlund today, I was supposed to pick her up. \n But the Church has some urgent matters, so I'd appreciate it if you could help me receive her at Blackthorn. \n You've seen her in Mr. Fool's history; although it's been a few years and she might have grown taller, her appearance shouldn't have changed much. \n Here's your chance, make a good impression!",
    ["　　<Mark id=\"#159\">蒸汽机</>，如今连最贫苦的乞儿都知晓的发明，正是出自罗塞尔之手，自脱胎伊始便注定推动世界——用罗塞尔本人的话说——发明蒸汽机的初衷，就是为了解放这个世界的生产力。\n　　事实证明，他做到了，而与他后来的诸多成就相比，这个旷世杰作竟只是开始。\n　　……（大片被啃食的痕迹）\n　　罗塞尔大帝是历史记载以来最伟大的发明家，“工匠之神”的垂青证实了这一点。罗塞尔是忠实的“工匠之神”信徒，他统治期间，“工匠之神”教会得到了第五纪以来第一份公开神谕——将“工匠之神”改称为“蒸汽与机械之神”，将罗塞尔的发明写入神名。\n　　……（大片被啃食的痕迹）"] = "<Mark id=\"#159\"> Steam engine </>, an invention known even to the poorest beggar today, came from Roselle's hands. From its inception, it was destined to push the world forward—in Roselle's own words—the original intention of inventing the steam engine was to liberate the productivity of this world. \n Facts have proven that he succeeded, and compared to his many later achievements, this masterpiece was just the beginning. \n ... (Large areas of gnawed marks) \n Emperor Roselle is the greatest inventor recorded in history, and the favor of the \"God of Craftsmanship\" confirms this. Roselle was a loyal believer of the \"God of Craftsmanship.\" During his reign, the Church of the \"God of Craftsmanship\" received the first public oracle since the Fifth Epoch—renaming the \"God of Craftsmanship\" to the \"God of Steam and Machinery\" and writing Roselle's inventions into the divine name. \n ... (Large areas of gnawed marks)",
    ["　　<Mark id=\"#159\">隐匿贤者</>最初只是一名非人格化的神灵。\n　　相比起神灵，祂更接近于一种理念，一种自然法则，或者说，知识本身。\n　　信仰祂的摩斯苦修会掌握着<Mark id=\"#159\">“窥秘人”</>途径的魔药与晋升方式……会内流传着一句格言——<InvHighlight_HW>为所欲为，但勿伤害</>——这也为许多“窥秘人”所信奉并践行。\n　　……贝尔纳黛殿下似乎也很喜欢。"] = "<Mark id=\"#159\"> The Hidden Sage </> was initially just an impersonal deity. \n Compared to a god, It was closer to a concept, a natural law, or rather, knowledge itself. \n The Moses Ascetic Order, which believes in It, possesses the potions and advancement methods of the <Mark id=\"#159\"> \"Mystery Pryer\" </> pathway... A maxim circulates within the order—<InvHighlight_HW> Do what you will, but do no harm </>—which is also believed in and practiced by many \"Mystery Pryers.\" \n ... Her Highness Bernadette seems to like it as well.",
    ["　　<TarotTextCurrent>{{PlayerName}}</>与<TarotTextCurrent>黑荆棘安保公司</>签订本合同。经双方协商，签订如下条款：\n\n　　即日起，立约人加入黑荆棘安保公司，成为正式员工。薪资及保密补贴另议。立约人须严格遵守保密条款，违反条款将受到黑夜女神教会仲裁庭的直接审判。\n\n　　本合同有效期为十四年，期满后可视情况，决定是否续签。\n\n　　出于安全考虑和保密原则，立约人如离开廷根市，须保证公司已知情或批准。"] = "<TarotTextCurrent>{{PlayerName}}</> enters into this contract with <TarotTextCurrent>Blackthorn Security Company</>. Through mutual negotiation, the following terms are agreed upon: \n\n Effective immediately, the signatory joins Blackthorn Security Company as a formal employee. Salary and confidentiality subsidies are to be discussed separately. The signatory must strictly abide by the confidentiality clauses; violation of these clauses will result in a direct trial by the Nighthawks' Tribunal of the Evernight Goddess Church. \n\n This contract is valid for fourteen years, after which it may be renewed depending on the circumstances. \n\n For safety and confidentiality reasons, if the signatory leaves Tingen, they must ensure the company is informed or has granted approval.",
    ["　　——更离奇的是，每当读者试图翻到“营救公主”章节时，书页总会自动跳转到“如何烹饪仰望星空派”的食谱。"] = "　　—Even more bizarrely, whenever the reader tries to flip to the \"Rescue the Princess\" chapter, the page always automatically jumps to the recipe for \"How to Cook Stargazy Pie.\"",
    ["　　“不要在意什么‘毒素专家’，我是一个很友好的人，只要不面对那些该死的家伙！我最大的爱好是研究土壤、作物和品种杂交技术，相信我，这才是人类的未来。”\n　　“但大地母神教会的人不相信。”嘉德丽雅用非常隐蔽的方式为克莱恩做了介绍。\n　　原本是大地母神的人？品种杂交技术挺好的啊，只有产量提升，才能养活更多的人类，让贫困的底限变高……克莱恩看向弗兰克·李，半是礼貌半是真心地平静说道：\n　　“这是好事。”\n　　“……你果然是一位不在乎世俗观点的冒险家！非常棒，非常棒！这个世界上就是你这样的人太少了！”弗兰克·李蓝色的眼睛里露出明显的惊喜，“我只是试图把公牛、母牛和小麦杂交在一起，让小牛可以像麦子一样长出来，就差点被母神教会的人送上审判庭，仁慈的母亲啊，他们根本没有真正理解您的意志！”\n　　公牛、母牛和小麦杂交……你这个恶魔……克莱恩这才发现自己理解的品种杂交技术和对方口中的完全不是一回事情。\n\n　　——第三卷《旅行家》第一百五十六章 毒素专家"] = " \"Don't mind the 'Poison Expert' thing; I am a very friendly person, as long as I'm not facing those damn guys! My biggest hobby is researching soil, crops, and cross-breeding technology. Believe me, this is the future of humanity.\" \n \"But the people of the Earth Mother Church don't believe it.\" Cattleya introduced Klein in a very subtle way. \n Originally from the Earth Mother Church? Cross-breeding technology is quite good. Only by increasing production can we feed more people, raise the bottom line of poverty... Klein looked at Frank Lee and said calmly, half-politely and half-sincerely: \n \"This is a good thing.\" \n \"...You really are an adventurer who doesn't care about worldly views! Very good, very good! There are too few people like you in this world!\" Frank Lee's blue eyes showed obvious surprise. \"I just tried to cross-breed bulls, cows, and wheat together so that calves could grow like wheat, and I was almost sent to the tribunal by the Mother Church. Merciful Mother, they didn't really understand your will at all!\" \n Cross-breeding bulls, cows, and wheat... You devil... Klein only then realized that the cross-breeding technology he understood was completely different from what the other party was talking about. \n \n —— Volume 3 \"Traveler\", Chapter 156, Poison Expert",
    ["　　“他们赤身裸体，无衣无食，在寒冷中毫无遮掩。”\n　　“他们被大雨淋湿，因为没有躲避之处，就紧抱磐石。”\n　　“他们是孩子被夺走的母亲，他们是失去了希望的孤儿，他们是被逼离开了正道的穷人。”\n　　“黑夜没有放弃他们，给予了他们眷顾。”"] = "“They are naked, without clothing or food, exposed in the cold.” \n “They are drenched by heavy rain, and having no shelter, they cling to the rocks.” \n “They are mothers whose children have been taken, they are orphans who have lost hope, and they are the poor who have been forced off the righteous path.” \n “The Evernight Goddess did not abandon them, but bestowed Her favor upon them.”",
    ["　　“内部资料”的卖家已经<Letter_Highlight>自首</>，涉事人员已接受相应处理。\n　　同时为保证正常教学秩序和考试公平，历史系将于下周三开启<Letter_Highlight>重考</>和<Letter_Highlight>补考</>。\n　　请同学们引以为戒，认真复习，诚实作答。"] = "　　The seller of the \"internal materials\" has <Letter_Highlight>turned themselves in</>, and the individuals involved have been dealt with accordingly.\n　　Meanwhile, to ensure normal teaching order and examination fairness, the History Department will hold <Letter_Highlight>retakes</> and <Letter_Highlight>make-up exams</> next Wednesday.\n　　Students, please take this as a warning, study diligently, and answer honestly.",
    ["　　“内部资料”的卖家已经<Letter_Highlight>自首</>，涉事人员已接受相应处理。\n　　同时为保证正常教学秩序和考试公平，历史系将于下周三开启<Letter_Highlight>重考和补考</>。\n　　请同学们引以为戒，认真复习，诚实作答。"] = "　　The seller of the \"internal materials\" has <Letter_Highlight>turned themselves in</>, and the individuals involved have been dealt with accordingly.\n　　Meanwhile, to ensure normal teaching order and examination fairness, the History Department will hold <Letter_Highlight>retakes and make-up exams</> next Wednesday.\n　　Students, please take this as a warning, study diligently, and answer honestly.",
    ["　　“发生了什么事情？”克莱恩心头咯噔了一下。\n　　他害怕这个疯狂的“杂交学家”的实验出了问题，导致“未来号”众人陷入可怕的生态灾难里。\n　　弗兰克呆滞摇头道：\n　　“我不是给你说过那些小东西吗？\n　　“它们原本需要安眠一段时间才有可能生长和繁殖，结果……”\n　　“结果什么？”克莱恩的脸色已变得凝重。\n　　蹲着的弗兰克抬头上望道：\n　　“它们刚才完成了大规模的繁殖，还发生了异变。\n　　“这，这简直是神迹！”\n　　“然后呢？它们去了哪里？还在你的‘实验室’内吗？”克莱恩直觉地认为这不是好事。\n　　弗兰克用两秒钟的时间消化了问题，挽起袖子，露出体毛浓密的手臂。\n　　他敲了敲面前的甲板，露出疑惑的笑容道。\n　　“它们钻进了这里，好像在，在改造‘未来号’……”\n　　沉闷的敲击声中，甲板上突然涌出了一股疑似牛奶的乳白喷泉，溅了弗兰克·李满头满脸。\n　　他舔了嘴边的液体一口，惊喜出声道：\n　　“‘未来号’，‘未来号’产奶了！”\n\n　　——第三卷《旅行家》第一百七十四章 疯狂的异变"] = "“What happened?” Klein’s heart skipped a beat. \n He was afraid that this crazy “Hybridizer’s” experiment had gone wrong, causing the people on the Future to fall into a terrifying ecological disaster. \n Frank shook his head dully and said: \n “Didn’t I tell you about those little things? \n They originally needed to slumber for a period of time before they could grow and reproduce, but as a result…” \n “As a result of what?” Klein’s expression had become grave. \n Frank, who was squatting, looked up and said: \n “They just completed large-scale reproduction, and a mutation occurred. \n This, this is simply a miracle!” \n “Then what? Where did they go? Are they still in your ‘laboratory’?” Klein intuitively felt that this was not a good thing. \n Frank took two seconds to digest the question, rolled up his sleeves, and revealed his hairy arms. \n He knocked on the deck in front of him and said with a puzzled smile. \n “They drilled in here, it seems they are, they are modifying the Future…” \n Amidst the dull knocking sound, a milky white fountain suspected to be milk suddenly gushed out from the deck, splashing Frank Lee all over his head and face. \n He licked the liquid by his mouth and said in surprise: \n “The Future, the Future is producing milk!” \n \n —— Volume 3: Traveler, Chapter 174: Crazy Mutation",
    ["　　“啊对，有个前提，你必须牢记，并严格遵守！”\n　　老尼尔放好两根蜡烛，侧过身体，看向克莱恩，非常严肃地说道：\n　　“低序列者本身还不够强大，能进行的几乎所有仪式魔法都是向外在祈求力量，请求帮助，所以，只能考虑女神、风暴之主等正统神灵，绝对，绝对不要试图沟通未知的、难以预料的存在，哪怕有人信奉祂们，哪怕记载的承诺充满诱惑！”\n　　“相信我，不要抱有侥幸的心态，只要尝试过一次，你就会不可避免地滑向深渊，一切的努力，一切的抗争，都只能延缓速度，无法扭转趋势。”\n\n　　——第一卷《小丑》第五十三章 接地气的仪式魔法"] = " \"Oh right, there is a prerequisite that you must keep in mind and strictly follow!\" \n Old Neil placed the two candles, turned his body to look at Klein, and said very seriously: \n \"Low-sequence Beyonders are not yet powerful enough, and almost all Ritual Magic that can be performed is to beg for power and request help from the outside. Therefore, you can only consider orthodox gods like the Goddess and the Lord of Storms. Absolutely, absolutely do not try to communicate with unknown, unpredictable existences, even if someone worships them, and even if the recorded promises are full of temptation!\" \n \"Believe me, do not hold a lucky mindset. As long as you try it once, you will inevitably slide into the abyss. All efforts and all struggles can only delay the speed, not reverse the trend.\" \n \n —— Volume 1 \"Clown\", Chapter 53, Grounded Ritual Magic",
    ["　　“在吃的法则里，风味重于一切。”当我吃到库克的菜时，才领会到了这句话的真谛。\n　　如今，库克将海岸线的美味带到了廷根，和海岸线餐厅一同登上廷根餐厅榜首。"] = "\"In the laws of eating, flavor is more important than anything else.\" It was only when I tasted Cook's cooking that I truly understood the essence of this sentence. \n Now, Cook has brought the delicious flavors of the coastline to Tingen, and together with Coastline Restaurant, they have topped the Tingen restaurant rankings.",
    ["　　“在成为值夜者之前，我的梦想是做一位画家。”弗莱的语气没有一点起伏。\n　　“那为什么不去实现梦想呢？”克莱恩疑惑问道。\n　　弗莱放好铅笔，手拿燕尾服小丑的肖像道：\n　　“我的父亲是女神的牧师，希望我也成为一名牧师，这是足够体面的职业。”\n　　“你做过牧师？”克莱恩愕然再问。\n　　他很难想象弗莱这种性格这种气质的人做牧师。\n　　“嗯，做得还不坏。”弗莱表情冷漠，嘴角隐有点上翘地回答道，“后来遇见了一些事情，经历了一些事情，就成为值夜者了。”\n\n　　——第一卷《小丑》第七十八章 心理阴影"] = " \"Before becoming a Nighthawk, my dream was to be a painter.\" Frye's tone had no fluctuations at all. \n \"Then why not realize your dream?\" Klein asked in confusion. \n Frye put away his pencil and held the portrait of the tailcoat clown: \n \"My father was a priest of the Goddess and hoped that I would also become a priest. It's a decent enough profession.\" \n \"You were a priest?\" Klein asked again in astonishment. \n He found it hard to imagine someone with Frye's personality and temperament being a priest. \n \"Hmm, and I wasn't bad at it.\" Frye replied with a cold expression and a slightly upturned corner of his mouth, \"Later, I encountered some things, experienced some things, and became a Nighthawk.\" \n \n —— Volume 1 \"Clown\", Chapter 78, Psychological Shadow",
    ["　　“它是通灵的好帮手，也是足够迷人的花精……”\n　　随着戴莉的娓娓述说，克莱恩只觉她的声音从四面八方传来。\n　　迷惑望向四周，克莱恩发现所有事物都在摇晃，都在模糊，像是笼罩了一层又一层的浓雾，连带着自己的身体都跟着摇晃，跟着模糊，跟着发飘，跟着失去了重量。\n　　红的更红，蓝的更蓝，黑的更黑，色彩混杂如同印象派油画，迷离而梦幻，而周围细碎重叠的呢喃一阵阵传来，像是有数不清的无形之人在议论。\n　　“这和我之前做‘转运仪式’时的感觉类似啊，但没有那种让人疯狂，让人想要爆炸的味道……”克莱恩看着这一切，疑惑想道。\n　　就在这时，他的视线被一双晶莹如同绿宝石的眼眸吸引了，穿黑袍的戴莉坐在模糊的“沙发”上，目光诡异地集中于克莱恩的头顶，嗓音温柔地笑道：\n　　“正式认识一下，我，‘通灵者’戴莉。”\n\n　　——第一卷《小丑》 第十四章 信"] = "\"It's a great helper for Spirit Mediumship, and also a charming flower spirit...\"\n As Daly spoke, Klein felt her voice coming from all directions.\n Looking around in confusion, Klein found that everything was swaying and blurring, as if shrouded in layers of thick fog. Even his own body was swaying, blurring, floating, and losing its weight.\n The reds became redder, the blues bluer, and the blacks blacker, the colors mixing like an impressionist oil painting, hazy and dreamlike. The fragmented, overlapping whispers around him came in waves, as if countless invisible people were discussing.\n \"This is similar to the feeling I had when I did the 'Fortune-Turning Ritual', but without that flavor that makes people go crazy or want to explode...\" Klein thought, looking at all this in confusion.\n Just then, his gaze was drawn to a pair of eyes as crystalline as emeralds. Daly, dressed in a black robe, sat on a blurry \"sofa,\" her gaze strangely focused on the top of Klein's head, her voice smiling gently:\n \"Let's get to know each other formally. I am the 'Spirit Medium', Daly.\"\n\n — Volume 1: Clown, Chapter 14: Letter",
    ["　　“审判官”带我见了个人。穿着黑袍，说话像机器，自称是“蒸汽与机械之神教会”的使徒。他说非凡力量是通往更高存在的阶梯，只要我愿意，他可以帮我踏入非凡。为了向我展示这一点，他们当着我的面让一个瘦子变成了狼人！真是一群疯子。\n　　我问他，需要付出什么。\n　　他说，忠诚。\n　　我心里骂了他十遍。我只忠诚于廷根。但我没说出口。我需要他的力量，等我变强了，谁忠诚谁还不一定。\n　　但狼人也太他妈丑了，“通识者”也许不错。"] = " The \"Inquisitor\" brought me to meet someone. He was wearing a black robe, spoke like a machine, and claimed to be an Apostle of the God of Steam and Machinery. He said that Beyonder power is a ladder to a higher existence, and as long as I am willing, he can help me step into the extraordinary. To show me this, they turned a skinny man into a werewolf right in front of me! They are truly a bunch of madmen. \n I asked him what I needed to pay. \n He said, loyalty. \n I cursed him ten times in my heart. I am only loyal to Tingen. But I didn't say it out loud. I need his power; once I become stronger, it's not certain who will be loyal to whom. \n But the werewolf is also too damn ugly; \"Savants\" might be good.",
    ["　　“我们是守护者，也是一群时刻对抗着危险和疯狂的可怜虫。”\n　　窗外走廊封闭，石墙冰冷，屋内灯火照耀，明亮发黄，邓恩·史密斯的转述在这样的环境里余音袅袅，一下一下敲打在克莱恩的心头，让他短暂竟说不出话来。\n　　见克莱恩默然，邓恩摇头笑道：\n　　“是不是很失望？非凡者和你想象的并不一样，我们一直在与危险同行。”\n　　“有获得，就肯定有代价。”克莱恩从刚才的震撼里平复，斟酌着语气回答。\n　　他确实没想到非凡者光耀、超常、不同于普通的一面外，还有这样的隐患，不过或许是因为只听到描述，还没真切遭遇，也或许是由于本身已经卷入这个漩涡，说不定什么时候就有诡异事件落到身上，他的害怕、忐忑、担心和畏惧等情绪很快便降低到可以控制的程度。\n\n　　——第一卷《小丑》第二十章 起源和原因"] = "\"We are guardians, and also a bunch of poor wretches constantly fighting against danger and madness.\"\n Outside the window, the corridor was sealed and the stone walls were cold. Inside, the lamplight shone bright and yellow. Dunn Smith's retelling lingered in such an environment, striking Klein's heart beat by beat, leaving him momentarily speechless.\n Seeing Klein silent, Dunn shook his head and smiled:\n \"Disappointed? Beyonders aren't what you imagined; we are always walking alongside danger.\"\n \"With gain, there must be a price.\" Klein recovered from the shock and replied, weighing his words.\n He truly hadn't expected that beyond the glorious, extraordinary, and unique aspects of being a Beyonder, there were such hidden dangers. Perhaps it was because he had only heard the description and hadn't truly encountered them yet, or perhaps because he was already caught in this vortex and could face bizarre events at any time, his fear, anxiety, and worry quickly subsided to a controllable level.\n\n — Volume 1: Clown, Chapter 20: Origin and Reason",
    ["　　“看来我需要证明自己。”\n　　她缓步走到门边，伸出右掌，按在了把手的位置。\n　　霍然间，奥黛丽眼前一花，似乎看见佛尔思女士变成幻影，穿透了大门。\n　　她心中惊骇，凝神再看，发现佛尔思已不在原地。\n　　几秒之后，把手转动，反锁住的房门被直接打开，佛尔思·沃尔含笑从外面走了进来，守在门口不远处的女仆安妮却丝毫没有察觉到背后发生的事情。\n　　“这真是神奇的能力啊。”格莱林特赞叹出声。\n\n　　——第一卷《小丑》第一百零七章 佛尔思"] = "\"It seems I need to prove myself.\"\n She walked slowly to the door, extended her right palm, and pressed it against the handle.\n Suddenly, Audrey's vision blurred, and she seemed to see Ms. Fors turn into a phantom and pass through the door.\n She was horrified and looked again, only to find that Fors was no longer in her original spot.\n A few seconds later, the handle turned, and the locked door was opened directly. Fors Wall walked in from outside with a smile, while the maid Annie, who was guarding not far from the door, had not noticed what happened behind her at all.\n \"This is truly a magical ability,\" Gregrace exclaimed.\n\n — Volume 1: Clown, Chapter 107: Fors",
    ["　　“红手套”有紧急任务，我需要暂时离开几天。\n　　黑荆棘安保公司是“愚者”先生非凡之旅的开始之地，无论你想进一步了解“愚者”先生，还是开始属于自己的非凡故事，在这里成为值夜者小队成员，将是一个不错的选择，弗莱是一位值得信赖的队长。最后保管好“愚者”先生留下的金币。"] = "The \"Red Gloves\" have an emergency mission, and I need to leave for a few days.\nBlackthorn Security Company is where Mr. Fool's extraordinary journey began. Whether you want to learn more about Mr. Fool or start your own extraordinary story, becoming a member of the Nighthawks squad here is a good choice. Frye is a trustworthy captain. Finally, keep the gold coin left by Mr. Fool safe.",
    ["　　“魔术师”佛尔思悄然吸了口气道：\n　　“我想求购食灵者的胃袋和20毫升深海枪鱼的血液，用金镑支付。”\n　　我还有430镑，能买得起一件……她默默鼓励了自己一句。\n　　至于剩下那件的钱从哪里来，她一时半会也没有办法。\n       这就是制约许多非凡者晋升的主要原因之一……人呐，真的不能尝试超过本身能力的消费，如果不是为了彻底摆脱满月呓语的影响，成为“戏法大师”，有了相对丰富的超凡手段之后，我都不会再考虑晋升的问题，甚至不再接触这个圈子，写写书，攒攒钱，喝喝茶，和休一起逛逛街，等她完成那件事情后，就到北大陆南大陆不同的地方旅行，不害怕危险和意外，好好享受生活……佛尔思的思绪忽然有些发散。\n\n       ——第二卷《无面人》第一百四十七章 一个困难的问题"] = "\"Magician\" Fors quietly took a breath and said:\n \"I would like to purchase the stomach of a Spirit Eater and 20ml of blood from a Deep Sea Marlin, paying with gold pounds.\"\n I still have 430 pounds, I can afford one... she encouraged herself silently.\n As for where the money for the other item would come from, she had no idea for the moment.\n This is one of the main reasons that restricts the advancement of many Beyonders... People really shouldn't try to consume beyond their own means. If it weren't for completely getting rid of the influence of the full moon's whispers and becoming a \"Faceless,\" having relatively rich extraordinary means, I wouldn't even consider advancement, or even touch this circle. I'd just write books, save money, drink tea, go shopping with Xio, and after she finishes that matter, travel to different places in the Northern and Southern Continents, not fearing danger or accidents, and enjoy life properly... Fors's thoughts suddenly wandered.\n\n — Volume 2: Faceless, Chapter 147: A Difficult Question",
    ["　　……\n\n　　<InvHighlight>卡拉</>\n　　女孩，12岁，无固定住所，玫瑰精油厂工人，负责玫瑰花瓣清洗。\n　　无近亲在世。\n\n　　<InvHighlight>玛格丽特</>\n　　女性，历史案件关联人员，生前居住于贝克兰德桥区\n　　儿子皮特；女儿伊妮德；丈夫失踪。\n\n　　……"] = "... \n \n <InvHighlight> Carla </> \n Girl, 12 years old, no fixed residence, worker at a rose essential oil factory, responsible for cleaning rose petals. \n No close relatives alive. \n \n <InvHighlight> Margaret </> \n Female, person associated with a historical case, lived in the Backlund Bridge area before her death \n Son Pete; daughter Enid; husband missing. \n \n ...",
    ["　　……\n\n　　<InvHighlight>米格尔</>\n　　男性，42岁，居住于金梧桐区，著名进出口贸易商人。\n　　妻子帕梅拉；情人雷妮、玛莎；儿子保罗；女儿维尔拉；私生子贝克。\n\n　　<InvHighlight>贝丝</>\n　　女性，24岁，纺织工人，有严重关节和肺部疾病。\n　　母亲维纳；弟弟迪恩。\n\n　　……"] = "... \n \n <InvHighlight> Miguel </> \n Male, 42 years old, resides in the North Borough, a famous import and export merchant. \n Wife Pamela; mistresses Renée, Martha; son Paul; daughter Vera; illegitimate son Baker. \n \n <InvHighlight> Beth </> \n Female, 24 years old, textile worker, has severe joint and lung diseases. \n Mother Vina; younger brother Dean. \n \n ...",
    ["　　……\n\n　　使用银制 <Mark id=\"#159\">仪式匕首</>，取<InvHighlight>双腕鲜血少许</>、混合后涂抹于仪式法阵之上，坚定以自身意志主动束缚灵魂的决心……服下不朽苔的汁液，念诵：“躯壳暂归永夜，真名藏于灰烬。” \n\n　　……<Tips stylename=\"Letter_Highlight\" id=\"#160\">躯体呈现所有死亡表征</>，七日后恢复如常。"] = "... \n \n Use a silver <Mark id=\"#159\"> Ritual Dagger, </> take <InvHighlight> a little blood from both wrists, </> mix it, and smear it on the ritual magic circle, firming the determination to actively bind the soul with one's own will... Take the juice of the Immortal Moss and chant: \"The shell temporarily returns to the eternal night, the true name is hidden in the ashes.\" \n \n ... <Tips stylename=\"Letter_Highlight\" id=\"#160\"> The body presents all the signs of death, </> and returns to normal after seven days.",
    ["　　……\n\n　　取受术者发丝与施术者 <Mark id=\"#159\">发丝纠缠</>，用双生草根须榨取的汁液1:1混合<InvHighlight>施术者掌心血</>，浸泡整夜。日出前取该液体绘制法阵，念诵：“彼此照映的星星啊，离开既定的轨道。此星晦暗，彼星长明。”\n\n　　……命运错轨，<Tips stylename=\"Letter_Highlight\" id=\"#160\">必死者重获新生</>。 "] = "... \n \n Take the hair of the subject and the <Mark id=\"#159\"> hair </> of the caster, mix it 1:1 with the juice extracted from the roots of the Twin Grass and <InvHighlight> the blood from the caster's palm, </> and soak it overnight. Before sunrise, use this liquid to draw a magic circle and chant: \"Oh, stars that reflect each other, leave the established orbit. This star is dim, that star shines long.\" \n \n ... The fate is derailed, <Tips stylename=\"Letter_Highlight\" id=\"#160\"> and the one who must die is reborn. </>",
    ["　　……\n　　1350年\n　　贝克兰德非凡聚会中，有人出售来自南大陆帕斯河谷的“<Mark id=\"#159\">月亮木偶</>”，并引发追杀案件。\n\n　　1352年\n　　廷根技术学院十四名学生在郊外举行邪恶仪式，导致现场<Mark id=\"#159\">植物</>疯狂生长，仅一人幸存。\n\n　　1353年\n　　一片安葬贝克兰德大雾霾死难者的坟墓被河水冲毁，几座空坟中均发现破旧的“月亮木偶”。\n　　……"] = "... \n 1350 \n During a Beyonder gathering in Backlund, someone sold a \"<Mark id=\"#159\">Moon Puppet</>\" from the Pas River Valley in the Southern Continent, triggering a murder case. \n \n 1352 \n Fourteen students from the Tingen Technical College held an evil ritual in the suburbs, causing <Mark id=\"#159\"> plants </> to grow wildly at the scene, with only one survivor. \n \n 1353 \n A patch of graves burying the victims of the Backlund Smog was washed away by the river, and broken, old \"Moon Puppets\" were found in several empty graves. \n ...",
    ["　　……\n　　6月13日\n　　<InvHighlight>金梧桐区</>五十户居民家中<Mark id=\"#159\">下水道</>堵塞，清理时发现管道被<Mark id=\"#159\">植物藤蔓</>塞满。\n\n　　6月14日\n　　富商米格尔死于<InvHighlight>金梧桐区</>的玻璃花房，被发现时身上结满紫红色葡萄。\n\n　　6月18日\n　　纺织工人贝丝在<InvHighlight>南区</>捡到三根蜡烛和一段木头手臂，现场有<Mark id=\"#159\">邪恶仪式</>的痕迹。\n　　……"] = "... \n June 13th \n <InvHighlight> North Borough </> In the homes of fifty residents <Mark id=\"#159\"> sewers </> were blocked, and during cleaning, it was discovered that the pipes were stuffed with <Mark id=\"#159\"> plant vines </>. \n \n June 14th \n Wealthy merchant Miguel died in a <InvHighlight> glass conservatory in the North Borough </>, and when discovered, his body was covered in purple-red grapes. \n \n June 18th \n Textile worker Beth found three candles and a wooden arm in the <InvHighlight> South District </>, and there were traces of an <Mark id=\"#159\"> evil ritual </> at the scene. \n ...",
    ["　　……\n　　……\n　　玫瑰葬身风暴，\n　　侠盗痛失所爱。\n——————\n批注：\n　　自由，也许比生命更加珍贵。\n　　而爱，将使人永远铭记。\n\n　　如果那个人知道我一直在等待，\n　　他会出现吧，\n　　就像英雄，从天而降。"] = "... \n ... \n The rose was buried in the storm, \n The Phantom Thief lost his beloved. \n —————— \n Annotation: \n Freedom may be more precious than life. \n And love will make people remember forever. \n \n If that person knew I had been waiting, \n He would appear, right? \n Just like a hero, descending from the sky.",
    ["　　……\n　　一个贵族夫人遇到了凶恶的劫匪。\n　　玫瑰夫人不禁哀叹自己生命的短暂与脆弱，心中盛满了悲伤。\n　　……\n　　……\n　　没有想到，英雄从天而降，拯救了陷入泥沼的玫瑰。\n　　……\n　　……\n　　这一刻，她忘记了方才的危险与过往无趣的生活，她仿佛看到了一本世界上最有趣的冒险小说，而自己竟然就是故事书的女主人公！\n　　……"] = "... \n A noble lady encountered a vicious robber. \n Lady Rose could not help but lament the brevity and fragility of her life, her heart filled with sadness. \n ... \n ... \n Unexpectedly, a hero descended from the sky and saved the rose that had fallen into the mire. \n ... \n ... \n At this moment, she forgot the danger just now and her boring life in the past; she felt as if she had seen the most interesting adventure novel in the world, and she was actually the heroine of the storybook! \n ...",
    ["　　……\n　　不知从什么时候起，<Mark id=\"#159\">隐匿贤者</>疑似活化。\n　　祂疯狂地追逐着每一个摩斯苦修会的成员，甚至是每一个“窥秘人”，这种现象被称为<Mark id=\"#159\">“知识逐人”</>。\n　　当海潮般的知识灌注而来时，受灌输者要么放开心灵防线，接受祂的<Hide id=\"#157\">改造</>，要么凭毅力支撑。\n　　当知识灌注冲破毅力防线的那一刻，便会引发<Hide id=\"#157\">失控</>。\n　　但，我想，祂的灌输，未必没有用处。"] = "... \n I do not know when it started, but the <Mark id=\"#159\"> Hidden Sage </> is suspected to have become active. \n It madly pursues every member of the Moses Ascetic Order, and even every \"Mystery Pryer.\" This phenomenon is known as <Mark id=\"#159\"> \"Knowledge Pursuit.\" </> \n When the tidal wave of knowledge pours in, the recipient must either open their mental defenses and accept Its <Hide id=\"#157\"> transformation, </> or support themselves with willpower. \n The moment the infusion of knowledge breaks through the defense of willpower, it triggers <Hide id=\"#157\"> loss of control. </> \n However, I think Its infusion may not be without its uses.",
    ["　　……\n　　不知从什么时候起，“隐匿贤者”疑似活化。\n　　祂是无处不在的灵数，是知识本身，祂疯狂地追逐着每一个摩斯苦修会的成员，甚至是每一个“窥秘人”，这种现象被称为“知识逐人”。\n　　当海潮般的知识灌注而来时，受灌输者要么放开心灵防线，接受“隐匿贤者”的改造，要么凭毅力支撑。\n　　当知识灌注冲破毅力防线的那一刻，便会引发失控。\n　　但，我想，祂的灌输，未必没有用处。"] = "... \n I do not know when it started, but the \"Hidden Sage\" is suspected to have become active. \n It is the ubiquitous spiritual number, the knowledge itself. It madly pursues every member of the Moses Ascetic Order, and even every \"Mystery Pryer.\" This phenomenon is known as \"Knowledge Pursuit.\" \n When the tidal wave of knowledge pours in, the recipient must either open their mental defenses and accept the transformation by the \"Hidden Sage,\" or support themselves with willpower. \n The moment the infusion of knowledge breaks through the defense of willpower, it triggers a loss of control. \n However, I think Its infusion may not be without its uses.",
    ["　　……\n　　失踪者家属聚集警局门口抗议，警方表示“失踪案件均已登记处理”。据悉，近期此类事件已发生十余起，多为政府雇员。\n　　……\n\n<Note_Normal_HW>这些是我们的人，这家伙在干嘛！</>\n<Note_Normal_HW>他疯了，赶紧处理掉，不要留下把柄！</>\n<Note_Normal_HW>查理先生马上要参选了，这时候不能出任何丑闻！</>"] = "……\n The families of the missing have gathered at the police station to protest. The police stated that \"all missing persons cases have been registered and are being processed.\" It is reported that over a dozen such incidents have occurred recently, mostly involving government employees. \n …… \n\n<Note_Normal_HW> These are our people, what is this guy doing! </>\n<Note_Normal_HW> He's gone mad, deal with him quickly, don't leave any evidence behind! </>\n<Note_Normal_HW> Mr. Charlie is about to run for office, we cannot have any scandals at this time! </>",
    ["　　……\n　　玫瑰夫人坐在海岸线餐厅，身边的好友们在谈论着长裙的剪裁、座钟的位置，她却无心倾听。\n　　……\n　　玫瑰夫人对贵族女人的生活感到了厌倦——无趣而又自负的丈夫、和丈夫一个模子刻出来的儿子、永远要保持“体面”的虚伪等等。\n　　……\n　　或许是女神听到了她的祈求，让她和本不应该出现在此的侠盗黑皇帝产生了交集。\n　　……"] = "... \n Lady Rose sat in the Coastline Restaurant, while her friends were talking about the tailoring of long skirts and the position of the grandfather clock, but she had no heart to listen. \n ... \n Lady Rose felt bored with the life of a noblewoman—a boring and conceited husband, a son who was a carbon copy of his father, the hypocrisy of always having to maintain \"decency,\" and so on. \n ... \n Perhaps the Goddess heard her prayer and allowed her to have an intersection with the Phantom Thief Black Emperor, who should not have appeared there. \n ...",
    ["　　……\n　　第五纪1173年，罗塞尔以上校身份平复了叛乱，推翻了腐朽的索伦王室的统治。\n　　他担任执政官，将<InvHighlight>因蒂斯王国</>改为<InvHighlight>因蒂斯共和国</>，带领这个伟大的国度正式踏入最为辉煌的罗塞尔时代。\n　　……（大片被啃食的痕迹）\n　　由于执着于对船只的改良与世界的探索，罗塞尔大帝除了自身热衷于探险之外，还积极组建<Mark id=\"#159\">探索队</>，他于狂暴海的风暴与乱流中开辟了通向<InvHighlight>南大陆</>的航道，让这片尘封于历史隔绝于世的广阔土地沐浴了新时代的阳光。\n　　……（大片被啃食的痕迹）"] = "... \n In 1173 of the Fifth Epoch, Roselle quelled the rebellion as a colonel and overthrew the rule of the corrupt Solon royal family. \n He served as Consul and changed the <InvHighlight> Kingdom of Intis </> to the <InvHighlight> Intis Republic </>, leading this great nation to officially step into the most glorious Roselle era. \n ... (Large areas of gnawed marks) \n Because of his obsession with the improvement of ships and the exploration of the world, in addition to his own enthusiasm for adventure, Emperor Roselle also actively organized <Mark id=\"#159\"> exploration teams </>. He opened up the shipping route to the <InvHighlight> Southern Continent </> amidst the storms and turbulence of the Berserk Sea, allowing this vast land, which had been sealed off from history and isolated from the world, to bathe in the sunshine of the new era. \n ... (Large areas of gnawed marks)",
    ["　　……<Highlight>贝茨太太</>前往黑市购物惨遭欺诈，重金买下<Highlight>鱼血</>等无用物品。两日后贝茨太太<Highlight>失踪</>，推测为发现受骗后离家出走。据悉，贝茨太太平日表现古怪，疑似患有<Highlight>精神疾病</>……"] = "... <Highlight> Mrs. Bates </> went shopping in the black market and was defrauded, spending a large sum of money to buy useless items like <Highlight> fish blood </>. Two days later, Mrs. Bates <Highlight> went missing </>, presumed to have run away from home after discovering she had been deceived. It is reported that Mrs. Bates had been acting strangely, suspected of suffering from <Highlight> mental illness </>...",
    ["　　……什么烂戏，真没意思。\n　　男主角说话简直比我的房东康妮太太还啰嗦、还无聊！\n　　坐在这里的每一秒钟，我都在后悔没有选择去看马戏团的表演。\n　　幸好我带了纸笔，可以写写画画消磨一下时间。\n\n\n画点什么呢？一只小乌龟怎么样……"] = "...What a lousy play, really boring. \n The male lead speaks even more long-windedly and boringly than my landlady, Mrs. Connie! \n Every second I sit here, I regret not choosing to watch the circus performance. \n Fortunately, I brought paper and pen, so I can write and draw to pass the time. \n \n \n What should I draw? How about a little turtle...",
    ["　　……任何两个整数，若它们除以某个正整数的余数相等，则称它们关于该模数同余。同余理论是数论的基石，然而在更广阔的代数数域中，唯一分解律并不总是成立。\n　　我们不得不引入理想数的概念来弥补这一缺陷。\n　　这一缺陷最初只是作为反例被注意到——在某些二次域中，同一个整数可以被分解为不同的素因子乘积，分解的唯一性荡然无存。这对整个算术大厦构成了根本性的动摇。"] = " ...Any two integers, if their remainders when divided by a certain positive integer are equal, are said to be congruent with respect to that modulus. Congruence theory is the cornerstone of number theory, yet in the broader algebraic number field, the law of unique factorization does not always hold. \n We have to introduce the concept of ideal numbers to make up for this defect. \n This defect was initially noticed only as a counterexample—in some quadratic fields, the same integer can be decomposed into products of different prime factors, and the uniqueness of decomposition vanishes. This constitutes a fundamental shaking of the entire arithmetic edifice.",
    ["　　……古弗萨克语的“知识”一词，词根可追溯至更古老的时代，原意为“背负”。在古弗萨克人的观念中，知识不是财富，是需要背负的东西。本书试图考证这一词根在语族中的流变，然而材料有限，迄今未能得出确凿结论。\n　　这一发现本身就值得深思。在多数文明的隐喻中，知识被比作光、比作水、比作可以囤积的财货。而古弗萨克人选择了另一个意象：负重。"] = "　　...The root of the word \"knowledge\" in the ancient Futhark language can be traced back to an even older era, originally meaning \"to carry on one's back.\" In the worldview of the ancient Futhark people, knowledge was not wealth; it was something that needed to be carried. This book attempts to examine the evolution of this root within the language family, yet materials are limited, and no definitive conclusion has been reached to date. \n　　This discovery itself is worth pondering. In the metaphors of most civilizations, knowledge is compared to light, water, or goods that can be stockpiled. The ancient Futhark people, however, chose a different image: bearing a burden.",
    ["　　……热效率的理论极限受卡诺定理约束：任何热机的工作效率都不可能超过工作在相同高低温热源之间的可逆热机。实践中的效率远低于理论值。\n　　这一差距并非工程上的偶然疏忽，而是热力学定律本身划下的鸿沟。即便摩擦被消除、热损失被降至最低、一切机械部件臻于完美，热机依然无法逾越那道由温差决定的效率上限。这是自然界对人造机械施加的绝对禁令。"] = "　　...The theoretical limit of thermal efficiency is constrained by Carnot's theorem: the efficiency of any heat engine cannot exceed that of a reversible heat engine operating between the same high and low-temperature heat sources. Efficiency in practice is far lower than the theoretical value. \n　　This gap is not an accidental oversight in engineering, but a chasm drawn by the laws of thermodynamics themselves. Even if friction were eliminated, heat loss minimized, and every mechanical component perfected, a heat engine would still be unable to surpass that efficiency ceiling determined by the temperature difference. This is an absolute prohibition imposed by nature upon man-made machinery.",
    ["　　……记不清了。只记得有人喊我英雄，有人喊我叛徒。\n　　替我告诉那个影子：廷根烂透了，到处都是脓肿和腐肉，继续挖下去。别像我一样。 "] = " ...I can't remember clearly. I only remember some people calling me a hero, and some calling me a traitor. \n Tell that shadow for me: Tingen is rotten to the core, full of abscesses and rot; keep digging. Don't be like me.",
    ["　　……造物主从混沌中醒来，打破了幽暗，制造了第一缕光，自己则彻底融入宇宙，化身为万物。\n　　祂的身躯成为大地，成为星辰，祂的眼睛一只变为太阳，一只化作红月，祂的部分血液奔腾为大海与江河，滋润和孕育了生命……"] = "…The Creator woke from chaos, broke the darkness, and created the first ray of light, then completely merged into the universe, transforming into all things. \n His body became the earth and the stars, one of His eyes became the Blazing Sun, the other turned into the red moon, and parts of His blood surged into the seas and rivers, nourishing and nurturing life…",
    ["　　一想到你要独自去那种地方，我就忍不住担忧你的安危。但我又与你一样好奇：他们真的和我们一样吗？无论是外表，还是内心？\n此次调查无疑是一项艰巨的任务，路途凶险，还请你务必保重。\n　　如果那里能收到来信，希望你能抽空报个平安。小玛莎和我一直期待着去廷根火车站接你回家的那天！\n　　愿女神庇佑你的归途平安无阻！"] = "Thinking that you have to go to such a place alone, I can't help but worry about your safety. But I am just as curious as you: are they really the same as us? Both in appearance and in heart? \n This investigation is undoubtedly a difficult task, and the journey is dangerous, so please take care. \n If you can receive letters there, I hope you can find time to report that you are safe. Little Martha and I are looking forward to the day we go to Tingen Train Station to pick you up! \n May the Goddess protect your return journey safely!",
    ["　　不用意外！我预先知道你会到这里，留下了这封信，其他人看不到。\n　　我赶稿实在抽不开身，麻烦帮我把这本新书带给塔罗会的“月亮”先生。书钱我已经付过了！\n　　“月亮”目前以大地母神教会执事的身份，在金秋湖调查“丰饶污染”事件。你们正好可以借此认识一下。\n　　对了，“月亮”先生是血族，请一定不要叫他“吸血鬼”——那很不礼貌！\n　　附一张他自己很满意的画像，方便你辨认。\n（字迹越来越潦草……似乎没时间写更多了。） "] = "Don't be surprised! I knew you would come here, so I left this letter; others cannot see it. \n I'm too busy with my manuscript to get away, so please help me bring this new book to Mr. \"Moon\" of the Tarot Club. I've already paid for the book! \n \"Moon\" is currently investigating the \"Abundance Corruption\" incident at Golden Autumn Lake under the guise of a deacon of the Earth Mother church. You can take this opportunity to get to know each other. \n By the way, Mr. \"Moon\" is a vampire, please do not call him a \"blood-sucker\"—that's very impolite! \n Attached is a portrait he is quite satisfied with, to help you identify him. \n (The handwriting is becoming increasingly messy... it seems there's no time to write more.)",
    ["　　不知道还能不能回伦堡，鲁恩的天气太阴沉了，雨水多不适合作物生长。\n\n\n　　主教让我负责后勤保障，顺带研究一下怎么加速魔药消化。\n\n\n　　消化丰收祭司的魔药……要不我在临时据点里种点什么？"] = "I don't know if I can ever return to Lenburg. The weather in Loen is too gloomy, and the rain is not suitable for crop growth. \n \n \n The Bishop asked me to be responsible for logistics and, by the way, research how to accelerate potion digestion. \n \n \n Digesting the Harvest Priest potion... Should I plant something in the temporary stronghold?",
    ["　　为筹备今年的冬礼日，<Highlight>黑夜女神教会</>开始招收唱诗班成员。希望您是黑夜女神的虔诚信徒，有一定的歌唱或朗诵基础。\n　　前往圣赛琳娜教堂面试，教会将给予3苏勒交通和餐饮补贴。"] = "In preparation for this year's Winter Festival, the <Highlight> Evernight Goddess Church </> has begun recruiting choir members. We hope you are a devout believer of the Evernight Goddess and have some singing or recitation foundation. \n Go to Saint Selena Cathedral for an interview; the church will provide a 3-sol transport and meal subsidy.",
    ["　　为给诸位更体面的购物环境，本店将\n　　于即日起暂停营业六周，全店翻修。\n\n　✦  新增进口原木打造专柜\n　✦  全店换装吊灯\n　✦  扩建二楼贵宾厅\n\n　　重新开业日期暂未确定，详情请关注 《贝克兰德邮报》\n　　凭报纸当日到店可享九折优惠"] = "　　To provide a more respectable shopping environment for all, this store will \n　　suspend operations for six weeks starting today for a full renovation.\n\n　✦  Added display counters crafted from imported logs\n　✦  Installed new chandeliers throughout the store\n　✦  Expanded the second-floor VIP lounge\n\n　　The reopening date has yet to be determined; for details, please follow the \"Backlund Post.\"\n　　Present the newspaper on the day of your visit to pay nine-tenths of the regular price.",
    ["　　主教建议我种点水稻，早年她从精灵食谱中学过一种水稻做的美食，又甜又软，十分弹牙。\n\n\n　　种植培育记录就这样写好了：\n　　《“耕种者”途径对农田土壤肥力及作物生长的长期影响：以金秋湖地下遗迹的水稻种植为例》"] = "The Bishop suggested I plant some rice. Years ago, she learned a delicacy made of rice from an elf cookbook, which was sweet, soft, and very chewy. \n \n \n The planting and cultivation record is written like this: \n \"Long-term Effects of the 'Planter' Pathway on Farmland Soil Fertility and Crop Growth: A Case Study of Rice Planting in the Underground Ruins of Golden Autumn Lake\"",
    ["　　乌莎啊乌莎，要坚持自己的想法！\n\n\n　　坚持！一种！作物！\n\n\n　　不要再换了！\n\n\n　　就种水稻！明天就种！这次绝对不改了！"] = "　　Usha, oh Usha, you must stick to your ideas!\n\n\n　　Stick to it! One kind! Of crop!\n\n\n　　Don't change it again!\n\n\n　　Just plant rice! Plant it tomorrow! Definitely won't change it this time!",
    ["　　书桌背后，一个戴着骷髅船长帽、脸色苍白的中年男子看着阿尔杰一步一步过来，愤怒地咬牙说道：\n        “我不会屈服的！”\n        “我相信你做得到。”阿尔杰平静地就像在说今天天气不太好。\n        “你……”中年男子一下怔住，似乎没预料到会是这样的回答。\n        就在这时，阿尔杰身体微弓，突然前冲，瞬间将两人的距离拉近到只剩书桌。\n        啪！\n        他肩膀一紧，右手猛地探出，捏住了中年男子的喉咙。\n        没给对方反应的机会，他手背浮现出片片虚幻鱼鳞，五指疯狂用力。\n\n        ——第一卷《小丑》第八章 新的时代"] = "Behind the desk, a middle-aged man wearing a skull captain's hat and a pale face watched Alger walk over step by step, saying through gritted teeth in anger:\n \"I will not submit!\"\n \"I believe you can do it.\" Alger was as calm as if he were saying the weather today wasn't very good.\n \"You...\" The middle-aged man was stunned, as if he hadn't expected such an answer.\n Just then, Alger's body arched slightly, and he suddenly lunged forward, instantly closing the distance between the two to just the desk.\n Slap!\n His shoulder tightened, and his right hand reached out violently, gripping the middle-aged man's throat.\n Without giving the opponent a chance to react, phantom fish scales appeared on the back of his hand, and his five fingers exerted crazy force.\n\n — Volume 1: Clown, Chapter 8: A New Era",
    ["　　亲爱的赞伯，当你看到这封信时，我已经离开廷根，前往贝克兰德了。\n　　与富有的彭巴特小姐订婚，得到一大笔金镑，很幸福吧？你背弃作为未婚妻的我，诬陷我偷盗财产，将我成功赶出廷根的时候，很得意吧？\n　　这一切的一切，我都记得，我迟早会还回来。"] = "Dear Zamber, by the time you read this letter, I will have already left Tingen for Backlund.\nEngaged to the wealthy Miss Pumbat and receiving a large sum of gold pounds—you must be very happy, right? You betrayed me, your fiancée, framed me for theft, and successfully drove me out of Tingen—you must be very proud of yourself, right?\nI remember every single bit of this, and sooner or later, I will make you pay.",
    ["　　今双方协定，将名下小型城堡领地完整让渡于<TarotTextCurrent> {{PlayerName}} </>：\n\n　　自本契约签署之日起，<TarotTextCurrent> {{PlayerName}} </>即取得该领地的完全所有权、排他使用权与自主经营管理权。\n\n　　领地归<TarotTextCurrent> {{PlayerName}} </>永久持有并自由支配；领地所产生的一切收益、产出及未来增值，均归受<TarotTextCurrent> {{PlayerName}} </>独享。\n\n　　本契约为永久让渡，一经双方签署即生效，具有不可撤销之法律效力。"] = "Both parties hereby agree to the complete transfer of the small castle territory under the name to <TarotTextCurrent> {{PlayerName}} </>: \n\n From the date of signing this contract, <TarotTextCurrent> {{PlayerName}} </> shall obtain full ownership, exclusive usage rights, and autonomous management rights of the territory. \n\n The territory shall be held permanently and freely disposed of by <TarotTextCurrent> {{PlayerName}} </>; all income, output, and future appreciation generated by the territory shall belong exclusively to <TarotTextCurrent> {{PlayerName}} </>. \n\n This contract is a permanent transfer, effective upon signing by both parties, and holds irrevocable legal force.",
    ["　　今天下雨了，适合画一幅蓝色的廷根。"] = "It rained today, a perfect day to paint a blue Tingen.",
    ["　　今天休假，画一张大一些的吧。"] = "　　I'm on leave today, let's paint a larger one.",
    ["　　今天我在那个遗迹里找到一本旧书！\n　　书上提到一种起死回生的魔法，说是要通过仪式向神祈祷，借助丰饶之树的力量什么的。\n　　神指的是女神吗？仪式需要的东西倒是很简单，用平时攒下的零花钱就能买全了！\n　　等着吧，小云，你回来后，我一定给你摘最甜的树莓吃！\n　　这事可不能告诉妈妈，唉，她太爱大惊小怪。\n　　等我把小云带回家，她肯定会吓一大跳吧，嘿嘿。"] = "Today I found an old book in those ruins! \n The book mentions a magic to bring the dead back to life, saying it requires praying to a god through a ritual, using the power of the Tree of Abundance or something. \n Does the god refer to the Goddess? The things needed for the ritual are quite simple; I can buy them all with the pocket money I've saved up! \n Just you wait, Little Cloud, when you come back, I will definitely pick the sweetest raspberries for you to eat! \n I can't tell Mom about this; sigh, she is too prone to making a fuss. \n When I bring Little Cloud home, she will definitely be shocked, hehe.",
    ["　　今天画了一幅画，同学说很好看，我也觉得很好看。\n　　但是父亲说这很丑，他需要我种出好看的白菜，南瓜，去市场上卖个好价钱。\n　　我说好看的画，在画廊也能卖出好价钱。他说菜市场没有门，我们能走过去。画廊的门，我们可推不开。\n　　“永暗的蜡烛，不毁的身躯”，<Letter_RedBig>我觉得这个时代很坏，我不想在这个时代浪费时间了。</>"] = "　　I drew a picture today, my classmate said it was very beautiful, and I think so too.\n　　But father said it was ugly, he needs me to grow good-looking cabbages and pumpkins to sell for a good price at the market.\n　　I said a beautiful painting can also sell for a good price in a gallery. He said the vegetable market has no doors, we can walk right in. The doors of the gallery, we can't push open.\n　　“Candle of Eternal Darkness, Indestructible Body”,<Letter_RedBig> I think this era is very bad, I don't want to waste time in this era anymore.</>",
    ["　　今日，为女神带去了两束薄荷深眠花束。\n\n　　女神庇佑，只要能通过政府雇员考试，让考官爱上我我也愿意！\n\n　　……\n\n　　……\n\n　　失败了……\n\n　　努力出摊，售卖猪腿，争取为女神带去一整个深眠花园。"] = "Today, I brought two bouquets of mint and deep-sleep flowers to the Goddess. \n\n Goddess Protection, as long as I can pass the government employee exam, I'm even willing to make the examiner fall in love with me! \n\n ... \n\n ... \n\n Failed... \n\n I will work hard at my stall, selling pork legs, and strive to bring an entire deep-sleep garden to the Goddess.",
    ["　　今日，哈罗德百货上架新款女士连衣裙、男士衬衫西裤套装，以及每位绅士必备的丝绸礼帽与镶金手杖。对此，老板表示：“这些货都是从海外进口的最新款，欢迎大家前来选购。”……"] = "　　Today, Harold Department Store has stocked new ladies' dresses, men's shirt and trouser suits, as well as silk top hats and gold-inlaid canes that every gentleman must have. Regarding this, the boss said: \"These goods are the latest styles imported from overseas. Everyone is welcome to come and shop.\"...",
    ["　　从我们毕业到现在，已经过去了五年。战争的阴霾已从家乡的上空离开，一切都回到了最初的模样，甚至比当初更好。我想，贝克兰德一定恢复的比这里更迅速。\n　　听说现在的你成了大经理，我由衷地为你闪耀的前途而感到高兴，小镇出身的姑娘如今走到这样的高度，命运终于恰当的奖赏了应当奖赏的人。\n　　我本想来贝克兰德当面庆贺，但小米勒最近的身体状况不大好，因此你的旅游邀约我不得不暂时拒绝。但别担心，亲爱的，我想我们未来总会有时间再见一面。"] = "It has been five years since we graduated. The shadow of war has lifted from our hometown, and everything has returned to how it was, or even better. I imagine Backlund must have recovered even faster than here.\nI heard you have become a great manager now, and I am sincerely happy for your bright future. A girl from a small town has reached such heights; fate has finally rewarded those who deserve it.\nI intended to come to Backlund to congratulate you in person, but little Miller's health hasn't been great lately, so I have to decline your travel invitation for now. But don't worry, my dear, I believe we will have time to meet again in the future.",
    ["　　他们竟然在事先没找我商量的情况下，决定让我和阿贝尔家族的玛蒂尔达订婚！\n　　天啊，我甚至都还没有见过她！\n　　不行，我要拒绝！\n　　我就算离家出走，就算从此自力更生，受尽打压，也要反抗这桩包办婚姻！"] = "They actually decided to have me engaged to Matilda of the Abel Family without discussing it with me beforehand! \n God, I haven't even met her! \n No, I refuse! \n Even if I run away from home, even if I have to make a living on my own and suffer suppression, I will resist this arranged marriage!",
    ["　　他们竟然称呼我为蒸汽之子，我很喜欢。​"] = "　　They actually call me the Son of Steam. I like it very much.",
    ["　　他看着西迦·特昂道：\n　　“我打算申请加入‘红手套’。”\n　　“‘红手套’？可他们的最低要求是序列7……而且，‘红手套’面对的危险成倍于普通的值夜者小队。”西迦·特昂疑惑中带着关切地说道。\n　　伦纳德勾勒出一抹没有笑意的笑容：\n　　“我差不多可以晋升了。”\n　　他的眼眸转冷，咬牙切齿地无声自语道：\n　　我要报仇！\n　　因斯·赞格威尔，你一定要活着等到我强大起来！\n\n　　——第一卷《小丑》第二百一十一章 葬礼"] = "He looked at Xiga and said:\n \"I intend to apply to join the 'Red Gloves'.\"\n \"'Red Gloves'? But their minimum requirement is Sequence 7... and the dangers the 'Red Gloves' face are exponentially higher than those of a standard Nighthawk team.\" Xiga said, her voice filled with confusion and concern.\n Leonard sketched a smile that didn't reach his eyes:\n \"I'm almost ready for advancement.\"\n His eyes turned cold, and he muttered silently through gritted teeth:\n I must have my revenge!\n Ince Zangwill, you must stay alive until I become strong enough!\n\n — Volume 1: Clown, Chapter 211: Funeral",
    ["　　代号3-888，罗塞尔大帝时期命名为“莫比乌斯环”，又称“无尽的迷途”。\n\n　　……长方形金箔纸，一端扭转180度后，与另一端相接，形成只有一个平面的环形…… \n……起点即是终点。\n\n由一位“通识者”途径序列6的机械专家制作而成……\n……在一场仪式中因失误而沟通邪神，进一步失控变为怪物……\n……封印物3-888被其死后的血污染，特性改变。\n\n\n原本由塔罗学派接管，近期在执行任务过程中<Mark id=\"#159\">失踪</>。"] = "Codename 3-888, named \"Mobius Strip\" during the era of Emperor Roselle, also known as the \"Endless Lost Path.\" \n \n ... A rectangular piece of gold foil, with one end twisted 180 degrees and then connected to the other end, forming a ring with only one plane... \n ... The starting point is the end point. \n \n Created by a Sequence 6 mechanical expert of the \"Savant\" pathway... \n ... Due to a mistake during a ritual, he communicated with an evil god, further losing control and turning into a monster... \n ... Sealed Artifact 3-888 was contaminated by his blood after death, and its characteristics changed. \n \n \n Originally taken over by the Tarot Club, it went missing recently while executing a mission <Mark id=\"#159\"> </>.",
    ["　　作者：匿名流浪骑士 \n\n\n　　这是一本记载于羊皮卷上的荒诞冒险手记，全书以癫狂的笔触描述了一位第四纪自称“被诅咒的勇者”的离奇经历——他走遍大陆收集了117枚古代邪神硬币，解开了83处遗迹谜题，甚至帮某位商人送了200次快递，却始终拒绝营救被封印在宫殿的莱拉公主。\n　　本书列举了此勇者不救公主的一百种理由。"] = "Author: Anonymous Wandering Knight \n \n \n This is an absurd adventure journal recorded on parchment. The whole book describes with a frantic touch the bizarre experiences of a person in the Fourth Epoch who called himself the \"Cursed Hero\"—he traveled across the continent collecting 117 ancient evil god coins, solved 83 ruin puzzles, and even helped a certain merchant deliver 200 packages, yet he always refused to rescue Princess Laila who was sealed in the palace. \n This book lists one hundred reasons why this hero did not save the princess.",
    ["　　你应该会在场景内看到几根线缆，它们有着不同的颜色。\n　　每道谜题出现后，按照<InvHighlight>从上到下</>的顺序依次对照规则，直到你觉得你找到了答案。\n　　勇敢剪断其中的一根吧，时间在追赶你。"] = "　　You should see a few cables in the scene, they have different colors.\n　　After each puzzle appears, follow the order <InvHighlight>from top to bottom</> to check against the rules until you feel you have found the answer.\n　　Bravely cut one of them, time is chasing you.",
    ["　　你睁开眼睛，看见熟悉的廷根湖——一切起始之地。\n　　可你清楚地记得，<M_Red>自己已经失去了最后一点理智。记忆在疯狂中碎裂，意识被黑暗吞没，某种冰冷的力量甚至开始抹去你身为“人”的痕迹。</>\n　　在坠入疯狂深渊的最后，你看见了无边无际的灰雾。而那灰雾穿过冥界，来到永暗之河前，将你从永眠的尽头拉回。\n\n　　你目前的理智值为<M_Orange>30</>，理智值上限暂时降至<M_Orange>70</>。精神上的裂痕无法自行消失，但<M_Orange>其他非凡者施予的安魂</>能够帮助你恢复理智值上限。\n　　在接下来的<M_Orange>一个月</>里，那道来自灰雾的力量仍会跟随着你，守护着你的清醒，使你的理智值不会降至<M_Orange>1</>以下。\n\n　　<M_Link>这是一场由愚者亲手赋予的奇迹。</>\n　　　<M_Link>赞美愚者！</>"] = "　　You open your eyes and see the familiar Tingen Lake—the place where everything began. \n　　But you clearly remember <M_Red> that you had already lost your last bit of sanity. Memories shattered in madness, consciousness was swallowed by darkness, and a certain cold power even began to erase the traces of you being \"human.\" </>\n　　At the very end of falling into the abyss of madness, you saw the boundless gray fog. And that gray fog passed through the Underworld, arrived before the River of Eternal Darkness, and pulled you back from the end of eternal sleep. \n\n　　Your current sanity value is <M_Orange>30</>, and your maximum sanity value has temporarily dropped to <M_Orange>70</>. The cracks in your spirit cannot disappear on their own, but <M_Orange>the Soul Soothing bestowed by other Beyonders</> can help you restore your maximum sanity value. \n　　In the next <M_Orange>month</>, that power from the gray fog will still follow you, guarding your clarity and ensuring your sanity value will not drop below <M_Orange>1</>. \n\n　　<M_Link>This is a miracle personally bestowed by The Fool. </>\n　　　<M_Link>Praise The Fool! </>",
    ["　　克莱尔说，种马铃薯也是个不错的选择……"] = "　　Claire said that planting potatoes is also a good choice...",
    ["　　克莱恩看着那很难说是一杯还是一块的深蓝色粘稠液体，艰难地吞了口唾沫道：\n　　“就这样喝下去？”\n　　“不需要另外的准备吗？比如仪式、咒文或者祈祷语？”\n　　老尼尔“呃”了一声道：\n　　“准备？有的，你先来杯因蒂斯的奥尔米尔葡萄酒，再抽上一根迪西雪茄，然后哼一节悠扬的旋律，跳一段轻快的宫廷舞，你喜欢踢踏舞也可以，最后再来局昆特牌……”\n　　见克莱恩的表情越来越呆愣，老尼尔笑了笑，给出前面描述的总结：\n　　“如果你感觉紧张。”\n　　……你还挺幽默嘛……克莱恩嘴角抽搐了两下，忍住了拔枪的冲动。\n\n　　——第一卷《小丑》第三十四章 灵视"] = "Klein looked at the dark blue viscous liquid, which was hard to say if it was a cup or a block, and swallowed hard: \n \"Just drink it like this?\" \n \"Don't you need other preparations? Like rituals, incantations, or prayers?\" \n Old Neil went \"uh\" and said: \n \"Preparations? There are some. First, you have a cup of Intis Olmier wine, then smoke a Dicy cigar, then hum a melodious tune, dance a light court dance—you can do tap dance if you like—and finally, play a game of Gwent...\" \n Seeing Klein's expression becoming increasingly dazed, Old Neil smiled and gave a summary of the previous description: \n \"If you feel nervous.\" \n ...You're quite humorous... Klein's mouth twitched twice, and he resisted the urge to draw his gun. \n \n —— Volume 1 \"Clown\", Chapter 34, Spirit Vision",
    ["　　关于近期在镇上传闻的“沼泽女巫”一事，现郑重声明：此传闻是个别好事者恶意散布的谣言，部分镇民反映的噩梦现象，与其近期接触过多探险小说有关，请大家无需恐慌。\n\n　　我们呼吁各位镇民保持理性，明辨是非，不轻信、不传播未经证实的消息，共同维护小镇的安宁与和谐。"] = "Regarding the recent rumors of the \"Swamp Witch\" in town, we hereby solemnly declare: This rumor is a malicious fabrication spread by certain troublemakers. The nightmares reported by some townspeople are related to their recent excessive reading of adventure novels. Please do not panic.\n\nWe urge all townspeople to remain rational, distinguish right from wrong, refrain from believing or spreading unverified news, and work together to maintain the peace and harmony of our town.",
    ["　　其他厨师不敢尝试的“自然馈赠”，库克总是第一个采集，捡拾，挖掘，捕捞，并以最美妙的方式烹饪上桌。\n　　对美食的执着，让库克成为真正的厨王之王。"] = "For \"natural gifts\" that other chefs dare not try, Cook is always the first to collect, pick, dig, catch, and cook them in the most wonderful way. \n His persistence in gourmet food makes Cook the true King of Chefs.",
    ["　　准备好了。“审判官”从教会偷来了“机械之灵核心”，先藏在炼钢工厂，就等着仪式启动。他现在喜欢称我为“主人”，他说等我晋升成功，就能重塑肉体，成为半神，到时候他就是我的首席打手。\n　　我把核心握在手里，凉得刺骨。\n　　为了这个，死了很多人，包括警队内部的兄弟，安迪、老柯林、小玛莎……\n　　那一刻我突然想问自己：值得吗？\n　　但答案没有意义了，已经走得太远，没法回头了。"] = " Ready. The \"Inquisitor\" stole the \"Core of Mechanical Spirit\" from the church and hid it in the steel mill, just waiting for the ritual to start. He now likes to call me \"Master\"; he says that once I successfully advance, I can reshape my body and become a Demigod, and by then he will be my chief enforcer. \n I held the core in my hand; it was bone-chillingly cold. \n For this, many people died, including brothers within the police force, Andy, Old Colin, Little Martha... \n At that moment, I suddenly wanted to ask myself: Is it worth it? \n But the answer is meaningless; I have already gone too far and cannot turn back.",
    ["　　几年过去了，我从序列9一步步爬到序列5，成了“天文学家”。每天晚上观测星象，计算仪式节点，离“炼金术士”只剩一步之遥。\n　　但这一步需要的东西太多，钱，资源，还有……人。\n　　子弹的事是我经手的，三百发特种弹药，我叫它们“金弹”，能让人短暂获得强大的力量。\n　　我亲手改档案，报消耗，分批次运出去。“审判官”现在已经是我忠诚的仆人，他会用这些金弹来吸引足够多的人——小偷、流氓、杀手……管他是谁，让那些对现状不满的底层们有个投奔的地方。等他们聚集起来，仪式就能启动。\n　　他们会成为祭品。没关系，反正都是些渣滓，腐肉，清理掉也对廷根有好处。"] = " Years have passed, and I have climbed step by step from Sequence 9 to Sequence 5, becoming an \"Astronomer.\" Every night I observe the stars and calculate the ritual nodes, and I am only one step away from becoming an \"Alchemist.\" \n But this step requires too many things: money, resources, and... people. \n The matter of the bullets was handled by me; three hundred special ammunition, I call them \"Gold Bullets,\" which can allow people to briefly gain powerful strength. \n I personally altered the files, reported the consumption, and shipped them out in batches. The \"Inquisitor\" is now my loyal servant; he will use these Gold Bullets to attract enough people—thieves, hooligans, killers... whoever they are, let those at the bottom who are dissatisfied with the status quo have a place to go. Once they gather, the ritual can be started. \n They will become sacrifices. It doesn't matter; they are all scum and rot anyway, and cleaning them up is good for Tingen.",
    ["　　刚参加完“廷根英雄”表彰大会，心情还是有些激动，有了这个荣誉，看来上头很快就会提名我为下一任局长了。我也得把下面一些得力的人拔起来。\n　　那个愣头青不错，实力很强，就是嘴有点臭，整天把“该死的”挂在嘴边，整体还是很合我胃口的。\n　　光靠抓人可不够。我需要站得更高。只有站在更高的地方，才能把那些城市的腐肉连根挖掉。"] = " Just finished attending the \"Hero of Tingen\" commendation ceremony, and my mood is still a bit excited. With this honor, it seems that my superiors will soon nominate me as the next police chief. I also need to promote some capable people below me. \n That hot-headed kid is not bad; his strength is very strong, it's just that his mouth is a bit foul, and he keeps \"damn it\" on his lips all day, but overall he is still very much to my liking. \n Just catching people is not enough. I need to stand higher. Only by standing in a higher place can I dig out the rot of those cities by the roots.",
    ["　　占卜可以按获得“启示”的方式分为三类：\n　　第一类，借助询问人自身的“力量”，通过“感应”获得启示，比如塔罗占卜和扑克占卜。\n　　第二类，由占卜人主导，通过对自然界或询问人提供的信息进行计算和推测来获得启示，如灵数、占星。\n　　第三类，向第三者寻求答案，常见的是“魔镜占卜”。这种占卜方式实在太有趣了！通常是向七位正神祈求答案，如果我向其他存在祈求会怎么样？\n\n备注：\n　　今天格拉西斯先生说这里曾有一位真正的占卜家，那位只是看了他一眼，就知道他肺部有问题，这又是什么原理？真希望有机会见见那位莫雷蒂先生。"] = "Divination can be divided into three categories based on how \"revelations\" are obtained: \n The first category is to obtain revelations through \"sensing\" by using the \"power\" of the person asking, such as Tarot divination and poker divination. \n The second category is led by the diviner, obtaining revelations through calculation and speculation based on information provided by nature or the person asking, such as numerology and astrology. \n The third category is seeking answers from a third party, the most common being \"Magic Mirror Divination.\" This method of divination is really interesting! Usually, one prays to the seven orthodox gods for answers. What would happen if I prayed to other existences? \n \n Note: \n Today, Mr. Glacis said that there was once a real Seer here. That person only took one look at him and knew he had lung problems. What is the principle behind this? I really hope to have the chance to meet that Mr. Moretti.",
    ["　　又落榜了……已经数不清是第几次落榜了……\n\n　　或许我生来就不适合成为一名政府雇员，仔细经营好那个小肉摊、和一个美丽的妻子一起过日子才是我应该过的生活。\n\n　　她会为我洗衣服，我会为她炖肉，让她成为全廷根吃过最多肉的女人。\n\n　　真是美好的生活……我该振作起来，努力去找一个妻子了。"] = "　　Failed the exam again... I've lost count of how many times I've failed... \n \n　　Perhaps I wasn't born to be a government employee. Carefully managing that little meat stall and living a life with a beautiful wife is the life I should be living. \n \n　　She will wash my clothes, and I will stew meat for her, making her the woman who has eaten the most meat in all of Tingen. \n \n　　What a wonderful life... I should pull myself together and work hard to find a wife.",
    ["　　发现了一个不在安全航道上的无名小岛，上面有不少超凡物种，不，我更喜欢称呼它们为超凡种，这样更有逼格。\n　　除了它们，小岛上还有许多奇奇怪怪的生物，我想，如果达尔文穿越过来，肯定没办法再写出进化论。"] = "　　Discovered an unnamed small island off the safe shipping lanes. There are quite a few extraordinary species on it—no, I prefer to call them Extraordinary Species; it sounds more prestigious. \n　　Besides them, there are many strange creatures on the island. I think if Darwin traveled here, he definitely wouldn't be able to write the Theory of Evolution again.",
    ["　　各位亲爱的廷根市民，出于维持园内安全和肃穆的需要，现全面禁止除步行以外的交通方式。逝者的安眠需要大家共同维护，感谢配合！"] = "Dear citizens of Tingen, in order to maintain safety and solemnity within the park, all modes of transportation other than walking are strictly prohibited. The eternal rest of the deceased requires everyone's cooperation. Thank you!",
    ["　　名称：看见我\n　　外观描述：一块<Letter_Highlight>透明水晶</>，约拇指大小，清澈无瑕。\n　　能力评估：持有者可“看见”他人的真实情绪与表层想法。持续注视目标可使其产生短暂的“认同感”，从而微妙引导对方行为。\n　　副作用警示：每次使用，持有者<Letter_Highlight>随机丢失</>一段属于自己的<Letter_Highlight>记忆</>。\n\n　　备注：三周前失窃，占卜显示仍处于<Letter_Highlight>激活</>状态。"] = " Name: See Me \n Appearance Description: A <Letter_Highlight> transparent crystal </>, about the size of a thumb, clear and flawless. \n Ability Assessment: The holder can 'see' others' true emotions and surface thoughts. Continuous staring at the target can cause them to produce a brief 'sense of agreement', thereby subtly guiding the other party's behavior. \n Side Effect Warning: Each time it is used, the holder <Letter_Highlight> randomly loses </> a segment of their own <Letter_Highlight> memory </>. \n\n Note: Stolen three weeks ago; divination shows it is still in an <Letter_Highlight> active </> state.",
    ["　　哈珀说大麦比水稻更容易生长，还给了我一瓶促生长药剂。有道理，在地下弄水田是有些麻烦……\n\n\n　　种植培育记录得改改：\n　　《“生命之语”非凡药剂对作物种子萌发及幼苗生长的促进作用研究：以不肯发芽的大麦田为例》"] = "Harper said barley is easier to grow than rice and gave me a bottle of growth-promoting potion. It makes sense; making a paddy field underground is a bit troublesome... \n \n \n The planting and cultivation record needs to be changed: \n \"Research on the Promotion of Crop Seed Germination and Seedling Growth by 'Life's Word' Beyonder Potion: A Case Study of a Barley Field That Refuses to Sprout\"",
    ["　　嘿，我亲爱的玩家！\n　　既然你要和“国王”玩选择游戏，不了解规则可不行。所以我亲自为你编写了这份终极傻瓜……哦不，是《终极扑克速成指南》！\n\n　　<Letter_Highlight>五条</>：五张完全一样的扑克。\n\n　　<Letter_Highlight>顺子</>：数字连续的五张扑克。\n\n　　<Letter_Highlight>同花</>：花色相同的五张扑克。\n\n　　<Letter_Highlight>同花顺</>：花色相同，且数字连续的五张扑克。\n\n　　祝你好运……或者，祝你能看穿“好运”背后的把戏！"] = "　　Hey, my dear player! \n　　Since you want to play a choice game with the 'King', you can't do it without knowing the rules. So I personally wrote this ultimate dummy... oh no, the 'Ultimate Poker Crash Course'! \n\n　　<Letter_Highlight> Five of a Kind </>: Five identical poker cards. \n\n　　<Letter_Highlight> Straight </>: Five poker cards with consecutive numbers. \n\n　　<Letter_Highlight> Flush </>: Five poker cards of the same suit. \n\n　　<Letter_Highlight> Straight Flush </>: Five poker cards of the same suit with consecutive numbers. \n\n　　Good luck... or, I hope you can see through the tricks behind 'good luck'!",
    ["　　因报名人数过少，威廉·海默教授的<Letter_Highlight>《黑铁时代经济史》</>10小时大型讲座将<Letter_Highlight>取消</>，请周知。"] = "　　Due to insufficient enrollment, Professor William Hamer's 10-hour grand lecture on <Letter_Highlight>\"Economic History of the Iron Age\"</> will be <Letter_Highlight>cancelled</>. Please be informed.",
    ["　　因突发事件和任务需要，现特批准许廷根市值夜者小队文职人员克莱恩·莫雷蒂先生成为非凡者：序列9“占卜家”。\n　　请协助克莱恩·莫雷蒂完成序列晋升。"] = "Due to unexpected events and mission requirements, Mr. Klein Moretti, a civilian staff member of the Tingen Nighthawks, is hereby specially approved to become an Extraordinary: Sequence 9 \"Seer\".\nPlease assist Klein Moretti in completing his sequence advancement.",
    ["　　在吃的法则里，风味重于一切。 多年前，我第一次在南方吃到库克的菜时，就体会到了这句美食的真谛。\n　　库克是第一个将自然的馈赠以最美妙的方式采集，捡拾，挖掘，捕捞，并最终烹饪上桌的人。\n　　还在南方时，库克就会将猪油熬制后封存数日，加入蔬菜……在一道简单的猪油炸蔬菜上桌之前，库克往往会花费五个月，甚至更长的时间去准备原食材。\n　　现在，库克将南方海岸线的美味带到了鲁恩，带到了廷根，我认为这是“厨王之王”送给廷根最好的礼物。\n　　　　——刊于老实人报美食版面"] = "In the laws of eating, flavor is above all else. Many years ago, when I first tasted Cook's cooking in the South, I realized the true meaning of this gourmet philosophy. \n Cook was the first person to collect, pick, dig, fish, and finally cook the gifts of nature in the most wonderful way. \n While still in the South, Cook would render lard and seal it for several days, adding vegetables... Before a simple dish of lard-fried vegetables was served, Cook would often spend five months or even longer preparing the raw ingredients. \n Now, Cook has brought the delicacies of the southern coastline to Loen, to Tingen. I believe this is the best gift the \"King of Chefs\" has given to Tingen. \n ——Published in the Gourmet section of the Honest Man Newspaper",
    ["　　在海上厨师的层层包围之中，格尔如一道迅捷的闪电，他瞬间隐没在滚滚烟尘之中，周遭突然静地出奇。忽地人群中炸出一声惊呼：在那！\n　　只见格尔凌空跃起，一铲、两铲、三铲……伴随着油花炸响的，还有海上大美食家的名号！\n\n\n　　铁铲和油锅的味道还在海风中震颤，格尔的身影又一次消失了。厨师们惊惶四顾，手中的刀叉因恐惧而微微颤抖——他们甚至没能看清肉块是从哪个方向入锅的！"] = "Surrounded by the sea chefs, Ger was like a swift bolt of lightning. He instantly vanished into the rolling smoke and dust, and the surroundings suddenly became eerily quiet. Suddenly, an exclamation exploded from the crowd: Over there! \n I saw Ger leap into the air, one shovel, two shovels, three shovels... Accompanying the crackling of oil was the name of the great gourmet of the sea! \n \n \n The smell of iron shovels and oil pans was still trembling in the sea breeze, and Ger's figure disappeared again. The chefs looked around in panic, their knives and forks trembling slightly with horror—they didn't even see from which direction the meat entered the pot!",
    ["　　在霍纳奇斯山脉下有一处终年被银色雾气包裹的森林，里面住着各自各样的珍稀动物。其中，有一头叫做邓恩的麋鹿住在森林的最深处，它有着云朵般柔软的灰色皮毛和比橡木还要坚实的巨大鹿角，走路时的蹄声沉稳地如同森林的呼吸。它是这座森林的守护者，拥有洞察森林每一个角落的力量，但这份力量也伴随着诅咒——每年第一场雪落下的时候，它就会开始遗忘。\n\n　　先是刚刚的对话，然后是昨天帮助过的动物，最后连自己的名字都如同飘落的雪花，落在地上了无痕迹。他只好把重要的事情都刻下来，做成木牌挂在鹿角上提醒自己。\n\n　　有一只叫戴莉的知更鸟住在森林的东边，雾气更加浓郁的地方。它有着绯红色的羽毛，它可以用歌声编织出金色的旋律，为迷路的生灵指引方向。但这里藏着它的秘密：每编织一段完整的旋律，它就会掉落一根羽毛，掉落的羽毛不会再生长。"] = "　　At the foot of the Hornacis Mountain Range, there is a forest covered in silver mist all year round, where various rare animals live. Among them, a reindeer named Dunn lives in the deepest part of the forest. It has gray fur as soft as clouds and huge antlers stronger than oak, and its hoofbeats when walking are as steady as the forest's breathing. It is the guardian of this forest and possesses the power to gain insight into every corner of the forest, but this power comes with a curse—every year when the first snow falls, it begins to forget. \n\n　　First, it's the conversation just now, then the animals it helped yesterday, and finally even its own name falls to the ground like falling snowflakes, leaving no trace. It has to carve important things onto wooden boards and hang them on its antlers to remind itself. \n\n　　There is a robin named Daly living in the east of the forest, where the mist is thicker. It has crimson feathers, and it can weave golden melodies with its singing to guide lost creatures. But here lies its secret: every time it weaves a complete melody, it loses a feather, and the lost feathers will not grow back.",
    ["　　塔罗学派必读榜前五的优秀作品，贝尔纳黛会长倾心推荐！\n　　《观众的自我修养》据说是一位半神级观众领域的导师指导编纂的。\n　　《赞美太阳》“赞美太阳”不应流于表面，而该发自内心。\n　　《海上八万里》一本讲述海上生活的小说，书籍粉丝常因为作者是真水手还是假水手争论不休。\n　　《秘密的秘密》一本加入了神秘学元素的侦探小说，其开放式结局引发了巨大的争议。\n　　《学会看书》白塔途径学员的必修书目，同时是塔罗学派最热门的通识书籍。"] = "　　Top five excellent works on the Tarot Club's must-read list, highly recommended by President Bernadette! \n　　\"Self-Cultivation of a Spectator\" is said to have been compiled under the guidance of a demigod-level mentor in the Spectator pathway. \n　　\"Praise the Sun\": \"Praise the Sun\" should not be superficial, but come from the heart. \n　　\"Eighty Thousand Miles at Sea\": A novel about life at sea, where book fans often argue about whether the author is a real sailor or a fake one. \n　　\"Secret of Secrets\": A detective novel with occult elements, its open ending has sparked huge controversy. \n　　\"Learning to Read\": A required book for students of the White Tower pathway, and also the most popular general knowledge book in the Tarot Club.",
    ["　　失败了。\n　　值夜者闯进仪式现场，“审判官”的锯刀挡不住他们，他被当场击毙。核心也碎了，那个我一手带起来的愣头青，我最忠诚的仆人，菲尔，为了守住门口，被子弹打成了筛子。\n　　我浑身像被火烧过一样，但侥幸没有失控。我逃了出来。\n　　回到住处，发现有人等在那里。黑夜教会的人。他们说，已经查清了我做的一切。作为惩罚，他们将抹除我所有的记忆、能力和事迹。从此以后，廷根再也没有我这个人。\n　　曾经的“廷根英雄”，没想到如今走到了这一步。\n　　我想反抗，但动不了。最后一刻，我听见他们说：“市民们会忘记你的名字——崔佛·墨菲，但也许会在心底留下一个影子，一个替他们维系正义的影子。”\n　　那影子……会代替我吗？"] = " Failed. \n The Nighthawks broke into the ritual site; the \"Inquisitor's\" saw blade couldn't stop them, and he was shot dead on the spot. The core was also shattered. That hot-headed kid I raised with my own hands, my most loyal servant, Phil, was riddled with bullets while guarding the door. \n My whole body felt like it had been burned by fire, but I luckily didn't lose control. I escaped. \n Returning to my residence, I found someone waiting there. People from the Church of the Evernight. They said they had already found out everything I had done. As punishment, they would erase all my memories, abilities, and deeds. From now on, Tingen will no longer have a person like me. \n The former \"Hero of Tingen,\" I didn't expect to end up at this point today. \n I wanted to resist, but I couldn't move. At the last moment, I heard them say: \"The citizens will forget your name—Trevor Murphy, but perhaps they will leave a shadow in their hearts, a shadow that maintains justice for them.\" \n That shadow... will it replace me?",
    ["　　奥黛丽当即开动脑筋，边思索边说道：\n　　“您是‘愚者’先生，来自塔罗牌，那作为一个定期的、长期的、隐秘的‘聚会’，称号得尽量一致，嗯，我也从塔罗牌里挑吧。”\n　　她的口吻慢慢变得愉快：\n　　“决定了，我的称号是，‘正义’！”\n　　这是塔罗牌二十二张主牌之一。\n\n　　——第一卷《小丑》第七章 代号"] = "　　Audrey immediately put her mind to work, thinking as she said: \n　　\"You are Mr. Fool, from the Tarot cards. As a regular, long-term, and secret 'gathering,' the titles should be as consistent as possible. Hmm, I'll pick from the Tarot cards too.\" \n　　Her tone gradually became cheerful: \n　　\"Decided, my title is, 'Justice'!\" \n　　This is one of the twenty-two Major Arcana cards. \n\n　　——Volume 1: Clown, Chapter 7: Codename",
    ["　　奥黛丽站了起来，走向门口，对无聊趴坐在外面的金毛大狗笑道：\n　　“苏茜，你这个样子可不够淑女。”\n　　苏茜警惕地左右看了一眼，抽了抽鼻子，然后才开口说道：\n　　“这是猎犬训练时最标准的动作。”\n　　可你并不是合格的猎犬……奥黛丽腹诽了一句，笑着说道：\n　　“我还以为你会这么回答我：奥黛丽，我只是一条狗~”\n　　苏茜认真回应道：\n　　“过于重复的话语容易被别人把握到自身的习惯和心理活动。\n　　“奥黛丽，那本心理学的书上是这么说的。”\n　　……奥黛丽一时竟找不到语言应对。\n\n　　——第四卷《不死者》第十四章 同样的夜晚"] = "Audrey stood up, walked to the door, and smiled at the golden retriever lying bored outside: \n \"Susie, you aren't being very ladylike like that.\" \n Susie looked left and right vigilantly, sniffed, and then spoke: \n \"This is the standard posture for hound training.\" \n But you aren't a qualified hound... Audrey muttered to herself, smiling as she said: \n \"I thought you would answer me like this: Audrey, I am just a dog~\" \n Susie responded seriously: \n \"Excessively repetitive words are easily grasped by others as one's own habits and psychological activities. \n \"Audrey, that's what that psychology book said.\" \n ... Audrey was momentarily unable to find a response. \n \n —— Volume 4 \"Undying\", Chapter 14, The Same Night",
    ["　　奥黛丽缓缓吐了口气，绽放出优雅明丽的笑容，在父亲和母亲的陪伴下，走出休息室，进入晚会大厅。\n　　她一路走上最前方的高台，在一道道惊艳的目光里，将戴着及肘白纱手套的手递给了王后。\n　　王后牵着她，走向高台边缘，面对所有宾客。稍有停顿，王后微笑道：\n　　“虽然这是贝克兰德历史上的黑暗时段，但我们依然有一颗足以照亮整座城市的宝石，她的智慧，她的美貌，她的品格，她的礼仪，都无可挑剔。\n　　“今天，我将她正式介绍给你们。\n　　“奥黛丽·霍尔小姐。”\n　　砰！砰！砰！\n　　落地窗外，烟花升空，炸出一片又一片梦幻的光亮。\n　　1349年最后一天的晚上，奥黛丽在社交意义上正式成年了。\n\n　　——第二卷《无面人》第二百六十九章 辞旧迎新"] = "　　Audrey exhaled slowly, blooming with an elegant and bright smile, and accompanied by her father and mother, she walked out of the lounge and into the ballroom. \n　　She walked all the way to the high platform at the front, and amidst the stunning gazes, she handed her hand, covered in white lace gloves reaching to the elbows, to the Queen. \n　　The Queen took her hand and walked to the edge of the high platform, facing all the guests. After a slight pause, the Queen smiled: \n　　\"Although this is a dark period in Backlund's history, we still have a gem capable of illuminating the entire city. Her wisdom, her beauty, her character, and her etiquette are all impeccable. \n　　\"Today, I officially introduce her to you. \n　　\"Miss Audrey Hall.\" \n　　Bang! Bang! Bang! \n　　Outside the floor-to-ceiling windows, fireworks rose into the sky, bursting into patches of dreamy light. \n　　On the night of the last day of 1349, Audrey was officially an adult in the social sense. \n\n　　——Volume 2: Faceless, Chapter 269: Ringing Out the Old and Ringing In the New",
    ["　　她的个性，她的气质，都是我喜欢的那型，我开始期待我们的婚姻了。​"] = "　　Her personality, her temperament, are both the type I like. I am starting to look forward to our marriage.",
    ["　　她眸中已多了一抹疯狂，看起来用不了多久灵体就会被彻底污染，完全失控。\n　　但是，洛薇雅这一刻的目光里更多是理智和决绝。\n　　她知道自己在做什么，也很清楚自己现在的状态和之后的结局。\n　　呜的风声里，她崩溃的身体连带那阴影“斗篷”落在了“暗天使”萨斯利尔体表。\n　　蠕动的血肉侵蚀了进去，浓厚的阴影飞快扩张，将两道身影一起束缚。\n　　无需洛薇雅开口，科林·伊利亚特已明白了她的意图，当即低沉吼了一声：\n　　“进攻！”\n　　砰！\n　　他的两把晨曦直剑同时斩破虚空，让银白的光芒在纠缠于一的洛薇雅和“暗天使”萨斯利尔身周爆发开来。\n　　笼罩着森然阴影的宫殿一下变亮，布满神圣火焰的巨大光球凭空浮现，将“暗天使”和洛薇雅包容于内，飞快消融着他们，点燃了血肉。\n　　“阳炎”！\n　　这灿烂的光辉里，洛薇雅那双淡灰的眼眸流露出了实质般的痛苦，她的声音虚幻飘渺地回荡了起来：\n　　“我没有背叛白银城……”\n\n　　——第六卷《逐光者》 第一百一十三章 最后的守护"] = "There was already a touch of madness in her eyes, and it looked like it wouldn't be long before her spirit body would be completely corrupted and she would lose control entirely. \n However, in Lovia's gaze at this moment, there was more reason and determination. \n She knew what she was doing, and she was very clear about her current state and her subsequent ending. \n In the howling wind, her collapsing body, along with the shadow \"cloak,\" fell onto the surface of the Dark Angel Sasrir. \n The wriggling flesh and blood eroded into it, and the thick shadows expanded rapidly, binding the two figures together. \n Without needing Lovia to speak, Colin Iliad already understood her intention and immediately roared in a low voice: \n \"Attack!\" \n Bang! \n His two Dawn Greatswords slashed through the void simultaneously, causing silver-white light to erupt around the entangled Lovia and the Dark Angel Sasrir. \n The palace shrouded in grim shadows suddenly brightened, and a huge ball of light filled with holy flames appeared out of thin air, enveloping the Dark Angel and Lovia within it, rapidly dissolving them and igniting their flesh. \n \"Sunlight\"! \n In this brilliant radiance, Lovia's pair of light gray eyes revealed substantial pain, and her voice echoed in a phantom and ethereal manner: \n \"I did not betray the City of Silver...\" \n \n —— Volume 6 \"Light Chaser\", Chapter 113, The Final Guard",
    ["　　好久不见。\n　　自廷根湖异变后，值夜者封锁了廷根湖边区域处理遗留的污染，目前已经处理完毕，重新解除了封锁。\n　　不过最近巡逻的同事告诉我，湖边近日忽然多了几张桌椅和帐篷，应该解除封锁后，有人来到这边进行了活动。\n　　保险起见，值夜者需要调查来到这边的人是否安全。如果你有时间的话，我希望你可以来廷根湖这边协助我们调查。\n　　新同事，期待着与你再一次见面。"] = "Long time no see. \n Since the Tingen Lake anomaly, the Nighthawks have sealed off the area by Tingen Lake to handle the residual corruption. It has now been processed, and the blockade has been lifted. \n However, colleagues on patrol recently told me that a few tables, chairs, and tents have suddenly appeared by the lake. It seems someone has been active here since the blockade was lifted. \n To be safe, the Nighthawks need to investigate whether the people who came here are safe. If you have time, I hope you can come to Tingen Lake to assist us with the investigation. \n New colleague, looking forward to seeing you again.",
    ["　　如你所知，当下的廷根并不算风平浪静。就在几天前，我们又收到了一份郡警察厅的案件报告。经过一定的考虑和评估，我们一致认为，你是接手这个案件的合适人选。\n　　这个案件风险适中，是个不错的练手机会。在调查之余，也请你保护好自己——切记，安全第一。\n　　随信附上前期的调查档案，请仔细阅读。\n　　加油吧，新人值夜者。"] = "　　As you know, Tingen is not exactly peaceful right now. Just a few days ago, we received another case report from the County Police Department. After some consideration and evaluation, we unanimously agree that you are the right person to take on this case. \n　　This case has moderate risk and is a good opportunity for practice. While investigating, please also protect yourself—remember, safety first. \n　　Attached to this letter is the preliminary investigation file, please read it carefully. \n　　Good luck, new Nighthawk.",
    ["　　如果你正热衷于一个浪漫的爱情故事，那么请小心——\n　　也许你的大脑正被欺骗，\n　　也许你的幻想产生偏移，\n　　也许危险已经悄然来临。\n\n　　我曾被爱情故事蒙骗，以为在门外、在阳光下唱歌的就是带给我快乐的英俊王子。\n　　于是，我带着对所有故事里的浪漫幻想，投入了他的怀抱。\n　　终于，我被无尽的灰霾笼罩，从此见到了现实。\n　　我似乎已经等待了很久，等待一个英雄登场，带我奔赴自由的大海。"] = "If you are currently obsessed with a romantic love story, then be careful— \n Perhaps your brain is being deceived, \n Perhaps your fantasies are shifting, \n Perhaps danger has already arrived quietly. \n \n I was once deceived by a love story, thinking that the handsome prince singing outside the door, under the sun, was the one who would bring me happiness. \n So, I threw myself into his arms, carrying all the romantic fantasies from every story. \n Finally, I was shrouded in endless gray haze, and from then on, I saw reality. \n I seem to have been waiting for a long time, waiting for a hero's entrance to take me to the sea of freedom.",
    ["　　如果你看到了这些文字，那是我在女神的神国求得了恩典，灵魂将它带到了你的面前。\n　　那些海盗不会放过任何一个人，我也不例外。我的时间不多了。\n　　最近总是在问候我们的小天使奥莉薇，但最后的时间我想呼唤你。\n　　我爱你戴娜，你永远是我心中最美丽的姑娘。"] = "　　If you see these words, it is because I have obtained grace in the Goddess's Kingdom, and my soul has brought it to you. \n　　Those pirates won't let anyone go, and I am no exception. My time is running out. \n　　I have been greeting our little angel Olivia recently, but in my final moments, I want to call out to you. \n　　I love you, Dana, you will always be the most beautiful girl in my heart.",
    ["　　如果客人想在本店购买商品，请务必严格遵守以下规则，如有违者，后果自负。\n1.本店营业时间为每天3点至5点。\n2.店员工作时间为每天10点。\n3.请不要相信店员的话。\n4.购买三次商品后，请立即离开商店。"] = "　　If guests wish to purchase items at this store, please strictly adhere to the following rules. Violators will be responsible for the consequences. \n1. Our business hours are from 3 to 5 every day. \n2. The clerk's working hours are at 10 every day. \n3. Please do not believe the clerk's words. \n4. After purchasing items three times, please leave the store immediately.",
    ["　　如果忘词，就说灵体太强大，我需要更多苏勒才能继续沟通。\n　　注：请谨慎使用该方法，招致未知存在的可能性并非为零 。有些目光一旦投来，便不会移开。"] = "　　If you forget your lines, just say the spirit body is too powerful and I need more Sol to continue communicating.\n　　Note: Please use this method cautiously; the possibility of attracting an Unknown Existence is not zero. Once some gazes are cast, they will not move away.",
    ["　　威廉·海默教授指导的历史题材话剧《所罗门皇帝》将于下周三晚20:00在校园剧院首次出演，鉴于<Highlight>预约人数过多</>，现关闭正常申请渠道，实行<Highlight>公开准入、先到先得</>的分配方式。望同学们相互传告周知。\n　　"] = "The historical play \"Emperor Solomon,\" directed by Professor William Hamer, will premiere next Wednesday at 20:00 in the campus theater. Given the <Highlight> excessive number of reservations </>, the normal application channel is now closed, and a <Highlight> public access, first-come-first-served </> distribution method will be implemented. We hope students will inform each other. \n",
    ["　　威廉·海默教授的《历史学通识》选修名额已<Highlight>全部选满</>，请落选的同学及时关注和报选其他课程，切勿打扰威廉·海默教授的正常教学秩序。"] = "The elective spots for Professor William Hamer's \"General History\" have <Highlight> all been filled </>. Students who were not selected, please pay attention to and sign up for other courses in time, and do not disturb Professor William Hamer's normal teaching order.",
    ["　　子弹追回二十三颗……但死了很多人，这值不值得呢？我不知道。这城市烂透了。但总得有人去挖出这些烂肉——哪怕只剩我一个。\n　　如果下次再有这种事，我可能还得找你。毕竟我也没有其他可以信任的人了。\n　　最近我发现自己好像影子都变淡了，大概是酒喝多了。你也要注意身体。"] = "Twenty-three bullets recovered… but so many people died. Is it worth it? I don't know. This city is rotten to the core. But someone has to dig out this rotting flesh—even if I'm the only one left.\nIf something like this happens again, I might have to come to you. After all, I have no one else I can trust.\nRecently, I've noticed my shadow seems to be fading; it's probably because I've been drinking too much. You should take care of your health too.",
    ["　　对！睡莲！我是受人所托，来调查睡莲仙女传说的，真该死，就不该为了那点钱卖命！长着睡莲的水塘里有不干净的东西，我和那玩意对视后脑袋就时不时会像木头一样！\n　　但我也不是好惹的，我把那东西的一根手指砍下来收在背包里了！哈哈！活该！\n　　唉，希望之后追寻传说的人，能用这根手指找到一些线索吧……"] = "　　Right! The Water Lily! I was entrusted by someone to investigate the legend of the Water Lily Fairy. Damn it, I shouldn't have risked my life for that bit of money! There is something unclean in the pond where the water lilies grow. After I locked eyes with that thing, my head would feel like wood from time to time!\n　　But I'm not someone to be trifled with either. I cut off one of that thing's fingers and kept it in my inventory! Haha! Serves it right!\n　　Sigh, I hope those who pursue the legend later can use this finger to find some clues...",
    ["　　寻得三个预言之物，窥见真相，逃离噩梦。\n\n　　一物迷途，归家之音不再奏响。"] = "Find three objects of prophecy, glimpse the truth, and escape the nightmare. \n \n One object is lost, and the sound of returning home no longer plays.",
    ["　　寻得三个预言之物，窥见真相，逃离噩梦。\n\n　　一物迷途，归家之音不再奏响。\n　　一物暗淡，不见光明。"] = "Find three objects of prophecy, glimpse the truth, and escape the nightmare. \n \n One object is lost, and the sound of returning home no longer plays. \n One object is dim, and the light cannot be seen.",
    ["　　寻得三个预言之物，窥见真相，逃离噩梦。\n\n　　一物迷途，归家之音不再奏响。\n　　一物暗淡，不见光明。\n　　一物隐蔽，绯红照耀其中。"] = "Find three objects of prophecy, glimpse the truth, and escape the nightmare. \n \n One object is lost, and the sound of returning home no longer plays. \n One object is dim, and the light cannot be seen. \n One object is hidden, with crimson shining within it.",
    ["　　寻找我的弟弟——威廉·霍普金斯，三十六岁，褐色卷发，中等身材，身高约一米七五。失踪时身穿黑色风衣、白衬衫、深色长裤和棕色皮鞋。最后出现于<Letter_Highlight>金秋湖农场</>附近，时间约为三天前的傍晚。\n　　妻子去世后，他深受打击，精神恍惚，常自言自语，不愿与人交流。他没有攻击性，但状态极差，独自在外十分危险。\n　　如有任何线索请告知灰鸽旅馆，必有重谢。"] = "　　Searching for my younger brother—William Hopkins, 36 years old, brown curly hair, medium build, approximately 1.75 meters tall. When he went missing, he was wearing a black trench coat, a white shirt, dark trousers, and brown leather shoes. He was last seen near <Letter_Highlight>Golden Autumn Lake Farm</> around dusk three days ago.\n　　After his wife passed away, he was deeply devastated, mentally dazed, often talking to himself, and unwilling to communicate with others. He is not aggressive, but his condition is extremely poor, and it is very dangerous for him to be out alone.\n　　If you have any clues, please inform the Gray Pigeon Hotel. A generous reward will be offered.",
    ["　　尼尔总是向我展示他新得的琥珀，说里面有只虫子，我也看到了。那只虫子蜷成一团，像胎儿一样。\n　　尼尔真是幸运，希望他的好运能陪伴我们整个旅程。"] = "　　Neil is always showing me his new amber, saying there is a bug inside, and I saw it too. The bug is curled up in a ball, like a fetus.\n　　Neil is really lucky. I hope his good luck will accompany us throughout the entire journey.",
    ["　　工匠之神的教会给了我两个选择，两条序列途径的起始，一个是“通识者”，这属于他们自身所掌握的那个完整序列链条，一个是“窥秘人”，从摩斯苦修会得到，缺乏更高的序列。​"] = "The Church of the God of Steam and Machinery gave me two choices, the start of two Sequence pathways: one is \"Savant,\" which belongs to the complete sequence chain they possess themselves, and the other is \"Mystery Pryer,\" obtained from the Moses Ascetic Order, which lacks higher sequences.",
    ["　　庆功宴将持续一整晚……\n　　正当大家准备散场时，有人大喊——戈登失踪了。\n　　听声音是戴维。据他所说，他们本来在一起喝酒，戈登突然就不见了。\n　　曼斯教授让所有人帮忙找，大家从营地找到营地外，都没有找到。\n　　当所有人回到营地后，戴维也不见了。\n　　戈登和戴维是最先发现山顶遗迹的人，也是最早失踪的。营地里去过山顶遗迹的人，都担心下一个失踪的是自己。\n　　尽管接下来的几天里没有人失踪，但曼斯教授和几位研究员都提议暂时撤离，我们只好收拾东西，准备离开。"] = "　　The celebration party will last all night...\n　　Just as everyone was preparing to disperse, someone shouted—Gordon is missing.\n　　It sounded like David. According to him, they were drinking together when Gordon suddenly disappeared.\n　　Professor Mans asked everyone to help look for him. Everyone searched from the camp to outside the camp, but couldn't find him.\n　　When everyone returned to the camp, David was also gone.\n　　Gordon and David were the first to discover the ruins at the summit, and they were also the first to go missing. Everyone in the camp who had been to the summit ruins was worried that they would be the next to disappear.\n　　Although no one went missing in the following days, Professor Mans and several researchers proposed a temporary withdrawal, so we had to pack our things and prepare to leave.",
    ["　　廷根市“色彩派”画家昨日发布新作品，在一幅夜间山水风景画中，使用<Highlight>银白色</>作为月亮颜色，引发许多人讨论……"] = "A \"Colorist\" painter from Tingen released a new work yesterday. In a night landscape painting, he used <Highlight> silver-white </> as the color of the moon, sparking discussion among many...",
    ["　　廷根晨报，入室抢劫杀人案\n\n　　……据警察部门透露，韦尔奇先生的家里场面惨不忍睹，并且丢失了所有的黄金、珠宝和钞票，以及一切值钱的、便于拿走的物品，甚至连铜便士都没有剩下。有理由相信，这是一伙残忍凶恶的歹徒，他们会毫不犹豫杀掉看见了他们长相的无辜者，比如韦尔奇先生，比如娜娅女士。\n\n　　这是对王国法律的践踏！这是对公共安全的挑衅！没有人希望遭遇类似的事情！当然，一个好消息是，警察部门已经锁定了凶手，抓到了主犯，我们将尽快给出后续报道。\n\n　　记者：约翰·勃朗宁"] = "Tingen Morning Post, Home Invasion and Murder Case \n \n ... According to the police department, the scene at Mr. Welch's home was horrific. All the gold, jewelry, and banknotes were missing, as well as everything valuable and easy to carry, not even a single copper penny was left. There is reason to believe that this is a group of cruel and vicious criminals who would not hesitate to kill innocent people who saw their faces, such as Mr. Welch and Ms. Naya. \n \n This is a trampling of the kingdom's laws! This is a provocation to public safety! No one wishes to encounter such things! Of course, one piece of good news is that the police department has identified the culprits and caught the main perpetrator. We will provide follow-up reports as soon as possible. \n \n Reporter: John Browning",
    ["　　廷根著名占卜者，俱乐部常驻导师，擅长各种占卜方式，每次收费<Hide stylename=\"Transparent\" id=\"#161\"> 4苏勒</>。"] = "A famous diviner in Tingen, a resident mentor at the Club, skilled in various divination methods, 4 sol <Hide stylename=\"Transparent\" id=\"#161\"> </> per session.",
    ["　　当你展开这封信笺时，芬芳的气息已将你包裹。这并非偶然，而是必然的命运——你被选中了。\n\n　　在贝克兰德雾气弥漫的街头，在廷根宁静的小巷深处，有这样一群人：他们追求极致的美丽，拥抱命运的无常，在灾厄中翩翩起舞。\n\n　　我们是春夜舞会。\n\n　　我们侍奉的是不幸与美丽的源头，是将灾难化作艺术的存在。在祂的庇护下，我们明晰了一个真理：\n\n　　真正的美，诞生于毁灭与重生之间。\n\n　　若你愿意加入我们，请前往\"珠宝店\"门口右侧。\n\n　　记住，我们不接受怯懦者，不欢迎虚伪者。唯有敢于凝视深渊，敢于拥抱真实的人，才配得上这场永不落幕的舞会。\n\n　　期待你的到来。"] = "　　As you unfold this letter, a fragrant scent already envelops you. This is no coincidence, but an inevitable fate—you have been chosen. \n\n　　In the fog-drenched streets of Backlund, deep within the quiet alleys of Tingen, there exists a group of people: they pursue ultimate beauty, embrace the impermanence of fate, and dance gracefully amidst disaster. \n\n　　We are the Spring Night Ball. \n\n　　We serve the source of misfortune and beauty, the existence that transforms catastrophe into art. Under His shelter, we have realized a truth: \n\n　　True beauty is born between destruction and rebirth. \n\n　　If you are willing to join us, please head to the right side of the \"Jewelry Store\" entrance. \n\n　　Remember, we do not accept the cowardly, nor do we welcome the hypocritical. Only those who dare to gaze into the abyss and dare to embrace the truth are worthy of this ball that never ends. \n\n　　Looking forward to your arrival.",
    ["　　当午夜的钟声敲响，当星辰在天幕闪烁，当你在梦境与现实的边界徘徊——你听到了吗？那来自深处的低语，那安宁的呼唤。\n\n　　我们是安魂诗社。\n\n　　在女神的注视下，我们是夜晚的守护者，是亡者的歌者，是秘密的守卫。我们相信：\n\n　　黑夜不是恐惧的源头，而是安宁的居所。死亡不是终结的悲哀，而是解脱的开始。我们用诗歌抚慰失眠者，用仪式安抚亡灵，用沉默守护那些不能言说的秘密。\n\n　　若你愿意加入我们，请在新月之夜来到拉斐尔墓园深处，吟诵祷词：\n\n　　\"女神啊，请让安宁降临，\n　　让梦境包裹疲惫的灵魂，\n　　让黑夜庇护迷途的羔羊。\"\n\n　　我们会在黑暗中迎接你。\n　　我们会在静谧中认可你。\n　　我们会在诗歌中铭记你。\n\n　　但请记住，成为安魂诗社的一员，意味着你将承担起相应的责任——在他人入眠时保持清醒，在世界喧嚣时保持沉默，在光明炽烈时拥抱黑暗。\n\n　　你，准备好了吗？  愿黑夜庇护你，愿安宁与你同在。"] = "When the midnight bell tolls, when the stars twinkle in the sky, when you wander on the boundary between dreams and reality—do you hear it? The whisper from the depths, the call of peace. \n\n We are the Requiem Poetry Society. \n\n Under the Goddess's gaze, we are the guardians of the night, the singers for the dead, and the keepers of secrets. We believe: \n\n The night is not the source of horror, but a dwelling of peace. Death is not the sorrow of an ending, but the beginning of liberation. We use poetry to soothe the insomniac, rituals to pacify the spirits, and silence to guard the secrets that cannot be spoken. \n\n If you are willing to join us, please come to the depths of Raphael Cemetery on the night of the new moon and recite the prayer: \n\n \"Goddess, please let peace descend, \n Let dreams wrap the weary soul, \n Let the night shelter the lost lamb.\" \n\n We will welcome you in the darkness. \n We will recognize you in the silence. \n We will remember you in poetry. \n\n But remember, becoming a member of the Requiem Poetry Society means you will take on corresponding responsibilities—staying awake while others sleep, remaining silent when the world is noisy, and embracing the darkness when the light is intense. \n\n Are you ready? May the night shelter you, may peace be with you.",
    ["　　您的好意一如既往，您的行为让我困惑。\n　　您真的只是可怜我吗？这就是您的心意？\n　　您能至少与我面对面说一次话吗？\n　　……想必这封信也不会收到您的答复，但我会一直在这里，等待着您的出现。\n　　我从未见过春天，我的世界里，只有您来了。"] = "    Your kindness is as always, your behavior confuses me. \n    Are you really just pitying me? Is this your true intention? \n    Can you at least speak to me face-to-face once? \n    ...I suppose this letter won't receive a reply from you either, but I will always be here, waiting for your appearance. \n    I have never seen spring; in my world, only you have arrived.",
    ["　　感谢您那日陪我完成这趟奇特的旅程。不瞒您说，我至今仍觉得周身萦绕着那罐头的味道，怕是好几天都散不掉。\n　　但您猜怎么着？女儿看了那些照片，笑得前仰后合。她终于愿意跟我聊聊天了——虽然多半是在笑话我，但至少，我们又说上话了。 \n　　她还给我布置了个新任务：把正版《大冒险家》从头到尾读一遍，再写篇读后感交给她。 \n　　另外，那天在码头遇见的后援会朋友邀我们参加下次的活动。女儿听说后，竟说“一起去看看”。我想，这或许是个不错的开始。\n\n又及：那些照片我还留着。每次看到，都觉得……来都来了，总得留点什么。"] = "　　Thank you for accompanying me on this strange journey that day. To be honest, I still feel the smell of that canned food lingering around me, I'm afraid it won't dissipate for several days. \n　　But guess what? My daughter looked at those photos and laughed until she was doubled over. She is finally willing to talk to me—although mostly to make fun of me, but at least, we are talking again. \n　　She also gave me a new task: read the original \"Great Adventurer\" from beginning to end, and write a review for her. \n　　Also, the fan club friend I met at the dock that day invited us to participate in the next event. When my daughter heard about it, she actually said \"let's go see it together\". I think this might be a good start. \n\nP.S.: I still have those photos. Every time I see them, I feel... since I've already come, I have to leave something behind.",
    ["　　戈登和戴维发现了山顶一个被积雪覆盖的遗迹入口，他们回到营地，将消息报告给曼斯教授，教授当即带着一些学者和几个护卫往山上赶。\n　　而我和另外几个学员则留在了营地，准备必要的物资。边搬东西的时候我边想，不久后我也要称呼他们为\"研究员先生\"了吧。\n　　新遗迹的考古研究相当累人，研究员们还在遗迹入口考察建筑风格，而我们这些不受重视的学员就只能干剩下的粗重杂活……\n　　傍晚回到营地后，曼斯教授很兴奋，有几个研究员提议在营地开个庆功宴，曼斯教授也同意了，大家终于能放松一下了。"] = "　　Gordon and David discovered a ruins entrance covered by snow at the summit. They returned to the camp and reported the news to Professor Mans. The professor immediately took some scholars and a few guards and rushed up the mountain.\n　　As for me and a few other students, we stayed at the camp to prepare the necessary supplies. While moving things, I thought to myself that before long, I would also be calling them \"Mr. Researcher.\"\n　　The archaeological research of the new ruins is quite exhausting. The researchers are still examining the architectural style at the ruins entrance, while we, the undervalued students, can only do the remaining heavy, menial work...\n　　After returning to the camp in the evening, Professor Mans was very excited. Several researchers proposed holding a celebration party at the camp, and Professor Mans agreed. Everyone could finally relax a bit.",
    ["　　戏剧节纪念铜镜近日在二手市场引发收藏热潮，最高售价已达半个金镑。\n　　“之前我拿到的铜镜莫名其妙弄丢了，不然也能小赚一笔了！”某位市民抱怨道。据悉，有大批仿造品流入市场，在此提醒广大市民理性消费，谨防上当。"] = "　　Drama Festival commemorative copper mirrors have recently sparked a collection craze in the second-hand market, with the highest price reaching half a gold pound.\n　　\"The copper mirror I got before was lost for no reason, otherwise I could have made a small profit!\" one citizen complained. It is reported that a large number of imitations have flowed into the market. We remind the public to consume rationally and beware of being deceived.",
    ["　　我们要去贝克兰德和孩子一起过新年了，过完年就回来，提前祝大家新年快乐！\n\n\n歇业日期\n1349年12月20日~1350年1月5日"] = "We are going to Backlund to spend the New Year with our children. We will be back after the New Year. Wishing everyone a Happy New Year in advance! \n \n \n Closed Dates \n December 20, 1349 ~ January 5, 1350",
    ["　　我和几个学员从昨晚开始就在收拾东西，很快就能离开这诡异的地方了。\n　　可就在昨晚，又有两位研究员失踪了，还有几个人因为害怕而跑出了营地。我认为贸然跑出营地并不是理智的选择，因为野外的环境更加恶劣。\n　　我能看得出来曼斯教授也十分不安，但他是我们一行人的主心骨。他今天看起来是强撑着下达的指示，毕竟对于人类而言——未知是最古老最强烈的恐惧。"] = "　　I and a few students have been packing since last night, and we will soon be able to leave this eerie place.\n　　But just last night, two more researchers went missing, and several others ran out of the camp out of fear. I don't think running out of the camp rashly is a rational choice, because the environment in the wild is even harsher.\n　　I can tell that Professor Mans is also very uneasy, but he is the backbone of our group. He seemed to be forcing himself to give instructions today; after all, for humans—the unknown is the oldest and most intense horror.",
    ["　　我很享受“通识者”这个身份。\n　　一件奇怪的事情，当我以“通识者”自居，做的事情都符合它的定位时，那些让我几乎发疯的耳语安静了不少，我时不时爆发的脾气也得到了控制，并想起了日记这件事情。​\n　　这就是那位神秘的查拉图先生对我提过的“扮演”吗？这或许是解决魔药隐患的关键。​"] = "I really enjoy the identity of a \"Savant.\" \n A strange thing: when I consider myself a \"Savant\" and do things that fit its positioning, those whispers that almost drove me crazy quieted down quite a bit, my temper, which would erupt from time to time, was also brought under control, and I remembered the matter of the diary. \n Is this the \"Acting\" that the mysterious Mr. Zaratul mentioned to me? This might be the key to solving the hidden dangers of the potion.",
    ["　　我很喜欢您上次寄来的礼物，谢谢您。这架木雕钢琴或许制作粗糙，却正好适合摆在我的书桌上。\n　　听闻您在葬礼后，不眠不休，成功逮捕了凶手，感谢您的付出！毋庸置疑，您是一名优秀的警察，请不要因为旁人的评价与压力改变初心。\n　　随信附上台历回礼，您可以记录重要的事。\n　　祝您工作顺利！永不迟到！"] = "I really like the gift you sent last time, thank you. This wooden piano might be crudely made, but it's just right for my desk. \n I heard that after the funeral, you worked without sleep to successfully arrest the murderer. Thank you for your efforts! There is no doubt that you are an excellent police officer; please do not change your original intention because of others' evaluations and pressure. \n Enclosed is a desk calendar as a return gift; you can record important things. \n Wish you smooth work! Never be late!",
    ["　　我想起来，在上山的路上我和尼尔还碰到一个奇怪的人——一个身着整齐西装的男子，什么装备都没带，看样子四十来岁，很有气质，深蓝色的眼睛很好看。\n　　我很少这样注视一个人。但从见到他开始，我的目光就无法从他深蓝色的眼睛里移开——那里映着我的影子。我本想多看一会儿，却意识到这样很不礼貌，只好打消了这个念头。\n　　他友好地向我们询问下山的路，我指给他我们来时的路。"] = "　　I remember that on the way up the mountain, Neil and I also ran into a strange person—a man dressed in a neat suit, carrying no equipment, looking to be in his forties, very charismatic, with beautiful deep blue eyes.\n　　I rarely stare at someone like that. But from the moment I saw him, my gaze couldn't move away from his deep blue eyes—they reflected my own shadow. I wanted to look a little longer, but realized it was very impolite, so I had to give up the idea.\n　　He asked us for the way down the mountain in a friendly manner, and I pointed him toward the path we had come from.",
    ["　　我成为了一位“通识者”，靠着魔药的力量，我竟然完整回想起了以前学过的知识，物理，化学，等等，等等。​\n　　不仅回想起，我还深刻地理解和掌握了它们，哈哈，这简直是为我这个异域来客量身定做的“职业”嘛，能最大化地发挥我的优势！不得不说，如果我以这样的状态回去，回到高三，一定能成为状元，要是再有更规范更深入的专业学习，科学家不算太困难的目标。​"] = "I became a \"Savant.\" Relying on the power of the potion, I actually recalled all the knowledge I had learned before—physics, chemistry, and so on. \n Not only did I recall them, but I also deeply understood and mastered them. Haha, this is simply a \"profession\" tailor-made for an outsider like me; it maximizes my advantages! I must say, if I went back in this state, back to my senior year of high school, I would definitely become the top scholar. If I had more standardized and in-depth professional training, becoming a scientist wouldn't be too difficult a goal.",
    ["　　我校教授威廉·海默的最新著作《黑铁时代那些事儿》因其内容深入简出、语言风趣幽默，迅速成为了<Highlight>风靡全国的畅销书籍</>。从廷根到贝克兰德，从各大书店到公共图书馆，《黑铁时代那些事儿》往往刚放上书架，就被狂热的读者们席卷一空！\n　　"] = "Our school's Professor William Hamer's latest book, \"Things About the Iron Age,\" has quickly become a <Highlight> nationwide bestseller </> due to its profound yet accessible content and humorous language. From Tingen to Backlund, from major bookstores to public libraries, \"Things About the Iron Age\" is often swept away by enthusiastic readers the moment it hits the shelves! \n",
    ["　　我用一瓶您给的牛奶换来了邻居家孩子的代笔。\n　　请原谅我如此冒昧，您的出现已经成了我每周里最期待的事——一位由香气构成的朋友。\n　　我不知道你的姓名，也永远不会知道你的模样，但我希望能有一个认识您的机会。\n\n　　若您愿意，下次来时，可否多停留片刻？让我给您一杯水，问问您的名字？"] = " I used a bottle of milk you gave me to get the neighbor's child to write this for me. \n Please forgive my presumption; your appearance has become the thing I look forward to most every week—a friend made of fragrance. \n I don't know your name, and I will never know your appearance, but I hope to have a chance to get to know you. \n\n If you are willing, could you stay a little longer next time you come? Let me offer you a glass of water and ask your name?",
    ["　　我的兄弟，<Letter_Highlight_HW>艾拉的死</>让我们都很心碎。她在湖里溺亡的那个夜晚，我们都曾试图挽救，但她还是回到了睡莲的怀抱。\n　　你去贝克兰德打工期间，艾拉总说，她很想念你笑起来时眼角的皱纹，像她已经和你过了一辈子，十分安心。如今她走了，我知道你也随她一同死去了大半，但里埃尔，艾拉不会希望你这样活着。\n　　振作起来吧，回到生活里，<Letter_Highlight_HW>变回那个会大笑的里埃尔，而不是……</>"] = "　　My brother, <Letter_Highlight_HW>Ella's death</> has left us all heartbroken. On that night she drowned in the lake, we all tried to save her, but she still returned to the embrace of the water lilies.\n　　While you were working in Backlund, Ella always said she missed the wrinkles at the corners of your eyes when you smiled, as if she had already spent a lifetime with you and felt completely at ease. Now that she is gone, I know that a large part of you has died along with her, but Riel, Ella would not want you to live like this.\n　　Pull yourself together, return to your life, and <Letter_Highlight_HW>become that Riel who could laugh out loud again, instead of...</>",
    ["　　我的选择很简单，“通识者”！有完整序列的“通识者”！\n　　虽然掌握更多的神秘学知识有助于我找到回家的办法，但问题是，自身不够强大的情况下，穿越这种事情必然借助外力，而外力是好是坏，是善意还是恶意，无法控制，非常危险，既然如此，还不如让自身变得强大，靠自己的力量回去，所以，完整的序列是我考虑的首要因素！"] = "My choice was simple: \"Savant\"! A \"Savant\" with a complete sequence! \n Although mastering more occult knowledge helps me find a way home, the problem is that without being strong enough, crossing over requires external help, and whether that help is good or bad, well-intentioned or malicious, is uncontrollable and very dangerous. Since that's the case, it's better to become strong myself and rely on my own power to go back. Therefore, a complete sequence is the primary factor I consider!",
    ["　　我知道你是我认识的“工匠”里最信得过的一个，我这次想定一件<Hide stylename=\"Transparent\" id=\"#161\">你说过能“隐藏外貌、模糊辨识”的</>神奇物品。核心材料我会带来，是一份来自“无面人”的非凡特性，状态稳定，你拿去加工就行。\n　　价格按照你之前的口径，1000 镑没问题。\n　　老地方见面交接，我会提前确认周围没人跟着。"] = "　　I know you are the most trustworthy \"Artisan\" I know. This time, I want to commission a magical item that <Hide stylename=\"Transparent\" id=\"#161\">you mentioned could \"conceal one's appearance and blur recognition.\"</> I will bring the core material myself; it is a Beyonder characteristic from a \"Faceless,\" and its state is stable, so you can just take it and process it.\n　　As for the price, 1000 pounds as you previously stated is no problem.\n　　Let's meet at the usual place for the handover. I will confirm in advance that no one is following me.",
    ["　　我站在“黑王座号”的船头，张开双臂，对格林和爱德华兹他们说：“想要我的财宝吗？那就到迷雾海的尽头来寻找吧，我将所有的财宝都藏在了这里！”\n　　他们完全不懂我的幽默，竟然问我是不是真的有额外的财宝，真是无趣啊，你们这样是做不了我的天启四骑士的！"] = "I stood at the bow of the \"Black Throne,\" spread my arms, and said to Green, Edwards, and the others, \"Do you want my treasure? Then go find it at the end of the Fog Sea; I have hidden all my treasure there!\" \n They completely failed to understand my humor and actually asked if I really had extra treasure. How boring; you guys can't be my Four Horsemen of the Apocalypse like this!",
    ["　　我诚挚地邀请你和你的两位哥哥前来参加我十六岁的生日宴会。\n　　宴会将于明日晚上6点开始，地址为法尼亚街5号。\n　　期待你们一家人的到来。"] = "I sincerely invite you and your two brothers to attend my sixteenth birthday party.\nThe party will start at 6 PM tomorrow at 5 Fania Street.\nLooking forward to your family's arrival.",
    ["　　或许您永远不会注意到去年坐在台下的两位来自廷根的平凡观众，但我却因为您精彩的演出而爱上了您。因此，当在大学课堂遇到您时，我欣喜若狂。\n　　我应当感谢什么让您来到廷根？学术之风，您的头脑，还是命运？自从您到来，我开始感谢生活中的一切，真希望看见您的不足，好让我的心冷却一些。但请不要让我看到您的眼泪，因为即使只是杂志上对您表演时所流泪水的短短几行描述，也让我的心倍感痛楚。当然，我明白，这正是您的天赋所在，您正是为戏剧而生的。想到这点，我的爱更增千倍。"] = "Perhaps you will never notice the two ordinary audience members from Tingen who sat in the audience last year, but I fell in love with you because of your brilliant performance. Therefore, when I met you in a university lecture, I was ecstatic.\nWhat should I thank for bringing you to Tingen? The academic atmosphere, your mind, or fate? Since you arrived, I have begun to be grateful for everything in life. I truly wish to see your flaws so that my heart might cool down a little. But please do not let me see your tears, because even just the few lines in a magazine describing the tears you shed during your performance made my heart ache. Of course, I understand that this is your talent; you were born for the stage. Thinking of this, my love increases a thousandfold.",
    ["　　戴莉艰难地笑了笑，对抗着体表不断冒出的白色绒毛和漆黑鳞片道：\n　　“原来是你……\n　　“你之前不是问我，为什么不主动，主动向邓恩表白，将他推到，床上？”\n　　她吸了口气，苦涩笑道：\n　　“我过去有过，太多的放纵，他，他是一个保守的人，我，我很自卑。”\n　　她已快控制不住，即将变成怪物。\n　　这个时候，她听见克莱恩·莫雷蒂回应道：\n　　“队长其实很喜欢你，但你太优秀太年轻了，他也很自卑。”\n　　戴莉笑了，旋即在朦胧的视线里看见了那个身穿黑色风衣，发际线较高，有幽邃灰眸的男人，看见他以手按胸，弯腰伸掌，邀请自己跳舞。\n　　她探出了自己的手，她的思绪随之变得滞涩。\n　　穿黑风衣的灰眸男人拉起了异变逐渐退去的戴莉，在伦纳德的目光中，在喷泉乱流的破败广场里，跳起了轻快的舞蹈。\n　　一样样材料飞出，有金色的葡萄藤，有较为丑陋的橡皮面具，它们在灵性的引导下，逐渐糅合在一起，灌入了一个金属小瓶。\n　　美妙的舞蹈中，戴莉轻轻前靠，倚在了邓恩的怀里。\n\n　　——第四卷《不死者》第二百一十三章 故事的尾声"] = "Daly smiled with difficulty, fighting against the white fluff and pitch-black scales constantly emerging from her skin:\n \"So it was you...\n \"Didn't you ask me before why I didn't take the initiative, take the initiative to confess to Dunn and push him onto the bed?\"\n She took a breath and smiled bitterly:\n \"I've had too much indulgence in the past. He, he is a conservative person, and I, I am very insecure.\"\n She could no longer control herself and was about to turn into a monster.\n At this moment, she heard Klein Moretti respond:\n \"The Captain actually liked you very much, but you were too outstanding and too young, and he was also very insecure.\"\n Daly smiled, and then in her hazy vision, she saw the man in the black trench coat with a high hairline and deep gray eyes. She saw him place his hand on his chest, bow, and extend his palm to invite her to dance.\n She reached out her hand, and her thoughts became stagnant.\n The gray-eyed man in the black trench coat pulled up Daly, whose mutation was gradually receding. Under Leonard's gaze, in the dilapidated square with turbulent fountain water, they danced a light dance.\n Materials flew out one by one—golden grapevines, an ugly rubber mask—and under the guidance of spirituality, they gradually merged together and were poured into a small metal bottle.\n In the midst of the beautiful dance, Daly leaned forward gently and rested in Dunn's arms.\n\n — Volume 4: Undying, Chapter 213: The End of the Story",
    ["　　所有真挚的付出，最终都会回到你身边。"] = "　　All sincere efforts will eventually return to you.",
    ["　　托马斯·布莱克自少年时便在我家服侍，工作勤勉，诚实可靠。\n　　他擅长园艺与算数，最重要的是——有一颗忠诚的心。\n　　如今我即将远行，若不能归来，特此推荐他前往任何需要可靠人手之处。"] = "Thomas Blake has served in my family since he was a boy; he is diligent, honest, and reliable.\nHe is skilled in gardening and arithmetic, and most importantly—he has a loyal heart.\nNow that I am about to go on a long journey, if I cannot return, I hereby recommend him to any place that needs a reliable hand.",
    ["　　据官方消息，廷根大学一<Highlight>机械系大学生</>数日前失踪。学校师生表示，失踪的艾瑞丝是一位<Highlight>“狂热的机械迷”</>，有人提到她好像说到过要去<Highlight>“一个绝妙的根据地”</>进行一场“探险”。\n　　若您是知情者，请尽快联系警方。"] = "According to official news, a <Highlight> mechanical engineering student </> from Tingen University went missing several days ago. Teachers and students at the school stated that the missing Iris was a <Highlight> \"fanatical mechanical enthusiast.\" </> Someone mentioned that she seemed to have talked about going to <Highlight> \"a wonderful base\" </> to conduct an \"expedition.\" \n If you have any information, please contact the police as soon as possible.",
    ["　　据警察部门透露，韦尔奇先生家里惨不忍睹，还丢失了所有的财物。有理由相信，这是一伙残忍凶恶的歹徒，他们会毫不犹豫杀掉无辜的目击者，比如韦尔奇先生，比如娜娅女士。\n　　这是对王国法律的践踏！这是对公众安全的挑衅！好消息是，警察部门已经锁定了凶手、抓到了主犯。我们将尽快给出后续报道。"] = "According to the police department, the scene at Mr. Welch's home was horrific, and all his property was stolen. There is reason to believe that this is a group of cruel and vicious criminals who would not hesitate to kill innocent witnesses, such as Mr. Welch and Ms. Naya. \n This is a trampling of the kingdom's laws! This is a provocation to public safety! The good news is that the police department has identified the culprits and captured the main perpetrator. We will provide follow-up reports as soon as possible.",
    ["　　据警察部门透露，韦尔奇先生的家里场面惨不忍睹，并且丢失了所有的黄金、珠宝和钞票，以及一切值钱的、便于拿走的物品，甚至连铜便士都没有剩下。有理由相信，这是一伙残忍凶恶的歹徒，他们会毫不犹豫杀掉看见了他们长相的无辜者。\n　　一个好消息是，警察部门已经锁定了凶手，抓到了主犯，我们将尽快给出后续报道。"] = "According to the police department, the scene at Mr. Welch's home was horrific. All gold, jewelry, cash, and any valuable items that were easy to carry were stolen, leaving not even a copper penny behind. There is reason to believe that this is a group of cruel and vicious criminals who would not hesitate to kill any innocent person who saw their faces. \n A piece of good news is that the police department has identified the culprits and captured the main perpetrator. We will provide follow-up reports as soon as possible.",
    ["　　推理言情诡异奇幻小说《暴风山庄》现正火热发售中！\n　　小说叙述了女主角茜茜进入弗留斯山庄担任家庭教师的故事，受到读者的广泛称赞，跻身今年最畅销的小说榜单。"] = "　　The mystery, romance, and fantasy novel \"Storm Manor\" is now on sale!\n　　The novel tells the story of the heroine Cici entering Frieze Manor as a tutor. It has been widely praised by readers and has made it onto this year's bestseller list.",
    ["　　收到你的来信，我已从间海郡回到贝克兰德。多日的离别本就让我的心中燃烧痛苦的火焰，你所说的话语更是增添我的绝望。\n　　请不要怀疑我们之间情谊的程度，如果你要怀疑，就请看着我的眼睛再说出这些狠心的话语。\n　　我已在我们熟悉的餐厅订好一周的座位，不管如何，我每天都会在这里等你，请来见我吧。"] = "Received your letter; I have returned to Backlund from Intis. The days of separation were already burning a flame of pain in my heart, and your words have only added to my despair.\nPlease do not doubt the depth of our affection. If you must doubt it, please look into my eyes and say these cruel words again.\nI have booked a table at our familiar restaurant for a week. No matter what, I will be waiting for you there every day. Please come and see me.",
    ["　　教会传来消息，封印物2-327“看见我”失窃。占卜显示线索指向黑伍德庄园。\n　　黑伍德男爵今晚举办舞会。我们需要一个善于观察的人混入舞会调查——你是序列9“观众”，没有比你更合适的人选。\n　　你的身份已安排妥当：贝克兰德来的新兴商人，听闻庄园有投资机会，受邀赴宴。\n　　记住，观众不登台。\n　　观察，不要打草惊蛇。"] = "The Church has received news that Sealed Artifact 2-327 \"See Me\" has been stolen. Divination indicates the clues point to Heywood Manor. \n Baron Heywood is hosting a ball tonight. We need someone good at observing to infiltrate the ball and investigate—you are a Sequence 9 \"Spectator,\" and there is no one more suitable than you. \n Your identity has been arranged: an emerging merchant from Backlund, invited to the banquet after hearing about investment opportunities in the manor. \n Remember, the Spectator does not take the stage. \n Observe, do not alert the enemy.",
    ["　　斯林太太报案：珍妮周日缺勤面包房，次日未上班，可能失踪。珍妮社会关系简单，无固定住所。崇拜罗塞尔，自学备考廷根技术学校，但工厂和兼职已占满大部分时间。失踪时间约25日下午至26日凌晨。"] = "　　Mrs. Slin reported: Jenny was absent from the bakery on Sunday and did not come to work the next day; she may be missing. Jenny had simple social connections and no fixed address. She admired Roselle and was self-studying for the Tingen Technical School entrance exam, but her factory work and part-time jobs occupied most of her time. The time of disappearance was approximately from the afternoon of the 25th to the early morning of the 26th.",
    ["　　新生者，再次新生。\n　　这是他的第二十次噩梦，他已经在梦中死去十九次。\n　　这一次，他翻开了不该出现在此地的安提哥努斯笔记，死于污染后的失控。\n　　新生者，再次新生。\n　　这是他的第二十一次新生，他路过安提哥努斯笔记，带走了一张⬛⬛牌。\n　　……\n　　……\n　　新生者来到了开满鲜花的祭坛旁，他/她必须做点什么，他/她的内心有搞清楚一切真相的渴求。\n　　他/她观察了祭坛，获得了一张记载着滑稽言语的羊皮纸。\n　　羊皮纸上记录着一首规则之书。”"] = "The newborn, born again. \n This is his twentieth nightmare; he has already died nineteen times in his dreams. \n This time, he opened the Antigonus Notebook that shouldn't have appeared here and died from loss of control after corruption. \n The newborn, born again. \n This is his twenty-first rebirth; he passed by the Antigonus Notebook and took away a ⬛⬛ card. \n ... \n ... \n The newborn came to the altar full of flowers; he/she must do something. He/she has a desire to figure out the whole truth. \n He/she observed the altar and obtained a piece of parchment recording funny words. \n The parchment records a \"Book of Rules.\"",
    ["　　日前，本市一名市民在一家占卜场所内突发晕厥，并被紧急送医。记者了解到，该市民已持续昏迷超过七日，生命体征平稳，但具体病因仍未明确。\n　　医院与警方已成立联合调查组，以期尽快查明事件原委。"] = "Recently, a citizen in this city suddenly fainted in a divination venue and was rushed to the hospital. The reporter learned that the citizen has been in a coma for over seven days. Their vital signs are stable, but the specific cause of the illness remains unclear. \n The hospital and the police have established a joint investigation team to determine the cause of the incident as soon as possible.",
    ["　　日安！\n　　金秋湖最近越发热了，不知道您身体怎么样？如果您需要，可以托梦给我，我有最好的解暑茶。\n　　我最近很好。个头长高了一点，草药书看到了第六章，成功配出了咳嗽药剂，治好了汉娜婶婶的感冒。\n　　接下来我要开始练习更高级的药方。如果您不太忙的话，我想要几棵水刃草，用来做醒神药剂。因为没学会游泳，我一直没拿到它。\n　　如果您太忙也没关系！我会努力练习游泳的。"] = "Good day! \n Golden Autumn Lake has been getting hotter lately, I wonder how you are feeling? If you need anything, you can leave a message in my dreams, I have the best cooling tea. \n I've been doing well lately. I've grown a bit taller, finished the sixth chapter of the herbal book, and successfully concocted a cough syrup that cured Aunt Hannah's cold. \n Next, I'm going to start practicing more advanced prescriptions. If you're not too busy, I'd like a few stalks of Water Blade Grass to make a refreshing potion. Because I haven't learned to swim, I haven't been able to get it. \n If you're too busy, that's fine too! I will work hard on practicing swimming.",
    ["　　昨夜西区某工厂突发爆炸与骚乱，警方声称“疑似瓦斯泄漏”，已封锁现场。但目击者声称看到多道奇怪身影出现在工厂上空，并做出诡异的高速运动。专家解释，这些身影只是爆炸烟尘的扭曲投影，市民们无需惊慌。"] = "Last night, an explosion and riot broke out at a factory in the West District. The police claimed it was a \"suspected gas leak\" and have cordoned off the scene. However, witnesses claimed to have seen multiple strange figures appearing above the factory, moving at eerie, high speeds. Experts explained that these figures were merely distorted projections of the explosion's dust, and citizens need not panic.",
    ["　　最新吸血鬼爱情小说《月下来客》引发抢购热潮！书中描绘的\"黑蔷薇邀请函\"、”月下野餐“等浪漫桥段，正成为年轻人的示爱新风尚。"] = "The latest vampire romance novel \"Guest Under the Moon\" has sparked a buying frenzy! The romantic scenes described in the book, such as the \"Black Rose Invitation\" and \"Picnic Under the Moon,\" are becoming a new trend for young people to express their love.",
    ["　　最近还好吗？很高兴您能喜欢木雕钢琴。\n　　我能逮捕凶手，得益于同事的帮助和您的信任，我们会继续守护廷根。\n　　诚如您在葬礼上所言，冬天太过寒冷。所以，为了能在春天重逢，我们会努力生活，走出离别的阴霾。\n　　不知道您愿不愿意和我交个朋友，我认为，我们会有话可说。\n　　您寄来的礼物，我会好好使用，保证不忘记重要的日子，请放心。\n　　祝您工作顺利！"] = "　　How have you been lately? I'm glad you like the wooden piano. \n　　I was able to arrest the murderer thanks to the help of my colleagues and your trust; we will continue to guard Tingen. \n　　As you said at the funeral, winter is too cold. Therefore, in order to meet again in the spring, we will try our best to live and walk out of the haze of parting. \n　　I don't know if you are willing to be friends with me; I think we will have things to talk about. \n　　I will make good use of the gift you sent, and I promise not to forget important days, please rest assured. \n　　Wish you success in your work!",
    ["　　有一位匿名廷根市民寄信本报，请我们登报寻找一位名叫<Highlight>“奥斯瓦尔德”</>的中年男性。其外貌约30-40岁，自今年5月后下落不明，若有知情人士，请联系本报。"] = "An anonymous Tingen citizen sent a letter to this newspaper, asking us to publish a notice to find a middle-aged man named <Highlight> \"Oswald.\" </> He is approximately 30-40 years old and has been missing since May of this year. If anyone has any information, please contact this newspaper.",
    ["　　有点急事，待会回来。\n\n　　你可以在咖啡馆周围看看，旁边<Letter_Highlight_HW>中央广场</>上有一个叫做<Mark id=\"#159\">“旅行尖碑”</>的石碑，那是“魔术师”小姐和工匠制作的，开启后，就能在各地的旅行点之间穿梭。\n\n　　好东西，比走路快。\n\n　　注：不要走太远。\n"] = "　　In a bit of a rush, I'll be back in a moment. \n\n 　　You can look around the cafe. Beside it, on the <Letter_Highlight_HW>Central Plaza</>, there is a stone tablet called the <Mark id=\"#159\">\"Travel Obelisk\"</>. It was made by Miss \"Magician\" and the craftsman. Once activated, you can shuttle between travel points all over the place. \n\n 　　Good stuff, faster than walking. \n\n 　　Note: Don't go too far. \n",
    ["　　本报最近收到数封铁十字街附近居民的投诉信，称某条巷子里传来<Highlight>各种不明嗡鸣</>。一位居民这样说明情况，相当生动夸张：“女神啊，<Highlight>难道齿轮也会活过来吗？难道机器也会自己发动吗？</>”\n　　本报记者也认为这非常荒谬，但如果您有机械学相关知识可以为铁十字街居民解忧，欢迎联系本报。"] = "This newspaper has recently received several complaint letters from residents near Iron Cross Street, claiming that <Highlight> various unknown humming sounds </> are coming from a certain alley. A resident described the situation quite vividly and exaggeratedly: \"Goddess, <Highlight> could it be that gears have come to life? Could it be that machines are starting themselves? </>\" \n Our reporter also thinks this is very absurd, but if you have knowledge of mechanics that can help the residents of Iron Cross Street, please contact this newspaper.",
    ["　　来到海岸线餐厅，不得不品尝的就是猪油炸蔬菜。\n　　库克会将猪油熬制后封存数日，加入蔬菜。制作出来的猪油炸蔬菜，无论风味还是口感都无与伦比。"] = "When you come to Coastline Restaurant, you must taste the lard-fried vegetables. \n Cook will boil the lard and seal it for several days before adding it to the vegetables. The resulting lard-fried vegetables are unparalleled in both flavor and texture.",
    ["　　梦境捕手，捕食梦境的凶猛生物。\n　　它们痴迷曼哈尔鱼和牛奶的味道，这对它们有致命的吸引力。\n　　如果睡前喝几口浸泡曼哈尔鱼眼珠的牛奶……"] = "Dream Catcher, a fierce creature that preys on dreams. \n They are obsessed with the taste of Manhar fish and milk, which has a fatal attraction for them. \n If you drink a few mouthfuls of milk soaked with Manhar fish eyeballs before going to bed...",
    ["　　比星空更崇高，比永恒更久的黑夜女神，祂是隐秘之母，厄难与恐惧的女皇，安眠和寂静的领主。"] = "The Evernight Goddess, more sublime than the starry sky and longer-lasting than eternity, is the Mother of Concealment, the Empress of Calamity and Horror, and the Lord of Slumber and Silence.",
    ["　　沃尔女士说，真正的作家必须做一个记录者，深入最真实现场，切身感受故事的气息。\n　　雪怪算什么？我要写出最震撼人心的猎杀巨兽传奇！\n　　不对，那几拨探险家怎么打起来了？那是枪声吗？\n　　天啊，他们在争夺什么宝物？这比我原本的计划刺激多了！\n　　决定了，不写什么魔雪怪巨兽了。回去就写《雪山火拼记》！\n　　等等，他们怎么朝我来了？"] = "　　Ms. Wall said that a true writer must be a chronicler, delving into the most authentic scenes to personally feel the breath of the story. \n　　What's a snow monster? I'm going to write the most heart-shaking legend of hunting giant beasts! \n　　Wait, why are those groups of explorers fighting? Was that a gunshot? \n　　Oh my god, what treasure are they fighting over? This is much more exciting than my original plan! \n　　Decided. I'm not writing about magic snow monsters anymore. I'll write \"The Snowy Mountain Shootout\" when I get back! \n　　Wait, why are they coming towards me?",
    ["　　没有任何一个窈窕淑女会愿意嫁给一个肉贩子！没有！\n\n　　我恨我身上的肉骚味！我恨透了这个世界！\n\n　　我<Delete id=\"#157\">一些难以展示的鲁恩脏话，粗俗不堪，表达了一个生活不意的人对世界和命运的痛恨。</>\n\n　　如果我成为一名政府雇员呢？\n\n　　如果我再努力一些，哪怕只是在那方正的建筑里端盘子，会不会有人愿意爱我？"] = "No refined lady would ever want to marry a butcher! None! \n\n I hate the smell of raw meat on me! I hate this world! \n\n I <Delete id=\"#157\"> some unspeakable Loen profanities, crude and vulgar, expressing the hatred a person struggling in life feels toward the world and fate. </>\n\n What if I became a government employee? \n\n If I worked harder, even if it was just washing dishes in that square building, would anyone be willing to love me?",
    ["　　渴望美之人，你已被春夜选中。\n　　若你想要了解真相，想要触及美或毁灭，请前往珠宝店门口右侧， 寻找<Letter_Highlight_HW>莉丝·埃文斯</>。\n　　她会告诉你一切。"] = "　　You who yearn for beauty, you have been chosen by the spring night.\n　　If you wish to know the truth, or wish to touch beauty or destruction, please go to the right side of the jewelry store entrance and look for <Letter_Highlight_HW>Liz Evans</>.\n　　She will tell you everything.",
    ["　　漫山的雪。也许是第二天？也许是第三天？\n　　尼尔不见了。营地也不见了。\n　　东西都没了。还好身上还剩……\n<Delete id=\"#158\">面勹</>面包<Delete id=\"#158\">一个</>三分之一份\n糖3颗\n水<Delete id=\"#158\">1</>半瓶"] = "　　Snow all over the mountains. Maybe it's the second day? Maybe the third day?\n　　Neil is gone. The camp is also gone.\n　　Everything is gone. Fortunately, I still have...\n<Delete id=\"#158\">Bre-ad</>Bread<Delete id=\"#158\">One</>one-third portion\nSugar: 3 pieces\nWater<Delete id=\"#158\">1</>half a bottle",
    ["　　灰色的麋鹿突然仰首长鸣，它角上的羽毛纷纷发出柔光，飘到空中接续起了戴莉未完成的歌。它的鹿角记住了每片羽毛中储存的音符，它笨拙的收集无意中保存了戴莉所有的歌声。\n\n　　直到鹿角触碰到最后一个音符的时刻，光亮也在出现在眼前，猫头鹰长老在洞口拼命甩着翅膀欢迎英雄的归来。\n\n　　戴莉再次醒来是在温暖而干燥的落叶堆里，它惊讶地发现身上覆盖着全新的羽毛——银白色的，如雾般轻盈蓬松。邓恩安静地守在落叶堆旁，角上依然挂着木牌，最新一块刻着：“戴莉拥有了一身新的羽毛，记得赞美它。”\n\n　　后来，森林里流传着这样的故事：这里有两位守护者，深沉的鹿蹄声和清亮的鸟叫声完美交融，它们在歌声和鹿角中记录每一朵花的绽放，每条溪流的改道和每个生命的成长。邓恩的遗忘还在循环，但它每天都赞美戴莉的羽毛；戴莉的羽毛不再随歌声掉落，每段旋律都让羽毛更有光泽。\n\n　　有些记忆会在冬雪中被埋藏，有些记忆会在回响中永恒。即使遗忘，善良也会为弱者驻足，即使失去，爱会赋予重构的勇气。"] = "The gray elk suddenly raised its head and let out a long cry. The feathers on its antlers emitted a soft light, floating into the air to continue Daly's unfinished song. Its antlers remembered the notes stored in every feather, and its clumsy collection unintentionally saved all of Daly's singing. \n\n Until the moment the antlers touched the last note, light also appeared before its eyes. The Owl Elder was flapping its wings desperately at the cave entrance to welcome the hero's return. \n\n Daly woke up again in a warm and dry pile of fallen leaves. It was surprised to find that its body was covered with brand-new feathers—silver-white, as light and fluffy as mist. Dunn was quietly guarding by the leaf pile, with a wooden sign still hanging on his antlers, the latest one carved with: \"Daly has a new set of feathers, remember to praise it.\" \n\n Later, such a story circulated in the forest: there were two Guardians here, the deep sound of deer hooves and the clear chirping of birds blended perfectly. They recorded every blooming flower, every change in the course of the stream, and the growth of every life in their songs and antlers. Dunn's loss of control was still cycling, but he praised Daly's feathers every day; Daly's feathers no longer fell with the singing, and every melody made the feathers more lustrous. \n\n Some memories will be buried in the winter snow, and some memories will be eternal in the echoes. Even if forgotten, kindness will stop for the weak; even if lost, love will give the courage to reconstruct.",
    ["　　牢记以下五个步骤。\n第一步：深呼吸，眼神飘忽向上看。\n第二步：我看见了金色的光芒！\n第三步：描述守护灵——身披金甲，手持权杖，背后有光环。\n第四步：它说您三个月内会发大财。\n第五步：请客户为通灵仪式付费。"] = "　　Keep the following five steps in mind.\nStep 1: Take a deep breath, eyes drifting upward.\nStep 2: I see golden light!\nStep 3: Describe the Guardian Spirit—clad in golden armor, holding a scepter, with a halo behind it.\nStep 4: It says you will make a fortune within three months.\nStep 5: Please ask the client to pay for the Spirit Mediumship Ritual.",
    ["　　特大喜讯！特大喜讯！经过几个月的重新装修，位于廷根市豪尔斯街区的哈罗德百货商店于今日盛大开业！\n　　我们将推出特大优惠，购物每满十镑即减免一镑！整个七月，哈罗德百货惊喜不断、优惠不断，更有大量奖品等您领取！"] = "Great news! Great news! After months of renovation, Harold Department Store, located in the Howls Street district of Tingen, grandly opened today! \n We are launching a massive promotion: get one pound off for every ten pounds spent! Throughout July, Harold Department Store will have constant surprises and discounts, and there are plenty of prizes waiting for you to claim!",
    ["　　玛丽安女士说，她已经没有什么可以教导我的了。\n　　这意味着我要过上不再上课、不再读书、不再学习新知识的生活……大帝啊，这实在太可怕了……光是想象，就让我痛不欲生……\n　　不，我不能接受这样的生活！大帝曾说过<Letter_Highlight_HW>“人不读书和咸鱼有什么区别”</>，明天我要去请求玛丽安女士，只要能继续上课，要我做什么都可以！"] = "　　Ms. Marianne said that she has nothing left to teach me.\n　　This means I will have to live a life without classes, without reading, and without learning new knowledge... Oh, Emperor, this is truly terrifying... Just imagining it makes me wish I were dead...\n　　No, I cannot accept such a life! The Emperor once said, <Letter_Highlight_HW>\"What is the difference between a person who doesn't read and a salted fish?\"</> Tomorrow, I will go and beg Ms. Marianne; as long as I can continue taking classes, I will do anything!",
    ["　　玛蒂尔达小姐真漂亮啊。​"] = "　　Miss Matilda is truly beautiful.",
    ["　　生意真差，守着摊子简直是浪费时间。\n\n　　要不去“莴苣与肉类”市场出摊试试呢？\n\n　　……\n\n　　算了，我受不了和那群人竞争，他们抢夺客人的样子就像看到猎物的红眼鬣狗。\n\n　　还是努力通过考试，成为政府雇员吧，明年，明年我一定会成功的！"] = "Business is so bad, guarding this stall is just a waste of time. \n \n Maybe I should try setting up a stall at the \"Lettuce and Meat\" market? \n \n ... \n \n Forget it, I can't stand competing with those people; the way they snatch customers is like red-eyed hyenas seeing prey. \n \n I'd better work hard to pass the exam and become a government employee. Next year, next year I will definitely succeed!",
    ["　　生活太<Letter_RedBig>辛苦</>了，像我们这样穷苦的人，生来似乎就是为了劳作的。\n　　如果不劳作，今天吃完了饭，就要操心明天的饭在哪里。\n　　如果运气好，工厂给了我劳作的机会，今天工作结束，又要操心明天的工作。\n　　冷的时候，手上会长<Letter_RedBig>疮口</>，一点一点冻掉我的肉。\n　　热的时候，棉絮会钻进我的肺部，让我一点一点咳出我的<Letter_RedBig>灵魂</>。\n　　对我这样的人来说，明天是一种负担。\n　　“永暗的蜡烛，不毁的身躯”，我想要什么也不管，什么也不顾……直接睡过去。"] = "　　Life is too <Letter_RedBig>hard</>. For poor people like us, we seem to be born just to toil.\n　　If we don't toil, once we finish today's meal, we have to worry about where tomorrow's will come from.\n　　If we are lucky and the factory gives me a chance to work, once today's work is done, I have to worry about tomorrow's work.\n　　When it's cold, sores grow on my hands, <Letter_RedBig>sores</> that slowly freeze away my flesh.\n　　When it's hot, cotton fibers drill into my lungs, making me cough out my <Letter_RedBig>soul</> bit by bit.\n　　For someone like me, tomorrow is a burden.\n　　\"Candle of Eternal Darkness, Indestructible Body,\" I want to ignore everything, not care about anything... and just fall asleep.",
    ["　　由于蒂亚女士在工作过程中，并未按照要求完成工作任务，多次迟到、旷工，本工厂通知劝退蒂亚女士，一切后果由蒂亚女士本人承担。\n\n四月六日"] = "Because Ms. Tia did not complete her work tasks as required during her employment, and was late and absent from work multiple times, this factory hereby notifies Ms. Tia of her dismissal. All consequences shall be borne by Ms. Tia herself.\n\nApril 6th",
    ["　　畅销作家佛尔思·沃尔的短篇小说《时代守护者》将正式扩展为长篇连载，该故事一经刊登便广受好评，报纸加印三次仍供不应求。作者表示，故事的真正作者是所有在长夜中选择成为光的人，就如小说结尾所言：“黑暗从未远去，但光明永不会熄灭。”"] = "Bestselling author Fors Wall's short story \"Guardian of the Era\" will be officially expanded into a long-form serial. Once published, the story was well-received, and the newspaper had to be reprinted three times to meet demand. The author stated that the true authors of the story are all those who chose to become light in the long night, just as the end of the novel says: \"The darkness has never gone away, but the light will never be extinguished.\"",
    ["　　畅销小说家佛尔思·沃尔全新力作<Highlight>《大冒险家》</>第二部火热连载中！一经发表即成为社交舞会必备话题……\n　　佛尔思小姐透露，在第二部中，环游世界的海上冒险家将继续探索未知领域，结识新的同伴，让我们共同期待冒险家先生的崭新旅程！"] = "Bestselling novelist Fors Wall's brand new masterpiece <Highlight> \"The Great Adventurer\" </> Part 2 is now being hotly serialized! Once published, it became an essential topic for social balls... \n Ms. Fors revealed that in the second part, the adventurer who travels the world by sea will continue to explore unknown territories and meet new companions. Let us look forward to the adventurer's brand new journey!",
    ["　　稍后，我们要吃掉一部分食物（减轻行李重量），然后启程。\n　　我决定一路记录所见的一切。就在刚才，我看见一个活生生的人从我眼前消失。我已经做好最坏的打算，或许这本日记将是我留在这个世界上的最后一抹痕迹。 一旁的学员转过头对我说，曼斯教授也不见了，下一个会——"] = "　　Later, we are going to eat some of the food (to reduce the weight of the luggage) and then set off.\n　　I have decided to record everything I see along the way. Just a moment ago, I saw a living person disappear right before my eyes. I have prepared for the worst; perhaps this diary will be the last trace I leave in this world. A student beside me turned his head and said to me that Professor Mans is also gone, and who will be next—",
    ["　　第一轮：黛丝不是前来占卜的顾客，<InvHighlight>是一位占卜师</>。\n　　第二轮：黛丝并非死于割伤，而<InvHighlight>是死于法阵</>。 \n　　第三轮：黛丝的死和邪恶仪式无关，<InvHighlight>和她的占卜有关</>。\n　　第四轮：黛丝的死与反锁的占卜室无关，而<InvHighlight>与占卜的结果、前来占卜的顾客有关</>。\n\n　　桌面的线索：一本《仪式魔法：向神明祈求之术》，有两页被折了角，分别是《假死与复生》和《命运的交换》，分别记载着<InvHighlight>不同的仪式魔法内容</>。"] = "Round 1: Daisy was not a customer who came for divination, <InvHighlight> but a diviner. </> \n Round 2: Daisy did not die from the cut, but <InvHighlight> died from the magic circle. </> \n Round 3: Daisy's death has nothing to do with an evil ritual, <InvHighlight> but with her divination. </> \n Round 4: Daisy's death has nothing to do with the locked divination room, but <InvHighlight> with the result of the divination and the customer who came for it. </> \n \n Clues on the table: A book \"Ritual Magic: The Art of Praying to Gods,\" with two pages dog-eared, namely \"Feigned Death and Resurrection\" and \"Exchange of Fate,\" which record <InvHighlight> different ritual magic contents. </>",
    ["　　第十三个了，太爽了！太爽了！\n　　这金色子弹的效果太好了，有了它我还当什么雇佣杀手！\n　　不过那位先生的条件也够奇怪，不管目标是谁，只要在特定地点，特定时间杀……\n　　不管了，反正警察也不会真的抓我，他们说好了的！\n　　按照约定，明天晚上，一切就结束了。"] = "    Thirteenth one, so satisfying! So satisfying! \n    The effect of this gold bullet is too good; with it, why would I still be a hired killer! \n    But that gentleman's conditions are strange enough; no matter who the target is, as long as it's at a specific location, at a specific time, kill... \n    Whatever, anyway, the police won't really catch me; they agreed to it! \n    According to the agreement, tomorrow night, everything will be over.",
    ["　　精通各种占卜，擅长手相、面相等占卜方式，每次收费<Hide stylename=\"Transparent\" id=\"#161\"> 8便士</>。"] = "Proficient in various divination methods, skilled in palmistry, face reading, and other divination methods, 8 pence <Hide stylename=\"Transparent\" id=\"#161\"> </> per session.",
    ["　　索菲亚提出来一个大胆的建议，如果种植豌豆的过程里进行一些改良，加入非凡影响，是不是可以变成一种武器？\n\n\n　　培育预测情况：\n　　第一代：陷阱豌豆*打人豌豆\n　　第二代：都是陷阱豌豆\n　　第三代：陷阱且打人豌豆、陷阱不打人豌豆、打人无陷阱豌豆、不打人也无陷阱豌豆……\n　　种植培育记录……就这样吧：\n　　《“丰收祭司”能力与植物杂交的机制研究：以陷阱豌豆和打人豌豆为例》"] = "Sophia proposed a bold suggestion: if we make some improvements during the process of planting peas and add Beyonder influence, could they become a weapon? \n \n \n Cultivation prediction: \n First generation: Trap Pea * Striking Pea \n Second generation: All are Trap Peas \n Third generation: Trap and Striking Pea, Trap and Non-Striking Pea, Striking and No-Trap Pea, Non-Striking and No-Trap Pea... \n The planting and cultivation record... let's just do it like this: \n \"Research on the Mechanism of 'Harvest Priest' Abilities and Plant Hybridization: A Case Study of Trap Peas and Striking Peas\"",
    ["　　紫丁香的味道很好闻，我把它插在窗前的花瓶里，也许您路过时能看见它们。\n\n　　您最近会多在门口停留一会儿，那我开门时，您又为什么总是一言不发呢？\n\n　　如果是秋天的风太凉，春天的时候，能和我见面吗？"] = "　　The scent of lilacs is very pleasant. I put them in the vase by the window; perhaps you can see them when you pass by.\n\n　　You have been lingering at the door for a while lately, so why are you always speechless when I open the door?\n\n　　If the autumn wind is too cold, can we meet in the spring?",
    ["　　终于逃离了那该死的战争。风暴在上，也感谢爵位和家族的人脉，我可算能在这雪山脚下找到宁静。\n　　村中磨坊里工作的艾莉卡的眼睛像湖水一样蓝……而今天进山时遇到的山民姑娘贝丝，她的笑容像阳光。\n　　我的心从未如此活跃过。或许我应该……顺从心灵的指引？"] = "Finally escaped that damned war. The Storm be above, and thanks to my title and family connections, I can finally find peace at the foot of this snowy mountain.\nErika, who works at the village mill, has eyes as blue as a lake… and Beth, the mountain girl I met when I went into the mountains today, her smile is like sunshine.\nMy heart has never been so alive. Perhaps I should… follow the guidance of my heart?",
    ["　　罗珊新购入了一些手磨咖啡，味道不错，和几年前一样，欢迎回黑荆棘品尝。\n　　放心，不需要执行任务。"] = "Roselle has purchased some new hand-ground coffee; it tastes good, just like a few years ago. Welcome back to Blackthorn to have a taste.\nDon't worry, no mission execution required.",
    ["　　美丽的蒂亚，你是整个码头最娇美的鲜花，你愿意和我一起参加舞会吗？"] = "Beautiful Tia, you are the most delicate flower on the entire wharf. Would you like to attend the ball with me?",
    ["　　老师死了，工坊也倒闭了。\n　　我做不好蜡烛，也救不回老师。\n　　糖厂的工作不适合我，糖是甜的，但糖厂是发苦的。\n　　我什么都做不好，谁也救不回。\n　　“永暗的蜡烛，不毁的身躯”，<Letter_RedBig>请带走我这个无用之人吧。</>"] = "　　The teacher is dead, and the workshop has closed down. \n　　I can't make candles well, and I can't save the teacher. \n　　The job at the sugar factory doesn't suit me; sugar is sweet, but the sugar factory is bitter. \n　　I can't do anything right, and I can't save anyone. \n　　\"Candle of Eternal Darkness, Indestructible Body,\" <Letter_RedBig> please take away this useless person. </>",
    ["　　艾莉卡发现了。她质问我和贝丝的关系……争吵……我发誓我不是故意的……但磨坊烧起来了……她还在里面，她……\n　　……即使我出身贵族，发生这么大的事治安官也会找上门来。我必须去找贝丝。她在骨桥等我。她说会带我躲进山里……\n　　等等……贝丝身边的那个人是谁……那张脸……那不是艾莉卡吗？！她不是已经……\n　　她们在笑……向我走来……她们的脸在变化……变得和我……一样……"] = "    Erika found out. She questioned my relationship with Beth... an argument... I swear I didn't mean to... but the mill caught fire... She was still inside, she...\n    ...Even with my noble background, the magistrate will come knocking after such a major incident. I must find Beth. She's waiting for me at the Bone Bridge. She said she would take me into the mountains to hide...\n    Wait... who is that person next to Beth... that face... isn't that Erika?! Didn't she already...\n    They are laughing... walking toward me... their faces are changing... becoming the same... as mine...",
    ["　　艾莉卡白天在磨坊工作，我每天都去找她。但晚上……不知为何，我总是无法拒绝贝丝的邀约。\n　　狄安娜意识到了这些……她带着孩子去了间海的亲戚家。她说无法忍受这里的寒冷和单调……我想是我这个丈夫让她伤心了……\n　　……睡眠很差……但我舍不得离开……"] = "Erika works at the mill during the day, and I go to see her every day. But at night… for some reason, I can never refuse Beth's invitations.\nDiana has realized this… She took the children to her relatives' place in the Intis. She said she couldn't stand the cold and monotony here… I think it was me, her husband, who broke her heart…\n…My sleep is very poor… but I can't bear to leave…",
    ["　　若你听到了安宁的呼唤，请前往拉斐尔墓园，寻找守夜人<Letter_Highlight_HW>赛勒斯·莫宁</>。\n　　他会为你揭示真相。\n　　愿黑夜庇护你。"] = "　　If you have heard the call of peace, please go to Raphael Cemetery and look for the Night Watchman <Letter_Highlight_HW>Cyrus Morning</>.\n　　He will reveal the truth to you.\n　　May the Goddess protect you.",
    ["　　若你是那鲜红的玫瑰，我便是那刺手的荆棘。小小的纺织女工，怎敢接受一个公爵的爱？别爱我，没结果！\n　　罗塞尔文学奖获得者温弗里德又一力作！玫瑰与荆棘是否能摆脱世俗的压力，见证永恒之爱？"] = "　　If you are that bright red rose, I am that thorny briar. A tiny textile worker, how dare I accept a duke's love? Don't love me, there's no result!\n　　Another tour de force by Roselle Literature Prize winner Winfred! Can the rose and the briar escape the pressures of the secular world and witness eternal love?",
    ["　　药量还是老样子，每日一次，禁止加量。上周你私自加量的事，不要再有第二次。\n　　心悸的频率没有下降，这是我目前最担心的，再这样下去，你的心脏撑不了多久了。\n       如果下次又半夜发作，别硬扛，不管几点，都要让约翰先生来找我。\n       霍克斯先生，我是你的医生，观察你是我的本分，这不是监视！如果你连我都开始怀疑，那恰恰说明，那东西对你的影响比我想的还要深，这让我很不安。\n　　下周四下午三点，我会准时到。希望那个时候，你还是我认识的那个霍克斯先生。"] = "    The dosage is the same as before, once a day, increasing the dose is prohibited. Do not let the incident where you increased the dose without permission last week happen a second time. \n    The frequency of palpitations has not decreased, which is my biggest concern right now. If this continues, your heart won't last much longer. \n    If it happens again in the middle of the night, don't try to tough it out. No matter what time it is, have Mr. John come find me. \n    Mr. Hawks, I am your doctor, observing you is my duty, this is not surveillance! If you have started to doubt even me, that precisely shows that the thing has a deeper influence on you than I thought, which makes me very uneasy. \n    Next Thursday at 3 PM, I will arrive on time. I hope that by then, you are still the Mr. Hawks I know.",
    ["　　警告传说研究会的所有人！\n1、不得长时间直视水面！\n2、不得采摘湖心水底的那一颗睡莲！\n3、若在水边听见呼唤，不要回应！不要回应！不要回应！\n　　愿传说长存，愿我们小镇长青。"] = "Warning to everyone in the Legend Research Society! \n 1. Do not stare directly at the water surface for a long time! \n 2. Do not pick the water lily at the bottom of the lake! \n 3. If you hear a call by the water, do not respond! Do not respond! Do not respond! \n May the legends live on, and may our small town remain evergreen.",
    ["　　警方建议廷根市民减少夜晚外出，尽量不长时间逗留户外。提倡出行结伴，行踪提前告知家人好友。"] = "The police advise Tingen citizens to reduce going out at night and try not to stay outdoors for long periods. It is recommended to travel in groups and inform family and friends of your whereabouts in advance.",
    ["　　警方针对夜间出行发布紧急警示，特别是年轻女性，尽量避免夜间活动。据悉，近期多起失踪案均发生在深夜，受害者失踪前均收到不明约会邀请。"] = "　　The police have issued an emergency warning regarding night travel, especially for young women, advising them to avoid night activities as much as possible. It is reported that many recent missing persons cases occurred late at night, and the victims had received unknown dating invitations before disappearing.",
    ["　　认识“审判官”是偶然。他真名叫布莱克，是议院治安队的中间人，还挺能打的，我亲眼见过他用一把锯刀砍翻了十个人。\n　　但作为朋友，他说话和气，出手阔绰。第一次他请我喝酒，说只是想交个朋友。第二次他送我一块怀表，说是感谢我帮了他小忙。第三次他问我，有没有兴趣赚点外快。\n　　我说，我是警察。\n　　他说，警察也是人。\n　　我把怀表还给他，转身走了。但那个念头又冒出来——钱能买来更大的权力。我只是借用一下，等站稳脚跟，再收拾他们也不迟。\n　　一周后，我给他打了个电话。"] = "　　Meeting the \"Inquisitor\" was accidental. His real name is Black, and he is a middleman for the council's security team. He is quite capable of fighting; I have seen with my own eyes how he used a saw-blade to hack down ten people. \n　　But as a friend, he speaks gently and is generous with his money. The first time he treated me to a drink, he said he just wanted to make a friend. The second time he gave me a pocket watch, saying it was to thank me for helping him with a small favor. The third time he asked me if I was interested in earning some extra money. \n　　I said, I am a policeman. \n　　He said, policemen are also human. \n　　I returned the pocket watch to him and turned to leave. But that thought popped up again—money can buy greater power. I'm just borrowing it; it won't be too late to deal with them after I stand firm. \n　　A week later, I gave him a call.",
    ["　　让我猜猜……你肯定在想'这些牌到底怎么走'对不对？    \n　　放心，就算你不懂扑克，我也不会嘲笑你~\n 　　作为一个负责的主持人，我还是准备了这本宝典——《傻瓜都能懂的牌经》！\n\n 　　所谓<Letter_Highlight>顺子</>，就是连续的5个数字，比如：4-5-6-7-8。\n 　　明白了吗？必须一个跟一个，不能跳着来！也<Letter_Highlight>不能反悔！</>\n\n 　　花色？在这里，爱情不分种族~红心、黑桃、方块、梅花，混着来都行！\n 　　重要的只有<Letter_Highlight>数字顺序</>，记住了吗？\n\n 　　如果你踩错了……嘻嘻，你会摔下去，摔下去，再摔下去！\n\n 　　——爱你的解说员，小丑 敬上"] = "    Let me guess... You must be thinking 'how do these cards move', right?    \n    Don't worry, even if you don't understand poker, I won't laugh at you~\n     As a responsible host, I have prepared this treasure book—《Card Sutra for Dummies》!\n\n     The so-called <Letter_Highlight>Straight</> is 5 consecutive numbers, for example: 4-5-6-7-8.\n     Understand? They must follow one after another, no skipping! And <Letter_Highlight>no taking it back!</>\n\n     Suits? Here, love knows no race~ Hearts, Spades, Diamonds, Clubs, mix them all you want!\n     The only thing that matters is the <Letter_Highlight>numerical order</>, got it?\n\n     If you step wrong... hee hee, you will fall, fall, and fall again!\n\n     ——Yours truly, the commentator, Clown",
    ["　　该死的皮诺亚欺骗了我！\n\n　　他拿走了我整整3金镑，却没有替我通过考试！\n\n　　该死的老鼠！小偷！我绝对不会放过他！"] = "Damn Pinoia deceived me! \n\n He took my entire 3 pounds, but didn't help me pass the exam! \n\n Damn rat! Thief! I will never let him go!",
    ["　　说起来，离开伦堡前，我一直研究的是奇异果。毕竟吃一口就获得神奇的非凡力量，如果能大规模量产，是不是对战知识教会时也能用上？\n\n\n　　好，还是种奇异果吧！\n\n\n　　种植培育记录就用之前用过的标题：\n　　《“大地母神”信仰仪式对物种变异性的影响：以不同非凡能力的奇异果为例》"] = "Speaking of which, before leaving Lenburg, I was always researching kiwifruit. After all, you gain magical Beyonder powers after one bite. If it could be mass-produced, could it be used when fighting the Church of Knowledge? \n \n \n Okay, let's plant kiwifruit! \n \n \n The planting and cultivation record will use the title I used before: \n \"Effects of 'Earth Mother' Faith Rituals on Species Variation: A Case Study of Kiwifruit with Different Beyonder Abilities\"",
    ["　　请同学们自觉抵制“内部资料”，诚信参考。如有发现购买者，将按校规予以<Letter_Highlight>严格惩罚</>。"] = "　　Students are requested to consciously resist \"internal materials\" and take the exam with integrity. If any buyers are discovered, they will be <Letter_Highlight>strictly punished</> according to school regulations.",
    ["　　购买人：艾德温·霍克斯男爵\n　　出售方：<Hide id=\"#157\">夜鸦收藏会</>\n　　交易物品：<Hide id=\"#157\">疑思之镜</>\n　　年代：距今约八百年\n　　已知效果：\n　　佩戴后，可短暂提升观察力与记忆能力。持有者能够注意到常人难以察觉的细节，发现环境中的异常信息、矛盾与隐藏线索。\n\n　          <Letter_Highlight> ————警告————</>                        \n　　长期使用后，可能出现以下症状：\n　　持续性的被窥视感。对自身记忆产生怀疑。认知混乱。偶尔察觉视野边缘出现并不存在的人影。\n　　本组织不对使用者产生的任何精神异常负责。若出现严重症状，请立即停止使用并销毁该物品。\n\n<Note_Normal_HW>它让我看到了一些本不该知道的事。</>\n<Note_Normal_HW>好像，有什么东西跟随它进入了宅邸。</>"] = "　　Purchaser: Baron Edwin Hawkes\n　　Seller: <Hide id=\"#157\">Night Raven Collection Society</>\n　　Item: <Hide id=\"#157\">Mirror of Suspicion</>\n　　Age: Approximately 800 years old\n　　Known Effects: \n　　After wearing, it can briefly enhance observation and memory. The holder can notice details that are difficult for ordinary people to perceive, discovering abnormal information, contradictions, and hidden clues in the environment.\n\n　          <Letter_Highlight> ————WARNING————</>                        \n　　After long-term use, the following symptoms may occur:\n　　A persistent feeling of being watched. Doubts about one's own memory. Cognitive confusion. Occasionally perceiving the presence of non-existent figures in the periphery of one's vision.\n　　This organization is not responsible for any mental abnormalities caused to the user. If severe symptoms appear, please stop using immediately and destroy this item.\n\n<Note_Normal_HW>It made me see some things I shouldn't have known.</>\n<Note_Normal_HW>It seems like something followed it into the mansion.</>",
    ["　　近日，廷根市警察局多次接到报案，有青少年在公共盥洗室内点燃蜡烛，向自称“盥洗室之主”的未知神灵进行祈祷。警方提醒市民：请树立正确信仰，远离一切非正统祈祷活动。 "] = "Recently, the Tingen City Police Department has received multiple reports of teenagers lighting candles in public restrooms and praying to an unknown deity calling themselves the \"Lord of the Restroom.\" The police remind citizens: Please establish correct beliefs and stay away from all unorthodox prayer activities.",
    ["　　近日，警方在廷根市郊的一处公寓内，发现一名不明原因身亡的年轻女子。经核查，死者名为<Highlight>黛丝</>，是一名职业占卜师，数月前曾在一宗被官方认定为自杀的案件中登记为已故市民。\n　　鉴于存在<Highlight>“死者曾死而复生”</>的复杂情节，案件真相目前仍在深入调查中。"] = "Recently, the police discovered a young woman who died of unknown causes in an apartment on the outskirts of Tingen. Upon verification, the deceased was named <Highlight> Daisy </>, a professional diviner who had been registered as a deceased citizen months ago in a case officially ruled as suicide. \n Given the complex plot of <Highlight> \"the deceased having returned from the dead\" </>, the truth of the case is still under deep investigation.",
    ["　　近日，金秋湖连续出现多起少女死亡事件。所有死者颈部均留有清晰的穿刺创口。\n　　案发现场均呈现诡异的一致性：屋内散落着银质烛台与大量枯萎的玫瑰花瓣，似乎被刻意布置成古典婚礼现场。据调查，这些少女生前均热衷阅读《暮色之城》《惊情德古拉》等<Highlight>吸血鬼</>爱情小说。"] = "　　Recently, there have been a series of deaths of young girls at Golden Autumn Lake. All the victims had clear puncture wounds on their necks. \n　　The crime scenes all displayed an eerie consistency: silver candlesticks and a large number of withered rose petals were scattered throughout the rooms, as if they had been deliberately arranged to resemble a classical wedding scene. According to the investigation, all these young girls were avid readers of vampire romance novels such as \"City of Twilight\" and \"Dracula\" before their deaths. <Highlight>vampire</>",
    ["　　近期有不法人员在校内兜售历史系考试的“<Letter_Highlight>内部资料</>”，严重破坏考试公平。若有同学掌握相关情况，请向<Letter_Highlight>学术诚信办公室</>检举揭发。"] = "　　Recently, unauthorized individuals have been selling “<Letter_Highlight>inside information</>” for the history department exam on campus, seriously undermining exam fairness. If any students have relevant information, please report it to the <Letter_Highlight>Office of Academic Integrity</>.",
    ["　　近期，廷根<Highlight>离奇案件频繁发生</>。\n　　一位市民声称头顶长出红色蘑菇。一位富豪家中花房内的花藤疯狂生长，将他勒死在镶金的马桶上……\n　　警方提示，怪异传闻，多为幻觉。如遇此类事件，请立刻报警，或就近前往教堂求助。"] = "Recently, <Highlight> bizarre cases have occurred frequently </> in Tingen. \n A citizen claimed that red mushrooms grew on their head. The vines in a wealthy man's conservatory grew wildly, strangling him on his gold-inlaid toilet... \n The police remind citizens that strange rumors are mostly hallucinations. If you encounter such events, please call the police immediately or go to the nearest church for help.",
    ["　　还在为不会说话而烦恼吗？\n\n　　搜罗上百条因蒂斯传奇帝王罗塞尔·古斯塔夫的名言，数十名社会评论家联袂推荐，本书将为你解答罗塞尔大帝的说话之道！"] = "　　Are you still troubled by not knowing how to speak? \n\n　　Collecting hundreds of quotes from the legendary Intis Emperor Roselle Gustav, recommended by dozens of social critics, this book will answer the art of conversation of Emperor Roselle for you!",
    ["　　这一年的最后一天，森林遭遇了百年未遇的暴雪，猫头鹰长老召集起了一场紧急会议。\n\n　　 “北边山洞上方的积雪发生了崩塌，那里面还住着冬眠的蝙蝠一家，我们不能放着它们不管。”\n\n　　所有的动物都沉默了，它们基本不和蝙蝠来往，只有邓恩在去年春天去过那个洞穴，但它早就忘记里面什么样了。\n\n　　“我们去吧！”戴莉跳到了鹿角顶端，“就算你在里面迷失了方向，我的歌声也能把我们带到正确的道路上。”\n\n　　它们就这样进入了洞穴，里面结构错综复杂，邓恩和戴莉费了不少力气才找到受伤的蝙蝠一家。就在它们准备离开洞穴的时候，外面狂风大作，无数雪花被风裹挟而来，挡住了所有的光。邓恩又尝试了几个方向，比找不到出口更令人绝望的是蝙蝠一家越来越微弱的呼吸。\n\n　　戴莉飞到了它耳边开始歌唱，金色的旋律指引抚平了邓恩有些焦躁的心情，他沿着音符亮起的方向走去。十米，五十米，一百米……眼前仍然没有出现洞口的光亮，戴莉意识到前往出口的代价可能比想象中更多。\n\n　　没有犹豫。\n\n　　它飞得更高了，飞到邓恩根本看不清的地方，歌唱到背上的羽毛所剩无几，她开始下坠。\n\n　　眼前还是没有出现光亮。"] = "On the last day of the year, the forest encountered a blizzard unseen in a century, and the Owl Elder called an emergency meeting. \n\n \"The snow above the northern cave has collapsed, and a family of hibernating bats lives inside. We cannot leave them be.\" \n\n All the animals fell silent; they generally did not associate with bats. Only Dunn had visited that cave last spring, but he had long forgotten what it looked like inside. \n\n \"Let's go!\" Daly jumped onto the tips of the antlers. \"Even if you lose your way inside, my singing can lead us to the right path.\" \n\n They entered the cave just like that. The structure inside was intricate and complex, and it took Dunn and Daly quite some effort to find the injured bat family. Just as they were preparing to leave the cave, a gale blew outside, and countless snowflakes were carried by the wind, blocking all light. Dunn tried several more directions. More desperate than not finding the exit was the increasingly weak breathing of the bat family. \n\n Daly flew to his ear and began to sing. The golden melody guided and soothed Dunn's somewhat restless mood, and he walked along the direction where the notes lit up. Ten meters, fifty meters, one hundred meters... There was still no light from the cave entrance in sight. Daly realized that the price of reaching the exit might be higher than imagined. \n\n Without hesitation. \n\n She flew higher, to a place where Dunn couldn't see clearly, singing until there were few feathers left on her back, and she began to fall. \n\n There was still no light in sight.",
    ["　　这个小镇不对劲！\n　　所有人像木偶一样重复着同样的事，买的面包偶尔会是木头做的，也没人觉得有问题！还有什么？我的记性越来越差了！\n　　赞美睡莲……"] = "　　Something is wrong with this small town!\n　　Everyone repeats the same actions like a marionette. Sometimes the bread I buy is made of wood, and no one thinks there's a problem! What else? My memory is getting worse and worse!\n　　Praise the Water Lily...",
    ["　　这位“收尸人”的皮肤白皙到像是许久没晒过太阳，或是严重缺血，他大概三十来岁，黑发蓝眼，鼻梁高挺，嘴唇很薄，气质冰冷而阴暗，似乎有些许常年触碰尸体留下的淡薄味道。\n　　……\n　　这时，一个很像卷烟盒子的锡铁色方形小壶出现在了他的眼前。\n　　失去瓶塞的口部散发出类似于烟草、消毒水、薄荷叶等混杂的味道，让克莱恩的鼻子霍然发呛，整个人都精神了起来。\n　　浓烈的恶臭依旧缭绕于四周，但克莱恩再不觉得反胃，呕吐很快停止。\n　　他顺着那锡铁色方形小壶往上，看见了一只苍白不像活人的手，看见了黑色风衣的袖管，看见了气质冰冷阴暗的“收尸人”弗莱。\n　　“谢谢。”克莱恩彻底缓了过来，以手撑膝，重新站起。\n　　弗莱没有表情地点了点头：\n　　“习惯就好了。”\n\n　　——第一卷《小丑》第四十六章 画像"] = "This \"Corpse Collector's\" skin was so fair that it looked like he hadn't seen the sun for a long time, or he was severely anemic. He was about thirty years old, with black hair and blue eyes, a high nose bridge, and thin lips. His temperament was cold and dark, and he seemed to have a faint scent left over from years of touching corpses. \n ... \n At this moment, a small tin-colored square pot that looked very much like a cigarette case appeared before his eyes. \n The opening, which had lost its stopper, emitted a smell mixed with tobacco, disinfectant, mint leaves, etc., making Klein's nose suddenly sting and his whole person perk up. \n The intense stench still lingered in the surroundings, but Klein no longer felt nauseous, and the vomiting stopped quickly. \n He followed the small tin-colored square pot upward and saw a pale hand that didn't look like a living person's, saw the sleeve of a black trench coat, and saw the cold and dark-tempered \"Corpse Collector\" Frye. \n \"Thank you.\" Klein finally recovered completely, supported his knees with his hands, and stood up again. \n Frye nodded expressionlessly: \n \"You'll get used to it.\" \n \n —— Volume 1 \"Clown\", Chapter 46, Portrait",
    ["　　这地方太邪门了。已经失踪三个人了，寻宝队的其他人居然还要继续？他们有病吧？\n　　想不通，真的想不通。为什么这么多人发现怪事还不跑？考古的、勘探的、寻宝的……他们不要命了吗？\n　　算了，罗塞尔大帝曾说过，人各有命——我先逃了。顺着这条河划出去，然后找个教堂住下，天天祷告直到这邪门的事过去。\n　　再见了！这见鬼的霍纳奇斯山！"] = "This place is too evil. Three people have already gone missing, and the rest of the treasure hunting team actually wants to continue? Are they sick? \n I can't understand it, I really can't. Why don't so many people run away after discovering strange things? Archaeologists, surveyors, treasure hunters... don't they value their lives? \n Forget it, Emperor Roselle once said, everyone has their own fate—I'm escaping first. I'll row out along this river, then find a church to stay in, praying every day until this evil matter passes. \n Goodbye! This godforsaken Hornacis Mountain!",
    ["　　这时，邓恩·史密斯侧过头来，望向克莱恩，苍白的脸上带着温和而轻松的笑容，嗓音一如既往地醇厚：\n　　“我们拯救了廷根。”\n　　说完之后，他就像回到了二十岁那年，不再那么沉稳不再那么正经地对克莱恩挤了下左眼。\n　　克莱恩的表情凝固在了脸上，看见圣赛琳娜骨灰盒内的那颗心脏停止了跳动，化作璀璨的光点，消散往四周，看见队长的身体往后仰倒，双手松了开来。\n　　这一切就像一幅幅画面构成，但又让人无法阻止。\n\n　　——第一卷《小丑》 第二百一十一章 光"] = "At this moment, Dunn Smith turned his head to look at Klein, his pale face wearing a gentle and relaxed smile, his voice as mellow as ever:\n \"We saved Tingen.\"\n After saying this, he seemed to return to the year he was twenty, no longer as steady or serious as he winked at Klein with his left eye.\n Klein's expression froze on his face. He saw the heart inside Saint Selena's urn stop beating, turn into brilliant points of light, and dissipate into the surroundings. He saw the captain's body fall backward, his hands loosening.\n Everything was like a series of composed frames, yet one that no one could stop.\n\n — Volume 1: Clown, Chapter 211: Light",
    ["　　进了尖塔，戴里克直奔三楼，根据印象，找到了摆放神话资料和相应古籍的书架。\n　　他刚看中一本涉及创世神话的典籍，正打算抽出，却发现一只五指修长，皮肤白皙，形态好看的手掌抢先一步，拿走了那本图书。\n　　戴里克循着手臂望去，只看了一眼，就低下脑袋，以手按胸，沉声问候：\n　　“你好，洛薇雅长老。”\n　　拿走那本典籍的正是“六人议事团”成员，“牧羊人”洛薇雅。\n　　洛薇雅身穿绣有诸多神秘紫纹的黑色长袍，银灰色的头发茂密但带着点卷曲地披着。\n　　她脸庞光滑白嫩，眉眼大气艳丽，看起来也就三十出头，一双淡灰色的眼眸仿佛能洞穿灵魂。\n　　“嗯。”面对戴里克的问好，洛薇雅轻轻点了下头，没有多说什么，沉默地拿着那本典籍离开了两排书架之间。\n　　洛薇雅长老似乎变正常了，不像之前，总是在不同的状态间没有规律地切换，有时哭泣，有时冷笑，有时怒哼，有时漠然……戴里克下意识便闪过了这样的念头。\n　　突然，他莫名有些害怕。\n　　因为洛薇雅长老正常了……\n　　正常了……\n　　……\n\n　　——第2卷《无面人》 第一百零二章 重返丰收教堂"] = "Entering the spire, Derrick headed straight for the third floor and, based on his memory, found the bookshelf containing mythological materials and corresponding ancient texts. \n He had just taken a fancy to a classic involving creation myths and was about to pull it out when he found a palm with slender fingers, fair skin, and a beautiful shape snatching the book away first. \n Derrick followed the arm and looked up, and after just one glance, he lowered his head, pressed his hand to his chest, and asked in a deep voice: \n \"Hello, Elder Lovia.\" \n The one who took the classic was indeed a member of the \"Six-Member Council,\" the Shepherd Lovia. \n Lovia wore a black robe embroidered with many mysterious purple patterns, and her silver-gray hair was thick but slightly curly. \n Her face was smooth and fair, her features grand and beautiful, and she looked to be only in her early thirties, with a pair of light gray eyes that seemed to be able to pierce through the soul. \n \"Hmm.\" Facing Derrick's greeting, Lovia nodded slightly, didn't say much, and silently walked away between the two rows of bookshelves with the classic. \n Elder Lovia seems to have returned to normal, unlike before, where she was always switching between different states without any pattern, sometimes crying, sometimes sneering, sometimes snorting in anger, sometimes indifferent... Derrick subconsciously flashed such a thought. \n Suddenly, he felt inexplicably afraid. \n Because Elder Lovia was normal... \n Normal... \n ... \n \n —— Volume 2 \"Faceless\", Chapter 102, Returning to the Harvest Church",
    ["　　邓恩和戴莉认识之后，戴莉就以“自己的羽毛掉光了，好冷”为理由在邓恩头上筑了巢，并为他重复每个被遗忘的信息；邓恩则载着它巡视森林，用厚厚的灰色皮毛为它挡风，用鹿角为它摘下最高处的浆果。\n\n　　戴莉喜欢趴在它脑袋靠后一些的位置，并时常抱怨它额前的毛发不够厚实。\n\n　　一天，戴莉发现邓恩从地上捡起来什么东西，固定在角上后它发现是自己掉落的羽毛。\n\n 　　“这些羽毛太美了，我舍不得它们就这样被遗忘。”邓恩甩了甩头，“即使我明天就会忘记为什么要这么做，但我的角会记得这种发痒的感觉。”\n\n　　戴莉的心轻轻颤动，她激动地盘旋在邓恩的两角之间，准备一展歌喉抖落几根崭新的羽毛。邓恩阻止了它这种会让自己更冷的行为，请它帮忙整理那些收集好的羽毛。戴莉将它们和一个个木牌挂在一起，让它们在风雪中碰撞，与鹿蹄声和鸟鸣声组成森林的曲调。"] = "    After Dunn and Daly met, Daly built a nest on Dunn's head, using the excuse that 'my feathers have all fallen out, it's so cold,' and repeated every forgotten piece of information to him; Dunn carried it while patrolling the forest, shielding it from the wind with his thick gray fur and picking berries from the highest branches with his antlers. \n\n    Daly liked to lie on the back of his head and often complained that the fur on his forehead wasn't thick enough. \n\n    One day, Daly noticed Dunn picking something up from the ground and fixing it to his antlers, only to realize it was its own fallen feathers. \n\n     'These feathers are too beautiful, I can't bear to let them be forgotten like this.' Dunn shook his head. 'Even if I forget why I'm doing this tomorrow, my antlers will remember this itching sensation.' \n\n    Daly's heart fluttered gently. It circled excitedly between Dunn's two antlers, preparing to show off its voice and shake off a few brand-new feathers. Dunn stopped it from doing something that would make it even colder and asked it to help organize the collected feathers. Daly hung them together with wooden tags, letting them collide in the wind and snow, composing the forest's melody with the sound of deer hooves and bird calls.",
    ["　　金毛大狗似乎被花朵的香味迷乱了嗅觉，并未注意到身后的主人，它张开嘴巴，发出吊嗓子般的“啊啊啊”“呀呀呀”声音。\n　　紧接着，它让周围的空气振动，响起生涩不够圆润的单词：\n　　“你好。”\n　　“你好吗？”\n　　……\n　　奥黛丽的嘴巴一点点张开，完全忘记了优雅淑女该具备的礼仪，她完全不敢相信自己看到的这一幕场景和听到的僵硬声音。\n　　她猛地站起，脱口而出道：\n　　“苏茜，你会说话？你什么时候会说话了？”\n　　金毛大狗吓得跳了起来，转身面对了主人。\n　　它慌乱而快速地摇起尾巴，嘴部张合几次后才震荡了周围的空气道：\n　　“我……”\n　　“我不知道该怎么解释，毕竟我只是一条狗。”\n　　听到这句话，奥黛丽一时竟无言以对。\n\n　　——第一卷《小丑》第一百一十二章 阿兹克的解释"] = "The golden retriever seemed to have its sense of smell dazed by the fragrance of the flowers and did not notice its owner behind it. It opened its mouth and made \"ah-ah-ah\" and \"ya-ya-ya\" sounds like someone warming up their voice. \n Immediately after, it caused the surrounding air to vibrate, sounding out stiff and unpolished words: \n \"Hello.\" \n \"How are you?\" \n ... \n Audrey's mouth opened bit by bit, completely forgetting the etiquette a graceful lady should possess. She could not believe the scene she was seeing and the stiff voice she was hearing. \n She stood up abruptly and blurted out: \n \"Susie, you can talk? Since when could you talk?\" \n The golden retriever jumped up in fright and turned to face its owner. \n It wagged its tail in a flustered and rapid manner, and only after opening and closing its mouth several times did it vibrate the surrounding air to say: \n \"I...\" \n \"I don't know how to explain it, after all, I am just a dog.\" \n Hearing this, Audrey was left speechless for a moment. \n \n —— Volume 1 \"Clown\", Chapter 112, Azik's Explanation",
    ["　　金秋湖畔的小镇中，有人号称撞见了形似章鱼的谜之黑影。"] = "In a small town by Golden Autumn Lake, someone claimed to have encountered a mysterious black shadow resembling an octopus.",
    ["　　银雾森林迎来了今年的第一场雪，东边的雾气也越发浓厚，掉落了不少羽毛的戴莉在窝里冻得直发抖。枝头小小的巢穴无法抵御寒冷，顶上抖落的一坨雪将巢穴砸落下去，戴莉还没来得及发出叫声，就发现自己被温暖的灰色皮毛包裹——它落在了一只灰麋鹿的头顶。\n\n 　　“我察觉到这里有动物需要帮助，是你吗？”那只灰麋鹿这么说道。\n\n 　　“如果你是来给我带来温暖的，那确实是我。”恢复了体温的戴莉在麋鹿的头顶蹦跶了几下，继续说道：“我叫戴莉， 你的名字是什么？”\n\n　　 “我是……抱歉，我忘记了我的名字。”\n\n　　戴莉这才注意到，麋鹿的角上挂着许多小木牌，上面写着“我叫邓恩”、我是森林的守护者”、“每天巡逻看谁需要帮助”……\n\n　　 “你叫邓恩，”戴莉轻声说，她听树洞里的松鼠一家提起过这头每到冬天就会失忆的麋鹿，曾一天给他们送了三次松子，“你是银雾森林的守护者。”"] = "The Silver Mist Forest welcomed its first snow of the year, and the mist in the east became thicker. Daly, having lost many feathers, shivered in the nest. The small nest on the branch could not resist the cold, and a lump of snow shaken from above knocked the nest down. Before Daly could even make a sound, she found herself wrapped in warm gray fur—it had landed on the head of a gray elk. \n\n \"I sensed that an animal here needed help, is it you?\" the gray elk said. \n\n \"If you are here to bring me warmth, then it is indeed me.\" Having regained her body temperature, Daly hopped a few times on the elk's head and continued: \"My name is Daly, what is your name?\" \n\n \"I am... sorry, I forgot my name.\" \n\n Daly then noticed that the elk's antlers were hung with many small wooden signs, which read \"My name is Dunn\", \"I am the guardian of the forest\", \"Patrol every day to see who needs help\"... \n\n \"Your name is Dunn,\" Daly said softly. She had heard the squirrel family in the tree hole mention this elk that would lose its memory every winter, who had once delivered pine nuts to them three times in one day, \"You are the guardian of the Silver Mist Forest.\"",
    ["　　镜"] = "Mirror",
    ["　　阅览后发现，还真不是荒诞的随笔。时空逆转后，罗塞尔大帝与乔治三世灵魂互换，成为了鲁恩国王，他在1350年的战争中获得大胜，创造了无数跨时代的发明，但他仍解不开蒸汽教会的纠缠，最终度过了复杂的一生。\n　　乔治三世坐上罗塞尔的位置后，反而低调异常，直到晚年在疯狂中死去。\n　　命运如一条狡猾的蛇！真是一对传奇帝王啊！"] = "After reading it, I found it really wasn't just an absurd essay. After space-time was reversed, Emperor Roselle and George III swapped souls, and he became the King of Loen. He won a great victory in the war of 1350 and created countless epoch-making inventions, but he still couldn't untangle the entanglement of the Church of Steam, and eventually lived a complex life.\nAfter George III sat in Roselle's position, he was unusually low-key until he died in madness in his later years.\nFate is like a cunning snake! What a legendary pair of emperors!",
    ["　　阿尔杰再次发问：\n        “你觉得‘牧羊人’洛薇雅长老有可能会对白银城造成危害吗？只用回答是或者否，不要解释。”\n        “……是。”戴里克最终还是无法欺骗自己。\n        阿尔杰轻笑了一声道：\n        “所以，你是唯一知道这件事情，却暂时找不到办法提醒六人议事团其他长老的人，对吧？”\n        “嗯。”戴里克的神情逐渐变得凝重。\n        阿尔杰改变了下坐姿，往后微靠道：“那个任务的风险极大，这一点，你是知道的，如果你死在了那座半毁的神庙里，谁还能想办法揭露‘牧羊人’洛薇雅的古怪？谁还能让白银城免于灾难？‘堕落造物主’可是一位真正的邪神！”\n        “你不是因为自私才假装失控，欺骗其他人，你是为了拯救白银城！”\n\n       ——第五卷《红祭司》第一百二十九章 “老油条”阿尔杰"] = "Alger asked again:\n \"Do you think Shepherd Elder Lovia might pose a threat to the City of Silver? Just answer yes or no, don't explain.\"\n \"...Yes.\" Derrick ultimately could not deceive himself.\n Alger chuckled and said:\n \"So, you are the only one who knows about this, but you can't find a way to warn the other elders of the Six-Member Council for the time being, right?\"\n \"Yeah.\" Derrick's expression gradually became solemn.\n Alger changed his sitting posture and leaned back: \"The risk of that mission is extremely high. You know this. If you die in that half-destroyed temple, who else can find a way to expose Shepherd Lovia's strangeness? Who else can save the City of Silver from disaster? The 'Fallen Creator' is a true evil god!\"\n \"You aren't pretending to lose control and deceiving others out of selfishness; you are doing it to save the City of Silver!\"\n\n — Volume 5: Red Priest, Chapter 129: \"Old Fox\" Alger",
    ["　　随着<Highlight>罗塞尔大帝</>戏剧节临近，廷根各大报纸争相重温他的光辉历史。这位一百多年前的异国皇帝，曾推动工业革命的时代浪潮席卷北大陆各国。\n　　蒸汽轰鸣的时代，伟大的罗塞尔大帝的时代，仿佛又回来了！"] = "As the <Highlight> Emperor Roselle </> Drama Festival approaches, major newspapers in Tingen are competing to revisit his glorious history. This foreign emperor from over a hundred years ago once pushed the tides of the Industrial Revolution to sweep across the countries of the Northern Continent. \n The era of roaring steam, the era of the great Emperor Roselle, seems to have returned!",
    ["　　隐匿贤者最初只是一名非人格化的神灵。 \n　　相比起神灵，祂更接近于一种理念，一种自然法则。\n　　信仰祂的摩斯苦修会掌握着“隐者”途径的魔药与晋升方式，成员坚持着道德和戒律，坚持着对知识的追求，并严格守秘。入会者在成为“窥秘人”后，都要禁语五年，学会静默，以便修行和提高专注，甚至是对抗失控。\n　　会内流传着一句格言——为所欲为，但勿伤害——这也为许多“窥秘人”所信奉并践行……贝尔纳黛殿下似乎也很欣赏这句格言。"] = "The Hidden Sage was initially just an impersonal deity. \n Compared to a god, It was closer to a concept, a natural law. \n The Moses Ascetic Order, which believes in It, possesses the potions and advancement methods of the \"Hermit\" pathway. Its members adhere to morality and precepts, persist in the pursuit of knowledge, and strictly maintain secrecy. After becoming a \"Mystery Pryer,\" initiates must remain silent for five years, learning to be quiet in order to cultivate and improve focus, or even to resist loss of control. \n A maxim circulates within the order—Do what you will, but do no harm—which is also believed in and practiced by many \"Mystery Pryers\"... Her Highness Bernadette seems to appreciate this maxim as well.",
    ["　　非常抱歉！\n　　这是我自己做的木雕钢琴，请您小心边缘的毛刺。用它作为赔礼可能有点粗糙，但请您相信，我意识到了自己的错误。我只顾办案，两次忘记与您的约会，还麻烦您在餐厅帮我解围，绝非绅士所为。再次抱歉，既为失约，也为我的鲁莽。\n　　您十分优秀，一定可以找到更好的结婚对象，祝您幸福！"] = "I am very sorry!\nThis is a wooden piano I carved myself; please be careful of the burrs on the edges. Using it as an apology might be a bit crude, but please believe that I have realized my mistake. I was too focused on the case and forgot our dates twice, and I even troubled you to help me out of a tight spot at the restaurant; that was definitely not the behavior of a gentleman. Sorry again, both for missing our dates and for my recklessness.\nYou are excellent and will surely find a better marriage partner. I wish you happiness!",
    ["　　鸡蛋是大家熟悉的食物，当一颗幸运蛋混在一百枚鸡蛋里，你还能准确找出它吗？“百里挑蛋”挑战赛，火爆进行中，来试试看，下一个“万镑户”就是你！"] = "　　Eggs are a familiar food to everyone. When a lucky egg is mixed in with a hundred others, can you accurately find it? The \"One in a Hundred Eggs\" challenge is in full swing. Come and try it; the next \"ten-thousand-pound winner\" could be you!",
    ["　　黑夜女神教会即日起开设免费成人识字班，面向全市市民开放。\n　　课程内容包括识字、算术、书信写作及教会经文导读。有意者可前往圣赛琳娜教堂报名。"] = "The Church of the Evernight Goddess is opening free adult literacy classes starting today, open to all citizens of the city. \n Course content includes literacy, arithmetic, letter writing, and guided reading of church scriptures. Those interested may go to Saint Selena Cathedral to sign up.",
    ["　　黑夜女神教会唱诗班招新，赞美女神，获得宁静。有意向者可前往……"] = "Evernight Goddess Church choir is recruiting. Praise the Goddess and find peace. Those interested can go to...",
    ["　伦纳德玩世不恭般地笑笑道：“克莱恩，我们之间不需要假装，我目睹过你摆脱封印物‘2-049’的控制，知道你的特殊，而你也应该模糊感觉得出来我和一般非凡者不同。”\n　　他收敛笑容，迎着克莱恩的目光道：\n　　“我曾经对你说过，这个世界上有很多特殊的人，总是能做到别人做不到的事情，比如说你，也比如说我。”\n　　“这个世界拥有漫长的历史，存在这样或者那样的神奇物品，总会有人得到它们，掌握它们，成为不同戏剧的主角，这样的人不会太多，但肯定不可能只有那么一两位。”\n\n　　——第一卷《小丑》第一百二十一章 伦纳德的“猜测”"] = "Leonard smiled cynically and said, \"Klein, there's no need for us to pretend. I witnessed you break free from the control of the mystical item '2-049', so I know you're special. You should also be able to vaguely sense that I'm different from the average Beyonder.\"\n He reined in his smile and, meeting Klein's gaze, said:\n \"I once told you that there are many special people in this world who can always do things others cannot—like you, and like me.\"\n \"This world has a long history, and there are all sorts of mystical items. There will always be people who obtain them, master them, and become the protagonists of different dramas. There aren't many such people, but it's impossible for there to be only one or two.\"\n\n — Volume 1: Clown, Chapter 121: Leonard's \"Guess\"",
    ["　小丑们涌了过来，有的表演踩马车轮子不倒，有的匍匐于巨大的皮球上，有的往天空扔出一个个网球，又以滑稽的动作一一接住。\n　　梅丽莎看着这些表演，神情沉静地就像对方并不存在，班森努力了几次，并大声喝彩，可都没能调动起妹妹的情绪，自己也慢慢低沉。\n　　克莱恩紧抿嘴唇，远远望着这一幕，想要靠近却又不敢。\n　　忽然，他摸了下衣兜里的钱夹，有了一个想法。\n　　班森和梅丽莎继续前行，沉默地观看着各种表演。\n　　过了一阵，他们看到一个涂着红黄白等各色油彩的小丑跑了过来，先是往天上扔出一个个网球，接着在人们的注意力被吸引到半空时，不知从哪里变出了一束花，一束塞维亚菊。\n　　这束花凑到了梅丽莎和班森眼前，颜色金黄，象征着快乐。\n　　梅丽莎和班森略显茫然地望向对面的小丑，只见他满是红黄白等各色油彩的脸上，嘴角高高翘起，固定着一个快乐的笑容，浮夸的笑容，滑稽的笑容。\n\n　　——第一卷《小丑》第二百一十三章 再看一眼"] = "Clowns swarmed over, some performing by stepping on carriage wheels without falling, some crawling on huge leather balls, some throwing tennis balls into the sky, and catching them one by one with funny movements. \n Melissa watched these performances, her expression as calm as if the other party didn’t exist. Benson tried several times and cheered loudly, but couldn’t stir up his sister’s emotions, and he himself slowly became depressed. \n Klein pursed his lips, watching this scene from afar, wanting to approach but not daring to. \n Suddenly, he touched the wallet in his pocket and had an idea. \n Benson and Melissa continued to move forward, watching various performances in silence. \n After a while, they saw a clown painted with red, yellow, white, and other oil paints run over, first throwing tennis balls into the sky, and then when people’s attention was attracted to the air, he produced a bouquet of flowers from nowhere, a bouquet of Zinnia. \n This bouquet was brought to Melissa and Benson’s eyes, golden in color, symbolizing happiness. \n Melissa and Benson looked at the clown opposite with a slightly dazed look, only to see the corners of his mouth, which was full of red, yellow, white, and other oil paints, raised high, fixing a happy smile, an exaggerated smile, a funny smile. \n \n —— Volume 1: Clown, Chapter 213: Take Another Look",
