    ["佛尔思已经失去了耐心！"] = "Fors has lost her patience!",
    ["佛尔思庆祝开服"] = "Fors Celebrates Server Launch",
    ["佛尔思总是在截稿日前一夜才动笔。\n这不是拖延，而是一种奇怪的仪式——仿佛只有当死亡的阴影（或是编辑的怒吼）真正逼近时，那些沉睡在脑海中的故事才会苏醒。她窝在圣乔治区那间狭小的出租屋里，笔尖在纸上沙沙作响，咖啡凉透了也浑然不觉。这时候的她，不再是那个连出门买面包都觉得麻烦的懒散女人，而是主宰笔下人物命运的造物主。\n她写畅销小说，写《暴风山庄》，写那些冷静而智慧的侦探故事。读者称赞她的推理精妙，却不知那些让人拍案叫绝的情节，大多源于她和休在东区调查时遭遇的真实危险。生活总是比小说更荒诞，也更残酷。她把自己对危险的恐惧、对谜题的好奇，都藏进了字里行间。\n或许对远方世界的探索，一直是她命运的关键词。第一次看到穿墙而过的安丽萨太太时，那种对未知的渴望一下子被点燃了。她真的只想安于慵懒的生活吗？那神秘的力量不止是一个孤独老太太的馈赠，背后藏着无数危险——佛尔思知道的，那是来自未知世界的邀请。她将会一次又一次卷入危机，又一次次成功脱身，就像她笔下的主角一样，拥有无限危险而又精彩的人生。\n这一切或许早已注定。儿时匮乏的爱，让她习惯了以善意待人，这反而为她打开了非凡世界的大门。佛尔思早已不会怨恨谁，她知道自己远比想象中更强大，也更包容。等赚够了钱，她还要体验更多生活，写更好的故事。未来永远充满惊喜。\n毕竟，人生就是一篇等待完成的手稿啊。"] = "Fors always starts writing the night before the deadline.\n This isn't procrastination, but a strange ritual—as if only when the shadow of death (or the roar of an editor) truly approaches do the stories sleeping in her mind awaken. She huddles in that cramped rented room in the Saint George District, her pen scratching on paper, not even noticing when her coffee has gone cold. At this moment, she is no longer the lazy woman who finds even going out to buy bread a hassle, but the creator who controls the fate of the characters under her pen.\n She writes bestselling novels, writes \"Storm Mountain Villa,\" and writes those calm and wise detective stories. Readers praise her intricate reasoning, not knowing that those plots that make people applaud are mostly derived from the real dangers she and Xio encountered while investigating in the East District. Life is always more absurd and cruel than fiction. She hides her fear of danger and her curiosity about puzzles between the lines.\n Perhaps the exploration of distant worlds has always been the keyword of her fate. The moment she saw Mrs. Anlisa walk through a wall, that longing for the unknown was ignited. Does she really just want a lazy life? That mysterious power is not just a gift from a lonely old lady; it hides countless dangers behind it—Fors knows this; it is an invitation from an unknown world. She will be drawn into crises again and again, and escape successfully again and again, just like the protagonists in her books, possessing an infinitely dangerous yet wonderful life.\n Perhaps all of this was destined. The lack of love in her childhood made her accustomed to treating others with kindness, which in turn opened the door to the Extraordinary World for her. Fors no longer resents anyone; she knows she is far stronger and more inclusive than she imagined. Once she earns enough money, she will experience more of life and write better stories. The future is always full of surprises.\n After all, life is just a manuscript waiting to be completed.",
    ["佛尔思战斗区域"] = "Fors Combat Area",
    ["佛尔思换阵营无敌"] = "Fors faction change invincibility",
    ["佛尔思教你祈求，一起诵念赫密斯语尊名。\n“漫游星空的旅行者，黄黑之王的眷者，记录世界的法师。”\n“我向您祈求旅行的自由，我向您祈求穿梭的许可。”\n祈祷完成，尖碑开启"] = "Fors teaches you how to pray, and you recite the honorific name in Hermes together.\n \"The traveler who roams the stars, the Blessed of the Yellow and Black King, the mage who records the world.\"\n \"I pray to you for the freedom to travel, I pray to you for the permission to traverse.\"\n The prayer is complete, and the stele opens.",
    ["佛尔思狂暴"] = "Fors Berserk",
    ["佛尔思破防层数"] = "Fors Armor Break Stacks",
    ["佛尔思背面"] = "Fors Back View",
    ["佛尔思走1"] = "Fors Walking 1",
    ["佛尔思走2"] = "Fors Walking 2",
    ["佛尔思锁血1%"] = "Fors lock health 1%",
    ["佛尔思隐秘羁绊"] = "Fors Secret Bond",
    ["佛尔思隐秘羁绊奖励"] = "Fors secret bond reward",
    ["佛尔思：不管是不是A先生做的，我们都得将剩下的8000镑给他。"] = "Fors: Regardless of whether Mr. A did it, we have to give him the remaining 8000 pounds.",
    ["佛尔思：也许。"] = "Fors: Perhaps.",
    ["佛尔思：如果我们还想混这个圈子，就不能赖账！"] = "Fors: If we still want to hang around in this circle, we can't welch on the debt!",
    ["佛尔思：应该是，毕竟我们昨天才给了他2000镑，应该没别的人想刺杀那个贝克朗大使了吧……"] = "Fors: It should be, after all, we only gave him 2000 pounds yesterday, there shouldn't be anyone else wanting to assassinate that Ambassador Bakerland...",
    ["佛山"] = "Foshan",
    ["佛朗哥·"] = "Franco ",
    ["作业本1"] = "Exercise Book 1",
    ["作业本2"] = "Workbook 2",
    ["作业用椅子"] = "Work Chair",
    ["作为“仲裁人”途径的半神，我对秩序拥有更加敏锐的感知，维持现有的规则既是扮演的需要，也是多年以来的习惯。"] = "As a Demigod of the \"Arbiter\" pathway, I have a more acute perception of order. Maintaining existing rules is both a need for acting and a habit formed over many years.",
    ["作为“梦魇”，我可以进入他人的梦境。那时候他刚经历一场非凡事件，我需要确认他是否隐瞒了一些信息。"] = "As a 'Nightmare', I can enter other people's dreams. At that time, he had just experienced an Extraordinary incident, and I needed to confirm if he had withheld any information.",
    ["作为「召唤者」，可选取合适的幻象投影报名参战。每个幻象投影只能出战一次，请谨慎抉择。可提前报名后续场次，无需时刻在线。"] = "As a 'Summoner', you can select suitable phantom projections to register for the battle. Each phantom projection can only fight once, so please choose carefully. You can register for subsequent sessions in advance, no need to be online all the time.",
    ["作为一个“不眠者”，他每天只需要休息两个小时，那些工厂主和银行家肯定最喜欢这种魔药。"] = "As a Sleepless, he only needs two hours of rest every day. Factory owners and bankers must love this potion.",
    ["作为一个善于观察的作家，嘈杂的环境会给我更多灵感。"] = "As a writer who is good at observing, a noisy environment gives me more inspiration.",
    ["作为一个隐秘组织，我们的称号得尽量一致，而“愚者”先生的名字来自塔罗牌……决定了！"] = "As a secret organization, our titles should be consistent, and Mr. Fool's name comes from the Tarot cards... It's decided!",
    ["作为一名值夜者，你有了自由使用手枪和攻击敌人的权限。"] = "As a Nighthawk, you have the authority to freely use a revolver and attack enemies.",
    ["作为一名守护廷根的值夜者，我不能每天按时回家，给她讲睡前故事，只能向女神祈祷，愿她有个美梦。"] = "As a Nighthawk guarding Tingen, I can't go home on time every day to tell her bedtime stories, so I can only pray to the Goddess, wishing her sweet dreams.",
    ["作为一名神秘学爱好者，我当然要试下。"] = "As an occult enthusiast, of course I have to try it.",
    ["作为人类的“我”去世后，非凡特性和书中的知识结合，诞生了现在的“我”。"] = "After the human \"me\" passed away, the Beyonder characteristic combined with the knowledge in the books, giving birth to the current \"me\".",
    ["作为从金秋湖来到霍伊大学的学生，我感到非常骄傲。"] = "As a student from Golden Autumn Lake who came to Hoey University, I feel very proud.",
    ["作为他的朋友，我可真有点失职。你瞧，现在又找不着他了。"] = "As his friend, I've really been quite negligent. Look, I can't find him again now.",
    ["作为俱乐部战局的中枢，你的决策将改写沙盘上的历史走向。罗塞尔的视线凝视着你，祂在判断，你是否有资格触及更深的战争真相。"] = "As the hub of the club's war situation, your decisions will rewrite the historical direction of the sandbox. Roselle's gaze is fixed on you; He is judging whether you are qualified to touch the deeper truth of the war.",
    ["作为值夜者小队的文职人员，标准的非凡者，给邓恩写申请批准费用，属于工作的需要啊！"] = "As a civilian staff member of the Nighthawks squad, a standard Beyonder, writing an application for approval of expenses to Dunn is a work necessity!",
    ["作为值夜者小队的新人，你也被分派了一桩奇异的案件。"] = "As a newcomer to the Nighthawk squad, you have been assigned a strange case.",
    ["作为值夜者，我们永远相信队友。"] = "As Nighthawks, we always trust our teammates.",
    ["作为养料，留下你们的灵魂！"] = "Leave your souls behind as nourishment!",
    ["作为击弦乐器，钢琴最重要的部分，就是琴弦。"] = "As a percussion instrument, the most important part of a piano is its strings.",
    ["作为参赛者，参与歌剧魅影1次"] = "Participate in Phantom of the Opera once as a contestant.",
    ["作为唯一的幸存者和线索，我被值夜者拜访调查。而这一切似乎都是因为那本丢失的<P_Yellow>安提哥努斯笔记</>。"] = "As the only survivor and clue, I was visited and investigated by the Nighthawks. And all of this seems to be because of that lost <P_Yellow>Antigonus Notebook</>.",
    ["作为商人，我很高兴收到一大叠便士。"] = "As a merchant, I am very happy to receive a large stack of pennies.",
    ["作为商人，我很高兴收到一大叠苏勒。"] = "As a merchant, I am very happy to receive a large stack of Sol.",
    ["作为大律师学院的高材生，当然是去贝克兰德的希尔斯顿区，做一位体面的白领。"] = "As a top student at the Great Law School, of course, I'm going to the Hillston District in Backlund to be a decent white-collar worker.",
    ["作为女士，你还缺一根点缀这里的项链。"] = "As a lady, you are still missing a necklace to accent this.",
    ["作为女神的信徒，我不能违背自己的平等思想。"] = "As a believer of the Goddess, I cannot go against my own principles of equality.",
    ["作为学徒，我本想用点“特别的方式”穿墙取个宝箱， 结果……如你所见，把自己卡住了。 帮我出来，宝箱和钥匙都归你！"] = "As an Apprentice, I wanted to use a 'special method' to walk through the wall to get a treasure chest, but... as you can see, I got myself stuck. Help me out, and the treasure chest and the key are all yours!",
    ["作为安提哥努斯家族的后裔，他没有享受曾经这个姓氏带来的家族荣耀，却因为后裔身份，染上了难以抵抗的厄运。"] = "As a descendant of the Antigonus family, he did not enjoy the glory that once came with the name, but instead, due to his lineage, he was tainted by an irresistible misfortune.",
    ["作为廷根市唯一的高档百货，我们一直不知道背后的出资者是谁。"] = "As the only high-end department store in Tingen City, we have never known who the investor behind it is.",
    ["作为技能输入方向"] = "Used as the skill input direction.",
    ["作为整个廷根危机的策划者，在镜中廷根崩溃后，他从未现身，也未被确认死亡或捕获。"] = "As the mastermind behind the entire Tingen crisis, he never appeared after Tingen in the Mirror collapsed, nor was his death or capture confirmed.",
    ["作为新员工，你表现很不错。"] = "As a new employee, you performed very well.",
    ["作为早餐来说，黑麦面包是最实惠的选择。"] = "As a breakfast, rye bread is the most affordable choice.",
    ["作为普通人，我也会尽自己最大的努力，来配合你们的工作。"] = "As an ordinary person, I will also do my best to cooperate with your work.",
    ["作为曾经的佣兵小队，你们真的不考虑和我去进行一场冒险吗？"] = "As a former mercenary squad, are you really not considering going on an adventure with me?",
    ["作为最高保密等级，“0”级封印物的搜索传达一直都只有模糊的信息。这点，你应该很清楚。"] = "As the highest security level, the search for a Grade 0 Sealed Artifact has always only conveyed vague information. You should be very clear about this.",
    ["作为沉迷欲望的代价，你的行动变得迟缓。"] = "As the price for indulging in desire, your movements have become sluggish.",
    ["作为见证过真相的人，你再合适不过了！"] = "As someone who has witnessed the truth, you are more than suitable!",
    ["作为观众观看记忆"] = "Watch the memory as a Spectator",
    ["作为边框的繁花装饰，以盛放的姿态温柔环绕，在边缘处静听微风与花香的呢喃。\n重复获取将自动分解为绑定苏勒×10000。"] = "Floral decorations as a frame, gently surrounding in a blooming posture, listening to the whispers of the breeze and floral fragrance at the edges. \nRepeated acquisition will automatically decompose into Bound Sol ×10000.",
    ["作为顾客，这该死的钞票实在太不值钱。"] = "As a customer, this damn money is really worthless.",
    ["作为颜料，还算合格。"] = "As a pigment, it's passable.",
    ["作为驯兽师，我不可能驯服命运这头巨兽。但是作为一个塔罗爱好者，我却能解读它。"] = "As a Beast Tamer, I cannot tame the giant beast that is fate. But as a Tarot enthusiast, I can interpret it.",
    ["作为魅惑发起者战胜的TopK对手"] = "Top K Opponents Defeated as Charm Initiator",
    ["作为魅惑发起者胜利"] = "Victory as Charm Initiator",
