    ["戈登"] = "Gordon",
    ["戈登·"] = "Gordon ",
    ["戈登和戴维发现了山上一个被积雪覆盖的遗迹入口，他们回到营地将消息报告给曼斯教授，教授当即就带着一些学者和几个护卫往山上赶。\n而我和另外几个学员则留在了营地，准备必要的物资。边搬东西的时候我边想，不久后我也要称呼戈登和戴维他们“研究员先生”了吧。\n对于新遗迹的考古研究是相当累人的工作，研究员们还在遗迹入口确认遗迹的建筑风格，而我们这些不受重视的学员就只能干剩下的粗重杂活，像是搬运物资或是清理现场之类的。\n回到营地，曼斯教授很兴奋，有几个研究员提议在营地开个庆功宴，曼斯教授也同意了，终于能放松一下了。\n庆功宴将持续一整晚……"] = "Gordon and David discovered a ruins entrance covered in snow on the mountain. They returned to the camp to report the news to Professor Mans, who immediately rushed to the mountain with some scholars and a few guards. \n As for me and the other students, we stayed at the camp to prepare the necessary supplies. While moving things, I thought to myself that soon I would also be calling Gordon and David 'Mr. Researcher'. \n Archaeological research on new ruins is quite exhausting work. The researchers were still confirming the architectural style at the ruins entrance, while we, the undervalued students, could only do the remaining heavy labor, like moving supplies or cleaning up the site. \n Returning to the camp, Professor Mans was very excited. Several researchers suggested holding a celebration banquet at the camp, and Professor Mans agreed. Finally, we could relax a bit. \n The celebration banquet will last all night...",
    ["戈达德"] = "Goddard",
    ["戈黛娃夫人"] = "Lady Godiva",
    ["戏剧大师"] = "Drama Master",
    ["戏剧大师蒙特利的戏一票难求，只加几场戏恐怕根本不够。"] = "Tickets for the plays of the master dramatist Montley are hard to come by; adding just a few more shows probably won't be enough at all.",
