    ["比心"] = "Heart Gesture",
    ["比打打杀杀适合我。"] = "It suits me better than fighting and killing.",
    ["比星空更崇高 比永恒更久远的黑夜女神"] = "The Evernight Goddess, more noble than the starry sky, more lasting than eternity.",
    ["比星空更崇高、比永恒更久远的黑夜女神，您是隐秘之母，厄难与恐惧的女皇，安眠和寂静的领主！ "] = "Evernight Goddess, who is more noble than the starry sky and more eternal than eternity, you are the Mother of Concealment, the Empress of Calamity and Horror, and the Lord of Slumber and Silence!",
    ["比星空更崇高，比永恒更久远的女神，我祈求您的眷顾！"] = "Goddess who is more noble than the starry sky and more eternal than eternity, I pray for your favor!",
    ["比星空更崇高，比永恒更久远的黑夜女神"] = "Evernight Goddess, more noble than the starry sky, more eternal than eternity",
    ["比星空更崇高，比永恒更久远的黑夜女神。"] = "The Evernight Goddess, more noble than the starry sky, more eternal than eternity.",
    ["比星空更崇高，比永恒更久远的黑夜女神！"] = "Evernight Goddess, more noble than the starry sky, more eternal than eternity!",
    ["比星空更崇高，比永恒更久远的黑夜女神， 我在此向您忏悔。我路过这里时，听到有人说——"] = "Evernight Goddess, who is more noble than the stars and more eternal than eternity, I repent to you here. When I passed by here, I heard someone say—",
    ["比星空更崇高，比永恒更久远的黑夜女神，愿您庇佑您虔诚的信徒。"] = "The Evernight Goddess, who is more noble than the starry sky and more eternal than eternity, may you bless your devout believers.",
    ["比普通曼陀罗更深邃的黑暗。"] = "Darkness deeper than ordinary Datura.",
    ["比武大会"] = "Tournament",
    ["比武大会下一阶段"] = "Next stage of Martial Arts Tournament",
    ["比武大会战队操作"] = "Tournament Team Operations",
    ["比武大会的模式介绍"] = "Tournament Mode Introduction",
    ["比比拉布"] = "Bibilab",
    ["比永恒更永恒"] = "More eternal than eternity",
    ["比清醒状态下更容易发现线索而已。这能力……有利有弊。"] = "It's just easier to find clues than in a waking state. This ability... has its pros and cons.",
    ["比煤灰更厚重的黑夜里，唯有工厂区的酒馆保持着喧闹。\n大笑、咳嗽、无休止的抱怨……巡警咒骂着，像避开麻烦一样绕过噪音，走向远处的街区。\n“他们走了。”娜塔放下帘子，向清醒的人们宣告。\n工人们正把布条铺在地上，用木炭条写着明天要举的口号：“要工资”“要休息”“要像人一样生活”，孩子挤在角落，分装干粮与小瓶酒精。烛火昏暗，映出一双双发亮的眼睛。\n“等到明天，我们就能拿回应得的报酬了吗？”年长的工人问。\n“等到明天，我们就能保证十小时的休息吗？”年幼的孩子问。\n“……抱歉，我无法向你们担保。”娜塔沉默了。\n “我们的旗帜会倒下，但我们前进的每一步，都会在地上留下痕迹。”\n或许，远在另一个时代，已经有人沿着它走到天亮。"] = "In the night, thicker and heavier than coal dust, only the taverns in the factory district remained noisy. \n Laughter, coughing, endless complaints... The patrolmen cursed, avoiding the noise as if avoiding trouble, and walked toward the distant blocks. \n \"They're gone.\" Nata lowered the curtain and announced to those who were awake. \n The workers were laying cloth strips on the ground, using charcoal sticks to write the slogans they would hold up tomorrow: \"We want wages,\" \"We want rest,\" \"We want to live like human beings.\" Children huddled in the corner, dividing dry rations and small bottles of alcohol. The candlelight was dim, reflecting pairs of bright eyes. \n \"By tomorrow, will we be able to get the pay we deserve?\" an older worker asked. \n \"By tomorrow, will we be able to guarantee ten hours of rest?\" a young child asked. \n \"...Sorry, I cannot guarantee that to you.\" Nata fell into silence. \n \"Our flag may fall, but every step we take forward will leave a mark on the ground.\" \n Perhaps, far away in another era, someone has already followed it until dawn.",
    ["比煤灰更厚重的黑夜里，唯有工厂区的酒馆保持着喧闹。\n大笑、咳嗽、无休止的抱怨……巡警咒骂着，像避开麻烦一样绕过噪音，走向远处的街区。\n“他们走了。”娜塔放下帘子，向清醒的人们宣告。\n工人们正把布条铺在地上，用木炭条写着明天要举的口号：“要工资”“要休息”“要像人一样生活”，孩子挤在角落，分装干粮与小瓶酒精。烛火昏暗，映出一双双发亮的眼睛。\n“等到明天，我们就能拿回应得的报酬了吗？”年长的工人问。\n“等到明天，我们就能保证十小时的休息吗？”年幼的孩子问。\n“……抱歉，我无法向你们担保。”娜塔沉默了。\n“我们的旗帜会倒下，但我们前进的每一步，都会在地上留下痕迹。”\n或许，远在另一个时代，已经有人沿着它走到天亮。"] = "In the night, heavier than coal dust, only the taverns in the factory district remained noisy. \nLaughter, coughing, endless complaints... The patrolmen cursed, bypassing the noise as if avoiding trouble, heading toward the distant blocks. \n\"They're gone,\" Nata lowered the curtain and announced to the sober people. \nThe workers were laying cloth strips on the ground, using charcoal sticks to write the slogans they would raise tomorrow: \"We want wages,\" \"We want rest,\" \"We want to live like human beings.\" Children huddled in the corner, dividing dry rations and small bottles of alcohol. The candlelight was dim, reflecting pairs of shining eyes. \n\"By tomorrow, will we be able to get the pay we deserve?\" an older worker asked. \n\"By tomorrow, will we be able to guarantee ten hours of rest?\" a young child asked. \n\"...Sorry, I cannot guarantee that for you,\" Nata fell silent. \n\"Our flags may fall, but every step we take forward will leave a mark on the ground.\" \nPerhaps, far away in another era, someone has already followed it until dawn.",
    ["比煤灰更脏的，是善行触及不到的角落。"] = "Dirtier than coal ash are the corners that good deeds cannot reach.",
