    ["铁十字街·马车车夫"] = "Iron Cross Street - Carriage Driver",
    ["铁十字街下街134号1楼"] = "1st Floor, 134 Lower Street, Iron Cross Street",
    ["铁十字街下街的苔丝老太太缝制这个布偶时，手指早已佝偻变形。\n黑色的宫廷长裙，深邃的眼眸，紧抿的嘴唇——她倾尽了最后的手艺，却没人知道为什么要把它做得如此精致。\n“多少钱？”一位绅士问。\n“换一瓶毒堇汁。”老太太说。\n交易完成了。那天晚上，苔丝老太太和病重的丈夫一起喝下了毒药，带着解脱的微笑闭上了双眼。\n三天后，那位绅士在街上被马车撞倒。\n一周后，他的妻子突患重病。\n两周后，他的店铺失火。\n当值夜者找到他时，绅士已经疯了，死死抱着那个布偶，喃喃自语：“是她……她把所有的不幸都缝进去了……”\n布偶的裙摆上，污痕隐约是泪水的形状。"] = "When old Mrs. Tess of Iron Cross Street in the Lower Street sewed this doll, her fingers were already crooked and deformed. \n A black court dress, deep eyes, tightly pursed lips—she poured all her remaining craftsmanship into it, yet no one knew why she had made it so exquisite. \n \"How much?\" a gentleman asked. \n \"Trade it for a bottle of hemlock juice,\" the old lady said. \n The transaction was completed. That night, old Mrs. Tess and her critically ill husband drank the poison together, closing their eyes with a smile of relief. \n Three days later, the gentleman was hit by a carriage on the street. \n A week later, his wife fell suddenly ill. \n Two weeks later, his shop caught fire. \n When the Nighthawks found him, the gentleman was already insane, clutching the doll tightly and muttering: \"It's her... she sewed all the misfortune into it...\" \n On the hem of the doll's dress, the stains were vaguely in the shape of tears.",
    ["铁十字街东北角"] = "Northeast Corner of Iron Cross Street",
